__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,_d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"DREAM_SYMBOL_INTRO",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"DREAM_SYMBOLS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),e.symbolReference=function(o){const t=o.toLowerCase().trim();return t?n.find(o=>o.symbol===t||o.also.includes(t))??n.find(o=>t.split(' ').some(n=>n.length>2&&(o.symbol===n||o.also.includes(n))))??null:null};const o='These are starting points, not a dictionary. A dog means something different to someone who grew up with one than to someone who was bitten. Begin with what the thing means to you and how the dream felt; reach for these only when you\u2019re stuck.',n=[{symbol:'water',also:['sea','river','flood','rain','lake'],notes:'Often read as feeling: calm water for a settled heart, rough or rising water for emotion that feels bigger than you. Rivers can be time and change, crossings a threshold.',ask:'Was the water clear or murky, and were you in it, on it or watching?'},{symbol:'house',also:['home','rooms','attic','cellar'],notes:'Many read a house as the self. New rooms can be parts of you or your life you haven\u2019t used yet; cellars what\u2019s buried, attics what\u2019s stored away or remembered.',ask:'Whose house was it, and which room were you drawn to?'},{symbol:'teeth',also:['teeth falling out','losing teeth'],notes:'One of the most common dreams anywhere. Often linked with worry about how you come across, losing control, or a change in life stage. It\u2019s rarely about teeth.',ask:'What in waking life feels as if it\u2019s slipping, or on show?'},{symbol:'falling',also:['fall','dropping'],notes:'Commonly tied to feeling unsupported or out of control. The jolt as you drift off (a hypnic jerk) is a body thing and needn\u2019t mean anything at all.',ask:'Did you land, wake, or start to fly?'},{symbol:'flying',also:['flight','floating'],notes:'Often freedom, perspective or rising above something. Struggling to stay up can be effort that feels unsustainable. A common doorway into lucid dreaming.',ask:'Was it joyful, effortful, or frightening?'},{symbol:'being chased',also:['chase','pursued','running'],notes:'Frequently something avoided: a feeling, a task, a conversation. Some find that turning to face the pursuer in a later dream changes it.',ask:'What would happen if you stopped running?'},{symbol:'snake',also:['serpent','adder'],notes:'Carries opposite meanings across cultures: danger and betrayal, or healing, wisdom and renewal (the skin shed). In some folk traditions, such as the Baltic house snake, a guardian of the home and threshold.',ask:'Did the snake threaten, guard, or simply watch?'},{symbol:'dog',also:['hound','puppy','black dog'],notes:'Loyalty, protection, friendship, instinct. In British and Irish folklore a black dog can be a guardian of roads and churchyards, or an omen; to many now it names low mood.',ask:'Did the dog feel like a friend, a guard or a threat?'},{symbol:'cat',also:['kitten'],notes:'Independence, intuition, the private self; for many practitioners, a familiar. Folklore gave cats second sight and a footing in both worlds.',ask:'Was the cat yours, a stranger, or leading you somewhere?'},{symbol:'bird',also:['crow','raven','owl','robin'],notes:'Messages and messengers. Crows and ravens tie to prophecy and the dead in much folklore; owls to night wisdom; a robin, for many, to a loved one who has died.',ask:'What kind of bird, and did it bring or take something?'},{symbol:'the dead',also:['dead relative','ancestor','ghost','grandmother','grandfather'],notes:'Visitation dreams of the beloved dead are common in grief and often feel unlike other dreams: calm, clear, and brief. Many traditions take them as real visits; all of them hold them as precious.',ask:'What did they say or give you, and how did you feel waking?'},{symbol:'death',also:['dying','funeral'],notes:'Not a forecast. Usually an ending that makes room for something: a job, a role, a version of yourself.',ask:'What in your life is ending, or needs to?'},{symbol:'baby',also:['birth','pregnancy','child'],notes:'New beginnings, a project or part of yourself that needs care, or vulnerability. Children in dreams can also be your younger self.',ask:'Whose was it, and did you feel ready to care for it?'},{symbol:'moon',also:['full moon','crescent'],notes:'Cycles, intuition, the hidden and the feminine in many traditions. Note the phase you saw: a waxing moon for growth, a full one for culmination, a dark one for rest.',ask:'What phase was it, and how did its light fall?'},{symbol:'door',also:['gate','threshold','key','locked door'],notes:'Thresholds and choices. A locked door can be a boundary or something not yet ready; a key, access or an answer you already hold. Hedge work is threshold work, so watch these.',ask:'Did you go through, and what was on the other side?'},{symbol:'road',also:['path','crossroads','journey','lost'],notes:'The way your life is going. Crossroads are old places of choice and spirit meetings; being lost can be uncertainty about direction.',ask:'Were you choosing the way, or being carried?'},{symbol:'tree',also:['forest','woods','oak','hawthorn'],notes:'Growth, family, roots and reach. A forest can be the unknown or a place of refuge. The world tree links the realms in many traditions; a lone hawthorn was a fairy tree.',ask:'Was the tree flourishing, bare, or fallen?'},{symbol:'fire',also:['flames','burning','candle','hearth'],notes:'Passion, anger, transformation, purification. A hearth fire can be home and warmth; a house fire, change that feels out of hand.',ask:'Were you warmed by it or running from it?'},{symbol:'naked',also:['nudity','undressed'],notes:'Being exposed or seen as you are. Embarrassment points to fear of judgement; ease can mean acceptance.',ask:'Did anyone else notice?'},{symbol:'exam',also:['test','unprepared','late'],notes:'Feeling tested or judged, often long after school ends. Running late can be pressure, or a sense of missing a chance.',ask:'Where in waking life do you feel measured?'},{symbol:'mirror',also:['reflection'],notes:'Self-image and self-knowledge. A strange reflection can be a side of you not yet met. Mirrors are old scrying tools and doorways in folklore.',ask:'Did the reflection match you?'},{symbol:'spider',also:['web'],notes:'Weaving, patience, creativity and fate; or feeling caught. In many tales the spider is a storyteller and spinner of the world.',ask:'Were you weaving or caught?'},{symbol:'hare',also:['rabbit'],notes:'In British and Irish lore, the hare is a creature of the moon and of witches, said to be a witch in another shape; from India to China and Japan, a hare lives in the moon. Also speed, fertility and spring.',ask:'Did it run from you, or wait?'},{symbol:'stairs',also:['ladder','climbing','lift'],notes:'Moving between levels: going up toward aims or clarity, going down into memory and the deeper self, a common image in journeying.',ask:'Up or down, and was it easy?'}]},2558,[]);
