__d(function(e,t,a,o,n,r,s){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(r,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(r,"HELP",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return i}});const i=[{id:'getting-started',title:'Getting started',intro:'The five tabs, how guests and accounts differ, and how to keep your work safe.',topics:[{id:'find-your-way-around',title:'Find your way around the five tabs',summary:'The bar along the bottom of the app holds everything.',steps:['Look at the bar along the bottom of the screen.','Today shows the moon, the holidays from your calendars and what is yours to do today. What is on the horizon sits just below the moon. Switch to "Sky & Lore" at the top for the sky, the day\u2019s correspondences and what suits your practice.','Altar is where you build and tend altars. Switch between "Personal", your own altars, and "Coven", the altars you tend with your covens, at the top.','Practice holds three sections, switched at the top: Grimoire (your own book and the Living Library), Rituals (ritual work: beginning, planning and building rituals and spells, the Workings library, Community Rituals, dedication journeys and your ritual journal) and Craft (the tools that aren\u2019t rituals: Cycle & Moon, astrology, divination, the sigil maker and the Craft tools for each path). The Practice tab reopens whichever you used last.','Coven is where you find, join and take part in covens: Messages, rites, the coven\u2019s altars, initiation and training. Switch between "My covens" and "Find a coven" at the top.','More holds Search, the Community, My chronicle, Settings (notifications and reminders, accessibility, your account and backup among them) and Help & legal, with "How to use the app" and support.'],keywords:['tabs','navigation','menu','bottom bar','where is','practice','coven','grimoire','rituals','craft']},{id:'welcome-tour',title:'Create your sanctuary or carry on as a guest',summary:'Choose how to start: with an account, or just on this phone.',steps:['On the welcome screen, tap "Create your sanctuary" to make an account, or "Sign in" if you already have one.','Sign in with the same account you use on the Salt & Sovereignty website to bring your altars and grimoire with you.','Or choose "Continue as a guest" to start straight away.','The first time you arrive, a short tour shows each main part of the app. Swipe or tap "Next", then "Begin". Tap "Skip" to leave it.'],keywords:['sign up','register','log in','login','guest','welcome','tour','onboarding']},{id:'replay-welcome-tour',title:'Watch the welcome tour again',summary:'The tour of every main part of the app, whenever you want it.',steps:['Open More, then "How to use the app". (It is also at the top of More, then Settings.)','Tap "Watch the welcome tour again".','Swipe, or tap "Next" and "Back", to move through the pages.','Tap "Begin" on the last page, or "Skip" at any time, to close it.'],href:'/more/help',keywords:['tour','intro','introduction','welcome','onboarding','replay','overview','what can it do','features']},{id:'guest-or-account',title:'Know the difference between a guest and an account',summary:'A guest keeps everything on this phone; an account keeps it in your Sanctuary and on the website too.',steps:['Open More, then Account. It says "Guest \xb7 saved on this device" or "Signed in as" with your email.','As a guest, altars, rituals and settings stay on this phone.','Signed in, your altars, Grimoire, ritual journal, templates, practice tools, My Practice notes and settings sync with the website.','Some things need an account: the Grimoire, ritual templates, My Practice entries, covens and My submissions.'],tips:['Before you remove the app as a guest, save a guest backup from More, Backup and restore.'],href:'/more/account',keywords:['sync','cloud','offline','website','account types']},{id:'sign-in-account',title:'Sign in',summary:'Use your Salt & Sovereignty account so your work follows you.',steps:['Tap "Sign in" wherever you see it, or open More, then Account.','Tap "Continue with Apple" or "Continue with Google" if you see them, or type your email and password.','Tap "Sign in". To make a new account, choose "Create your sanctuary" on the welcome screen and tap "Create account".','Forgotten your password? Tap "Forgot your password?".'],keywords:['log in','login','apple','google','password','forgot']},{id:'ways-to-sign-in',title:'Sign in more than one way',summary:'Add Apple, Google, or an email and password to your account, so every way you sign in opens the same sanctuary.',steps:['Sign in the way you did before.','Open More, then Account, and find "Ways to sign in". It lists every sign-in that opens this account.','Tap "Add Apple", "Add Google" or "Add email and password", and finish signing in with it.','To stop using one, tap "Remove" beside it, then "Yes, remove". Your last way to sign in always stays.'],tips:['If the app says that Apple ID or Google account already has its own Salt & Sovereignty account, you made a second account with it. Sign in with it and delete that account from More \u2192 Settings \u2192 Account first, or write to us and we\u2019ll help bring the two together.','Ways to sign in are kept with your account, so the website shows the same list.'],href:'/more/account',keywords:['link','linked','connect','apple','google','password','two accounts','duplicate account','merge','sign in methods']},{id:'bring-guest-work',title:'Bring guest work into your account',summary:'If you used the app as a guest first, move that work into your account after signing in.',steps:['Sign in. If the phone still holds guest work, the app offers to bring it over.','Or open More, then Account, then "Bring it into your account".','Tap "Save a guest backup first" if you want a copy to be safe.','Tap "Bring it into my account". Anything your account already has is kept as it is.','In Practice \u2192 Rituals, rituals from before signing in are moved with "Bring them into my account".'],tips:['If anything goes wrong, the guest copy stays on the phone untouched.'],href:'/more/guest-data',keywords:['migrate','move','transfer','import guest','guest data']},{id:'how-sync-works',title:'See whether your work is saved and synced',summary:'Your account screen shows the cloud status and the last successful sync.',steps:['Open More, then Account.','Read "Cloud status": Connected, Saving\u2026, Saved, Offline, Cloud unavailable, Guest data only, or Some changes weren\u2019t saved.','Check "Last successful sync" for the time of the last save.','On lists such as Altar and Grimoire, pull down to refresh.'],tips:['Offline, changes are kept on the phone and sent when you are back online.','If an altar change is refused, the Altar tab offers "Try again" or "Discard these changes".'],href:'/more/account',keywords:['offline','saving','cloud status','refresh','pull down','not saved']},{id:'backup-complete',title:'Back up your Sanctuary',summary:'Save a copy of your work as a file you keep somewhere private.',steps:['Open More, then "Backup and restore".','Under "Back up", tap "Save complete backup". As a guest the button reads "Save guest backup".','To save only your Grimoire, tap "Export Grimoire".','Choose where to keep the file. The same file restores on the website.'],tips:['A backup can hold names, spiritual writing, ritual records and images, so keep it somewhere private.'],href:'/more/backup',keywords:['export','save copy','download data','backup file']},{id:'backup-restore',title:'Restore from a backup',summary:'Merge a backup file into your Sanctuary without deleting anything.',steps:['Open More, then "Backup and restore".','Under "Restore", tap "Choose a backup file" and pick your file (up to 25 MB).','When it says the backup is checked, tap "1 \xb7 Save a safety backup first".','Read what will be added, then tap "2 \xb7 Merge with my Sanctuary".'],tips:['Restoring merges. It adds what isn\u2019t here yet and keeps your current copy of anything that matches.'],href:'/more/backup',keywords:['import','recover','merge','restore data','lost']},{id:'search-everything',title:'Search your whole practice',summary:'One search covers the Living Library, your Grimoire, your ritual journal and templates, your readings and your dreams.',steps:['Open More and tap "Search your practice".','Type at least two letters, such as a herb, an intention or a moon phase.','Look under Living Library, Your Grimoire, Ritual journal, Ritual templates, Divination readings and Dreams.','Tap a result to open it.'],href:'/more/search',keywords:['find','lookup','search bar']},{id:'text-size-accessibility',title:'Change text size, spacing, contrast and motion',summary:'Make the app easier to read and calmer to look at.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then Accessibility.','Choose a "Text size" percentage.','Under Reading, switch on "Line spacing", "Letter spacing" or "Readable font".','Under Display, switch on "High contrast" or "Reduce motion".','Tap "Reset all" to return to the defaults.'],tips:['These are kept on this device. Your phone\u2019s own text size setting still applies on top.'],href:'/more/accessibility',keywords:['font','bigger text','large print','dyslexia','contrast','animation','motion','a11y','readable']},{id:'open-settings',title:'Open your settings',summary:'Every choice in the app is in Settings, in seven groups.',steps:['Open More, then Settings.','You: Identity, and Location & hemisphere. Your practice: Your crafts, Path & traditions, My deities, Calendars & holidays.','Screens: Today, Grimoire, Living Library, Divination and Altar. Then Reminders, Accessibility, Covens & privacy, and Account & data.','Change what you like. Each change saves itself, with a quiet "Saved" beneath.'],tips:['Signed in, settings are shared with the website. As a guest they stay on this device.'],href:'/more/settings',keywords:['preferences','options','configure']},{id:'support-contact-policies',title:'Reach support, privacy and contact links',summary:'The Help group at the bottom of More holds crisis lines, contact and policies.',steps:['Open More and scroll to Help.','Tap "Support" for crisis, grief and other support lines.','Tap "Contact us" to email us.','Tap "Privacy Policy" or "Submission Terms" to read them in your browser.'],keywords:['help','email','privacy','terms','contact us','feedback','version']},{id:'send-a-correction',title:'Send a correction, note or addition',summary:'Everything here was researched with care, and notes on anything that looks wrong or missing are always welcome.',steps:['Open the page you have a note about: a Living Library entry, a deity, a holiday, a dedication journey, a card, rune or stave, or the Closed & living traditions guide.','Scroll to the foot of the page and tap "Send a note".','Your mail app opens with the page named in the subject, such as "Note on: Hekate". Write what you\u2019d like to share and send it.','For a note about the research as a whole, open More, scroll to Help and tap "A note on our research", then "Send a note".'],tips:['If your mail app doesn\u2019t open, write to the address shown under the button. Every note is read.'],href:'/more/research',keywords:['correction','mistake','wrong','error','report','research','sources','addition','suggest a tradition','feedback']}]},{id:'today',title:'Today',intro:'The first tab: the moon, the day, what is coming and a question to sit with.',topics:[{id:'read-today',title:'Read the Today screen',summary:'See the date, the moon, the sign and the day\u2019s ruling planet at a glance.',steps:['Open the Today tab. At the top, switch between "Today" and "Sky & Lore". Today opens on the one you used last; tap Today in the bar at the bottom to come back to "Today".','On "Today", the date line and the day\u2019s ruler show which planet governs today. Calendars you keep can name the day in their own way above or below it.','The moon shows tonight\u2019s phase, its sign and how much of it is lit. Tap it to read about this moon.','Below it, "On the horizon" shows the next moon phase and holiday. Then come "Your next working", your covens, what wants tending, anything to look back on, and last night\u2019s dream in the morning.','At the end, "Set tonight\u2019s altar" and a "Reflect" question.','On "Sky & Lore" come "Today\u2019s sky", "Correspondences" and "For your practice".'],href:'/today?tab=today',keywords:['moon phase','date','ruler','planet of the day','home']},{id:'today-on-the-horizon',title:'See the next moon phase and holiday',summary:'"On the horizon" always shows what is coming next.',steps:['Open the Today tab and stay on "Today" at the top.','"On the horizon" sits just below the moon and today\u2019s holidays.','Read the two tiles: the next moon phase and the next holiday from your calendars.','Below them, the next new or full moon and any eclipse are listed.'],href:'/today?section=horizon',keywords:['upcoming','next full moon','next holiday','eclipse']},{id:'today-holidays',title:'See today\u2019s holiday and what it means',summary:'A holiday from your chosen calendars appears on Today on the day itself.',steps:['Open the Today tab on a holiday.','Read the holiday card: its name, the traditions that keep it and its meaning.','Tap the card to open the day\u2019s own page: who is honoured, its history, how to keep it today and a working. A holiday without a page opens Holidays ahead, with "Choose calendars \u203a" to change them.'],tips:['The holiday card only appears on days that have a holiday.'],href:'/today/calendar',keywords:['sabbat','feast day','festival','wheel of the year']},{id:'today-holy-pages',title:'Read about a moon or holy day, and keep it in your Grimoire',summary:'Each main moon phase and many holidays have a page of their own.',steps:['On Today, tap the moon or a holiday card, or tap a tile under "On the horizon".','Read "Who is honoured, and why", "History", "Keeping it today", "A working" and its correspondences, with "What we know" and "What we don\u2019t".','Signed in, the page is kept in your Grimoire with room for your own notes. Under "In your Grimoire", tap "Open the page".','Tap "Open the working" to read its ritual, or "Plan a ritual" to choose a night.'],tips:['Tap a herb, crystal or deity under its correspondences to open it in the Living Library.'],keywords:['holy day','holiday page','moon page','full moon meaning','new moon meaning','sabbat meaning','festival','grimoire page','what does it mean']},{id:'today-sky',title:'Open the sky today',summary:'See the planets, retrogrades and eclipses, and where they sit.',steps:['On Today, choose "Sky & Lore" at the top and find the "Today\u2019s sky" card.','Tap "The sky today".','Read the sections: Sun and Moon, Planets, Retrogrades, Eclipses and "Where you are".'],tips:['The Moon card tells you when the moon is void of course and what that suggests.'],href:'/today/sky',keywords:['astrology','retrograde','eclipse','planets','void of course','voc','mercury retrograde']},{id:'set-location',title:'Set your location for sunrise, moonrise and planetary hours',summary:'Your place is kept on the phone and never sent anywhere.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Location & hemisphere". ("The sky today" and Today have a link to it too.)','Tap "Use my location", or type a latitude and longitude and tap "Save location".','Under Hemisphere, choose "From my place", Northern or Southern for the seasons and moon names.','To remove it, tap "Forget my location".'],tips:['West and south are negative numbers. The location is rounded to about a kilometre.'],href:'/more/settings/location',keywords:['gps','place','latitude','longitude','sunrise','sunset','moonrise','hemisphere']},{id:'today-correspondences',title:'See the day\u2019s correspondences',summary:'Each weekday has its own colours, crystals, herbs, metal, incense and candle.',steps:['Open the Today tab and choose "Sky & Lore" at the top. The "Correspondences" card comes after "Today\u2019s sky".','Read the colours, crystals, herbs, metal, incense and candle for the day\u2019s planet.','Tap a crystal or herb that is underlined to open its Living Library entry.'],href:'/today?section=correspondences',keywords:['colours','colors','weekday','herbs of the day','crystals of the day','planetary day']},{id:'today-for-your-practice',title:'See what Today offers for your practice and your deities',summary:'A line from each practice you keep, your deities\u2019 days, and a working for tonight.',steps:['Choose your crafts in More, then Settings, then "Your crafts", and your gods in "My deities".','On Today, choose "Sky & Lore" at the top and find "For your practice".','Each line comes from one of your practices or deities, such as tonight\u2019s planting moon or the next tide. On a deity\u2019s holy day its line shows in gold.','Tap a line to open that tool, or "A working for tonight" to read a premade working that suits the night.'],href:'/today?section=practice',keywords:['practice card','deity','patron','holy day','working for tonight','suggestion','for you']},{id:'today-card-of-the-day',title:'Draw a card for the day',summary:'A small line on Today opens a one-card draw, and shows the card once you keep it.',steps:['On Today, tap "Draw a card for the day \u203a".','Tap "Shuffle and draw", turn the card over and read what it means.','Write what you make of it if you like, and tap "Keep this reading".','Back on Today, the line shows today\u2019s card. Tap it to open the reading.'],tips:['Near a new or full moon or a festival, a line beneath offers a spread for it.','To hide the line, tap "Customise Today \u203a" at the bottom of Today (or open More, then Settings, then Today), and switch off "A card for the day".'],href:'/rituals/divination/draw',keywords:['daily card','card of the day','tarot','one card','today card']},{id:'today-customise',title:'Choose what Today shows',summary:'The moon and holiday panels, a card for the day, Hekate\u2019s Deipnon and the morning dream prompt.',steps:['At the bottom of Today, tap "Customise Today \u203a". (Or open More, then Settings, then Today.)','Under "The moon and the day\u2019s holiday", choose what shows and how it is laid out.','Switch "A card for the day", "Hekate\u2019s Deipnon" or "Last night\u2019s dream" on or off. Each change saves itself.'],tips:['Which holidays show comes from Settings \u2192 Calendars & holidays.'],href:'/more/settings/today',keywords:['customise today','customize today','today layout','hide card','dream prompt','side by side']},{id:'today-deipnon',title:'Keep Hekate\u2019s Deipnon each month',summary:'On the last day of each Attic month, a gentle note: clear and cleanse the house, leave her supper at a crossroads, and draw the Crossroads spread.',steps:['Keep the Hellenic monthly days (More, then Settings, then "Calendar & holidays"), or keep Hekate as your patron in "My deities".','On the Deipnon, Today shows "Hekate\u2019s Deipnon" with what to do. Tap "Draw the Crossroads spread" to draw it.','In the phone app, a reminder comes that morning, at the time you chose for sacred days.','To turn it off, open Settings, then Today, and switch off "Hekate\u2019s Deipnon".'],tips:['What is given to Hekate is left, and not eaten.'],href:'/today?section=deipnon',keywords:['deipnon','hekate','hecate','dark moon','supper','crossroads','hellenic','monthly','cleansing','attic calendar']},{id:'today-next-working',title:'Plan or continue a ritual from Today',summary:'The Today screen shows your next planned working, or the one under way.',steps:['On Today, find the card headed "Your next working".','If a ritual is running, tap "Continue the ritual".','If one is planned, tap "Open the plan".','If nothing is planned, tap "Plan a ritual".'],href:'/today?section=working',keywords:['next ritual','resume ritual','planned']},{id:'today-tonights-altar',title:'Set tonight\u2019s altar',summary:'Get a starter altar chosen for today\u2019s planet, moon or holiday.',steps:['On Today, tap "Set tonight\u2019s altar".','Read the note that says what the altar is set for.','Move, swap or add anything you like. Tap a piece and "Swap it" for something with the same correspondence.','Tap "Save" to keep it. Tap "Why these pieces" to read why each piece is there.'],tips:['Tonight\u2019s altar is not kept until you save it.','It works for every calendar you keep or show: on a festival night, or while a festival of several days runs, it sets out one of that festival\u2019s seasonal things, such as diya lamps at Diwali, the kalash at Navaratri, Holi\u2019s colours, or the lamps of the five days during the Epagomenal Days. The Hindu and Kemetic festivals count when you show that calendar under "Also show" in "Calendar & holidays", on the dates it gives where you are.','When festivals from two calendars share a night, the one whose altar is being set comes first, and only one seasonal thing is set out, so the altar stays uncrowded.'],keywords:['starter altar','daily altar','tonight altar','suggested altar','festival','diwali','navaratri','holi','epagomenal','wep ronpet']},{id:'today-reflect-prompt',title:'Sit with the day\u2019s question',summary:'Today ends with a question to reflect on.',steps:['Scroll to the bottom of the "Today" tab on Today.','Read the line under "Reflect".','On the new, quarter or full moon, a line shows what you kept last time the moon looked like this. Tap it to open that journal entry.'],keywords:['prompt','journal prompt','reflection','last full moon']}]},{id:'calendars',title:'Calendars and holidays',intro:'The holidays you keep, your own days, and the moon\u2019s and the old calendars\u2019 ways of counting them.',topics:[{id:'choose-calendars',title:'Choose the calendars and holidays you keep',summary:'Pick the traditions whose holidays you want to see on Today.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Calendar & holidays".','Switch on the calendars you keep, such as Wheel of the Year, Norse & Heathen or Roman.','Scroll to "The year ahead" to see every holiday for the next twelve months.','Each change saves itself.'],tips:['Tap "Hide" on a calendar you never want to see. Tap "Show hidden calendar" in the same place to bring it back.'],href:'/more/settings/calendar',keywords:['holidays','sabbats','wheel of the year','celtic','hellenic','slavic','christian','southern hemisphere']},{id:'today-main-calendar',title:'Choose which tradition names your day',summary:'Your main calendar names the day at the top of Today.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Calendar & holidays".','Switch on the calendars you keep under "Your calendars".','If you chose more than one, pick one under "Main calendar".','Each change saves itself.'],href:'/more/settings/calendar',keywords:['tradition','athenian','norse','roman','date line','primary calendar']},{id:'calendar-count-by-moon',title:'Count your days by the moon',summary:'Let Today lead with the moon\u2019s month and the day of it.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Calendar & holidays".','Under "Count my days by", choose "The moon". The ordinary date shows beneath it on Today.','Under "Hemisphere", choose "From my place", "Northern" or "Southern", so the seasons and the moons\u2019 names fit where you are.','Each change saves itself.'],tips:['"From my place" uses the location you set on the sky screen.','Under the moon\u2019s months, choose how the months are named, where the year begins and what a Blue Moon is. Tap "About this calendar" for where each comes from.'],href:'/more/settings/calendar',keywords:['lunar calendar','moon months','moon date','hemisphere','southern','count days','blue moon','lunar new year']},{id:'calendar-moon-follow',title:'Let the moon\u2019s months follow your calendar',summary:'Name the moons and begin the year as the Attic, Coligny or Hindu calendar does.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Calendar & holidays".','Under "Also show", tick the calendar you follow: the Attic (Athenian), Coligny (Gaulish) or Hindu lunar calendar.','Under the moon\u2019s months, choose "As the Attic calendar" (or the one you ticked) under "The year begins": for the Attic calendar, the first new moon after the summer solstice, when Hekatombaion begins.','Under "Name the months", choose "The Attic months" (or the Coligny or Hindu months) to call each moon by that calendar\u2019s month.','Each change saves itself.'],tips:['Each choice says where it comes from. The moon\u2019s day 1 is still the day of the new moon, so the Attic date, which begins the next day, runs a day behind.','If you stop showing that calendar, the moon goes back to the folk names or the winter solstice for the moment, and Settings says so. Show it again and your choice comes back.','The southern names and the Blue Moon have no calendar to follow: no calendar here defines them, so they stay as they are.'],href:'/more/settings/calendar',keywords:['attic new year','hekatombaion','hellenic new year','samonios','chaitra','ugadi','follow calendar','month names','year begins','lunar new year']},{id:'calendar-old-calendars',title:'Show the Athenian, Roman and other old calendars',summary:'See today\u2019s date as the old calendars counted it, under the date on Today.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Calendar & holidays".','Under "Also show", tick the calendars you want: the Attic (Athenian) calendar, Roman days, the Kemetic (Egyptian) calendar, the Coligny calendar (Gaulish), the Old Icelandic calendar, Slavic months and the Old Style, or the Hindu lunar calendar (panchang). Calendars of your path come first.','Tap "About this calendar" to read where it comes from and how sure we can be. Some have choices of their own.','Each change saves itself. On Today, tap one of their lines for more.'],href:'/more/settings/calendar',keywords:['attic','athenian','greek calendar','roman','kalends','kemetic','egyptian','coligny','gaulish','icelandic','norse','slavic','hindu','panchang','traditional calendar','old calendar']},{id:'own-calendar-events',title:'Add your own events and single holidays',summary:'Keep your own dates, or pick single holidays from any calendar.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Calendar & holidays".','Switch on "Your own calendar".','Under "Add an event", give it a name, choose how it repeats (Every year, Every month, Every week or Once), then a month and day.','Tap "Add event". It saves itself.','Under "Holidays from other calendars", open a calendar and switch on single holidays without turning on the whole calendar.'],href:'/more/settings/calendar',keywords:['custom holiday','birthday','anniversary','coven gathering','dedication day','personal date']},{id:'today-layout',title:'Change what Today shows and how it is laid out',summary:'Show the moon, the holiday or both, one above the other or side by side.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Calendar & holidays".','Under "On Today", choose "Moon and holiday", "Moon only" or "Holiday only".','If you chose both, choose "One above the other" or "Side by side".','Each change saves itself.'],href:'/more/settings/calendar',keywords:['layout','hide moon','hide holiday','side by side','stacked']}]},{id:'reminders',title:'Reminders',intro:'Gentle notes on this phone for the moon, your plans, your holidays, tending your altar and its plants, offerings, crystals and candles, planning rituals, and your covens. Each kind can be shaped as you like.',topics:[{id:'reminders-everything',title:'Choose which reminders you get',summary:'One Reminders page in Settings, a line for each kind, and a page for each.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Reminders". (Practice \u2192 Rituals has a "Reminders" row that opens the same page.)','Each row says what is on: "Moon and rituals", "Holidays", "Tending", "Ritual planning", "Daily practice", "Covens", "Quiet hours and pause" and "Your calendar".','Tap a row to open its page and choose.'],tips:['Holidays, tending, planning, quiet hours and the pause follow you to the website and to your other phones when you\u2019re signed in. The moon, ritual, devotion and dream choices are kept on this phone.','Android can mute each kind on its own: open the phone\u2019s Settings, then Notifications, then Salt & Sovereignty.'],href:'/more/settings/notifications',keywords:['notifications','alerts','reminders','bell','customise reminders','customize reminders']},{id:'moon-reminders',title:'Get reminded of the moon',summary:'Choose which phases to hear about, and when.',steps:['On Today, tap "Remind me of the moon", or open Settings \u2192 Reminders, then "Moon and rituals".','Under "Moon phases", switch on New Moon, First Quarter, Full Moon or Last Quarter.','Add earlier heads-ups under "Also remind me": "The day before", "A week before", or "At the exact moment".','Under "At", choose the time of day the reminders arrive.','Optionally type your own note for a phase, such as "Write your intentions".'],tips:['If notifications are off for the app, tap "Open Settings" on that screen to turn them on.'],href:'/today/reminders?section=moon',keywords:['notifications','new moon reminder','full moon reminder','alerts','bell']},{id:'holiday-reminders',title:'Be reminded of your holidays',summary:'Every holiday in the calendars you keep, or just the ones you pick, as far ahead as you like.',steps:['Open Settings \u2192 Reminders, then "Holidays", and switch on "Remind me of my holidays".','Under "How far ahead", choose any of "On the day", "The day before", "3 days before" and "A week before", and under "At" the time of day.','Under "Calendars", tap a calendar to turn it on or off, give it its own timing, or pick its holidays: "All", "None", or one by one. Long calendars have "Find a holiday".','Under a holiday, tap "Change its timing \u203a" to give that one day its own heads-ups.'],tips:['The calendars are the ones you keep and show in Settings \u2192 Calendars & holidays (the Hindu and Kemetic calendars among them), the Hellenic monthly days with Hekate\u2019s Deipnon, your own days, and your deities\u2019 sacred days.','Hekate\u2019s Deipnon is one of the Hellenic monthly days here. Turning it off in Settings \u2192 Today turns off its note on Today and its reminder together.'],href:'/more/settings/notifications?section=holidays',keywords:['holiday reminder','sabbat reminder','samhain reminder','deipnon reminder','sacred days','festival','diwali','notification']},{id:'tending-reminders',title:'Be reminded to tend plants, altars, offerings, crystals and candles',summary:'Each on its own schedule, at its own time.',steps:['Open Settings \u2192 Reminders, then "Tending".','Plants: choose "When it\u2019s thirsty" (by how often you water each and when you last did) or "On a schedule" (every few days, or on chosen days). Tap "Its own way \u203a" under a plant to give it its own. A plant taken off its altar stops asking.','Altars: how often, at what time, and which altars.','Offerings: when one is going over (on the day, or the day before), and a regular refresh if you like.','Crystals: each full moon, new moon, both, or every few weeks. Each stone is listed with how to cleanse it safely: selenite and other soft stones stay dry, and stones that fade stay out of the sun.','Candles: when one burning on your altar is nearly burned down, to light a part-burned working again, or a daily candle practice.'],href:'/more/settings/notifications?section=tending',keywords:['water reminder','plant reminder','offering reminder','crystal cleanse reminder','candle reminder','altar reminder','tending']},{id:'tend-your-own',title:'Keep your own day-to-day tending on To tend',summary:'Cleansing the house, warding, salt lines, a spiritual bath: when you last did it and when it\u2019s next due.',steps:['Open Today \u2192 To tend, and tap "Add your own".','Name it ("Cleanse the house"), choose what kind it is (Cleansing, Warding / protection refresh, Salt lines, Spiritual bath, Wash altar cloths, Charge water, or Something else in your own words) and add notes if you like.','Under "How often", choose Every day, Every week, Every few days (then how many, 1 to 365), By the moon or Until a day. "Every few days" works for anything else on the list too.','When you\u2019ve done it, open it, tick how (for a cleansing: Incense / smoke, Florida Water mop, Floor wash, Sound / bells, Salt, Sprays, or Other in your words), add a note and tap "Done today". Turn on "Done on another day" to mark a day that\u2019s past.','It then shows when it was last done and when it\u2019s next due: "Last done 9 days ago \xb7 due in 5 days", "due today" or "overdue by 2 days". "Its history" keeps the last 50 times; "Take this one out" removes one marked by mistake.','Turn on "Remind me" for a reminder on the day it\u2019s due, with your other reminders, quiet hours and any pause. Due things also show on Today\u2019s To tend card and in the widgets.','Turn on "Also note it in my Grimoire" (off until you choose it) and each time you mark it done, a short page is added under Tending in your Grimoire. "Change or remove it" edits it or takes it off your list.','Without an account, your own things are kept on this device; signed in, they follow you to the website and your other phones.'],href:'/today/tend',keywords:['own tending','cleanse the house','cleansing','warding','protection','salt lines','spiritual bath','altar cloths','charge water','every few days','last done','chores','routine','to tend']},{id:'planning-reminders',title:'Be reminded to plan a ritual',summary:'Before your holidays, and before your coven\u2019s, earlier if you lead it.',steps:['Open Settings \u2192 Reminders, then "Ritual planning".','Switch on "Remind me to plan a ritual" and choose how many days before each holiday. A holiday you\u2019ve already planned a ritual for doesn\u2019t ask.','Under "Your covens", reminders are on for covens you lead (as head of the coven, or in a position that leads or schedules rites), two weeks ahead unless you choose otherwise. Turn each coven on or off, and choose how far ahead.'],tips:['Rites you\u2019ve said you\u2019ll come to are reminded the day before and an hour before.'],href:'/more/settings/notifications?section=planning',keywords:['plan ritual reminder','coven reminder','high priestess','head of coven','sabbat planning']},{id:'quiet-reminders',title:'Quiet hours, a pause, and busy days',summary:'Keep the nights quiet, pause everything for a while, and gather a busy day into one note.',steps:['Open Settings \u2192 Reminders, then "Quiet hours and pause".','Switch on "Pause all reminders" and choose how long: a day, a week, a month, or until you turn them back on.','Switch on "Keep quiet at night" and choose when quiet hours begin and end.','Leave "Gather a busy day into one note" on to hear about a busy day once, in the morning.'],tips:['A phone holds only so many reminders at once. The soonest and most important are always kept, and more are added each time you open the app.'],href:'/more/settings/notifications?section=quiet',keywords:['quiet hours','do not disturb','pause notifications','too many notifications','summary']},{id:'ritual-reminders',title:'Be reminded before a planned ritual',summary:'Ritual reminders ring before the night you planned.',steps:['Open Settings \u2192 Reminders, then "Moon and rituals".','Under "Planned rituals", switch on "Remind me before a planned ritual".','Choose "15 minutes before", "An hour before" or "Three hours before".'],href:'/rituals/reminders?section=moon',keywords:['plan reminder','notification','before ritual']},{id:'sky-to-calendar',title:'Add moon phases, holidays and eclipses to your phone calendar',summary:'Let your phone\u2019s calendar show the sky.',steps:['Open Settings \u2192 Reminders, then "Your calendar".','Switch on "Moon phases you chose", "Holidays" or "Eclipses & retrogrades".','Allow calendar access when asked. If you have several calendars, choose one under "Add events to".','Tap "Event settings \u203a" beside a switch to change how those events look.'],href:'/rituals/reminders?section=calendar',keywords:['ics','apple calendar','google calendar','sync to calendar','calendar export']},{id:'calendar-subscribe',title:'Subscribe to your practice in Google or Apple Calendar',summary:'A private link your calendar keeps up to date: planned rituals, coven gatherings, holidays, moon phases and your ancestors\u2019 days.',steps:['Sign in, open Settings \u2192 Reminders, then "Your calendar".','Under "Subscribe in your calendar", tap "Make my calendar link".','Tap "Open in your calendar", or "Copy the link" and add it in your calendar: in Google Calendar, Other calendars, then From URL; in Apple Calendar, File, then New Calendar Subscription.','Under "What it carries", choose what it shows.'],tips:['Anyone with the link can see what it carries. "Reset the link" makes a new one and stops the old one working.','Calendars refresh subscriptions on their own schedule, from every few hours to a day.','Holidays and moon phases follow your calendars and choices; the app brings them up to date each day you open it.'],href:'/rituals/reminders?section=calendar',keywords:['webcal','ical','subscribe','calendar feed','google calendar','apple calendar','outlook']}]},{id:'altar',title:'Altar',intro:'Build altars piece by piece, tend them over time and keep them with your account.',topics:[{id:'altar-build-new',title:'Build a new altar',summary:'Start with an empty altar and add things from the cabinet.',steps:['Open the Altar tab.','Tap "Build a new altar".','Tap "Open the cabinet" and choose what belongs.','Tap "Save" at the top when you are happy with it.'],href:'/altar',keywords:['create altar','new altar','start altar','empty altar']},{id:'altar-save',title:'Save an altar',summary:'Name it and keep it, on this phone or in your Sanctuary.',steps:['On the altar screen, tap "Save".','Type a name under "Altar name".','Tap "Save altar". For an altar you already saved, tap "Save changes".','To keep the original and make a copy, tap "Save as a new altar".'],tips:['A small label above the altar\u2019s name says "Unsaved changes" until you save.'],keywords:['name altar','keep altar','save as','copy altar','duplicate altar']},{id:'altar-open-saved',title:'Open or continue an altar',summary:'Your saved altars are listed on the Altar tab, under "Personal".',steps:['Open the Altar tab. At the top, switch between "Personal" and "Coven". Altar opens on the one you used last; tap Altar in the bar at the bottom to come back to "Personal".','On "Personal", tap an altar in the list to open it.','If you left one unsaved, tap the "Unsaved changes" card to continue your working altar.'],href:'/altar?tab=personal',keywords:['saved altars','list','resume','draft','working altar','personal']},{id:'altar-place-objects',title:'Add candles, herbs, crystals and more from the cabinet',summary:'The cabinet holds everything you can set on an altar.',steps:['On the altar screen, tap "Open the cabinet".','Choose a drawer: Candles, Herbs, Crystals, Tools, Deities, Vessels, Natural, Seasonal, Plants or Offerings. Or type in "Search the cabinet".','Tap an item to place it in the middle of the altar.','For an item with several forms, tap the form you want.'],tips:['The cabinet shows each item\u2019s best-known uses, so you can choose with meaning.','Tap the star on any item to keep it in Favourites, the first drawer, here and on the website.'],keywords:['cabinet','drawers','add object','place item','items','tools','deity statues','vessels','plants','offerings']},{id:'altar-natural-and-tools',title:'Add natural finds and everyday tools',summary:'Feathers, a hag stone, shells and acorns; a scrying mirror, red cord, a lantern or a singing bowl.',steps:['Open the cabinet and choose the Natural drawer for feathers, stones, shells, wood, antler, leaves and other finds.','Or choose Tools for divination tools, cords and wax, candle care, drums and bowls, lamps and figures.','Each says a few words about itself. Tap one to place it.'],tips:['An oil lamp, lantern or salt lamp is set down glowing. Tap "Glow" to turn it off or on.','Tap a bell on your altar for "Ring the bell" (one chime) or "Ring to cleanse the space" (three chimes). Ringing to cleanse is kept in that altar\u2019s History as "Space cleansed with the bell"; it doesn\u2019t change anything on To tend. On a coven altar everyone there hears it. The chime follows Candle sounds in Accessibility, and as you rang it on purpose it sounds even with an iPhone\u2019s silent switch on.'],keywords:['natural','feathers','hag stone','shells','sea glass','acorns','antler','scrying mirror','crystal ball','red cord','witch\u2019s ladder','lantern','oil lamp','singing bowl','drum','stang','bell','ring the bell','cleanse the space']},{id:'altar-seasonal',title:'Set out seasonal things for the festivals',summary:'Lanterns at Samhain, the Yule log, Brigid\u2019s cross, the eiresione at the Pyanepsia, the drinking horn at the bl\xf3t, the May bush at Bealtaine, tapers at the Saturnalia, the Advent wreath, the didukh at Koliada, lamps at Diwali, the Osiris bed for the days upon the year, and snowdrops in late winter.',steps:['Open the cabinet and choose the Seasonal drawer.','Its things are grouped by calendar: the Wheel of the Year, the Greek festivals, Norse & Heathen, the Celtic festivals, the Roman festivals, the Christian & folk calendar, the Slavic festivals, the Hindu festivals, the Kemetic (Egyptian) festivals, and the turning seasons. Each one names the festivals it is kept for.','In the week before a festival from a calendar you keep, and while it runs, the drawer comes first and that festival\u2019s things are at the top, under "For Samhain" (or whichever is coming). The monthly Greek days (the Noumenia, the Agathos Daimon and Hekate\u2019s Deipnon) come round every month, so theirs come to the top only the day before and on the day.','The season\u2019s own thing (snowdrops in late winter, a blossoming branch in spring, wildflowers in summer, leaves in autumn) comes next, under "This season", whatever calendars you keep. If you keep the Wheel of the Year for the Southern Hemisphere, the seasons follow it.','Tap one to place it on the altar.'],tips:['Which festivals count follows the calendars you keep (More, then Settings, then "Calendar & holidays"): the Wheel of the Year unless you choose others. Holidays you add one by one to your own calendar count too.','Search the drawer by a festival or a god: "Dionysus", "Anthesteria", "Hekate", "Odin", "Brigid", "Lughnasadh", "Saturn", "Vesta", "Candlemas", "St Michael", "Kupala", "Diwali", "Ganesha", "Osiris".','The Celtic things come to the top at the matching sabbats too: the May bush at Beltane, the bilberries at Lammas, the Br\xedde\xf3g at Imbolc. The Lammas loaf comes at the Wheel\u2019s Lammas as well as the Christian one.','The Hindu and Kemetic festivals follow their own calendars: they come to the top only if you show the Hindu lunar calendar (panchang) or the Kemetic (Egyptian) calendar under "Also show" in "Calendar & holidays", on the dates that calendar gives where you are. The days upon the year, the birthdays of Osiris, Horus, Set, Isis and Nephthys, come together as the Epagomenal Days, from a week before the first of them and all through them; then Wep Ronpet, the new year.','The Hindu things are customs many households keep (Diwali\u2019s lamps and rangoli, Holi\u2019s colours, modak for Ganesha, bilva leaves for Shiva, the Navaratri kalash), and the Kemetic ones come from the ancient temple calendars as Kemetic practice keeps them today. Confirm a Hindu festival\u2019s day with a local panchang or temple.','The Christian & folk calendar keeps the old household customs: chalk and blessed water for the Epiphany house blessing, Candlemas candles, Easter lilies and red eggs, the Assumption\u2019s herb bundle, Michaelmas daisies, the Advent wreath, and holly and ivy. If you hide the Christian calendar in "Calendar & holidays", its things leave the drawer too, and never come to the top.','The food ones are real food: apples, gourds and a pomegranate soften and brown over a couple of weeks; the bilberries, the pot of beans, the kykeon, the moon cake, Hekate\u2019s supper, the Parentalia offering, the mola salsa, the Lammas loaf, the red eggs, the kutia, the Dziady supper, the bread and salt, the modak and the offering table\u2019s bread go over in a day or few, and ask to be tended as other offerings do. Flowers and cut branches (the May bush, the Midsummer birch, Flora\u2019s flowers, Juno\u2019s garland, the Neptunalia boughs, Easter lilies, Pentecost peonies, Michaelmas daisies, the holly and ivy, the Kupala wreath, the marigolds, the bilva leaves, the blue lotus, snowdrops, blossom and wildflowers) wilt as cut flowers do. The woven, straw and carved things, the Lemuria\u2019s dried black beans, the chalk, candles, blessed water, dried herb bundle and Advent wreath, Marzanna, the didukh and the carollers\u2019 star, the lamps, rangoli, colours and kalash, the Osiris bed and the sistrum, and the autumn leaves, keep.','The phiale and the drinking horn hold a libation, as a bowl or chalice does.','On a festival night from any calendar you keep or show, the Hindu and Kemetic ones included, "Set tonight\u2019s altar" sets out one of its seasonal things too, all through a festival of several days. A hidden calendar\u2019s festivals never do.'],keywords:['seasonal','sabbat','wheel of the year','samhain','yule','imbolc','ostara','beltane','litha','lammas','mabon','pumpkin','harvest','greek','hellenic','festival','pyanepsia','anthesteria','dionysia','eleusinian','noumenia','deipnon','hekate','dionysus','apollo','norse','heathen','bl\xf3t','odin','celtic','irish','brigid','lughnasadh','bealtaine','roman','saturnalia','parentalia','lupercalia','floralia','lemuria','vestalia','saturn','vesta','sol invictus','christian','folk','epiphany','candlemas','easter','pentecost','assumption','michaelmas','advent','christmas','holly','house blessing','slavic','marzanna','kupala','dziady','koliada','kutia','hindu','diwali','holi','navaratri','ganesh chaturthi','shivaratri','ganesha','lakshmi','shiva','kemetic','egyptian','epagomenal','wep ronpet','osiris','isis','season','snowdrops','autumn leaves']},{id:'altar-ancestor-frame',title:'Set a photo of an ancestor in a frame',summary:'A gilt or wooden frame with a photo of your own, and their name and dates.',steps:['Open the cabinet, choose Tools, and tap Ancestor Frame in the style you like.','With the frame selected, tap "Choose a photo" and pick one. It is cropped to fill the frame\u2019s opening.','Tap "Old sepia" to soften it to an old print, or again to show it as it is.','Tap "Add a name" to give their name and dates, or choose them from your Ancestors in Hedge. Tap "Save".','Tap "Look closer" to see the photo large, with "In memory of" and their dates beneath it.'],tips:['You can set as many frames on an altar as you like.','Signed in, the photo is kept with your account and shows on the website too. As a guest it stays on this device.','A frame named from your Ancestors shows their days and what they loved when it\u2019s selected.'],keywords:['photo frame','picture frame','ancestor photo','memorial','in memory','beloved dead','sepia','portrait']},{id:'altar-potted-plants',title:'Keep your houseplants on the altar',summary:'A pot for each of your real plants: its name, its water, its harvests and its journal.',steps:['Open the cabinet, choose Plants, and tap the plant you keep: snake plant, pothos, basil, rosemary, mint, lavender, sage or thyme. Set down as many as you have.','With it selected, tap "Name it" to give its name, where it lives, its light and how often you water it, and when it was last watered.','Choose Young, Established or Lush for the picture that matches your plant now. It doesn\u2019t grow on its own.','Tap "Watered" when you water it. As it runs past its day it droops and dulls a little; watered, it perks up. It never dies.','Tap "Add a photo" to keep a picture of the real plant with it.','For the herbs, tap "Harvest", say how much, and set a fresh sprig on the altar or keep it for a spell jar or sachet.','Tap "Add to its journal" for a feed, repotting, a new leaf, a cutting or a note. Each entry keeps that day\u2019s moon.'],tips:['Reminders \u2192 "Remind me when a plant would like water" sends a note on the day one comes due. It is off unless you turn it on.','Its notes say what it is kept for, and honestly whether it is safe around cats and dogs.','Signed in, the photo of your plant is kept with your account and shows on the website too. As a guest it stays on this device.'],keywords:['plant','plants','houseplant','pot','potted','water','watering','harvest','snake plant','pothos','basil','rosemary','mint','lavender','sage','thyme','green witchcraft']},{id:'altar-make-own-item',title:'Make your own cabinet item',summary:'Add something from your own shelf, with a photo.',steps:['Open the cabinet and choose a drawer.','Tap "Make your own".','Choose what it is, give it a name, and add a picture.','Link it to a Living Library entry if you like, then tap "Add to my cabinet".'],tips:['To change or delete one, tap "Edit" beside its name in the cabinet.'],keywords:['custom item','own object','photo','upload picture','personal item']},{id:'altar-own-picture',title:'Use your own picture for a cabinet item',summary:'Replace the painted picture of a built-in item with a photo of yours.',steps:['Sign in, then open the cabinet.','Press and hold the item or form you want to change.','Tap "Choose a picture" (or "Replace picture").','To go back, press and hold again and tap "Use the original".'],keywords:['custom image','replace image','photo of my candle']},{id:'altar-move-resize-rotate',title:'Move, resize and turn an object',summary:'Arrange things with your fingers, or with the buttons.',steps:['Tap an object on the altar to select it.','Drag it to move it. Pinch to resize it. Twist two fingers to turn it.','Or use the Arrange buttons: "Turn left", "Turn right", "Smaller" and "Larger".','Tap "Done" to deselect it.'],tips:['Tap "Undo" or "Redo" if you change your mind.'],keywords:['drag','pinch','rotate','size','bigger','smaller','position']},{id:'altar-flip',title:'Flip an object',summary:'Mirror an object left to right.',steps:['Tap an object on the altar to select it.','Under Arrange, tap "Flip".'],keywords:['mirror image','reverse','flip horizontally']},{id:'altar-lock',title:'Lock an object in place',summary:'A locked object can\u2019t be moved, turned or resized by accident.',steps:['Tap an object to select it.','Scroll to the "More" row and tap "Lock". It reads "Locked in place" at the top.','Tap "Unlock" in the same place to free it.'],keywords:['freeze','pin','fix position','unlock']},{id:'altar-layers',title:'Bring things forward or send them back',summary:'Decide what sits in front.',steps:['Select an object and, under "Layer", tap "To front", "Forward", "Backward" or "To back".','Or tap "Layers" with nothing selected to see the whole stack.','In that list, tap a name to select it, or use the arrows to reorder.'],keywords:['z-order','in front','behind','stack','order']},{id:'altar-group',title:'Group objects so they move together',summary:'Gather a working, a spell or a shrine into one group.',steps:['Tap "Select" (or press and hold something on the altar), tap each thing you want in the group, then tap "Group".','Or, with nothing selected, tap "Group" under Add and tick the things in the list.','Give the group a name, such as "Ritual Working", and tap the button that reads "Group 2 things" (or however many you picked).','Tap one member to see the rest of its group outlined. To split them up, tap "Ungroup" in its More row.'],tips:['Grouped things move, turn and resize together.','Choosing one member in Select mode chooses the whole group.'],keywords:['combine','select multiple','ungroup','shrine','cluster']},{id:'altar-select-several',title:'Choose several things at once',summary:'Move, group, layer or delete a handful of things in one go.',steps:['Tap "Select" in the row under the altar, or press and hold something on the altar.','Tap things to choose them; tap again to leave one out. "Choose all" takes everything.','Drag any chosen thing and they all move together, keeping their places to one another.','Use the panel to group them, bring them to the front or send them back, light or snuff the candles among them, lock them, or delete them.','Tap "Done" when you\u2019re finished.'],tips:['Deleting asks once, naming how many, and Undo puts them all back in one step.'],keywords:['multi select','multiple','select all','bulk','delete several','move several']},{id:'altar-cord-cutting',title:'Cord cutting on the altar',summary:'A cord tied between two candles burns through when they burn down to it.',steps:['Tap "Workings", then "Cord cutting". Or select a candle and tap "Tie a cord to another candle".','Choose how far down to tie it, the cord\u2019s colour, and, if you like, a line on what it stands for.','Choose two candles on the altar, or set out a fresh pair of chime candles with the cord already tied.','Light the candles. When either has burned down to the cord, it catches, burns along and parts, and the two ends fall.','Tap one of its candles to see the cord, change its height while it\u2019s tied, untie it, or record the cutting in your Grimoire once it\u2019s cut.'],tips:['The altar keeps count while the candles burn, even with the app closed. Snuff them and the cord waits.','With real candles, never leave them burning unattended, and keep the cord\u2019s ends away from anything that could catch.'],keywords:['cord','cutting','release','let go','ending','knot','tie']},{id:'altar-cast-circle',title:'Cast the circle and call the quarters',summary:'Trace a ring of light round the altar with an athame or wand, and light the four quarters.',steps:['Set an athame or a wand on the altar from the cabinet\u2019s Tools (the selenite athame and the crystal wand work too), and select it.','Tap "Cast the circle", choose the colour of the light (or type your own), and trace round the altar with the tool, sunwise (clockwise). A thin line of light follows it; once you\u2019ve gone most of the way round, it closes into a glowing ring and says "Circle cast". "Cast it for me" draws the ring without tracing.','Tap "Call the quarters" for the circle panel. Call East (air, yellow), South (fire, red), West (water, blue) and North (earth, green); each lights a marker at that edge of the altar. "Colour" changes a quarter\u2019s colour to your own.','In a coven ritual the planner can choose the order the quarters are called in (North first, say); the circle panel follows it, and release goes in reverse of it.','To close, release the quarters in reverse (North first), then tap "Release the circle" and trace the ring back anticlockwise, or tap "Release it for me".'],tips:['While anything is open, a line under the altar reminds you what\u2019s left to release before you end.','Casting, calling and releasing are kept in the altar\u2019s History. On a coven altar everyone there sees the ring and the quarters.','Casting a circle and calling the quarters is modern practice, mostly from Wicca and the ceremonial magic it drew on. The colours here are common modern ones, not the only ones; many traditions use others, or none.'],keywords:['circle','cast the circle','athame','wand','quarters','watchtowers','directions','elements','deosil','widdershins','open the circle','release the circle']},{id:'altar-singing-bowl',title:'Strike or ring the singing bowl',summary:'Strike it once, or let it ring every few minutes, in one of eight tones.',steps:['Set a singing bowl on the altar from the cabinet\u2019s Tools, and select it.','Choose its tone: one of the seven chakra notes (root C, sacral D, solar plexus E, heart F, throat G, third eye A, crown B) or 432 Hz.','Tap "Strike once", or choose how often (every 1 to 10 minutes) and tap "Ring every\u2026". Tap "Stop ringing" to let it fall still.'],tips:['The bowl follows Candle sounds and Vibration in Accessibility. As you struck it on purpose, it sounds even with an iPhone\u2019s silent switch on.','Pairing chakras with the notes of a C major scale is a modern Western convention, one of several, and 432 Hz is a modern preference, not an old tuning.','On a coven altar everyone there hears it.'],keywords:['singing bowl','bowl','sound','tone','chakra','432','meditation','strike','ring']},{id:'altar-chalice-besom',title:'The chalice and the besom',summary:'Fill, raise and pour from the chalice; sweep the altar clean with the besom.',steps:['Select a chalice and fill it with wine, water, juice or mead. The cup shows how full it is.','Tap "Raise it in a toast", "Pour a libation" (into an offering bowl on the altar if there is one, where it\u2019s kept as an offering) or "Drink", which empties it.','Select a besom and tap "Sweep the altar" to clear the incense ash, spent matches, the ash of burned petitions and burned cords.'],tips:['Each is kept in the altar\u2019s History. On a coven altar the others see the toast, the libation and the sweep.'],keywords:['chalice','cup','wine','mead','toast','libation','drink','besom','broom','sweep','clean','ash']},{id:'altar-light-by-hand',title:'Light with a match or lighter, or snuff a candle',summary:'Bring the matches, a lighter or a snuffer to a candle and tap the button that appears.',steps:['Set matches, a lighter or a candle snuffer on the altar from the cabinet\u2019s Tools (Candle care).','Drag it near or over an unlit candle or incense. A small "Light candle" button appears; tap it to light it, with the strike of a match or the click of a lighter.','Drag the snuffer to a lit candle and tap "Snuff candle". Move away and the button goes.'],tips:['Nothing is ever lit or put out on its own: only when you tap. A struck match is left beside the candle until you sweep the altar.'],keywords:['match','matches','lighter','snuffer','light candle','snuff','strike']},{id:'altar-pendulum',title:'Ask the pendulum',summary:'Show it once how it says yes, no and maybe, then ask your question and watch it swing.',steps:['Set a pendulum on the altar from the cabinet\u2019s Tools, and select it.','The first time, choose the swing for each answer: towards and away from you, side to side, or in a circle either way. "Use the usual ones" sets yes to and fro, no side to side and maybe clockwise. It\u2019s kept in your settings, so the website knows it too; "Change how it answers" sets it again.','Type your question, for a yes or no, and tap "Ask". The pendulum swings its answer.'],tips:['Each answer is kept in your readings (Craft, Divination) and in the altar\u2019s History, like any draw.','On the screen the swing is chosen at random. A real pendulum moves with tiny movements of your own hand that you don\u2019t notice making (the ideomotor effect), so take it as a way to hear what you already sense.'],keywords:['pendulum','dowsing','yes or no','calibrate','divination','ask']},{id:'altar-divination-answer',title:'The answer in the altar\u2019s corner, and your notes',summary:'After the pendulum, a draw from a deck, a scrying sit or a candle reading, the answer stays in the corner of the altar, with room for your notes.',steps:['Ask the pendulum, draw from a tarot deck, rune bag or ogham staves, scry, or read a candle after its burn. A small card in the altar\u2019s corner shows the answer: "Yes", the card and which way up it fell with a few keywords, the rune or stave, or "Scrying \xb7 10 min".','It stays until you tap \xd7 or do another divination. Tap \u2013 to fold it to a small chip, and tap the chip to open it again.','Tap "Add notes" to write what you make of it. The notes are kept on that reading (its "What you make of it"), so they show wherever your readings show; a candle\u2019s are kept with its reading, in its story. Tap "Your notes" to change them, or "Open reading" to see the whole reading.'],tips:['A scrying sit is kept in your readings as well as your journal, so its notes sit with your other divinations.','On a coven altar the card shows only to you when you draw for yourself. A card someone else lays on the coven altar shows to everyone there; notes you add to it start a reading of your own, which only you see.'],keywords:['result','answer','notes','reading','tarot','rune','ogham','scrying','pendulum','candle reading','divination']},{id:'altar-scrying-mirror',title:'Scry in a mirror, the cauldron or a crystal ball',summary:'The altar dims, the candlelight shows in the glass, a timer keeps the time, then a few words on what you saw.',steps:['Set a scrying mirror or crystal ball on the altar from the cabinet\u2019s Tools, select it and tap "Scry in the mirror". Light a candle first and its flame shows in the glass.','Or select a cauldron and tap "Fill it with water to scry", then sit with the dark water.','Choose 5, 10 or 15 minutes and tap Begin. When the time is up (or you tap "I\u2019m finished"), write what you saw, any symbols and how it felt.'],tips:['What you write goes to your ritual journal, and the sit is kept in the altar\u2019s History. The water bowl in Workings is the same sit with a bowl of water.'],keywords:['scrying','scry','mirror','black mirror','crystal ball','cauldron','gaze','visions']},{id:'altar-mortar',title:'Grind herbs in the mortar and pestle',summary:'Add herbs and resins, grind them into a loose blend, and place, burn, bag or keep it.',steps:['Set a mortar and pestle on the altar from the cabinet\u2019s Tools, and select it.','Add herbs, resins and incense from the altar or the cabinet (or type your own), then tap "Grind".','Choose what to do with the blend: set it on the altar as a herb mix, burn it as loose incense, bag it as a sachet, or "Save as an Apothecary recipe" to keep it in My Apothecary.'],tips:['What went in and what you did with it are kept in the altar\u2019s History. On a coven altar the others see it ground.'],keywords:['mortar','pestle','grind','herbs','resin','blend','loose incense','sachet','apothecary','recipe']},{id:'altar-bolline-cauldron',title:'The bolline and the cauldron',summary:'Cut a cord, harvest a sprig or carve a candle with the bolline; simmer, burn or scry in the cauldron.',steps:['Select a bolline: tap a tied cord to cut it by hand (the besom sweeps it later), "Harvest a sprig" to take one from a potted plant, or "Carve a candle" to carve a name or sigil into an unlit candle.','Select a cauldron: choose a few things for a simmer pot and tap "Start the simmer pot"; steam rises from it for about three hours, then it wants topping up. "Take it off" stops it.','"Burn a petition in it" opens the petition box to burn one. "Fill it with water to scry" begins a scrying sit.'],tips:['The bolline as the white-handled working knife, kept apart from the athame, comes from modern Wicca, after the Key of Solomon. Simmer pots are a modern kitchen-witch habit.','For real fire, keep a cauldron on a heatproof surface with sand or salt in the bottom, and never leave a simmer pot unattended.'],keywords:['bolline','boline','knife','cut','cord','harvest','carve','cauldron','simmer pot','steam','burn petition']},{id:'altar-crystal-charge-grid',title:'Charge a crystal by moon, sun or selenite, and make a grid',summary:'Set a stone to charge and watch its glow build; join stones into a grid with the wand.',steps:['Select a crystal and choose "Under the moon", "In the sun" or "On selenite". Its glow builds as it sits (about three hours, one hour or two). Tap "Take it up" and the charge is kept in its own charging history, with how it was charged.','The moon charges only at night, from your sunset to sunrise (set your place on The sky today; without one it goes by the clock, 18:00 to 06:00). It shows how full the moon is: the charge is stronger near the full moon. By day it says when moonlight returns. The sun charges only in daylight.','On selenite needs a piece of selenite on the altar, and the stone resting on it so they touch. With none there, tap "Place selenite from the cabinet" and a cluster is set under the stone.','If the stone holds an intention, a charge renews it; if not, it is a general charge. Add an intention, or change it, from the same panel at any time.','For a grid: tap Select, choose three or more crystals, and tap "Activate with the wand". Lines of light join them, round the outside and out from the middle stone. Or select a wand and tap "Activate every crystal here as a grid".','To end it, select a stone in the grid, or the wand, and tap "Let the grid rest".'],tips:['Some stones fade in strong sun (amethyst, rose quartz, fluorite and citrine among them). Charging by light and crystal grids are modern crystal practice.','On a coven altar the grid and each stone\u2019s glow are shared with everyone there.'],keywords:['crystal','charge','moon','sun','selenite','grid','crystal grid','wand','glow','intention','night','daylight','full moon']},{id:'altar-crystal-wear',title:'Crystal wear, and when something came at you',summary:'Stones dull, cloud and may crack with use; cleansing clears most of it. Off, Gentle or Realistic in Settings.',steps:['Choose how stones wear in Settings \u2192 Altar \u2192 Crystal wear: Off, Gentle (the usual: wear shows over months) or Realistic (over weeks).','A crystal takes on strain slowly while it sits on the altar uncleansed, and faster while it does protective work (an intention or spell of protection, warding, banishing or uncrossing, or a protective altar intention) or is held in a spell over days.','It shows on the stone: a duller sheen, then clouding, then a hairline crack. Its card says "Heavily used \u2014 it could do with a cleanse." Cleansing clears the strain of time and all but a fifth of the rest.','When something came at you, tap "Something came at me" (under Tend, or on a protective spell\u2019s card or stone). It is logged in the altar\u2019s History, and the stones doing protective work take the brunt; the most worn takes the most and may crack through.','Time alone never breaks a stone. When one breaks, its card asks what you would like to do: thank it and bury it, return it to the earth, keep the pieces (it keeps its cracked look), or cleanse it and keep it as chips. Nothing is taken away until you choose, and it is kept in the stone\u2019s history.'],tips:['The idea that a stone takes on what it guards against, and breaks when it has given all it can, is modern crystal folk belief rather than old tradition. Real stones do crack, often from heat, knocks or old flaws.','On a coven altar each stone\u2019s wear is kept with the stone, so everyone there sees it.'],keywords:['crystal wear','cracked crystal','broken crystal','cloudy','strain','something came at me','psychic attack','protection','warding','banishing','uncrossing','cleanse','bury','chips','gentle','realistic']},{id:'altar-draw-deck',title:'Draw from a deck, rune bag or ogham staves on the altar',summary:'Tap the deck where it sits to draw one; it\u2019s laid beside it and kept in your readings.',steps:['Set a tarot deck, rune bag or ogham staves on the altar from the cabinet\u2019s Tools, and select it.','Type a question if you have one, and tap "Draw a card" (or rune, or stave). It\u2019s drawn as in Divination, laid on the altar beside the deck, and kept in your readings.'],tips:['The tarot draws from your chosen deck, with reversals if you\u2019ve turned them on in Divination settings.'],keywords:['tarot','deck','card','rune','rune bag','ogham','staves','draw','reading']},{id:'altar-ritual-mode',title:'Ritual mode',summary:'Dim everything around the altar, keep one small bar, and soften the sounds while you work.',steps:['Tap "Ritual mode" in the altar\u2019s toolbar. The room goes dark round the altar and the tools step back.','Tap anything on the altar, then "Tools", to use it; "Hide tools" puts them away again.','Tap "Leave ritual mode" when you\u2019re done. Leaving the altar ends it too.'],tips:['Candle sounds, the bell and the singing bowl play more softly while it\u2019s on.'],keywords:['ritual mode','focus','dim','quiet','minimal','distraction']},{id:'altar-glow-duplicate-rename-remove',title:'Glow, duplicate, rename or remove an object',summary:'The More row holds the everyday editing tools.',steps:['Select an object, then scroll to the "More" row.','Tap "Glow" for a soft glow, "Duplicate" for another one, or "Rename" to change its label on this altar.','To take it off, tap "Remove", then "Remove from altar" to confirm.'],tips:['Renaming only changes that object on this altar. Its Living Library entry keeps its name.'],keywords:['delete object','copy object','label','name object','glowing']},{id:'altar-undo-redo-zoom',title:'Undo, redo and zoom',summary:'Step back, step forward and look closely.',steps:['With nothing selected, find the row of tools under the altar.','Tap "Undo" or "Redo" to step through your changes.','Tap "Zoom in" to get closer and "Zoom out" to return. When zoomed, drag an empty spot to look around.'],keywords:['magnify','step back','revert']},{id:'altar-full-screen',title:'Turn the altar sideways to fill the screen',summary:'Work on a bigger stage.',steps:['With nothing selected, tap "Full screen".','Use "Cabinet", "Tools" or "Show details" along the top to keep working.','Tap "Save" (it reads "Saved" when up to date) to keep your changes.','Tap "Done" to leave full screen.'],keywords:['landscape','rotate','big view','sideways']},{id:'altar-background',title:'Change the altar\u2019s background',summary:'Set the scene behind your altar.',steps:['With nothing selected, tap "Background".','Tap a scene under "Set the scene".','To use your own, sign in, type a name, and tap "Choose a picture".'],tips:['Backgrounds you upload are kept in your account and appear on the website too.'],keywords:['scene','wallpaper','backdrop','upload background','custom background']},{id:'altar-default-background',title:'Choose the default background for new altars',summary:'A new altar starts on this scene.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then Altar.','Under "Default altar background", tap a scene, or "No default".','Each change saves itself.'],href:'/more/settings/altar',keywords:['default scene','new altar background']},{id:'altar-sky-season',title:'Let the altar follow the real sky',summary:'Show the real light of day and tonight\u2019s moon on your altar.',steps:['With nothing selected, tap "Sky & season".','Switch on "The real sky" so the light follows your sunrise, sunset and the season.','Switch on "Tonight\u2019s moon" for a small window showing the moon\u2019s real phase.','Switch on "Charge under the New Moon too" to count New Moons for charging.'],tips:['Save the altar to keep these choices with it. Set your place on the sky screen for your real sunrise and sunset.'],keywords:['moon window','ambient light','daylight','time of day','real sky']},{id:'altar-light-snuff',title:'Light and snuff a candle',summary:'A lit candle burns in real time.',steps:['Tap a candle on the altar to select it.','Tap "Light the candle". The label above it reads "Burning".','To put it out, tap "Snuff the candle".','To light or snuff every candle at once, tap "Light all candles" or "Snuff all" when nothing is selected.'],tips:['Lighting a candle also counts as tending today\u2019s step of a spell you are working with it.'],keywords:['flame','burn','extinguish','light all','put out']},{id:'altar-burn-time',title:'See how long a candle has burned and set its length',summary:'Candles burn for a realistic time, then go out on their own.',steps:['Select a candle. A line shows "Burning time", how long it has burned, and about how long is left.','Before you first light it, tap "How long it burns".','Choose a length, from ten minutes to nine days, if your candle is bigger or smaller than usual.','When a candle burns down it goes out on its own and a notice tells you.'],keywords:['burn duration','time left','timer','candle life','burned down']},{id:'altar-fresh-candle',title:'Put a fresh candle in place of a spent one',summary:'A burned-down candle keeps its history; a new one takes its place.',steps:['Tap the spent candle. It reads "Burned all the way down".','Tap "Put a fresh candle here".','Light the new candle with "Light the candle".'],tips:['The old candle\u2019s burns stay in its story.'],keywords:['replace candle','new candle','spent','burned out','renew']},{id:'altar-dress-anoint',title:'Dress a candle with oil or herbs',summary:'Anoint a candle with an oil and roll it in herbs, and see them on the wax.',steps:['Select a candle.','Tap "Dress & anoint".','Choose an oil, or type your own blend, then search and pick herbs to roll it in.','Choose which way: the buttons set the direction you work.','Tap "Dress the candle".'],tips:['Read "Together" on that sheet for what your chosen oil and herbs mean as a blend.'],keywords:['anoint','oil','dressing','herbs on candle','rolling','dress candle']},{id:'altar-dress-from-altar',title:'Dress a candle from what is on the altar',summary:'Use a loose herb or oil already sitting on your altar.',steps:['Place a loose herb or an oil on the altar first.','Select the candle and tap "Dress from the altar".','Tap the herb or oil you want.'],tips:['If nothing on the altar can dress a candle, the sheet says to place a loose herb or an oil first.'],keywords:['dress candle with herb on altar','loose herb']},{id:'altar-undress',title:'Remove a candle\u2019s dressings',summary:'Take the oil and herbs off the wax.',steps:['Select a dressed candle.','Tap "Undress".'],keywords:['clean candle','remove herbs','remove oil']},{id:'altar-carve',title:'Carve a word into a candle',summary:'Carve a name, word, date or sigil\u2019s name into the wax.',steps:['Select a candle and tap "Carve".','Type a short word, such as "Abundance".','Tap "Carve".','Or, under "Or carve a sigil", tap one of the sigils you kept, or "Make a sigil".','To smooth one away, tap that carving in the list "Carved into it".'],tips:['A carving melts away from the top as the candle burns.'],keywords:['engrave','inscribe','write on candle','sigil','name on candle']},{id:'altar-look-closer',title:'Look closer at an object',summary:'See an object large, with every mark on it.',steps:['Select an object.','Tap "Look closer".','Read the lines beneath for how it burned, melted, aged or charged, and what it carries.'],keywords:['close up','zoom object','detail','wax melt','inspect']},{id:'altar-read-candle',title:'Read how a candle burned',summary:'Record the flame, the smoke and the wax while they are fresh in your mind.',steps:['When a candle has finished burning, select it and tap "Read the candle". Later you can tap "How it burned".','Tick what you noticed about the flame, smoke and wax, and add notes if you like.','Tap "Keep this reading", or "Save to my journal" to add it to your ritual journal too.','If wax is left, choose "Keep it", "Bury it" or "Bin it" under the remnant.'],keywords:['ceromancy','flame reading','candle divination','remnant','wax reading']},{id:'altar-its-story',title:'Read an object\u2019s story',summary:'Everything that happens to an object is kept as its story.',steps:['Select an object.','Scroll to "Its story" to see dated lines: lit, dressed, charged, offered and more.','Tap "Show all" to see every line.','Tap "About" for its History and its Living Library information.'],keywords:['history of object','log','timeline']},{id:'altar-incense',title:'Light incense and choose its kind',summary:'Incense burns down to ash like a candle burns down to wax.',steps:['Select an incense object.','Tap "Light the incense". Tap "Put it out" to stop it, or "Clear the ash" once it has burned down.','To change its form, tap "Stick, cone or resin".','Choose Stick, Cone or Resin on charcoal, and how long it burns.'],keywords:['smoke','stick','cone','resin','ash','frankincense','cleansing smoke']},{id:'altar-offerings-vessel',title:'Set out an offering in a bowl or dish',summary:'Offerings freshen and fade over real time.',steps:['Place a bowl, dish or other vessel on the altar and select it.','Tap "Set out an offering".','Choose what it is, such as Water, Fruit, Bread or Cut flowers, and optionally type exactly what.','Tap "Set it out".','Later tap "Refresh" to set it out fresh, "Leave it be" to let it age without asking, "Return to nature", or "Remove" to empty the vessel.'],tips:['Fresh offerings age on the altar. A note says when one is ready to be refreshed.','Fruit, bread, sweets, a meal, flowers or honey in the comb are drawn heaped in the bowl, dish, chalice or cauldron, and go over there: bread dries, fruit browns, a meal spoils, flowers wilt and drop their petals.','For one tap, open the cabinet\u2019s Offerings drawer: bread, fruit, sweets, a meal, cut flowers and honeycomb to set straight on the altar, and a bowl of water, a chalice of wine, a dish of milk or honey already poured. Each is fresh as you place it and goes over from then.'],keywords:['food offering','libation','milk and honey','wine','flowers','fresh','wilts','fruit bowl','honeycomb','offerings drawer']},{id:'altar-offerings-drawer',title:'Set out food, flowers and drink from the Offerings drawer',summary:'Offerings ready to place, that freshen and fade in real time.',steps:['Open the cabinet and choose the Offerings drawer.','Tap one to place it: bread, fruit, sweets, a meal, cut flowers or honeycomb on their own, or a Bowl of Water, a Chalice of Wine, a Dish of Milk, a Honey Dish, a Bowl of Fruit or a Dish of Bread already filled.','It is fresh as you place it and goes over from then: bread dries, fruit browns, a meal spoils, flowers wilt and drop their petals.','Select it to tend it: "Refresh", "Leave it be", "Return to nature" or "Remove".'],tips:['Reminders \u2192 "Remind me when an offering wants tending" sends one gentle note on a day something on your altars goes over. Offerings you chose to leave be won\u2019t ask.'],keywords:['offerings','offering drawer','food','bread','fruit','flowers','wine','milk','honey','water','libation','goes off','ages','wilts']},{id:'altar-deity-offering',title:'Make an offering to a deity',summary:'Record what you offer, and tend it afterwards.',steps:['Place a deity statue and select it.','Tap "Offering", then "Record a new offering".','Choose the types and what you offer, add an intention and a prayer if you like.','Tap "Make the offering" for a short guided moment, or "Just record it".','Later, tap "Refresh", "Return to nature" or "Remove" on the offering line.'],tips:['Tap "Reason for presence" to record why this deity is on your altar.'],keywords:['devotion','god','goddess','statue','prayer','gift to deity']},{id:'altar-petitions',title:'Write a petition and keep a petition box',summary:'Fold your words under a candle or keep them in the box, and release them on a good night.',steps:['Save the altar first. With nothing selected, tap "Petitions".','Tap "Write a petition", give it a name and your words.','Choose the timing, and "In the petition box" or "Under" one of your candles.','Tap "Place the petition".','Later open "Petitions" and tap "Burn", "Bury", "Release on a night" or "Release now".'],keywords:['wish paper','prayer paper','burn bowl','bury petition','release night','dark moon']},{id:'altar-crystal-care',title:'Cleanse, charge or dedicate a crystal',summary:'Log how you care for a stone, and play the moment on the altar.',steps:['Select a crystal.','Tap "Cleanse" or "Charge", choose which crystals, then tap "Continue".','Pick a reason, the methods and any supports, then tap "Complete cleansing" or "Complete charge".','To dedicate it, tap "Dedicate", choose a type and who it is for, then tap "Save dedication".'],keywords:['cleansing','charging','dedication','program stone','smoke cleanse','moonlight']},{id:'altar-moon-charging',title:'Charge crystals and moon water under the moon',summary:'Things left on a saved altar through a Full Moon are charged under it.',steps:['Place crystals or a bowl of water on a saved altar.','Leave them there through a Full Moon.','Select the crystal later: a line says "Charged under the" moon, with the date.','To count New Moons as well, open "Sky & season" and switch on "Charge under the New Moon too".'],keywords:['moon water','full moon charge','new moon charge','lunar charging']},{id:'altar-about-sheet',title:'Learn what an object means',summary:'The About sheet shows its Living Library information.',steps:['Select an object and tap "About".','Read what is On this altar, its History, and your My Practice and Traditional Information.','Tap "Open in Living Library" for the whole entry, or "Edit My Practice" to add your own notes.'],tips:['Choose what this sheet shows in Settings \u2192 Altar \u2192 About sheet.'],keywords:['correspondences','meaning','companion','information']},{id:'altar-tonights-altar',title:'Understand tonight\u2019s altar and swap pieces',summary:'Tonight\u2019s altar tells you why each piece is there.',steps:['Start from Today with "Set tonight\u2019s altar".','Select a piece to read "Why it\u2019s here tonight".','Tap "Swap it" to choose something with the same correspondence.','Tap "Why these pieces" for every piece at once, then "Save" to keep it.'],tips:['On a festival night from any calendar you keep or show, the festival\u2019s seasonal thing says which festival it is set out for, Diwali or Wep Ronpet as much as Samhain.'],keywords:['starter altar','daily altar','swap','suggested pieces','festival']},{id:'altar-widget',title:'Put an altar on your home screen',summary:'Light candles, tend offerings and cleanse crystals from your home screen.',steps:['Save the altar first, then with nothing selected tap "Home screen".','Choose its place: "Altar 1", "Altar 2" and so on. Tap "Let the app choose" to use the most recent.','Press and hold an empty spot on your home screen, add a Salt & Sovereignty widget and choose Altar.','On the widget, tap its buttons. What you do there is carried onto the altar the next time the app opens.'],tips:['The sheet shows a "Widget status" line so you can check the widget was updated.','A coven altar can go on the widget too: open it from your coven, tap "Home screen" and choose its place. What you tend there everyone in the coven sees. While a ritual is under way there, or you can\u2019t tend it, the widget shows it without buttons.'],keywords:['widget','lock screen','home screen','android widget','ios widget','coven altar']},{id:'altar-widget-cleansing',title:'Set a crystal\u2019s or deity\u2019s widget action',summary:'Choose what the home screen widget does for a crystal or a deity.',steps:['Select a crystal and tap "Widget cleansing", or a deity and tap "Widget offering".','Choose the reason, methods and supports, or the offering types and what you offer.','Tap "Save widget offering" (or save the cleansing).','Save the altar to use it on your home screen. Tap "Clear it" to remove it.'],keywords:['widget crystal','widget deity','one tap cleanse']},{id:'altar-apothecary',title:'Make something new in your Apothecary',summary:'Record a jar, oil, sachet or other working as a recipe you can place on the altar.',steps:['With nothing selected, tap "Apothecary".','Tap "Make something new".','Choose what you are making, name it, and add ingredients from the altar, cabinet, Library or your apothecary.','Add an intention, notes, and choose tending reminders if you want them.','Under "Did it work? Look back", keep the day that suits its intention or choose another.','Tap "Save to your Apothecary and place it".'],tips:['In the Apothecary list, tap "Place" to put one on the altar or "Recipe" to open its recipe.','On its look-back day you\u2019re asked whether it worked: on Today, in the journal under "Apothecary: jars & sachets", and with a reminder if look-back reminders are on. Answers count in What works for you.','A herb mix or tending blend stands in a labelled glass jar, an oil in a labelled dropper bottle, and a water (a name with "water" in it) in a labelled bottle. Under "Its label" write what it says (its name until you do) and choose the label and writing; the words show on the jar on the altar, small enough to read when you zoom in.'],keywords:['recipe','oil','tincture','blend','label','jar label','bottle label','potion','crafted item','workshop','did it work','look back','spell jar','sachet']},{id:'altar-tending-status',title:'Track tending, activation and review dates for a crafted item',summary:'Crafted items remind you when they need feeding or replacing.',steps:['Select a crafted object on the altar and tap "Status".','Tap "I tended it today" to reset the next tending date.','Under "Review or replace by", tap "In a month", "In 3 months", "In 6 months" or "None".','Type how it was activated or the amount remaining, then tap "Save".'],tips:['Tap "Begin Practice" (when it appears) to record today\u2019s tending, or a charge, ritual or journal note.'],keywords:['feed','remaining','expires','review date','tend schedule','activation']},{id:'altar-spell-jar',title:'Build a spell jar',summary:'Build a jar in layers, a word spoken with each, and seal it with wax.',steps:['With nothing selected, tap "Workings", then "Spell jar".','Choose what it is for and the glass (a clear jar or a green bottle), then tap "Begin the layers".','Add each layer from the herbs, salts and stones, and roll in a petition if you like. Each layer shows in the jar, bottom first.','Tap "Seal it", choose the wax colour (or drip it from a lit candle), then "Place on the altar". The jar shows its layers and seal on the altar.','When it would like a shake, it appears in To tend. Select the jar and tap "Shake to renew".'],keywords:['jar spell','witch jar','protection jar','shake jar','layers','petition','wax seal','to tend']},{id:'altar-sachet',title:'Make a sachet or charm bag',summary:'Fill it, tie it with knots, and carry it or keep it on the altar.',steps:['Tap "Workings", then "Sachet or charm bag".','Fill the bag and choose "Carry it with me" or "Keep it on the altar".','Tap "Tie it and place it".','Later, select it and tap "Feed it" when it is due.'],keywords:['charm bag','gris-gris','mojo','pouch','amulet']},{id:'altar-spell-over-days',title:'Keep a spell over days',summary:'A seven-day candle, nine nights or a moon\u2019s jar: the altar keeps count.',steps:['Save the altar. Tap "Workings", then "Spell over days". Or select an object and tap "Spell over days".','Tap "Start a spell" and set it up.','Each day, tap "Tended today" on the spell, or light its candle.','To finish, tap "Close the spell", or "End it early".'],keywords:['nine night','seven day candle','timer','multi-day spell','novena']},{id:'altar-scrying',title:'Scry with a bowl of water',summary:'A quiet timed sit, then a few words on what came.',steps:['Save the altar. Tap "Workings", then "Scrying bowl".','Choose how many minutes, then tap "Begin".','Sit quietly. Tap "I\u2019m finished" if you want to stop early.','Write a few words and tap "Save to my journal", or close it to keep it with the altar.'],keywords:['water scrying','divination','dark mirror','bowl']},{id:'altar-gratitude-bowl',title:'Fill a gratitude bowl',summary:'A bead for each thing you are thankful for, filling through the moon.',steps:['Save the altar. Tap "Workings", then "Gratitude bowl".','Type what you are grateful for and choose a bead.','Tap "Drop it in the bowl".','Tap "Earlier moons" to see past bowls.'],keywords:['thankful','thanks','beads','gratitude jar']},{id:'altar-begin-ritual-here',title:'Begin a ritual on an altar',summary:'Run a ritual with its steps over the altar, lighting candles as steps begin.',steps:['Save the altar. Tap "Workings", then "Begin a ritual here".','Choose "From the book" or "Your templates", then pick one.','Tap the button that reads "Begin on" and your altar\u2019s name.','The ritual runs over the altar. Tap "Carry on at the altar" from the ritual screen to come back to it.'],tips:['You can also choose "Begin on an altar" on any template or premade ritual.'],keywords:['ritual on altar','altar ritual','run ritual altar','candles follow steps']},{id:'altar-from-practice',title:'Bring an ancestor, stone, plant or card to the altar',summary:'Place things from your practice tools straight onto the altar.',steps:['With nothing selected, tap "Workings".','Under "From your practice", tap "Ancestor", "My stone", "My plant" or "Tonight\u2019s card or rune".','Choose the person, stone, plant or reading.','Tap the button to place it.'],tips:['An ancestor candle can be lit from the altar with "Light a candle for them".'],keywords:['ancestor candle','my stone','my plant','card on altar','rune','memorial']},{id:'altar-read-intention',title:'Read your altar and set its intention',summary:'See what an altar speaks of, and say what it is for.',steps:['With nothing selected, tap "Read & arrange".','Tap "Read this altar" for its elements, planets and one thing to round it out.','Tap "Intention" and type a few words on what the altar is for, then tap "Set it".','Tap a suggestion to place it on the altar.'],tips:['The intention is kept with the altar, so save the altar first.'],keywords:['altar reading','elements balance','purpose','what is my altar for']},{id:'altar-layouts-snap',title:'Arrange an altar by meaning',summary:'Lay it out as the four directions, a triangle, a pentacle and more.',steps:['Tap "Read & arrange", then "Layouts with meaning". Or select an object and tap "Layouts".','Choose a layout, such as the four directions or God and Goddess.','Tap the button that reads "Arrange as" and the layout\u2019s name. Undo puts it back.','To have things settle onto directions as you drag, switch on "Snap to meaning".'],tips:['Select an object with a twin and tap "Mirror its pair" to mirror them across the altar.'],keywords:['pentacle','quarters','directions','compass','sacred geometry','snap']},{id:'altar-history',title:'Look back at an altar\u2019s history',summary:'A picture of the altar is kept each day it changes.',steps:['Save the altar. With nothing selected, tap "History".','Tap a date to see how the altar looked.','Scroll the list to see what happened on it, with the day and time.'],keywords:['past altar','snapshots','timeline','how it looked']},{id:'altar-share',title:'Share a picture of your altar',summary:'A card of your altar, made on your phone and not uploaded.',steps:['With at least one object on the altar, tap "Share".','Look at the card.','Tap "Share the picture" and choose where to send it.'],tips:['The picture stays private until you choose where to send it.'],keywords:['screenshot','export image','post altar','social']},{id:'share-as-card',title:'Share or print a ritual, spell, Library entry or reading as a card',summary:'A styled picture to send or save, a page to print, or the words to share.',steps:['Open a ritual template, a working from the workings library, a spell in the builder, a Living Library entry or one of your readings.','Tap "Share as card" and look at the card.','Tap "Share the picture" (on the web, "Download the picture"), "Print" on the web, or "Share the words".'],tips:['The card is made on your device and goes only where you send it. On a phone, the share sheet\u2019s Print prints the words.'],keywords:['share card','print','printable','picture','image','social','export']},{id:'altar-record-grimoire',title:'Record an altar or group in your Grimoire',summary:'Turn what you set up into a page in your Grimoire.',steps:['Sign in, then with nothing selected tap "Record in Grimoire". To record a group, select one of its objects and tap "Send group to Grimoire".','Name the working and choose its type.','Fill in as much as you like, such as intention, moon phase, words spoken and results.','Tap "Create Page". The new page opens in the editor.'],keywords:['save to book of shadows','spell record','log altar','write up']},{id:'altar-link-page',title:'Link an object to a page in your Grimoire',summary:'Open a page from an object with one tap.',steps:['Select an object.','Tap "Link a page".','Choose the page. Tap "Change" later to pick another.','Tap "Open the page" to read it.'],keywords:['attach page','grimoire link','connect page']},{id:'altar-clear-delete',title:'Clear or delete an altar',summary:'Empty an altar, or remove it for good.',steps:['With nothing selected, scroll to the bottom of the altar tools.','To empty it, tap "Clear altar", then "Take everything off". Tap "Keep it" to cancel.','To set a saved altar aside, tap "Archive altar" here, or "Archive" under it in your list of altars. It keeps everything and moves to "Archived altars" at the bottom of the list, resting from reminders and the To tend list until you tap "Restore".','To remove a saved altar entirely, tap "Delete altar", then "Delete this altar for good". Your Grimoire pages made from it stay in your Grimoire.'],tips:['Clearing can be undone with "Undo" before you leave. Deleting cannot.'],keywords:['remove altar','start over','empty','erase','archive','restore','hide altar']}]},{id:'grimoire',title:'Grimoire',intro:'Your Grimoire: pages you write, your dreams, and the Living Library as a section of it.',topics:[{id:'grimoire-open-book',title:'Open your Grimoire',summary:'Practice \u2192 Grimoire holds the book you keep on the website.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Grimoire.','If you see "Sign in", tap it. The Grimoire needs a Salt & Sovereignty account.','Your pages are listed under "Pages", grouped by section.','Tap a page to read it.'],tips:['Open your book once while online. After that you can read it offline.'],href:'/grimoire',keywords:['book of shadows','bos','grimoire','pages','journal book']},{id:'grimoire-mundane-mode',title:'Switch to plain, everyday language',summary:'Mundane mode shows your book in everyday words.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Grimoire, or any page.','Switch on "Mundane" at the top right.','The Mundane switch is one choice, kept with your settings, so it is the same on every device. It is also in More \u2192 Settings \u2192 Grimoire.'],href:'/more/settings/book',keywords:['plain language','discreet','hidden','non-magical words','privacy mode']},{id:'grimoire-read-page',title:'Read a page',summary:'A page shows its type, title, date, moon phase and what was on the altar.',steps:['In Practice \u2192 Grimoire, tap a page under "Pages".','Read the title block, then "On the altar" if the page records a working.','Scroll for its text, and "Linked pages" at the end. Tap a linked page to open it.'],keywords:['view page','open page','linked pages']},{id:'grimoire-edit-page',title:'Edit a page',summary:'Write on a page. Changes save as you go.',steps:['Open a page and tap "Edit".','Change the title at the top, or tap in a block to write.','Tap "\u2726 Add page element" to add more (see the next topic).','Tap "Done" when you have finished.'],tips:['A small status at the top shows that your page is saving.'],keywords:['write','edit grimoire','rename page','type']},{id:'grimoire-add-elements',title:'Add paragraphs, lists, images and more to a page',summary:'Pages are made of blocks you can add, move and remove.',steps:['Open a page, tap "Edit", then "\u2726 Add page element".','Choose from Writing (Paragraph, Heading, Note / Quote), Structure (Divider, Checklist, Bulleted List, Numbered List), Magical (Ingredient List, Correspondence) or Media & Links (Image, Page Link).','To reorder, tap "Move up" or "Move down" on a block. To delete one, tap "Remove".'],keywords:['blocks','heading','checklist','image','list','callout','divider','reorder']},{id:'grimoire-format-text',title:'Make text bold or italic, or add a link',summary:'Use the small toolbar when you are writing in a text block.',steps:['Tap into a paragraph while editing a page.','Use the toolbar above the text: "Bold", "Italic" or "Underline".','To add a web link, tap "Add a link", type the address, and tap "Add link".'],keywords:['formatting','underline','hyperlink','rich text']},{id:'grimoire-add-template',title:'Add a template to a page',summary:'Start a herb entry, a dream journal, a ritual or another set of sections.',steps:['Open a page, tap "Edit", then "Add a template".','Choose one, such as Herb Entry, Crystal Entry, Deity Entry, Dream Journal, Spell or Working, Ritual, Tarot Reading or Moon Journal.','Confirm "Add template". Its sections are added to the end; nothing is removed.'],keywords:['page template','herb entry','dream journal template','tarot reading template','moon journal']},{id:'grimoire-link-pages',title:'Link pages that belong together',summary:'Link a herb page to the ritual that uses it.',steps:['Open a page and tap "Edit".','Scroll to "Linked pages" and tap "Link a page".','Choose a page. To undo it, tap "Unlink".'],keywords:['connect pages','cross reference','backlinks']},{id:'grimoire-delete-page',title:'Delete a page',summary:'Return a page to ashes.',steps:['Open a page and tap "Edit".','Scroll to the bottom and tap "Return page to ashes".','Confirm "Return to ashes". This cannot be undone.'],keywords:['remove page','erase page','trash']},{id:'grimoire-new-pages',title:'Know where new pages come from',summary:'In the app, new pages are made from your workings; the rest come from the website.',steps:['To make a page from an altar, tap "Record in Grimoire" on the altar screen.','Saving a spell or ritual as a template also puts it in your book.','A sigil you give a page, and the page of a moon or holy day you open from Today, are added too.','Pages you make on the website appear here when you pull down to refresh.'],tips:['You can add to any page with "Edit".'],keywords:['create page','new page','how do i add a page']},{id:'grimoire-shelves',title:'Browse My Practice and Traditional entries in the Grimoire',summary:'Practice \u2192 Grimoire also shelves your Living Library: My Practice, Dreams and Traditional Information.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Grimoire and look above "Pages".','Type in "Search your Grimoire" to filter.','Tap a shelf such as My Practice, a section, then a group to open it.','Tap an entry to read it. Tap "Back to your Grimoire" to return.'],keywords:['library shelves','my practice shelf','traditional information','herbs shelf']},{id:'practice-dream-journal',title:'Keep a dream journal',summary:'Write dreams down, with the moon they came under.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Grimoire and open the Dreams shelf, then "Open Dreams" (or Practice \u2192 Craft, then Hedge, then "Dream journal").','Tap "Write down a dream".','Type the dream and a title, choose "Which morning?", and add symbols and feelings.','Optionally mark it Lucid or Recurring, then tap "Keep this dream".'],tips:['Tap "Symbols and moons" to see what keeps returning and the phases your dreams cluster in.','Turn on "Last night\u2019s dream" under Remind me for a gentle morning nudge. In the morning, Today also offers a place to catch a line or two.','To hide the Dreams shelf, switch off "Show Dreams" in More, then Settings, then "Grimoire".'],href:'/grimoire/dreams',keywords:['dreams','dreamwork','symbols','lucid','recurring dream']},{id:'journals-overview',title:'Keep a shadow, deity, ancestor or omen journal',summary:'Four private journals for the inner work of the craft, each kept with your account like your dreams.',steps:['Open Journal (Practice \u2192 Rituals \u2192 Journal, the Grimoire, or More \u2192 Journal): every journal is there, newest first; tap a kind to see only it, or "New entry" to write one.','Choose Shadow work, Deity & spirit, Ancestors or Omens & signs.','Tap the write button at the top, or "Write to this prompt" for a gentle prompt.','Fill in what you like, add tags, and link a Grimoire page or a dream if it belongs with one. The moon at the time is noted for you.','Tap "Keep this". Search and tags at the top of each journal find it again.'],tips:['Each journal can be a section of your Grimoire, after Dreams, or a journal of its own under Rituals \u2192 Journal. Choose under "Where this journal lives" at the foot of the journal, or in More, then Settings, then "Grimoire". Moving it keeps every entry.','A Grimoire page or a dream shows the journal entries that link to it, under "In your journals".','Today offers a journal prompt now and then: a sign to look back on, a day for the dead, a holy day of one of your deities, or the waning and dark moon.'],href:'/grimoire/journals',keywords:['journal','shadow work','deity journal','devotional journal','ancestor journal','omens','signs','book of shadows']},{id:'journals-shadow',title:'Do gentle shadow work',summary:'Prompts for noticing triggers and patterns, with the moon and its Cycle & Moon season noted as you write.',steps:['Open Journals, then Shadow work.','Read the note at the top: this is reflective journalling, not therapy, and support lines are a tap away.','Tap "Write to this prompt", or choose another under "Choose a prompt" in the form.','Write what came up, what set it off, whether you have met it before, and what you would like to do with it. Leave anything blank.'],tips:['On the waning and dark moon the prompts turn to letting go and to what you have been avoiding. Cycle & Moon has a door to this journal too.','Stop whenever you need to. The Support page lists people to talk to.'],href:'/grimoire/journals',keywords:['shadow','shadow work','triggers','patterns','integration','jung','dark moon','therapy']},{id:'journals-deity',title:'Keep a journal with a god or spirit',summary:'Log offerings, prayers, devotional acts and signs for each deity you honour.',steps:['Open Journals, then Deity & spirit, and tap "Write in your deity journal".','Choose from your own deities (More, then Settings, then "My deities") or the Living Library, or type a name in your own words.','Choose what it was: an offering, a prayer, a devotional act, a sign or a reflection, and for offerings, what you gave and how it was received.','Keep it. The journal groups your entries by god or spirit.'],tips:['A deity\u2019s Library page shows your journal with them, and an entry links to their dedication journey and how far you are on it.','On the altar, choose a deity and tap "Deity journal".'],href:'/grimoire/journals',keywords:['deity','devotion','offerings','prayer','patron','signs','dedication']},{id:'journals-ancestors',title:'Keep an ancestor journal',summary:'Offerings, dreams of them, family recipes and stories, visits and family history, about the people you keep in Hedge \u2192 Ancestors.',steps:['Add your people in Hedge \u2192 Ancestors, with their dates and where they were born and died.','Open Journals, then Ancestors, and tap "Write in your ancestor journal".','Choose what it is about and who, then write.'],tips:['A photo set in an ancestor frame on your altar, named for them, shows beside their name.','Samhain and the other days for the dead, and Hekate\u2019s Deipnon, link here, and so does an ancestor frame or memorial candle on your altar ("Write about them").'],href:'/grimoire/journals',keywords:['ancestors','beloved dead','family recipes','genealogy','samhain','deipnon','family history']},{id:'ancestor-profiles',title:'Keep a page for each of your ancestors',summary:'Their name, who they are to you, dates and places, a photo, stories, the foods and offerings they liked, and the days you keep for them.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft \u2192 Hedge \u2192 Ancestors and tap "Add someone", or open a person and tap "Edit".','Add what you know. Under "Other days you keep for them", write one day to a line, such as "24 June Name day".','Tap "Add a photo" to choose one, then save.','To be reminded of their days, open Settings \u2192 Reminders \u2192 Your ancestors\u2019 days and turn it on.'],tips:['Their days in the coming week show on Today.','Name an ancestor frame on your altar from them (Tools in the cabinet, Ancestor Frame, "Add a name") to link the two.','Their page opens your ancestor journal entries about them.'],href:'/rituals/craft/hedge/ancestors',keywords:['ancestor profile','family tree','death anniversary','name day','feast day','memorial','beloved dead']},{id:'journals-omens',title:'Note an omen or sign, and look back later',summary:'What you saw, where, the moon and planetary hour at the time, what it might mean, and whether it came to pass.',steps:['Open Journals, then Omens & signs, and tap "Note a sign".','Choose the kind of sign, write what you saw and where, and what it might mean.','Choose when to look back: in a week, a moon, or three months.','When the day comes, Today asks "Did it come to pass?". Open the sign and choose how it turned out.'],tips:['The planetary hour is noted when your place is set on The sky today.','A sign\u2019s page offers dream-symbol notes and Living Library entries that match what you saw, as places to start.'],href:'/grimoire/journals',keywords:['omens','signs','synchronicity','animal','numbers','divination','planetary hour']},{id:'practice-dream-symbols',title:'Look up common dream symbols',summary:'Associations to start from; yours matter most.',steps:['Open Dreams in the Grimoire and tap "Dream symbols" ("Symbols and moons" once you have a few dreams).','Open a symbol to read its notes and a question to ask yourself.','See "What keeps returning" for your own repeated symbols.'],href:'/grimoire/dreams/symbols',keywords:['dream dictionary','dream meaning']},{id:'grimoire-divination-pages',title:'Read about every tarot card, rune, ogham letter, Lenormand and Kipper card',summary:'The Grimoire\u2019s Traditional Information holds a page for each.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Grimoire and open the Traditional Information shelf.','Open Divination, then Tarot, Runes, Ogham, Lenormand or Kipper. Tarot is grouped by the Major Arcana and each suit, the runes by their three aettir, the ogham by its four aicm\xed, Lenormand and Kipper twelve cards at a time.','Tap a card or stave for its picture or letter, its three words and its page.'],tips:['Practice \u2192 Craft \u2192 "Card meanings" opens the same pages, with a search.','They follow the Traditional Information setting in More, then Settings, then "Living Library".'],keywords:['tarot meanings','card meaning','rune meaning','ogham meaning','futhark','major arcana','minor arcana','lenormand meanings','kipper meanings','playing card insert']},{id:'grimoire-year-review',title:'Look back over your year',summary:'Your year in review gathers a year of your practice by your own new year, with questions to write a year-end page.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Grimoire and tap "Your year in review". Around your year\u2019s turn, Today shows it too.','Read the year: rituals journaled and planned, whether your workings worked, the full and new moons and holidays you kept, your readings and the cards that came most, new Grimoire pages and dreams, journeys and courses, offerings, changes at your altars and coven gatherings.','Tap "\u2039 The year before" to look further back.','Under "Reflect", tap "Write a year-end page in my Grimoire" for a page with the questions and room to answer, under "Year in review".','Under "Where your year begins", choose "As my calendar counts it", "1 January", "Samhain" or "The moon\u2019s new year".'],tips:['Only you see it. "A card to share" holds counts only, never your questions, cards, dreams, workings or Cycle & Moon, and nothing leaves your device unless you share or copy it.','Cycle & Moon shows only when you keep it and it is open on this device.','A moon or holiday counts as met when a ritual, a reading or an offering falls on it, or the day either side.'],href:'/grimoire/year',keywords:['year in review','year review','look back','samhain','new year','reflection','year end','wrapped','statistics']},{id:'grimoire-new-entry',title:'Add your own notes to a herb, crystal or deity',summary:'The "New Library note" button adds a My Practice entry to the Living Library.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Grimoire and tap "New Library note".','Choose a category, then search the Library or type a new name.','Fill in the fields, such as Meaning, Uses, Pairs With, Substitutions and Notes.','Tap "Create entry".'],tips:['Entries are saved to your account and appear on the website too.'],keywords:['my practice entry','personal notes','custom herb','custom crystal','new practice entry']},{id:'grimoire-share-page',title:'Share a page with a coven or the Sanctuary',summary:'Share\u2026 on a page offers both ways to share it.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Grimoire and tap a page.','Tap "Share\u2026".','Tap "Suggest to a coven" to send a copy to a coven\u2019s book, for those who approve its pages.','Or tap "Make an offering" to offer it to the Community Grimoire. The form starts with the page\u2019s title and words, for you to change before you send it.'],tips:['Your own page is never changed by either.'],keywords:['share','suggest to a coven','coven book','offering','community grimoire','publish a page']},{id:'grimoire-page-font',title:'Change the font on your pages',summary:'Pick the look of the writing in your Grimoire.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Grimoire".','Under "Page font", choose Classic Serif, Dark Academia, Soft Journal or Handwritten.','Each change saves itself.'],href:'/more/settings/book',keywords:['typeface','handwriting','page look']},{id:'grimoire-traditional-pages-setting',title:'Keep Traditional Library pages in your book on the website',summary:'A setting for people who use the website\u2019s Grimoire too.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Grimoire".','Switch on "Add Traditional Library pages".','Each change saves itself.'],href:'/more/settings/book',keywords:['sync library to grimoire','traditional reference pages']}]},{id:'rituals',title:'Rituals',intro:'Plan a night, run a ritual step by step, and write down what happened.',topics:[{id:'my-shelves',title:'Keep track of what you own on My Shelves',summary:'My Shelves holds the real things you keep (crystals, herbs and resins, oils and waters, candles, tools, decks, books, statues, jars and spell bottles) on painted shelves or as a list.',steps:['Go to Practice \u2192 Rituals and tap "My Shelves" (it is also on To tend, and "I own this" in the altar cabinet and the Living Library brings you here).','Tap "Add something", find it in the cabinet, or tap "Add my own" and "Add a photo".','Fill in how much you have (a count, or full, half or low), where it\u2019s kept, where it came from, when you got it, an intention and notes.','Tap "Put it on my shelves".','Tap "List" to search and sort by shelf, what needs tending, what\u2019s running low, name or date added; "Shelves" takes you back to the cabinet.'],tips:['In the altar cabinet, "I own this" under any item adds it with the cabinet\u2019s picture; once added it says "On my shelves".','Where it\u2019s kept suggests the places you\u2019ve used before.','Each shelf is painted as its own furniture: crystals on carved shelves, herbs and jars in an apothecary cupboard, oils and waters on a bottle rack, candles on a candle shelf, books and decks in a bookcase, and statues, tools and the rest on a wall shelf. Things stand on its planks, a few to a plank, and a second cabinet appears when one is full.','Herbs and resins stand in a glass jar, oils in a dropper bottle, waters in a corked bottle, decks in their box and books by their spine, each with a label. Tap "Change", then under "Its label" write what it says (it says the name until you do), and choose aged paper, kraft or black with gold, and ink serif, script or handwritten.','Signed in, your shelves sync with your account and the website; as a guest they stay on this device.'],href:'/altar?tab=shelves',keywords:['inventory','collection','what i own','stock','supplies','crystals','herbs','oils','decks','books','statues','i own this','shelf','label','jar','bookcase']},{id:'my-shelves-tending',title:'Tend what\u2019s on your shelves',summary:'Each shelf has its own way of being tended, which shows in To tend and on Today, and you can change it for any one thing.',steps:['Open something on My Shelves.','Under "Tending", see its rhythm and when it\u2019s next due; tap "Tended today" (or "Checked or replaced today" for herbs and oils) when you\u2019ve done it.','To change it, tap "Change", then under "Tending" choose another rhythm or turn "Tend it in To tend" off.'],tips:['Until you choose otherwise (common modern practice, not tradition): crystals are cleansed and recharged at each full moon; herbs, resins and oils are checked about a year after you got them (many oils keep up to two years); moon water and other waters are made fresh each full moon; jars and spell bottles are checked on each month; statues and tools are dusted and cleansed each month.','Decks are cleansed when you feel they need it, after heavy use, so nothing is set for them; candles and books ask nothing; living plants are tended in your garden instead.','Only the thing you added is put on To tend, linked by its own id: tending it never marks anything else done.'],href:'/altar?tab=shelves',keywords:['best by','expiry','cleanse crystals','recharge','moon water','dust statues','witch bottle']},{id:'my-shelves-shopping',title:'Keep a shopping list of what\u2019s running low',summary:'Mark something running low and it goes on your shopping list, grouped by shelf.',steps:['Open something on My Shelves and tap "Running low: add to my shopping list" (choosing "Low", or counting down to none, does the same).','Your shopping list is at the bottom of My Shelves.','When you\u2019ve bought more, tap "Restocked": it comes off the list and its quantity goes back up.'],href:'/altar?tab=shelves',keywords:['shopping','restock','low','buy','running out']},{id:'my-shelves-altar-spells',title:'Use things from your shelves on the altar and in spells',summary:'Place the very thing you own on your altar, and see what you already have when you build a spell or open a premade working.',steps:['Open something on My Shelves and tap "Place on my altar": your most recent altar opens with it set down.','Its charges and cleansings there are kept in its story on My Shelves, under "Its story".','In the spell builder or a premade working, the ingredient check counts what\u2019s on your shelves; tap "Used it" by one to keep it in its story.','To have it counted down each time, open it, tap "Change" and turn on "Count down when used in a spell".'],href:'/altar?tab=shelves',keywords:['place on altar','ingredients','you have','gather','count down','used in spell','story']},{id:'rituals-home',title:'Find your way around Practice \u2192 Rituals',summary:'Practice \u2192 Rituals holds your ritual work: what you do, what you learn and what you record.',steps:['Open Practice and choose Rituals at the top (Grimoire \xb7 Rituals \xb7 Craft).','The top cards show a ritual under way, and "Your next working".','Under Do: "Begin a ritual", "Plan a ritual" and "Build a spell".','Under Learn: "Workings library", "Community Rituals" and "Dedication journeys".','Under Record: your latest rituals, "Record a ritual", Journal, "Your moon" and Apothecary.'],tips:['Cycle & Moon, astrology, divination, the sigil maker and the Craft tools are under Craft, the third section at the top. Their old links still open them.'],href:'/rituals',keywords:['rituals','workings','spells','overview','where is divination','where is cycle']},{id:'ritual-plan-night',title:'Plan a ritual for the right night',summary:'Choose an intention and the app finds nights whose moon and weekday suit it.',steps:['Open Rituals and, under Do, tap "Plan a ritual" (the screen is called "Find the night").','Under "What is it for?", choose an intention such as Protection, Prosperity, Love or Healing.','Tap a night under "Best nights in the next month", or step to a night of your own with "\u22127", "\u2039", "\u203a" and "+7".','Choose a time and "Which ritual?" (a template, or "Decide later"), and optionally add a name.','Tap "Plan it for" and the night\u2019s name.'],href:'/rituals/planner',keywords:['schedule','moon timing','weekday magic','best night','calendar','intention']},{id:'ritual-plan-gather',title:'Pick ingredients to gather for a plan',summary:'The planner suggests candles, herbs and crystals from the Library.',steps:['In the planner, choose an intention.','Scroll to "From the Library".','Tap the candles, herbs and crystals you want to gather.','Tap "Plan it for" to save the plan with your list.'],keywords:['shopping list','ingredients','what do i need']},{id:'ritual-plan-open',title:'Open, change or remove a plan',summary:'A plan shows its night, sky, reminder and calendar.',steps:['Open Rituals and tap "Open the plan", or a plan under "Also planned".','Tap "Change the night or time" to edit it, then "Save changes".','Tap "Remove plan" and confirm to take it away, with its reminder and calendar event.'],keywords:['edit plan','delete plan','reschedule','cancel plan']},{id:'ritual-plan-calendar',title:'Add a plan to your calendar',summary:'Put a planned ritual in your phone\u2019s calendar.',steps:['Open a plan, or switch on "Add to my calendar" while planning.','On the plan, under Calendar, tap "Add to my calendar".','Allow calendar access if asked.','To remove it, tap "Take it out of my calendar".'],tips:['Where the phone calendar isn\u2019t available, "Add to Google Calendar" or "Download for my calendar (.ics)" appear instead.'],keywords:['google calendar','ics','apple calendar','event']},{id:'ritual-begin-free',title:'Begin a working of your own',summary:'No steps, just a clock. Finish when you are ready.',steps:['Open Rituals and tap "Begin a ritual".','Under "A working of your own", optionally name it and write your intention.','Tap "Begin".'],href:'/rituals/templates',keywords:['free ritual','quiet working','impromptu','timer']},{id:'ritual-run',title:'Run a ritual step by step',summary:'Follow each step with its words and its gentle timer.',steps:['Begin a ritual from a template, a spell, a plan or the premade book.','Read the step and any words to speak.','Tap "Complete step" when you are done, or "Skip this step". The last one reads "Complete the last step".','Tap "Pause" to stop the clock and "Resume" to carry on.'],tips:['Timed steps move on by themselves, and your phone rings softly when it is time.'],href:'/rituals/run',keywords:['guided ritual','step','timer','pause','skip','continue ritual']},{id:'ritual-finish',title:'Finish a ritual and journal it',summary:'Close the circle and write down what happened while it is fresh.',steps:['When every step is done, tap "Finish and journal". Or tap "Finish now and journal" at any time.','Fill in the journal form and tap "Save to my journal".','To skip the journal, tap "Finish without journaling".','To leave without saving anything, tap "End without saving".'],keywords:['end ritual','complete','abandon','stop ritual']},{id:'ritual-build-spell',title:'Build a spell: purpose, form, ingredients, timing and words',summary:'A guided builder: the Living Library suggests what suits, you choose, and the steps follow until you make them your own.',steps:['Open Rituals and tap "Build a spell", or tap "Use in a spell" on a herb, stone, candle or deity in the Library, "Adapt this in the builder" on a premade working, or "Build a spell" on a planet guide or in the timing advisor.','Choose what it is for (the same list as the timing advisor) and its form: candle, jar, sachet, charm bag, oil, knot, sigil, petition, poppet, bath, powder, simmer pot or your own.','Tap suggested candles, herbs and stones (things you own are marked), swap any for a substitute, add things of your own, and read "Take care" for fire, skin and poisonous plants.','If you like, choose deities to honour (each shows whether their tie is ancient or modern), the moon and the day, or tap "Find a good time".','Write your words, then reorder, change, add or remove steps. "Keep in my Grimoire" saves it; open it again from the saved spell with "Open in the spell builder".','After you have done it, the journal asks whether it worked, and the answers show in the builder.'],href:'/rituals/spell',keywords:['spell builder','create spell','petition','candle spell','custom spell','spell jar','sachet','sigil','ritual oil','charm bag','correspondences','substitute']},{id:'ritual-moon-sabbat-kits',title:'Use a moon or sabbat kit',summary:'For each phase of the moon and each sabbat: an altar set in one tap, correspondences, a short ritual, a journal prompt and a reading.',steps:['On Today, tap "Tonight\u2019s kit" (the sabbat\u2019s near its day, otherwise tonight\u2019s moon), or open any moon phase or sabbat page.','Under the kit, tap "Set the altar for it" for a starter altar from the cabinet. Move or swap anything, then Save to keep it.','Tap a herb, stone or colour to open it in the Library, "Open the ritual" for a short working, and the spread button for a reading.','Write to the prompt in your journal.'],href:'/today',keywords:['kit','tonight\u2019s kit','moon kit','sabbat kit','esbat','full moon','new moon','samhain','yule','altar set-up','journal prompt','spread']},{id:'ritual-correspondence-finder',title:'Find correspondences, then build a spell',summary:'Look by intention, herb, stone, colour, planet, day or moon, choose what suits, and open the spell builder with it.',steps:['Open Rituals and tap "Correspondence finder", or tap "Find by correspondence" at the top of the spell builder.','Choose what the work is for, type a word (a herb, a stone, a use), or open "By planet, day, colour or moon".','Tap herbs, stones and candle colours to choose them. Your own correspondences are included and marked "Yours", and your pairings are offered once you choose their entry.','Read the suggested moon and day, and the timing advisor\u2019s best time this week, then tap "Build a spell". The builder opens with your choices, the intention and that moon and day.'],href:'/rituals/finder',keywords:['correspondence finder','correspondences','find herbs','what herb for','colour','planet','moon phase','build a spell','ingredients']},{id:'ritual-templates-use',title:'Begin a ritual from one of your templates',summary:'Templates are your own written rituals, kept in your account.',steps:['Sign in, open Rituals, then tap "Begin a ritual".','Under "Your templates", tap one to read its preparation and steps.','Tap "Begin this ritual", or "Begin on an altar" to run it over one of your altars.','Tap "Plan a night for it" to schedule it.'],href:'/rituals/templates',keywords:['ritual template','my rituals','saved ritual']},{id:'ritual-template-write',title:'Write a ritual template',summary:'Write your own steps, words and timers once and reuse them.',steps:['Sign in, open Rituals, tap "Begin a ritual", then "New template".','Fill in "Ritual name", "Purpose or intention" and "Preparation".','For each step, add a "Step title", "Guidance", "Words to read or speak" and a "Timer in minutes".','Choose what candles do when each step begins and ends. Tap "Add another step" for more.','Add "Closing words or instructions", then tap "Save template".'],tips:['Use "Move up", "Move down" and "Remove" on a step to rearrange. On an existing template, "Archive template" removes it.'],href:'/rituals/templates/edit',keywords:['create ritual','custom ritual','write ritual','new template','edit template']},{id:'ritual-template-candles',title:'Have candles light and go out with the steps',summary:'Link a template to an altar, and its candles follow the ritual.',steps:['Open or write a template and choose a "Linked altar setup".','For each step, choose "No candle action", "Light all candles" or "Extinguish all candles" for "When this step begins" and "When this step ends".','Save the template.','Begin it. Each step lists what it will do to the candles.'],keywords:['automation','altar linked','light candles automatically']},{id:'ritual-premade-book',title:'Find a ritual or spell in the premade book',summary:'Workings for the Wheel of the Year, folk ways and every practice.',steps:['Open Rituals and, under Learn, tap "Workings library".','Look at "For you tonight", then search or filter by Kind, Practice, Intention or Path.','Tap a working to read its summary, safety notes, what you will need and steps.','Tap "Begin this ritual", "Begin on an altar" or "Plan a night for it".'],tips:['Tap "Save a copy to my templates" to change it however you like. Sign in first.'],href:'/rituals/premade',keywords:['premade','ready made','sabbat ritual','moon ritual','library of rituals','book']},{id:'ritual-community-share',title:'Share a ritual with the community',summary:'Offer one of your templates, or a coven\u2019s you lead, to Community Rituals. It is reviewed before it appears.',steps:['Open a template (Rituals \u2192 "Begin a ritual", then a template) and tap "Share with the community". Or open Rituals, under Learn tap "Community Rituals", then "Share a ritual" and choose one.','For a coven\u2019s template: open the coven, Rituals, "The coven\u2019s templates", then "Share with the community". Only the coven\u2019s head and those who lead its rituals can.','Check the title, kind, tradition, deities, occasion, moon, materials, steps, safety notes and "Its roots", and change anything you like.','Under "Credit it to", choose your preferred or magical name, Anonymous, or the coven.','Read the community guidelines, switch on "I agree to the Submission Terms and these guidelines", and tap "Send for review".','Follow it under Community \u2192 Mine: waiting, returned for changes (with the moderators\u2019 note), published or not accepted.'],tips:['A copy is shared: your template stays yours. A coven\u2019s roles, members and notes are never shared.','From "My shared rituals" you can change one that is waiting or returned, send an update to a published one (it stays up until the update is published), or withdraw it.','There are no notifications for this yet: check "My shared rituals" to see a decision.','To keep a ritual you did without a template, open it in your Journal and tap "Keep it as a template". Coven rites have "Save to my templates" under "Keep it".'],href:'/rituals/community/share',keywords:['share ritual','publish ritual','community rituals','submit ritual','coven template','send for review','withdraw']},{id:'ritual-community-find',title:'Find and use community rituals',summary:'Search rituals the community has shared, then add one to yours, do it once, or add it to a coven.',steps:['Open Rituals and, under Learn, tap "Community" (or More \u2192 Community); Rituals is the first part.','Search by sharer, title, deity, herb or holiday, and filter by Kind and Moon. Tap "More filters" for tradition, deity, occasion and what it needs, and choose a Sort: Newest, Most saved or A to Z.','Tap a ritual to read it all: who shared it, safety notes, its roots, what you\u2019ll need and the steps.','Tap "Add to my rituals" for your own copy (credited to the sharer, yours to change), "Do it once" to begin it without saving, or "Plan a night for it".','If you lead a coven\u2019s rituals, tap "Add to a coven\u2019s rituals" and choose the coven.'],tips:['After doing one once, the journal page offers "Add it to my rituals".','Tap "More from" and the sharer\u2019s name to see everything they\u2019ve shared.','Tap "Report" to email the moderators, "Hide" to stop showing it, or "Block this person" (or "Hide this coven"). Tap "Show rituals and people you\u2019ve hidden" to see them again.'],href:'/rituals/community',keywords:['community rituals','shared rituals','search rituals','add to my rituals','do it once','most saved','block','report']},{id:'ritual-check-ingredients',title:'Check what you need for a premade working',summary:'Each working lists its ingredients and links them to the Library.',steps:['Open a working in the Workings library.','Read the ingredient check, then "You\u2019ll need".','Tap an underlined ingredient to open it in the Living Library.'],keywords:['ingredients','shopping','supplies','what to gather']},{id:'ritual-reminders-settings',title:'Change your ritual reminders',summary:'Reminders live with the moon reminders.',steps:['Open a plan and tap "Reminder settings", or open More, tap "Reminders", then "Moon and rituals".','Under "Planned rituals", switch "Remind me before a planned ritual" on or off.','Choose how long before.'],href:'/rituals/reminders',keywords:['notifications settings','plan alert']},{id:'ritual-journal-record',title:'Record a ritual in your journal',summary:'Write down what you did, felt and noticed.',steps:['Open Rituals and tap "Record a ritual".','Name the ritual, write the intention, choose when it was, and choose the moon phase.','Open "Before and during" and "After the flame" to write more.','Tap "Save to my journal".'],tips:['When you finish a ritual here, the form opens with the facts already held.'],href:'/rituals/journal/new',keywords:['journal','ritual log','diary','reflection','record ritual']},{id:'ritual-journal-browse',title:'Read, edit or delete a journal entry',summary:'Your rituals are kept in order, newest first.',steps:['Open Rituals and scroll to Journal. Tap "See all" if there are more than five.','Tap an entry to read it, with its steps and what was on the altar.','Tap "Edit reflections" to change it, or "Plan it again" to schedule it.','Tap "Delete" to remove it here and on the website.'],href:'/rituals/journal',keywords:['past rituals','history','delete entry','edit journal']},{id:'ritual-did-it-work',title:'Say whether a ritual or spell worked',summary:'Choose a day to look back, and on that day you are asked: did it work?',steps:['When you journal a ritual, choose a day under "Did it work? Look back". The moon that suits its intention comes first; or choose "In a week", "In a month", "Another day" or "Not needed".','On that day the question shows on Today and at the top of your Journal under "Did it work?", with a reminder if look-back reminders are on.','Choose "Yes", "Partly", "Not yet" or "No", write "What happened", and tap "Save the answer". If it is too soon to say, choose when to look again and tap "Keep waiting".','To answer before the day, open the entry and tap "Say what happened now". Tap "Change the answer" to change it later.'],tips:['Readings work the same way: choose a day under "Come back to it" as you keep one.'],href:'/rituals/journal',keywords:['did it work','look back','look-back','results','outcome','follow up','success','manifest']},{id:'ritual-check-ins',title:'Check in on a spell a day, a week and four weeks on',summary:'Follow a working through: how it is going, and any signs, kept with the working in your Journal.',steps:['After you record a ritual or spell, its journal page offers "Follow it through". Tap "Check in with me".','A day, a week and four weeks later a reminder asks how it is going. Open the working, choose how it feels, note any signs and tap "Save the check-in".','At four weeks you can answer "Did it work?" in the same check-in. Each check-in shows in the Journal on the day you wrote it.','Turn the reminders off in Settings \u2192 Reminders under "Check in on spells and workings", or stop them for one working with "Stop the check-ins".'],href:'/rituals/journal',keywords:['check in','check-in','follow up','follow through','signs','spell results','did it work','reminder']},{id:'apothecary-did-it-work',title:'Look back on a spell jar, sachet or anything you made',summary:'What you make in your Apothecary can be asked "Did it work?" too.',steps:['As you make a spell jar, sachet or something in your Apothecary, keep the look-back day that suits its intention under "Did it work? Look back", or choose another.','Open Practice \u2192 Rituals and, under Record, tap Apothecary (or Journal, then "Apothecary: jars & sachets") to see what is "Looking back soon", "Looked back on" and has "No look-back day yet".','On its day, Today and your Journal ask whether it worked. Tap it to answer, and to read "What went into it".'],href:'/rituals/apothecary',keywords:['spell jar','sachet','charm bag','poppet','oil','apothecary','did it work','look back']},{id:'ritual-what-works',title:'See what works for you',summary:'As you answer "Did it work?", your own patterns gather.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Rituals, scroll to Journal, and tap "Your moon".','Scroll to "What works for you".','Read the lines at the top, then "By moon phase", "By intention", "By day and its planet", "Candle colours", "Herbs and oils" and "Stones".'],tips:['A yes counts whole and a partly counts half. Groups with fewer than three answers are early notes, not patterns.'],href:'/rituals/journal/insights',keywords:['patterns','what works','statistics','best moon','best candle colour','results']},{id:'ritual-your-moon',title:'See the patterns in your practice',summary:'"Your moon" shows which moons you work under, and what for.',steps:['Open Rituals, scroll to Journal, and tap "Your moon".','After a few journaled rituals, read the lines that gather at the top.','See "Last" and the moon phase for what you did last time the moon looked like this.','Check "By phase", "What works for you" and "Still watching for" for results you are waiting on.'],href:'/rituals/journal/insights',keywords:['insights','patterns','moon phases chart','statistics','analytics']},{id:'ritual-bring-device-rituals',title:'Bring rituals from this phone into your account',summary:'If you kept rituals before signing in, move them across.',steps:['Sign in, then open Practice \u2192 Rituals.','Find the card "Rituals from this phone".','Tap "Bring them into my account".'],keywords:['migrate rituals','sync rituals','device rituals']},{id:'ritual-library-ingredient',title:'Read about an ingredient while building a spell',summary:'Peek at a herb, crystal or candle\u2019s meaning without leaving your work.',steps:['In "Build a spell", pick some ingredients.','Under "Read about them in the Library", tap a name with a "\u203a".','Read its uses, "A beginning" and "With care", then tap an intention under "Plan a working with it" to plan one.'],keywords:['ingredient info','herb info','safety']},{id:'cycle-moon',title:'Cycle & Moon',summary:'Keep your cycle beside the moon: log your bleeds and days, see where each bleed falls in the lunar month, and find practice for your inner season. Or follow the moon alone.',steps:['Open Practice, choose Craft at the top, and tap "Cycle & Moon" under "Body & moon".','The first time, choose "Set a passphrase" to keep it with your account, or "Keep it on this phone".','Tap "Add past periods" to give it your history: pick the days on a calendar or paste a list of dates (see "Log past periods").','Tap "Log today" to mark "My bleed began this day", the flow, symptoms, and how the day feels: energy, intuition, mood, body, dreams and anything else.','The card at the top shows the day of your cycle, your inner season and the moon, with a gentle estimate of your next bleed when there\u2019s an honest one ("may start in about 3 days, around 3 November", or "between 3 and 7 November" when you\u2019ve set a range).','Under it is "Today\u2019s reading": your cycle day, inner season and phase (menstrual, follicular, ovulatory or luteal) read against the moon\u2019s exact phase, how much of it is lit and when it next turns, with what the two together suggest, a practice that opens in the app and a journaling prompt. There\u2019s one for each season under each of the eight moon phases.','Below are "What am I?" (your moon pattern from your history), symptoms and insights, the moon wheel (this lunar month, with your seasons and where your recent bleeds began), and what your notes show over time.','Tap "Inner seasons and moon patterns" for what suits each season, journaling prompts, the White, Pink, Red and Purple Moon patterns, and folk notes on moon time.','If you don\u2019t bleed (after menopause or a hysterectomy, while pregnant, or for any reason), open "Settings and privacy" and choose "The moon alone" under Follow: the moon\u2019s dark becomes your inner winter, its waxing your spring, its full your summer and its waning your autumn.'],tips:['It\u2019s for reflection and practice, not medical advice. It never predicts fertility and must never be used as contraception. See a doctor or nurse for pain, very heavy bleeding or very irregular cycles.','The inner seasons and moon patterns are modern spiritual and folk frameworks, not biology. People move between the patterns.','In "Settings and privacy", under "Cycle length", choose "Work it out from my history" (the default; it needs two cycles logged), "Exactly" a number of days, or "A range" such as 27 to 31 days. It sets your cycle day, the seasons and the next-bleed estimate. Inner autumn (the luteal side) is taken as about 14 days, so a longer or shorter cycle mostly changes your spring.','In "Settings and privacy" you can also tell it your cycles are irregular, or about hormonal birth control, pregnancy, a recent birth or perimenopause, so the wording and estimates fit. You can also turn on the archetype lens (off unless you choose it), the moon-time altar, a Moon Time section in your Grimoire, and reminders.','Today shows one small card from it, only when there\u2019s something to say. Turn it off with "A small card on Today".'],href:'/rituals/cycle',keywords:['period','menstrual','cycle tracker','moon cycle','bleed','menstruation','inner seasons','red moon','white moon','moon time','menopause','perimenopause','archetypes','cycle length','luteal','moon phase reading','today\u2019s reading']},{id:'cycle-moon-past',title:'Log past periods',summary:'Add the periods you remember, many at once, so Cycle & Moon knows your history.',steps:['Open Practice, then Craft, then "Cycle & Moon", then "Past periods".','On the calendar, tap the day each period began. Use "\u2039 Earlier" to go back a month. Days already logged are shaded.','Under "Each lasted about", choose how many days they usually lasted, or "Not sure", then tap "Add".','Or paste a list: one period a line, such as "2026-09-29", "1 September 2026 to 5 September 2026" or "04/08/2026, 5 days". Choose whether slashed dates are day first or month first, tap "Read these dates", check them, then tap "Add".','To change or remove one, tap it under "Logged", change the dates and tap "Keep the change", or "Remove this period".'],tips:['Dates in the future, and periods that overlap one already logged, aren\u2019t added; it tells you which and why.','Rough dates are fine. Everything is kept encrypted, like the rest of your Cycle & Moon notes.'],href:'/rituals/cycle/past',keywords:['past periods','period history','import periods','add periods','last period','edit period','delete period']},{id:'cycle-moon-history',title:'What am I? Your moon pattern from your history',summary:'From the periods you\u2019ve logged: your average cycle and how much it varies, how long your bleeds last, and the moon pattern they lean to.',steps:['Open Practice, then Craft, then "Cycle & Moon", then "What am I?".','At the top is your moon pattern, such as "Based on 6 cycles: Red Moon, strongly" or "mixed between White and Pink Moon", with what it means and how it has shifted over time.','Under "Your rhythm" are your average cycle, the shortest and longest, how long your bleeds last, and how your cycle sits beside the moon\u2019s 29.5-day month.','Under "Each bleed and the moon" is the moon phase and lunar day each bleed began on.'],tips:['White Moon: bleeding near the new moon. Pink: under a waxing moon. Red: near the full moon. Purple: under a waning moon.','These are modern folk and spiritual names, not biology. Studies haven\u2019t found that cycles follow the moon, and many people move between patterns.','It needs at least three bleeds to say anything more than "too early to say".'],href:'/rituals/cycle/history',keywords:['moon pattern','red moon cycle','white moon cycle','pink moon','purple moon','average cycle','cycle length','what am i']},{id:'cycle-moon-symptoms',title:'Log symptoms and see insights',summary:'Log symptoms with how strongly you feel them, see patterns across your cycles and the moon, and find folk and herbal comfort with safety notes.',steps:['Open Cycle & Moon and tap "Log today" (or any day).','Under "Symptoms", tap a symptom once for mild, twice for moderate, three times for strong, and once more to clear. They\u2019re kept as you tap.','To add your own, type it under "Add a symptom of your own" and tap "Add it". It\u2019s offered again next time.','Open "Symptoms and insights" from Cycle & Moon to see what your notes show, such as "Headaches tend to come on cycle days 25\u201327" or "You sleep worse near the full moon", with what each rests on.','Below are comfort ideas for what you\u2019ve logged lately: teas, warmth, baths, stones and small rituals, each with its own safety note and links to the Living Library.'],tips:['Patterns show only once a symptom appears on 3 or more days across at least 2 cycles; the moon\u2019s part needs 14 days logged over six weeks or more. They can be chance, and grow surer as you log.','Herbs can interact with medicines. Check with a doctor or pharmacist first if you\u2019re pregnant, breastfeeding, taking medicines or have allergies.','It isn\u2019t medical advice. If it notices something worth a doctor\u2019s eye, such as heavy flow logged again and again, it says so gently. See a doctor for severe pain, very heavy bleeding, missed periods or anything worrying.'],href:'/rituals/cycle/insights',keywords:['symptoms','cramps','pms','headache','bloating','mood','insights','herbal remedies','raspberry leaf','period pain','heavy bleeding','witchy remedies']},{id:'cycle-moon-private',title:'Keep Cycle & Moon private (passphrase and sync)',summary:'Your Cycle & Moon notes are encrypted on your phone or browser before they\u2019re kept anywhere, and only your passphrase or recovery key opens them.',steps:['Open Practice, then Craft, then "Cycle & Moon", then "Settings and privacy".','To keep it with your account (so it shows on other phones and the website), choose "Keep it with my account (set a passphrase)". Choose one you\u2019ll remember; it isn\u2019t your account password.','Write down the recovery key it shows you and keep it somewhere safe. It won\u2019t be shown again.','On another phone or on the website, open Cycle & Moon and enter the same passphrase once; that device remembers it after that.','To keep it on this phone only, choose "Keep it on this phone only". Your account\u2019s encrypted copy is deleted.','To delete everything, choose "Delete all my Cycle & Moon data" at the foot of the page. It\u2019s removed from this phone and your account.'],tips:['If you lose both your passphrase and your recovery key, nobody can open your notes again, including the people who run Salt & Sovereignty. You can delete them and start again.','The phone remembers the key in the app\u2019s own storage. If others can open your apps, turn on "Ask for my passphrase each time"; reminders then ring only while Cycle & Moon has been opened.','Reminders are off unless you turn them on, and say only "Cycle & Moon has a note for you" unless you turn on "Say what it\u2019s about".','Deleting your account deletes your Cycle & Moon data too. Nothing from it is used for ads or analytics.'],href:'/rituals/cycle/settings',keywords:['encryption','passphrase','recovery key','privacy','sync','period privacy','delete cycle data','lock']},{id:'cycle-moon-share',title:'Share that you\u2019re in moon time with your coven',summary:'If you want to, let chosen covens or people see a few words by your name, like \u201cIn moon time \xb7 resting\u201d. Never dates or notes.',steps:['Open Practice, then Craft, then "Cycle & Moon", then "Share with my covens".','Choose what it says: "In moon time", "In moon time \xb7 resting", "Resting \xb7 gentle days" or "Keeping quiet for a few days".','Choose for how long: it clears itself after 1 to 7 days.','Choose the covens whose members may see it, or open "Or only certain people" and choose them.','Tap "Share it". They see a small moon and those words by your name on the coven\u2019s Members page.','To stop at any time, tap "Stop sharing now".'],tips:['It\u2019s separate from your encrypted notes: only the words you choose are shared, and only with the covens and people you choose.'],href:'/rituals/cycle/share',keywords:['moon time','coven status','resting','share period','red tent']}]},{id:'journeys',title:'Dedication journeys',intro:'A season of study, practice and discernment toward dedicating yourself to a path or a god. Nothing is ever failed.',topics:[{id:'journeys-browse',title:'Browse dedication journeys',summary:'Choose a path or a deity to study toward.',steps:['Open Rituals and tap "Dedication journeys".','Read the introduction: a dedication is a promise you make yourself, not an initiation.','Search, or browse "Paths" and "Deities". Your path\u2019s journeys come first.','Tap one to read about it.'],tips:['Choose your path in Settings, Living Library, My path to put its journeys first.'],href:'/rituals/journeys',keywords:['dedication','self-dedication','path','deity journey','hekate','norse']},{id:'year-and-a-day',title:'Follow A Year and a Day alone',summary:'Thirteen moons of study and practice for someone practising alone, ending in a self-dedication if you choose it.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Rituals and tap "A Year and a Day" (it is also on Dedication journeys, the Solitary page and the Grimoire).','Choose your track: Eclectic, or a tradition\u2019s lens: Wicca, Celtic, Norse & Heathen or Hellenic.','Choose when to begin: today, the next new moon, a coming festival of your calendar, or a day you type in. Tap "Begin my year and a day".','Open a moon to see what to read (lessons from the courses), what to practise (with the festivals and the moon\u2019s rite that fall in it), its reflection and its self-checks.','Tap a lesson to read it, then "I\u2019ve read this". Turn on "Done" under each practice when you have kept it.','Write the moon\u2019s reflection and tick the self-checks that are true for you. They are private and never graded.','On the day of dedication, a year and a day after you began, open "The day of dedication" for the rite, then tap "I have made my dedication" once you have kept it.'],tips:['Today shows where you are ("Moon 3 of 13") while your year is under way.','Turn on "Remind me" for a note when each moon begins, a nudge to reflect before it ends, and the day itself. On the website they come as a calendar file.','You can read ahead, fall behind, move your first day or change your track; nothing is locked or failed.','Your progress syncs with your account, so it is the same in the app and on the website.'],href:'/rituals/year',keywords:['year and a day','solitary','thirteen moons','13 moons','self-dedication','course','study alone','dedicant','wicca','heathen']},{id:'journeys-patron',title:'Read the guide to patron deities',summary:'What a patron is, how to know if one is calling you, and how to answer.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Rituals, then "Dedication journeys", then "Patron deities".','Read it through, with "What we know, and what we don\u2019t" and "Reading further".','Tap "My deities" to keep the gods you are getting to know, or "Dedication journeys" to study toward one.'],href:'/rituals/journeys/patron',keywords:['patron','matron','patron deity','calling','signs from a god','deity']},{id:'practice-my-deities',title:'Keep your deities and your patron',summary:'Name the gods you are exploring, have dedicated to, or keep as your patron. None is required.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "My deities".','Under "Add a deity", search the Living Library by name or pantheon and tap one, or add one in your own words.','Under "Yours", choose how close you are to each: Exploring, Dedicated or Patron. Add "Since" and "A note for yourself" if you like.','Each change saves itself.'],tips:['Switch on "Remind me on their sacred days" for a note on the holy days of your patron and dedicated deities, with a small devotion. Their days show on Today under "For your practice" too.'],href:'/more/settings/deities',keywords:['my deities','patron','dedicated','exploring','gods','goddess','sacred days','holy days']},{id:'journeys-begin',title:'Begin a journey',summary:'Read the welcome and begin at your own pace.',steps:['Open a journey from "Dedication journeys".','Read "Before you begin" and "Things to know first".','Tap "Begin this journey".','Tap "Open this stage" to go to your first stage.'],tips:['A deity\u2019s Living Library page also offers "Begin a dedication journey".'],keywords:['start journey','six stages','welcome']},{id:'journeys-stages-lessons',title:'Move through the six stages',summary:'Each stage has lessons to read and practices to do.',steps:['Open a journey and look at "The six stages". Tap a stage.','Under Lessons, tap one to read it, then "Mark as read".','Under Practices, tap one, and "I did this" each time you do it.','When the stage is ready, tap "Move on to" the next stage\u2019s name. You can move on early.'],keywords:['lessons','practices','progress','next stage','tick off']},{id:'journeys-practice-note',title:'Log a practice and keep a note',summary:'Mark each time you do a practice, with a note if you like.',steps:['Open a stage and tap a practice.','Optionally type "A note (optional)", and switch on "Also keep it in my journal".','Tap "I did this".','To take a time back, tap "Remove" under "Times you\u2019ve done it".'],keywords:['practice log','habit','daily practice']},{id:'journeys-discernment',title:'Take time to discern before dedicating',summary:'Honest questions, then your choice: continue, pause, set it down, or choose another.',steps:['In the Discernment stage, tap "Discern".','Answer the questions and tap "Keep my answers". Tap "Keep them in my journal too" to copy them to your journal.','Optionally add "A word about why".','Tap "Continue", "Pause", "Set it down" or "Look at other journeys".'],tips:['Setting a journey down is a good outcome, not a failure. You can begin again any time.'],keywords:['decide','questions','should i dedicate','stop journey']},{id:'journeys-rite',title:'Do the rite of dedication',summary:'Run the rite as a guided ritual, or mark it done if you did it your own way.',steps:['Open the rite from its stage and read "Take care", "You\u2019ll need" and the steps.','Tap "Begin the rite", or "Continue the rite" if it is under way.','When it ends, it is marked done. If you did it in your own way, tap "I\u2019ve done it".','After a dedication, tap "On to the year after".'],keywords:['dedication ritual','self dedication','initiation rite','rite']},{id:'journeys-year-after',title:'Keep your dedication: holy days and rededication',summary:'The year after has holy days, small daily practices and a yearly renewal.',steps:['Open your journey and tap "Holy days and rededication".','Read "Holy days coming up" and tap practices under "Keeping it".','When a year has turned, tap "Read the dedication rite again" if you like.','Tap "I\u2019ve rededicated" to keep the day.'],keywords:['anniversary','renew','rededicate','ongoing','holy days']},{id:'journeys-pause',title:'Pause or pick a journey up again',summary:'A journey waits for you exactly as it is.',steps:['Open the journey.','Tap "Pause for now" and confirm.','Later, tap "Pick it up again".'],keywords:['resume journey','break','hold']},{id:'journeys-set-stage',title:'Return to or jump to a stage',summary:'Make any stage your current stage without losing anything.',steps:['Open the journey and tap a stage under "The six stages".','Tap "Make this my current stage" and confirm "Make it my stage".'],keywords:['go back','skip ahead','change stage']}]},{id:'divination',title:'Divination and sigils',intro:'Tarot, runes, ogham, Lenormand, Kipper and decks of your own, laid out in their spreads; your readings and the sigil maker. Open to every practice.',topics:[{id:'practice-draw',title:'Draw tarot cards, runes or ogham',summary:'A card for the day, three cards, the Celtic Cross and many more spreads, runes or ogham staves, with what each means; or a spread of your own.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft and, under "Divination & sigils", tap "Divination", then "Draw cards, runes or ogham". On Today, "Draw a card for the day" opens it too.','Choose Tarot, Runes or Ogham. Tap the spread to see the others, grouped Quick, Classic, Moon & seasons, Deep work and Your spreads, each with a picture of its shape.','Tap "Shuffle and draw" ("Cast the runes" or "Draw the staves"), then tap each card to turn it over and read what it means in its place, or "Turn them all over". Big spreads scroll sideways; "Look closer" makes them bigger.','Write what you make of it, choose a day to come back to it, and tap "Keep this reading". It goes into your readings under Divination, and lays out in its shape again when you open it.'],href:'/rituals/divination/draw',keywords:['tarot','draw a card','card of the day','daily card','celtic cross','three card spread','rune cast','ogham','reversed cards','blank rune','spreads','horseshoe','tree of life','new moon spread','full moon spread','samhain spread','make your own spread','custom spread']},{id:'psychic-development',title:'Practise psychic development and see your results',summary:'Card and colour guessing, remote viewing, Tomorrow\u2019s card, psychometry and warm-ups, each scored honestly against chance and kept in your Journal.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft \u2192 Psychic development. Optionally start with a warm-up: grounding, opening, third eye or aura sensing.','Card & colour guessing: choose symbols, suits, colours or yes and no, and 10 or 25 trials. The hidden target is chosen before you guess; it is shown after each trial.','Remote viewing: write impressions of a hidden altar picture, choose it blind from four pictures, then see the answer and rate how close you were.','Tomorrow\u2019s card: guess a suit or the major arcana (and a number) today. Draw tomorrow\u2019s card of the day in Divination and the guess is scored for you.','Telepathy: make a session for a pair (invite a friend with a code, or a member of your coven) or for a whole coven. Choose symbols, suits, colours or a picture, the rounds, the seconds a round, a start time and who sends. At the start time everyone\u2019s screen follows the same clock: the sender sees the target and holds it in mind, receivers write impressions and choose, then everyone sees the target and each hit or miss. There is no call. Targets are drawn on the server and kept from receivers until the round is over.','Open "Your results" for hit rate against chance, a chart by day, streaks, time of day and moon phase.'],tips:['We only say "above chance" when the exact binomial p-value is below 0.05 over at least 50 trials. Fewer trials, or a lower score, reads as in line with chance, or too few to tell.','Short runs wander widely, and slicing by moon or hour makes many small groups, so some will look good by luck.','Nothing here claims you are or are not psychic. Controlled tests of these abilities have not shown them; the exercises are practice in attention.'],href:'/rituals/craft/psychic',keywords:['psychic','esp','zener','remote viewing','precognition','psychometry','intuition','clairvoyance','aura','third eye','guessing']},{id:'divination-study',title:'Learn the cards with flashcards and a quiz',summary:'Study the tarot (in your deck\u2019s own reading), runes, ogham, Lenormand, Kipper or a deck of your own, a few cards a day.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft \u2192 Divination and tap "Learn the cards".','Read today\u2019s card to learn, then choose a deck.','Tap "Flashcards": look at the card, tap "Show the meaning", then "I knew it" or "Not yet". Or tap "Quiz" and choose the right meaning.'],tips:['Cards move through five boxes. One you know comes back after a day, then three, seven, fourteen and thirty; one you miss goes back to the first box.','Seven new cards join each day, so a deck of 78 is met in under a fortnight.','Your progress is kept with your account, per deck.'],href:'/rituals/divination/study',keywords:['learn tarot','flashcards','quiz','study','spaced repetition','memorise','runes','ogham','lenormand']},{id:'divination-deck',title:'Choose a tarot deck',summary:'Draw with the Rider\u2013Waite\u2013Smith, the Tarot de Marseille or the Sola Busca: the same 78 cards, each deck with its own pictures and its own way of reading them.',steps:['Open More \u2192 Settings \u2192 Divination and choose a deck; it saves itself. Or, as you draw tarot, tap a deck under "Deck" before you shuffle.','The Rider\u2013Waite\u2013Smith (Pamela Colman Smith, 1909) is the default. Nicolas Conver\u2019s Tarot de Marseille (1760) numbers Justice VIII and Strength XI, and its numbered cards show only their suit signs. The Sola Busca (Italy, about 1491) names its trumps after heroes of Rome and the Bible and calls its suits batons, cups, swords and coins.','Each deck reads its cards in its own way. The Rider\u2013Waite\u2013Smith keeps A. E. Waite\u2019s meanings; the Tarot de Marseille is read as French cartomancy and Marseille readers read it, its numbered cards by number and suit; the Sola Busca has a reading of its own too. Where a deck titles a card its own way, its title shows under the card\u2019s name, and a card a deck has no reading of its own for yet reads as Waite\u2019s, and says so.','A kept reading remembers the deck it was drawn with and opens in it again, with that deck\u2019s meanings. Your Grimoire\u2019s tarot pages show each card in your deck, leading with that deck\u2019s reading and then the Rider\u2013Waite\u2013Smith\u2019s in depth, with the other decks a tap away.'],href:'/more/settings/divination',keywords:['tarot deck','deck','marseille','tarot de marseille','conver','sola busca','rider waite smith','rws','card pictures','change deck']},{id:'divination-own-spread',title:'Make a spread of your own',summary:'Name it, give it a shape, and say what each place means.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, tap "Divination", then "Make a spread". Or, as you draw, tap the spread, then "Make your own".','Give it a name and what it\u2019s for, then choose what to draw and its shape: a line, a cross, an arc, a circle or a grid.','Name each place and add a line on how to read it. Tap "Add a place" for another, or "Take this place out".','Tap "Keep this spread". It is under "Your spreads" when you draw; tap "Change this spread" there to change it, or "Delete this spread".'],href:'/rituals/divination/spread',keywords:['custom spread','own spread','layout','positions','tarot spread','make spread']},{id:'divination-lenormand',title:'Draw Lenormand or Kipper cards',summary:'Thirty-six cards each: Lenormand read in pairs and lines, Kipper read around the main person, up to the Grand Tableau of all thirty-six.',steps:['Open the draw screen and choose Lenormand or Kipper.','Lenormand: one card, a pair, a line of three or five, the 3\xd73 box, or the Grand Tableau (four rows of eight and four beneath, each place a house). Kipper: three cards, nine, or its Grand Tableau of four rows of nine.','Turn the cards over and tap each for its meaning. For Lenormand, "Read in pairs" reads each card with the next: the first says what, the second says what kind (Ship then Rider: a journey, soon).','Big spreads are laid out small to see whole; "Look closer" makes them bigger and scrolls sideways.'],tips:['The Lenormand pictures are a Belgian printing of the 1890s. No complete old Kipper printing could be found free to use, so the Kipper cards are drawn in words: number, name and German name.','Each card has its page in the Grimoire\u2019s Traditional Information, under Divination.'],href:'/rituals/divination/draw',keywords:['lenormand','petit lenormand','kipper','kipperkarten','grand tableau','houses','pairs','combinations','line of three','3x3','box spread','main person']},{id:'divination-own-decks',title:'Add an oracle deck of your own',summary:'Your own deck\u2019s cards, with photos and meanings, to draw from or to log the cards you pull by hand.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, tap "Divination", then "Your oracle decks", then "Make a deck". Or choose "Your decks" on the draw screen.','Name it, and add a cover photo if you like. Turn on "Read reversals" if you read cards upside down.','Add cards one at a time (name, a few words, what it means, a photo of the card), or paste in a whole list, one "Name \u2014 meaning" to a line.','Tap "Keep this deck". On the draw screen, choose "Your decks" and the deck, then any spread: its own, any tarot spread, or one of yours.'],tips:['Signed in, decks and their photos are kept with your account and show on the website too. As a guest they stay on this phone.'],href:'/rituals/divination/decks',keywords:['oracle deck','own deck','my deck','bring your own deck','oracle cards','card photos','import cards','paste list']},{id:'divination-physical-pull',title:'Log the cards you pulled by hand',summary:'Drew real cards? Pick which card lay in each place, and keep it as a reading.',steps:['On the draw screen, choose what you drew from (tarot, Lenormand, Kipper or a deck of your own) and the spread you laid.','Under "How", choose "Log a physical pull".','For each place in turn, tap the card you drew. Tap a place to take its card out; mark any that came up reversed.','Tap "Lay it out" to see the spread and the meanings, then keep it like any reading.'],href:'/rituals/divination/draw',keywords:['physical pull','real cards','own deck','by hand','log cards','pulled','record spread']},{id:'divination-crossroads',title:'Draw the Crossroads spread',summary:'Five cards for a place where roads meet: where you stand, the roads to either side, the road behind, and a word from the guardian of the crossroads.',steps:['Open "Draw cards, runes or ogham" and choose Tarot.','Tap the spread, then under Deep work choose "The crossroads". Its picture shows the three roads meeting, and the guardian\u2019s card set apart above.','Tap "Shuffle and draw", turn the cards over, and read each in its place.','Write what you make of it and tap "Keep this reading".'],tips:['Many hear Hekate in the guardian\u2019s card, with her torches and keys; hear whoever guards the ways for you.','On Hekate\u2019s Deipnon, Today offers it.'],href:'/rituals/divination/draw',keywords:['crossroads','hekate','hecate','trivia','guardian','roads','decision','spread']},{id:'divination-dream-reading',title:'Read a dream with the cards',summary:'Three cards for a dream that stays with you: what it shows, what it stirs in you, what it asks of you.',steps:['Open the dream in Grimoire \u2192 Dreams and tap "Read this dream". Or, as you draw, choose "Dream reading" under Deep work, then the dream under "The dream it\u2019s for".','Tap "Shuffle and draw", turn the cards over, and tap "Keep this reading".','The reading shows on the dream\u2019s page under "Readings of this dream", and the reading says which dream it was for.','In "Symbols and moons", "Cards that keep coming up" counts the cards that return across your dream readings.'],href:'/grimoire/dreams',keywords:['dream','dream reading','dream tarot','dream meaning','interpret dream','symbols','recurring cards']},{id:'divination-before-working',title:'Draw before a ritual or spell',summary:'Three cards before a working: the working itself, what to watch for, and the likely outcome, kept beside "Did it work?".',steps:['Open a planned working from Rituals or Today, and tap "Draw before you begin". Or, as you draw, choose "Before a working" under Quick, then the working under "The working it\u2019s for".','Tap "Shuffle and draw", turn the cards over, and tap "Keep this reading".','Begin the working from its plan as usual. When you look back on it, the reading shows under "Drawn before you began", next to "Did it work?".','Once you\u2019ve said whether it worked, say whether the reading bore out: "It bore out", "Partly" or "It didn\u2019t".'],tips:['In the journal\u2019s insights, What works for you says how often your pre-readings bore out.'],href:'/rituals/divination/draw',keywords:['before a working','pre-reading','spell reading','ritual reading','did it work','outcome','divination before spell']},{id:'divination-sabbat-spreads',title:'Draw a spread for a sabbat',summary:'Each of the eight sabbats has its own spread, offered in the days around it.',steps:['In the week or so around a sabbat, Today and the draw screen show a line such as "Yule is in 3 days: Yule: the returning light". Tap it.','Or open "Draw cards, runes or ogham", choose Tarot, tap the spread, and pick one under Moon & seasons: Samhain, Yule, Imbolc, Ostara, Beltane, Litha, Lammas or Mabon.','Tap "Shuffle and draw", turn the cards over, and keep the reading.'],tips:['If you keep the Wheel of the Year for the Southern Hemisphere, the spreads follow your dates.'],href:'/rituals/divination/draw',keywords:['sabbat','yule','imbolc','ostara','beltane','litha','lammas','lughnasadh','mabon','samhain','wheel of the year','seasonal spread','solstice','equinox']},{id:'divination-patron-deity',title:'Draw for one of your deities',summary:'Four cards: what this god asks of you, what they offer, how to honour them, and what stands between you.',steps:['Open a deity\u2019s dedication journey and tap "Draw the Patron deity spread", or tap it in the patron deities guide. Or, as you draw, choose "Patron deity" under Deep work, then the god under "The god it\u2019s for".','Tap "Shuffle and draw", turn the cards over, and keep the reading.','Readings for that god show on their journey under "Readings for this god".'],href:'/rituals/journeys/patron',keywords:['patron','deity','god','goddess','devotion','offering','honour','patron spread']},{id:'practice-readings',title:'Log a divination reading and come back to it',summary:'Record cards, runes or other readings, then see how they turned out.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft and, under "Divination & sigils", tap "Divination", then "Log a reading". Your readings are listed below it. Divination is open to every practice.','Choose a method such as Tarot, Oracle cards, Runes, Tea leaves, Scrying, Pendulum or Ogham.','Type the question and what came up, and add cards or runes drawn.','Under "Come back to it", choose a day, then tap "Keep this reading".','When the day comes, open it and tap "Save what happened".'],href:'/rituals/divination',keywords:['tarot','runes','oracle','pendulum','divination log','look back']},{id:'divination-patterns',title:'See the patterns in your readings',summary:'Your patterns shows what your own draw log says over time.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, tap "Divination", then "Your patterns". Today, a card\u2019s page and your year in review link there too.','Choose "All time", "Past year", "Past 90 days" or "Past 30 days".','Read the cards drawn most (tap one for its page, in the deck you drew it with most), your tarot decks, suits and elements, the runes\u2019 aettir, the ogham\u2019s aicm\xed and Lenormand\u2019s playing suits, and how many cards came reversed.','Under "Around your questions", see the cards that came more than once for a kind of question, or for a dream, a working or a deity.','See your readings by the moon\u2019s phase and by the day and its planet, your streaks, and "Cards you haven\u2019t met yet", each a tap from its page.'],tips:['Only you see it; it is worked out from your readings and nothing is stored.','The elements beside the tarot suits are the Golden Dawn\u2019s, the usual modern reading; some readers swap Wands and Swords.'],href:'/rituals/divination/patterns',keywords:['patterns','statistics','most drawn','tarot stats','reversals','suits','elements','streak','cards not drawn']},{id:'practice-sigil',title:'Make a sigil',summary:'A statement of intent made into one mark: from its letters, on a planetary square, or drawn by hand.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft and, under "Divination & sigils", tap "Sigil maker". It is open to every practice; Eclectic, the altar and the Grimoire open it too.','Under "Your statement of intent", write it as if it were already so. Switch on "Strike out the vowels too" if you like.','Under "How to make it", choose "From the letters", "On a planetary square" or "Draw it yourself", then choose how it looks and whether it has "A circle around it".','Under "Keep it", name it and tap "Keep it with my sigils", or "Give it a page in my Grimoire".'],tips:['Sigils you keep are listed under "Your sigils", and wait in the candle\u2019s Carve sheet, ready to carve.'],href:'/rituals/sigil',keywords:['sigil','sigil maker','kamea','planetary square','chaos magic','intent','carve a sigil','spare']}]},{id:'my-practice',title:'Craft and the Craft tools',intro:'Practice\u2019s third section: the tools that aren\u2019t rituals, and ten practices with tools of their own. Choose yours to put them first.',topics:[{id:'craft-home',title:'Find your way around Practice \u2192 Craft',summary:'Craft holds the practice tools that aren\u2019t rituals: your cycle and the moon, the sky, divination and the tools for each path.',steps:['Open Practice and choose Craft at the top (Grimoire \xb7 Rituals \xb7 Craft).','Under "Body & moon": "Cycle & Moon".','Under "The sky": "Astrology", "Planetary hours", "Find a good time" and "Learn astrology".','Under "Divination & sigils": "Divination", "Draw cards, runes or ogham", "Card meanings" (in the app) and "Sigil maker".','Under "Craft tools by path": your crafts first, then the other practices, and "Choose your crafts".','Under "Elsewhere in Practice": "Dedication journeys" and the "Workings library", which stay under Rituals, and your dreams, which live in your Grimoire.'],tips:['The Practice tab reopens whichever of Grimoire, Rituals and Craft you used last.'],href:'/rituals/craft',keywords:['craft','tools','cycle','astrology','divination','sigil','where is','overview','practice tools']},{id:'practice-choose',title:'Choose how you practise',summary:'Pick as many practices as fit; their tools and workings come first.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Your crafts".','Switch on the practices you keep: Eclectic, Green, Kitchen & hearth, Hedge, Solitary, Cosmic & celestial, Crystal, Elemental, Sea, or Traditional & folk.','Each change saves itself.'],tips:['Every practice\u2019s tools stay open to you either way.'],href:'/more/settings/practice',keywords:['green witch','kitchen witch','hedge witch','eclectic','solitary','sea witch','tradition']},{id:'practice-hub',title:'Open the tools for your practice',summary:'The Craft home lists each kind of craft and its tools, under "Craft tools by path": your own crafts with each tool listed, and a row for every other practice.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft (My practice) and look under "Craft tools by path".','Tap one of your crafts under "Your crafts", or any under "Other practices".','Tap a tool on that practice\u2019s page.','Tap its premade workings row, such as "Green workings", for rituals and spells made for it.'],href:'/rituals/craft',keywords:['craft tools','practice tools','hub']},{id:'practice-green-moon',title:'Plant by the moon',summary:'What to sow, tend and harvest tonight.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Green, then "Planting by the moon".','Read tonight\u2019s phase, what suits it and why.','Look at "The moon\u2019s sign" and "The next fourteen nights".','Tap "Log it in My garden" or "What\u2019s in season now".'],href:'/rituals/craft/green/moon',keywords:['biodynamic','gardening','sowing','almanac','moon planting']},{id:'practice-green-season',title:'Use the garden and foraging calendar',summary:'Month by month: what to sow and plant, gather and forage where you are, and which of your own plants, patches and shelf herbs are in season.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Green, then "Garden & foraging calendar". Foraging under Hearth links here too.','Tap a month. The hemisphere follows Settings \u2192 Location; choose "Northern" or "Southern" to change it here.','Under "Yours", see what of your garden, foraging patches, potted plants and shelves is ready. Tap "Log a plant" or "Log a find" to add more.','Tap a herb for its Living Library page, or a wild plant for its foraging page. "The whole year, month by month" shows every plant at a glance.'],href:'/rituals/craft/green/season',keywords:['harvest','foraging','herbs month','sow','gather']},{id:'practice-garden-add',title:'Keep a magical garden',summary:'Track your plants, sowings and harvests.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Green, then "My garden".','Tap "Add a plant".','Name it, optionally link it to its Living Library herb, and say where it grows.','Choose "Sowed as seed" or "Planted", and the date, then tap "Add to my garden".'],href:'/rituals/craft/green/garden',keywords:['plants','sowing','herb garden','windowsill']},{id:'practice-garden-log',title:'Log watering, harvests and blessings for a plant',summary:'Each plant keeps a history, with the moon recorded for you.',steps:['Open "My garden" and tap a plant.','Under "Log something", choose Sowed, Planted out, Watered or fed, Harvested, Blessing or offering, or Note.','Choose "When", add any amount or note, and tap the log button.','To mark a plant finished, open "It\u2019s gone from the garden" and tap "Mark as gone".'],keywords:['harvest log','water plant','garden journal','plant history']},{id:'practice-kitchen-pantry',title:'Look up a pantry ingredient\u2019s correspondences',summary:'Salt, honey, cinnamon and the rest of the cupboard.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then "Kitchen & hearth", then "Pantry correspondences".','Search, or choose a Shelf, an Element, or "Good for\u2026".','Tap an item to read its lore, how to use it and "Take care".','Tap "Open \u2026 in the Library" when it has a full entry.'],href:'/rituals/craft/kitchen/pantry',keywords:['spices','cupboard','honey','salt','cinnamon','kitchen magic']},{id:'practice-simmer-pot',title:'Make a simmer pot',summary:'A pot for your home from what you have, for an intention and a season.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then "Kitchen & hearth", then "Simmer pot".','Under "What\u2019s it for?", choose an intention, then a Season.','Read the ingredients and "At the stove".','Tap "Begin as a ritual" to be guided through it.'],href:'/rituals/craft/kitchen/simmer',keywords:['stovetop potpourri','home blessing','kitchen','hearth']},{id:'practice-home-moon',title:'Do housework by the moon',summary:'Which tasks suit tonight.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then "Kitchen & hearth", then "Home by the moon".','Read the part of the moon\u2019s month and its list of tasks.','Tick tasks off as you do them.','Tap a working under "Workings that suit tonight".'],href:'/rituals/craft/kitchen/moon',keywords:['cleaning','chores','domestic','house magic']},{id:'practice-kitchen-spellbook',title:'Use the kitchen spell book',summary:'Recipes as workings: breads, broths, washes and blessings.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then "Kitchen & hearth", then "Kitchen spell book".','Search, or choose a "For" intention.','Tap a recipe to read ingredients, method and the words to say.'],href:'/rituals/craft/kitchen/spells',keywords:['recipes','kitchen spells','bread spell','broth']},{id:'practice-bath-mixes',title:'Use bath mixes, build your own and log your baths',summary:'Thirty spiritual and comfort baths by intention, moon and season, with safety notes worked out for you, your shelves, and a log in the Journal.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then "Kitchen & hearth", then "Bath & body". Filter by Everyday, Moon, Seasons or Gentle, or by intention.','Open a mix to read its ingredients with amounts, how to prepare it (sachet, tea or infusion, or loose), the best moon, day and hour, the words to speak, and what to do with the water and herbs afterwards.','Read "Before you bathe": cautions for skin, pregnancy, children, pets and stones appear on their own for whatever the mix contains. Stones are marked water-safe or keep out of the water.','Under "On your shelves" see "You have X of Y ingredients", and tap "Add what\u2019s missing" to put the rest on your running-low list.','Tap "Find a good time" for the timing advisor, "Log this bath" to record how it felt in your Journal, and a rhythm under "Make it a rhythm" (each new moon, weekly and so on) to have it in To tend.','Tap "Build your own": choose an intention, choose from the herbs and stones the Library suggests, set amounts and a method, and save it as one of your mixes.'],tips:['Never put essential oil straight in the water: mix it into a carrier oil, milk or salts first. No premade mix uses oils.','Salty water goes down the drain, never on plants. Loose herbs go on the compost, not down the plug-hole.','Moon and sabbat kits suggest a matching bath, and Library herb and stone pages list the mixes that use them.','A comfort practice, not a treatment: see a doctor or pharmacist for any health concern.'],href:'/rituals/craft/bath',keywords:['bath','spiritual bath','ritual bath','bath salts','cleansing bath','uncrossing','milk bath','foot soak','herbal bath','soak','epsom']},{id:'practice-ancestors',title:'Remember your ancestors and the beloved dead',summary:'Keep the people you carry, with their days and a candle to light.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Hedge, then "Ancestors".','Tap "Add someone".','Type their name and who they are to you, add born and died dates, and what they loved.','Tap "Remember them".'],href:'/rituals/craft/hedge/ancestors',keywords:['dead','memorial','shrine','anniversary','family','beloved dead']},{id:'practice-ancestor-candle',title:'Light a candle for an ancestor',summary:'A short guided rite of about ten minutes.',steps:['Open "Ancestors" and tap a person.','Tap "Light a candle".','Follow the short rite: light a candle, say their name, remember, and tell them what you need to.'],tips:['Never leave a flame unattended.'],keywords:['memorial candle','rite for the dead','ancestor altar']},{id:'practice-chart-add',title:'Add your birth chart (or someone else\u2019s)',summary:'Your birth date is enough; a time and place add your rising sign and houses. The place search fills in the time zone for that moment, summer time included.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then "Astrology", then "All charts", and tap "Add my chart" (or "Add someone\u2019s chart").','Give it a name and choose "Mine" or "Someone else\u2019s".','Enter the birth date and, if you know it, the birth time. If you don\u2019t, turn on "I don\u2019t know the time".','Search for the birth town and tap it. The UTC offset at that moment appears under "Time zone at the birth".','If a birth record shows a different clock time (wartime or local time), turn on "Set the offset myself" and enter it.','Tap "Save".'],tips:['The place list holds every town of 15,000 people or more (from GeoNames); for a village, choose the nearest town, or open "Enter coordinates instead".','The time zone database is very good from 1970 and good before. Where the clocks jumped or went back that night, the screen says which time it used and how to choose the other.','Before standard time zones (around 1890), most places kept local mean time; the screen shows what that was there.','Only add someone\u2019s chart with their blessing. It stays with you.'],href:'/rituals/craft/cosmic/charts',keywords:['natal chart','birth chart','astrology','birth time','rising sign','ascendant','time zone','daylight saving','birthplace']},{id:'practice-chart-read',title:'Read your birth chart',summary:'The wheel, every placement, the aspects, the balance of elements and modalities, and the whole chart read in full.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then "Astrology", then "My chart".','On "Wheel", tap any planet, sign, house number or aspect line to see what it means there.','Use the chips along the top for "Placements", "Aspects" (with the grid and the patterns), "Balance" and "Read in full".','Under "Read in full", every part of the chart is read in turn; pieces still being written show a short sketch and the words to learn.'],tips:['Without a birth time there are no houses or rising sign; "Show solar chart houses" draws houses from your Sun instead, clearly marked.','Astrology here is a language of traditional meanings, offered for reflection. Nothing in a chart decides who you are or what you\u2019ll do.'],href:'/rituals/craft/cosmic/chart',keywords:['big three','sun sign','moon sign','rising','houses','aspects','natal','chart wheel','stellium','grand trine','t-square','dignity']},{id:'practice-chart-explanations',title:'Learn what any astrology word means (Simple or Detailed)',summary:'Every underlined astrology word, anywhere in the app, opens its explanation; choose how much it says.',steps:['Tap any gold, dotted-underlined word, like Ascendant, retrograde or void of course.','Choose "Simple" for a sentence or two, or "Detailed" for the astronomy, history, how traditions read it, its use in the craft and what to take care over.','Your choice is kept for everywhere ("Explanations" on All charts). Any card can be switched on its own with its own Simple \xb7 Detailed switch.','For the whole glossary, open Cosmic & celestial, then "Learn astrology", and search or browse from "The basics".'],href:'/rituals/craft/cosmic/learn',keywords:['glossary','learn astrology','beginner','explain','what does it mean','simple','detailed']},{id:'practice-chart-transits',title:'See transits, returns and progressions',summary:'What today\u2019s sky (or any date\u2019s) is doing to your chart, your solar and lunar returns, and your secondary progressions.',steps:['Open your chart and tap "Transits". Choose "Now", "Tomorrow", "In a week", "In a month" or type a date.','The outer ring of the wheel is the sky at that moment; the list shows each contact, closest first, and the retrogrades with their shadow periods.','Tap "Returns" for this year\u2019s solar return (the Sun back to its birth degree) and the next lunar return, cast for your birthplace or where you are now.','Tap "Progressions" for your progressed Moon, its next change of sign, and the progressed lunar phase.'],tips:['Today\u2019s strongest transit to your chart also shows on Today, in "Today\u2019s sky".'],href:'/rituals/craft/cosmic/chart',keywords:['transits','solar return','lunar return','progressions','progressed moon','saturn return','retrograde shadow']},{id:'practice-chart-synastry',title:'Compare two charts (synastry)',summary:'The aspects between two charts and where each person\u2019s planets fall in the other\u2019s houses.',steps:['Add at least two charts.','Open "All charts" and tap "Compare two charts (synastry)".','Choose the first and second charts; tap any contact for what it means.'],tips:['Only charts you entered yourself can be compared.'],href:'/rituals/craft/cosmic/synastry',keywords:['synastry','compatibility','relationship astrology','two charts']},{id:'practice-chart-relationship',title:'How your charts meet',summary:'Two saved charts read for a romance, friendship, family or coven bond, with a composite chart, good days together and matching spells. No scores.',steps:['Open a saved chart and tap "Compare" (or "How your charts meet" in All charts).','Choose the other chart and the kind of relationship.','Read the sections, pick good days, then build a spell, write in your journal or share a card.','In a coven, "Chart sharing" lets you opt in to share your planets\u2019 positions (never birth details).'],tips:['Keep someone else\u2019s birth details only with their blessing.','House overlays need both birth times.'],href:'/rituals/craft/cosmic/relationship',keywords:['relationship','compare charts','composite','good days together','coven chart','synastry']},{id:'practice-chart-craft',title:'Use your chart in your craft',summary:'Your planetary allies, a natal altar, your ruler\u2019s hours, and the deities tied to your strongest planets.',steps:['Open your chart and tap "In your craft".','Your chart ruler and the rulers of your Sun and Moon signs are shown with their day, metal, colours, herbs and stones; tap a herb or stone for its Living Library entry.','Tap "Set a \u2026 altar" for a starter altar in your chart ruler\u2019s colours and pieces.','Under "Deities tied to your strongest planets", open a deity\u2019s Library entry or dedication journey.'],tips:['These are places to start, never assignments: each deity is approached through their own tradition.'],href:'/rituals/craft/cosmic/chart',keywords:['chart ruler','natal altar','planetary correspondences','deity','personal correspondences']},{id:'practice-chart-settings',title:'Choose your house system, zodiac and orbs',summary:'Placidus, Whole Sign or Equal houses; tropical or sidereal (Lahiri); true or mean nodes; minor aspects and orbs.',steps:['Open Cosmic & celestial, then "All charts".','Under "How charts are drawn", choose what you prefer. Every chart redraws.'],tips:['Inside the polar circles Placidus houses can\u2019t be drawn; Porphyry houses are used there and the chart says so.','Sidereal shifts the signs by the ayanamsa (about 24\xb0); it doesn\u2019t bring in the other techniques of Vedic astrology.'],href:'/rituals/craft/cosmic/charts',keywords:['house system','placidus','whole sign','equal houses','sidereal','vedic','lahiri','orbs','minor aspects']},{id:'practice-chart-privacy',title:'Keep your birth details private (and synced)',summary:'Charts are encrypted on your device; to sync them, protect them with a passphrase only you know.',steps:['Open Cosmic & celestial, then "All charts", then "Privacy and syncing".','By default charts are encrypted and kept on this device only.','To have them on the website and your other devices, choose a passphrase (at least 10 characters) and tap "Keep with my account". Write down the recovery key it shows you.','On another device, open your charts once with the passphrase.','To remove everything, tap "Delete all my charts".'],tips:['Only encrypted text reaches the server; nobody at Salt & Sovereignty can read it. Lose both the passphrase and the recovery key and the synced copy can\u2019t be opened by anyone.','A chart you entered before this was kept in plain form with your account; it moves into the encrypted vault the first time you open your charts, and the old copy is deleted.'],href:'/rituals/craft/cosmic/keep',keywords:['privacy','encryption','passphrase','recovery key','birth data','delete chart']},{id:'practice-planetary-hours',title:'Find the planetary hour for your working',summary:'The day\u2019s planet, the 24 hours as a wheel from your real sunrise and sunset, and a way to plan or be reminded at the next hour of any planet.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then "Cosmic & celestial", then "Planetary hours".','The wheel shows the day\u2019s 24 hours, the one you\u2019re in in gold, and how long it has left. Tap any hour for what it suits.','Under "Find the next hour of", tap a planet to see its next hours, and the next one on its own day (a Venus hour on a Friday).','Tap "Remind me at the next \u2026 hour on \u2026" to put a working in your planner with a reminder, or "Plan a working then" to open the planner at that time.','In the ritual planner, "Planetary hours that day" shows which hour your time falls in and lets you pick a planet\u2019s hour.'],tips:['Planetary hours need your place. Set it with "Use my location" on that screen.','Each planet has its own guide: tap it under "The seven planets".'],href:'/rituals/craft/cosmic/hours',keywords:['planetary hour','planetary day','void of course','timing','sunrise hours','magical hours','chaldean order','remind me']},{id:'practice-spell-timing',title:'Find a good time for a spell or ritual',summary:'The spell timing advisor: say what a working is for, and see the best times in the next week, month or three months, each with a score and the reasons behind it.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft and, under "The sky", tap "Find a good time". It is also on "Planetary hours", "Cosmic & celestial", each planet\u2019s guide, "The sky today", the ritual planner, the spell builder, each premade working and each plan.','Under "What is it for?", choose love, money and luck, protection, banishing, healing, divination, communication, courage, ancestors, endings, new beginnings, cleansing or peace. From a working or a plan, it is chosen for you.','Choose how far ahead: the next week, month or three months.','"Right now" says how this hour measures up; "Good enough now" means there is little to gain by waiting.','Each time below shows the moon, a score and its main reasons. Tap "Why" for every factor and what it added or took away.','Tap "Set a ritual for then" on a time. "Build a new ritual for then" opens the ritual builder with the time and its reasons at the top; saving keeps the ritual in your Grimoire and sets it for then, so it shows under Practice \u2192 Rituals with your ritual reminders.','Or tap one of your own rituals to set it for that time straight away, or, if you lead rituals in a coven, "Plan it with" the coven to open its ritual builder with the date, time and intention filled in. "Just pick the time in the planner" opens the planner instead.','Opened from a plan, the spell builder or one of your rituals, it hands the time back instead: "Plan it then", or "Move the plan to then" to change a plan\u2019s time.','Under "Weigh the factors", turn the moon phase, Moon sign, void-of-course Moon, planetary day and hour, retrogrades, your festivals, your deities and your chart up, down or off, and choose whether to include the small hours.'],tips:['It weighs traditional correspondences, not rules: waxing to draw in, waning to release, Mercury retrograde for words, the Deipnon for Hekate\u2019s work, and so on.','Planetary hours need your place (Settings \u2192 Location). Without it, it judges three-hour stretches of each day.','Your festivals come from Settings \u2192 Calendars, and your patron and dedicated deities from My deities. Your birth chart counts only while your charts are open on this device, and is optional.','The website has the same advisor under Practice \u2192 Craft.'],href:'/rituals/craft/cosmic/timing',keywords:['timing','when','best time','electional','spell timing','good time','moon phase','void of course','mercury retrograde','planetary hour','advisor','when to cast']},{id:'practice-planet-guides',title:'Read a planet\u2019s guide',summary:'Each of the seven planets in depth: nature, rulerships, metal, colours, herbs, stones, incense, angels and gods across traditions, and the magic it suits.',steps:['Open "Planetary hours" and tap a planet under "The seven planets", or tap "\u2026 : the full guide" anywhere it appears.','Tap a herb, stone or god for its Living Library entry or dedication journey.'],tips:['The correspondences are the common ones of Western magic (Agrippa, the Heptameron), with their sources shown.'],href:'/rituals/craft/cosmic/planet',keywords:['planet guide','correspondences','venus','saturn','jupiter','mars','mercury','sun','moon','angels','metals']},{id:'practice-stones',title:'Keep a collection of stones and track their cleansing',summary:'Your collection, and when each stone was last cleansed.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Crystal, then "My stones".','Tap "Add a stone", search the Library or type your own name, and choose its form.','Add where it came from and what it is working on, then tap "Save stone".','Under "When stones fall due", choose how often cleansing is due.'],href:'/rituals/craft/crystal/stones',keywords:['crystals','collection','cleansing schedule','tumbled','raw','cluster']},{id:'practice-stone-log',title:'Log cleansing, charging or programming a stone',summary:'Keep a history of how you care for each stone.',steps:['Open "My stones" and tap a stone.','Under "Log care", choose Cleansed, Charged or Programmed.','Pick the method, add a note, or fill in "On an earlier day?".','Tap the log button. Remove a mistake with "Remove" in the History.'],keywords:['cleanse stone','charge crystal','program crystal','stone history']},{id:'practice-stone-care',title:'Check which stones are safe in water, sun and salt',summary:'Some stones dissolve, fade or are toxic.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Crystal, then "Stone care".','Read "Reading the badges".','Type in "Find a stone" or use the filters.','Open a stone to see its hardness, notes and safe cleansing methods.'],href:'/rituals/craft/crystal/care',keywords:['water safe','sun fade','toxic crystals','selenite','crystal elixir','mohs']},{id:'practice-elements',title:'See the balance of the elements in your work',summary:'Earth, air, fire and water in what you use.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Elemental, then "Elements in your work".','Read "Your balance" and which element lags behind.','Tap "Begin" a suggested rite, or "Read it first".','Open "How this is worked out" for the details.'],href:'/rituals/craft/elemental/balance',keywords:['earth air fire water','balance','four elements']},{id:'practice-weather',title:'Plan around the weather',summary:'Rain, wind, storm and clear skies for the next three days.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Elemental, then "Weather for working".','Tap "Use my location", or "Enter it by hand".','Read each day and tap a suggested working.','Pull down to refresh the forecast.'],tips:['Only your rounded location is sent to a free weather service.'],href:'/rituals/craft/elemental/weather',keywords:['forecast','storm magic','rain','wind','open-meteo']},{id:'practice-tides',title:'Follow the tides',summary:'Springs and neaps anywhere; high and low water for US coasts.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Sea, then "Tides".','Read "By the moon, everywhere" and "Springs and neaps ahead".','For high and low water on a US coast, tap "Choose a station".','Choose "Feet" or "Metres".'],href:'/rituals/craft/sea/tides',keywords:['tide times','high tide','low tide','noaa','king tide','springs']},{id:'practice-tide-station',title:'Choose your tide station',summary:'Pick the NOAA station nearest the shore you work at.',steps:['Open "Tides" and tap "Choose a station".','Tap "Use my location" to see the nearest, or search by station, bay or town.','Tap a station to use it.','Tap "Stop using a station" to clear it.'],href:'/rituals/craft/sea/station',keywords:['noaa station','nearest tide','harbour']},{id:'practice-shore-finds',title:'Log shells, sea glass and driftwood',summary:'Record where the tide left them and what you will ask of them.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Sea, then "Shore finds".','Tap "Log a find".','Choose what it is, such as Shell, Sea glass, Hagstone or Driftwood, then its colour, where and when.','Add what it is for and notes, then tap "Save find".'],href:'/rituals/craft/sea/finds',keywords:['beachcombing','sea glass','hagstone','driftwood','shells','strandline']},{id:'practice-folk-calendar',title:'Read the folk calendar',summary:'Old customs through the year, and a way to keep each now.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then "Traditional & folk", then "Folk calendar".','Read "The next 30 days".','Tap a month under "Through the year".','Open a custom to read what people did and "Keeping it now".'],href:'/rituals/craft/folk/calendar',keywords:['customs','old calendar','folklore year','wassail','saints days']},{id:'practice-local-lore',title:'Write down local lore',summary:'A notebook for the lore of where you live.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then "Traditional & folk", then "Local lore".','Tap "Write down some lore".','Choose what kind: Place, Spirit or being, Story, Custom, Saying, or Plant or creature lore.','Add a title, where, the lore itself and who told you, then tap "Keep this lore".'],href:'/rituals/craft/folk/lore',keywords:['folklore','holy well','local spirits','sayings','oral history']},{id:'practice-weather-lore',title:'Read weather lore for the month',summary:'Old sayings with a plain note on whether the weather bears them out.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then "Traditional & folk", then "Weather lore".','Tap a month to read its sayings.','South of the equator, tap "Use my location" and switch on "Follow my seasons".'],href:'/rituals/craft/folk/weather',keywords:['proverbs','rhymes','weather sayings']},{id:'practice-daily-devotion',title:'Keep a daily devotion',summary:'A few minutes in the morning and at night, gently kept.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Solitary, then "Daily devotion".','Read the prompt for this morning or evening.','Tap "I kept my morning practice" or "I kept my evening practice".','Optionally write "A note for today" and tap "Save note".'],tips:['Switch on "Morning devotion" or "Evening devotion" under "Remind me" on that screen.'],href:'/rituals/craft/solitary/devotion',keywords:['morning practice','evening practice','habit','prayer','streak']},{id:'practice-correspondences',title:'Write your own correspondences',summary:'What things mean to you, beside the Library\u2019s meanings.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Eclectic, then "My correspondences".','Tap "Add a correspondence".','Name the thing, or pick it from the Library to see the traditional view beside yours.','Write what it means to you. Optionally add what you pair it with (separated by commas), element, planet, day, colour and where it came from.','Tap "Save".','Or, on any Living Library entry, tap "Add your own correspondence" under "Your correspondences". Your notes and pairings show there, and the correspondence finder uses them.'],href:'/rituals/craft/eclectic/correspondences',keywords:['upg','personal gnosis','own meanings','custom correspondences','pairings','personal notes','library notes']},{id:'practice-eclectic-borrow',title:'Borrow a tool from every path',summary:'The Eclectic page offers one tool from each practice, changing daily.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Eclectic.','Scroll to "From every path".','Tap a tool to open that practice.'],href:'/rituals/craft/eclectic',keywords:['mix','variety','try other practice']},{id:'practice-land-card',title:'Learn whose land you are on',summary:'A prompt to learn the Indigenous history of where you practise.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then Green, Hedge, or "Traditional & folk".','Scroll to the card "Whose land are you on?".','Tap "Open the Native Land map" to look up your place in your browser.'],tips:['The app sends nothing about you. You search the map yourself.'],keywords:['native land','indigenous','territory','land acknowledgement']},{id:'hearth-land-journal',title:'Keep a land journal',summary:'Your places, and what they do through the year, read against the moon, the Wheel and your calendars.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft and choose "Land journal" under Hearth & land.','Tap "Add a place": your home, a garden, a wood, a shore. Write its spirit, what you give there and who it belongs to.','Tap "Note what you see". Choose the day, the place and what kind of note it is: weather, frost, birdsong, a bloom, fruit, animals, water or an offering.','Add the Library herbs and trees you saw, plants from My garden, or the potted plants on your altars.','Tap "Keep this note". It shows the moon that evening, where the day sits on the Wheel of the Year and the holy days of your calendars.'],tips:['Mark the first frost of autumn and the last of spring: the journal keeps your own frost dates year by year.','A place\u2019s rough location is kept only on your phone. It is never saved to your account.'],href:'/rituals/craft/hearth/land',keywords:['nature journal','phenology','genius loci','land spirits','frost dates','birdsong','wheel of the year','places']},{id:'hearth-last-year',title:'See what the land did this time last year',summary:'Notes from the same weeks of every earlier year.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then "Land journal".','Tap "This time last year".'],tips:['Today\u2019s Hearth & land page also says when you have notes from these weeks.'],href:'/rituals/craft/hearth/land/last-year',keywords:['last year','anniversary','year ago','compare years']},{id:'hearth-foraging',title:'Forage safely through the year',summary:'What to gather this month where you are, with look-alikes, law and care.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft and choose "Foraging & garden".','Read "Before you gather", and "Safety, law and taking with care".','Choose a month to see what can be gathered then; the months turn for the southern hemisphere when your place is set.','Tap a plant for how to know it, its look-alikes (the deadly first), how to take it with care and its Living Library page.','Tap "Add something that grows" to note what grows on each of your places.'],tips:['Never eat anything you can\u2019t identify with complete certainty. The app is not a field guide and gives no help with fungi.'],href:'/rituals/craft/hearth/forage',keywords:['foraging','wild food','hedgerow','look-alikes','poisonous','elderflower','blackberries','what grows where']},{id:'hearth-harvests',title:'Log a harvest and keep a store cupboard',summary:'What you gather, with its moon, and what\u2019s still in the jar.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft, then "Foraging & garden", then "Harvest log".','Tap "Log a harvest", say what and how much, where from and what it\u2019s for.','Switch on "Still in the store cupboard" for what you dry or jar.','Make something from it in the altar\u2019s Apothecary; the Apothecary page links back to your store cupboard.'],href:'/rituals/craft/hearth/forage/harvests',keywords:['harvest','drying herbs','store cupboard','apothecary','inventory']},{id:'hearth-recipes',title:'Cook with intent: kitchen witchery',summary:'Recipes for festivals, offerings and workings, kept in your Grimoire.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft and choose "Kitchen witchery".','See the recipes for the festivals ahead in your calendars, or choose an intent.','Open a recipe for its ingredients and their correspondences, method, words, allergies and where it comes from.','Tap "Keep it in my Grimoire" to keep it as a page under Kitchen witchery, or "Find a good time to cook it" for the timing advisor.','Tap "Write your own recipe", or "Make my own version" of a starter.'],tips:['Holy-day pages and Living Library herb pages show the recipes that belong to them.'],href:'/rituals/craft/hearth/recipes',keywords:['kitchen witch','recipes','festival food','soul cakes','offerings','cooking','allergies']},{id:'meditation-timer',title:'Meditate with a timer and bells',summary:'A calm countdown with a bell to begin, bells along the way and three to end, with time to settle in and come back.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft and choose "Meditation".','Choose how long (5 to 60 minutes, your own length, or open-ended), minutes to settle in and to come back, and the bells you want.','Turn on "Vibrate instead of a bell" for a silent sit.','Tap "Begin". When it ends, tap "Keep it in your log" to note how it went.'],tips:['The bell is the altar bell. It rings even with the silent switch on, since you chose it; Candle sounds and Vibration in Accessibility still apply.','The time is kept from when you began, so it stays true if the screen dims. If the app is put away, the end bell comes as a notification.','To meditate at your altar, open one of your altars and choose Workings \u2192 "Meditate here". You can light a candle as you begin.'],href:'/rituals/craft/meditation',keywords:['meditation','meditate','timer','bell','sit','mindfulness','grounding','centring','centering','candle gazing']},{id:'tuning-forks',title:'Strike a tuning fork',summary:'Solfeggio, planetary, chakra, grounding and clearing forks, struck once or kept as a backdrop, and on your altar.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft \u2192 "Meditation" \u2192 "Listen" (or a sit\u2019s Sound) and find "Tuning forks". Choose a set, then tap a fork to strike it and let it ring out.','Switch the layer on to have the set struck in turn every 30 seconds to 5 minutes. Pairs (128 + 136.1 Hz) are struck together, so you hear them beat.','In Craft \u2192 Timing \u2192 Planetary hours, "Strike this hour\u2019s fork" sounds the Cosmic Octave pitch of the hour\u2019s planet.','On the altar, place a Tuning Fork from the cabinet\u2019s Tools, tap it and choose Strike. A crystal\u2019s Charge panel also offers "Clear with a tuning fork (4096 Hz)", kept in its cleansing history.','In the ritual builder, add "Strike the tuning fork" or "Cleanse the space with sound" next to the bell.'],tips:['The sets are modern conventions (Solfeggio from the 1970s, Cosmic Octave from Hans Cousto, 1978), and what any pitch does is a tradition of practice, not an established effect.','The 4096 Hz fork is piercing, so it is played quietly. Pairs of forks beat at the difference of their pitches: 136.1 minus 128 is about 8 Hz.','The tuning fork borrows the wand\u2019s picture on the altar until one is painted.'],href:'/rituals/craft/meditation/listen',keywords:['tuning fork','tuning forks','solfeggio','cosmic octave','136.1','om','128 hz','4096','crystal clearing','sound healing','fork','planetary hour']},{id:'meditation-breath',title:'Pace your breath',summary:'A circle that grows as you breathe in and shrinks as you breathe out: box breathing, 4-7-8 or your own count.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft \u2192 "Meditation", then "Breath pacing".','Choose Box breathing, 4-7-8 or Your own, and tap "Begin".','Breathe with the circle. Tap "Stop" when you\u2019re done.'],tips:['There is no sound. Never strain: if you feel light-headed, stop and breathe normally.'],href:'/rituals/craft/meditation/breath',keywords:['breathing','box breathing','4-7-8','breathwork','pranayama']},{id:'meditation-log',title:'Log your sits and see their patterns',summary:'Note the kind of practice, how settled you felt and what came up, then see your streak, minutes and what helps you settle.',steps:['After a sit, tap "Keep it in your log", or open Meditation and tap "Log a sit".','Choose the kind of practice, how settled you felt from 1 to 5, and write what came up. Tags mark images, messages, a deity or spirit, emotions or body sensations.','Turn on "Save to my Grimoire" to keep it as a page under Meditation.','Open "Your patterns" for your streak, minutes this week, month and year, and how settled you\u2019ve felt by time of day, weekday and moon phase.'],tips:['Tap a sit in "Your sits" to change or delete it.','On To tend, turn on "Count my meditations" for a thing of your own, and each finished sit marks it done for the day.','A daily reminder to sit is in Settings \u2192 Reminders, under your practice.','Your year in review counts your sits too.'],href:'/rituals/craft/meditation',keywords:['meditation journal','meditation log','streak','patterns','what came up']},{id:'meditation-together',title:'Sit together with your coven or friends',summary:'A shared meditation in which everyone\u2019s timer starts at the same moment, wherever they are.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Rituals \u2192 "Rituals together" and tap "Set up a sit together".','Choose the length and bells, and when everyone begins: in a few minutes, or when the leader begins.','Tap "Open the sit for others to join" and share the link or code.','Each person\u2019s timer starts at the chosen moment and rings their own bells. When it ends, each can keep it in their log.'],tips:['Choose "A frame drum" or "Singing bowls" under "Sound for everyone, in step", and each person hears it on their own device, started from the same moment.'],href:'/rituals/together?sit=1',keywords:['group meditation','coven meditation','meditate together','sit together','shared drum']},{id:'meditation-public-sits',title:'Join or schedule a public sit',summary:'Group meditations in Community, open to anyone signed in. Everyone\u2019s timer starts at the same moment.',steps:['Open Community (from More, or Practice \u2192 Rituals) and tap "Sits".','Tap a sit coming up, then "Join the sit". When it begins, your timer starts with everyone\u2019s; open it late and it picks up where everyone is.','To lead one, tap "Schedule a sit": its name, when it begins, its length and its sound (a frame drum or bowls in step for all, or a binaural layer for headphones).'],tips:['Nothing is heard or seen of anyone, only how many are sitting.','Report, Hide and Block on a sit work as they do for Community Rituals.'],href:'/rituals/community?tab=sits',keywords:['public sit','group sit','community meditation','meditate with others','sit with strangers']},{id:'meditation-sound',title:'Sound for a sit: drone, noise, rain, drum, bowls and binaural layers',summary:'Mix your own sound under a sit: each layer at its own level, faded in as you begin and out as it ends, stopping with the timer.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Craft \u2192 "Meditation", then "Sound", and turn on "Play sound with the sit".','Set each layer to Off, Soft, Medium or Full: a drone in the key you choose, pink or brown noise, rain, wind, a fire, a frame drum, singing bowls or binaural layers.','For the frame drum choose its beats a second (3 to 7; 4.5 is the usual). On a timed sit of three minutes or more it changes to a callback near the end, to bring you back.','Singing bowls are struck every 15, 30 or 60 seconds, round the seven tones (C to B, root to crown), at 432 Hz, or both.','Tap "Begin". The mix is remembered on this device.'],tips:['Binaural layers need headphones. Research into them is mixed. Don\u2019t use them if you have epilepsy or a seizure disorder, and never while driving.','Every sound is made by us, not recorded. The tones given to the chakras are a modern crystal-bowl convention.','In the app the sound stops if you put the app away; the time keeps and the end bell still comes. In a browser, tap "Let the sound play" if it asks.'],href:'/rituals/craft/meditation',keywords:['binaural','binaural beats','drone','pink noise','brown noise','rain','drum','drumming','shamanic drum','singing bowl','432','chakra','sound bath']},{id:'meditation-guidance',title:'Guidance on screen, and presets before a ritual',summary:'A meditation given one line at a time, paced to the length of your sit, and two short presets to ground before ritual.',steps:['In Meditation, open "Guidance on screen" and choose one: Grounding & centring, Clearing, The three cauldrons, Meeting a guide, Elemental journey, Body scan or Deep rest.','Tap "Begin". Each line fades in at its turn and rests until the next.','Under "Before a ritual", "Ground & centre" (3 minutes) and "Clearing" (5 minutes) begin straight away.','In a coven ritual, choose "A timed sit for everyone" under "At the altar" on a step, and each person\u2019s step shows a button that starts that sit on their own screen.'],tips:['After a sit, the log offers questions to write to, matched to the kind of practice.'],href:'/rituals/craft/meditation',keywords:['guided meditation','script','pathworking','cauldron','yoga nidra','body scan','grounding','centring','clearing']},{id:'meditation-focus',title:'Something to look at: candle, moon, mandala or sigil',summary:'A candle flame for candle gazing, the moon as she is tonight, a mandala, or one of your saved sigils turning slowly, full screen if you like.',steps:['In Meditation, open "Something to look at" and choose one. For a sigil, pick which of your saved sigils.','Tap "Begin", then "Fill the screen". Tap anywhere to close it.'],tips:['Breath pacing has a wave and a square path too, beside the circle: the square suits box breathing, one side for each part.'],href:'/rituals/craft/meditation',keywords:['trataka','candle gazing','mandala','yantra','sigil','moon','focus','box breathing']},{id:'meditation-mala',title:'Count a mala, and walk',summary:'Tap anywhere for each bead of a 27, 54 or 108 mala, with a buzz for each; and walking meditation with your steps counted.',steps:['In Meditation, tap "Mala and mantra". Write the mantra or chant if you like, and choose how many beads.','Tap the space for each bead. A round ends with a stronger buzz; press and hold for the guru bead, which closes the round where you are.','Tap "Keep it in your log" to keep the mantra and the count.','For walking meditation, tap "Walking meditation". On a phone with a step counter your steps are counted, and kept in the log.'],tips:['Buzzes follow Vibration in Accessibility. Step counting asks for motion permission and isn\u2019t available in a browser.'],href:'/rituals/craft/meditation/mala',keywords:['mala','japa','mantra','chant','beads','rosary','counter','walking meditation','steps','pedometer']},{id:'meditation-listen',title:'Listen: binaural beats and sound on their own',summary:'Play binaural beats, pink or brown noise, rain, wind, fire, a drone, a frame drum or singing bowls without a sit, each at its own level, with a stop timer.',steps:['In Meditation, tap "Listen". Choose a level for each layer you want, and for binaural layers a preset (the slow descent from alpha to theta, a fixed beat, or your own beat and carrier).','Under "Stop after", choose 15, 30, 45, 60 or 90 minutes, or "Until I stop". The slow descent spans the time you choose, or 30 minutes if it plays until you stop it.','Tap "Play". It fades in; "Pause" holds it, and "Stop" fades it out. When it ends, "Keep it in your log" notes it as a Listening sit, if you like.','To use the same mix with a sit, open Sound in Meditation and tap "Use my last Listen mix".'],tips:['Binaural layers need headphones. Research into what they do is mixed; don\u2019t use them if you have epilepsy or a seizure disorder, or while driving.','Sound plays only while the screen is open: in the app it pauses if you switch away or lock the phone. It plays with the silent switch on. The last mix is remembered on each device.'],href:'/rituals/craft/meditation/listen',keywords:['binaural','binaural beats','theta','alpha','delta','white noise','pink noise','brown noise','rain sounds','sleep sounds','ambient','soundscape','listen','sound bath']},{id:'meditation-programmes',title:'Meditation programmes, and before and after',summary:'7 days of grounding, a 28-day moon cycle and Sabbat sits, with how you feel before and after each sit.',steps:['In Meditation, tap "Programmes" and "Begin day 1". Each day\u2019s sit has its focus and guidance.','The moon cycle\u2019s focus follows the moon\u2019s phase each day. Sabbat sits are one for each yearly festival in your calendars, sat on the day.','Tap "Add to To tend" to put a programme on your list with "Count my meditations" on.','Before a sit, open "What you bring to it" for an intention and how you feel (1 to 5); afterwards you\u2019re asked again. "Your patterns" shows the change.'],tips:['Programmes under way, and a Sabbat sit on a festival day, show on Today. "For today" in Meditation suggests a sit for the moon\u2019s phase, a festival, and the deities you keep.'],href:'/rituals/craft/meditation/programmes',keywords:['meditation programme','meditation course','moon cycle','sabbat','challenge','mood','before and after','intention']}]},{id:'living-library',title:'Living Library',intro:'Herbs, crystals, candles, deities, tools and vessels, with their meanings, lore and your own notes.',topics:[{id:'library-browse',title:'Browse and search the Living Library',summary:'Find an entry by name, meaning or tradition.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Grimoire and tap "Living Library".','Type in "Search the Library".','Choose a filter under "Show": All, My path, My Practice, Herbs, Crystals, Candles, Deities, Tools or Vessels.','Tap an entry to open it.'],href:'/grimoire/library',keywords:['library','herbs','crystals','deities','correspondences','lookup']},{id:'library-read-entry',title:'Read an entry in its layers',summary:'An entry shows My Practice, Traditional Information and Community layers.',steps:['Open an entry from the Library, or from an object\u2019s "About" sheet.','Read the facts at the top, then each layer in turn.','Tap a tag to jump to a related entry.','Scroll to "Connected To" and "Your Journey with" the entry.'],keywords:['traditional information','layers','my practice layer','community layer']},{id:'library-add-practice',title:'Add your own notes to an entry',summary:'My Practice sits beside the traditional information.',steps:['Sign in and open an entry.','Tap "Add to My Practice". (If you already have notes it reads "Edit My Practice".)','Fill in Meaning, Uses, Pairs With, Substitutions and Notes.','Tap "Save". To clear them, tap "Delete my practice notes".'],keywords:['personal notes','my practice','annotate','edit entry']},{id:'library-new-practice-entry',title:'Make an entry of your own',summary:'Create a custom herb, crystal, candle, deity, tool or vessel.',steps:['Sign in. Open Practice \u2192 Grimoire and tap "New Library note".','Choose a category, then type a new name in "Search the Library, or type a new name".','Tap the row that begins "Create".','Fill in your notes and tap "Create entry".'],keywords:['custom entry','add herb','new entry','library note','own deity']},{id:'library-relationships',title:'Connect entries to each other',summary:'Add your own relationships between entries.',steps:['Sign in and open an entry.','Under "Connected To", tap "Manage relationships".','Choose a relationship, search for the connected entry and tap it.','Tap "Add Relationship". Edit or delete existing ones in the same sheet.'],keywords:['link entries','related to','connections','pairs']},{id:'library-my-path',title:'Put your tradition first in the Library',summary:'My path puts the traditions you keep ahead of everything else.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Living Library".','Under "My path", choose "Follow my calendars", "Choose my own" or "Off".','If you chose your own, switch on the traditions you keep.','Optionally switch on "Hide deities from other traditions".','Each change saves itself.'],href:'/more/settings/library',keywords:['path','tradition','my path','hide deities','norse','hellenic','celtic']},{id:'library-layers-settings',title:'Choose which layers and fields the Library shows',summary:'Turn layers on and off, reorder them and choose their fields.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then "Living Library".','Under "Layer order", choose the order of My Practice, Traditional Information and Community.','Under "Show on Library pages", switch layers on or off.','Under "What each layer shows", tap a layer and switch fields such as Meanings, Uses or Warnings.','Each change saves itself.'],href:'/more/settings/library',keywords:['hide layer','fields','show warnings','order']},{id:'library-companion-panel',title:'Choose what the altar\u2019s About sheet shows',summary:'The Companion panel can copy your Library settings or use its own.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then Altar, then "About sheet".','Leave "Copy my Living Library page settings" on to match the Library, or switch it off.','If off, choose the layer order and switch on each layer and its fields.','Each change saves itself.'],href:'/more/settings/about-sheet',keywords:['about sheet','companion','altar information']},{id:'library-living-objects',title:'Choose what an object\u2019s living state shows',summary:'Statuses, dates and activity on the altar\u2019s About sheet.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then Altar, then "About sheet", and look under "Its living state".','Switch on or off rows like "Show status", "Show last tended", "Show expiration reminder" and "Show recent activity".','Each change saves itself.'],href:'/more/settings/about-sheet',keywords:['living state','tending info','about sheet fields']},{id:'library-how-traditions-shown',title:'Understand how traditions are shown',summary:'Entries show where a custom comes from; your calendars and path shape the order.',steps:['Open an entry and read its "Traditional Information" layer. It names the traditions it belongs to.','Open More, then Settings, then "Calendar & holidays" and "Living Library" to choose which traditions you keep.','The Library shows them first. Others stay available.'],keywords:['tradition labels','cultures','origins','pantheon']},{id:'library-sourcing',title:'Read about sourcing with care',summary:'Plants, resins and stones to buy thoughtfully, and what to use instead.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Grimoire, then "Living Library".','Tap "Sourcing with care".','Search the notes. Each says "Why care" and "Instead".','Tap "Open its Library page" to read the entry.'],tips:['An entry with a concern shows a "Sourcing with care" card near the top.'],href:'/grimoire/library/sourcing',keywords:['white sage','palo santo','sandalwood','ethical','endangered','sustainable']},{id:'library-closed-traditions',title:'Read the Closed & living traditions guide',summary:'What the app doesn\u2019t teach, and why.',steps:['Open Practice \u2192 Grimoire, then "Living Library", then "Closed & living traditions".','Read "What closed means and why it matters".','Search, or filter by openness, then tap a tradition.','Read its sections, "How people come in", "Myths \u2192 truth" and "How to learn".'],tips:['Tap "Send a correction" at the top of any entry to email us.'],href:'/grimoire/library/closed',keywords:['closed practice','cultural appropriation','initiatory','hoodoo','voodoo','santeria','indigenous','respect']},{id:'library-deity-journey',title:'Begin a dedication journey from a deity\u2019s page',summary:'Some deity entries offer a journey.',steps:['Open a deity\u2019s entry in the Living Library.','Tap "Begin a dedication journey".','Read the overview and tap "Begin this journey".'],keywords:['deity journey','god study']}]},{id:'covens',title:'Covens',intro:'Practise with others: find and join a coven, take part, and go through its initiation and training.',topics:[{id:'covens-mine',title:'See your covens at a glance',summary:'"My covens" holds the covens you belong to, each as a card with what is happening there.',steps:['Open the Coven tab. It opens on "My covens" when you belong to a coven, and on "Find a coven" when you don\u2019t; after that, on whichever you used last.','At the top, "Your covens" shows your turn in a rite, rites coming up and work waiting for you, as it does on Today.','Under "Covens you belong to", each coven\u2019s card shows your position there, unread messages, its next gathering and any applications or requests to advance waiting for you. Tap a card to open the coven.','Applications you have sent that are still waiting show under "Waiting to hear back".'],tips:['Pull down to bring everything up to date.'],href:'/coven?tab=mine',keywords:['my covens','my coven','unread','next gathering','position','rank','application waiting']},{id:'covens-together',title:'Do a ritual together, live',summary:'Run a ritual with your coven or friends from different places: everyone sees the same step as the leader moves on.',steps:['Open a ready-made working, one of your saved rituals or spells, or a coven gathering, and tap "Begin together".','Tap "Open the ritual for others to join". Share the link, or, for a coven gathering, everyone it is for can join from its page.','As host, tap "Light the candle together", then "Begin the ritual" and "Next step". "Pass the lead" lets someone else lead; "Take the lead back" returns it.','At the end each person taps "It is done", and can keep a note in their own ritual journal.'],tips:['Text only: no camera or microphone. Turn on "Quiet mode" to hide the chat, or, as host, "Quiet for everyone".','The host can ask someone to leave. You can report or block anyone, and you won\u2019t see messages from people you\u2019ve blocked.','Rituals together use your community profile (18+).'],href:'/rituals/together',keywords:['ritual together','live ritual','group ritual','remote','distance','online ritual','shared ritual','invite link','candle together']},{id:'covens-mentorship',title:'Find a mentor, or mentor someone',summary:'Pair an experienced witch with someone learning: a private conversation, shared goals and reading, and check-ins. Adults only, on both sides.',steps:['Open the Coven tab and tap "Mentorship".','Set up your mentorship profile: what you offer or look for, traditions and topics, and whether to show in the open directory or to your covens. Confirm you are 18 or older and agree to the boundaries.','Under "Directory", choose "Find a mentor" or "Find someone to mentor", filter by tradition and topics, and ask with a short note.','When you both say yes, the pairing opens: add goals and a reading list linked to journeys, lessons and pages, check in, and write to each other.'],tips:['In a coven, Members \u2192 "Mentorship" shows its members who mentor or are looking. Those who run its programs can suggest a pairing; it begins only if both say yes, and they see only that it exists, never what is said.','Either of you can end it at any time. Blocking someone ends any mentorship between you.'],href:'/coven/mentorship',keywords:['mentor','mentee','mentorship','teacher','student','guidance','apprentice','learn from']},{id:'covens-join',title:'Find and join a coven',summary:'Covens are for adults; each has its own creed, rules and way of joining.',steps:['Open the Coven tab and choose "Find a coven" at the top.','Tap "Make your coven profile" the first time: the name other members see, and confirming you are 18 or older.','Search under "Find a coven" and tap "Visit".','Read the coven\u2019s pages, then tap "Join this coven" or "Apply to join", sign its agreements, and answer its questions.'],tips:['Applications still waiting for an answer show under "Waiting to hear back" on "My covens".','Invited? An invitation lets you join without applying, even a coven that isn\u2019t listed. Invitations sent to you show under "Invitations" at the top of "My covens"; an invite link opens the coven\u2019s invitation, or paste it under "Have an invite?" on "Find a coven".'],href:'/coven?tab=find',keywords:['coven','join','apply','circle','group','directory','invitation','invite code']},{id:'covens-invite',title:'Invite people to your coven',summary:'Share an invite link, or invite someone in the app by name. An invitation lets them join without applying.',steps:['Open your coven and tap "Invite" (or "Manage", then "Invite people").','To share a link: under "Share an invite link", choose how long it lasts and how many people can use it, tap "Make a link", then "Share" or "Copy link".','To invite someone in the app: under "Invite someone in the app", search by the name they use in covens, tap them, add a message if you like, and tap "Send invitation". They hear about it on their phone and see it at the top of "My covens".','Links still working and invitations waiting are listed below, each with "Revoke" to take it back.','Those who lead the coven choose whether members may invite people too, under "Who may invite".'],tips:['Those who lead or review the coven can always invite; other members can when the coven\u2019s leaders turn on "Members may invite people".','Whoever joins still makes a coven profile (confirming they are 18 or older) and signs the coven\u2019s agreements first. They join at the coven\u2019s first position.','Someone removed from the coven can come back only through an invitation sent to them by name, never a link. Someone banned from it can\u2019t.','The link opens the website\u2019s invitation page, which opens the app for those who have it. Choose whether you hear when someone accepts in Settings \u2192 Reminders \u2192 Covens.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['invite','invitation','invite link','share link','add member','bring a friend','code','unlisted','revoke']},{id:'covens-found',title:'Found a coven',summary:'Start a coven of your own, with its creed, its ways of joining and its positions.',steps:['Open the Coven tab, choose "Find a coven" at the top and tap "Found a coven". Make your coven profile first if asked.','Give it a "Coven name", a "Web address", "One line about the coven" and "Who you are and how you practise", with its tradition, when you gather and tags if you like.','Choose "How witches join" (By application, Open or Not yet), whether it is Listed in the "Directory", and "Your title as leader".','Agree to lead it by the community guidelines, then tap "\u2726 Found the coven".'],tips:['Afterwards, "Manage" holds the coven\u2019s details, its creed, rules and agreements, positions, questions for applicants and practice calendar.'],href:'/coven/new',keywords:['start a coven','create coven','found','new coven','lead','high priestess']},{id:'covens-initiation',title:'Go through your coven\u2019s initiation or training',summary:'Each coven designs its own programs: stages of tasks, signed off by you, your mentor or its leaders.',steps:['Open your coven from "My covens" on the Coven tab and tap "Initiation & training".','Tap your program under "Your programs" to see each stage and its tasks.','Read the step\u2019s lessons, practise, and log what you did: "Log this session" for each practice, "Log one", "Mark done" or "Send for sign-off" for the rest. Write in the answer box when a step asks.','Steps with a test are finished by passing it. Tap "Take the test".','Your mentor or the coven\u2019s leaders sign your work off and confirm each stage. Your next task also shows on Today.'],tips:['The coven\u2019s head can sign off anyone\u2019s training, her own included: she signs off her own steps, scores her own written answers, confirms her own stages and finishes her own program. Each step shows who signed it off. Mentors and those who manage programs never sign off their own. See "Sign off someone\u2019s training".','Each step has its own conversation with your mentor and the coven\u2019s leaders: tap "Talk with \u2026 about this step".','Practice steps count your sessions ("4 of 10 sessions"). Timed ones have a timer: "Start the timer", then "Use these minutes" before you log.'],keywords:['initiation','training','degree','year and a day','mentor','lessons','program','dedicant','practice','log','session','timer']},{id:'covens-course-lessons',title:'Course lessons and tests',summary:'Read each step\u2019s lessons, then take its test. Choice questions are scored at once; written answers by your mentor.',steps:['Open your program from "Initiation & training" and find the step. Its lessons are listed under it: tap one to read it.','Each lesson says about how long it takes. When you\u2019ve read it, tap "Mark as read", then "Next" for the step\u2019s next lesson.','On a step with a test, tap "Take the test", then "Begin the test". Answer one question at a time, or tap "The whole test" to see them all.','Your answers are kept on your device as you go. Tap "Hand it in" when you\u2019re done.','Choice questions are scored straight away. Written answers wait for your mentor or the coven\u2019s leaders. Your result shows your score and which questions you got right, with your mentor\u2019s points and comments on the written answers.','The right answers and their explanations open to you once you\u2019ve passed the test, on every attempt you made at it.'],tips:['You pass when your score reaches the test\u2019s pass mark (usually 80%), and the step is then done.','If you don\u2019t pass, look at the questions you missed, go back over the lessons, ask your mentor, and take it again after the wait (usually a day). Each test allows a few attempts; the coven\u2019s leaders can allow one more.','Every attempt is kept under "Your attempts".'],href:'/coven',keywords:['lesson','lessons','read','test','quiz','exam','score','pass','retake','mark as read','course','reading time']},{id:'covens-score-test',title:'Scoring a test',summary:'Mentors and those who manage programs score the written answers, with points and a comment on each.',steps:['Open "Initiation & training". Tests waiting for you are under "Waiting for you": tap "Score: \u2026".','The choice questions are already scored. For each written answer, read it against the guide ("What a full answer includes"), give its points and a comment.','Add a note on the whole test if you like, then tap "Give the result". The score, and whether it passes, show as you type.','Or tap "Save for later" to come back to it; the trainee still sees it waiting.'],tips:['A pass marks the step done. A trainee who doesn\u2019t pass sees their score, which questions they got right and your comments, and can try again after the wait. The right answers and explanations open to them once they pass.','If you\u2019re taking the same test yourself and haven\u2019t passed it, your mentee\u2019s attempts show without the answers: you can still score their written answers.','The coven\u2019s head can score anyone\u2019s test, her own included, and allow herself another attempt. Mentors and those who manage programs can\u2019t score their own.','Those who manage programs can tap "Allow one more attempt" on a test whose attempts are used up.','Change a test\u2019s questions, pass mark, retakes and wait under "Lessons and tests". Attempts already made keep the questions as they were.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['score','scoring','mark','grade','test','quiz','rubric','written answer','mentor','retake']},{id:'covens-sign-off-training',title:'Sign off someone\u2019s training',summary:'Sign off a step, pass a stage or score a test for those you oversee. The coven\u2019s head can sign off anyone\u2019s, her own included.',steps:['Open the Coven tab, tap your coven, then "Review". "Training to sign off" at the top lists work sent for sign-off, stages ready to pass and written answers to score. Tap one to open it.','Or open "Members", tap their name, and under "Training" tap their program to open their path.','On a step sent for sign-off, add a note if you like and tap "Sign it off" or "Send back". On any other unfinished step, tap "Sign it off" to sign it off directly, without waiting for them to send it.','When every task in the stage is signed off, tap "Confirm the stage is passed" (or "Confirm they\u2019ve finished" on the last stage). Those who manage programs and the head can also "Pass the stage early".','For a test, tap "Score: \u2026", give each written answer its points, then "Give the result".'],tips:['The coven\u2019s head can sign off anyone\u2019s training, her own included: on her own path she sees "You\u2019re the coven\u2019s head, so you can sign off your own steps." Mentors and those who manage programs never sign off their own.','Each step shows who signed it off, and whether it was signed off directly. The head\u2019s own sign-offs say so.','The coven\u2019s page shows "Initiation & training" with how many are waiting to sign off, and "Review" counts them too.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['sign off','signoff','approve','check off','pass stage','graduate','complete','progress','high priestess','head','own training','mentor']},{id:'covens-training-talk',title:'Talking with your trainee',summary:'Every step of every program has its own conversation between the trainee and those who oversee them.',steps:['On a step, tap "Talk with \u2026 about this step". From a test\u2019s result, tap "Talk about your result".','Write your message and tap "Send". It stays with that step, so the context is always there.','Mentors: "Waiting for you" lists new messages from those you mentor, and a "Message" button beside work waiting for sign-off.'],tips:['Only the trainee, their mentor, those who manage the coven\u2019s programs and the coven\u2019s head read a step\u2019s conversation. No one else in the coven does.','"Initiation & training" on the coven\u2019s page counts new messages. Choose whether they reach your phone with "Training messages" in Settings \u2192 Reminders \u2192 Covens.','You can remove a message you wrote.'],href:'/more/settings/notifications?section=covens',keywords:['message','conversation','thread','trainee','mentor','ask','question','training messages','notification']},{id:'covens-lead-programs',title:'Design initiation and training for your coven',summary:'Start from a ready-made program for your coven\u2019s calendar, or make your own, with lessons and tests on its steps.',steps:['Open your coven, then "Initiation & training" and "Design and assign" (those the coven\u2019s head allows).','Under "Start a program", ready-made paths come first: Seeker \u2192 Devotee \u2192 Initiate \u2192 Elder \u2192 High Priestess. Tap "Use this" on one, or "Use all five" for the whole path. Each is copied as a draft, with its lessons and tests.','Or tap "Make your own initiation". Add stages and tasks, choose who signs each off, and add lessons and a test to a task. Save.','Open the program, tap "Assign", and choose a person or a whole position. Choose mentors under "Mentors".','The coven\u2019s head chooses who manages programs and who sees everyone\u2019s progress in Manage \u2192 "Who runs training", or on a position.'],tips:['Each ready-made program raises those who finish it to a position, matched to your coven\u2019s own. The coven\u2019s head can change it before copying, or later in the program.','Finishing keeps to the position\u2019s places: when it\u2019s full, or others are already waiting for it, the graduate joins its waiting list instead, in the order they finished. See "Waiting lists for positions".','"Lessons and tests" holds the coven\u2019s own copies: change any lesson or test, write new ones, and add a PDF or a picture to a lesson. Only the coven\u2019s members can read them.'],keywords:['design program','assign','mentor','high priestess','leader','progress','template','ready-made','lessons','tests','course','path']},{id:'covens-calendar',title:'Set your coven\u2019s practice calendar',summary:'The holidays the coven keeps, as you choose your own in Settings.',steps:['Open your coven, tap "Manage", then "Practice calendar".','Tick the calendars the coven keeps, and choose single holidays if you only keep some.','Add the coven\u2019s own days, then tap "Save the calendar".'],keywords:['coven calendar','holidays','sabbats','festivals','practice calendar']},{id:'covens-moon-calendar',title:'Set the coven\u2019s calendar',summary:'How the coven counts its days: the moon\u2019s months, its new year and the calendars beside the date.',steps:['Open your coven, tap "Manage", then "Practice calendar".','Under "How the coven counts its days", choose Standard or The moon.','Tick the calendars the coven keeps beside the date, such as the Attic (Athenian) calendar.','Choose the moon\u2019s month names, where the year begins (as the Attic calendar, for one, when the coven shows it) and what a Blue Moon is.','Tap "Save how the coven counts".'],tips:['Those who manage the coven set it, and the head of a mother coven too.','Members see it on the coven\u2019s page under "What the coven follows". It never changes anyone\u2019s own settings unless they choose to take it.'],keywords:['coven calendar','moon calendar','lunar calendar','new year','attic','hellenic','count days','coven moon']},{id:'covens-follow-calendar',title:'Follow your coven\u2019s calendar',summary:'See how your coven counts its days, and take it for your own if you like.',steps:['Open your coven. Under "What the coven follows" are its calendars and its moon calendar in plain words, with today\u2019s date by the coven\u2019s count.','Tap "Use the coven\u2019s calendar for my own" to see what would change in your Settings, then "Yes, use it". Or tap "Keep my own".','Changed your mind? Tap "Put back my own calendar" to have your settings as they were.'],tips:['Calendars you already show are kept; the coven\u2019s are added.','If the coven changes its calendar later, you are asked whether to update yours. Nothing changes by itself.','Gatherings show their date by the coven\u2019s moon count too, when it differs from yours.'],keywords:['coven calendar','follow coven','moon calendar','use coven calendar','keep my own','undo','new year']},{id:'covens-altars',title:'Tend your coven\u2019s altars together',summary:'Each coven altar is a whole altar, like your own, that everyone sees change as it happens.',steps:['Open your coven and tap "Altars". The ritual altar is first; members can start more.','Or open the Altar tab and choose "Coven" at the top: every coven altar you can see, under each coven\u2019s name, the ritual altar first. Tap "Start a coven altar" to start one; if you\u2019re in more than one coven, it asks which first.','Open one to tend it with the cabinet, candles, offerings and workings, as at your own altar. Who else is there shows at the top.','If you can only watch, the altar says why: a ritual step that isn\u2019t yours, or a keeper who chose others to tend it.','Changes save for the coven by themselves: the line over the altar\u2019s name says "Saving\u2026", then "Saved \u2713".','Tap \u2922 by the altar\u2019s name (or "Full screen" among its tools) to fill the screen. Tap "Done" to come back.','At the bottom, "Messages" and, while a rite is under way, "Ritual" open one small panel over the altar. Tap "Hide" to fold it back to its slim bar; the altar above stays in view and you can keep tending it.','"Keep a copy" saves it among your own altars. Keepers choose who tends it under "Who tends it".'],href:'/altar?tab=coven',keywords:['coven altar','shared altar','ritual altar','tend together','keeper','who tends','save','full screen','coven tab','start a coven altar']},{id:'covens-chat',title:'Message your coven, or one person in it',summary:'Talk with the whole coven, one to one, or in a small group, without sharing phone numbers.',steps:['Tap "Messages" on any coven screen. The coven\u2019s chat is first, then your conversations.','Tap "New message" and choose one person for a one-to-one chat, or several for a group.','Under "Phone notifications", tap "Notification settings \u203a" to choose whether the coven\u2019s chat and your conversations notify your phone (Settings \u2192 Reminders \u2192 Covens). Mute one conversation from its \u24d8 button.','Press and hold a message (on the website, tap or hover it and tap "React") to react: \ud83d\udd6f\ufe0f \ud83c\udf19 \u2728 \ud83d\udd25 \ud83d\ude4f \u2764\ufe0f \ud83d\ude02 \ud83d\udc4d, or "More" for any emoji. Tap a reaction under a message to add or take back yours, and its number to see who.','From the same place, "Remove, report or block\u2026" reports a message, blocks its writer, or removes your own.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['chat','message','talk','gathering','unread','phone number','direct message','dm','group','notifications','mute','react','reaction','emoji']},{id:'covens-reply-buttons',title:'Ask with reply buttons, and remind the coven before a gathering',summary:'Buttons under a message that people tap to answer, with a tally, and a reminder posted in Messages before a gathering begins.',steps:['Above the message box, tap "Add reply buttons" and choose "Gathering" (Coming \xb7 Running late \xb7 Can\u2019t make it), "Yes / No", or "Custom" with two to four labels of your own. Then write and send the message.','In the coven\u2019s chat, Gathering buttons can be linked to one of the coven\u2019s upcoming gatherings: then Coming and Running late also set that person\u2019s RSVP to going, and Can\u2019t make it to not going.','Under the message, a tally such as "Coming 5 \xb7 Late 1 \xb7 Can\u2019t 2" shows how people answered. Tap it to see who. Tap another button to change your answer, or yours again to take it back.','When planning a gathering, under Details choose "Post a reminder in Messages before it starts": 10, 15 or 30 minutes, or an hour, before. A gentle reminder then appears in the coven\u2019s chat, from whoever planned it, with the Gathering buttons linked to it.','In Settings \u2192 Reminders \u2192 Covens, "Reactions to my messages" (off at first) and "Answers to my reply buttons" (on at first) choose what reaches your phone. Answers are gathered into one note every few minutes.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['reply buttons','quick reply','poll','yes no','coming','running late','rsvp','reminder','gentle reminder','answers','tally','reactions']},{id:'covens-reading',title:'Draw a reading together as a coven',summary:'A card for the coven as a whole, and one for each member who joins, laid out together in the chat.',steps:['Open "Messages" and the coven\u2019s chat, or a conversation.','Tap "Begin a coven reading", say what it\u2019s about if you like, and tap "Draw the coven\u2019s card and share it".','The reading shows in the chat with the coven\u2019s card in the middle. Each member taps "Draw my card" to draw their own into it; up to nine can join, and no card comes up twice.','Tap a card for its meaning.'],tips:['Each card is also a message in the chat, so it reads plainly anywhere.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['coven reading','group reading','tarot together','shared spread','draw together','coven tarot']},{id:'covens-rituals',title:'Plan and hold a rite with your coven',summary:'Rites with steps for each person, held together on the coven\u2019s altar.',steps:['Open your coven, then "Rituals and rites". Those who can lead rituals tap "Plan a ritual".','Name it, add its intention and what members should know or bring, choose an occasion and a day from "Coming moons and holidays", then add its steps. Each step asks five things in turn: what happens (one line), "Who does it?" (one at a time, everyone together, or one person), "At the altar" (one choice, and the items to place), "What to do" (with its words), and "Who moves it on" (the leader unless you choose someone else). "Copy steps from one of your rituals" starts from your own.','Tap "Read it through", then "What members will see", to read the pop-up each step will show everyone. Anything worth a second look (a candle spoken of but none placed, turns for a role no one plays yet) shows under the outline.','"At the altar" is one choice, as a kind of step or within any step: something each person does for real at the coven\u2019s altar (write a petition, an intention or a gratitude note, make an offering, pour a libation, place an item, charge water, light a candle, burn incense, anoint and dress or carve a candle, draw a card, scry, charge a crystal, make a spell jar or sachet, ring the bell, burn, bury or release a petition, tie and burn a cord), something asked of each person in the ritual (a vow, an ancestor\u2019s name, a question, a reflection, a candle of their own), or what the altar does by itself (a candle lit, every candle put out, the papers released). During the ritual a step done at the altar shows a button that opens the same writer, picker or candle there, and doing it counts as your Done.','Tap "Plan the ritual", then "Put it on the calendar" when it is ready.','Members answer "Will you be there?": Going, Maybe or Can\u2019t make it. When it begins, tap "Join the ritual"; when a step is yours, "Open the ritual" shows on the coven\u2019s page.','Whoever leads taps "Start the ritual", moves with "Skip to the next step" or "Back a step", and finishes with "End the ritual".'],keywords:['coven ritual','group ritual','rite','esbat','sabbat','rsvp','circle','plan ritual','who moves it on','what members will see','at the altar','petition at the altar','ring the bell']},{id:'covens-ritual-steps',title:'Follow each step of a coven rite',summary:'Everyone stays at the coven\u2019s altar: each step lives in the Ritual panel along the bottom, which opens by itself when a step begins or your turn comes.',steps:['While a rite is under way, everyone stays on the coven\u2019s altar. Opening the ritual from anywhere else takes you to its altar once; everything else happens there.','As each step begins, the Ritual panel opens by itself with a soft chime: "Step 2 of 7", its name, whose turn it is, how to do it, the words to speak, and who moves the circle on. It takes no more than about a third of the screen, so the altar stays in view and can be tended while it is open.','Fold it down with "Hide" and its bar keeps the step in a line, like "Step 3 \xb7 Your turn: Call the quarters". Tap the bar, the Ritual tab, or "under way here" at the top of the altar to open it again.','How to: the planner\u2019s own directions when they wrote them, otherwise a plain how-to for that kind of step (which thing to tap on the altar, and what to do).','Things to place show as tiles: tap one to set it on the altar, then move it where it belongs on the altar itself. They tick off as they go down.','Candles, the circle, the quarters, the chalice, the bell, the singing bowl, the besom and the other tools: what to tap glows on the altar for the person whose turn it is (on a step done together, for everyone doing it; never for those watching). Doing it there counts as your Done. "Show me" begins it for you, and "Cast it for me" still draws the circle when there is no athame or wand.','A petition is written in the panel and placed straight on the altar; an intention, gratitude note, card, spell jar or sachet opens the altar\u2019s own sheet over the altar. A card drawn or the pendulum\u2019s answer shows in the panel.','A sit (Ground & centre, Clearing, Candle gazing) runs in the panel for everyone at once, from the moment the leader starts the step, never before: the clock, the guidance, a breath circle, bells and sound, as you choose in Settings \u2192 Covens & privacy \u2192 During coven rituals. Candle gazing looks at the lit candle on the altar, which glows for you.','One at a time: when it is your turn the panel opens on your part. Tap "I\u2019ve done my part" to pass to the next person.','The quarters: while a quarters step is under way, each quarter\u2019s spot shows faint and unlit at its edge of the altar (North at the back, East to the right), and tapping a spot calls that quarter, or releases it on a release step. A step for one quarter ("Call the East", "Release the North") glows that quarter alone for whoever does it.','Calling the quarters one at a time: the planner chooses who calls each quarter and the words for each, and the ritual\u2019s order (which quarter first; East, South, West, North unless they chose otherwise). The panel takes them in turn ("Your turn: call the East") with your own words, and only your quarter glows for you. Tapping it calls it and passes the turn. Release goes in reverse of the ritual\u2019s order.','Everyone together: tap "Done" when you have finished (or "Not yet" to take it back). The step is finished when everyone here has tapped Done, or when its time runs out.','One person: the step is finished when they tap "Done". Items to place tick off as each goes on the coven altar.','When the step is finished, the panel opens for the one who moves it on (the leader, unless the planner chose someone) with "Move to the next step?". Everyone else sees whom they are waiting for. They can tap "Move on anyway" sooner.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['ritual step','your turn','done','move on','pop-up','ritual panel','one at a time','together','leader','live ritual','glow','sit in a ritual','candle gazing','during coven rituals','call the quarters','call the east','quarter order','release the quarters']},{id:'covens-book',title:'Write in your coven\u2019s Book of Shadows',summary:'The coven\u2019s own pages, approved before they go in.',steps:['Open your coven, then "Book of Shadows". Tap a page to read it.','Tap "Write a page", give it a title, a section and the page, then tap "Send for approval" or "Save as a draft".','To change a page, open it and tap "Suggest a change".','Those who approve pages tap "Approve" or "Send back" under "Waiting for approval".'],keywords:['coven book','shared grimoire','coven pages','book of shadows']},{id:'covens-petitions',title:'Ask your coven to hold a petition',summary:'Each petition gets its own altar, and the coven tends it while it\u2019s open.',steps:['Open your coven and tap "Petitions", then "Ask the circle".','Name what the circle should hold, add more if you like, and choose its candle\u2019s colour.','Its altar has your candle lit with the petition folded at its foot. Tap "Open its altar" to visit it.','Tap "Tend it" (once every twelve hours) to light a candle in your name beside it.','When it\u2019s done, the person who asked taps "It was answered" or "Close it", and its altar is archived.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['petition','prayer request','hold','tend','candle','circle']},{id:'covens-shelf',title:'Keep the coven\u2019s things on a shared shelf',summary:'What the coven owns together, who holds it, where it\u2019s kept, what\u2019s running low and what needs cleansing.',steps:['Open your coven and tap "Shared shelf", then "Add something".','Name it, choose its shelf and how much there is, who holds it (or the coven\u2019s store) and where it\u2019s kept.','Turn on "Running low" or "Needs cleansing" when it does; "Cleansed today" clears it.','Whoever added a thing or holds it can change it; those who lead the coven\u2019s rites can change anything.'],tips:['A rite\u2019s steps say when the coven already has an item they use, and who holds it.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['coven shelf','shared inventory','coven supplies','who has the chalice','running low','cleansing']},{id:'covens-rota',title:'Share the duties with a rota',summary:'Who brings the candles, calls the quarters, hosts and clears up, turning from one gathering to the next.',steps:['Those who lead the coven\u2019s rites open the coven, tap "Duties rota", then "Add a duty".','Name the duty, choose which gatherings it turns at and the people it turns among, in order.','Each gathering goes to the next person in turn. Someone who answers "Can\u2019t make it" is passed over that once.','Your duty shows on Today, on the coven\u2019s home and on the gathering\u2019s page. To swap, open the gathering, tap "Ask someone to swap", choose who, and (if they have a duty that day) offer to take theirs in return.','The one asked accepts or declines from the gathering\u2019s page or the rota. Leaders can reassign a duty for one gathering.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['rota','duties','who brings','quarter calls','host','clean up','swap']},{id:'covens-year',title:'Look back on the coven\u2019s year',summary:'Gatherings held, sabbats kept, who joined, pages added and what went on the altar, to share as text.',steps:['Open your coven and tap "Year in review". In December and January it is offered on the coven\u2019s home too.','Choose the year at the top. Tap "Share as text" or "Copy" to pass it on.'],tips:['Everyone\u2019s attendance shows only to those who keep the coven\u2019s record; anyone else sees their own. Nothing comes from anyone\u2019s journal.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['year in review','coven year','wrapped','summary','look back','share']},{id:'covens-record',title:'Keep track of who is taking part',summary:'The members\u2019 record: every rite each member came to, their studies and their mentoring, for the coven\u2019s head and those they choose.',steps:['Open your coven and tap "Members", then "Members\u2019 record".','Everyone is listed least active first, with how many rituals they came to, when they last took part, their studies and their mentor. Choose how far back to look, and narrow it to positions or people under "Only these".','Tap someone for every ritual since they joined, whether they were there, sent word or were excused, their studies, their mentoring, and private notes only the record\u2019s keepers read.','Someone counts as there when they open the ritual while it\u2019s under way. Tap "Was there in person" or "Wasn\u2019t there" to correct it, and "Excuse the absence" when they sent word.','The coven\u2019s head chooses who else keeps the record, and whether mentees read their mentor\u2019s check-ins, at the foot of the record.'],tips:['Every member sees their own under My standing \u2192 "Your record", without the leaders\u2019 notes. Mentors log their check-ins there too.','The record never shows what anyone wrote, or their one-to-one and group conversations: only counts and kinds.'],keywords:['attendance','participation','record','standing','inactive','revoke membership','remove member','mentor check-in','excused','can\u2019t make it']},{id:'covens-paths',title:'See the paths in your coven',summary:'What share of the coven practises each way, keeps each path and honours each deity as patron or otherwise, never who.',steps:['Open your coven: "Paths in the coven" is on the coven\u2019s page, under "The coven", for its head, those who keep the members\u2019 record, and everyone once the head shows it to the whole coven.','Each bar is a share of those who have said: how they practise (Settings \u2192 Your crafts), their path (Settings \u2192 Living Library \u2192 My path) and their deities (Settings \u2192 My deities), as patrons, as deities dedicated to, and honoured in any way.','The coven\u2019s head always sees it, as do those who keep the members\u2019 record. The head can switch on "Show it to the whole coven" at the foot of it.'],tips:['It never shows who keeps what. Anything fewer than three share is gathered under "Other (fewer than 3)", and nothing shows until five members have shared.','To be left out of every coven\u2019s count, open Settings \u2192 Covens & privacy and turn off "Count me in my covens\u2019 paths overview".'],keywords:['paths','traditions','patron','deities','percentage','green witch','overview','anonymous','privacy','statistics']},{id:'covens-powers',title:'Decide what each position in your coven can do',summary:'The coven\u2019s head decides who can do everything: positions carry the powers.',steps:['Open your coven, tap "Manage", then "Positions".','Make a position or open one, and tick what it can do: lead rituals, moderate, start, tend or keep altars, talk in the chat, manage initiation and training, and more.','Give people their positions from "Members". The head always has every power.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['positions','roles','powers','permissions','access','high priestess','leader']},{id:'covens-review-members',title:'Review applications and look after members',summary:'Approve who joins and who rises, and keep the gathering safe.',steps:['Open your coven and tap "Review": approve or decline "Applications to join" and "Requests to advance", with a note if you like. The number on the Coven tab and beside "Review" is how many are waiting.','Tap "Members" on the coven\u2019s page, and tap a person to change their position, pause their messages, or remove or ban them.','The coven\u2019s head can hand on leadership from the same place: tap the person, then "Hand on leadership", and choose what you keep. By default you become Elder (or keep your position without the power to lead); or step down to a position you choose. Only one person leads the coven.'],tips:['Each request to advance shows what the position asks, checked as it stands now (\u2713 met, \u2717 not yet, \u25cb for you to decide), their answers to its questions, and how many places are left.','Tick what you confirm, and their mentor\u2019s approval if you\u2019re their mentor or one of the coven\u2019s leaders, before tapping "Approve". While the position is full, tap "Approve: add to the waiting list" instead; they\u2019re told, and take their turn when a place frees.','When a place frees in a full position, a card on Review says who is next in line. Nobody is moved until the coven\u2019s head or a leader confirms it.','The head has no "Leave" button: hand on leadership first. Name who leads next under Manage \u2192 "Leadership" (see "Name a successor").'],keywords:['applications','approve','decline','members','ban','remove member','pause','hand on','leader','checklist','requirements']},{id:'covens-daughter',title:'Found a daughter coven',summary:'Hive off a new coven from yours. It runs itself day to day under its own High Priestess, and the mother coven\u2019s head has final say over it.',steps:['Open your coven and tap "Daughter covens" (under "The coven"), then "Found a daughter coven". It\u2019s there when your position allows it (on for the leading position and Elder) or the head has named you.','Give the new coven a name and address, and choose what carries across from your coven: the creed, rules and agreements, positions and their powers, initiation and training programs, the Book sections shared with daughters, ritual templates, and the practice calendar.','Choose what becomes of your place in your coven: stay as you are, become a visitor (you stay in its chat, rites and Book, without a position or powers), or leave.','Tap "Ask to found it". The head of your coven approves it, choosing who leads it (usually you) and what carries across. When the head founds one, it\u2019s founded at once.','The new coven shows "Hived from \u2026" and your coven lists it under "Daughter covens", each linked for those who may see it.'],tips:['Nothing personal ever comes across: no members, signatures, records, messages, attendance, progress, or altars with members\u2019 things on them. Agreements arrive as drafts, for the new coven to adopt.','Everyone who joins a daughter coven is told first, on its page, on the join screen, in invitations and in its member agreement, that it is a daughter coven and whose final say it is under.','The mother coven\u2019s head (and the head of any coven above it) has every power in the daughter: they can change anything there, and choose or change its High Priestess. Each change they make is kept in the daughter\u2019s lineage log, and its High Priestess is told. Members\u2019 private things stay private from them, as from the coven\u2019s own head.','That final say belongs to whoever heads the mother coven at the time: when the mother coven\u2019s leadership is handed on, it passes to its new head.','Only the mother coven\u2019s head can end the link and release a daughter to stand on its own. The daughter\u2019s High Priestess can ask, under "Daughter covens" \u2192 "Ask to be released"; the mother coven\u2019s head approves or declines. Once released, the mother coven\u2019s head has no say there.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['daughter coven','hive','hiving','found','new coven','mother coven','lineage','release','independent','final say']},{id:'covens-share-daughters',title:'Share with your daughter covens',summary:'Mark what your daughter covens may copy in, and push an update over a daughter\u2019s copy when you need to.',steps:['Open your coven, tap "Daughter covens", then "Share with your daughter covens". (For the coven\u2019s head.)','Switch on what daughters may copy: pages, positions, programs, Book sections and pages, ritual templates and the practice calendar. They show as "Shared with daughter covens".','In a daughter coven, its leaders open "Daughter covens", then "From your mother coven", and tap "Copy in". When something changes in the mother coven, it says so; "Copy again" adds a new copy beside theirs, never over it.','To push an update into a daughter, choose the daughter at the top, then "Push\u2026" beside something shared. You see what will change first; then "Push this update" overwrites the daughter\u2019s copy. Its High Priestess is told, and it\u2019s kept in its log.'],tips:['The records and minutes shelves, and pages kept to some members, are never shared.','Each copy says where it came from: "Copied from \u2026", and "From \u2026\u2019s Book" on Book pages.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['share','daughter coven','copy','library','mother coven','push update','book of shadows','templates','programs']},{id:'covens-successor',title:'Name a successor',summary:'Say who leads the coven next, and a second, so the coven is never left without a head.',steps:['Open your coven, tap "Manage", then "Leadership".','Under "Succession plan", choose a successor and, if you like, a second, and tap "Save the plan". They\u2019re told.','If you close your account, the coven goes to your successor (or the second). With no one named, it goes to the most senior member in a leading position; with no one at all, it\u2019s archived and its members are told.','If you go quiet and can\u2019t be reached, the coven\u2019s elders can tap "The head can\u2019t be reached" on the coven\u2019s page. It goes to the site moderators, who see the plan and decide.'],tips:['For a daughter coven, its High Priestess or the mother coven\u2019s head sets the plan; the mother coven\u2019s head can always change it.','Under "Leadership" you also choose which positions may ask to found a daughter coven, and name people who may.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['successor','succession','next leader','heir','step down','hand on','unreachable','head gone','delete account']},{id:'covens-request-notes',title:'Hear about new applications and answers',summary:'A note on your phone when someone asks to join or advance in a coven you review, and when your own is answered.',steps:['Open Settings \u2192 Reminders, then "Covens". A coven\u2019s "Review" and "Messages" have a "Notification settings \u203a" link to the same page.','Under each coven you review, switch on "New applications". "Tell me about new applications" under "Every coven" turns them all on or off.','Switch on "When my own is answered" to hear back about your application or your request to advance. A tap opens the coven.','These come as coven notifications: "On this phone" at the top says whether this phone gets them, and turns them on or off.'],tips:['The website shows the same counts on a coven\u2019s Review tab and your covens list while the page is open, and keeps the same choices under Reminders.','Pausing reminders pauses these too.'],href:'/more/settings/notifications?section=covens',keywords:['applications','notification','coven requests','advance','approved','declined','badge','count','review']},{id:'covens-my-path',title:'Sign agreements, rise to a higher position, or leave',summary:'Your place in a coven, from its page.',steps:['Open your coven and tap "My standing".','Under "Agreements", tap "Read and sign" for any the coven asks of you.','Under "Rise to a higher position", "Open positions" shows each position open to you, with its places left, when applications close and what it asks: \u2713 for what you\u2019ve met, \u2717 for what you haven\u2019t yet, \u25cb for what the reviewer decides.','When nothing is marked \u2717, tap "Apply for" the position, answer its questions, say why you\u2019re ready, and tap "Send my application". The coven\u2019s reviewers decide.','Under "Leaving", tap the button to leave the coven.'],tips:['Open positions also show on the coven\u2019s home. Choose whether you hear when one opens in Settings \u2192 Reminders \u2192 Covens, under "Positions opening".','One request at a time. While it waits, its checklist shows under "Rise to a higher position".','If you\u2019re on a position\u2019s waiting list, My standing says where: "You\u2019re 2nd in line for Initiate". Tap "Leave the waiting list" to take yourself off it.'],keywords:['advance','degree','position','agreements','sign','leave coven','my standing','my path','record','open position','apply for a position']},{id:'covens-open-position',title:'Open a position for applications',summary:'Say how many may hold a position, open it for applications, and choose who hears.',steps:['Open your coven, tap "Manage", then "Positions", and tap the position.','Under "Places", write how many may hold it (leave it empty for no limit) and tap "Save places". You see who holds it now and how many places are left.','Under "Open for applications", add a note saying why it\u2019s open and, if you like, the date applications close.','Choose who hears that it\u2019s open: everyone who could apply, only those who already meet what it asks, or no one. Then tap "Open for applications".','To stop taking applications, tap "Close applications". Requests already waiting stay for the reviewers to decide.'],tips:['The positions list shows each one as "Open \xb7 2 of 3 places", "Full" or "Closed".','When the last place is filled, the position closes by itself. A request still waiting then can be approved onto its waiting list, or given more places, or declined.','A full position keeps a waiting list under "Waiting list" on its screen. See "Waiting lists for positions".','You can lower the places below those who hold it now. Nobody loses their position; it shows as over the limit, and no one new is given it until there\u2019s room.','Changing an open position\u2019s note or date tells no one again. Those who have turned off "Positions opening", or who have blocked you, aren\u2019t told.','Only the coven\u2019s leaders open and close positions.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['open position','vacancy','places','seats','limit','applications','close applications','deadline','high priestess','notify']},{id:'covens-position-queue',title:'Waiting lists for positions',summary:'When a position is full, those who qualify wait in line, and the coven\u2019s head confirms each move up.',steps:['Someone joins a position\u2019s waiting list when they finish a program that raises them to it while it\u2019s full, or when a reviewer taps "Approve: add to the waiting list" on their request. They\u2019re in line in the order they qualified, and told where they are.','When a place frees (someone leaves, is removed or moves to another position, or you give it more places), the next in line is proposed. The coven\u2019s head and those who manage the coven get a notification, and a card on Review: "A place is free in Initiate. Rowan is next in line."','On the card, tap "Promote" to give them the place, "Choose someone else" to pick another from the list or any member who could hold it, or "Not now" to keep the place empty for the moment.','To see and change a list, open your coven, tap "Manage", then "Positions", and tap the position. Under "Waiting list", move people up or down, add someone, or take someone off with the reason.'],tips:['Nobody is moved up without the head or a leader confirming it.','Choosing someone else keeps the person proposed in their place in line, unless you tick "Take them off the list" and say why.','Anyone who leaves the coven, or is no longer in good standing (an agreement unsigned, paused, or banned from the site), is taken off the list when their turn comes.','Everything done to a list, and by whom, is kept under "What happened" on the position\u2019s screen.','Members see their place on My standing and can leave the list themselves. Notifications come under "Coven requests".'],href:'/coven',keywords:['waiting list','queue','in line','full','places','seats','promote','next in line','graduate','vacancy','high priestess']},{id:'covens-position-requirements',title:'Set requirements for a position',summary:'Choose what a position asks of those who apply, and the questions they answer.',steps:['Open your coven, tap "Manage", then "Positions", and tap the position.','Under "What it asks", tap a kind to add it: time in the coven, time in a position (such as Dedicant for a year and a day), holds a position, rites attended, a program completed, a page signed, their mentor\u2019s approval, or something in your words.','Choose the details for each: the position, how long, how many rites, which program or page.','Under "Questions for those who apply", add any questions, and tick "Required" for those they must answer.','Tap "Save what it asks".'],tips:['The coven checks time, positions, rites, programs and pages from its own record. Someone can apply only once each of those is met.','Their mentor\u2019s approval and anything in your words are ticked by whoever decides the request, on Review. Only their mentor or the coven\u2019s leaders give the mentor\u2019s approval.','What you write under "What it asks, in your own words" still shows, as "In their words", beside the checklist.'],href:'/coven',keywords:['requirements','prerequisites','year and a day','dedicant','rites attended','mentor approval','questions','checklist','eligibility']},{id:'covens-moderation',title:'Moderate covens (Salt & Sovereignty moderators)',summary:'Reports, every coven, site bans and moderators.',steps:['Open the Coven tab and tap "Coven moderation".','Work through Reports: mark them reviewing, resolved or dismissed, remove a reported message, ban someone from all covens, or pause a coven.','Open, pause or archive any coven under Covens, and lift bans under Site bans.','Under "Heads gone", see covens whose elders say their head can\u2019t be reached: how long the head has been away, its succession plan and who leads with them. "Hand it on" gives the coven to the person you choose (the named successor first), or close the report without changing anything.'],tips:['A daughter coven\u2019s mother coven head can also choose who leads it. Moderators can still release a daughter coven from its mother to keep someone safe.'],href:'/coven/moderation',keywords:['moderation','reports','ban','pause coven','moderator','safety']}]},{id:'community',title:'Community',intro:'Pages shared by others, and a way to offer your own.',topics:[{id:'community-browse',title:'Read the Community Grimoire',summary:'Browse pages the community has shared.',steps:['Open More, tap "Community" and choose Writings.','Search by title, tag or keyword, and use "Filter by type".','Tap a page to read it.'],href:'/more/community',keywords:['community pages','shared grimoire','offerings','stories']},{id:'community-field-note',title:'Add a Field Note to a community page',summary:'Share an outcome, substitution, question or reflection.',steps:['Open a page in the Community Grimoire.','Scroll to "Practitioner Field Notes" and tap "Offer a Field Note or question".','Choose the kind of note, write it, and optionally add a display name.','Tick that Field Notes are reviewed first, then tap "Offer Field Note".'],keywords:['comment','feedback on page','reply','question']},{id:'community-report-hide',title:'Report or hide a page or person',summary:'Look after yourself in the community.',steps:['Open a community page or note.','Tap "Report" to email the moderators, "Hide" to stop showing it on this device, or "Hide this person".','To see hidden things again, tap "Show pages and people you\u2019ve hidden" at the bottom of the Community Grimoire.'],keywords:['block','moderation','flag','safety','mute']},{id:'community-offer',title:'Make an offering',summary:'Share a ritual, dream or story for review.',steps:['Open More and tap "Make an offering".','Choose "What would you like to offer?", then a title and "Your offering".','Choose how to be named under "Publish or reference as", and add tags.','Tick that it is your own work, and that you agree to the Submission Terms.','Tap "\u2726 Offer to the Sanctuary".'],tips:['Your "Magical name" in Settings, Identity can be used instead of your preferred name.','To offer a page you\u2019ve written, open it in your Grimoire, tap "Share\u2026", then "Make an offering".'],href:'/more/community/offer',keywords:['submit','contribute','share a ritual','publish','story','dream experience']},{id:'community-submission-terms',title:'Read the Submission Terms',summary:'What you agree to when you offer something.',steps:['Open More, then "Make an offering".','Next to "I have read and agree to the Submission Terms", tap the link to read them.','Or open More, scroll to Help, and tap "Submission Terms".'],href:'/more/community/terms',keywords:['terms','rules','permission','licence']},{id:'community-my-submissions',title:'See the status of your submissions and read replies',summary:'Follow the review of each offering and reply to us.',steps:['Sign in, open More, tap "Community" and choose Mine.','Tap a submission.','Read "Response from Salt & Sovereignty" and the Conversation.','Type under "Reply or ask a question" and tap "Send reply".'],href:'/more/community/mine',keywords:['review status','moderation reply','my offerings']}]},{id:'sanctuary',title:'Your Sanctuary',intro:'The More tab: your journey, names, settings, account and support.',topics:[{id:'sanctuary-journey',title:'Read My chronicle',summary:'A chronicle of your practice, drawn from what you keep.',steps:['Open More and tap "My chronicle".','Search the chronicle, and choose what to "Show", the "Order" and "Group by" Month or Year.','Tap an item to open it.','Scroll for "First Pages", "Recorded Patterns" and "Recent Threads".'],tips:['My chronicle is not a measure of progress. Quiet chapters count too.'],href:'/more/journey',keywords:['chronicle','my journey','timeline','history','milestones','first pages']},{id:'sanctuary-identity',title:'Set your names and pronouns',summary:'Choose how the app greets you.',steps:['Open More, then Settings, then Identity.','Type your "Preferred name", "Pronouns" and "Magical name".','Under "Greet me with", choose "Preferred name", "Magical name" or "No name".','Each change saves itself.'],tips:['Offerings can be credited to your magical name instead of your preferred name.'],href:'/more/settings/identity',keywords:['name','pronouns','greeting','magical name','craft name','welcome']},{id:'sanctuary-account',title:'Open your account',summary:'See your sign-in method and sync status, and sign out.',steps:['Open More and tap Account.','Read "Signed in as", "Sign-in method", "Cloud status" and "Last successful sync".','Tap "Sign out" to sign out. Nothing is deleted; sign back in to see it again.'],href:'/more/account',keywords:['sign out','logout','profile','cloud']},{id:'sanctuary-change-password',title:'Change your password',summary:'Set a new password for an email sign-in.',steps:['Open More, then Account, and find Security.','Type a "New password" and "Confirm new password".','Tap "Change password".'],tips:['If you sign in with Google, there is no password to change here.'],href:'/more/account',keywords:['reset password','security','new password']},{id:'sanctuary-change-email',title:'Change your email address',summary:'Confirm the change at your old and new addresses.',steps:['Open More, then Account, and find Security.','Under "Change email", type the "New email" and "Confirm new email".','Tap "Request email change".','Check your email and confirm. The account email changes once that is done.'],href:'/more/account',keywords:['email address','update email','new email']},{id:'sanctuary-recovery-link',title:'Get a password recovery link',summary:'Email yourself a link to choose a new password.',steps:['Open More, then Account.','Under "Password recovery link", tap "Send recovery link".','Open the email and follow the link.'],href:'/more/account',keywords:['forgot password','reset link','locked out']},{id:'sanctuary-delete-account',title:'Delete your account',summary:'Permanently remove your account and private data.',steps:['Open More, then Account, then under Danger zone tap "Delete account".','Read "What happens". Published Community Grimoire pages stay, without your name.','Optionally tap "Save complete backup" first.','If asked, tap "Sign in again". Type the confirmation phrase.','Tap "Delete my account forever".'],tips:['This cannot be undone. The account stops working on the app and the website.'],href:'/more/delete-account',keywords:['remove account','close account','erase data','gdpr','forget me']},{id:'sanctuary-support',title:'Find crisis, grief and other support lines',summary:'Free lines for when something feels too heavy to carry alone.',steps:['Open More and tap "Support" under Help.','Under "Show lines for", choose your country. Others follow yours.','Choose from Crisis and suicide, Grief and bereavement, Pregnancy and baby loss, Domestic abuse, Eating disorders, and Alcohol and drugs.','Tap "Call", "Text" or "Website" on a line.'],tips:['In danger now? Call your local emergency number (911, 999, 112, 000).','Ritual and journey screens show a link to this page where the work can stir deep things.'],href:'/more/support',keywords:['crisis','suicide','hotline','helpline','grief','abuse','emergency','mental health']},{id:'sanctuary-contact',title:'Contact us',summary:'Write to the Salt & Sovereignty team.',steps:['Open More and scroll to Help.','Tap "Contact us" to open an email.','In the Closed & living traditions guide, tap "Send a correction" to write about a specific entry.'],keywords:['email','feedback','bug','report','help','contact']}]},{id:'widgets',title:'Home screen widgets',intro:'Five widgets put the moon, holidays, your next ritual and an altar on your home screen.',topics:[{id:'widgets-add-day',title:'Add the moon, holiday, coming up or ritual widget',summary:'Tonight\u2019s Moon, Next Holiday, Coming Up and Next Ritual.',steps:['Press and hold an empty spot on your home screen.','Open the widget list (tap Edit then Add Widget on iPhone, or Widgets on Android) and find Salt & Sovereignty.','Choose "Tonight\u2019s Moon", "Next Holiday", "Coming Up" or "Next Ritual" and the size you like.','Open the app now and then so the widgets stay up to date.'],tips:['"Tonight\u2019s Moon" adds today\u2019s holiday and what it means. "Next Holiday" counts down to the next one. "Coming Up" lists the next moon phases and holidays. "Next Ritual" shows your next planned working, its intention and what you will need.'],keywords:['widget','lock screen','moon widget','holiday countdown','next ritual widget','coming up']},{id:'widgets-add-altar',title:'Add the Altar widget',summary:'Tend one of your altars without opening the app.',steps:['In the app, open a saved altar and tap "Home screen". Or open More \u2192 Settings \u2192 Altar \u2192 "Home screen widget" to see what is in each place and choose for any altar.','Choose "Altar 1", "Altar 2" or another place, or "Let the app choose".','Press and hold your home screen, add the Salt & Sovereignty Altar widget, and choose its place.','On Android, a screen titled "Which altar" lets you pick the place.'],tips:['Its buttons light and snuff candles, tend offerings and cleanse crystals. What you do is carried onto the altar the next time the app opens.'],href:'/more/settings/widget',keywords:['altar widget','candle widget','lock screen altar','widget settings']}]}]},2933,[]);
