__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MOON_IN_SIGN_READING",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o={Aries:{simple:'With the Moon in Aries your feelings are quick and fiery. You need freedom, action and honesty to feel safe, and your moods flare and pass fast.',detailed:'An Aries Moon reacts first and reflects later. Feelings arrive as impulses to do something, and you tend to meet hurt with anger or movement rather than tears. You are emotionally brave and direct, and you need room to be independent.\n\nYou soothe yourself best by moving: exercise, a new project, a fresh start. The growth is in pausing long enough to feel what is under the spark.',magic:'Your emotional reset is fire: lighting a candle and naming what you feel, burning written worries, a brisk walk at dawn. When the Moon is in Aries each month you may feel more yourself; it is a good time for courage spells.',shadow:'Temper, impatience with your own and others\' feelings.'},Taurus:{simple:'With the Moon in Taurus your feelings are steady and grounded. You need comfort, routine, good food and touch to feel safe.',detailed:'The Moon is exalted in Taurus: feelings here are calm, warm and loyal. You are slow to upset and slow to let go, and you find peace in the body and the senses: a garden, a meal, a soft blanket, a familiar walk.\n\nYou soothe yourself best through the senses and through things staying the same. The growth is in trusting change when it comes.',magic:'Your emotional reset is earth: hands in soil, a herbal bath, a slow meal made as ritual, holding a stone. The monthly Taurus Moon is a strong time for money, home and self-care spells.',shadow:'Holding on to hurts, and comfort-seeking that avoids feeling.'},Gemini:{simple:'With the Moon in Gemini you understand feelings by talking them through. You need conversation, variety and mental play to feel at ease.',detailed:'A Gemini Moon processes emotion through words: talking, writing, texting, reading about it. Your moods change quickly and you can be lively, funny and curious company, with a restless inner life.\n\nYou soothe yourself best by naming things and by change of scene. The growth is in letting a feeling be felt before it is explained.',magic:'Your emotional reset is air and words: journaling, a letter you burn or keep, talking to a friend, a change of place. The monthly Gemini Moon suits divination, study and communication spells.',shadow:'Over-thinking feelings, and nervous restlessness.'},Cancer:{simple:'With the Moon in Cancer, its own sign, your feelings run deep and tender. You need home, belonging and people to care for to feel safe.',detailed:'The Moon is at home in Cancer: you are intuitive, nurturing, protective and strongly tied to memory, family and place. You feel others\' moods as if they were your own and you give care naturally.\n\nYou soothe yourself best at home, in water, and by being looked after. The growth is in letting others care for you as you care for them, and in not carrying every tide.',magic:'Your emotional reset is water and hearth: a bath, a home-cooked meal, tidying your altar, sitting by moonlight. The monthly Cancer Moon is one of the strongest times for home, family, healing and dream work.',shadow:'Moodiness, clinging, and retreating when hurt.'},Leo:{simple:'With the Moon in Leo your feelings are warm, proud and generous. You need to be appreciated and to express yourself to feel safe.',detailed:'A Leo Moon wears its heart openly. You are affectionate, loyal and playful, and you feel best when you can create, perform or simply be noticed and loved. Hurt can show as pride.\n\nYou soothe yourself best with joy: play, creativity, music, being with people who delight in you. The growth is in knowing your worth without needing it shown back.',magic:'Your emotional reset is sun and joy: dancing, making something, dressing up, a candle for your own heart. The monthly Leo Moon suits confidence, glamour and creative spells.',shadow:'Wounded pride and needing reassurance.'},Virgo:{simple:'With the Moon in Virgo you feel safest when life is in order. You show care through practical help and need to be useful.',detailed:'A Virgo Moon handles feelings by doing something useful with them: cleaning, organising, fixing, helping. You are modest, observant and attentive to the body and health, and you notice what others need.\n\nYou soothe yourself best with routines and small tasks done well. The growth is in letting feelings be messy and in being as gentle with yourself as you are with others.',magic:'Your emotional reset is cleansing and craft: tidying, a herbal tea brewed with intention, sorting your herbs, a cleansing wash. The monthly Virgo Moon suits healing, herbcraft and practical magic.',shadow:'Worry, self-criticism, and anxiety in the body.'},Libra:{simple:'With the Moon in Libra you feel safest in harmony. You need fairness, beauty and good company, and conflict unsettles you.',detailed:'A Libra Moon finds emotional balance through relationship. You are considerate, gracious and attuned to others, and you often soothe the room before yourself. Ugliness and discord affect you deeply.\n\nYou soothe yourself best with beauty, music, kind company and fair resolution. The growth is in naming your own needs, not only weighing everyone else\'s.',magic:'Your emotional reset is beauty: arranging flowers, art, music, a pretty altar, time with a friend. The monthly Libra Moon suits love, friendship and harmony spells.',shadow:'Avoiding conflict and losing your own feelings in someone else\'s.'},Scorpio:{simple:'With the Moon in Scorpio your feelings run deep and private. You need trust, loyalty and emotional honesty to feel safe.',detailed:'The Moon is in fall in Scorpio: feelings here are intense, all-or-nothing and often hidden. You are perceptive, loyal and fiercely protective, and you can sit with pain others turn away from, which makes you a strong friend in crisis.\n\nYou soothe yourself best in privacy and with people you trust completely. The growth is in letting things go and letting yourself be seen.',magic:'Your emotional reset is the dark: candlelight, shadow work, a release ritual, time alone. The monthly Scorpio Moon is a strong time for banishing, protection and transformation.',shadow:'Brooding, suspicion, and holding grudges.'},Sagittarius:{simple:'With the Moon in Sagittarius you need freedom, meaning and adventure to feel safe. You cheer yourself and others with hope and humour.',detailed:'A Sagittarius Moon meets feelings with optimism and movement. You need space, honesty and something to look forward to; being fenced in makes you restless. You recover from sorrow by finding its meaning.\n\nYou soothe yourself best outdoors, travelling, learning, or laughing. The growth is in staying with hard feelings without rushing to the bright side.',magic:'Your emotional reset is the open sky: a long walk, a journey, a sacred text, a question to the cards. The monthly Sagittarius Moon suits luck, travel and expansion spells.',shadow:'Restlessness and skipping over pain.'},Capricorn:{simple:'With the Moon in Capricorn you feel safest when you are in control and doing something useful. You are self-reliant and keep your feelings close.',detailed:'The Moon is in detriment in Capricorn: feelings here are held carefully and handled responsibly. You may have grown up early, and you show love through reliability and effort. You are steady in a crisis and slow to show hurt.\n\nYou soothe yourself best with structure and accomplishment. The growth is in letting yourself need others and in feeling without fixing.',magic:'Your emotional reset is structure: a list, a routine, a walk among stones and old trees, a protective charm. The monthly Capricorn Moon suits goals, boundaries and binding.',shadow:'Holding feelings in until they come out as tiredness or coldness.'},Aquarius:{simple:'With the Moon in Aquarius you need freedom and friendship to feel safe. You understand feelings by stepping back and thinking them through.',detailed:'An Aquarius Moon is cool, kind and independent. You care deeply but from a little distance, and you feel most at home among friends and like-minded people. You need space to be yourself and dislike emotional pressure.\n\nYou soothe yourself best with friends, causes and time alone to think. The growth is in letting feelings close enough to be felt.',magic:'Your emotional reset is air and community: a group ritual, a coven gathering, helping a cause, stargazing. The monthly Aquarius Moon suits breaking habits, freedom and friendship spells.',shadow:'Detachment and intellectualising feelings.'},Pisces:{simple:'With the Moon in Pisces you feel everything, your own feelings and others\'. You need quiet, imagination and spiritual connection to feel safe.',detailed:'A Pisces Moon is deeply empathic, imaginative and intuitive. You absorb the moods around you and need time alone to sort yours from everyone else\'s. Music, art, water and the spirit restore you.\n\nYou soothe yourself best by retreating, dreaming and creating. The growth is in boundaries and in grounding your sensitivity so it stays a gift.',magic:'Your emotional reset is water and dream: a ritual bath, music, meditation, a dream journal. The monthly Pisces Moon is one of the strongest times for divination, dreamwork and spiritual healing.',shadow:'Overwhelm, escapism, and taking on others\' pain.'}}},3050,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PATTERN_READINGS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const t={'grand-trine':{simple:'Three planets in the same element, each 120\xb0 from the others: a closed circle of ease and natural talent in that element.',detailed:'A grand trine joins three planets in the three signs of one element, fire, earth, air or water. Energy flows round it without resistance, so it shows a gift that comes so naturally you may not notice it: inspiration in fire, practical skill in earth, ideas and social ease in air, feeling and intuition in water.\n\nThe classic caution is that a grand trine is self-contained. Because nothing pushes against it, it can make for comfort rather than achievement. Planets that square or oppose the trine (a kite, or a T-square elsewhere) are often what put the gift to work. Read the three planets for what the gift is about, and the houses for where it shows.',magic:'A grand trine is a ready-made triangle of power: work it with three candles in a triangle, one for each planet, in the element\'s colours (red for fire, green for earth, yellow for air, blue for water). It is excellent for blessing others, since the energy circulates easily.',shadow:'Complacency, and gifts left unused because they never had to be fought for.'},'t-square':{simple:'Two planets opposite each other, both square a third: a driving tension that pushes you to act, with the third planet as the outlet.',detailed:'A T-square is made of an opposition and two squares meeting at one planet, the apex. The opposed planets pull against each other and both press on the apex, which becomes the place where the tension is released: the area of life you keep returning to, and where you achieve most.\n\nThe empty point opposite the apex (the "missing leg") is often read as the key to balance: the sign and house there show what to develop to ease the pressure. T-squares are common in the charts of people who get things done; the energy is restless but productive. Note whether the planets are cardinal (crisis and action), fixed (endurance and stubbornness) or mutable (scattered, adaptable) signs.',magic:'Treat the apex planet as the focus of your workings: its day, hour and correspondences turn the chart\'s pressure into power. A three-cornered working with the apex candle taller than the other two suits it, and so does building up the empty leg\'s sign with its element.',shadow:'Stress, overwork and pushing through when the answer is to step back to the missing leg.'},'grand-cross':{simple:'Four planets in a square, each opposite one and square two others: great strength under constant tension, often in one modality.',detailed:'A grand cross, or grand square, is two oppositions crossing at right angles, so four planets square one another all round. It usually falls in signs of one modality: cardinal (action and crisis), fixed (will and endurance) or mutable (adaptability and nerves).\n\nIt is a demanding pattern: pulled four ways at once, you may feel there is no easy direction. It is also a pattern of immense resilience and capacity; people with it often carry heavy loads well and achieve a great deal. The work is to move round the cross rather than being stuck at one arm, giving each planet its turn.',magic:'Four is the number of the quarters: a grand cross loves circle work with each planet at a direction. Call each in turn, and balance them deliberately; it is a strong pattern for protection and grounding.',shadow:'Feeling trapped or torn, and exhaustion from carrying too much.'},yod:{simple:'Two planets sextile each other, both 150\xb0 from a third: the "finger of fate", a pointed sense of mission at the third planet.',detailed:'A yod is two planets in sextile, each making a quincunx (150\xb0) to a third, the apex. The quincunxes join signs with nothing in common, so the apex planet feels awkward, special or constantly adjusting, and it becomes the focus of a sense of calling. Modern astrologers nicknamed it the finger of God or the finger of fate.\n\nThe sextile base gives skills and resources; the apex shows what they are for. Many people with a yod describe a life of course-corrections that eventually reveal a purpose. The point opposite the apex (the "reaction point") is often sensitive when transits touch it. Read it as vocation and adjustment, never doom.',magic:'A yod suits divination about purpose and workings of dedication: the apex planet\'s correspondences are your strongest tools. Draw the yod as a long triangle and place your intention at its point.',shadow:'A feeling of being out of step, and pressure to find "the" purpose all at once.'},kite:{simple:'A grand trine with a fourth planet opposite one corner: the trine\'s natural gifts given a direction and a reason to use them.',detailed:'A kite is a grand trine plus a fourth planet that opposes one of its corners and sextiles the other two. The opposition supplies the tension the grand trine lacks, so its easy flow is pulled toward one point, the kite\'s tail (opposite the corner it faces).\n\nIt is read as one of the most productive patterns: talent plus motivation. The tail planet shows where the gifts are aimed; the corner opposite it shows the main resource. People with a kite often have a clear area in which they excel.',magic:'Fly it like a kite: anchor your working on the tail planet and let the trine lift it. Four candles, the tail apart from the triangle, lit last.',shadow:'Over-reliance on talent, if the tail\'s pull is ignored.'},stellium:{simple:'Three or more planets in one sign or one house: a concentration of energy that makes that sign or area central to your life.',detailed:'A stellium gathers three or more planets in one sign or house. That sign\'s qualities, or that house\'s matters, become a theme you cannot avoid: everything you do passes through it. People often identify more with a stellium sign than with their Sun sign.\n\nThe gift is depth and focus; the care is imbalance, since other areas may be neglected. Look for the sign\'s ruler, which becomes very strong (it governs all those planets), and at how the stellium planets relate to each other: a mix of personal and outer planets reads differently from a group of personal ones.',magic:'A stellium is a power base: work in its element and sign\'s season, with the ruler\'s day and hour. When the transiting Moon passes through it each month, your workings there are amplified.',shadow:'Tunnel vision, and neglecting the rest of the chart.'}}},3051,[]);
__d(function(g,_r,_i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PLANET_IN_HOUSE_BY_BODY",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PLANET_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return p}});var E=_r(d[0]),_=_r(d[1]),N=_r(d[2]),O=_r(d[3]),U=_r(d[4]),t=_r(d[5]),S=_r(d[6]),n=_r(d[7]),r=_r(d[8]),H=_r(d[9]),I=_r(d[10]),R=_r(d[11]),P=_r(d[12]),u=_r(d[13]),o=_r(d[14]),T=_r(d[15]),D=_r(d[16]),i=_r(d[17]);const c=(E,_)=>E.map((E,N)=>(0,D.deepen)(E,_[N])),s={Sun:I.SUN_IN_HOUSE,Moon:t.MOON_IN_HOUSE,Mercury:U.MERCURY_IN_HOUSE,Venus:P.VENUS_IN_HOUSE,Mars:c(O.MARS_IN_HOUSE,o.MARS_DEEPER),Jupiter:c(_.JUPITER_IN_HOUSE,o.JUPITER_DEEPER),Saturn:c(H.SATURN_IN_HOUSE,o.SATURN_DEEPER),Uranus:c(R.URANUS_IN_HOUSE,u.URANUS_DEEPER),Neptune:c(S.NEPTUNE_IN_HOUSE,u.NEPTUNE_DEEPER),Pluto:c(r.PLUTO_IN_HOUSE,u.PLUTO_DEEPER),Chiron:c(E.CHIRON_IN_HOUSE,T.CHIRON_DEEPER),'North Node':c(n.NORTH_NODE_IN_HOUSE,T.NORTH_NODE_DEEPER),'South Node':c(n.SOUTH_NODE_IN_HOUSE,T.SOUTH_NODE_DEEPER),Lilith:c(N.LILITH_IN_HOUSE,T.LILITH_DEEPER)},p=Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(s).flatMap(([E,_])=>_.map((_,N)=>[i.keys.planetInHouse(E,N+1),_])))},3052,[3053,3054,3055,3056,3057,3058,3059,3060,3061,3062,3063,3064,3065,3066,3067,3068,3069,3046]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CHIRON_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o=[{simple:"With Chiron in the first house the tender place is your body, appearance or sense of self. Accepting yourself becomes a gift you pass on.",detailed:"Chiron near the Ascendant often points to an early feeling of being wrong in yourself: unwanted, too different, or uneasy in your body. Some people with this placement had illness or injury young; others simply felt they had to justify their existence.\n\nAs you come to accept yourself, you often become someone whose very presence tells others they are allowed to be as they are. Coaches, healers and body workers often have this placement.\n\nIn relationships you may need reassurance that you are wanted as you are. At work you may be drawn to coaching, body work or advocacy.",magic:"Self-blessing is your medicine: a daily anointing with oil, a mirror ritual, and protective charms for your body. Rose Quartz, Carnelian and Calendula help; Asclepius, the healer Chiron taught, is a patron for this work.",shadow:"Self-rejection, or proving yourself endlessly."},{simple:"With Chiron in the second house the tender place is worth and money. Learning that you are valuable as you are becomes your gift.",detailed:"With Chiron in the second house, self-worth and resources can be sore: scarcity, shame about money, or a sense that you must earn your right to exist. You may struggle to charge for your work.\n\nAs you heal, you often help others find their worth: financial counselling, coaching, or simply modelling enough-ness.\n\nAt work you may need to learn to ask for what you are worth. Many people with this placement become gifted helpers with money and self-worth.",magic:"Worth and prosperity healing suits you: gratitude rituals, spells to value your talents, and abundance work done from kindness. Green Aventurine, Rose Quartz and basil help.",shadow:"Underselling yourself."},{simple:"With Chiron in the third house the tender place is your voice and mind. Finding your words becomes a gift for others.",detailed:"With Chiron in the third house, learning, speaking or sibling relationships may hold an old hurt: feeling stupid at school, being silenced, or a painful bond with a brother or sister.\n\nAs you heal, you often become a gentle teacher or writer who helps others find their voice.\n\nSiblings may have been a source of pain or a responsibility. You may be a gifted teacher for those who learn differently.",magic:"Voice and word healing suits you: journaling, speaking affirmations, unsent letters and study blessings. Blue Lace Agate, Fluorite and lavender help.",shadow:"Fear of speaking."},{simple:"With Chiron in the fourth house the tender place is home and family. Making a safe home becomes your gift.",detailed:"With Chiron at the root of the chart, family and home may hold old wounds: an absent or hurt parent, a home that did not feel safe, or a sense of not belonging.\n\nAs you heal, you often create a home that shelters others and become a keeper of chosen family.\n\nA parent may have been absent or hurting. Making a home for yourself, and later for others, is the healing.",magic:"Hearth and ancestor healing suits you: ancestor work, home blessings and family pattern release. Moonstone, Rose Quartz and Lemon Balm help.",shadow:"Feeling homeless in yourself."},{simple:"With Chiron in the fifth house the tender place is joy, creativity and love. Learning to play becomes your gift.",detailed:"With Chiron in the fifth house, play, creativity or romance may carry old hurts: creativity criticised, love rejected, or childhood joy cut short. Children may be a tender subject.\n\nAs you heal, you often help others find their creative courage and inner child.\n\nChildren may be a tender subject, through longing, loss or difficulty. Creative work done for its own sake heals.",magic:"Creative and joyful healing suits you: art as healing, play as ritual and self-love. Carnelian, Rose Quartz and Calendula help.",shadow:"Fear of creative judgement."},{simple:"With Chiron in the sixth house the tender place is health and work. Caring for your body becomes your gift to others.",detailed:"With Chiron in the sixth house, the body or daily work may be a source of pain: chronic health issues, feeling not good enough at work, or overwork.\n\nAs you heal, you often become a gifted healer, herbalist or carer.\n\nChronic health matters may be part of your story, and you may be drawn to healing professions because of them.",magic:"Herbal and healing magic suits you: herbal remedies (beside proper care), cleansing rituals and gentle routine. Amazonite, Moss Agate and Chamomile help.",shadow:"Perfectionism and health worry."},{simple:"With Chiron in the seventh house the tender place is partnership. Learning to relate as equals becomes your gift.",detailed:"With Chiron in the seventh house, relationships may hold old wounds: rejection, betrayal, or being drawn to wounded partners.\n\nAs you heal, you often become a wise counsellor or a deeply understanding partner.\n\nPartners may mirror your own hurts. Choosing equals, not patients or rescuers, is the work.",magic:"Relationship healing suits you: cord cutting, self-love and partnership blessings. Rose Quartz, Rhodonite and rose help.",shadow:"Rescuing wounded partners."},{simple:"With Chiron in the eighth house the tender place is trust, intimacy and loss. Facing the depths becomes your gift.",detailed:"With Chiron in the eighth house, intimacy, loss or shared resources may hold old wounds: early grief, betrayal or crisis.\n\nAs you heal, you often become a guide for others through grief and transformation.\n\nEarly loss may have shaped you. You may be drawn to therapy, hospice or grief work.",magic:"Deep healing suits you: grief rituals, shadow work and protection. Obsidian, Rhodochrosite and Wormwood help.",shadow:"Distrust and fear of loss."},{simple:"With Chiron in the ninth house the tender place is faith and meaning. Finding your own truth becomes your gift.",detailed:"With Chiron in the ninth house, belief, education or travel may hold old wounds: religious harm, disrupted study or a loss of faith.\n\nAs you heal, you often become a wise, humble teacher.\n\nFaith may have been wounded by a religion or teacher. Finding your own path heals.",magic:"Seeking healing suits you: devotion, pilgrimage and study as healing. Turquoise, Lapis Lazuli and Sage help.",shadow:"Cynicism about meaning."},{simple:"With Chiron in the tenth house the tender place is career and recognition. Defining success your way becomes your gift.",detailed:"With Chiron in the tenth house, career or public life may hold old wounds: failure, criticism, or a parent's harsh ambition.\n\nAs you heal, you often become a mentor or a healer in public life.\n\nA parent's ambition may have weighed on you. Defining success on your own terms heals.",magic:"Career healing suits you: gentle success spells, protection of reputation and ancestor work. Onyx, Garnet and bay laurel help.",shadow:"Fear of failure."},{simple:"With Chiron in the eleventh house the tender place is belonging and friendship. Finding your people becomes your gift.",detailed:"With Chiron in the eleventh house, friendships or groups may hold old wounds: exclusion, betrayal by friends, or feeling like an outsider.\n\nAs you heal, you often build inclusive communities.\n\nExclusion from a group may have left its mark. Building inclusive communities heals.",magic:"Communal healing suits you: friendship spells, group ritual and belonging work. Amethyst, Rose Quartz and lavender help.",shadow:"Feeling like an outsider."},{simple:"With Chiron in the twelfth house the tender place is hidden and spiritual. Tending your inner life becomes your gift.",detailed:"With Chiron in the twelfth house, the wound may be hard to name: inherited sorrow, hidden fears, or spiritual loneliness.\n\nAs you heal, you often become a compassionate spiritual healer.\n\nInherited sorrow or hidden fears may weigh on you. Spiritual practice and quiet service heal.",magic:"Spiritual healing suits you: meditation, dreamwork, retreat and ancestor healing. Amethyst, Moonstone and mugwort help.",shadow:"Hidden, inherited sorrow."}]},3053,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"JUPITER_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o=[{simple:"With Jupiter in the first house you come across as warm, open and optimistic. People trust you, and you tend to meet life expecting the best.",detailed:"Jupiter rising gives a big, generous presence. You may be tall or broad, or simply seem larger than life; you laugh easily, encourage others and often seem lucky. Traditional astrologers counted Jupiter on the Ascendant as one of the best signs for health, protection and a good reputation.\n\nYour faith in yourself can open doors, and people are drawn to your goodwill. The risk is excess: overconfidence, overcommitting, overeating, or promising more than any one person can deliver. Learning when enough is enough is part of the gift.\n\nIn relationships you are a generous, encouraging partner, and you need someone who shares your appetite for life. At work you suit teaching, leadership, sales, law and travel, anywhere optimism is an asset.",magic:"You carry luck with you: personal good-fortune charms, blessings on new ventures and protective amulets work well for you. Thursdays and Jupiter hours suit self-work. Citrine, Turquoise, nutmeg and Sage support a lucky, generous spirit.",shadow:"Overconfidence and excess in body or promise."},{simple:"With Jupiter in the second house money and resources tend to grow. You are generous with what you have, and you often find what you need.",detailed:"Jupiter in the house of livelihood is a classic sign of abundance: income may come easily, through several streams, or through teaching, law, publishing, travel or anything Jupiterian. You are likely generous and think big about money.\n\nThe flip side is that money flows out as easily as in. Overspending, overconfidence in investments, or a belief that more will always come can undo the luck. Your values are often broad and humane, and your worth is rooted in faith in yourself.\n\nMany people with this placement do well in teaching, publishing, law, finance or anything that grows with confidence. In partnership you are generous with gifts, and you value a partner who shares your faith in abundance.",magic:"Prosperity magic is a natural strength: abundance grids, money jars, Thursday offerings of coins to a god of plenty, and gratitude rites. Green Aventurine, Pyrite, cinnamon and basil draw growth; Fortuna and Lakshmi are old faces of good fortune.",shadow:"Overspending, and faith that luck will always cover it."},{simple:"With Jupiter in the third house your mind is broad and optimistic. Learning, writing and conversation bring growth and luck.",detailed:"With Jupiter in the third house, everyday learning is a blessing. You may love books and talk, enjoy teaching, write well or have good relations with siblings and neighbours. Opportunities often come through local connections, short trips and the written word.\n\nYou may know a little about everything and talk more than you listen; scattered optimism can stop you finishing what you start. Your gift is spreading hope and knowledge in daily life.\n\nSiblings and neighbours may be lucky connections or teachers to you. Writing, media, teaching and travel work suit you, and you may find that a simple local course or a conversation on a train changes your life.",magic:"Word and travel luck suit you: petitions for good news, travel blessings, and study rituals before exams. Thursdays and Wednesdays suit you. Citrine, Sodalite and Star Anise help.",shadow:"Talking more than listening, and scattered enthusiasm."},{simple:"With Jupiter in the fourth house home and family are a source of blessing. You may have a big, warm home, or grow more fortunate as life goes on.",detailed:"With Jupiter at the root of the chart, home is generous. You may come from a large or supportive family, live in a spacious home, own property or land, or simply be someone whose door is always open. Many astrologers read this placement as a promise of a good later life.\n\nYou can overextend at home, filling it with people or things, or idealise family. The work is generosity that still keeps a door you can close.\n\nProperty and land are often good to you, and many people with this placement find their luck improves the more they invest in home and family. A generous parent, or the memory of one, may still guide you.",magic:"Hearth and ancestor magic brings blessing: home prosperity spells, ancestor offerings, a blessing of land or garden, and household gods honoured at the hearth. Thursdays and Mondays suit you. Citrine, Moonstone and bay laurel bless the home.",shadow:"Excess at home, and idealising family."},{simple:"With Jupiter in the fifth house joy, creativity, romance and children are areas of blessing. You know how to have a good time.",detailed:"With Jupiter in the fifth house, pleasure expands. You may be creatively gifted, love parties and play, enjoy romance generously, and have warm relationships with children. Luck may come through creative projects, games or speculation.\n\nToo much of a good thing is the risk: gambling, indulgence, or chasing pleasure endlessly. At its best, this placement teaches others how to enjoy life.\n\nWith children you are a joyful, indulgent presence, and you may have a large family or many godchildren. Artistic, theatrical or sporting work can be very fortunate, and romance is generous and warm.",magic:"Joyful and creative magic is your strength: creative success spells, fertility blessings, love-drawing and celebration rites. Thursdays and Fridays suit you. Citrine, Carnelian and Sunflower bring joy.",shadow:"Gambling and endless indulgence."},{simple:"With Jupiter in the sixth house work and health are areas of growth. You may find meaningful work and recover well from illness.",detailed:"With Jupiter in the sixth house, daily work can be a blessing. You may have good colleagues, enjoy helping others, or work in health, teaching, law or service. Your health is often robust, though Jupiter's excess can show as weight or overindulgence.\n\nYou may take on too much work, or overdo food and drink. Your gift is generous service that makes everyday life better.\n\nYou may find fulfilment in health care, teaching, animal care or any service with meaning. Colleagues often like you, and good work tends to find you. Moderation in food and drink is the main health advice.",magic:"Health and work magic suits you: blessings for good work, healing (beside proper care), and cleansing routines. Thursdays and Wednesdays suit you. Amazonite, Citrine and Chamomile help.",shadow:"Overwork and overindulgence."},{simple:"With Jupiter in the seventh house partnerships bring growth and good fortune. You may attract generous, wise or worldly partners.",detailed:"With Jupiter in the seventh house, others bring blessings. Marriage, business partnerships and collaborations can be fortunate, and you may attract partners who are older, wiser, foreign or generous. You are often a generous partner yourself.\n\nYou may idealise partners or expect them to bring your luck, and some people with this placement marry more than once. Growth comes through relationship.\n\nBusiness partnerships can expand your world, and clients may come from far away. Legal matters often go your way. Your growth comes through others, so choose partners who share your values.",magic:"Partnership blessings are your strength: marriage and partnership rites, sweetening spells and agreements blessed. Thursdays and Fridays suit you. Lapis Lazuli, Rose Quartz and rose help; Juno and Hera, keepers of marriage, are fitting patrons.",shadow:"Expecting partners to bring your luck."},{simple:"With Jupiter in the eighth house you may benefit through shared resources, inheritance or partners' money. You grow through depth and transformation.",detailed:"With Jupiter in the eighth house, other people's resources can be fortunate: inheritance, investment, a partner's income, grants or loans. You may also grow through crisis, finding meaning and resilience in hard times, and be drawn to psychology or the occult.\n\nOverconfidence with debt or shared money is the danger, and so is excess in intensity. Your gift is faith that carries you through the depths.\n\nYou may be drawn to finance, insurance, therapy, hospice or occult study, and to rites that help others through loss. Intimacy can be generous and healing. Traditional astrologers read Jupiter here as a sign of a peaceful death after a long life.",magic:"Deep magic with blessing suits you: prosperity for shared finances, ancestor rituals, divination and transformation rites. Thursdays and the dark Moon suit you. Citrine, Obsidian and Wormwood help.",shadow:"Debt and overconfidence with others' money."},{simple:"With Jupiter in the ninth house, its natural place, faith, travel and learning bring great growth. You are a natural seeker and teacher.",detailed:"The ninth house is Sagittarius's natural house, and Jupiter is strong here. You may love travel, foreign cultures, religion, philosophy, law or higher education, and you may teach or publish. Faith comes naturally, and luck often follows when you follow your sense of meaning.\n\nPreachiness, restlessness and overconfidence in your beliefs are the risks. Your gift is wisdom shared generously.\n\nYou may live abroad, marry someone from another culture, or find your faith on the road. Many people with this placement become lifelong students, and the old texts read Jupiter here as wisdom and good dreams.",magic:"Devotional and seeking magic is your strength: pilgrimage, prayer, study as devotion, travel blessings and divination. Thursdays suit you. Turquoise, Lapis Lazuli and Sage help; Zeus and Jupiter are the old patrons.",shadow:"Preachiness and dogmatism."},{simple:"With Jupiter in the tenth house career and reputation tend to grow. You may achieve recognition and positions of trust.",detailed:"With Jupiter near the Midheaven, public life is blessed. You may rise in your career, be respected, and work in law, teaching, publishing, politics, religion or business. Traditional astrologers counted this among the best places for honour.\n\nOverambition and arrogance are the risks, and success can bring its own excess. Your gift is leadership that inspires.\n\nYou do best in fields where you can lead with integrity and inspire others: teaching, law, ministry, publishing, management. A mentor or patron often opens a door for you.",magic:"Success and honour magic suits you: career spells, blessings for leadership, and gratitude rites for achievements. Thursdays and Sundays suit you. Citrine, Sunstone and bay laurel help.",shadow:"Arrogance and overambition."},{simple:"With Jupiter in the eleventh house friends and groups bring blessings. Your hopes tend to grow and be fulfilled.",detailed:"The eleventh house is Jupiter's joy in ancient astrology, the house of the good spirit, and Jupiter rejoices here. Friends are generous, groups welcoming, and hopes often come true. You may be a generous friend and a natural networker.\n\nToo many friends and too little depth, or relying on others for luck, are the risks. Your gift is goodwill that brings people together.\n\nFriends often help your career and your hopes, and you may be a generous patron to others. Groups, clubs, covens and causes are good places for your energy. Wishes made with friends tend to come true.",magic:"Communal magic is your strength: group rituals, coven work, friendship spells and wishes made at the new Moon. Thursdays and Saturdays suit you. Amethyst, Citrine and lavender help.",shadow:"Many friends and little depth."},{simple:"With Jupiter in the twelfth house you have hidden protection and spiritual gifts. Faith grows in solitude, and help comes quietly.",detailed:"With Jupiter in the twelfth house, blessings come behind the scenes. Many astrologers read this as a guardian angel placement: protection in difficult times, help from unseen sources. You may be drawn to spirituality, charity, retreat or work in hospitals and institutions.\n\nEscapism and hidden excess are the risks. Your gift is compassion and faith that carry others.\n\nYou may give anonymously, volunteer, or work in hospitals, charities or monasteries. Solitude is often fruitful for you, and dreams can be prophetic. Traditional astrologers read Jupiter here as protection from hidden enemies.",magic:"Devotional and protective magic suits you: meditation, prayer, retreat, dreamwork and charity as offering. Thursdays and Mondays suit you. Amethyst, Moonstone and Sandalwood help.",shadow:"Escapism and hidden excess."}]},3054,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"LILITH_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n=[{simple:"With Lilith in the first house your wildness shows. You may have been judged for your looks, presence or refusal to fit in.",detailed:"Lilith near the Ascendant gives a magnetic, untamed presence that others notice and sometimes resist. You may have been told you were too much, too strange or too sexual, simply for existing as you are.\n\nReclaiming it means letting yourself be seen without apology. Many people with this placement become living permission for others to be wild.\n\nIn relationships you need a partner who welcomes your wildness rather than trying to tame it. At work you may be the one who breaks the mould.",magic:"Self-reclaiming rituals at the dark Moon suit you: a mirror rite, an anointing, a glamour of power. Obsidian, Garnet and Dragon\u2019s Blood help; Lilith herself is an image of the self that will not bow.",shadow:"Rejection used as armour."},{simple:"With Lilith in the second house your wildness lives in worth, money and the body's pleasures.",detailed:"With Lilith in the second house, money, possessions and sensual pleasure may carry shame or defiance. You may refuse conventional security, or feel judged for wanting comfort.\n\nReclaiming it means valuing yourself and your pleasures on your own terms.\n\nMoney may be a place of defiance: earning in unconventional ways, or refusing to measure yourself by it.",magic:"Sensual prosperity magic suits you: oils, baths, and money spells that honour pleasure. Garnet, Pyrite and patchouli help.",shadow:"Shame about wanting."},{simple:"With Lilith in the third house your wildness lives in your words and mind.",detailed:"With Lilith in the third house, your voice may have been silenced or called dangerous. You may say what others will not.\n\nReclaiming it means speaking and writing your truth fearlessly.\n\nSiblings or schooling may have tried to silence you. Writing, speaking and activism may be your power.",magic:"Word magic suits you: writing what you were forbidden to say, and spoken charms of freedom. Blue Lace Agate, Obsidian and peppermint help.",shadow:"Silence, or words as weapons."},{simple:"With Lilith in the fourth house your wildness lives in home, family and the mother.",detailed:"With Lilith at the root of the chart, family may have rejected a part of you, or the mother figure may have been complicated. You may refuse conventional home life.\n\nReclaiming it means making a home that welcomes your whole self.\n\nThe mother figure may have been complicated, or family may have refused part of you. Healing the female line can be part of your work.",magic:"Hearth magic for the wild self suits you: a dark Moon home altar and ancestor work on the female line. Moonstone, Obsidian and jasmine help.",shadow:"Rejection at home."},{simple:"With Lilith in the fifth house your wildness lives in pleasure, creativity and romance.",detailed:"With Lilith in the fifth house, sexuality, creativity or joy may have been shamed. You may love in unconventional ways or create taboo-breaking art.\n\nReclaiming it means unashamed pleasure and creative freedom.\n\nPleasure and creativity can be powerful, unashamed and taboo-breaking. Children may challenge you to accept the wild in them too.",magic:"Creative and sensual magic suits you: art as rebellion, pleasure as ritual. Garnet, Carnelian and Damiana help.",shadow:"Shame about pleasure."},{simple:"With Lilith in the sixth house your wildness lives in work, health and the body's routines.",detailed:"With Lilith in the sixth house, you may resist routine, conventional work or medical authority. The body may carry suppressed feeling.\n\nReclaiming it means working and caring for your body on your own terms.\n\nYou may resist routine and conventional work. Designing your own way of working and caring for your body is the healing.",magic:"Wild healing magic suits you: herbs gathered ethically, body rituals and routines of your own design. Moss Agate, Obsidian and Yarrow help.",shadow:"Rebellion against all care."},{simple:"With Lilith in the seventh house your wildness meets you through partners.",detailed:"With Lilith in the seventh house, you may attract wild, untamed partners, or find relationships where power and desire are charged. You may refuse conventional partnership.\n\nReclaiming it means relationships of equals where your whole self is welcome.\n\nPartners may embody your own wildness. Relationships of equals, where power is honest, are the healing.",magic:"Relationship magic for freedom suits you: cord cutting from unequal bonds and self-love. Rose Quartz, Obsidian and rose help.",shadow:"Projecting your wildness onto partners."},{simple:"With Lilith in the eighth house your wildness lives in sex, power and the depths.",detailed:"With Lilith in the eighth house, Lilith is strong. Sexuality, power and taboo are charged. You may have strong psychic gifts and a fearless relationship with death and the dark.\n\nReclaiming it means owning your power with integrity.\n\nSexuality, power and taboo are charged. Owning your power with integrity is the healing.",magic:"Deep, dark magic suits you: shadow work, sex magic with consent, and dark Moon ritual. Obsidian, Garnet and Dragon\u2019s Blood help; Lilith, Hekate and Ereshkigal are old faces of these depths.",shadow:"Power used to wound."},{simple:"With Lilith in the ninth house your wildness lives in faith, freedom and truth.",detailed:"With Lilith in the ninth house, you may reject religious authority or seek forbidden knowledge. Your truth may make others uncomfortable.\n\nReclaiming it means a spiritual path of your own.\n\nReligious authority may have judged you. Your own spiritual path is the healing.",magic:"Seeking magic suits you: forbidden lore studied with care, outdoor ritual and pilgrimage. Turquoise, Obsidian and Sage help.",shadow:"Rejecting every belief."},{simple:"With Lilith in the tenth house your wildness lives in career and public life.",detailed:"With Lilith near the Midheaven, you may refuse to conform at work, or be publicly judged for being different. Authority may feel threatening.\n\nReclaiming it means a career on your own terms.\n\nYou may be publicly judged for being different. A career on your own terms is the healing.",magic:"Power and career magic suits you: success spells for the unconventional path. Onyx, Obsidian and cypress help.",shadow:"Public rejection, or rebellion against all authority."},{simple:"With Lilith in the eleventh house your wildness lives in friendships and groups.",detailed:"With Lilith in the eleventh house, you may be the outsider in groups, or drawn to radical communities.\n\nReclaiming it means finding people who welcome your difference.\n\nGroups may have excluded you. Finding your fellow outsiders is the healing.",magic:"Communal rebellion magic suits you: group ritual with fellow outsiders. Amethyst, Obsidian and lavender help.",shadow:"Exclusion."},{simple:"With Lilith in the twelfth house your wildness lives in hidden places, dreams and spirit.",detailed:"With Lilith in the twelfth house, the wild self may be hidden even from you. Dreams may be powerful, and the unconscious full of refused feeling.\n\nReclaiming it means bringing the hidden self gently into light.\n\nThe wild self may be hidden even from you. Dreamwork and solitude bring it gently into light.",magic:"Dream and shadow magic suits you: dreamwork, dark Moon retreat and trance. Amethyst, Obsidian and mugwort help.",shadow:"The wild self kept hidden."}]},3055,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MARS_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o=[{simple:"With Mars in the first house you come across as energetic, direct and bold. You meet life head-on and people feel your drive at once.",detailed:"Mars near the Ascendant gives a strong, quick, physical presence. You may be sporty, restless, impatient or simply vivid; people sense that you get things done. Many people with this placement have a scar, a ruddy complexion or a love of physical challenge, and traditional texts read it as courage and a certain heat of temper.\n\nIn relationships you are direct and passionate, and you want a partner who can match your pace. At work you suit leadership, sport, emergency work, entrepreneurship and anything that needs nerve. The challenge is coming on too strong: impatience, accidents from rushing, and anger that flashes before you have thought.\n\nMars's sign shows the flavour of the fire, from hot-headed in Aries to strategic in Scorpio or gentle in Pisces.",magic:"Your body is a battery of Mars power: exercise or dance before spellwork raises it, and protection magic works strongly for you. Tuesdays and Mars hours suit self-work. Carnelian, Bloodstone, Red Jasper and nettle are allies.",shadow:"Aggression, haste and accidents from rushing."},{simple:"With Mars in the second house you work hard for money and fight for your security. You earn through effort and initiative.",detailed:"With Mars in the second house, money is something you go out and get. You may be enterprising, competitive about earning, or quick to spend. Income may come through physical work, sport, tools, engineering, sales or starting your own business.\n\nIn relationships you may show love by providing, and feel strongly about your own possessions. The challenge is impulsive spending, conflict over money, or measuring yourself by what you have won.\n\nMars's sign shows how you fight for your resources.\n\nIn relationships, money arguments are the ones to watch; agreeing who pays for what early saves a lot of heat. Traditional astrologers warned that Mars here spends as fast as it earns, and modern ones add that your drive to earn is also a drive to prove your worth to yourself.",magic:"Active prosperity magic suits you: money spells with red and green candles, a working to remove obstacles to income, and a charm carried when asking for a raise. Tuesdays and Thursdays suit you. Pyrite, Garnet, cinnamon and basil draw effort-earned money.",shadow:"Impulsive spending and money fights."},{simple:"With Mars in the third house you speak and think with force. You are quick, direct and a natural debater.",detailed:"With Mars in the third house, words are action. You speak frankly, argue well and think fast. Sibling relationships may be competitive or protective, and daily travel may be rushed (drive carefully). You may write with passion or campaign for causes locally.\n\nIn relationships you enjoy lively debate but may need to watch the edge of your tongue. At work you suit journalism, sales, teaching, law, transport and activism. The challenge is arguments, sharp words and restless nerves.\n\nMars's sign shows how you fight with words.\n\nSiblings often matter here: an elder brother or sister you competed with, or a younger one you defended. Many people with this placement are fearless writers and campaigners, the ones who write the letter to the council when everyone else just complains.",magic:"Spoken and written power suits you: binding petitions, spoken protections, travel protection charms and courage spells for speaking up. Tuesdays and Wednesdays suit you. Carnelian, Tiger Eye and ginger help; a protection charm in the car is a good third-house working.",shadow:"Sharp tongue, and arguments that run away with you."},{simple:"With Mars in the fourth house you put great energy into home and family, and you fight to protect your roots. Home can be busy or heated.",detailed:"With Mars at the root of the chart, the home is a place of activity, and sometimes conflict. You may renovate, move often, work from home or be fiercely protective of family. Early home life may have been lively or tense, and the parent connected with this house may have been strong-willed.\n\nThe gift is a protective, energetic drive that builds a home. The challenge is temper at home, or old family anger that resurfaces.\n\nMars's sign shows how you defend your nest.\n\nMars at the IC can show a restless need to build, dig, garden or renovate, and you may feel most at peace after physical work around the house. In later life, many people with this placement mellow into fierce, devoted guardians of the family.",magic:"Home protection is your strength: wards at the doors, iron at the threshold, a witch bottle buried by the house, and a hearth fire blessed. Tuesdays and Mondays suit you. Black Tourmaline, Garnet, rosemary and garlic protect the home.",shadow:"Temper at home, and old family anger."},{simple:"With Mars in the fifth house you pour passion into play, romance and creativity. You love competition, sport and bold self-expression.",detailed:"With Mars in the fifth house, fun is energetic. You may love sport, games, performance, adventure and passionate romance. Creativity is bold and physical, and you may be a lively, active parent.\n\nThe gift is passion and courage in self-expression. The challenge is risk-taking, gambling, or romance as conquest.\n\nMars's sign shows how you play.\n\nIn love you enjoy the chase and the spark, and you may be drawn to partners who challenge you. With children you are the parent who teaches them to climb trees and stand up for themselves. Creative work comes in fierce bursts, and deadlines help you.",magic:"Passionate, creative magic suits you: love-drawing with fire, creative courage spells, sport as ritual and a celebration rite. Tuesdays and Fridays suit you. Carnelian, Garnet and cinnamon help.",shadow:"Reckless risk and romance as conquest."},{simple:"With Mars in the sixth house you put tremendous energy into work and routine. You are a tireless worker who needs physical outlets.",detailed:"The sixth house is the joy of Mars in ancient astrology: Mars rejoices in this house of toil. You are a hard, efficient worker, often happiest when busy. You may be drawn to physical work, medicine, surgery, the military, engineering or sport. Exercise is essential for your health.\n\nThe gift is industry and the ability to fight illness and problems. The challenge is overwork, conflict with colleagues, inflammation or stress in the body.\n\nMars's sign shows how you work.\n\nBecause Mars rejoices here, the old texts read it as an able worker who masters toil; it can also show cuts, fevers and inflammations, so care with tools and rest after strain are wise. A workplace where you have a clear task and some autonomy suits you best.",magic:"Health and work magic suits you: exercise as ritual, protection at work, spells for a good job, and healing (beside proper care). Tuesdays suit you. Carnelian, Hematite and rosemary help.",shadow:"Overwork and conflict at work."},{simple:"With Mars in the seventh house partnerships are passionate and lively. You may attract bold partners, or meet conflict through others.",detailed:"With Mars in the seventh house, relationships have energy. You may be attracted to strong, assertive partners, or find that partnership brings out your own fight. Business partnerships may be competitive, and you may deal with opponents in law or sport.\n\nThe gift is passion and the courage to face others directly. The challenge is arguments, power struggles, or projecting your own anger onto partners.\n\nMars's sign shows the kind of partner who stirs you.\n\nBusiness partnerships can be energising if each of you has a clear domain. Traditional astrologers called the seventh the house of open enemies as well as partners, and Mars here can make you a strong advocate, litigator or competitor for others.",magic:"Relationship protection and passion magic suits you: spells for courage in partnership, passion for a consenting couple, and justice in disputes. Tuesdays and Fridays suit you. Garnet, Rose Quartz and Vervain help.",shadow:"Fights with partners, and blaming them for your fire."},{simple:"With Mars in the eighth house your passions run deep and intense. You are drawn to power, sex, transformation and crisis.",detailed:"With Mars in the eighth house, desire is strong and private. You may be drawn to crisis work, surgery, research, finance, psychology or the occult. Shared money may be a source of conflict or of enterprise.\n\nThe gift is courage in the depths and powerful regenerative energy. The challenge is power struggles, jealousy and risk.\n\nMars's sign shows how your deepest desire moves.\n\nIn finances you may take bold risks with shared money or investments, and do well in fields others find too dark or difficult. Desire and sexuality are strong and private, and honesty about power in intimacy keeps it healthy.",magic:"Deep, powerful magic suits you: banishing, protection, transformation rites and shadow work. Tuesdays and the dark Moon suit you. Obsidian, Garnet and Dragon\u2019s Blood help.",shadow:"Power struggles and jealousy."},{simple:"With Mars in the ninth house you fight for your beliefs. You are adventurous, passionate about ideas and love travel and challenge.",detailed:"With Mars in the ninth house, belief is action. You may campaign for causes, love adventurous travel, or argue passionately about philosophy and religion. You may study law, sport or theology.\n\nThe gift is courage of conviction. The challenge is fanaticism, preachiness and conflict over belief.\n\nMars's sign shows how you fight for your truth.\n\nYou may be drawn to adventurous travel, extreme sport, martial arts, law or the clergy militant of any faith. Learning is a contest you want to win, and you argue best about the things you believe most.",magic:"Seeking and protective magic suits you: travel protection, courage for a pilgrimage, and spells for justice. Tuesdays and Thursdays suit you. Carnelian, Turquoise and Juniper help.",shadow:"Fanaticism and preachiness."},{simple:"With Mars in the tenth house you are ambitious and driven in your career. You want to achieve and lead.",detailed:"With Mars near the Midheaven, ambition is strong. You may be a leader, an entrepreneur, or work in a competitive field: sport, the military, surgery, engineering, politics. You fight for your reputation.\n\nThe gift is drive and courage in public life. The challenge is conflict with authority, ruthlessness and burnout.\n\nTraditional astrologers counted Mars at the top as strong, sometimes harsh: a career with battles in it.\n\nYou often work best when you lead or run your own show, and you may change jobs after clashes with authority until you find a field worth fighting in. Your reputation is for energy, courage and getting things done.",magic:"Career and courage magic suits you: success spells, protection at work, and banishing obstacles. Tuesdays and Saturdays suit you. Carnelian, Garnet and bay laurel help.",shadow:"Ruthless ambition and conflict with bosses."},{simple:"With Mars in the eleventh house you put your energy into friends, groups and causes. You are an active, passionate team player.",detailed:"With Mars in the eleventh house, friendship is active. You may be a campaigner, team captain or organiser, and your friends may be lively and bold. You fight for your hopes and your community.\n\nThe gift is energy for collective goals. The challenge is conflict within groups, or burning out for a cause.\n\nMars's sign shows how you act with others.\n\nYour friends tend to be energetic doers rather than talkers, and you may meet them through sport, protest or shared projects. When a friendship ends, it may end with a bang; when it lasts, it is fiercely loyal.",magic:"Communal and activist magic suits you: spells for a cause, group protection and team blessings. Tuesdays and Saturdays suit you. Carnelian, Amethyst and Hematite help.",shadow:"Conflict in groups and burnout for causes."},{simple:"With Mars in the twelfth house your drive works behind the scenes. Anger may be hidden, and energy goes into private or spiritual work.",detailed:"With Mars in the twelfth house, energy is private. You may work alone, behind the scenes, or in hospitals, prisons or retreats. Anger may be hard to express directly and can turn inward.\n\nThe gift is quiet strength and spiritual courage. The challenge is hidden anger, self-sabotage and fatigue.\n\nTraditional astrologers counted the twelfth as the house of hidden enemies; Mars here asks you to know your own hidden fire.\n\nPhysical outlets help: swimming, walking alone, martial arts practised as meditation. Many people with this placement find their strength in service, fighting for those who cannot fight for themselves, often unseen.",magic:"Spiritual warrior magic suits you: protection during sleep, meditation with movement, and banishing hidden fears. Tuesdays and Mondays suit you. Obsidian, Amethyst and mugwort help.",shadow:"Hidden anger and self-sabotage."}]},3056,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MERCURY_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n=[{simple:"With Mercury in the first house you come across as quick, curious and talkative. Your mind is part of your personality, and people meet your thoughts first.",detailed:"Ancient astrologers called the first house the joy of Mercury: the place it rejoices. With Mercury here you tend to be alert, expressive and youthful, with a face and hands that move as you talk. You may be known for your wit, your questions or your opinions, and you often think on your feet.\n\nYou can talk to anyone and adapt to almost any room, which serves you well in sales, teaching, media and any job that meets the public. The cost is nervous energy and a tendency to live in the head, explaining yourself rather than simply being. Sleep and stillness may need deliberate care.\n\nThe sign Mercury is in shows how that mind works: fast and fiery, slow and solid, deep or dreamy.",magic:"You are a natural spell-speaker: spoken charms, affirmations and sigils drawn on your own skin suit you. Wednesdays and Mercury hours are your times for self-work. Citrine and lavender keep a busy head clear.",shadow:"Nervous restlessness and over-explaining."},{simple:"With Mercury in the second house you think a lot about money and value, and you can earn through your mind, words or trade.",detailed:"The second house is resources and self-worth. Mercury here gives a practical, commercial mind: you are often good with numbers, prices, negotiating and spotting a bargain. You may earn through writing, teaching, talking, trading, or more than one job at once.\n\nYou can think your way to income, and you often value knowledge as a resource in itself: books, courses and skills feel like wealth. Worry about money can loop in your head, and you may value yourself only for what your mind produces.\n\nMercury's sign shows the style; its aspects show whether thinking about money calms or stirs you.",magic:"Money and word magic together: written prosperity petitions, a ledger blessed at each new Moon, and charms for good trade. Wednesdays and Thursdays suit you. Citrine, Green Aventurine and basil draw clever abundance.",shadow:"Money worry and restless spending."},{simple:"With Mercury in the third house, its natural place, you love to learn, talk, write and wander locally. Your mind is quick and always busy.",detailed:"The third house is Gemini's natural house, and Mercury is strong and comfortable here. You are curious about everything near you: neighbours, siblings, local news, books, short trips. You may write, teach or work with information, and you often have several conversations going at once.\n\nFluency comes easily, and so does a lifelong appetite for learning; many people with this placement are still taking classes at eighty. The difficulty is scattering: gossip, too many tabs open, and trouble with stillness.\n\nThe third house's old link with omens and rites can make you a sharp reader of signs as well as of books.",magic:"Word, travel and omen magic suit you: letter spells, travel blessings, divination by signs, and a grimoire kept in your own words. Wednesdays are yours. Citrine and peppermint help; Hermes, god of roads and messages, is a fitting patron.",shadow:"Scattered attention and idle talk."},{simple:"With Mercury in the fourth house your mind is rooted in home and family. Much thinking, talking and learning happens at home.",detailed:"The fourth house is home and roots. With Mercury here, the home is often full of books, talk and comings and goings. You may work from home, have learned a great deal from family, or think often about the past and your ancestry. Family conversations shaped your mind, for better or worse.\n\nYou often have a deep memory and a mind for history, genealogy and heritage, and you may be the family's storyteller or archivist. Dwelling on the past is the risk, as are family arguments that never quite end.\n\nMercury's sign shows the kind of home your mind needs: lively or quiet, orderly or full of piles of paper.",magic:"Hearth and memory magic suits you: ancestor research as devotion, family recipes as spells, and a written home blessing kept by the door. Wednesdays and Mondays suit you. Fluorite, Moonstone and rosemary (for remembrance) help.",shadow:"Dwelling on the past, and family quarrels."},{simple:"With Mercury in the fifth house your mind is playful and creative. You love games, stories, wit and making things with words.",detailed:"The fifth house is play and creativity. With Mercury here you have a playful mind: puzzles, games, storytelling, flirting and creative writing come naturally. You may enjoy teaching children, writing for them, or simply keeping a youthful wit all your life.\n\nCreative intelligence and fun are your gifts, and you may fall for people who make you laugh. Flippancy is the risk: not taking things seriously when they need it, or gambling with words and ideas for the thrill.\n\nMercury's sign shows how your mind likes to play.",magic:"Creative word magic suits you: writing spells as poems, games of divination, and creative sigils. Wednesdays and Fridays suit you. Citrine, Carnelian and mint keep play bright.",shadow:"Flippancy and verbal games."},{simple:"With Mercury in the sixth house your mind is busy with work, health and routine. You are an organiser, an analyst and a problem-solver.",detailed:"The sixth house is daily work and health. With Mercury here, you think a lot about how things work and how to improve them. You may be excellent at detailed, practical work, and drawn to health, medicine, editing, accounting, technical roles or anything with systems.\n\nEfficiency and analytical skill make you valuable at work, and you may be the person colleagues ask when something breaks. Worry is the cost, especially about health, and nervous tension can show in the body: digestion, breathing, sleep.\n\nMercury's sign shows how your mind likes to work; a tidy list is often your best medicine.",magic:"Practical and healing magic suits you: herbal study, cleansing rituals, a tidy workspace blessed, and lists that work like spells. Wednesdays suit you. Amazonite, Fluorite and fennel calm a busy, worried mind.",shadow:"Worry and nervous tension."},{simple:"With Mercury in the seventh house you think best with someone else. Conversation and partnership sharpen your mind.",detailed:"The seventh house is partnership. With Mercury here you need a partner you can talk to, and you often think things through in dialogue. You may be drawn to law, counselling, negotiation, agency or client work, and you may attract clever, talkative partners, sometimes younger ones.\n\nDiplomacy and an ability to understand others' points of view are strengths. The risk is relying on others to make up your mind, or turning partnership into a running debate.\n\nContracts are a seventh-house matter; read them carefully, as Mercury here notices the small print best when you slow down.",magic:"Relationship and agreement magic suits you: honest communication spells, contract blessings and sweetening jars. Wednesdays and Fridays suit you. Blue Lace Agate, Rose Quartz and lavender help.",shadow:"Arguing with partners, or letting them think for you."},{simple:"With Mercury in the eighth house your mind goes deep. You are drawn to research, secrets, psychology and the mysteries.",detailed:"The eighth house is depth and transformation. With Mercury here you have an investigative mind: you want to know what is hidden, and you are good at research, psychology, finance, tax, insurance and the occult. You may think a lot about death, sex and power, and talk about them more frankly than most.\n\nPenetrating insight is your gift; you hear what people are not saying. Obsessive thinking, secrecy and suspicion are the risks, and so is keeping secrets that weigh on you.\n\nMercury's sign shows how your mind digs, and where it might find gold.",magic:"Occult and divinatory magic suits you: tarot, scrying, research as devotion, and written banishings. Wednesdays and Tuesdays suit you. Obsidian, Labradorite and Wormwood sharpen the inner eye.",shadow:"Obsessive thinking and suspicion."},{simple:"With Mercury in the ninth house your mind reaches for big ideas, faith and faraway places. You are a natural student and teacher.",detailed:"The ninth house is philosophy and higher learning. With Mercury here you love ideas that explain the world: religion, philosophy, law, languages, cultures and travel. You may study deeply, teach, translate or publish.\n\nA broad, curious mind is your gift, and you often see how different systems of thought connect. Preachiness is the risk, as is skipping the details in favour of the big picture.\n\nMercury's sign shows the kind of truth you seek, and whether you seek it in books, on roads or in conversation.",magic:"Seeking and study magic suits you: bibliomancy, study as devotion, travel blessings and prayer. Wednesdays and Thursdays suit you. Turquoise, Lapis Lazuli and Sage help.",shadow:"Preachiness and carelessness with facts."},{simple:"With Mercury in the tenth house your mind is your career. You may work with words, ideas or communication in public.",detailed:"The tenth house is career and reputation. With Mercury here you may be known for your intelligence, writing or speaking. Careers in media, teaching, business, law, technology or trade often suit you, and you may have more than one over a lifetime, or at once.\n\nA clever, communicative public presence opens doors. Restlessness in career is the risk, as is a reputation built on words that must then be backed by deeds.\n\nMercury's sign shows how you communicate in public; its aspects show how easily your voice is heard.",magic:"Career and word magic suits you: petitions for success, blessing your work tools, and spells for a good interview. Wednesdays and Saturdays suit you. Citrine, Fluorite and bay laurel help.",shadow:"Restless career changes, and words without deeds."},{simple:"With Mercury in the eleventh house you think best among friends. Networks, groups and shared ideas excite your mind.",detailed:"The eleventh house is friends and groups. With Mercury here you love conversations with friends, group projects, societies and online communities. You may be the connector of your social circle, introducing people and passing on news, and you are often drawn to causes and the future.\n\nYour mind is made for collaboration and brainstorming. The risk is being swayed by the group's thinking, or having many acquaintances and few deep friends.\n\nMercury's sign shows the kind of friends who stimulate you.",magic:"Communal magic suits you: group sigils, online circles, friendship spells and shared divination. Wednesdays and Saturdays suit you. Amethyst, Citrine and lavender help.",shadow:"Following the crowd's thinking."},{simple:"With Mercury in the twelfth house your mind is intuitive, private and dreamy. You think deeply but may keep your thoughts hidden.",detailed:"The twelfth house is solitude and the hidden. With Mercury here your mind works in images, dreams and intuitions. You may be a private thinker, a writer who works alone, or someone who finds words hard to speak but easy to write.\n\nIntuition and a rich inner life are your gifts, and you may sense things before you can explain them. Self-doubt about your mind is common, especially if early schooling did not suit you, and secret worries can grow in silence.\n\nJournaling, meditation and creative writing help you hear yourself.",magic:"Dream and meditative magic suits you: dream journals, automatic writing, meditation and private devotion. Wednesdays and Mondays suit you. Amethyst, Moonstone and mugwort help.",shadow:"Secret worries and silenced thoughts."}]},3057,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MOON_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o=[{simple:"With the Moon in the first house your feelings show on your face. You are sensitive, responsive and changeable, and people sense your moods at once.",detailed:"The Moon on or near the Ascendant puts your emotional life in plain view. You react visibly to your surroundings, absorb atmospheres and often look different from one week to the next. Many people find you approachable and caring, and strangers may tell you their troubles on a bus.\n\nYour emotional honesty and talent for reading a room are real gifts, and you may be drawn to nurturing roles at work and at home. The cost is that moods can rule how you meet the world, and other people's feelings can feel like your own. Anchoring yourself through routine, rest and time alone helps you tell the difference.\n\nThe Moon's sign and phase at your birth add much to this picture; traditional astrologers read a Moon this close to the horizon as strong and influential on the body and health, and some say your body follows the monthly tides more than most.",magic:"Your own body is a lunar instrument: track your moods against the Moon's phases in a journal, and time self-work accordingly. Mondays and the full Moon suit self-blessing. Moonstone and Selenite worn on the body steady and protect.",shadow:"Moodiness that rules every meeting."},{simple:"With the Moon in the second house you feel safe when you have enough. Money, possessions and comforts are emotionally important to you.",detailed:"The Moon is exalted in Taurus, the second sign, and it often sits comfortably in the second house too. Your emotional security is tied to resources: savings, a stocked cupboard, familiar belongings, a body that is well fed. Income may rise and fall like a tide, and you may spend or save according to your mood.\n\nYou often have a good instinct for looking after money and things, and you may keep objects for their memories as much as their use. When you feel low, a little comfort helps; when you feel unsafe, you may cling to what you own. Learning that your worth is not your bank balance is the long lesson.\n\nWork that involves food, care, homes or the public can suit you, and your earning may follow the needs of the people around you.",magic:"Lunar prosperity magic suits you: money spells begun at the new Moon and grown through the waxing, moon-charged coins in a jar, and gratitude for what you have at each full Moon. Moonstone, Green Aventurine and basil help.",shadow:"Emotional spending, or never feeling you have enough."},{simple:"With the Moon in the third house you process feelings by talking, writing and moving about. You need conversation and variety to feel at ease.",detailed:"The third house is the joy of the Moon in ancient astrology, called the house of the goddess, and the Moon is said to rejoice here. Your feelings move through words: journals, letters, long phone calls with a sibling, voice notes to a friend. You may love short trips, local walks and the familiar faces of your neighbourhood.\n\nYou can name feelings and help others name theirs, and you are often a lively, sympathetic correspondent. The difficulty is a restless, worrying mind: thoughts can circle at night, and it is easy to talk about a feeling instead of feeling it.\n\nThe old link of this house with rites, omens and the goddess suits a lunar mind well: you may notice signs and synchronicities more than most, and daily devotions can steady you.",magic:"Word and omen magic suits you: a moon journal, letter spells, divination by signs, and blessings for daily travel. Mondays and Wednesdays suit you. Moonstone, Blue Lace Agate and Lemon Balm calm a busy heart.",shadow:"Restless worry and talking feelings to death."},{simple:"With the Moon in the fourth house you need a true home. Family, roots and a private nest are at the heart of your emotional life.",detailed:"The fourth house is the Moon's natural place, the house of Cancer and of home. Your emotional life is rooted in family, memory and where you live. You may be deeply attached to a parent (often the mother), to a place, or to family tradition, and you may keep recipes, photographs and stories that others forget.\n\nYou have a strong instinct for nurturing and for making a home feel safe, and others often come to your kitchen to be comforted. The risk is being ruled by family patterns, or feeling lost and unsettled without your nest. Some people with this placement move often, searching for the right home; others never leave.\n\nThe fourth house also speaks of later life; many astrologers read the Moon here as a sign that home becomes more and more precious with age.",magic:"Hearth magic is natural for you: home blessings, ancestor altars, kitchen witchery and moon water for the household. Mondays and the full Moon suit you. Moonstone, Selenite and jasmine bless the home.",shadow:"Clinging to the nest, and family patterns that rule you."},{simple:"With the Moon in the fifth house you need joy, play and creative expression. Romance and children can be emotionally central to you.",detailed:"The fifth house is pleasure, creativity, romance and children. With the Moon here, you feel most yourself when you are playing, creating or in love. You may be very attached to children, your own or others', or to your own inner child, and your creative work is likely to be deeply personal and emotional.\n\nYou bring warmth and delight to the people around you, and you can make an ordinary evening feel like a party. Moods can swing with your love life, though, and you may need constant fun or reassurance to feel okay; romance can carry more emotional drama than it needs to.\n\nCreative routines help: a regular time to make something, however small, keeps your heart fed.",magic:"Joyful, creative magic suits you: art as offering, play as ritual, fertility spells and moonlit celebration. Mondays and Fridays suit you. Moonstone, Carnelian and rose bring joy.",shadow:"Emotional drama, and needing constant delight."},{simple:"With the Moon in the sixth house you feel safe through routine, useful work and care for the body. Your health and moods are closely linked.",detailed:"The sixth house is daily work, health and service. With the Moon here, your emotional wellbeing depends on routine and on feeling useful. You may be a natural carer at work or at home, and you may find comfort in tidying, cooking, gardening or looking after animals.\n\nYour body reacts strongly to stress, often through digestion, sleep or the skin, and it tells you clearly when something is wrong. You can bring a nurturing touch to any workplace. The risk is emotional overwork, worrying about health, or caring for everyone at the cost of yourself.\n\nWork that changes with the seasons or involves people's daily needs often suits you; a rigid job with no human warmth does not.",magic:"Healing and routine magic suits you: herbal teas, cleansing rituals, a daily devotion and care for animals. Mondays and Wednesdays suit you. Moonstone, Amazonite and Chamomile soothe.",shadow:"Worry, and caring for others at the cost of your health."},{simple:"With the Moon in the seventh house you need close partnership to feel safe. You are sensitive to others and find comfort in one-to-one bonds.",detailed:"The seventh house is partnership and the people you meet face to face. With the Moon here, your emotional life is bound up with partners and close others. You may seek a nurturing partner, or play the nurturer yourself, and you often marry or partner young or for emotional security.\n\nYou are emotionally attuned to others, a good listener and often a sought-after confidant or counsellor. Your moods may follow the moods of those closest to you, and being alone can feel unsafe. The work is to keep your own feelings while caring for someone else's.\n\nWorking with the public, clients or patients can suit you well, since you sense what people need.",magic:"Relationship magic suits you: sweetening spells, partnership blessings, and love-drawing at the waxing Moon. Mondays and Fridays suit you. Moonstone, Rose Quartz and jasmine support tender bonds.",shadow:"Emotional dependence on partners."},{simple:"With the Moon in the eighth house your feelings run deep and private. You need emotional intimacy, and you are drawn to life's mysteries.",detailed:"The eighth house is intimacy, death, shared resources and transformation. With the Moon here, your emotional life is intense and often hidden. You may have met loss or crisis early, or felt things in your family that nobody spoke about. You are drawn to depth, and you can be a powerful, steady presence when others are in crisis.\n\nEmotional courage and psychic sensitivity are part of this placement, and many people with it are drawn to therapy, hospice, research or the occult. Trust comes slowly, and you may hold feelings so privately that partners never quite know where they stand.\n\nShared money, inheritance and a partner's resources can be emotionally charged; clear agreements keep the peace.",magic:"Deep, lunar magic suits you: dark Moon rituals, ancestor work, shadow work and divination. Mondays and Tuesdays suit you. Moonstone, Obsidian and mugwort support the work.",shadow:"Secrecy, intensity and fear of being vulnerable."},{simple:"With the Moon in the ninth house you need meaning, faith and wide horizons to feel safe. Travel and learning nourish your soul.",detailed:"The ninth house is faith, philosophy, travel and higher learning. With the Moon here, you feel at home in the search for meaning. You may love travel, foreign places, religion, philosophy or study, and your beliefs are deeply emotional: you believe with your heart.\n\nYou may find home far from where you were born, or feel a strange homesickness for places you have never been. Faith and ritual can comfort you deeply. The risk is restlessness, or escaping feelings into big ideas and the next journey.\n\nTeaching, publishing and travel work can suit you, as can any role that cares for people far from home.",magic:"Seeking and devotional magic suits you: pilgrimage, travel blessings, study as devotion and divination. Mondays and Thursdays suit you. Moonstone, Turquoise and Sage support the search.",shadow:"Restless searching, and feelings escaped into ideas."},{simple:"With the Moon in the tenth house your feelings are on public view. You may be drawn to caring or public roles, and your reputation matters emotionally.",detailed:"The tenth house is career and public life. With the Moon here, your emotional life is tied to your work and reputation. You may be drawn to caring professions, to work with the public, to food, homes or history, or to roles that change over time. A parent, often the mother, may have shaped your ambitions strongly.\n\nYou have public warmth and an instinct for what people need, and people often feel you understand them. Your standing may rise and fall like the Moon, and criticism at work can hurt deeply. Feeling exposed is the price of being visible.\n\nTraditional astrologers counted the Moon at the top of the chart as prominent and popular; its sign shows the kind of public role that suits you.",magic:"Public and success magic suits you: career spells begun at the new Moon, blessings for your work, and glamour for public moments. Mondays and Saturdays suit you. Moonstone, Citrine and bay laurel help.",shadow:"Feeling exposed, and moods that shake your reputation."},{simple:"With the Moon in the eleventh house you feel safe among friends and in community. Shared hopes and groups nourish you.",detailed:"The eleventh house is friends, groups and hopes, and the joy of Jupiter in ancient astrology. With the Moon here, your emotional life is tied to friendship and community. You may have many friends, or a few who feel like family, and you care about causes and the future.\n\nYou have a talent for friendship and belonging, and you may be the one who keeps the group chat warm. Your moods can follow the crowd, and you may depend on the group's approval. Friendships may change with the phases of your life, which is natural.\n\nCommunity work, clubs and covens can be a second home for you.",magic:"Communal magic suits you: group rituals, coven work, friendship spells and full Moon circles. Mondays and Saturdays suit you. Moonstone, Amethyst and lavender support connection.",shadow:"Needing the group's approval to feel okay."},{simple:"With the Moon in the twelfth house your feelings run hidden and deep. You need solitude, rest and spiritual practice to feel safe.",detailed:"The twelfth house is solitude, the unconscious and the hidden. With the Moon here, your feelings may be private, even to yourself, and you may only know what you felt days later. You may be very sensitive, psychic, and in need of regular retreat. Dreams may be vivid and meaningful.\n\nYou often have a deep inner life and great compassion, and you may be drawn to care for people others overlook: in hospitals, hospices, prisons or shelters. The risk is hiding feelings, absorbing others' pain, and loneliness. Family may have carried a hidden sorrow you picked up young.\n\nThe twelfth was a hard house in ancient astrology; modern astrologers see the Moon here as a gifted, intuitive soul who needs a sanctuary.",magic:"Dream and spiritual magic suits you: dreamwork, meditation, ritual baths and dark Moon retreat. Mondays suit you. Moonstone, Amethyst and mugwort support the work.",shadow:"Hidden feelings and absorbed pain."}]},3058,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"NEPTUNE_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n=[{simple:"With Neptune in the first house you come across as gentle, dreamy and hard to define. People see in you what they want to see.",detailed:"Neptune near the Ascendant gives a soft, mysterious or glamorous presence. You may be very sensitive to your surroundings, absorb others' feelings, and seem to change with the company you keep. Many people with this placement are artistic, psychic or deeply compassionate.\n\nBecause people project onto you, it can be hard to feel truly seen. Strong boundaries, regular cleansing and knowing your own wants help you stay yourself.\n\nIn relationships you are tender and compassionate, and you need a partner who sees the real you. At work you suit the arts, healing, photography, film or anything with imagination.",magic:"Glamour and veiling magic is natural for you, as is cleansing after crowds. Ritual baths, protective amulets and dreamwork suit you. Amethyst, Aquamarine and mugwort help.",shadow:"Losing yourself in others' projections."},{simple:"With Neptune in the second house money and values may be idealistic or unclear. You may earn through art, healing or spiritual work.",detailed:"With Neptune in the house of resources, money can slip through your fingers or arrive from inspired work. You may value spiritual or artistic things over material ones, and be generous to a fault.\n\nClarity about money, clear records and honest budgets protect your dreams. Confusion and being taken advantage of are the risks.\n\nWork in the arts, healing or charities may suit you, and money may come through inspiration more than planning. Clear accounts and a trusted adviser help.",magic:"Inspired prosperity magic suits you, with practical checks: money spells for creative work and clarity rituals for finances. Amethyst, Green Aventurine and jasmine help.",shadow:"Financial confusion and over-giving."},{simple:"With Neptune in the third house your mind is imaginative and intuitive. You think in images and pick up what is not said.",detailed:"With Neptune in the third house, everyday thought is poetic. You may be a gifted writer, musician or storyteller, with strong intuition. Learning may be non-linear, and details can slip.\n\nYour words can heal and inspire. Confusion, forgetfulness and misunderstanding are the risks; writing things down helps.\n\nSiblings may be elusive or idealised, and early schooling may have felt dreamy. Poetry, music, photography and film may be natural languages for you.",magic:"Dream and word magic suits you: automatic writing, poetry as prayer and divination. Amethyst, Celestite and lavender help.",shadow:"Confusion and misunderstanding."},{simple:"With Neptune in the fourth house home is a sanctuary or a mystery. Family may be idealised, elusive or spiritual.",detailed:"With Neptune at the root of the chart, home and family can be dreamy, confusing or deeply spiritual. A parent may have been absent, idealised or unwell. You may long for an ideal home, or live near water.\n\nYou can make home a sacred sanctuary. Idealising family or escaping into home are the risks.\n\nA parent may have been absent, idealised or unwell, and you may have learned early to sense moods. Home near water or with a garden can be deeply healing.",magic:"Sacred hearth magic suits you: a home altar, ancestor dreamwork, moon water and home cleansing. Moonstone, Amethyst and jasmine help.",shadow:"Idealising family and escaping into home."},{simple:"With Neptune in the fifth house romance is idealistic and creativity inspired. You love beauty, music and imagination.",detailed:"With Neptune in the fifth house, pleasure is dreamy. You may be artistically gifted, love music and film, and fall in love with ideals. Romance can be magical or disillusioning.\n\nYour creativity can be truly inspired. Romantic illusion and escapism are the risks.\n\nChildren may be imaginative and sensitive, and you may be a gentle, inspiring parent. Creative work can be truly inspired, especially in music and film.",magic:"Creative and devotional magic suits you: art as prayer, music as ritual, and love spells for clarity. Amethyst, Rose Quartz and jasmine help.",shadow:"Romantic illusion."},{simple:"With Neptune in the sixth house you serve with compassion. Health may be sensitive, and work needs meaning.",detailed:"With Neptune in the sixth house, daily work wants to be meaningful. You may be drawn to healing, care, the arts or spiritual service. Health may be sensitive to substances and stress.\n\nYou can bring compassion to daily work. Unclear routines, sensitivity and burnout are the risks; gentle, regular care keeps you well.\n\nWork in healing, care, the arts or spiritual service suits you. Sensitivity to medicines, alcohol and stress means gentle care for your body.",magic:"Healing and cleansing magic suits you: herbal remedies (beside proper care), ritual baths and gentle routine. Amethyst, Amazonite and Chamomile help.",shadow:"Burnout and unclear health issues."},{simple:"With Neptune in the seventh house you idealise partners. Love can be spiritual and compassionate, or confusing.",detailed:"With Neptune in the seventh house, partnership is dreamy. You may seek a soulmate, attract artistic or sensitive partners, or find yourself rescuing others.\n\nYou can love unconditionally. Idealisation, deception and self-sacrifice are the risks; seeing partners clearly is the work.\n\nPartners may be artistic, spiritual or in need of help. Business partnerships need clear contracts. Love can be a spiritual path for you.",magic:"Clear-sighted love magic suits you: spells for clarity in love, partnership blessings and self-love. Rose Quartz, Aquamarine and rose help.",shadow:"Idealising and rescuing partners."},{simple:"With Neptune in the eighth house intimacy is spiritual and deep. You may have strong psychic gifts.",detailed:"With Neptune in the eighth house, the depths are mystical. You may have psychic experiences, a deep connection to the dead, or unclear situations around shared money.\n\nYou can be a gifted medium or healer. Confusion in shared resources and boundary loss are the risks.\n\nShared finances and inheritance need clear paperwork. You may be drawn to mediumship, hospice work or the mysteries of death.",magic:"Mediumship and deep magic suits you, with protection: ancestor work, scrying and dreamwork. Amethyst, Obsidian and mugwort help.",shadow:"Boundary loss and financial confusion."},{simple:"With Neptune in the ninth house faith is mystical. You are drawn to spirituality, travel and the search for the divine.",detailed:"With Neptune in the ninth house, belief is devotional. You may be drawn to mysticism, pilgrimage, foreign spiritual traditions and art.\n\nYou can inspire faith in others. Following false teachers and escapism are the risks.\n\nYou may be drawn to mysticism, pilgrimage, foreign spiritual traditions and art. Travel by sea or to holy places can move you deeply.",magic:"Devotional magic suits you: prayer, meditation, pilgrimage and dreamwork. Amethyst, Turquoise and Sandalwood help.",shadow:"Spiritual escapism."},{simple:"With Neptune in the tenth house career may be artistic, spiritual or caring. Your public image can be glamorous or unclear.",detailed:"With Neptune near the Midheaven, vocation is a calling. You may work in the arts, film, music, healing or ministry. Public image may be idealised.\n\nYou can inspire many. Career confusion and a blurred image are the risks.\n\nYour public image may be glamorous, idealised or unclear. Work in the arts, film, music, healing or ministry suits you.",magic:"Inspired career magic suits you: spells for a calling, glamour for public moments, and clarity rituals. Amethyst, Citrine and jasmine help.",shadow:"Career confusion."},{simple:"With Neptune in the eleventh house friendships are compassionate and ideals high. You dream of a better world.",detailed:"With Neptune in the eleventh house, community is spiritual. You may be drawn to idealistic groups, have artistic friends, or dream big for humanity.\n\nYou can inspire collective hope. Disillusionment with friends and groups is the risk.\n\nFriends may be artists, healers or dreamers, and you may be drawn to spiritual or charitable groups. Your hopes are for a kinder world.",magic:"Communal spiritual magic suits you: group meditation, circles and spells for a cause. Amethyst, Aquamarine and lavender help.",shadow:"Disillusionment with friends."},{simple:"With Neptune in the twelfth house, its natural place, your inner life is vast and spiritual. You may have strong intuition and a need for solitude.",detailed:"The twelfth house is Pisces's natural house, and Neptune is at home here. You may be deeply intuitive, psychic, artistic and compassionate, with a rich dream life.\n\nYou can access profound spiritual depth. Escapism and isolation are the risks.\n\nYou may have strong intuition, a need for solitude, and a rich dream life. Work in hospitals, retreats or the arts suits you.",magic:"Dream and spiritual magic is natural for you: dreamwork, meditation, retreat and devotion. Amethyst, Moonstone and mugwort help; Neptune and Poseidon, lords of the deep, are its old patrons.",shadow:"Escapism and isolation."}]},3059,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"NORTH_NODE_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SOUTH_NODE_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const o=[{simple:"With the North Node in the first house you grow by putting yourself first and finding your own way. Your old habit is to live for partners.",detailed:"The North Node in the first house always pairs with the South Node in the seventh. Relationship comes easily to you, perhaps too easily: you may define yourself through partners, wait for others to lead, or reshape yourself to keep the peace. You can be a superb partner, adviser or right hand.\n\nThe growth is toward the self: knowing what you want before you ask what others want, taking initiative, looking after your body and appearance as your own, and being willing to disappoint people now and then. It can feel selfish at first. Over the years it makes your partnerships a choice rather than a need, and others often find you easier to love once you are more fully there.\n\nMedieval astrologers read the North Node rising as increase and visibility; modern astrologers read it as a life asked to become its own author.",magic:"Self-trust magic supports you: a self-dedication rite, courage spells before decisions that are yours alone, and a personal protection charm. Tuesdays and the new Moon suit you. Carnelian, Bloodstone and basil help.",shadow:"Losing yourself in others, or overcorrecting into selfishness."},{simple:"With the North Node in the second house you grow by building your own resources and trusting your own values. Your old habit is relying on others' money or living in crisis.",detailed:"The North Node in the second house pairs with the South Node in the eighth. Intensity, shared resources and other people's power come easily: you may lean on a partner's income, be drawn to dramatic situations, or feel most alive in crisis.\n\nThe growth is toward simple self-reliance: earning your own money, knowing what you value, enjoying ordinary pleasures and building slowly. Calm may feel dull at first, almost suspicious. In time it becomes a foundation that lets you meet the deep places from strength instead of need.\n\nVenus and the sign on this cusp show what kind of steady worth you are building.",magic:"Grounding prosperity magic supports you: a money jar fed weekly, gardening as devotion, and gratitude rituals for what is already yours. Fridays and the waxing Moon suit you. Green Aventurine, Moss Agate and thyme help.",shadow:"Dependence on others' resources, and restlessness when life is calm."},{simple:"With the North Node in the third house you grow by curiosity, listening and connecting with the people near you. Your old habit is preaching big truths.",detailed:"The North Node in the third house pairs with the South Node in the ninth. Philosophy, belief and the big picture come easily; you may be used to having the answers, travelling far in search of meaning, or holding opinions strongly.\n\nThe growth is toward the near and the particular: asking questions, learning from neighbours, siblings and everyday conversation, writing things down, and checking the facts. Wisdom becomes real when it can be explained simply to the person next to you.\n\nMercury's place shows how your mind learns best on this road.",magic:"Word and curiosity magic supports you: daily journaling, a one-card draw each morning, letter spells, and blessings for your street and neighbourhood. Wednesdays suit you. Citrine, Fluorite and peppermint help.",shadow:"Lecturing the people near you instead of learning from them."},{simple:"With the North Node in the fourth house you grow by tending home, family and your own feelings. Your old habit is hiding in career and achievement.",detailed:"The North Node in the fourth house pairs with the South Node in the tenth. Public roles, ambition and responsibility come easily; you may have been the capable one early, or built your sense of worth on achievement.\n\nThe growth is toward roots: making a home that truly holds you, tending family (born or chosen), letting yourself feel and be cared for, and building private life as seriously as you once built a career. This is not giving up ambition; it is giving it a hearth to come home to.\n\nThe Moon's place shows how you are best nourished on this road.",magic:"Hearth magic supports you: home blessings, ancestor offerings, kitchen witchery and a simple evening ritual at home. Mondays and the full Moon suit you. Moonstone, Rose Quartz and Lemon Balm help.",shadow:"Achievement as a hiding place from feeling."},{simple:"With the North Node in the fifth house you grow by creating, playing and loving boldly. Your old habit is hiding in the group.",detailed:"The North Node in the fifth house pairs with the South Node in the eleventh. Group life, friendship and detachment come easily; you may be at home in causes, networks and crowds, and uneasy with personal attention.\n\nThe growth is toward the heart: making things that are yours, falling in love, playing for its own sake, delighting in children or your own inner child, and letting yourself be seen as an individual. The risk feels like ego; it turns out to be joy, and joy you can then share with the group.\n\nThe Sun's place shows where your heart wants to shine.",magic:"Creative magic supports you: art as offering, play as ritual, love-drawing and joyful celebration. Sundays and Fridays suit you. Sunstone, Carnelian and Sunflower help.",shadow:"Hiding in the crowd to avoid being seen."},{simple:"With the North Node in the sixth house you grow by practical service, routine and caring for your body. Your old habit is escape and retreat.",detailed:"The North Node in the sixth house pairs with the South Node in the twelfth. Solitude, imagination, spirituality and escape come easily; you may drift, rescue, or withdraw when the world is too much.\n\nThe growth is toward the daily and the useful: good routines, steady work, honest health care, skill, and service with clear edges. Order may feel like a cage at first; it turns out to be the vessel your sensitivity needed.\n\nMercury's place shows how you are best organised on this road.",magic:"Routine and healing magic supports you: a short daily devotion, herbcraft, cleansing, and blessing your workspace. Wednesdays suit you. Amazonite, Fluorite and fennel help.",shadow:"Escape from daily life, and helping until you are drained."},{simple:"With the North Node in the seventh house you grow by partnership and cooperation. Your old habit is going it alone.",detailed:"The North Node in the seventh house pairs with the South Node in the first. Independence comes easily; you may be used to relying only on yourself, deciding quickly and alone, and finding other people's needs a distraction.\n\nThe growth is toward the other: partnership, listening, compromise, sharing credit and letting someone else's view change your mind. It can feel like losing yourself at first; it turns out to be a larger self. Many people with this placement find their life's work through a significant partner or client.\n\nVenus's place shows how you relate best on this road.",magic:"Partnership magic supports you: sweetening spells, partnership blessings and honest agreements made by candlelight. Fridays suit you. Rose Quartz, Lapis Lazuli and rose help.",shadow:"Going it alone by habit, not choice."},{simple:"With the North Node in the eighth house you grow by sharing, intimacy and letting go. Your old habit is holding on to your own.",detailed:"The North Node in the eighth house pairs with the South Node in the second. Self-reliance, security and comfort come easily; you may be very good at building and keeping, and wary of anything that means depending on someone else.\n\nThe growth is toward the deep: real intimacy, shared resources, trusting others with your money and your feelings, facing loss and change, and letting what is finished end. Change may feel like loss; it turns out to be renewal.\n\nMars and Pluto, the rulers of Scorpio, show how you meet change on this road.",magic:"Transformation magic supports you: release rituals at the waning Moon, shadow work, and divination. Tuesdays and the dark Moon suit you. Obsidian, Labradorite and Wormwood help.",shadow:"Holding on too tightly to what you have."},{simple:"With the North Node in the ninth house you grow by faith, travel and higher learning. Your old habit is busy, local chatter.",detailed:"The North Node in the ninth house pairs with the South Node in the third. Information, talk and quick connection come easily; you may know a little about everything and stay very busy.\n\nThe growth is toward meaning: choosing a direction, studying deeply, travelling far, exploring faith and philosophy, and trusting your intuition about the big picture. Committing to a belief can feel risky at first; it gives your life a compass.\n\nJupiter's place shows how you grow on this road.",magic:"Seeking magic supports you: pilgrimage, travel blessings, study as devotion and prayer in your own words. Thursdays suit you. Turquoise, Lapis Lazuli and Sage help.",shadow:"Busyness instead of meaning."},{simple:"With the North Node in the tenth house you grow by stepping into public life and responsibility. Your old habit is staying safe at home.",detailed:"The North Node in the tenth house pairs with the South Node in the fourth. Home, family and emotional care come easily; you may be the one who keeps the family together, or retreat to the familiar when the world feels cold.\n\nThe growth is toward contribution: a vocation, a public role, your own authority and a reputation built on purpose. Stepping out can feel exposing; over time it becomes the work you were made for, and your family benefits too.\n\nSaturn's place shows how you build on this road.",magic:"Career magic supports you: success spells, blessings for public work, and a ritual for each step of responsibility you take. Saturdays and Sundays suit you. Onyx, Citrine and bay laurel help.",shadow:"Hiding in the nest when the world calls."},{simple:"With the North Node in the eleventh house you grow by community and shared hopes. Your old habit is needing the spotlight.",detailed:"The North Node in the eleventh house pairs with the South Node in the fifth. Self-expression, romance and personal creativity come easily; you may be used to being the centre, or to measuring life by personal delight.\n\nThe growth is toward the collective: friendship, groups, causes, and working for a future that includes many people. Sharing the stage can feel like losing yourself; it turns out to be belonging.\n\nSaturn and Uranus show how you connect on this road.",magic:"Communal magic supports you: group rituals, friendship spells and wishes made for others at the new Moon. Saturdays suit you. Amethyst, Aquamarine and lavender help.",shadow:"Needing to be the centre when the group needs you."},{simple:"With the North Node in the twelfth house you grow by solitude, faith and surrender. Your old habit is busy, anxious work.",detailed:"The North Node in the twelfth house pairs with the South Node in the sixth. Routine, analysis, service and worry come easily; you may be most comfortable when busy and useful, and uneasy with rest.\n\nThe growth is toward the unseen: rest, retreat, spiritual practice, compassion, dreams and trust in something larger than your to-do list. Letting go can feel frightening at first; it becomes peace.\n\nJupiter and Neptune show how you open to spirit on this road.",magic:"Spiritual magic supports you: meditation, dreamwork, retreat and devotion. Thursdays and Mondays suit you. Amethyst, Moonstone and mugwort help.",shadow:"Worry in place of trust."}],t=[{simple:"With the South Node in the first house, self-reliance is your familiar ground. The North Node in the seventh asks you to share your life.",detailed:"The South Node shows a well-worn groove: talents you arrive with and habits you fall back on. In the first house it is independence and self-reliance. You know how to look after yourself, act alone and stand on your own feet, and that is a real strength.\n\nLeaning on it too much can make partnership feel like a threat, or leave you lonely in your competence. The growth is to bring that independence into relationship, where it becomes a gift rather than a wall.",magic:"Thank your self-reliance at the waning Moon, then light a second candle for partnership. Carnelian and Rose Quartz together help.",shadow:"Isolation dressed as strength."},{simple:"With the South Node in the second house, security and self-sufficiency are your familiar ground. The North Node in the eighth asks you to share and transform.",detailed:"In the second house the familiar groove is building, keeping and enjoying. You know how to earn, save and make life comfortable, and you may have a strong sense of your own values.\n\nHolding on too tightly can block intimacy and change, and comfort can become a place to hide. The growth is to open your hands: to share, to trust, and to let some things end.",magic:"Give something away with thanks at the waning Moon. Pyrite and Obsidian together help.",shadow:"Keeping things, and people, long after they have stopped feeding you."},{simple:"With the South Node in the third house, talk and information are your familiar ground. The North Node in the ninth asks you to seek meaning.",detailed:"In the third house the familiar groove is curiosity, conversation and quick connection. You learn fast, know many people and can talk your way through most things.\n\nStaying busy can keep you from the big questions, and information can stand in for wisdom. The growth is to choose a direction and trust it, even when not every fact is in.",magic:"Clear your mind at the waning Moon, then sit with one big question in silence. Fluorite and Sage help.",shadow:"Busyness instead of depth."},{simple:"With the South Node in the fourth house, home and family are your familiar ground. The North Node in the tenth asks you to step out.",detailed:"In the fourth house the familiar groove is nurture, family and the private nest. You know how to make a home and care for those in it.\n\nStaying there can keep you from your public calling, and family can become a reason not to risk the world. The growth is to take your care into work and public life.",magic:"Honour your family at the ancestor altar, then ask their blessing on your work. Moonstone and Onyx help.",shadow:"Hiding at home."},{simple:"With the South Node in the fifth house, self-expression and romance are your familiar ground. The North Node in the eleventh asks you to join with others.",detailed:"In the fifth house the familiar groove is creativity, play, romance and being seen. You know how to shine and how to have fun.\n\nNeeding the spotlight can keep you from belonging, and personal delight can crowd out shared purpose. The growth is to use your light for the group and the future.",magic:"Make a creative offering for your community, not for yourself. Sunstone and Amethyst help.",shadow:"Needing the spotlight."},{simple:"With the South Node in the sixth house, work and routine are your familiar ground. The North Node in the twelfth asks you to rest and trust.",detailed:"In the sixth house the familiar groove is usefulness, skill, routine and care for the body. You know how to keep things running and help.\n\nWorry and work can keep you from spirit, and busyness can become a way of not feeling. The growth is to let go, rest and trust.",magic:"Release a written list of worries at the waning Moon, then meditate. Amazonite and Amethyst help.",shadow:"Worry as a way of life."},{simple:"With the South Node in the seventh house, partnership is your familiar ground. The North Node in the first asks you to find yourself.",detailed:"In the seventh house the familiar groove is relationship: adjusting, supporting, mediating and seeing others' needs. You know how to be a good partner.\n\nLosing yourself in others can keep you from your own path. The growth is to know what you want, say it, and act on it.",magic:"Thank your gift for partnership, then light a red candle for your own will. Rose Quartz and Carnelian help.",shadow:"Losing yourself in others."},{simple:"With the South Node in the eighth house, intensity and shared resources are your familiar ground. The North Node in the second asks you to build your own.",detailed:"In the eighth house the familiar groove is depth: crisis, intimacy, other people's money and power, and transformation. You know how to survive.\n\nLiving in intensity can keep you from simple peace and self-reliance. The growth is steady, ordinary security built with your own hands.",magic:"After shadow work, always ground with earth and bread. Obsidian and Green Aventurine help.",shadow:"Living in crisis."},{simple:"With the South Node in the ninth house, belief and big ideas are your familiar ground. The North Node in the third asks you to listen.",detailed:"In the ninth house the familiar groove is philosophy, faith, travel and the big picture. You know how to inspire and teach.\n\nCertainty can keep you from curiosity, and the horizon can distract from the people nearby. The growth is to learn from those around you and check the details.",magic:"Honour your teachers, then learn something small from a neighbour. Turquoise and Citrine help.",shadow:"Preaching instead of listening."},{simple:"With the South Node in the tenth house, career and status are your familiar ground. The North Node in the fourth asks you to come home.",detailed:"In the tenth house the familiar groove is achievement, responsibility and public life. You know how to work, lead and be respected.\n\nWork can keep you from feeling and from family. The growth is to tend your roots and your heart as carefully as your career.",magic:"Bless your home and cook a meal as ritual. Onyx and Moonstone help.",shadow:"Work as a shield."},{simple:"With the South Node in the eleventh house, groups and friends are your familiar ground. The North Node in the fifth asks you to shine as yourself.",detailed:"In the eleventh house the familiar groove is community, networks and causes. You know how to belong to a crowd and work for shared hopes.\n\nHiding in the group can keep you from your own creativity and love. The growth is personal joy and expression.",magic:"Make something just for delight and keep it for yourself. Amethyst and Sunstone help.",shadow:"Hiding in the group."},{simple:"With the South Node in the twelfth house, solitude and spirit are your familiar ground. The North Node in the sixth asks you to serve in daily life.",detailed:"In the twelfth house the familiar groove is retreat, imagination, spirituality and compassion. You know how to dream and to feel what others feel.\n\nEscape can keep you from practical life, and sensitivity can become overwhelm. The growth is useful, grounded work with clear edges.",magic:"After dreamwork, write it down and act on one small thing. Amethyst and Amazonite help.",shadow:"Escape from the everyday."}]},3060,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PLUTO_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n=[{simple:"With Pluto in the first house you have an intense, magnetic presence. You may reinvent yourself several times in life.",detailed:"Pluto near the Ascendant gives a powerful, private, sometimes intimidating presence. People sense depth in you before you have said much. Early life may have involved crisis or survival, and you may go through dramatic personal transformations.\n\nYour resilience is remarkable, and others often come to you in crisis. Learning to soften control and let yourself be known is part of the path.\n\nIn relationships you need depth and honesty, and you may attract or repel strongly. At work you suit crisis work, research, therapy or any role with real power.",magic:"Transformation and protection magic is natural for you: rebirth rituals, personal wards and shadow work. Obsidian, Garnet and Wormwood help.",shadow:"Control and intimidation."},{simple:"With Pluto in the second house money and self-worth are deeply tied to power. Resources may be gained or lost dramatically.",detailed:"With Pluto in the house of resources, money and possessions are charged. You may have strong drives to build wealth, or experience dramatic gains and losses that remake your sense of worth.\n\nYou can rebuild from nothing. Obsession with security or using money as power are the risks.\n\nFinance, investment, research or recycling and renewal work may suit you. Your relationship with money may be transformed more than once.",magic:"Deep prosperity magic suits you: rituals to release scarcity, transformation of your relationship with money, and protection of resources. Obsidian, Pyrite and patchouli help.",shadow:"Money as power and obsession with security."},{simple:"With Pluto in the third house your mind is penetrating and your words powerful. You seek the truth beneath every story.",detailed:"With Pluto in the third house, thinking is investigative. You may be a powerful writer or speaker, drawn to research and secrets. Sibling relationships or early schooling may have been intense.\n\nYour words can transform people. Obsessive thinking and using words to control are the risks.\n\nSiblings may hold power or secrets in your life. Research, investigation, psychology and writing about hidden things may suit you.",magic:"Powerful word magic suits you: binding, banishing, and research as devotion. Obsidian, Fluorite and rosemary help.",shadow:"Obsessive thinking and manipulative words."},{simple:"With Pluto in the fourth house family and home hold deep power. You may transform your roots and heal family patterns.",detailed:"With Pluto at the root of the chart, family life may have been intense: power struggles, secrets, crisis or a dominant parent. Home may change dramatically through life.\n\nYou can break generational patterns and build a home that heals. Old family wounds and control at home are the risks.\n\nA parent may have been powerful or controlling, or family life marked by crisis. Breaking old patterns and making a home that heals is the work.",magic:"Ancestral healing magic is your strength: ancestor work, family pattern release and home protection. Obsidian, Smoky Quartz and rosemary help.",shadow:"Family power struggles."},{simple:"With Pluto in the fifth house creativity and romance are intense and transforming. You love deeply and create from the depths.",detailed:"With Pluto in the fifth house, pleasure has depth. Romance can be obsessive, creativity powerful and cathartic, and relationships with children intense.\n\nYour creative work can transform others. Possessive love and control are the risks.\n\nChildren may be a profound source of transformation. Creative work can be cathartic and powerful, and love affairs may change you.",magic:"Creative transformation magic suits you: art as catharsis, passion rituals and spells for creative power. Garnet, Obsidian and Damiana help.",shadow:"Obsessive romance."},{simple:"With Pluto in the sixth house work and health are areas of transformation. You may have great stamina and a drive to perfect.",detailed:"With Pluto in the sixth house, daily work is intense. You may be driven, transformative in your job, or drawn to healing and research. Health may undergo dramatic changes and recoveries.\n\nYou can regenerate remarkably. Obsessive work and control are the risks.\n\nHealth may go through dramatic changes and recoveries. Work in research, medicine, crisis work or anywhere you can transform systems suits you.",magic:"Healing and purification magic suits you: deep cleansing, healing (beside proper care), and banishing illness patterns. Obsidian, Amazonite and Hyssop help.",shadow:"Obsessive work."},{simple:"With Pluto in the seventh house partnerships are intense and transforming. You attract powerful people and meet power through others.",detailed:"With Pluto in the seventh house, relationships change you. You may attract intense, powerful partners, experience power struggles, or be transformed by marriage and its endings.\n\nYou can build deep, transforming bonds. Control and jealousy in partnership are the risks.\n\nPartners may be powerful or intense, and partnerships transforming. Business partnerships need clear agreements about power and money.",magic:"Relationship transformation magic suits you: cord cutting, partnership healing and protection. Obsidian, Rose Quartz and Vervain help.",shadow:"Power struggles with partners."},{simple:"With Pluto in the eighth house, its natural place, you go to the depths. Intimacy, crisis and transformation define your path.",detailed:"The eighth house is Scorpio's natural house, and Pluto is at home here. You may face death, crisis and transformation early or often, and be drawn to psychology, the occult, finance or healing.\n\nYou can be a powerful guide through crisis. Obsession with control and intensity are the risks.\n\nYou may be drawn to psychology, the occult, finance, surgery or healing. Crisis may come early and teach resilience.",magic:"Deep magic is natural for you: shadow work, death and rebirth rituals, ancestor work and protection. Obsidian, Garnet and Wormwood help; Hades and Persephone keep these depths.",shadow:"Obsession with control."},{simple:"With Pluto in the ninth house beliefs transform you. You seek truth intensely and may change faith dramatically.",detailed:"With Pluto in the ninth house, faith is a matter of life and death. You may undergo dramatic changes of belief, be drawn to intense spiritual or philosophical paths, or travel transformatively.\n\nYou can seek a truth that holds. Fanaticism is the risk.\n\nBeliefs may be transformed by travel, study or crisis. You may be drawn to intense spiritual paths and the study of power.",magic:"Seeking magic suits you: pilgrimage, intense study, and transformation through faith. Obsidian, Turquoise and Sage help.",shadow:"Fanaticism."},{simple:"With Pluto in the tenth house career and reputation hold power. You may rise to influence or transform your field.",detailed:"With Pluto near the Midheaven, ambition is deep. You may seek power, transform your profession, or face dramatic rises and falls in career.\n\nYou can wield authority for good. Ruthlessness and power struggles with authority are the risks.\n\nYou may seek influence, transform your profession, or face dramatic rises and falls in career. Integrity protects your power.",magic:"Power and success magic suits you: career transformation spells, protection of reputation, and banishing obstacles. Obsidian, Garnet and cypress help.",shadow:"Ruthless ambition."},{simple:"With Pluto in the eleventh house friendships and groups transform you. You may be drawn to powerful collectives and causes.",detailed:"With Pluto in the eleventh house, community is intense. Friendships may be deep and transforming, groups powerful, and hopes for the future radical.\n\nYou can transform society through collective work. Power struggles in groups are the risk.\n\nFriends and groups may be intense and transforming. You may work for radical change in society.",magic:"Communal transformation magic suits you: group ritual, spells for social change and protection for activists. Obsidian, Amethyst and lavender help.",shadow:"Power struggles in groups."},{simple:"With Pluto in the twelfth house transformation happens in hidden places. You may have deep psychic power and hidden strength.",detailed:"With Pluto in the twelfth house, the unconscious is powerful. You may have strong psychic gifts, hidden fears or a private, transforming spiritual life.\n\nYou can heal deeply hidden wounds. Hidden fears and self-undoing are the risks.\n\nYou may have strong psychic gifts, hidden fears or a private spiritual life. Therapy, shadow work and solitude help you heal.",magic:"Hidden, spiritual magic suits you: shadow work, dreamwork and retreat. Obsidian, Amethyst and mugwort help.",shadow:"Hidden fears and self-undoing."}]},3061,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SATURN_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const t=[{simple:"With Saturn in the first house you come across as serious, reserved and capable. You may have grown up fast, and you grow into your confidence over time.",detailed:"Saturn near the Ascendant gives a sober, steady presence. You may seem older than your years in youth and younger than them later on. Early life may have felt heavy with responsibility or self-consciousness, and you may have been shy or hard on yourself. Traditional astrologers read Saturn rising as a mark of endurance and of difficulties met head-on.\n\nWith time this becomes real authority: people trust you because you are reliable, and your confidence, once earned, is solid. The work is to treat yourself with patience rather than harsh judgement, and to let lightness in.\n\nIn relationships you may be slow to open up but deeply loyal once you do. At work you are often given responsibility early. The Saturn return around twenty-nine, and again near fifty-eight, is often when this placement comes good.",magic:"Protection and boundary magic suit you: personal wards, a protective amulet worn daily, and Saturday rites for strength and endurance. Onyx, Jet, Black Tourmaline and cypress are allies.",shadow:"Self-criticism and a heavy, guarded manner."},{simple:"With Saturn in the second house money and self-worth are built slowly through effort. You learn to value yourself and to manage resources wisely.",detailed:"With Saturn in the house of resources, security can feel hard-won. You may have known scarcity, or carry a strong fear of it. Money often comes through slow, steady work, and you can become very good at managing it.\n\nOver time you may build real, lasting wealth, but the deeper lesson is that worth is more than money. Anxiety about having enough, or a tight grip on what you have, can block the ease you have earned.\n\nAt work you are careful, reliable and good with long-term plans, budgets and stewardship. In relationships you may need financial security before you can relax. Generosity toward yourself is part of the lesson.",magic:"Slow prosperity magic suits you: a money jar fed every Saturday, gratitude rituals, and spells to dissolve scarcity fear. Smoky Quartz, Pyrite, Jet and comfrey help.",shadow:"Scarcity fear and hoarding."},{simple:"With Saturn in the third house you think and speak with care. Learning may have been hard early, and you become precise and wise in words.",detailed:"With Saturn in the third house, the everyday mind is serious. School may have been difficult, siblings a responsibility, or speaking up a struggle. You may doubt your intelligence long after others recognise it.\n\nWith time you often become a careful thinker, writer or teacher whose words carry weight. Pessimistic thinking and fear of speaking are what to watch for.\n\nSiblings may have been a responsibility, or distant. You may become an expert in a subject over many years, and your writing or teaching is valued because it is careful and true. Daily journeys and local life may feel like duties until you make them your own.",magic:"Structured word magic suits you: daily writing practice, carefully worded petitions, and binding spells against gossip. Fluorite, Sodalite and rosemary help.",shadow:"Pessimistic thinking and fear of speaking."},{simple:"With Saturn in the fourth house home and family carry responsibility. You build your own foundations carefully, often later in life.",detailed:"With Saturn at the root of the chart, early home life may have felt strict, cold or burdened by duty, or a parent may have been absent or demanding. You may carry family responsibility early.\n\nOver time you build your own solid foundations: a home, a family line, a sense of belonging earned through effort. Emotional reserve and old family burdens are the shadow to tend.\n\nIn later life many people with this placement become the family elder, the one who keeps the stories and holds things together. Property may come late, and be earned. Making peace with a parent is often part of the work.",magic:"Ancestor and hearth magic is healing for you: ancestor altars, family healing rituals, home protection and land offerings. Saturdays and Mondays suit you. Jet, Smoky Quartz and cypress help; Saturn, god of the ancient golden age and the harvest, was honoured at the hearth in Saturnalia.",shadow:"Emotional reserve and old family burdens."},{simple:"With Saturn in the fifth house joy and creativity may come slowly. You learn to play and create with discipline and grow into real mastery.",detailed:"With Saturn in the fifth house, fun can feel like something you have to earn. Creativity may be blocked early by fear of judgement, romance approached cautiously, and children a serious responsibility.\n\nOver time you may become a disciplined, masterful artist, or a devoted parent. Learning to play without guilt is the lesson; fear of judgement is the thing to outgrow.\n\nWith children you may be a serious, responsible parent, or have children later in life. Creative work may come into its own in middle age, when the inner critic quietens. Romance may be cautious and loyal.",magic:"Disciplined creative magic suits you: a daily creative practice as devotion, rituals to release fear of play, and blessings for children. Saturdays and Fridays suit you. Carnelian, Onyx and Calendula help.",shadow:"Guilt about pleasure and fear of judgement."},{simple:"With Saturn in the sixth house you are a dedicated, disciplined worker. Health and routine need care, and you become a master of your craft.",detailed:"With Saturn in the sixth house, work is serious. You may be very hard-working, perfectionist and dutiful, with routines that become strict. Health may need careful attention, especially chronic conditions.\n\nOver time you become a master of your craft and an excellent organiser. Overwork, worry and health neglected for duty are what to watch.\n\nChronic health matters, especially of the bones, joints, teeth or skin, may need patient care. You do well in roles that reward diligence: craft, medicine, administration, quality control. Resting is also work.",magic:"Health and routine magic suits you: steady devotions, healing (beside proper care), and protection at work. Saturdays and Wednesdays suit you. Amazonite, Hematite and Chamomile help.",shadow:"Overwork and health neglected for duty."},{simple:"With Saturn in the seventh house partnership is serious and committed. Relationships may come later, and grow strong with time.",detailed:"Saturn is exalted in Libra, and many astrologers find it surprisingly constructive in the seventh house. Partnership is taken seriously: you may marry later, choose older or more serious partners, or meet lessons through relationship.\n\nOver time you build lasting, committed bonds. Fear of commitment, or relationships that feel like duty, are the risks to watch.\n\nBusiness partnerships may be built on contracts and slow trust. Older, more serious partners may appeal to you. The Saturn return often brings partnership questions to a head.",magic:"Commitment and justice magic suits you: partnership blessings, agreements sealed, and spells for fairness. Saturdays and Fridays suit you. Lapis Lazuli, Jade and Vervain help.",shadow:"Fear of commitment, or love as duty."},{simple:"With Saturn in the eighth house intimacy and shared resources demand care. You learn to trust slowly and to face life's depths.",detailed:"With Saturn in the eighth house, the depths are serious. Trust in intimacy may be hard, shared money a source of responsibility or debt, and loss may come early.\n\nOver time you become resilient and wise about crisis, death and power. You may be a careful steward of others' resources. Fear of vulnerability and control are what to soften.\n\nYou may be drawn to finance, law, insurance, hospice, research or any field that handles weighty matters. Inheritance may come with responsibilities. Grief, when it comes, may be heavy and teaching.",magic:"Deep, slow transformation magic suits you: grief rituals, ancestor work, protection and shadow work. Saturdays and the dark Moon suit you. Obsidian, Jet and cypress help.",shadow:"Fear of intimacy and control."},{simple:"With Saturn in the ninth house faith and philosophy are built slowly. You take belief seriously and earn your wisdom.",detailed:"With Saturn in the ninth house, belief is serious. You may have grown up with strict religion, doubt, or obstacles to higher education or travel.\n\nOver time you build a philosophy of your own, tested by experience, and may become a serious teacher or scholar. Dogmatism and cynicism are the shadow.\n\nYou may come to religion or philosophy later, after doubt, and hold it all the more firmly. Long journeys may be for duty or study. Many people with this placement become respected teachers in middle age.",magic:"Study and devotion suit you: disciplined spiritual practice, pilgrimage, and long-term devotions. Saturdays and Thursdays suit you. Lapis Lazuli, Sodalite and Sage help.",shadow:"Dogmatism and cynicism."},{simple:"With Saturn in the tenth house you are ambitious, responsible and built for long-term achievement. Success comes with time.",detailed:"With Saturn near the Midheaven, career is a mountain to climb. You may carry heavy responsibility, have strict authority figures, and rise slowly but surely. Traditional astrologers warned that Saturn here can bring a fall if success is won unfairly; modern astrologers stress the reward of integrity.\n\nOver time you can achieve great respect and authority. Workaholism and fear of failure are the risks.\n\nYou may carry a sense that you must succeed or be seen to fail, often inherited from a parent. Building slowly, with integrity, brings lasting success, and many people with this placement are known for reliability and authority later in life.",magic:"Career and endurance magic suits you: long-term success spells, protection of reputation, and Saturday devotions. Onyx, Garnet and cypress help.",shadow:"Workaholism and fear of failure."},{simple:"With Saturn in the eleventh house friendships are few but loyal. You build community slowly and take your hopes seriously.",detailed:"With Saturn in the eleventh house, friendship is serious. You may have fewer friends, often older, and feel like an outsider in groups. Hopes may be delayed.\n\nOver time you build a loyal circle and may become a respected leader in groups. Loneliness and fear of rejection are what to watch.\n\nFriends may be few but lifelong, and you may hold responsibility in groups, as treasurer, organiser or elder. Your hopes are realistic and long-term, and they tend to come true slowly.",magic:"Communal and structured magic suits you: group rituals with clear roles, friendship spells and long-term wishes. Saturdays suit you. Amethyst, Hematite and lavender help.",shadow:"Loneliness and fear of rejection."},{simple:"With Saturn in the twelfth house you build strength in solitude. Hidden fears are faced slowly, and spiritual discipline becomes your anchor.",detailed:"The twelfth house is Saturn's joy in ancient astrology: Saturn rejoices in this house of solitude and sorrow, its own kind of place. You may need a great deal of time alone, carry hidden fears or old guilt, or work in institutions.\n\nOver time spiritual discipline becomes your strength, and you can be a powerful presence for others in suffering. Hidden fears and isolation are the shadow.\n\nYou may work in hospitals, prisons, monasteries or archives, or simply need regular solitude to stay well. Facing old fears in therapy, meditation or ritual brings lasting strength. Old age may be a time of peace.",magic:"Spiritual and protective magic suits you: meditation, retreat, ancestor work and banishing hidden fears. Saturdays and Mondays suit you. Amethyst, Smoky Quartz and mugwort help.",shadow:"Hidden fears and isolation."}]},3062,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SUN_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n=[{simple:"With the Sun in the first house you are hard to miss. Your personality comes through strongly, and life asks you to lead with who you are.",detailed:"The first house is the self, the body and the way you meet the world, and the Sun here puts your core identity right on the surface. People tend to see you clearly, and you often have a strong presence, good vitality and a natural confidence (or a strong wish to grow into one). Life tends to ask you to take initiative and be the author of your own story.\n\nThe gift is authenticity: what you see is usually what you get, and others feel warmed or energised by your directness. The challenge is that it can be hard to step back. You may take things personally, or feel unsure who you are when nobody is reflecting you back.\n\nTraditional astrologers counted the Sun on the Ascendant as strong and visible, a sign of a life lived in the open. Your rising sign and Sun sign together show the style of that shining.",magic:"You are your own best talisman: self-blessing, glamour and personal protection work come naturally. Sunday sunrise is a powerful time to set an intention for the year ahead, and your birthday (your solar return) is your strongest annual day. Sunstone, Citrine and St John\u2019s Wort carry solar strength.",shadow:"Self-absorption, and difficulty letting others lead."},{simple:"With the Sun in the second house you find yourself through what you build, earn and value. Your talents and resources are central to your sense of worth.",detailed:"The second house is money, possessions, skills and self-worth. With the Sun here, these matters become a stage for your identity: you may take great pride in being self-sufficient, in your talents, or in building something solid. Earning your own way can be deeply important.\n\nThe gift is a strong practical sense and the ability to turn talent into resources. You often know what you value, and you can make life comfortable for yourself and others. The challenge is tying your worth too tightly to what you have or earn, so that a loss of income feels like a loss of self.\n\nThe sign on the second cusp and the Sun's sign show how you build. Many people with this placement grow into a quiet, steady confidence that does not depend on the bank balance.",magic:"Prosperity magic is a natural strength: money jars, abundance grids, and spells to value your own skills. Sundays and Thursdays suit you, and the waxing Moon in Taurus. Citrine, Pyrite and cinnamon draw golden abundance.",shadow:"Measuring yourself by your possessions."},{simple:"With the Sun in the third house you shine through words, ideas and connections. Learning, talking and writing are central to who you are.",detailed:"The third house is communication, siblings, neighbours, short journeys and the everyday mind. With the Sun here, you come alive in conversation and exchange. You may be a lifelong learner, a writer, teacher, or the person who knows everyone in the neighbourhood. Siblings or close peers may have played a big part in shaping who you are.\n\nThe gift is a lively, curious mind and a talent for connecting people and ideas. The challenge is scattering your light across too many things, or living so much in thought that the heart gets left behind.\n\nAncient astrologers called the third house the house of the goddess (the Moon's joy); the Sun here can light up ritual, omens and devotion as well as everyday talk.",magic:"Word magic is your strength: written petitions, letter spells, journaling as ritual, and divination by signs and omens. Wednesdays and Sundays suit you. Citrine, Agate and lavender support a bright mind; blessing your car, bicycle or daily route is a good third-house working.",shadow:"Restless chatter, and knowing a little about everything."},{simple:"With the Sun in the fourth house you shine at home and among your roots. Family, heritage and a private inner life are central to who you are.",detailed:"The fourth house is home, family, ancestry and the private self, and it begins at the IC, the lowest point of the chart. With the Sun here, your identity is rooted in where you come from and where you live. You may be deeply attached to family or place, or spend much of life building the home you wish you had. Your best self may be the one only your family sees.\n\nThe gift is a strong foundation and a talent for creating warmth and belonging. Many people with this placement come into their own later in life. The challenge is retreating into private life or being defined too much by family patterns, especially those of a parent.\n\nThe sign on the IC and the Sun's sign show the kind of home you are building, inside and out.",magic:"Hearth and ancestor magic is your strength: home blessings, ancestor altars, land spirit offerings and family protection. Sundays and Mondays suit you, and the dark of the year when the Sun is lowest. Amber, Carnelian and bay laurel on the hearth bless the home.",shadow:"Hiding at home, and being ruled by family patterns."},{simple:"With the Sun in the fifth house you shine through creativity, play, romance and joy. You come alive when you make something or have fun.",detailed:"The fifth house is pleasure, creativity, children, romance and play, and the Sun is very much at ease here, since the fifth is the natural house of Leo. You are often expressive, warm and playful, with a strong need to create and to be appreciated for it. Children, your own or others', may be important to you, and you may stay young at heart.\n\nThe gift is joy and the ability to share it. You can be a wonderful artist, performer, teacher or parent. The challenge is needing applause, taking risks for the thrill, or chasing pleasure at the expense of depth.\n\nAncient astrologers called the fifth house good fortune, the joy of Venus; the Sun here often brings a life with real delight in it.",magic:"Creative magic is your strength: art as offering, performance as ritual, fertility and creativity spells, and joyful celebration rites. Sundays and Fridays suit you, and the Moon in Leo. Sunstone, Carnelian and Sunflower bring bright joy.",shadow:"Needing applause, and pleasure-seeking that avoids depth."},{simple:"With the Sun in the sixth house you shine through work, service and skill. Daily routines, health and being useful are central to who you are.",detailed:"The sixth house is daily work, health, routine and service. With the Sun here, you find yourself in doing things well: a craft, a job, a daily practice, caring for others or for animals. You may be the reliable one at work, and your health may be closely tied to how you feel about yourself.\n\nThe gift is diligence and real usefulness: you can improve things, heal and help. The challenge is overworking, worrying about health, or feeling you are only worth what you do for others.\n\nAncient astrologers called the sixth house bad fortune and the joy of Mars, a place of toil and illness. Modern astrologers see it more kindly, as the place where habits and service shape the self.",magic:"Practical, healing magic is your strength: herbal remedies (beside proper care), cleansing routines, spells for good work, and blessing your animals. Sundays and Wednesdays suit you. Amazonite, Carnelian and rosemary support steady health and work.",shadow:"Overwork, and worth measured only by usefulness."},{simple:"With the Sun in the seventh house you shine through partnership and one-to-one relationships. You often discover yourself through others.",detailed:"The seventh house is partnership, marriage, contracts and the people you meet face to face, and it begins at the Descendant. With the Sun here, relationships are central to your identity. You may come alive in close partnership, work well in pairs, or be drawn to counselling, law or client work. Partners may be strong, bright personalities.\n\nThe gift is a talent for relationship: you understand others and can bring out their best. The challenge is defining yourself through partners, or projecting your own light onto others rather than owning it.\n\nThe Sun opposite the Ascendant is visible to all and in public life; the sign on the seventh cusp shows the kind of partner who reflects your light.",magic:"Partnership magic is your strength: sweetening spells, partnership blessings, honest agreement rituals, and love-drawing workings. Sundays and Fridays suit you. Rose Quartz, Sunstone and rose bring warmth to bonds.",shadow:"Losing yourself in others, or seeing your light only in them."},{simple:"With the Sun in the eighth house you shine in the depths: intimacy, transformation and shared resources. You are drawn to life's mysteries.",detailed:"The eighth house is intimacy, death, inheritance, shared money and transformation. With the Sun here, you are often drawn to the hidden: psychology, the occult, research, healing or crisis work. You may go through deep transformations, and you may have a strong, private presence.\n\nThe gift is resilience and insight: you can face what others avoid and help them through it. The challenge is secrecy, control, or a sense that life is always intense.\n\nAncient astrologers called the eighth house idle and associated it with death; modern astrology reads it as transformation, intimacy and the power of what is shared.",magic:"Deep magic is your strength: shadow work, ancestor rituals, divination, transformation rites and grief work. Sundays and Tuesdays suit you, and the dark Moon. Obsidian, Labradorite and Wormwood support the work; Hekate and Persephone are old guides.",shadow:"Secrecy, control, and living in crisis."},{simple:"With the Sun in the ninth house you shine through faith, learning and travel. You are a seeker, a teacher, a lover of big ideas.",detailed:"The ninth house is philosophy, religion, higher learning, long journeys and the search for meaning. With the Sun here, your identity is built on what you believe and what you explore. You may travel widely, study deeply, teach, write or follow a spiritual path with real devotion.\n\nThe gift is vision and wisdom. You can inspire others with your sense of meaning. The challenge is preachiness, restless searching, or being so focused on the horizon that you miss what is near.\n\nThe ninth house is the joy of the Sun in ancient astrology, the house of god: the Sun rejoices here, and many astrologers read it as one of its best places.",magic:"Devotional and seeking magic is your strength: pilgrimage, prayer, study as devotion, travel blessings and divination. Sundays and Thursdays suit you. Citrine, Turquoise and frankincense support the work; Apollo and Sol are fitting patrons of solar wisdom.",shadow:"Preachiness, and searching instead of living."},{simple:"With the Sun in the tenth house you shine in public life and your calling. Career, reputation and achievement are central to who you are.",detailed:"The tenth house is career, reputation, public role and vocation, and it begins at the Midheaven, the highest point of the chart. With the Sun here, you are meant to be seen in the world. You may be ambitious, drawn to leadership, or deeply identified with your work. Recognition matters, and you often achieve it.\n\nThe gift is visibility and purpose. You can lead and inspire. The challenge is identifying too much with status, or neglecting private life for public success.\n\nTraditional astrologers counted the Sun near the Midheaven as one of its strongest places: high in the sky, seen by all.",magic:"Success and solar magic is your strength: career spells, rituals for recognition, and blessings for leadership. Sundays and Saturdays suit you, and noon is your hour. Sunstone, Citrine and bay laurel support success.",shadow:"Identity tied to status, and neglect of private life."},{simple:"With the Sun in the eleventh house you shine among friends, groups and shared hopes. Community and your vision for the future are central to who you are.",detailed:"The eleventh house is friends, groups, hopes and the good things that come through others. With the Sun here, you find yourself in community: friendship, networks, causes and shared dreams. You may be a natural organiser, a loyal friend or a visionary.\n\nThe gift is the ability to bring people together and inspire collective hope. The challenge is losing yourself in the group, or needing its approval.\n\nAncient astrologers called the eleventh house the good spirit, the joy of Jupiter, one of the best places in the chart: friends and allies often help you rise.",magic:"Communal magic is your strength: group rituals, coven work, spells for friendship and for a cause. Sundays and Saturdays suit you. Amethyst, Citrine and lavender support bright connection.",shadow:"Needing the group's approval, and losing your own vision."},{simple:"With the Sun in the twelfth house you shine in quiet, hidden and spiritual places. Solitude, dreams and inner life are central to who you are.",detailed:"The twelfth house is solitude, the unconscious, spirituality, retreat and hidden things. With the Sun here, your light may feel hidden, even from yourself. You may be private, intuitive, drawn to spiritual practice, art or service in places like hospitals, prisons or retreats.\n\nThe gift is a deep inner life and compassion. You can work wonders behind the scenes. The challenge is self-doubt, hiding, or feeling that you are not quite visible in the world.\n\nAncient astrologers called the twelfth house the bad spirit, a place of sorrow and hidden enemies. Modern astrologers read it as the house of the soul and the unseen, and many people with this placement find their greatest strength in solitude and spirit.",magic:"Spiritual and dream magic is your strength: meditation, dreamwork, retreat rituals, and devotional practice. Sundays and Mondays suit you, and the dark Moon. Amethyst, Moonstone and mugwort support the work.",shadow:"Hiding, self-undoing and self-doubt."}]},3063,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"URANUS_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n=[{simple:"With Uranus in the first house you come across as unusual, independent and hard to pin down. Being yourself, on your own terms, matters above all.",detailed:"Uranus near the Ascendant gives an original, sometimes electric presence. You may look or dress unconventionally, have sudden changes of direction, or simply feel different from those around you. Life may have begun with an unusual birth or early upheaval.\n\nYour independence can inspire others to be themselves. It can also make you restless, contrary or hard to get close to. Freedom is a need, not a whim; the work is to choose it rather than react with it.\n\nIn relationships you need a partner who gives you room and does not try to change you. At work you thrive in innovation, technology or self-employment.",magic:"Improvised, personal magic suits you: rituals you invent, sigils made on the spot, and spells cast in a sudden flash of inspiration. Labradorite, Amethyst and lavender steady the current.",shadow:"Contrariness and restlessness that keeps people away."},{simple:"With Uranus in the second house income and resources may be unpredictable. You earn in unusual ways and value freedom over security.",detailed:"With Uranus in the house of resources, money can come and go suddenly. You may earn through technology, innovation, freelance work or unusual talents, and your values may differ from your family's.\n\nYou can be inventive with money and unafraid of change. Learning to build some stability without losing freedom is the work; sudden spending or financial shocks are the risk.\n\nFreelance, technology, astrology, invention or crowdfunding may suit you better than a steady salary. Keep a cushion of savings for the surprises.",magic:"Experimental prosperity magic suits you: sigils for income, new methods of money magic, and grounding rituals for sudden changes. Green Aventurine, Labradorite and Pyrite help.",shadow:"Financial instability and impulsive spending."},{simple:"With Uranus in the third house your mind is original and quick, full of sudden insights. You think differently from those around you.",detailed:"With Uranus in the third house, the everyday mind is inventive. You may have flashes of genius, unusual learning patterns, or an interest in technology and new ideas. Sibling relationships or early schooling may have been unconventional.\n\nYou can see what others miss. Your mind can also be restless, scattered or contrary. Many people with this placement do their best thinking on the move.\n\nSiblings may be unusual, or relationships with them may change suddenly. You may change schools often or teach yourself. Technology, writing and new media suit you.",magic:"Innovative word magic suits you: digital sigils, coded spells and new forms of divination. Fluorite, Labradorite and peppermint help.",shadow:"Scattered, contrary thinking."},{simple:"With Uranus in the fourth house home life may be unusual or changeable. You need freedom even in your nest.",detailed:"With Uranus at the root of the chart, home may have been unconventional, unstable or full of sudden change. You may move often, live in unusual homes, or create a chosen family.\n\nYou can reinvent what home means. The challenge is never quite settling; a home with room to move, and rituals that ground you, help.\n\nA parent may have been unconventional, absent or unpredictable. Home may be a place where you invent your own rules, and you may never quite settle until you find a place that lets you be odd.",magic:"Grounding and inventive hearth magic suits you: home blessings in your own style, rituals for chosen family, and grounding work. Moonstone, Labradorite and Smoky Quartz help.",shadow:"Restlessness at home."},{simple:"With Uranus in the fifth house creativity is original and romance surprising. You need freedom in love and play.",detailed:"With Uranus in the fifth house, fun is unusual. Creative work may be experimental, romances sudden and unconventional, and your approach to children or parenting different from the norm.\n\nYou can create truly original work. Romantic instability and restlessness are the risks, and so is boredom with anything predictable.\n\nChildren may arrive unexpectedly, or be unusual and gifted. Your creative work may be ahead of its time.",magic:"Experimental creative magic suits you: improvised ritual, art as spell, and sudden celebrations. Carnelian, Labradorite and Sunflower help.",shadow:"Romantic instability and restlessness."},{simple:"With Uranus in the sixth house you need freedom and variety in daily work. Routines may be unusual and health sensitive to stress.",detailed:"With Uranus in the sixth house, daily life resists routine. You may work freelance, irregular hours, or in technology or alternative health. Nervous tension can affect health.\n\nYou can reinvent how work is done. The challenge is instability in work and health; a flexible routine, rather than none, keeps you well.\n\nYou may change jobs often until you find one that gives you freedom. Alternative therapies, technology and flexible work suit you. Nervous system care is health care for you.",magic:"Practical, inventive magic suits you: new routines blessed, alternative healing (beside proper care), and grounding. Amazonite, Labradorite and Chamomile help.",shadow:"Nervous tension and erratic routines."},{simple:"With Uranus in the seventh house partnerships need freedom and equality. You may attract unusual partners or sudden relationships.",detailed:"With Uranus in the seventh house, relationships are unconventional. You may meet partners suddenly, prefer open or unusual arrangements, or need lots of space within commitment.\n\nYou can build relationships of real equality. Sudden endings and fear of commitment are the risk.\n\nBusiness partnerships do best with clear agreements and room for each to experiment. You may attract inventive, unpredictable or brilliant partners.",magic:"Relationship magic with freedom built in suits you: honest agreements, partnership blessings and self-love rituals. Rose Quartz, Labradorite and lavender help.",shadow:"Sudden endings and fear of commitment."},{simple:"With Uranus in the eighth house transformation comes suddenly. Shared resources and intimacy may be unpredictable.",detailed:"With Uranus in the eighth house, crises and changes arrive without warning. You may experience sudden changes in shared money, intimacy or life circumstances, and be drawn to the occult or psychology in unusual ways.\n\nYou can transform quickly and radically. The challenge is instability in intimacy and finances.\n\nShared finances may change suddenly through windfalls or losses. You may have sudden insights into psychology, death and the occult.",magic:"Radical transformation magic suits you: sudden release rituals, shadow work and protection. Obsidian, Labradorite and Wormwood help.",shadow:"Instability in intimacy and shared money."},{simple:"With Uranus in the ninth house your beliefs are original and your travels unexpected. You need freedom of thought.",detailed:"With Uranus in the ninth house, faith and philosophy are unconventional. You may have sudden changes of belief, unusual education or travel, and a strong need to think for yourself.\n\nYou can open others' minds. Rejecting every tradition, or restless seeking, are the risks.\n\nYou may travel suddenly, study unusual subjects or change faith in a flash of insight. Astrology, science and philosophy may meet in you.",magic:"Eclectic, seeking magic suits you: new forms of devotion, travel spells and astrology. Turquoise, Labradorite and Star Anise help.",shadow:"Restless seeking."},{simple:"With Uranus in the tenth house career may be unusual or change suddenly. You need freedom in your work and public life.",detailed:"With Uranus near the Midheaven, career is unconventional. You may change direction suddenly, work in technology or innovation, or be known for being different. Conflict with authority is common.\n\nYou can pioneer new paths. Career instability and rebellion against authority are the risks.\n\nYou may be self-employed, a freelancer or an innovator, and you may be known for being different. Sudden changes in reputation are possible and often lead somewhere better.",magic:"Innovative career magic suits you: spells for unusual success and protection during sudden change. Labradorite, Citrine and cypress help.",shadow:"Career instability and rebellion against authority."},{simple:"With Uranus in the eleventh house, its natural place, friends are unusual and groups progressive. You are a natural networker for the future.",detailed:"The eleventh house is Aquarius's natural house, and Uranus is at home here. You may have unusual friends, be part of progressive groups, and have big hopes for the future.\n\nYou can bring people together for change. Detachment, and friendships that come and go suddenly, are the risks.\n\nFriends may be eccentric, brilliant or from very different backgrounds, and they may come and go. Your hopes are for a better future for everyone.",magic:"Communal and visionary magic suits you: online circles, group sigils and spells for a cause. Amethyst, Labradorite and lavender help.",shadow:"Detachment and unstable friendships."},{simple:"With Uranus in the twelfth house sudden insights come from the unconscious. You may have unusual spiritual gifts.",detailed:"With Uranus in the twelfth house, the hidden mind is electric. You may have sudden intuitions, unusual dreams, or a rebellious streak you keep private.\n\nYou can access radical spiritual insight. Nervous tension and hidden rebellion are the risks.\n\nYou may have sudden flashes of insight, unusual dreams, or a hidden rebellious streak. Meditation and solitude help you hear the signal under the noise.",magic:"Dream and spiritual magic suits you: dreamwork, meditation and new forms of spiritual practice. Amethyst, Labradorite and mugwort help.",shadow:"Hidden rebellion and nervous tension."}]},3064,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"VENUS_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o=[{simple:"With Venus in the first house you have natural charm. People find you easy to like, and grace, beauty or gentleness are part of how you come across.",detailed:"Venus near the Ascendant softens the whole manner. You may have an attractive face or style, a pleasant voice, or simply a way of putting people at ease. Many people with this placement care about appearance and present themselves with care; others just radiate warmth without trying.\n\nIn relationships you attract easily and are often liked before you have said much. At work, charm opens doors: you suit roles where first impressions count, such as hospitality, design, sales or anything with the public. The challenge is relying on being liked: avoiding conflict to keep your image pleasant, or wondering whether people love you or the surface.\n\nVenus's sign colours the style: earthy and sensual in Taurus, quick and flirtatious in Gemini, dramatic in Leo. Traditional astrologers counted Venus rising as a mark of grace and good fortune in love.",magic:"Glamour is your native craft: a beauty ritual done as devotion, perfume charged under the waxing Moon, a mirror blessed on a Friday. Self-love spells work powerfully for you. Rose Quartz, rose and jasmine are natural allies.",shadow:"Vanity, and keeping the peace to stay liked."},{simple:"With Venus in the second house you attract money and lovely things, and you value comfort and quality. Your talents can earn well, especially in beautiful work.",detailed:"The second house is Taurus's natural house, and Venus is at ease here. Money often comes through pleasant means: art, design, beauty, music, food, hospitality or simply being good with people. You likely have good taste and enjoy spending on beauty and comfort.\n\nIn relationships you show love through gifts, comfort and generosity, and you may feel most secure with a partner who shares your values. At work you suit anything where taste is a skill. The challenge is overspending on pleasure, or confusing self-worth with possessions and appearance.\n\nThe sign on the second cusp and Venus's sign show how you best earn and enjoy.",magic:"Prosperity with pleasure is your magic: money jars sweetened with honey, spells to value your own talents, and Friday gratitude for what you have. Green Aventurine, Rose Quartz, patchouli and cinnamon draw gentle abundance.",shadow:"Overspending, and worth measured by what you own."},{simple:"With Venus in the third house you speak with charm and grace. You enjoy pleasant conversation, writing, and good relationships with siblings and neighbours.",detailed:"With Venus in the third house, words come sweetly. You may write beautifully, speak diplomatically, or have a gift for languages, poetry or song. Relationships with siblings, cousins and neighbours tend to be warm, or are an important source of affection. You may love short trips, local markets and pretty places nearby.\n\nIn love you are attracted to conversation and often meet partners close to home or through learning. At work you suit writing, teaching, public relations, design for print and anything that needs a kind tongue. The challenge is saying what pleases rather than what is true.\n\nThe third house is the Moon's joy in ancient astrology; Venus here can make daily life a series of small pleasures.",magic:"Sweet word magic suits you: love letters and poems as spells, honey jars for good relations with neighbours or siblings, and blessings for a pleasant journey. Fridays and Wednesdays suit you. Blue Lace Agate, Rose Quartz and lavender help.",shadow:"Flattery, and avoiding honest words."},{simple:"With Venus in the fourth house you love your home and make it beautiful. Family life can be warm, and peace at home is deeply important to you.",detailed:"With Venus at the root of the chart, the home is a place of beauty and comfort. You likely put real care into your surroundings, love having people over, and may have warm memories of family (or a strong wish to create them). Some people with this placement inherit property or beautiful things.\n\nIn relationships you want a partner to share a nest with, and you show love through hospitality. At work you might suit interior design, property, hospitality, cooking or working from a lovely home. The challenge is avoiding conflict at home at all costs, or idealising family.\n\nMany astrologers read Venus here as a promise of a pleasant later life, since the fourth house also speaks of endings and old age.",magic:"Hearth and beauty magic suits you: home blessings with flowers, a love altar in the home, kitchen sweetening spells, and offerings to household spirits. Fridays and Mondays suit you. Rose Quartz, Moonstone and rose bless the home; Hestia and Vesta keep its fire.",shadow:"Peace at any price, and idealising family."},{simple:"With Venus in the fifth house you love romance, creativity, play and pleasure. Love affairs and the arts can bring you great joy.",detailed:"The fifth house is the joy of Venus in ancient astrology, the house of good fortune, and Venus rejoices here. Romance, courtship, creativity, children, parties and pleasure are where you shine. You may be artistically gifted, love to dress up and play, and fall in love with love.\n\nIn relationships you are romantic, affectionate and fun, and you want love to stay playful. At work you suit the arts, entertainment, design, working with children or anything joyful. The challenge is pleasure for its own sake: romance that stays light, or indulgence that avoids depth.\n\nThis is among Venus's happiest places; its sign shows the kind of joy you are made for.",magic:"Joyful love and creative magic is yours: love-drawing spells, art as offering, fertility (of any kind), and celebrations as ritual. Fridays and Beltane suit you. Rose Quartz, Carnelian, rose and Damiana bring delight; Aphrodite and Hathor love music, dance and laughter.",shadow:"Indulgence, and love that stays on the surface."},{simple:"With Venus in the sixth house you bring grace to daily work and care. You like a pleasant workplace and good relations with colleagues.",detailed:"With Venus in the sixth house, ordinary days can be lovely. You likely care about a pleasant workspace, get on well with colleagues, and may meet partners through work. You may be drawn to work that beautifies or heals: beauty, wellness, nutrition, gardening, design, caring for animals.\n\nIn relationships you show love through practical help and daily kindness. The challenge is overindulgence affecting health, or staying in a job because the people are nice rather than because it serves you.\n\nVenus's sign shows the kind of daily rhythm that keeps you well.",magic:"Gentle healing and routine magic suits you: herbal baths, beauty routines as ritual, a blessed workspace and care for animals. Fridays and Wednesdays suit you. Rose Quartz, Amazonite and Chamomile help.",shadow:"Indulgence that harms health, and staying for comfort."},{simple:"With Venus in the seventh house partnership is a source of joy. You attract partners easily and are gifted at relationship.",detailed:"The seventh house is Libra's natural house, and Venus is at home here. You are made for partnership: you know how to be a good partner, you value harmony and you often attract kind, attractive or artistic people. Marriage and close collaborations can be very happy.\n\nIn work you suit anything one-to-one: counselling, law, design for clients, diplomacy, partnership businesses. The challenge is depending on partnership for happiness, or avoiding conflict to keep the peace.\n\nTraditional astrologers read Venus here as a good sign for marriage and agreements.",magic:"Partnership magic is your strength: love-drawing spells, marriage blessings, honey jars and sweetening rites. Fridays suit you. Rose Quartz, Lapis Lazuli, rose and Vervain help; Aphrodite and Venus welcome offerings for love.",shadow:"Dependence on a partner for happiness."},{simple:"With Venus in the eighth house love is deep, intense and transforming. You may also benefit through shared money, inheritance or partners.",detailed:"With Venus in the eighth house, love is not casual. You want intimacy, depth and passion, and you may experience love as a transforming force. Shared resources can be fortunate: money through a partner, inheritance, investment or gifts.\n\nIn relationships you need trust and real emotional honesty. At work you may suit finance, therapy, beauty with depth, or anything dealing with others' resources. The challenge is jealousy, possessiveness, or love entangled with money and power.\n\nVenus's sign shows how you love in the depths.",magic:"Deep love magic, always with care for free will, suits you: rituals for intimacy, sex magic for a consenting couple, and spells for shared prosperity. Fridays and Tuesdays, and the dark Moon, suit you. Garnet, Rhodochrosite and Damiana help.",shadow:"Jealousy, and love tangled with control."},{simple:"With Venus in the ninth house you love travel, learning and other cultures. You may fall for someone from far away, or find beauty in faith and philosophy.",detailed:"With Venus in the ninth house, beauty lives on the horizon. You may love travel, foreign languages, art from other cultures, or religion and philosophy that feel beautiful. You may meet partners abroad or through study.\n\nIn relationships you want a companion for adventure and growth. At work you suit teaching, publishing, travel, the arts, law or spiritual work. The challenge is idealising the faraway and missing what is close.\n\nVenus's sign shows the kind of horizon that draws you.",magic:"Devotional and travel magic suits you: love blessings for a journey, devotion to gods of beauty, and pilgrimage to beautiful places. Fridays and Thursdays suit you. Turquoise, Rose Quartz and Sandalwood help.",shadow:"Idealising the faraway."},{simple:"With Venus in the tenth house you can shine in public through charm, art or diplomacy. Your reputation is often pleasant and your career graceful.",detailed:"With Venus near the Midheaven, the public sees your grace. You may be well liked at work, successful in the arts, design, beauty, diplomacy or any field where charm and taste matter. Partners may help your career, or you may work with a partner.\n\nThe gift is a pleasant, attractive reputation. The challenge is relying on charm rather than substance, or choosing work for its image.\n\nTraditional astrologers counted Venus at the top of the chart as fortunate for honour and favour.",magic:"Success through charm is your magic: glamour for public moments, career spells with rose and gold, and blessings for creative work. Fridays and Sundays suit you. Rose Quartz, Citrine and rose help.",shadow:"Image over substance."},{simple:"With Venus in the eleventh house you are a warm, popular friend. Love and good fortune often come through friends and groups.",detailed:"With Venus in the eleventh house, friendship is a great pleasure. You likely have many friends, enjoy social gatherings and groups, and may meet partners through friends. Your hopes for the future often include love and beauty.\n\nThe gift is popularity and good will. The challenge is many pleasant acquaintances and few deep bonds, or needing to be liked by the group.\n\nThe eleventh is the joy of Jupiter in ancient astrology, a good place; Venus here often brings real kindness from others.",magic:"Friendship and communal magic suits you: friendship spells, group rituals, and blessings for your circle. Fridays and Saturdays suit you. Rose Quartz, Amethyst and lavender help.",shadow:"Needing to be liked by everyone."},{simple:"With Venus in the twelfth house love is private, spiritual and sometimes secret. You may love quietly, or find beauty in solitude.",detailed:"With Venus in the twelfth house, love can be hidden, selfless or spiritual. You may have secret loves, love someone you cannot have, or give love without asking for return. Beauty may be found in solitude, art, music, nature or devotion.\n\nThe gift is compassion and a love of the unseen. The challenge is sacrificing yourself in love, or hiding your heart.\n\nThe twelfth was a hard house in ancient astrology, the bad spirit, and Venus there was read as love that meets sorrow or secrecy. Modern astrologers find more in it: a heart that loves the hidden, the suffering and the divine.",magic:"Devotional and dream magic suits you: love spells for self-acceptance, dreamwork, private altars and devotion to a beloved god. Fridays and Mondays suit you. Rose Quartz, Amethyst and jasmine help.",shadow:"Secret love, and self-sacrifice."}]},3065,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"URANUS_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"NEPTUNE_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PLUTO_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const o=[["You may have felt different from the start, and the feeling rarely leaves. That difference is the point: you are here to show that a life can be lived another way. Sudden changes of look, name, place or direction are common, often in sharp bursts around the Uranus transits at roughly seven-year intervals.\n\nThe nervous system runs fast, so rest, time outdoors and freedom of movement matter more than they would for most. When you stop trying to fit in or to shock, a clear, original presence is left, and people who feel odd themselves find you a relief.","Mark each reinvention with a small rite: cut a lock of hair or change one thing you wear, and leave a piece of Clear Quartz in a storm or under open sky to charge for the new self."],["Income may come in surprising ways, from unusual work, freelance projects, technology or several sources at once, and it may stop and start without warning. A fixed job can feel like a cage. The steadiest path for you is a flexible one with a cushion: savings that let you change course without panic.\n\nYour values may also be unconventional. You may not want what others are told to want, and that freedom is a kind of wealth. Watch impulse spending on the new and exciting; your best investments are in skills that travel with you.","Keep an emergency fund as a magical act: each new moon, set a coin aside in a jar with a pinch of salt and a scrap of foil, for freedom kept safe."],["Your mind jumps, connects and leaps ahead, and you may think in flashes that you can only explain afterwards. Early schooling may have been disrupted or ill-suited to how you learn. Siblings may be unusual, distant or suddenly close and suddenly apart.\n\nTechnology, writing for new media, invention and any field that needs a fresh angle suit you. The care is restlessness and half-finished ideas; a notebook that catches the flashes, and one project at a time carried to the end, make the genius usable.","Write sudden insights on scraps and keep them in a box with Clear Quartz; once a month, read them and choose one to act on."],["Home life may have been unsettled: moves, a parent who came and went, or a household that did not follow the usual pattern. You may move often as an adult, or make a home that is unconventional, shared, or full of experiment. Roots can feel like something you have to invent rather than inherit.\n\nThe gift is freedom from family scripts. The work is giving yourself enough stability to rest: a few belongings and rituals that travel with you can be home wherever you are.","Make a travelling hearth: a small tin holding a candle stub, salt, a key and a photograph, opened and lit wherever you sleep for the first time."],["Love affairs may begin suddenly and end suddenly, and you are drawn to people who are different, independent or unavailable in some way. Creative work is experimental and you may get bored once the idea is proved. Children, if you have them, may be unusual or bring unexpected change.\n\nYour joy comes from surprise and freedom. Let love have space and it may last; try to pin it down and it slips away. In art, the first spark is genuine, but finishing is where the originality becomes a gift to others.","Charge creative tools under a thunderstorm or at the first new moon of a season, and begin something new that same day."],["Routine may chafe, and you may work best with flexible hours, self-employment, technology or reform of how things are done. Jobs may change suddenly. The nervous system may react to stress through odd, shifting symptoms, so a gentle routine you choose for yourself works better than one imposed.\n\nYou are often the colleague who sees a better way to work. Offer it kindly; reform goes better with allies. Varied tasks, short bursts and the freedom to change tools keep you well and productive.","Change your altar layout with each season as a small act of freedom inside routine, and keep a piece of Amethyst by the bed for a busy mind."],["You need freedom inside commitment, and you may attract partners who are unusual, independent or erratic. Relationships may begin or end suddenly, or take an unconventional shape. Many with Uranus here do best with a partner who is also a friend and who respects time apart.\n\nThe work is owning your own need for space rather than finding it only through restless partners. When both people stay free, the bond can be lively and lasting; when one tries to cage the other, it breaks.","Write a partnership vow that names freedom as well as faithfulness, and seal it with two candles lit from one flame and then set a little apart."],["Change through crisis may come suddenly: inheritances, losses or shared money that shift without warning. Intimacy can be electric and unpredictable. You may also have sudden psychological insight, or an interest in astrology, the occult or the science of what is hidden.\n\nThe care is fear of loss expressed as detachment. Letting yourself be affected, and keeping finances with others clear and written down, steadies the ground. Your gift is seeing the truth of a situation in a flash, and helping others through sudden change.","At an eclipse or a dark moon, write what you fear losing on paper and tear it in two, keeping one half and giving one to the wind."],["Belief is something you work out for yourself, and you may change your faith or philosophy suddenly more than once. Travel can be sudden, and foreign places may wake you up. Higher education may be unusual or interrupted, or found through less ordinary routes.\n\nYou are drawn to astrology, new science, radical ideas and the future. The care is replacing one dogma with another. Keep your mind open, test your ideas, and you may become a genuine pioneer of thought.","Read the sky: keep a log of the planets you see each month, and on the night of an unexpected insight leave Clear Quartz out under the stars."],["Your career may take sudden turns, and you may change profession more than once or work in fields that did not exist when you were young. Authority can chafe, so self-employment, invention and reform suit you. You may be known for an unusual path.\n\nThe care is quitting just as things become stable. Look for work that changes within itself, so that you can stay and still be free. Your public role may be to bring something new into an old field.","At noon, write three possible futures for your work and leave them under Clear Quartz for a lunar month; act on the one that keeps calling."],["This is Uranus's own house, so friends, groups and causes are central. You may belong to unconventional communities, networks or movements, and your friends may come from every walk of life. Hopes for the future are bold and sometimes ahead of their time.\n\nThe care is detachment: being everyone's friend and no one's close one. A few deep friendships among many lighter ones keep you grounded. You may help groups change and grow, and your vision of a better world is part of your purpose.","Host a working with friends for a shared future: each writes a hope on paper, and all are woven into one cord kept by the group."],["Insight comes from the unconscious in flashes, dreams and sudden knowing. You may feel restless without knowing why, or have a hidden rebellious streak that breaks out unexpectedly. Spiritual life may be unusual, solitary or self-taught.\n\nTime alone helps, as does any practice that lets the mind settle: meditation, walking, journalling. The care is nervous exhaustion and sudden withdrawal. Your gift is intuition and a quiet freedom of spirit that others feel without being told.","Keep a dream book, and under a new moon write the strangest dream of the month on a slip of paper to place under your pillow with Amethyst."]],n=[["People project onto you: you may be seen as kinder, wiser or more mysterious than you feel, and you may take on the moods of whoever is near. Boundaries are the lifelong lesson. You may be sensitive to alcohol, medication and atmosphere, so take care with all three.\n\nThe gift is a presence that soothes and inspires, and a natural feel for art, music, healing or spiritual life. When you learn to know your own feelings from other people's, you can lend your sensitivity without losing yourself.","Each morning, wash your hands in water with a pinch of sea salt and say your own name aloud; it is a small shield for a porous self."],["Money can be vague: it comes and goes without your quite knowing how, and you may undervalue your work or give too much away. Income through art, music, healing, charity or spiritual work is common. The care is confusion, deception or wishful thinking about finances.\n\nClear accounts, an adviser you trust and written agreements are your protection. When you value what you give, and charge fairly for it, the money flows more steadily. Your deepest wealth is often not material, but you still need to eat.","On a Monday, write your true income and costs on paper, then rest Amethyst on it under the waxing moon to bring clarity to money."],["Your thinking is intuitive and image-led, and you may struggle with dry facts while excelling at poetry, music or story. Schooling may have been dreamy or difficult. Siblings may be idealised, absent or in need of care.\n\nYou pick up what is not said, which makes you a sensitive listener and sometimes a confused one. Check facts and keep notes. Your gift is words that move people: songs, poems, spoken prayer and any writing that carries feeling.","Write spells as poems, and read them aloud by a single blue candle; Neptune hears verse better than lists."],["Home may have been a place of mystery, sacrifice or confusion: a parent who was absent, ill, idealised or lost to addiction, or a family with secrets. You may long for a spiritual home and find it hard to settle.\n\nThe work is building a real home with clear walls and a soft heart: a place of retreat that is not an escape. Water near the home, a shrine, and music help. You may be a quiet spiritual centre for your family, as long as you look after yourself too.","Keep a bowl of water on the home altar, changed each Monday; pour the old water on a plant with a word of blessing for the house."],["Romance can be idealised, and you may fall for potential rather than the person. Creative gifts may be strong, especially in music, film, dance or anything that conjures a mood. Children may be deeply sensitive or bring a call to care.\n\nThe care is disappointment when the dream meets the real. Love the real person and make art from the longing; both will be the richer. Pleasure can tip into escape, so let joy include clear mornings as well as dreamy nights.","Make art at the full moon with music playing and a glass of water beside you, and offer the first piece to the sea or a river."],["Work needs meaning: you may be drawn to care, healing, the arts or service, and you may feel drained by jobs that ask you to be hard. Health can be sensitive, with vague symptoms or reactions to medicines and food, so get things checked rather than guessing.\n\nThe care is martyrdom at work, giving until there is nothing left. Gentle routines, clear hours, water, sleep and a practice of cleansing your energy after work keep you well enough to keep helping.","After a long working day, bathe or wash in water with a little sea salt and lavender and let the day run away down the drain."],["Partners may be idealised, needy, artistic or spiritual, and you may fall into rescuing or being rescued. You can be deeply compassionate in relationships and easily hurt. Clarity about what each person brings is your protection.\n\nWhen it goes well, partnership is a spiritual union with real tenderness. Look at people as they are, not as you hope they will become. Contracts and business partnerships need extra care with the small print.","Before a commitment, ask for a dream that shows the truth of the person, with Amethyst under your pillow for three nights."],["Boundaries in intimacy and shared money can blur: you may give too much, be deceived, or merge so deeply you lose yourself. Psychic sensitivity is often strong. You may be drawn to mediumship, grief work, hospice or the occult.\n\nThe care is confusion in joint finances and inheritances, and escape from pain through substances. With clear agreements and a grounded practice, this placement gives a rare gift for sitting with others at the threshold.","Before trance, dream work or spirit contact, draw a circle of salt and keep a black stone in hand to bring you back."],["Faith is mystical rather than doctrinal, and you may be drawn to many paths or to the sea and far horizons. Travel can be magical or confusing. Gurus and teachers may be idealised and later disappoint.\n\nThe gift is real spiritual sensitivity and an ability to see the sacred in many forms. Test teachers by their conduct, not their charisma. Your own experience is a better guide than any borrowed certainty.","Make a pilgrimage to water, a holy well, a river or the sea, and leave a small offering of clean water or a flower."],["Career may be in the arts, healing, charity, film or spiritual work, and you may struggle to name a single calling. Your public image can be glamorous, vague or misunderstood. A parent's influence may have been unclear or idealised.\n\nThe care is drifting, or being blamed for things that are not yours. A clear practical plan alongside the dream keeps you on course. When the work serves something larger, this placement can bring a public life of real inspiration.","At noon on a Monday or Thursday, write the dream of your work on paper and the first practical step beneath it; burn the dream and keep the step."],["Friends may be artists, healers, dreamers or people in need, and groups may be spiritual or idealistic. You may be disappointed by friends who were not what they seemed, or give too much to causes.\n\nThe gift is compassion for the community and a vision of a kinder world. Keep friendships honest and causes practical. Spiritual or creative groups can feel like family when you choose them with open eyes.","In group workings, lead a shared visualisation or a song; the group's dream becomes a spell when everyone holds the same picture."],["This is Neptune's own house, so the inner world is rich and the boundary with the unseen thin. You may need much solitude and may be drawn to retreat, prayer, music, dream work or hidden service.\n\nThe care is escape: sleep, substances or fantasy as a way out of life. A gentle daily practice gives the sensitivity a channel. Your gift is a direct line to the sacred and a quiet compassion for those who suffer out of sight.","Keep a small hidden shrine, a box or drawer, with a shell, a candle and a written prayer, opened only for your own quiet work."]],t=[["The body itself may carry the story: illness, surgery or a dramatic change of appearance can mark the turning points, and each time you come back altered. You may have learned early to watch a room before you spoke, and that watchfulness becomes a gift for reading people.\n\nThe work is letting yourself be seen without armour. When power is used for your own renewal rather than to control others, you become someone who helps people face what they fear simply by being unafraid.","At the dark moon, wash in water with salt and a sprig of rosemary, and name one old self you are leaving behind."],["Your relationship with money and possessions carries a charge that is more than practical: it may echo old survival fears or family patterns of power. You may build great security or lose it and build again, learning each time what you truly value.\n\nThe gift is resourcefulness and a nose for hidden value, in investments, salvage, research or skills others overlook. The care is using money to control or to feel safe from all harm; real worth is something no loss can remove.","Bury a coin wrapped in a bay leaf at the dark moon and dig it up at the next new moon, as a rite for wealth renewed."],["You notice what people avoid saying, and you may have grown up around secrets or heavy silences. Your words can heal or wound deeply, and you may be drawn to investigative writing, research, therapy or any field that asks hard questions.\n\nSibling relationships may involve power struggles or a deep bond through hardship. The work is speaking truth with care: honest without needing to win, searching without needing to expose.","Write a truth you need to say on paper, keep it under Obsidian for three nights, then say it plainly and burn the paper."],["The roots run deep and sometimes dark: family secrets, inherited trauma or a parent who held strong power. You may be the one who ends a family pattern, at a real cost and with real reward.\n\nHome is where you transform, and you may renovate houses, move after crises, or make a home that is a sanctuary from the world. Ancestral work is especially powerful, as long as you include healing for yourself, not only for the line.","Light a black candle for the ancestors at the dark moon and speak aloud the pattern you will not pass on; let the candle burn out safely."],["Love affairs can be consuming, and you may be drawn to intense, transforming relationships. Creativity comes from the depths, and art may be how you survive and make sense of things. Children can bring profound change.\n\nThe care is jealousy, possessiveness or using love as a way to hold power. When pleasure and creation are allowed to be free, they become a source of renewal, not control. Your art can carry other people through their own dark places.","Make art at the dark moon from what hurts, and offer it at the following full moon by showing it to one trusted person."],["Work can be intense and transforming: you may take on crisis, research, healing, investigation or jobs that change people's lives. You may also face power struggles at work. The body may push you to change your habits through illness or exhaustion.\n\nYou can regenerate remarkably when you listen. Treat health as a partnership with the body, not a battle. Purposeful work, clear limits and deep rest let you go further than most.","On a Saturday, write one habit to let go of, tie it to a small stone with black thread, and drop it into running water."],["Partners may be powerful, intense or transforming, and relationships can be where you meet your own shadow. Power struggles in marriage or business are possible. You may also be a profound influence on others through one-to-one work.\n\nThe work is equality: neither ruling nor being ruled. Honest conflict, trust earned slowly and a willingness to be changed by love make partnership a place of deep growth rather than control.","Two black candles and one red, lit together at the dark moon, suit a working for honest power between partners."],["This is Pluto's own house, so depth comes naturally: intimacy, shared resources, death, rebirth and the hidden are all charged. You may have strong psychic or psychological insight and a gift for crisis work, research or the occult.\n\nThe care is control, secrecy and fear of loss. You go through deep transformations more than once, and each leaves you stronger. Your gift is fearlessness at the edge of life, and you can guide others through the dark.","Keep a death and rebirth rite for each major ending: a black candle at the dark moon, and a white one lit from it at the new moon."],["Belief is a matter of life and death to you, and you may undergo profound conversions or crises of faith. Travel or study abroad can change you completely. You seek the truth behind every teaching.\n\nThe care is fanaticism or using belief as power. Your gift is depth: a philosophy forged in experience, an ability to teach about transformation, and a fearless interest in what lies behind the obvious.","Study one mystery tradition deeply for a year, and mark the end with a rite of passage that you design yourself."],["Career may involve power, crisis or transformation: you may rise to authority, work in medicine, research, finance or psychology, or rebuild your vocation after a fall. Your public image can be magnetic or controversial.\n\nThe care is using status as control or fearing exposure. Integrity is your protection. You may be called to transform an institution or to stand where power is used, and to use it well.","At noon, burn a written statement of how you will use power in your work, and keep the ashes in a jar with Obsidian."],["Friendships may be few and intense, or groups may bring power struggles. You may be drawn to movements that seek to transform society. Friends may change your life, and you theirs.\n\nThe care is control in groups or cynicism after betrayal. The gift is real influence: a capacity to help communities face hard truths and change for the better.","Before joining a cause, write what you hope it will change in you as well as in the world, and keep it on the altar under Obsidian."],["The deepest powers work in the unconscious: hidden fears, inherited secrets and intense dreams. You may sense what others hide, and be drawn to therapy, research, hospice, prison work or the occult.\n\nThe care is self-undoing through secrecy or buried anger. Shadow work, therapy and a steady spiritual practice turn this into a quiet, formidable strength. You can go into the dark for others and come back.","Keep a shadow journal by a black candle at the dark moon, writing one thing you have hidden even from yourself."]]},3066,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MARS_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"JUPITER_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SATURN_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const o=[["Over a lifetime the work is learning that not every moment is a fight. The body is Mars's instrument here: hard exercise, a physical trade or a martial art can take the edge off temper and give the courage somewhere honest to go. Watch the first few seconds of any situation, when you react before you have chosen; that small pause is where this placement matures.","Charge a red cord at sunrise on a Tuesday and wear it at the wrist as a reminder to choose your fights."],["Money comes fastest when you can see the link between effort and reward, so piecework, commission, your own business or anything with a clear target suits you better than a slow salary ladder. The care is spending in the same rush you earn. Decide in a calm hour what the money is for, then let the drive serve the plan rather than the mood.","A coin warmed in the hand and set under a red candle on a Tuesday, then saved rather than spent, keeps the drive tied to a goal."],["Daily life moves quickly for you: short journeys, quick messages, the neighbourhood and the people in it. Arguments with siblings or neighbours can flare and fade in an afternoon. Learning to argue a point without needing to win it, and to write when you are angry before you speak, turns a sharp tongue into a persuasive one.","Write the hot words on paper, read them aloud once, then burn them in a red candle's flame; what is left is what needs saying."],["Home is where your energy gathers, and sometimes where it boils over. Many with Mars here put real effort into the house itself, building, mending and digging, and that is the healthiest outlet. If you grew up with anger in the house, the work is to make your own home a place where conflict is honest and short, not a weather that never clears.","Sweep the threshold outwards on a Tuesday, then lay a line of salt and a sprig of rosemary to keep quarrels from settling."],["Play is serious business for you: sport, performance, flirtation and anything you make with your hands are where you feel most alive. With children you can be a lively, physical presence. The care is turning everything into a contest; let some joys be for their own sake, with no score kept and nothing to prove.","Dance or move hard before a creative working; raise the heat in the body, then pour it into the piece you are making."],["You work best with a task you can attack and finish, and you may be the person who gets things done when others stall. The body speaks plainly here, through tension, inflammation or minor injuries when you push too hard. Regular movement, real rest and honest limits keep the engine running for decades rather than in bursts.","Bless your tools on a Tuesday with a little oil and a word of thanks, and set a red stone on the desk where the work is hardest."],["You may meet Mars through other people: partners who are bold, competitive or quick-tempered, or relationships that begin with a spark of challenge. You can be a fierce advocate for those you love. The growth is owning your own fire, so that you are not always waiting for someone else to start the fight or to fight for you.","Light two red candles facing each other and speak one plain truth you have been holding back from a partner, then let them burn down."],["Desire runs deep and is not easily spoken, and you can meet crises with surprising nerve. Shared money, debts and inheritances may bring friction, so clear agreements matter. Treat your intensity as a strength to be directed, through research, crisis work, sexuality honestly expressed or the long work of facing what frightens you.","At the dark moon, hold an iron nail and name one fear; bury the nail at a crossroads or deep in a pot of earth."],["Your beliefs are worth fighting for, and you may travel, study or change faith in sudden leaps. Debate excites you. The care is making a crusade of every opinion. Your best teachers are the ones who can argue with you and win; seek them out, and let a conviction be tested before you carry it into the world.","Before a journey or exam, carry Carnelian and speak a short vow of courage at the first step out of the door."],["Career is a field of action: you want visible results, responsibility and the freedom to lead. You may clash with bosses until you become one. Ambition is healthy here, as long as it is aimed at a goal rather than at a rival; ask what you would build if no one were watching, and aim the drive there.","Write your goal on a bay leaf at noon on a Tuesday and burn it in a red flame, asking for strength rather than for victory."],["Friends and groups draw out your energy: teams, campaigns and causes give you a place to fight beside others. You may also quarrel with friends, or lead a group whether or not you meant to. Choose causes you can stay with, and remember that the friendship is worth more than winning the point at the meeting.","Before a group working, pass a red cord round the circle so each person holds it, then tie one knot for the shared aim."],["Your drive works behind the scenes, and anger may go underground before it surfaces in odd ways: fatigue, tension, or a sudden outburst that seems to come from nowhere. Quiet, solitary effort suits you: research, care work, retreat or physical practice done alone. Learning to notice anger early, and name it to yourself, is the key.","In a quiet Mars hour, write what you are angry about and why, then fold it and keep it under a black stone until you can act on it calmly."]],t=[["Luck often arrives through your own presence: people take to you, doors open when you walk in, and you are given chances on the strength of a first meeting. The care is weight, appetite and promises, all of which grow easily here. Your faith in life is contagious; use it to lift others, and keep your word small enough to keep.","A Thursday self-blessing with a drop of oil on the brow and a pinch of sage in the pocket keeps the luck warm."],["Money tends to come, though not always to stay. You are generous and may be careless with it, so a simple habit of saving a fixed share works better for you than any scheme. Your sense of worth grows with what you can give; generosity is your wealth magic, as long as you include yourself in it.","Keep a jar for Thursday coins; when it is full, give a tenth away and spend the rest on something that lasts."],["Learning is a joy, and you may be a born teacher, writer or talker who makes ideas feel big and exciting. Siblings and neighbours can be a source of help. The care is starting more than you finish; one book written is worth ten planned. Short journeys and everyday conversations often bring your best luck.","Open a well-loved book at random on a Thursday morning and take the first line you read as the day's counsel."],["Home is where blessings collect: you may live in larger houses as life goes on, keep an open door, or come from a generous family. Property can be lucky. The care is overfilling the house with people and things. Make the home a place of welcome that still has one quiet room for you.","Hang a sprig of bay over the kitchen door and refresh it each Thursday, thanking the house for its shelter."],["Pleasure, children and creative work are where you are most blessed. You may be generous with children, your own or others', and your art is often warm, large and hopeful. The care is excess in play, gambling or romance; enjoy, and keep proportion, and your joy will feed other people as well as you.","On a Thursday, make something beautiful purely for pleasure and give it away the same week as an offering to Jupiter."],["Work grows best when it serves something you believe in. You may be lucky with colleagues and find meaning in ordinary tasks. The body needs proportion: Jupiter here can mean appetite, liver strain or doing too much because you feel well. A steady routine that includes rest is the real blessing.","Bless the working week on Thursday morning with a blue candle and a list of three tasks, no more."],["Partners and close allies tend to bring luck, teaching or wider horizons. You may marry someone from a different background or with a strong faith. The care is expecting the other person to provide the meaning or the money. Contracts and partnerships generally go well when you bring your own generosity to them.","Two blue candles lit together on a Thursday, with a shared wish spoken by both partners, suit this placement."],["Shared resources, inheritance and other people's money can come easily. Crises tend to resolve better than you fear, and you may have a gift for helping people through hard passages. Depth is lucky for you; research, therapy and the occult are fields where your faith grows rather than shrinks.","At the dark moon, give thanks for help received through others, with a blue candle and a spoonful of honey given to the earth."],["This is Jupiter's own house, so faith, study and travel are strongly favoured. You may live abroad, teach, publish or follow a spiritual path with real conviction. The care is preaching. The best of this placement is the lifelong student who keeps asking questions, and who is glad to be proved wrong.","Bibliomancy on a Thursday suits you: ask a clear question, open a sacred or beloved book, and read where your finger falls."],["Career can bring recognition, and you may rise through goodwill as much as effort. Roles that teach, lead, advise or publish suit you. The care is promising too much in public, or resting on reputation. Let your work be a gift to the world and the public life tends to look after itself.","At noon on a Thursday, burn a bay leaf with your calling written on it and ask that your name be used well."],["Friends, groups and causes bring luck: many with Jupiter here find their best chances through people they know. You may lead a community or belong to many. The care is spreading yourself thinly across too many circles. A few good friendships and one cause you truly believe in give the most.","Host a shared meal for friends on a Thursday and pour the first cup as an offering for the group's good fortune."],["Help comes from unseen places: a quiet guardian, a lucky escape, a stranger's kindness at the right moment. You may have a rich inner life of faith and a gift for care, retreat or spiritual work. The care is escaping into hope instead of acting; time alone is your blessing, as long as you come back from it.","Before sleep on a Thursday, ask for a dream of guidance and keep a notebook by the bed for the morning."]],n=[["Saturn on the Ascendant often looks older when young and younger when old: life asks for seriousness early and rewards it later. You may have felt awkward or restricted in the body. Discipline in health, posture and daily rhythm pays you back more than most, and the reserve that once felt like a wall can become dignity.","On a Saturday at sunrise, stand straight, name one promise you will keep to your own body, and keep a piece of Onyx with you."],["Security matters deeply, often because there was once too little of it. You may earn slowly but build reliably, and you are rarely careless with money. The care is scarcity thinking that never lets you enjoy what you have. Set a modest rule, keep it, and allow yourself to spend a little without guilt.","Bury a coin in salt on a Saturday and leave it for a full month as a charm for steady savings."],["Words matter to you, and you may have been made to feel slow or silenced early. Your thinking is careful and thorough, and a talent for writing, teaching or detail work grows with practice. Study later in life can be especially rewarding. Speak plainly and give yourself time; your words carry weight because you weigh them.","Keep a written record of what you learn each week, and close it on Saturday with a single line on what you now know."],["Home and family may have been strict, cold or burdened, or you may have taken on responsibility young. The deep work is building your own foundation: a home you have made by your own effort, often later in life. Property, ancestry and family duty run through the life. What you build here tends to last.","Set an ancestor shelf with a black candle and a stone from somewhere you have lived, and tend it each Saturday."],["Joy may have been earnest work for you; play and creative risk can feel exposing. Some with Saturn here have children late, or take parenting very seriously. Your art matures slowly and gains depth with time. Practise enjoyment as a discipline: a fixed hour for play is still play, and it counts.","Make one small creative thing every Saturday for a season and keep them together; the collection is the spell."],["Work is where Saturn trains you: you may carry heavy responsibilities, or feel you must earn your place through effort. You are reliable and thorough. The body may hold stress in bones, joints, skin or teeth, and benefits from routine. The care is overwork as proof of worth; rest is part of the job.","On Saturday, write your week's duties on a strip of paper, tie it with black thread and lay it under Onyx until they are done."],["Relationships ask for commitment and patience, and may come later or with an older or more serious partner. Partnership can feel like a weight before it feels like a shelter. You keep promises. The growth is letting a partner be an equal rather than a duty, and not mistaking control for care.","A Saturday handfasting cord, tied with three knots for loyalty, patience and fairness, suits partnership vows under this placement."],["Shared money, intimacy and grief may all arrive with weight, teaching you to face loss and endings with steady courage. You may handle other people's money or affairs responsibly. The care is clinging to control in matters you cannot control. Learning to trust slowly, and to let go cleanly, is the long work.","At a waning moon on a Saturday, write what you must release, wrap it in black cloth with salt and bury it."],["Beliefs are earned rather than given: you may question faith hard, study formally, or come to a spiritual path late and keep it seriously. Travel and higher learning may be delayed but are worth the wait. The care is rigid belief; the gift is a philosophy you have tested and can stand on.","Choose one text to study through a whole season, reading a little every Saturday by a single black candle."],["Career is Saturn's natural ground, and you may climb slowly to real authority. Early setbacks often prove useful. You want work that lasts and a name that means something. The care is sacrificing everything else to status. Build steadily and keep your integrity; reputation earned here is hard to lose.","At noon on a Saturday, set a black candle on a written plan for the next year and light it for patience and endurance."],["Friendship is selective and loyal: you may have few friends, often older, and keep them for life. Groups can feel uncomfortable, or you may end up running them. The care is loneliness disguised as independence. Join one group where you have a role, and let belonging grow slowly, as Saturn prefers.","Give a small, lasting gift to an old friend on a Saturday, with a word of thanks for the years."],["Fears tend to live in the quiet places: worry at night, unspoken guilt, or a feeling of being held back by something you can't name. Solitude, therapy, retreat and service in hidden places all help. Facing these fears slowly, with support, turns them into a deep inner strength and an ability to sit with others in their dark.","On a Saturday night, write a fear on paper, fold it away from you, and keep it under a bowl of salt until the next new moon."]]},3067,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CHIRON_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"NORTH_NODE_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SOUTH_NODE_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"LILITH_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}});const o=[["The wound here is often about simply being: a sense, from early on, that your body, face or way of being in the world was wrong, too much or not enough. You may have been ill, teased or overlooked as a child, and learned to hide or to perform. It can show as shyness that looks like confidence, or the reverse.\n\nThe healing comes through presence. As you learn to live in your own body without apology, you become a quiet permission for others to do the same. Many with Chiron here become teachers, healers or role models simply by being visibly themselves.\n\nChiron returns to its birth place at about fifty, and that return is often the time when this wound finally becomes a gift you can name.","Stand before a mirror at sunrise with a green candle and Yarrow nearby, and speak one kind sentence to the person you see; repeat it until it stops feeling strange."],["The wound touches worth: money, possessions and the quiet question of whether you deserve to have. You may have known scarcity, or plenty with strings attached, and learned to measure yourself by what you earn or own.\n\nHealing comes through finding value that cannot be taken away: your skills, your care, your body's simple goodness. Many with Chiron here become wise about money for others, as counsellors, advisers or teachers of practical skills, because they know the fear behind it.\n\nWatch for undercharging and over-giving. Fair exchange is part of the medicine.","Write a list of what you are worth that has nothing to do with money, and keep it in your purse or wallet with a sprig of chamomile."],["The wound sits in learning and speech: being told you were slow, being talked over, a difficult school or a sibling who outshone you. You may still hesitate before you speak or write, even when you know the answer.\n\nThe healing is finding your own voice and your own way of learning. Many with Chiron here become patient teachers, writers or translators who can explain things to people who have been made to feel stupid, because they remember the feeling.\n\nNotice the inner critic that sounds like an old teacher. Answer it, kindly and firmly.","Write a letter to the child who was afraid to speak, and read it aloud by a green candle on a Wednesday."],["The wound is at the roots: home, family and belonging. You may have felt like an outsider in your own family, lost a parent, moved often, or carried a family grief that was never spoken.\n\nHealing comes through making a home that holds you, and often through ancestral work that lets old griefs be named at last. Many with Chiron here create a family of choice, or become the person in the family who helps others heal.\n\nThe Chiron return around fifty may bring a reckoning with the family story, and a new peace with it.","Set a bowl of water and a green candle on the ancestor shelf, and name one family hurt to be healed, asking the kindly dead for help."],["The wound is in joy itself: play, creativity, romance or the confidence to be seen enjoying yourself. You may have been shamed for showing off, or had a childhood without much play. Children may be a source of pain or of healing.\n\nThe healing is letting yourself create and play badly before you play well. Many with Chiron here become teachers of art, drama or play, gifted at drawing out shy children and adults, because they know what it took.\n\nTake one small creative risk at a time. Joy is a skill that can be relearned.","Play for its own sake on a Friday: paint, sing or dance for ten minutes with no aim, then light a green candle in thanks."],["The wound lives in work and the body: health problems, feeling useless, or being valued only for what you do. You may push yourself hard or feel guilty resting.\n\nHealing comes through a kinder relationship with the body and with daily work. Many with Chiron here are drawn to healing professions, herbalism, nursing, therapy or animal care, and are good at them because they understand chronic struggle from the inside.\n\nYour body is not a machine to be fixed but a companion to be listened to. Routines that care for it are part of the medicine.","Make a weekly tea from chamomile and lemon balm as a small healing rite, and drink it slowly with a hand on the place that hurts."],["The wound is in partnership: rejection, betrayal, an early sense that you could not be loved as you are, or a pattern of rescuing wounded partners. Relationships may be where old pain resurfaces.\n\nHealing comes through honest, equal love and through counselling or one-to-one work, where you may become a gifted listener. Many with Chiron here become therapists, mediators or advisers.\n\nThe work is to stop choosing the wound and start choosing the healing: partners who meet you, rather than ones who need fixing.","Two green candles, lit together, with a written promise to yourself about what you will no longer accept in love, suit this placement."],["The wound is deep and private: loss, abuse, betrayal in intimacy, or an early meeting with death. Trust may be very hard. Shared money or inheritance may also carry pain.\n\nHealing comes slowly, often through therapy, grief work or a spiritual practice that faces the dark directly. Many with Chiron here become counsellors, hospice workers, researchers or healers of trauma, with a rare ability to stay present with pain.\n\nGo gently. This wound heals in layers, and each layer is a gift you can give to others.","At the dark moon, write what hurt you, fold it into a green cloth with Yarrow and salt, and bury it where nothing will be planted."],["The wound is in meaning: a lost faith, a rigid upbringing, an interrupted education or a sense of being shut out of learning and travel. You may doubt your right to have a philosophy of your own.\n\nHealing comes through finding a faith or meaning that is truly yours, often through study, travel or a long spiritual search. Many with Chiron here become teachers of philosophy, religion or healing, able to help others recover from spiritual harm.\n\nYour doubts are part of your wisdom. Keep asking.","Make a pilgrimage, even a short walk to a meaningful place, and leave a green ribbon there for the faith you are making."],["The wound touches vocation and public life: a fear of being seen, a feeling that you have failed or not lived up to expectations, or a parent's ambition that weighed on you.\n\nHealing comes through a calling that uses the wound itself. Many with Chiron here become healers, teachers or public advocates for the very thing they struggled with, and their visibility helps others.\n\nThe Chiron return around fifty often brings a turn in career towards this healing work, and with it a peace about success.","At noon, write the work you would do if the old fear were healed, and keep it under a green candle lit each Sunday for a season."],["The wound lives in belonging: being left out of groups, a feeling of never quite fitting, or hurt from friends. You may hover at the edge of communities.\n\nHealing comes through finding or making groups that welcome difference, and many with Chiron here create support groups, healing circles or communities for outsiders. Your gift is making others feel included because you know what exclusion costs.\n\nStart small: one friendship, one group, one place where you can be yourself.","Host a small healing circle with friends, passing a cup of chamomile tea and letting each person speak without interruption."],["The wound is hidden, perhaps inherited or unconscious: a sorrow you cannot name, a fear with no clear cause, or a sense of carrying something for others. You may be very sensitive to suffering.\n\nHealing comes through spiritual practice, retreat, dream work and compassion for yourself. Many with Chiron here become chaplains, hospice workers, dream workers or quiet healers who work out of sight.\n\nYour hidden gift is a deep compassion. Give it to yourself first.","Keep a dream book, and on waking after a hard dream, light a green candle and ask what the dream asks you to heal."]],t=[["The direction of growth is towards yourself: your own needs, body and choices, after a pull in the past or in habit towards partners and other people's needs. You may find it easier to adapt than to lead, and the call is to lead your own life.\n\nSmall acts of self-direction count: choosing for yourself, starting things, saying what you want. It can feel selfish at first. It is not; it is your contribution.","On a new moon, write one choice made only for yourself and carry it with dragon's blood resin wrapped in red cloth."],["Growth lies in building your own resources and values, after a pull towards shared money, crisis and other people's power. Simplicity, steady work and pleasure in the body are the medicine.\n\nYou may need to learn that you can stand on your own ground. Saving, making and earning your own way bring a calm that intensity never did.","At each new moon, add a coin and a pinch of earth from your own garden or a plant pot to a jar kept on the altar."],["Growth comes through curiosity, listening and everyday learning, after a habit of preaching or holding big beliefs. Neighbours, siblings, short journeys and conversation teach you more than distant gurus.\n\nAsk questions. Take notes. The path is in the details, and your great ideas grow wiser for being shared in plain words.","Write a question each new moon and keep it with a feather; let the month answer it through ordinary conversation."],["Growth points to home, family and inner life, after a pull towards career and public role. Rest, roots and private care are the work.\n\nYou may have achieved much in the world and still feel hungry. The nourishment you seek is at the hearth. Building a home and tending feelings is not a step back; it is the way forward.","Light a candle at the hearth or kitchen table at each new moon and speak one thing you will do for home this month."],["Growth comes through joy, creativity and self-expression, after a habit of hiding in groups or causes. You are asked to step into the light as yourself.\n\nMake things, play, love openly and take personal risks. It may feel vulnerable. That vulnerability is the gift; your heart is meant to be seen.","On a new moon, begin a creative work and dedicate it to the North Node with a gold candle and a sprig of sunflower or calendula."],["Growth is through practical service, routine and the care of the body, after a pull towards escape, dream and retreat. Daily life is the spiritual path here.\n\nOrder, health and useful work ground you. Make the spiritual practical: tea at the same hour, a tidy altar, a job well done.","Keep a small daily ritual at the same time each day, with a cup of herbal tea and a lit candle, and keep it for a full lunar month."],["Growth comes through partnership, cooperation and listening to others, after a habit of going it alone. You are asked to let others in and to share decisions.\n\nThis can feel like losing yourself; it is finding yourself in relationship. Compromise, fairness and honest negotiation are skills to build.","Light two candles from one flame at the new moon and name one way you will meet another person halfway this month."],["Growth goes into depth, intimacy and shared resources, after a pull towards comfort and keeping things safe and simple. You are asked to let go of control and let yourself be changed.\n\nTrust, vulnerability and facing endings bring growth. Let others help you; share what you have; meet the deep waters.","At the new moon after an eclipse, write what you hold too tightly and release it into running water."],["Growth lies in meaning, travel, study and faith, after a habit of living in the details and the everyday. You are asked to look up and out.\n\nBig questions, foreign places and higher learning feed the soul. Trust your intuition as well as the facts; the wider view is the way forward.","On a new moon, choose one subject or place to explore this year and mark it with a blue candle and a bay leaf."],["Growth points to career, public life and responsibility, after a pull towards home and private comfort. You are asked to step into the world and build something lasting.\n\nTaking on authority may feel uncomfortable. Do it anyway, gently. Your contribution is meant to be visible.","At noon at the new moon, write a goal for your vocation and keep it under a black stone for steady progress."],["Growth comes through friendship, community and shared hopes, after a habit of seeking personal glory. You are asked to belong and to contribute to something bigger than yourself.\n\nGroups, causes and networks bring the growth. Let your gifts serve others' hopes as well as your own.","At the new moon, write a wish for a community you belong to, and give the paper to the group or burn it with them."],["Growth lies in spirituality, solitude, compassion and surrender, after a pull towards busy routine and control. You are asked to trust what cannot be measured.\n\nRetreat, prayer, dreams and quiet service are the way. Let go of needing to fix everything; let something larger hold you.","Spend the night of a new moon in silence, with a candle, a bowl of water and a prayer of surrender spoken before sleep."]],n=[["You arrive knowing how to look after yourself, act alone and make your mark, and these instincts are real strengths. The trap is staying there: making every situation about your own needs, or never letting another person share the wheel.\n\nThe opposite house, the seventh, is where the North Node points. Use the old self-reliance to give partners the steadiness they need, and let relationship teach you what independence cannot.\n\nIn practice, notice how often you decide alone. Try deciding with someone.","Light a white candle for the North Node and a black one for the South at the full moon, and let the black one burn down first."],["You carry an instinct for comfort, security and holding on to what is yours. You may be good with money and loyal to habits. The trap is clinging: to possessions, to old ways, to a safety that keeps you small.\n\nThe North Node in the eighth asks you to share, risk and be changed. Use the steadiness you bring as a base for depth, not as a wall against it.\n\nLet go of one thing you hold out of fear, and notice what comes in.","At the full moon, give away one possession you hold onto out of fear, with a word of thanks, and burn a black candle for the old habit."],["You arrive with a quick mind, a talent for detail and an instinct for gathering facts. The trap is staying busy with information and never stepping back to ask what it all means.\n\nThe North Node in the ninth points to meaning, faith and the long view. Use your skill with words to carry larger truths, not just to collect more facts.\n\nTry reading less and reflecting more; let one idea sink in before reaching for the next.","At the full moon, burn a list of facts you have been chasing, and write one question about meaning to keep instead."],["You carry deep instincts for home, family and emotional care. You may be the one who looks after everyone. The trap is hiding at the hearth, keeping the world at bay or staying a child in the family pattern.\n\nThe North Node in the tenth asks you to step out and take responsibility in the world. Use your care as a strength in public life, as a leader who looks after people.\n\nLet the home be your base, not your boundary.","At the full moon, light a black candle on the hearth for old family roles and a white one at a window for the world you are stepping into."],["You arrive with confidence in self-expression, play and the spotlight. The trap is needing to be special, the centre of every story, or seeking applause over connection.\n\nThe North Node in the eleventh points to community and shared hopes. Use your creativity and warmth for the group, and let others shine too.\n\nJoin something where you are one voice among many; that is where you will find what the spotlight could not give.","At the full moon, offer a creative piece to a group or friend rather than performing it, and burn a black candle for the old need to be seen."],["You carry skills in service, routine, health and practical help. You may be the reliable one who fixes things. The trap is busyness, worry and perfectionism that leave no room for the spirit.\n\nThe North Node in the twelfth asks for surrender, rest and faith. Use the old habits of care to tend your inner life, and let some things stay undone.\n\nTrust that the world will not fall apart if you stop for a while.","At the full moon, write a list of tasks you will let go of this month, and burn it with a black candle and a pinch of lavender."],["You arrive knowing how to relate, please and keep the peace. The trap is losing yourself in others, letting partners decide, or needing approval before you act.\n\nThe North Node in the first points to independence and self-direction. Use your skill with people as a strength, but make your own choices.\n\nPractise saying what you want first, before asking what others want.","At the full moon, write one decision you will make for yourself, and burn a black candle for the old habit of waiting for permission."],["You carry instincts for crisis, intensity, depth and other people's resources. You may be good in emergencies and at seeing through people. The trap is living from crisis to crisis, or depending on others' power and money.\n\nThe North Node in the second asks for simplicity, self-reliance and steady value. Use your depth to build something of your own.\n\nNotice when you create drama to feel alive, and try a quiet pleasure instead.","At the full moon, bury a black candle stub with salt to close an old crisis, and plant a seed in a pot for steady growth."],["You arrive with strong beliefs, a love of big ideas and an instinct to teach or preach. The trap is certainty: being sure you know, and not listening to the people in front of you.\n\nThe North Node in the third points to curiosity, conversation and learning from everyday life. Use your wisdom to ask questions, not just to give answers.\n\nTalk to neighbours; listen to siblings; let small conversations teach you.","At the full moon, write a belief you hold too tightly and burn it, keeping a question in its place on the altar."],["You carry instincts for ambition, achievement and public responsibility. You may be competent and respected. The trap is defining yourself by status, or neglecting home and feelings in service of a role.\n\nThe North Node in the fourth asks you to come home: to feelings, family and private life. Use your competence to build a home that nourishes you.\n\nYour worth is not your work.","At the full moon, set aside a symbol of your work and light a black candle for the old role, then spend the evening at home."],["You arrive at ease in groups, networks and causes, with an instinct to belong. The trap is hiding in the crowd, following the group's wishes or avoiding personal risk.\n\nThe North Node in the fifth points to personal expression, creativity and love. Use your sense of community as a base from which to shine as yourself.\n\nTake one creative risk on your own, outside any group.","At the full moon, light a black candle for the old need to blend in, and make something only you could make."],["You carry instincts for retreat, dream, compassion and the unseen. You may be deeply spiritual and sensitive. The trap is escape: drifting, withdrawing or avoiding practical life.\n\nThe North Node in the sixth asks for daily structure, service and care of the body. Use your sensitivity as a healer in practical ways.\n\nGround the spiritual in daily tasks; the sacred is in the washing up as well as the dream.","At the full moon, write one practical task to complete this month, and burn a black candle with a sprig of mugwort for the old drift."]],s=[["Lilith here sits on the body and the self you show. You may have been told you were too much, too wild or too strange, and learned either to hide or to provoke. People react strongly to your presence, sometimes before you speak.\n\nThe work is owning that power without apology or performance. When you stop shrinking and stop shocking, you become someone who simply refuses to be made smaller, and that is a quiet revolution.","At the dark moon, stand bare-faced before a mirror by a black candle and say your own name with all its power."],["Lilith here touches money, possessions and self-worth. You may have felt that your value was defined by others, or reject material things entirely as a kind of defiance. Pleasure and the body's appetites may carry shame.\n\nThe work is claiming your own worth and pleasure on your own terms, free of both greed and guilt. You may earn in unusual or taboo ways, or teach others to value what the world dismisses.","At the dark moon, buy or make something beautiful purely for your own pleasure and dedicate it to Lilith with a red candle."],["Lilith here sits in speech and mind. You may have been silenced, or have said what others would not and paid for it. Your words can be sharp, taboo or prophetic.\n\nThe work is speaking your truth without needing to shock and without swallowing it. Writing, poetry and honest speech about hidden things are your power.","Write the words you were never allowed to say on paper at the dark moon, read them aloud, and keep them under a black stone."],["Lilith here touches home and family. There may be a story of a rejected or rejecting mother, family secrets, or an outsider's place in the household. You may struggle with domestic roles.\n\nThe work is making a home that holds your wildness, and healing the family pattern without taking on its shame. Your home can become a sanctuary for others who have been cast out.","Set a small shrine to the outcast women of your line at the dark moon, with a black candle, a pomegranate seed and a bowl of water."],["Lilith here sits in love, pleasure and creativity. Desire may be strong, unconventional or shamed, and you may be drawn to intense or forbidden romances. Creative work may be raw and daring.\n\nThe work is enjoying pleasure without shame and without using it as power. Your art can speak for the parts of life that others hide.","Make art from desire at the dark moon, and keep it for yourself as an offering to Lilith."],["Lilith here touches work, health and routine. You may resist being told what to do, or feel trapped by drudgery. The body may hold buried anger in tension or chronic symptoms.\n\nThe work is finding work that does not cage you, and listening to the body's protests. You may be a reformer of how work is done, especially for those who are exploited.","At the dark moon, write the ways you refuse to be used, and burn the paper in a black candle's flame."],["Lilith here sits in partnership. You may attract partners who reject, dominate or idealise you, or refuse conventional relationships. Power and equality in love are live questions.\n\nThe work is meeting a partner as an equal: neither submitting nor controlling. Honest negotiation of desire, freedom and fairness is your path.","At the dark moon, write the terms of an equal love on paper, sign it yourself, and keep it under a red candle."],["This is a natural home for Lilith: intimacy, death, sex and the hidden. Desire and power run deep, and you may be drawn to taboo, the occult and the edges of experience.\n\nThe work is owning these depths without shame, and without using them to control. You may have a gift for working with the forbidden, the grieving and the transformed.","Work with Lilith at the dark moon with a black candle, a pomegranate and a bowl of water, and ask her to show you your own power."],["Lilith here touches belief and faith. You may reject orthodox religion, be drawn to heresy or to goddess traditions, or carry wounds from a religious upbringing.\n\nThe work is finding a faith that includes the wild and the feminine, and that does not ask you to deny yourself. You may teach heretical or reclaimed wisdom.","Study one figure who was cast out by a tradition, and honour her at the dark moon with a black candle and a written prayer."],["Lilith here sits on career and public life. You may be seen as rebellious, controversial or outside the system, or refuse to play by its rules. Authority may be a battle.\n\nThe work is building a public life on your own terms, and using your voice for those who are silenced. You may make your name by refusing to fit.","At noon at the dark moon, write the work you will do on your own terms and keep it under Obsidian."],["Lilith here touches friendships and groups. You may feel rejected by groups, or reject them first, and be drawn to outsider communities.\n\nThe work is finding or creating communities that welcome the wild and the different, and helping them stay honest. Your friendships can be fiercely loyal once trust is won.","Gather with outsiders and kindred spirits at the dark moon, sharing a cup of red wine or juice poured first for Lilith."],["Lilith here sits in the unconscious: hidden anger, buried desire, and old shame. You may have dreams of wildness and exile. The deepest power is hidden, even from you.\n\nThe work is shadow work: meeting what you have hidden, without fear. Dream work, therapy and solitary ritual can turn this into a quiet, powerful self-knowledge.","Keep a shadow journal by a black candle at the dark moon, writing down any dream in which you are wild or cast out."]]},3068,[]);
__d(function(g,_r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"deepen",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const t=(t,n)=>n?{...t,detailed:`${t.detailed}\n\n${n[0]}`,magic:`${t.magic} ${n[1]}`}:t},3069,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PLANET_IN_SIGN_BY_BODY",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return U}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PLANET_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return P}});var N=r(d[0]),_=r(d[1]),I=r(d[2]),t=r(d[3]),n=r(d[4]),S=r(d[5]),u=r(d[6]),o=r(d[7]),G=r(d[8]),O=r(d[9]),c=r(d[10]),s=r(d[11]),E=r(d[12]);const U={Mercury:S.MERCURY_IN_SIGN,Venus:s.VENUS_IN_SIGN,Mars:n.MARS_IN_SIGN,Jupiter:I.JUPITER_IN_SIGN,Saturn:O.SATURN_IN_SIGN,Uranus:c.URANUS_IN_SIGN,Neptune:u.NEPTUNE_IN_SIGN,Pluto:G.PLUTO_IN_SIGN,Chiron:_.CHIRON_IN_SIGN,'North Node':o.NORTH_NODE_IN_SIGN,'South Node':o.SOUTH_NODE_IN_SIGN,Lilith:t.LILITH_IN_SIGN},P=Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(U).flatMap(([_,I])=>N.SIGNS.map(N=>[E.keys.planetInSign(_,N),I[N]])))},3070,[2705,3071,3072,3073,3074,3075,3076,3077,3078,3079,3080,3081,3046]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CHIRON_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o={Aries:{simple:"Chiron in Aries points to a tender place around your right to exist, act and take up space. Healing comes as you learn courage, and you can help others find theirs.",detailed:"In myth Chiron was the wise centaur, teacher of heroes, who could heal others but not his own wound. In the chart he points to a sore place that becomes a source of wisdom. In Aries the sore place is identity and self-assertion: you may have felt, early on, that being yourself or being angry was dangerous, or that you had to fight simply to be allowed. Some people with this placement doubt their right to be here at all; others over-prove it.\n\nThe healing is learning to act from your own centre, to be brave without armour, and to be angry in clean, honest ways. As you do, you often become someone who helps others find their courage: a coach, advocate or teacher of confidence.\n\nChiron stayed in Aries for years at a time (around 1968 to 1977 and 2018 to 2027), so many people share it. Its house shows where the wound and the gift live in your life.",magic:"Courage and self-blessing magic is healing for you: a daily candle lit for your own life, a self-dedication rite, and protection spells for your right to take up space. Carnelian, Bloodstone and nettle support the work; Asclepius, the healer Chiron taught, is an old patron for this road.",shadow:"Self-doubt, or over-fighting to prove your right to exist."},Taurus:{simple:"Chiron in Taurus points to a tender place around worth, security and the body. Healing comes as you learn to feel safe and valuable, and you help others do the same.",detailed:"With Chiron in Taurus the sore place is security and self-worth: perhaps scarcity, a difficult relationship with the body or food, or a feeling that your value depends on what you have or produce. You may hold on tightly to comfort, or feel you never quite have enough.\n\nThe healing is learning that your worth is inherent, that the body is a home rather than a problem, and that safety can be built from within. People with this placement often become gifted at helping others with money, body image or grounding.\n\nChiron was in Taurus around 1976 to 1983 (and returns around 2026 to 2034). Its house shows where this work lives for you.",magic:"Grounding and body magic is healing for you: herbal baths, gardening as prayer, prosperity spells done from gratitude rather than fear, and self-love rituals. Rose Quartz, Smoky Quartz and patchouli steady and comfort.",shadow:"Scarcity fear, and difficulty receiving pleasure or plenty."},Gemini:{simple:"Chiron in Gemini points to a tender place around your voice, mind and learning. Healing comes as you trust your intelligence, and you become a gifted communicator.",detailed:"With Chiron in Gemini the sore place is the mind and the voice: perhaps you felt stupid at school, were not listened to, or had a difficult relationship with a sibling. You may doubt your intelligence or over-talk to prove it.\n\nThe healing is learning that your way of thinking is valid and valuable, and finding your own voice. People with this placement often become excellent teachers, writers and translators for those who struggle to be understood.\n\nChiron was in Gemini around 1983 to 1988. Look to its house for the part of life where you most fear being misunderstood, and where your words can most heal.",magic:"Word and voice magic is healing for you: journaling, speaking affirmations aloud, writing letters you may never send, and blessing your study space. Blue Lace Agate, Fluorite and lavender support a clear, kind voice.",shadow:"Self-doubt about your mind, and fear of speaking."},Cancer:{simple:"Chiron in Cancer points to a tender place around home, family and being cared for. Healing comes as you learn to nurture yourself, and you become a true carer.",detailed:"With Chiron in Cancer the sore place is belonging and nurture: perhaps a family that could not care for you as you needed, a home that did not feel safe, or a feeling of being emotionally alone. You may give care easily but struggle to receive it.\n\nThe healing is learning to mother yourself, building a home that holds you and letting others in. People with this placement often become deeply compassionate carers, therapists and keepers of chosen family.\n\nChiron was in Cancer around 1988 to 1991. Its house shows which room of your life most needs mothering, by you.",magic:"Hearth and moon magic is healing for you: moon water baths, ancestor healing, home blessings and kitchen magic. Moonstone, Rose Quartz and Lemon Balm comfort and soothe.",shadow:"Fear of abandonment, and caring for everyone except yourself."},Leo:{simple:"Chiron in Leo points to a tender place around being seen, loved and creative. Healing comes as you learn to shine for yourself, and you help others find their light.",detailed:"With Chiron in Leo the sore place is self-expression and recognition: perhaps you felt unseen or unappreciated as a child, or that play and joy were not safe. You may hide your light, or need constant reassurance that you matter.\n\nThe healing is learning that you are worthy of love and attention as you are, and finding joy in creating for its own sake. People with this placement often become generous mentors who help others shine.\n\nChiron was in Leo around 1991 to 1993. Its house shows where you hide your light, and where you will one day help others find theirs.",magic:"Creative and solar magic is healing for you: art as devotion, confidence rituals, play as sacred practice, and celebrating yourself on your birthday. Sunstone, Citrine and Calendula support a warm heart.",shadow:"Hiding your light, or needing applause to feel real."},Virgo:{simple:"Chiron in Virgo points to a tender place around being good enough, useful and well. Healing comes as you accept imperfection, and you become a gentle healer.",detailed:"With Chiron in Virgo the sore place is perfection and health: perhaps you felt you had to be perfect to be loved, or struggled with illness, anxiety or a body that did not cooperate. You may be harsh with yourself about small mistakes.\n\nThe healing is learning self-acceptance, kindness toward the body and the value of good enough. People with this placement often become skilled healers, herbalists and helpers who understand from the inside.\n\nChiron was in Virgo around 1993 to 1995. Its house shows where you are hardest on yourself, and where gentleness heals most.",magic:"Herbal and healing magic is your own medicine: herbal remedies (beside proper care), cleansing rituals, and self-acceptance spells. Amazonite, Moss Agate and Chamomile soothe the inner critic.",shadow:"Perfectionism, and anxiety about health or worth."},Libra:{simple:"Chiron in Libra points to a tender place around relationship, fairness and balance. Healing comes as you learn to be whole on your own, and you become a wise partner.",detailed:"With Chiron in Libra the sore place is relationship: perhaps an early experience of unfairness, a parent's difficult marriage, or a fear of being alone. You may lose yourself in partners or keep the peace at your own cost.\n\nThe healing is learning to be whole on your own, to stand up for fairness to yourself, and to choose partnerships of equals. People with this placement often become gifted counsellors, mediators and advocates.\n\nChiron moved through Libra quickly, around 1995 to 1996 (and again around 1945 to 1946). Its house shows the kind of relationship where the old hurt and the new wisdom meet.",magic:"Relationship and balance magic heals you: self-love rituals, cord cutting from unhealthy bonds, and spells for justice. Rose Quartz, Lapis Lazuli and rose support a balanced heart.",shadow:"Codependence, and peacekeeping at your own cost."},Scorpio:{simple:"Chiron in Scorpio points to a tender place around trust, intimacy and loss. Healing comes as you face the depths, and you become a guide through crisis.",detailed:"With Chiron in Scorpio the sore place is trust and power: perhaps early loss, betrayal or a crisis that taught you the world is not safe. You may guard yourself fiercely or test people before letting them close.\n\nThe healing is learning to trust again, to share power and to let go. People with this placement often become powerful healers, therapists and guides for others through grief and transformation.\n\nChiron was in Scorpio around 1996 to 1999. Its house shows where trust is hardest won and most precious.",magic:"Deep healing magic suits you: shadow work, grief rituals, cord cutting and protection. Obsidian, Rhodochrosite and Wormwood support the work; Persephone, who returned from the underworld, is a fitting companion.",shadow:"Distrust, and control as protection."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Chiron in Sagittarius points to a tender place around faith, meaning and freedom. Healing comes as you find your own truth, and you become a wise teacher.",detailed:"With Chiron in Sagittarius the sore place is meaning and belief: perhaps a strict or broken faith, or a feeling that life has no meaning. You may search endlessly or reject every belief.\n\nThe healing is finding your own philosophy through experience, and holding it with humility. People with this placement often become teachers and guides who help others find meaning. Sagittarius is itself pictured as a centaur, and some ancient writers took the archer for Chiron, so astrologers often feel the link strongly here.\n\nChiron was in Sagittarius around 1999 to 2001. Its house shows where you are searching, and where your hard-won truth can guide others.",magic:"Seeking and devotional magic heals you: pilgrimage, study as devotion, and gratitude rituals. Turquoise, Lapis Lazuli and Sage support steady faith.",shadow:"Cynicism, and endless searching without arriving."},Capricorn:{simple:"Chiron in Capricorn points to a tender place around success, authority and responsibility. Healing comes as you define success your own way, and you become a wise elder.",detailed:"With Chiron in Capricorn the sore place is achievement and authority: perhaps a demanding parent, early responsibility, or a feeling that you will never achieve enough. You may overwork or fear failure deeply.\n\nThe healing is learning that your worth is not in your achievements, and defining success on your own terms. People with this placement often become mentors and leaders who use authority with kindness.\n\nChiron was in Capricorn around 2001 to 2005. Its house shows where you push hardest, and where rest is part of the healing.",magic:"Structured, ancestral magic heals you: ancestor rituals, boundary charms, and spells for gentle, sustainable success. Onyx, Garnet and comfrey support steady healing.",shadow:"Fear of failure, and working to be worthy."},Aquarius:{simple:"Chiron in Aquarius points to a tender place around belonging and being different. Healing comes as you embrace your uniqueness, and you help outsiders find their place.",detailed:"With Chiron in Aquarius the sore place is belonging: perhaps feeling like an outsider, rejected by groups, or too different to fit in. You may hide your uniqueness or push others away first.\n\nThe healing is embracing your difference and finding your true community. People with this placement often become champions for outsiders and builders of inclusive communities.\n\nChiron was in Aquarius around 2005 to 2011. Its house shows where you feel most like an outsider, and where you can make a place for others.",magic:"Communal and inventive magic heals you: group rituals, friendship spells, and rituals that honour your difference. Amethyst, Aquamarine and lavender support a clear, free heart.",shadow:"Isolation, and feeling like an outsider everywhere."},Pisces:{simple:"Chiron in Pisces points to a tender place around boundaries, spirit and feeling everything. Healing comes as you learn to protect your sensitivity, and you become a spiritual healer.",detailed:"With Chiron in Pisces the sore place is sensitivity and boundaries: perhaps you absorbed others' pain early, felt overwhelmed by the world, or struggled to know where you end and others begin. You may escape or over-give.\n\nThe healing is learning to protect your sensitivity, to ground spiritual gifts, and to serve without dissolving. People with this placement often become compassionate healers, artists and spiritual guides.\n\nChiron was in Pisces for years at a time (around 1960 to 1968 and 2010 to 2019), so many people share it. Its house shows where your sensitivity is most exposed, and where it is most needed.",magic:"Dream and water magic heals you: cleansing baths, protection rituals for sensitive people, meditation and dreamwork. Amethyst, Black Tourmaline and mugwort support boundaries and vision.",shadow:"Overwhelm, escapism, and losing yourself in others' pain."}}},3071,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"JUPITER_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o={Aries:{simple:"With Jupiter in Aries you grow by being brave. Luck tends to come when you take the first step, back yourself and lead.",detailed:"Jupiter in Aries puts faith into action. You believe in initiative and independence, and your opportunities often come from going first: starting the business, applying before you feel ready, speaking up for what is right. You can be a natural pioneer and an inspiring leader, generous with encouragement and quick to back a person or idea you believe in.\n\nThe gift is optimistic courage. You recover quickly from setbacks and trust that there is always another beginning. The challenge is excess in the Aries direction: overconfidence, impatience, and starting more than you can sustain. Jupiter makes things bigger, including the temper and the rush.\n\nBecause Jupiter stays about a year in each sign, everyone born within a twelvemonth of you shares it; the house it falls in and the planets it touches make it yours. Mars rules Aries, so Jupiter here works through Mars: look to your Mars to see how your luck likes to move.",magic:"Luck magic for you is active: a candle lit on the day you begin something, a courage-and-fortune charm carried to interviews, and spells cast at the first new Moon of spring. Thursdays and Tuesdays suit you. Carnelian, Citrine, cinnamon and Star Anise draw bold good fortune.",shadow:"Overconfidence, haste, and believing that will alone is enough."},Taurus:{simple:"With Jupiter in Taurus you grow through patience, the senses and steady building. Abundance comes slowly and stays.",detailed:"Jupiter in Taurus finds the sacred in the material world: good food, land, beauty, the body, money well earned and well kept. You tend to trust what you can touch, and your faith is practical. Wealth often grows for you through patience, sound investment, craft or the earth, and you are generous with comfort and hospitality.\n\nThe gift is a genuine talent for enjoying and sharing abundance. You can make a home or garden flourish and help others feel secure. The challenge is excess of comfort: indulgence, materialism, or so much attachment to stability that you miss the growth that change brings.\n\nEveryone born in your year has Jupiter in Taurus too. What sets yours apart is its house, which shows where in life the abundance gathers. Venus rules Taurus, so Jupiter here works through Venus, and your Venus says what kind of abundance truly feeds you.",magic:"Prosperity magic suits you very well: money jars filled over months, a herb or vegetable garden blessed at each planting, and gratitude offerings of bread, honey and coins. Thursdays and Fridays, and the waxing Moon in Taurus, suit you. Green Aventurine, Pyrite, basil and cinnamon draw steady abundance.",shadow:"Overindulgence, materialism, and comfort mistaken for growth."},Gemini:{simple:"With Jupiter in Gemini you grow by learning, talking and connecting. Luck comes through ideas, words, networks and curiosity.",detailed:"Jupiter is in detriment in Gemini, opposite its home in Sagittarius. Traditionally this means Jupiter's big vision is pulled into Gemini's many small pieces of information. In life that often gives a mind hungry for everything: languages, books, facts, people, places. Your opportunities often come through communication, teaching, writing, trading or simply knowing the right person.\n\nThe gift is breadth: you can see connections across many fields and are often a generous, entertaining teacher. The challenge is depth and wisdom. Collecting information is not the same as understanding, and Jupiter's tendency to overdo can scatter you across too many projects.\n\nYour whole school year shares this Jupiter. Its house is the personal part, the area of life where curiosity pays. Mercury rules Gemini, so look to your Mercury to see how your luck likes to talk.",magic:"Your fortune magic works through words and travel: petitions written for opportunities, luck charms carried on short journeys, and divination for guidance. Thursdays and Wednesdays suit you. Citrine, Fluorite, Star Anise and peppermint open the way for good news.",shadow:"Scattered enthusiasm, knowing a little about everything, and talking more than understanding."},Cancer:{simple:"With Jupiter in Cancer, where it is exalted, you grow through caring, belonging and home. Your generosity is warm and your luck often flows through family.",detailed:"Jupiter is exalted in Cancer, which traditional astrologers read as one of its most honoured places: generosity at its most nurturing. You have a big heart and a strong instinct to protect and provide. Family, roots, home, the past and emotional security are where your faith lives, and you often have a gift for making people feel welcome and fed.\n\nThe gift is real kindness and the ability to create a home that blesses everyone in it. Opportunities may come through family, property, the land, food or caring work. The challenge is over-protection and sentimentality: smothering, holding on to the past, or giving so much that you neglect yourself.\n\nA year's worth of births share it; your Jupiter's house shows which part of life most wants your generosity. The Moon rules Cancer, so your Moon shows how your generosity is best received.",magic:"Hearth and family magic is where your fortune lives: kitchen blessings, ancestor offerings, a prosperity spell for the household, and moon water used to bless the home. Thursdays and Mondays, and the full Moon, suit you. Moonstone, Selenite, Lemon Balm and a bowl of salt at the hearth draw protection and plenty home; Demeter and Ceres, mothers of the harvest, are fitting patrons.",shadow:"Smothering, clinging to the past, and giving until there is nothing left."},Leo:{simple:"With Jupiter in Leo you grow by shining, creating and leading with your heart. Your generosity is big, warm and a bit theatrical.",detailed:"Jupiter in Leo is a king's Jupiter: generous, proud, warm and grand. You believe in joy, play and self-expression, and you can lift a whole room with your enthusiasm. Opportunities often come through creativity, performance, leadership, children or anything where your heart is visibly involved.\n\nThe gift is magnanimity: you are generous with praise, encouragement and celebration, and you inspire others to believe in themselves. The challenge is grandiosity: needing to be the centre, overspending on show, or taking yourself too seriously. Pride can blind you to good advice.\n\nClassmates born near you share it, so look to its house for where your own faith in life is strongest. The Sun rules Leo, so your Sun says much about where your fortune wants to shine.",magic:"Solar success and joy magic suits you: a spell for recognition, a creative work offered as thanks, a celebration ritual at Lughnasadh or midsummer. Thursdays and Sundays suit you. Sunstone, Citrine, Calendula and Sunflower draw warmth and success; Apollo and Lugh, gods of many skills and the sun's bright strength, are fitting patrons.",shadow:"Grandiosity, showing off, and pride that will not take advice."},Virgo:{simple:"With Jupiter in Virgo you grow through service, skill and doing things well. Your luck comes from attention to detail and practical help.",detailed:"Jupiter is in detriment in Virgo, opposite its home in Pisces. Traditionally this means Jupiter's broad faith is narrowed into Virgo's detail. In life it often gives a person whose generosity is practical: you help by fixing, teaching skills, healing and improving. You believe in work, health and craft, and your opportunities often come through competence.\n\nThe gift is useful wisdom: you can make big ideas practical and help many people in small, real ways. The challenge is that Jupiter's tendency to expand can turn Virgo's precision into worry, perfectionism or a never-ending list of improvements. Faith may need to be found in the process rather than the finish line.\n\nLike everyone born that year you carry it, and its house shows where your quiet usefulness grows into luck. Mercury rules Virgo, so your Mercury colours how your gifts are offered.",magic:"Herbcraft, healing and household magic are your fortune: remedies made with care, cleansing rituals, a well-kept grimoire, and spells for good, steady work. Thursdays and Wednesdays, and the harvest months, suit you. Amazonite, Moss Agate, fennel and Chamomile support health and steady luck.",shadow:"Worry, perfectionism, and missing the forest for the trees."},Libra:{simple:"With Jupiter in Libra you grow through partnership, fairness and beauty. Luck often comes through other people and through being gracious.",detailed:"Jupiter in Libra believes in justice, harmony and relationship. You are often generous in partnership, good at bringing people together, and drawn to law, diplomacy, the arts and anything where fairness matters. Opportunities tend to arrive through partners, collaborators, clients and social connections.\n\nThe gift is graciousness: people enjoy working with you, and you can build bridges between very different sides. The challenge is overdoing the wish to please: promising too much, avoiding necessary conflict, or relying on others for your growth instead of building your own.\n\nIt is shared by a whole year of births. Its house shows where partnership most opens doors for you. Venus rules Libra, so your Venus shows how your luck is shared.",magic:"Your fortune magic is about relationship and justice: sweetening spells for business partnerships, petitions for a fair outcome, beauty rituals as devotion. Thursdays and Fridays, and the Moon in Libra, suit you. Lapis Lazuli, Rose Quartz, rose and Vervain are allies; Athena and Maat are fitting patrons of wise judgement.",shadow:"People-pleasing, overcommitting, and growth that waits for someone else."},Scorpio:{simple:"With Jupiter in Scorpio you grow through depth, intensity and transformation. Your luck is often found in crisis, research and shared resources.",detailed:"Jupiter in Scorpio looks for meaning in the depths. You are drawn to psychology, the occult, research, healing and the mysteries of life, death and sex. Your faith is not easy optimism but something tested and earned. Opportunities can come through other people's money, inheritance, investment, or work that others are afraid of.\n\nThe gift is regenerative power: you can find gold in the dark, help others through crisis and rebuild after loss. The challenge is excess intensity: obsession, power struggles, or using your insight to control rather than heal.\n\nA whole year shares it; your Jupiter's house shows where you dig for treasure and find it. Mars and Pluto, the traditional and modern rulers of Scorpio, colour how this Jupiter seeks.",magic:"Deep magic suits your fortune: divination, shadow work, transformation rituals, and protection for shared finances. Thursdays and Tuesdays, and the dark Moon, suit you. Obsidian, Labradorite, Wormwood and Dragon\u2019s Blood are allies; Hekate and Persephone, keepers of the hidden ways, are fitting patrons.",shadow:"Obsession, power games, and suspicion of good fortune."},Sagittarius:{simple:"With Jupiter in Sagittarius, its own sign, you grow through faith, travel, learning and adventure. Your optimism is natural and catching.",detailed:"Jupiter is at home in Sagittarius, and here it is at its most expansive. You are a natural seeker: philosophy, religion, foreign lands, higher learning and big ideas are where you feel alive. You have faith in life's goodness, and your generosity is open-handed and frank. Opportunities often come through travel, teaching, publishing or simply saying yes.\n\nThe gift is real wisdom and an infectious enthusiasm for life. You can be a wonderful teacher and a generous friend. Traditional astrologers read Jupiter in its own sign as strong and beneficent. The challenge is excess: overpromising, overconfidence, preachiness, or restlessness that never lets you settle into what you have found.\n\nYour year shares it, and every twelve years Jupiter comes home to its own place in your chart, a return many people feel as a fresh start. As Jupiter rules this sign, Jupiter here is its own ruler: the story is told by its house and aspects.",magic:"Expansive, lucky magic is yours: travel blessings, spells for success in study or publishing, and devotions to the gods of your path. Thursdays and Jupiter hours, and the Moon in Sagittarius, suit you. Turquoise, Lapis Lazuli, Sage and nutmeg draw luck and wisdom; Zeus and Jupiter themselves are the old patrons of this placement.",shadow:"Overconfidence, preachiness, and promising more than you can give."},Capricorn:{simple:"With Jupiter in Capricorn you grow through discipline, responsibility and long-term ambition. Luck comes slowly, earned by hard work.",detailed:"Jupiter is in fall in Capricorn, opposite its exaltation in Cancer. Traditional astrologers read this as Jupiter's generosity constrained by Saturn's caution. In life it often gives someone who believes in effort, structure and earned success rather than easy luck. You can be very good at building institutions, businesses and careers, and your faith grows with each real achievement.\n\nThe gift is practical wisdom and the ability to make dreams real and lasting. The challenge is scarcity thinking: doubting that good things can come easily, being too cautious to take an opportunity, or measuring worth only by status and results.\n\nYour birth year shares it, and its house shows where patient work turns into fortune. Saturn rules Capricorn, so your Saturn shows what your growth is built on.",magic:"Your fortune magic is structured and patient: career spells worked over a season, a prosperity plan blessed at each new Moon, and ancestor rites for guidance on the long road. Thursdays and Saturdays suit you. Garnet, Onyx, Pyrite and cypress support steady, earned success.",shadow:"Pessimism about luck, status-seeking, and too much caution."},Aquarius:{simple:"With Jupiter in Aquarius you grow through friendship, community and new ideas. Luck comes through networks, causes and thinking ahead.",detailed:"Jupiter in Aquarius believes in humanity, progress and freedom. You are often drawn to science, technology, social causes and groups, and your generosity is directed toward the collective. Opportunities may come through friends, networks, online communities or innovative projects.\n\nThe gift is visionary thinking and an open mind: you can imagine a better future and help build it with others. The challenge is detachment and dogma: loving ideas more than people, or holding your progressive views as fiercely as any orthodoxy.\n\nYour year shares this Jupiter; its house shows where your friendships and networks are luckiest. Saturn and Uranus, the traditional and modern rulers of Aquarius, both colour this Jupiter.",magic:"Communal and future-minded magic suits your fortune: group rituals, coven work, spells for a cause, and astrological timing for new projects. Thursdays and Saturdays, and the Moon in Aquarius, suit you. Amethyst, Aquamarine, Labradorite and lavender help vision stay grounded.",shadow:"Detachment, ideological rigidity, and loving humanity more than the person in front of you."},Pisces:{simple:"With Jupiter in Pisces, its traditional home, you grow through compassion, imagination and spiritual faith. Your generosity is boundless.",detailed:"Jupiter is at home in Pisces, its night house, and here it is gentle, mystical and kind. You believe in the unseen, in compassion and in the oneness of all things. You are often drawn to spirituality, the arts, healing and service, and your generosity can be selfless. Opportunities may come through intuition, faith, creative work or simply being in the right place at the right time.\n\nThe gift is spiritual wisdom and deep compassion: you can comfort, heal and inspire. Traditional astrologers read Jupiter in its own sign as strong and beneficent. The challenge is boundaries and escapism: giving too much, believing too easily, or avoiding the hard edges of life.\n\nYour year shares it with you; its house shows where you are most likely to feel held by something larger. As the traditional ruler of Pisces, Jupiter here is its own ruler; Neptune, the modern ruler, adds its dreaming.",magic:"Devotional, dreamy magic is yours: meditation, prayer, dreamwork, healing spells and offerings to the gods of the sea. Thursdays and Mondays, and the Moon in Pisces, suit you. Amethyst, Aquamarine, Sandalwood and jasmine open the way; a bowl of water on the altar, refreshed each Thursday, is a simple, lovely devotion.",shadow:"Escapism, gullibility, and giving until you dissolve."}}},3072,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"LILITH_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n={Aries:{simple:"Lilith in Aries is a wild, independent fire that refuses to ask permission. Your raw anger and will may have been shamed, and reclaiming them is power.",detailed:"Black Moon Lilith is the point where the Moon swings farthest from Earth, and astrologers read it as the part of us that would not be tamed: desires and instincts we were taught to hide, and the fierce freedom that comes when we stop hiding them. It is named for Lilith of Jewish folklore, who in later legend refused to lie beneath Adam and left Eden rather than submit.\n\nIn Aries, Lilith is the right to want, to fight and to be first. You may have learned early that your anger, your independence or your desire to win was unattractive or dangerous, especially if you were raised as a girl. The result can be suppressed rage, or a fierce, solitary streak that will not compromise.\n\nThe reclaiming is letting your fire be clean and yours: anger as honest information, independence as a choice rather than a wound. Its house shows where this wildness lives.",magic:"Fire and freedom magic suits your Lilith: a rite of reclaiming anger (writing what you were not allowed to say and burning it), protection for your independence, and dark Moon candle work. Bloodstone, Obsidian and nettle are allies; Lilith herself and Sekhmet are old images of fierce, unapologetic power.",shadow:"Rage turned inward or let loose without aim."},Taurus:{simple:"Lilith in Taurus is the wild, sensual body that refuses shame. Pleasure, appetite and desire may have been judged, and reclaiming them is power.",detailed:"In Taurus, Lilith lives in the body and its appetites: food, touch, sex, comfort, money. You may have been shamed for wanting pleasure, for your body's size or shape, or for wanting to own and keep things. The result can be denial of pleasure, or a defiant, almost stubborn indulgence.\n\nThe reclaiming is honouring your body's wisdom and appetites without apology, and owning your worth and desire. Many people with this placement become powerful, earthy sensualists who give others permission to enjoy.\n\nIts house shows where this sensual wildness lives.",magic:"Body and earth magic suits your Lilith: sensual self-love rituals, oils and baths, dance, and offerings of food and flowers. Garnet, Rose Quartz and patchouli honour the body; Lilith and Aphrodite welcome unashamed pleasure.",shadow:"Shame about appetite, or stubborn indulgence as rebellion."},Gemini:{simple:"Lilith in Gemini is the wild, uncensored voice. Your words, questions or wit may have been silenced, and reclaiming your voice is power.",detailed:"In Gemini, Lilith lives in speech and thought. You may have been told you talked too much, asked the wrong questions, or said things that made people uncomfortable. The result can be self-censorship, or a sharp, taboo-breaking tongue.\n\nThe reclaiming is speaking your truth, writing what others will not, and trusting your restless mind. People with this placement often become fearless writers and speakers.\n\nIts house shows where this voice wants to be heard.",magic:"Word magic suits your Lilith: writing what you were never allowed to say, spoken charms, and sigils of freedom. Blue Lace Agate, Obsidian and peppermint support a free voice.",shadow:"Silence out of fear, or words used as weapons."},Cancer:{simple:"Lilith in Cancer is the wild mother and the feelings that would not be tamed. Your needs, moods or relationship to motherhood may have been judged.",detailed:"In Cancer, Lilith lives in the realm of nurture, family and emotional need. You may have been shamed for needing too much, for being too emotional, or for your choices about motherhood or care. The mother figure in your life may have been complicated.\n\nThe reclaiming is honouring your feelings and needs without shame, and nurturing in your own wild way, which may look nothing like the expected. People with this placement often redefine what care and family mean.\n\nIts house shows where this wild tenderness lives.",magic:"Moon and water magic suits your Lilith: dark Moon rituals, emotional release baths, and rituals that honour the wild mother. Moonstone, Obsidian and jasmine support the work; Lilith and Hekate both keep watch over the night.",shadow:"Shame about needing, or mothering that smothers."},Leo:{simple:"Lilith in Leo is the wild, radiant self that refuses to dim. Your desire to be seen and adored may have been shamed, and reclaiming it is power.",detailed:"In Leo, Lilith lives in self-expression, pride and the need to be seen. You may have been called vain, attention-seeking or too much for wanting to shine. The result can be hiding, or a defiant, dramatic display.\n\nThe reclaiming is letting yourself shine fully and without apology, and taking up space with joy. Many people with this placement become magnetic, unashamed performers and creators.\n\nIts house shows where this radiance lives.",magic:"Glamour and solar magic suits your Lilith: confidence rituals, performance as devotion, and adorning yourself as an act of power. Sunstone, Obsidian and Sunflower support the work.",shadow:"Hiding your light, or demanding the stage."},Virgo:{simple:"Lilith in Virgo is the wild healer who refuses perfection. Your body, imperfections or way of serving may have been judged.",detailed:"In Virgo, Lilith lives in the body, health and the need to be useful. You may have been shamed for imperfection, for your body's functions, or for refusing to serve as expected. The result can be anxious perfectionism, or a defiant refusal of all routine.\n\nThe reclaiming is accepting your imperfect body, serving on your own terms, and finding sacred wildness in craft and healing. People with this placement often become unconventional healers.\n\nIts house shows where this wild craft lives.",magic:"Herbal and healing magic suits your Lilith: wild-gathered herbs (ethically and safely), body acceptance rituals, and cleansing. Moss Agate, Obsidian and Yarrow support the work.",shadow:"Perfectionism, or rejection of all care."},Libra:{simple:"Lilith in Libra is the wild partner who refuses to please. Your desires in relationship may have been judged, and reclaiming them is power.",detailed:"In Libra, Lilith lives in relationship, beauty and fairness. You may have been expected to be agreeable, pretty and accommodating, and shamed for wanting your own way in love. The result can be people-pleasing, or a defiant refusal of convention in partnership.\n\nThe reclaiming is choosing relationships on your own terms, owning your desire for beauty and justice, and refusing to shrink to keep the peace.\n\nIts house shows where this wildness lives.",magic:"Relationship and beauty magic suits your Lilith: self-love rituals, cord cutting from unequal bonds, and glamour as power. Rose Quartz, Obsidian and rose support the work.",shadow:"Pleasing at all costs, or rejecting partnership altogether."},Scorpio:{simple:"Lilith in Scorpio is the wild, intense, sexual self in full power. Your depth, desire or anger may have been feared, and reclaiming it is power.",detailed:"In Scorpio, Lilith is especially strong: sexuality, power, intensity and taboo. You may have been shamed for your desires, your anger or your interest in the dark. The result can be secrecy, or a fierce, magnetic intensity.\n\nThe reclaiming is owning your full power and desire with integrity, and transforming shame into strength. Many people with this placement become powerful healers, witches and guides through the dark.\n\nIts house shows where this intensity lives.",magic:"Deep, dark magic suits your Lilith: shadow work, sex magic with consent and care, banishing and protection, and dark Moon rituals. Obsidian, Garnet and Dragon\u2019s Blood support the work; Lilith, Hekate and Kali are old images of this fierce power.",shadow:"Secrecy, control, and power used to wound."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Lilith in Sagittarius is the wild seeker who refuses dogma. Your beliefs or need for freedom may have been judged.",detailed:"In Sagittarius, Lilith lives in faith, freedom and truth. You may have been shamed for questioning religion, for wanting to roam, or for blunt truth-telling. The result can be hidden doubt, or a rebellious rejection of all belief.\n\nThe reclaiming is finding your own spiritual path and living your truth freely. People with this placement often become unconventional teachers and spiritual rebels.\n\nIts house shows where this freedom lives.",magic:"Seeking and wild magic suits your Lilith: pilgrimage, outdoor ritual, and spells for spiritual freedom. Turquoise, Obsidian and Sage support the work; Artemis, wild and free, is a fitting companion.",shadow:"Rebellion against every belief, or hidden doubt."},Capricorn:{simple:"Lilith in Capricorn is the wild ambition that refuses to be kept down. Your desire for power or success may have been judged.",detailed:"In Capricorn, Lilith lives in ambition, authority and status. You may have been shamed for wanting power, success or control, or told that ambition was unbecoming. The result can be hidden ambition, or a cold, fierce drive.\n\nThe reclaiming is owning your ambition and authority without apology, and building power on your own terms.\n\nIts house shows where this ambition lives.",magic:"Power and success magic suits your Lilith: career spells, rituals for authority, and ancestor work. Onyx, Obsidian and cypress support the work.",shadow:"Hidden ambition, or ruthless drive."},Aquarius:{simple:"Lilith in Aquarius is the wild outsider who refuses to conform. Your difference may have been judged, and reclaiming it is power.",detailed:"In Aquarius, Lilith lives in difference, rebellion and the collective. You may have been shamed for being strange, for unconventional ideas, or for refusing to fit in. The result can be hiding your difference, or a defiant isolation.\n\nThe reclaiming is owning your uniqueness and finding others who share your vision. People with this placement often become radical innovators.\n\nIts house shows where this rebellion lives.",magic:"Rebellious and communal magic suits your Lilith: rituals for freedom, group workings, and sigils for change. Amethyst, Obsidian and lavender support the work.",shadow:"Isolation, or rebellion without a cause."},Pisces:{simple:"Lilith in Pisces is the wild mystic who refuses to be grounded on others' terms. Your sensitivity, dreams or spiritual gifts may have been judged.",detailed:"In Pisces, Lilith lives in spirit, imagination and sensitivity. You may have been shamed for being too sensitive, too dreamy, or for psychic experiences. The result can be hiding your gifts, or escaping into fantasy.\n\nThe reclaiming is honouring your sensitivity and spiritual gifts as real power. People with this placement often become visionary artists, mystics and healers.\n\nIts house shows where this mystic wildness lives.",magic:"Dream and water magic suits your Lilith: scrying, trance, dreamwork, and ritual baths at the dark Moon. Amethyst, Obsidian and mugwort support the work.",shadow:"Escapism, or hiding your gifts."}}},3073,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MARS_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n={Aries:{simple:"With Mars in Aries, its own sign, you act fast, bravely and directly. You have strong drive, a competitive streak and a short fuse that burns out just as quickly.",detailed:"Mars is at home in Aries, and here it is pure, clean fire. You know what you want and you go for it, often before anyone else has moved. Energy comes in bursts: you are brilliant at starting, defending, competing and rescuing, and you need physical outlets or the fire turns inward as frustration. Anger is quick, honest and usually short-lived.\n\nThe gift is courage and initiative. You are the one who acts in an emergency, stands up to bullies and gets things moving. Traditional astrologers read Mars in its own sign as strong and able, its heat well directed. The challenge is impatience and recklessness: rushing in, picking fights that are not worth it, or leaving projects once the first thrill wears off.\n\nIn relationships you are passionate and direct, and you want a partner who can match your fire without being burned by it. At work you suit leadership, sport, emergency services, entrepreneurship and anything that rewards nerve. Exercise is not optional for you; it is how you stay sweet.",magic:"Yours is fire magic at full strength: courage spells, protection and warding, cord cutting, and candle work to break through obstacles. Tuesdays and Mars hours, and the waxing Moon in Aries, suit you. Carnelian, Bloodstone, basil and nettle are allies; Ares, Tyr and Sekhmet are among the old powers of righteous fight, approached through their own traditions.",shadow:"Temper, recklessness, and fighting for the sake of it."},Taurus:{simple:"With Mars in Taurus you act slowly, steadily and with great staying power. You are hard to push, very determined, and you build what you want one solid step at a time.",detailed:"Mars is in detriment in Taurus, opposite its home in Scorpio, which traditionally means Mars's quick heat is slowed by Venus's earth. In life that slowness becomes stamina. You do not start in a rush, but once you are moving you are almost impossible to stop. You work well with your hands and body, have a strong physical presence, and your desire is sensual and patient.\n\nThe gift is endurance: you finish what you begin, you can work long and hard for what you value, and you defend your home and resources without fuss. The challenge is stubbornness and slow-burning anger. You may tolerate too much for too long and then erupt, or refuse to budge even when moving would serve you.\n\nIn relationships you are loyal, physical and steady, and you want a partner who appreciates the pleasures of the body. At work you suit building, farming, crafts, cooking, finance, property and anything that grows over time. Venus rules Taurus, so Venus's sign shows what your drive is really for.",magic:"Slow, cumulative magic suits your Mars: prosperity spells worked over many nights, protection charms buried in the garden, wards of salt and iron at the doors, and body magic like dance or bread-making. Tuesdays and Fridays, and the Moon in Taurus, suit you. Red Jasper, Garnet, Smoky Quartz and thyme bring steady strength.",shadow:"Stubbornness, simmering resentment, and digging in long after it helps."},Gemini:{simple:"With Mars in Gemini you act through words and ideas. You are quick, versatile and restless, and you can argue, sell or debate brilliantly.",detailed:"Mars in Gemini fights with the mind and the tongue. Your energy is quick and scattered, moving between many projects, conversations and interests. You often have nervous energy that needs an outlet, and you are excellent at multitasking, negotiating and thinking on your feet. You can win an argument by being cleverer and faster than everyone else.\n\nThe gift is versatility and mental drive: you get many things started, you learn fast, and you can turn your hand to almost anything. The challenge is focus. Energy spreads thin, and you may start ten things and finish none. Sharp words can become your weapon of choice, and anger can come out as sarcasm or nagging rather than plain truth.\n\nIn relationships you are drawn to people who stimulate your mind and keep up with you, and you enjoy playful sparring. At work you suit writing, journalism, sales, teaching, trading, driving and anything fast and varied. Mercury rules Gemini, so Mercury's place shapes how you fight.",magic:"Your Mars works through words: binding and banishing petitions, spoken protections, sigils, knot charms and spells for winning a debate, interview or exam. Tuesdays and Wednesdays, and the Moon in an air sign, suit you. Citrine, Tiger Eye, peppermint and ginger focus the scattered fire; a written list of goals kept on the altar helps you finish what you begin.",shadow:"Scattered energy, sharp tongue, and arguing to show off."},Cancer:{simple:"With Mars in Cancer you act from feeling and protect what you love fiercely. Your drive is strongest when you are defending home, family or the vulnerable.",detailed:"Mars is in fall in Cancer, the sign opposite its exaltation in Capricorn. Traditional astrologers read this as Mars's directness made indirect: water rather than fire. In life it often looks like someone who moves sideways rather than head-on, acts on instinct and mood, and is ferocious in defence of their own. You may find it hard to be openly angry, and more likely to withdraw, sulk or use hurt as a weapon.\n\nThe gift is protective strength and emotional courage. You will fight for family, home and anyone who needs looking after, and your drive can build a safe nest for many. The challenge is indirect anger and moodiness. Old hurts can fuel present arguments, and feelings may come out as passive aggression rather than honest words.\n\nIn relationships you are tender, protective and deeply sensual, and you need emotional safety before you can be bold. At work you suit caregiving, cooking, property, history, family business and anything with a strong sense of belonging. The Moon rules Cancer, so its sign and phase show what moves you to act.",magic:"Protective hearth magic is your Mars: home warding, threshold charms, protective soups and breads, witch bottles for the house, and spells to guard children and family. Mondays and Tuesdays, and the full Moon, suit you. Moonstone, Black Tourmaline, rosemary and garlic protect the home; the moon water you make can be charged with protection as well as calm.",shadow:"Moodiness, passive aggression, and old hurts fuelling new fights."},Leo:{simple:"With Mars in Leo you act with pride, warmth and flair. You have big-hearted drive, love to lead, and fight for what you believe in with your whole self.",detailed:"Mars in Leo burns steadily and brightly. You act from the heart and want your actions to mean something; you love to create, perform, lead and be seen for your courage. Your energy is warm, generous and dramatic, and you can inspire others to follow you. Leo is a fixed sign, so once you commit you are determined and loyal.\n\nThe gift is courageous leadership and creative fire: you bring passion and joy to whatever you do, and you defend the people you love with pride. The challenge is ego. If your pride is wounded you may react with anger or stubbornness, and you can need recognition to keep going. Learning to act well when nobody is watching is part of the growth.\n\nIn relationships you are passionate, romantic and generous, and you want to be admired by your partner. At work you suit performance, management, teaching, sport, creative industries and anything with a stage. The Sun rules Leo, so your Sun shows what your fire is really for.",magic:"Your Mars magic is solar and creative: confidence and success spells, a fire ritual to burn away self-doubt, a creative project made as an offering, and protection that works by shining rather than hiding. Sundays and Tuesdays, and the Moon in Leo, suit you. Sunstone, Carnelian, cinnamon and St John\u2019s Wort lend warmth and courage; Sekhmet, the lioness, is a fierce old power of the same fire.",shadow:"Pride, needing recognition to act, and dramatic temper."},Virgo:{simple:"With Mars in Virgo you act carefully, skilfully and precisely. You put your energy into work, health and getting the details right, and you are a tireless helper.",detailed:"Mars in Virgo is a craftsperson's fire. You put your drive into doing things well: improving, fixing, organising and serving. You are often hard-working, efficient and practical, with stamina for long, detailed tasks that would bore others. Your energy is precise rather than explosive, and you prefer a plan to a charge.\n\nThe gift is skill and service: you can get things done properly, solve practical problems and keep everyone healthy and organised. You often take good care of the body through routine, diet and exercise. The challenge is that anger can turn into criticism, of yourself or others, and frustration can show as nagging or worry. Perfectionism can stop you from acting at all.\n\nIn relationships you show desire and love through helpfulness, and you appreciate a partner who is reliable. At work you suit medicine, engineering, craft, research, editing, nutrition, animal care and anything where accuracy counts. Mercury rules Virgo, so its sign and house shape how you work.",magic:"Careful, skilled magic suits your Mars: herbal remedies made with precision, cleansing and purification, health spells (beside proper care), and protection for the workplace. Tuesdays and Wednesdays, and the harvest months, suit you. Amazonite, Carnelian, rosemary and fennel steady and focus; a working for self-acceptance helps cool the inner critic.",shadow:"Criticism as anger, perfectionism, and wearing yourself out serving others."},Libra:{simple:"With Mars in Libra you act through partnership and diplomacy. You fight for fairness, prefer to negotiate rather than force, and do your best work with others.",detailed:"Mars is in detriment in Libra, opposite its home in Aries, which traditionally means Mars's direct action is softened by Venus's wish for harmony. In life you may find it hard to assert yourself plainly, or feel guilty for wanting things for yourself. Yet you can be a formidable fighter on behalf of others and for justice: you know how to argue a case, win allies and change things through persuasion.\n\nThe gift is diplomacy in action: you can resolve conflict, bring people together for a common goal and fight fair. Your desire is often refined and romantic. The challenge is indecision and indirect anger. You may suppress irritation to keep the peace and then find it leaking out in other ways, or wait for someone else to make the first move.\n\nIn relationships you are charming and attentive, and partnership is where you act most boldly. At work you suit law, mediation, design, the arts, partnership businesses and advocacy. Venus rules Libra, so Venus's sign shows what you are really fighting for.",magic:"Your Mars magic seeks justice and balance: spells for a fair outcome in a dispute, petitions to calm conflict, partnership workings for a shared goal, and courage spells for saying what you need. Tuesdays and Fridays, and the Moon in Libra, suit you. Lapis Lazuli, Bloodstone, Vervain and basil help courage and fairness walk together; Maat, the Egyptian order of truth and justice, offers a model of balance that is also strength.",shadow:"Passive aggression, indecision, and losing yourself to keep the peace."},Scorpio:{simple:"With Mars in Scorpio, its traditional home, you act with intensity, focus and strategy. Your will is deep and strong, and you do not give up.",detailed:"Mars is at home in Scorpio, its night house, and here it works like still, deep water with a strong current underneath. You are strategic, patient and powerful, able to concentrate your will on a single goal and pursue it with complete focus. Desire is intense, loyalties are total, and you rarely show your hand before you are ready.\n\nThe gift is resilience: you can survive crisis, rebuild after loss and transform yourself under pressure. You are hard to defeat because you do not stop. Traditional astrologers read Mars in its own sign as strong and effective. The challenge is control and revenge. Anger may be held long and released in calculated ways, and jealousy or suspicion can poison relationships.\n\nIn relationships you are deeply passionate and loyal, and you want total commitment in return. At work you suit research, investigation, surgery, finance, crisis work, therapy and anything that needs nerve and depth. Pluto is the modern co-ruler of Scorpio, and its place adds to this story.",magic:"Yours is deep, powerful magic: banishing, hex-breaking, protection, shadow work and transformation rites, best done at the dark or waning Moon. Tuesdays and Mars hours suit you. Obsidian, Garnet, Black Tourmaline and Dragon\u2019s Blood strengthen and shield; The Morrigan and Hekate are old powers people with this placement often find themselves drawn toward.",shadow:"Revenge, jealousy, and control kept out of sight."},Sagittarius:{simple:"With Mars in Sagittarius you act with enthusiasm, optimism and a love of freedom. You fight for your beliefs and are always ready for the next adventure.",detailed:"Mars in Sagittarius is a crusader's fire. You act on principle and enthusiasm, and you love a quest: travel, exploration, sport, learning, a cause to champion. Your energy is restless and expansive, and you thrive with freedom of movement. You are frank, sometimes to a fault, and you defend what you believe in with conviction.\n\nThe gift is optimism and courage of conviction: you can inspire others, take big risks and recover quickly from setbacks. The challenge is follow-through and tact. Energy can scatter once the adventure becomes routine, and your honesty can become preachiness or carelessness with other people's feelings. You may overcommit and overreach.\n\nIn relationships you want a partner who shares your love of adventure and gives you space. At work you suit teaching, travel, outdoor work, sport, publishing, law, activism and anything with a mission. Jupiter rules Sagittarius, so Jupiter's place shows where your fire finds its meaning.",magic:"Your Mars magic is outward-bound: travel protection, spells for luck in a venture, courage for a big leap, and fire rituals at the solstices. Thursdays and Tuesdays, and the Moon in Sagittarius, suit you. Turquoise, Lapis Lazuli, Carnelian and Juniper bring luck and protection on the road; Artemis the archer is a fitting patron for aim and freedom.",shadow:"Recklessness, preachiness, and starting crusades you do not finish."},Capricorn:{simple:"With Mars in Capricorn, where it is exalted, you act with discipline, ambition and great control. You work hard, plan well and achieve your goals over time.",detailed:"Mars is exalted in Capricorn, which traditional astrologers read as Mars at its most honoured and effective: heat tempered by discipline. You direct your energy with purpose and patience, choosing your battles and playing the long game. You are often ambitious, hard-working and capable of great feats of endurance. Anger is controlled, and you prefer cool strategy to hot words.\n\nThe gift is achievement: you can climb any mountain you set your mind to, step by step, and you earn respect through competence. You make a good leader and a reliable ally. The challenge is that work can swallow everything, and control can harden into rigidity or ruthlessness. You may find it hard to rest or to act from feeling.\n\nIn relationships you are loyal, steady and responsible, often with a strong, earthy sensuality behind a reserved surface. At work you suit management, business, engineering, the military, government and any long-term ambition. Saturn rules Capricorn, so Saturn's place shows what your effort is building.",magic:"Structured, long-term magic suits your Mars: career spells worked over a season, boundary and protection charms, banishing obstacles at the waning Moon, and a ritual for each milestone reached. Saturdays and Tuesdays suit you. Onyx, Garnet, Hematite and cypress strengthen discipline and endurance.",shadow:"Workaholism, coldness, and ambition that forgets people."},Aquarius:{simple:"With Mars in Aquarius you act independently and for the greater good. You fight for causes, ideas and freedom, and you do things your own way.",detailed:"Mars in Aquarius acts on principle and from a little distance. You are drawn to causes, reforms and new ideas, and you put your energy into what you believe will make things better for everyone. You often work well in groups and networks, but on your own terms. Your drive can be inventive, rebellious and unpredictable.\n\nThe gift is courage for change: you can stand alone for an idea, challenge outdated systems and organise others for a cause. You think strategically about the future. The challenge is detachment and stubbornness. Anger may be cool and intellectual rather than heated, and you can be contrary or rigid in defence of your ideals, missing the human cost in the moment.\n\nIn relationships you need freedom, friendship and a partner who respects your independence. At work you suit technology, science, activism, community organising, invention and any role that reforms or innovates. Saturn and Uranus, the traditional and modern rulers of Aquarius, both colour how you act.",magic:"Your Mars magic is collective and inventive: spells for a cause, group workings, sigils for social change, and protection for activists and communities. Saturdays and Tuesdays, and the Moon in Aquarius, suit you. Amethyst, Labradorite, Hematite and lavender help focus revolutionary energy without burning out.",shadow:"Contrariness, cold anger, and loving humanity more easily than people."},Pisces:{simple:"With Mars in Pisces you act from intuition, compassion and imagination. Your drive is gentle but strong, and you fight best for the vulnerable and the dream.",detailed:"Mars in Pisces moves like water: finding its way around obstacles rather than through them. You act from feeling and intuition, and your energy rises and falls with your mood and environment. You are often drawn to creative, spiritual or caring work, and you can be a tireless defender of the weak, the sick and the forgotten.\n\nThe gift is compassionate action and creative drive: you can channel strong energy into art, music, dance, healing or service. You are adaptable and often have a strong, subtle sensuality. The challenge is directness. It can be hard to assert yourself, say no or express anger openly, and you may avoid conflict until it overwhelms you. Energy can drain away into other people's problems.\n\nIn relationships you are romantic, sensitive and giving, and you need a partner who respects your gentleness. At work you suit the arts, healing, care, ministry, film, music and anything with heart. Jupiter rules Pisces traditionally and Neptune in modern astrology; both show where your drive dissolves into something larger.",magic:"Your Mars magic flows: protection through glamour and veiling, water rituals for cleansing, dance or music as power-raising, and dreamwork to find your true direction. Thursdays and Tuesdays, and the Moon in Pisces, suit you. Aquamarine, Amethyst, mugwort and willow are allies; a cleansing bath after helping others keeps your energy your own.",shadow:"Avoidance, martyrdom, and anger that leaks out sideways."}}},3074,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MERCURY_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n={Aries:{simple:"With Mercury in Aries you think fast and speak plainly. Your mind loves a challenge, a debate and a fresh idea, and it reaches its conclusions before others have found the question.",detailed:"Mercury in Aries thinks in sparks. Ideas arrive whole and urgent, and you tend to say them as soon as they arrive. You are quick to see what needs doing, direct in how you put it, and often the first in a room to name the obvious thing nobody wanted to say. Many people with this placement learn best by doing: trying, failing fast and trying again rather than reading the manual.\n\nThe gift is courage of mind. You will argue for an idea, defend someone who is being talked over, and cut through waffle. The challenge is patience: with detail, with slower thinkers, and with your own first draft. Words said in heat can land harder than you meant, and the habit of interrupting can hide how much you care about getting things right.\n\nIn relationships you want honest talk and a partner who can take a little friction without sulking. At work you thrive where speed and decisiveness count: pitching, troubleshooting, emergencies, anything that needs a first move. Mercury has no dignity in Aries, so it takes on Mars's colouring; where Mars sits in your chart says a lot about how your mind fights and what it fights for.",magic:"Your words work best spoken aloud and with heat: a short, bold petition read over a red candle, a sigil drawn in one stroke, a binding cut with a single word. Tuesdays and the hour of Mercury on a Mars day suit spells for courage in speaking up. Carnelian at the throat, basil in your pocket and a pinch of black pepper in a speaking charm help sharpen and steady the voice.",shadow:"Snapping, arguing to win rather than to understand, and deciding before you have listened."},Taurus:{simple:"With Mercury in Taurus you think slowly, solidly and well. Once you have understood something it stays understood, and you speak with a calm, practical good sense people trust.",detailed:"Mercury in Taurus takes its time. You like to turn an idea over, test it against what you already know, and see whether it holds weight before you commit to it. Learning is often physical: you remember what you have handled, cooked, built or walked through. Your speech tends to be measured and warm, sometimes with a lovely voice, and you rarely say more than you mean.\n\nThe gift is staying power. You finish what you start, you are not easily swayed by fashion or fuss, and your opinions are earned. The challenge is the other side of that steadiness: a mind that, once set, can be very hard to move, even by good new evidence. Change of plan can feel like a threat rather than an option.\n\nIn relationships you show care through reliability and practical help more than speeches, and you like conversations that go somewhere real. At work you suit money, design, craft, gardening, cooking, music, valuing and anything where patience and sense produce something solid. Venus rules Taurus, so your Venus colours how you think about worth, beauty and comfort.",magic:"Slow, cumulative word magic suits you: a prosperity petition repeated for seven nights over a green candle, a charm bag you add to week by week, a spell written in your best handwriting and kept under a stone. Fridays and earth-sign moons are good times. Green Aventurine, Moss Agate, thyme and patchouli are steadying allies for money and study alike.",shadow:"Stubbornness dressed as common sense, and a slowness to hear what you would rather not."},Gemini:{simple:"With Mercury in Gemini, its own sign, your mind is quick, curious and full of connections. You love to talk, read, learn and play with words and ideas.",detailed:"Mercury is at home in Gemini, and here it works with real ease. You take in information fast, see links others miss, and can hold several threads of thought at once. Conversation energises you, and you often think best out loud or on paper. Many people with this placement are witty, good at languages or mimicry, and gifted at explaining one world to another.\n\nThe gift is versatility: you can learn nearly anything well enough to get going, and you bring lightness and humour to heavy subjects. The challenge is depth and follow-through. A mind this nimble can skim, get bored once the novelty fades, or talk around a feeling instead of into it. Nervous energy can show as restlessness or trouble sleeping when the head will not switch off.\n\nIn relationships you need a partner you can talk to, endlessly, about everything. At work you suit writing, teaching, sales, media, translation, research, and any job with variety and people. Traditional astrologers counted Mercury in its own sign as strong and clear: well able to do what Mercury does, for good or for mischief.",magic:"Word and air magic is your native tongue: sigils, written petitions, letter spells, knot charms with a word in each knot, and divination of all kinds. Wednesdays and Mercury hours are yours, as is the waxing Moon in an air sign. Agate, Citrine, lavender and peppermint keep a busy mind clear; Hermes and Thoth are the old patrons of this kind of quick, crossing intelligence.",shadow:"Scattering, gossip, and cleverness used to avoid feeling."},Cancer:{simple:"With Mercury in Cancer you think with your feelings and remember everything. You speak gently, listen well and understand people by sensing the mood under their words.",detailed:"Mercury in Cancer is a mind steeped in memory and feeling. You absorb atmosphere, read faces and tones, and often know what someone means before they have found the words. Your memory for personal detail is remarkable: the story your grandmother told, the song that played that summer, what a friend said three years ago. Thinking tends to move in circles rather than straight lines, returning to the same question until it feels settled.\n\nThe gift is emotional intelligence and a talent for making people feel heard. You can be a wonderful storyteller, carer, counsellor or keeper of family history. The challenge is objectivity: your mind can take things personally, cling to old hurts, or reason from mood. When you feel unsafe you may go quiet, or speak indirectly and hope to be understood.\n\nIn relationships you remember what matters to people, and you need conversations that feel safe enough to be soft in. At work you suit caring roles, history, cooking, homemaking, writing memoir, teaching children and anything where knowing people well is the skill. The Moon rules Cancer, so your Moon's sign and phase colour how you think.",magic:"Your words are strongest at home and by moonlight: a family blessing written and kept in the kitchen, a letter to an ancestor laid on the altar, a dream journal by the bed. Mondays and the waxing to full Moon suit you. Moonstone, Selenite, Lemon Balm and jasmine soften and clarify. Moon water used to wet the ink of a petition is a lovely Cancerian touch.",shadow:"Moody thinking, holding grudges in the memory, and saying things sideways."},Leo:{simple:"With Mercury in Leo you think and speak with warmth, flair and conviction. You are a natural storyteller who likes ideas that matter and words that move people.",detailed:"Mercury in Leo puts the heart behind the voice. You speak with colour and confidence, you like your ideas to be big and generous, and you can hold a room when you tell a story. Many people with this placement have a strong creative mind and a gift for performance, teaching or persuasion. You think in wholes and themes more than fiddly details, and you care that what you say is true to who you are.\n\nThe gift is inspiration: you can make other people believe in an idea, and your loyalty in speech is fierce. The challenge is pride of mind. It can be hard to admit you were wrong, easy to take criticism of an idea as criticism of yourself, and tempting to overstate for effect. Listening as generously as you speak is the growth.\n\nIn relationships you are warm, encouraging and expressive, and you want your words to be appreciated. At work you suit teaching, acting, presenting, leading, writing, design and any role with an audience. The Sun rules Leo, so where your Sun sits shows what your mind most wants to shine on.",magic:"Spoken charms, performed with full voice and gesture, work best for you: a declaration of confidence in front of a mirror, a poem offered to a god, a creative project dedicated as devotion. Sundays and Sun hours, and the Moon in Leo, suit you. Sunstone, Citrine, Calendula and Sunflower bring courage to speak and be seen.",shadow:"Dominating the conversation, stubborn pride in your opinions, and exaggerating to impress."},Virgo:{simple:"With Mercury in Virgo, where it is both at home and exalted, your mind is precise, practical and skilled. You notice details, analyse well and love to make things work better.",detailed:"Mercury rules Virgo and is exalted here, which traditional astrologers read as one of its very strongest places. Your mind sorts, refines and improves. You see the flaw in the plan, the typo in the contract, the small change that would make everything run smoothly. Learning is methodical and you like to understand how things actually work, not just the theory.\n\nThe gift is usefulness of mind: you can turn knowledge into skill and skill into real help for people. You are often an excellent editor, craftsperson, analyst, herbalist or healer. The challenge is that the same critical eye can turn inward and become worry or perfectionism, so nothing you make ever feels good enough. Over-thinking health, plans or small mistakes can wear you down.\n\nIn relationships you show love through practical acts and careful attention, and you appreciate partners who are reliable and honest. At work you suit medicine, research, editing, accountancy, craft, data, animal care and any job where accuracy saves the day. Mercury here is your own ruler doubled in strength; its house shows where that skill is meant to serve.",magic:"Careful, ordered magic suits you: herbcraft, measured recipes, spell jars made step by step, cleansing and household ritual, and keeping a precise grimoire. Wednesdays and Mercury hours, and the harvest months, are your times. Amazonite, Fluorite, fennel and lavender keep the mind clear and kind; a healing working for yourself, not only others, is worth doing.",shadow:"Perfectionism, anxious over-analysis, and criticism that forgets to be kind."},Libra:{simple:"With Mercury in Libra you think in terms of fairness and balance. You are diplomatic, graceful with words and good at seeing every side of a question.",detailed:"Mercury in Libra weighs things. You naturally consider how an idea looks from the other person's side, and you like conversation to be civil, considered and fair. You often speak beautifully and know how to say a hard thing kindly. Thinking tends to happen in dialogue: you understand your own mind best by talking it over with someone else.\n\nThe gift is diplomacy and a fine sense of justice. You can mediate, negotiate and bring people together, and you have a good eye for proportion in design, writing and argument. The challenge is decision. Seeing every side can make choosing feel impossible, and the wish to keep the peace can lead you to soften what needs to be said plainly.\n\nIn relationships you want a partner who talks, listens and treats you as an equal. At work you suit law, mediation, design, diplomacy, counselling, the arts and anything that needs good judgement and good manners. Venus rules Libra, so Venus's sign and house show what kind of harmony your mind is looking for.",magic:"Your best words are sweetening and balancing: honey jar spells for a relationship, petitions for justice in a dispute, a written agreement with yourself laid between two candles. Fridays and Venus hours, and the Moon in Libra, suit you. Rose Quartz, Lapis Lazuli, rose and Vervain support fair speech; a pair of scales or two matched stones on the altar make a good focus.",shadow:"Indecision, people-pleasing in speech, and avoiding conflict until it grows."},Scorpio:{simple:"With Mercury in Scorpio your mind goes deep. You see beneath the surface, keep secrets, ask the questions others avoid and rarely forget what you learn.",detailed:"Mercury in Scorpio is a detective's mind. You look for motive, hidden cause and what is not being said, and you are hard to fool. Your thinking is intense and focused; once a subject has your attention you will research it to the bottom. You tend to say less than you know, and when you do speak, your words can be quietly devastating or deeply healing.\n\nThe gift is penetrating insight: you are drawn to psychology, mystery, research, the occult and any field where the truth is hidden. You can hold other people's secrets and sit with hard subjects without flinching. The challenge is suspicion and control. A mind trained to look for hidden motives can find them where none exist, and a sharp tongue used in self-defence can wound.\n\nIn relationships you want depth and honesty, not small talk, and trust is earned slowly. At work you suit research, investigation, therapy, medicine, finance, crisis work and esoteric study. Mars rules Scorpio traditionally and Pluto in modern astrology; both colour how your mind digs.",magic:"Yours is the magic of secrets and the unseen: scrying, tarot, shadow work journals, written banishings burned at the dark Moon, sealed spell jars kept hidden. Tuesdays and the waning Moon suit you. Obsidian, Labradorite, Wormwood and mugwort sharpen the inner eye; Hekate, keeper of keys and crossroads, has long been called on for this kind of seeing.",shadow:"Suspicion, secrecy that isolates, and cutting words kept for when you feel cornered."},Sagittarius:{simple:"With Mercury in Sagittarius you think big, speak frankly and love ideas that open the world up. You are curious about meaning, travel, faith and philosophy.",detailed:"Mercury is in detriment in Sagittarius, the sign opposite its home in Gemini. That does not mean a weak mind: it means Mercury's love of detail is pulled toward Sagittarius's love of the big picture. You think in principles, journeys and grand connections, and you are often a natural teacher, storyteller or seeker. Your honesty can be startling, and your enthusiasm for an idea is catching.\n\nThe gift is vision and a generous, open mind. You learn through exploring: travel, other cultures, religions, philosophies and long conversations late into the night. The challenge is the small print. Facts, schedules and fine distinctions can bore you, and a habit of blunt truth-telling or overpromising can get you into trouble. You may be certain before you are correct.\n\nIn relationships you want a companion for adventures of the mind and body, and you need room to roam. At work you suit teaching, publishing, law, travel, ministry, sport and anything with horizon in it. Jupiter rules Sagittarius, so where Jupiter sits shows where your mind finds meaning.",magic:"Your words want to travel: blessings for a journey, prayers and hymns from the traditions you study, divination by bibliomancy (opening a book at random) and petitions sent on the wind. Thursdays and Jupiter hours suit you. Turquoise, Lapis Lazuli, Sage and Star Anise go well with seeking and study; a candle lit before a long read or a pilgrimage walk makes the learning a rite.",shadow:"Preaching, carelessness with facts, and promises made in enthusiasm and not kept."},Capricorn:{simple:"With Mercury in Capricorn you think in a careful, structured and ambitious way. You plan ahead, speak with authority and want ideas to be useful and proven.",detailed:"Mercury in Capricorn is a mind built for strategy. You think in steps, structures and long timelines, and you like to know what an idea is for before you invest in it. You tend to be serious, dry and to the point, often with a sharp, understated wit. People trust your judgement because you have clearly thought things through and do not waste words.\n\nThe gift is practical wisdom and discipline: you can master difficult subjects slowly and thoroughly, and you are good at organising other people's chaos into a plan. The challenge is a mind that can turn pessimistic or rigid, dismissing ideas that seem impractical, and a habit of worrying quietly about what could go wrong. You may doubt your own intelligence long after others recognise it.\n\nIn relationships you are loyal and steady in conversation rather than gushing, and you value partners who keep their word. At work you suit management, law, engineering, finance, government, history and any field where expertise is built over years. Saturn rules Capricorn, so Saturn's place in your chart shows what your mind takes most seriously.",magic:"Your magic is patient and structured: long-term goal spells worked over a whole season, written contracts with yourself, boundary charms, and petitions to ancestors for guidance in work. Saturdays and Saturn hours suit you, as does the waning Moon for clearing obstacles. Onyx, Garnet, cypress and comfrey support steady study and long effort.",shadow:"Pessimism, rigidity, and dismissing feelings as impractical."},Aquarius:{simple:"With Mercury in Aquarius your mind is original, independent and future-minded. You love ideas, systems and causes, and you think for yourself.",detailed:"Mercury in Aquarius thinks from a little distance, which lets you see patterns and systems others are too close to notice. You are often inventive, interested in science, technology, social questions or the unusual, and comfortable holding opinions nobody else in the room shares. Your mind likes a principle to be consistent, and it will follow logic wherever it leads.\n\nThe gift is originality and clear, objective thought. You can reform a broken system, explain a complex idea simply and see where the future is heading. The challenge is detachment and fixed opinion. It is possible to be so sure of the logic that you miss the human feeling in the room, or to argue for the sake of being different. Aquarius is a fixed sign, and once your mind is made up it rarely moves.\n\nIn relationships you need a friend as well as a partner, someone you can talk ideas with as equals. At work you suit science, technology, research, activism, astrology, invention and community organising. Saturn rules Aquarius traditionally and Uranus in modern astrology; both colour how your mind builds and breaks systems.",magic:"Your magic likes systems and the new: sigils built from a method, planetary squares, astrological timing worked out to the minute, group workings and online circles, and spells for a cause larger than yourself. Saturdays and Wednesdays, and the Moon in Aquarius, suit you. Amethyst, Fluorite, Labradorite and lavender keep a quick, electric mind grounded.",shadow:"Coldness in argument, contrariness, and certainty that will not hear feeling."},Pisces:{simple:"With Mercury in Pisces you think in images, feelings and intuitions. Your mind is imaginative, poetic and sensitive, and often knows things without knowing how.",detailed:"Mercury is in both detriment and fall in Pisces, which traditional astrologers read as a mind that struggles with Mercury's usual tools of list, logic and fact. Many modern astrologers see the other side: a mind that works by intuition, music, image and symbol rather than straight lines. You absorb ideas the way water absorbs colour, and you often understand through empathy what others reach through argument.\n\nThe gift is imagination and compassion of mind. You can be a poet, musician, artist, healer, or someone who hears what is not said and answers it kindly. Dreams and hunches are real information for you. The challenge is clarity: details slip, deadlines dissolve, and it can be hard to say no or to say exactly what you mean. Confusion and self-doubt can creep in when the world demands hard edges.\n\nIn relationships you are tender, understanding and forgiving, and you need a partner who can hear the feeling in your words. At work you suit the arts, music, film, therapy, care, ministry and any field where intuition matters. Jupiter rules Pisces traditionally and Neptune in modern astrology; both shape how your mind dreams.",magic:"Yours is dream and water magic: dream journals and dream pillows, scrying in a dark bowl, automatic writing, poetry offered as prayer, and spells sung rather than spoken. Thursdays and Mondays, and the Moon in Pisces, suit you. Amethyst, Aquamarine, mugwort and jasmine open the inner ear; a cleansing bath before divination helps sort your feelings from everyone else's.",shadow:"Vagueness, saying yes when you mean no, and escaping hard facts."}}},3075,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"NEPTUNE_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n={Aries:{simple:"Neptune in Aries marks a generation whose dreams are of courage, new beginnings and spiritual warriorship. In you it can show as an idealistic, crusading spirit.",detailed:"Neptune was in Aries from about 1861 to 1875 and entered it again in 2025, staying until 2039. The children born now are dreaming new heroes and new beginnings into being; the older generation saw nations remade and the first great movements of individual rights. The gift is inspired courage and a spiritual fire; the risk is fanaticism, or illusions about the self as saviour.\n\nPersonally, this matters most when Neptune touches your Sun, Moon, Mars or Ascendant, or sits on an angle. Then it can show as a romantic, heroic idealism and a need to act on visions. Its house shows where you are called to brave, inspired action.",magic:"Visionary fire magic suits this placement: candle scrying, spells for inspired courage, and rituals that honour the spiritual warrior. Carnelian, Amethyst and mugwort hold both vision and drive.",shadow:"Fanaticism, and acting on illusions of your own heroism."},Taurus:{simple:"Neptune in Taurus marks a generation that dreamed of material plenty and earthly beauty. Nobody alive now has it; it last occurred from 1874 to 1889.",detailed:"Neptune was last in Taurus from about 1874 to 1889, and will return around 2038. That generation's dream was of the earth made generous: industrial abundance, the beauty of the land in art and the Arts and Crafts movement. The gift is a sense of the sacred in the material world; the risk is illusions about money, comfort and security.\n\nIf you see this placement, you are likely looking at a historical chart, or at a chart cast for the coming years. For a person born then, its house showed where the earth and the senses became a spiritual path.",magic:"Earth devotion suits this energy: blessing the land, offerings to the spirits of a garden, and sensual ritual with oils, flowers and food. Rose Quartz, Moss Agate and rose honour sacred earth.",shadow:"Illusions about wealth, and comfort mistaken for peace."},Gemini:{simple:"Neptune in Gemini marks a generation that dreamed through words and new communication. Nobody alive now has it; it last occurred from 1887 to 1902.",detailed:"Neptune was last in Gemini from about 1887 to 1902, when telephones, radio and the first cinema transformed how people imagined talking across distance. That generation produced many poets, spiritualists and inventors of new language. The gift is imaginative communication and inspired ideas; the risk is confusion, rumour and deception.\n\nIf you see this placement, you are likely looking at a historical or future chart (it returns around 2051). For a person born then, its house showed where the imagination spoke.",magic:"Word and dream magic suits this energy: automatic writing, poetry as prayer, and divination by words and signs. Celestite, Fluorite and lavender suit an inspired, wandering mind.",shadow:"Confusion, gossip, and saying what people want to hear."},Cancer:{simple:"Neptune in Cancer marks a generation that dreamed of home, homeland and family. In you it can show as idealism about belonging and a deep longing for roots.",detailed:"Neptune was in Cancer from about 1901 to 1916. That generation grew up amid strong ideals of nation, home and motherhood, and lived through the losses of the First World War. The gift is compassionate devotion to home and kin; the risk is sentimental nostalgia and idealising the past.\n\nFor a living person this is rare now, but when it appears in an elder's chart and touches personal planets or angles, it can show as deep sensitivity to family, psychic gifts around the home, and a longing for a lost or ideal belonging. Its house shows where that longing lives.",magic:"Ancestral and hearth magic suits this placement: ancestor altars, moon water, dreamwork about family, and home blessings. Moonstone, Selenite and jasmine honour home and memory.",shadow:"Nostalgia that will not let go, and idealising family."},Leo:{simple:"Neptune in Leo marks a generation that dreamed through glamour, cinema and romance. In you it can show as creative imagination and idealism about love.",detailed:"Neptune was in Leo from about 1914 to 1929: the age of silent film, jazz, glamour and the dream of the star. That generation idealised romance and creativity. The gift is creative inspiration and a sense of the magical in play; the risk is illusion, ego and glamour hiding emptiness.\n\nFor those who have it, when Neptune touches personal planets or angles, it can show as an artistic or theatrical gift, romantic ideals and a love of the dramatic. Its house shows where you dream of being seen.",magic:"Glamour and creative magic suit this energy: performance as ritual, art as devotion, and spells for inspiration. Sunstone, Amethyst and Sunflower honour radiant imagination.",shadow:"Self-deception, and glamour that hides the real self."},Virgo:{simple:"Neptune in Virgo marks a generation that dreamed of service, health and a better-ordered world. In you it can show as compassionate, practical idealism.",detailed:"Neptune was in Virgo from about 1928 to 1943, through the Depression and into the Second World War. That generation idealised hard work, duty and service, and lived through great hardship and sacrifice. The gift is compassionate service and healing gifts; the risk is martyrdom, worry and confusion about health.\n\nFor those who have it, when Neptune touches personal planets or angles, it can show as intuitive healing gifts, devotion to work, and sensitivity in the body. Its house shows where you serve with your whole heart.",magic:"Healing and herbal magic suit this placement: herbal remedies made as prayer, healing rituals beside proper care, and service as devotion. Amethyst, Amazonite and Chamomile support gentle, intuitive healing.",shadow:"Martyrdom, and worry that blurs into illness."},Libra:{simple:"Neptune in Libra marks a generation that dreamed of peace, love and harmony. In you it can show as romantic and artistic ideals.",detailed:"Neptune was in Libra from about 1942 to 1957. That generation grew up after war and later carried the dream of peace and love into the 1960s. The gift is idealism about relationship and justice, and a strong sense of beauty; the risk is disillusionment in love and an idealised picture of partnership.\n\nFor those who have it, when Neptune touches personal planets or angles, it can show as romantic idealism, artistic talent and a yearning for a perfect partnership. Its house shows where you seek harmony.",magic:"Love and peace magic suits this energy: rituals for harmony, art as devotion, and spells for a fair world. Rose Quartz, Lapis Lazuli and rose honour gentle ideals.",shadow:"Romantic illusion, and avoiding conflict until it is too late."},Scorpio:{simple:"Neptune in Scorpio marks a generation drawn to the mysteries of sex, death and the psyche. In you it can show as psychic depth and a hunger for transformation.",detailed:"Neptune was in Scorpio from about 1955 to 1970. This generation grew up through the sexual revolution and a revival of interest in the occult, psychology and altered states. The gift is psychic sensitivity and fearlessness about the depths; the risk is addiction, obsession and confusion about power.\n\nPersonally, when Neptune touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as strong intuition, an attraction to the mysterious, and emotional intensity. Its house shows where you seek the hidden truth.",magic:"Deep, occult magic suits this placement: scrying, shadow work, trance, and transformation rituals. Obsidian, Labradorite and mugwort open the inner eye; Hekate is an old guide for these roads.",shadow:"Obsession, escape into intensity, and confusion about power."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Neptune in Sagittarius marks a generation that dreamed of spiritual freedom and global faith. In you it can show as a seeker's spirit.",detailed:"Neptune was in Sagittarius from about 1970 to 1984. This generation grew up as Eastern spirituality, travel and new religious movements spread widely in the West. The gift is spiritual openness and a search for universal truth; the risk is following false gurus or endless seeking.\n\nPersonally, when Neptune touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as idealism about faith, travel and learning, and a gift for inspiring others. Its house shows where you seek meaning.",magic:"Eclectic, devotional magic suits this energy: pilgrimage, prayer from many traditions honoured with respect, and divination for guidance. Turquoise, Amethyst and Sage support honest seeking.",shadow:"Spiritual escapism, and faith in the wrong teachers."},Capricorn:{simple:"Neptune in Capricorn marks a generation that dissolves and reimagines institutions. In you it can show as idealism about work and structure.",detailed:"Neptune was in Capricorn from about 1984 to 1998, alongside Uranus for much of it. This generation was born as the Cold War ended and institutions began to look less solid than they seemed. The gift is practical idealism: making dreams real through structure; the risk is disillusionment with authority, or idealising success.\n\nPersonally, when Neptune touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as dreams of a meaningful career, sensitivity to authority, and a gift for giving vision a form. Its house shows where you build your dreams.",magic:"Grounded spiritual magic suits this placement: rituals to give shape to dreams, ancestor work, and spells for meaningful success. Onyx, Amethyst and cypress hold vision steady.",shadow:"Disillusionment, and idealising status."},Aquarius:{simple:"Neptune in Aquarius marks a generation that dreams of global connection and humanitarian ideals. In you it can show as idealism about community.",detailed:"Neptune was in Aquarius from about 1998 to 2012. This generation grew up as online communities and global networks became part of daily life. The gift is idealism about humanity, technology and collective vision; the risk is losing oneself in the virtual, or confused loyalties to groups.\n\nPersonally, when Neptune touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as visionary ideas, sensitivity to the collective mood, and a longing for true community. Its house shows where you dream of a better world.",magic:"Communal and visionary magic suits this energy: group meditation, online circles, and spells for a cause. Amethyst, Aquamarine and lavender suit this dreaming, connected spirit.",shadow:"Escape into the virtual, and confused group loyalties."},Pisces:{simple:"Neptune in Pisces, its modern home, marks a generation of deep empathy, imagination and spiritual sensitivity. In you it can show as strong intuition and compassion.",detailed:"Neptune was in Pisces from about 2011 to 2026, the sign modern astrologers give it to rule. This generation is growing up immersed in images, music and virtual worlds, and with a growing awareness of mental health and the suffering of others. The gift is profound empathy and artistic imagination; the risk is overwhelm, confusion and escapism.\n\nPersonally, when Neptune touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as psychic sensitivity, artistic gifts and a need for spiritual practice. Its house shows where you dissolve into something larger.",magic:"Water and dream magic suits this placement: ritual baths, dream pillows, scrying in water, and devotions to the sea. Amethyst, Aquamarine and jasmine honour the dreaming; Neptune and Poseidon, lords of the sea, are its old patrons.",shadow:"Overwhelm, escapism, and losing the line between self and others."}}},3076,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"NORTH_NODE_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SOUTH_NODE_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const o={Aries:{simple:"With the North Node in Aries you grow by learning to stand on your own feet, choose for yourself and act with courage. Your comfort zone is keeping the peace for others.",detailed:"The North Node in Aries always pairs with the South Node in Libra. What comes easily to you is partnership, diplomacy, seeing the other side and adjusting yourself to keep things pleasant. Those are real gifts, but leaning on them can mean waiting for permission, deferring every decision, or losing track of what you want.\n\nThe growth direction is Aries: independence, initiative, healthy selfishness, honest anger, doing the brave thing first and asking afterwards. It can feel uncomfortable, even rude, at first. Over time it brings a clearer, stronger self who can then partner from a place of choice rather than need.\n\nIn medieval astrology the North Node was said to increase whatever it touches, and in Jyotish it is Rahu, a hungry, worldly force; both point to Aries matters growing in your life. Its house shows the area where this courage is most needed.",magic:"Courage and self-trust magic supports your path: a candle lit before each decision you make for yourself, a self-dedication rite, a crossroads working to choose your own road. Tuesdays and the new Moon, especially in Aries, suit you. Carnelian, Bloodstone and basil help.",shadow:"Swinging from people-pleasing to self-centredness without finding the middle."},Taurus:{simple:"With the North Node in Taurus you grow by building steady, simple security and trusting your own values. Your comfort zone is crisis, intensity and other people's resources.",detailed:"The North Node in Taurus pairs with the South Node in Scorpio. What comes easily is depth, intensity, crisis management and merging with others' power or money. You may be drawn again and again to drama or transformation, even when calm would serve you better.\n\nThe growth direction is Taurus: patience, simplicity, earning your own way, enjoying the body and the senses, and building something slow and solid. Peace can feel boring at first. With time it becomes the ground you stand on.\n\nIts house shows where this steadiness is most needed. Venus, ruler of Taurus, is a good guide: its sign and house show what kind of security truly feeds you.",magic:"Slow, earthy magic supports your path: a prosperity jar fed weekly, gardening as devotion, and grounding rituals with your hands in soil. Fridays and the new Moon in Taurus suit you. Green Aventurine, Moss Agate and thyme are steadying allies.",shadow:"Clinging to crisis because calm feels unfamiliar."},Gemini:{simple:"With the North Node in Gemini you grow by asking questions, listening and staying curious. Your comfort zone is already being sure you know the answer.",detailed:"The North Node in Gemini pairs with the South Node in Sagittarius. What comes easily is the big picture, strong beliefs, preaching and wandering off in search of meaning. You may be used to being the one with the answers.\n\nThe growth direction is Gemini: curiosity, local connection, listening, gathering facts, learning from neighbours and siblings, and holding opinions lightly. Over time this makes your wisdom grounded and your teaching real.\n\nIts house shows where curiosity is most needed. Mercury, ruler of Gemini, shows how your mind learns best.",magic:"Word and study magic supports your path: journaling, daily divination, letter spells, and blessing your local roads and neighbourhood. Wednesdays and the new Moon in Gemini suit you. Citrine, Fluorite and peppermint keep curiosity lively.",shadow:"Certainty that stops you listening."},Cancer:{simple:"With the North Node in Cancer you grow by letting yourself feel, nurture and belong. Your comfort zone is work, status and staying in control.",detailed:"The North Node in Cancer pairs with the South Node in Capricorn. What comes easily is responsibility, ambition, discipline and holding it together. You may be very good at achieving and very unpractised at resting or needing.\n\nThe growth direction is Cancer: emotion, home, family, vulnerability and care, given and received. It can feel like weakness at first, and it turns out to be the thing that makes your achievements worth having.\n\nIts house shows where this tenderness is most needed. The Moon, ruler of Cancer, shows how you are best cared for.",magic:"Hearth and moon magic supports your path: home blessings, ancestor offerings, moon water, and kitchen spells for those you love. Mondays and the full Moon suit you. Moonstone, Rose Quartz and Lemon Balm soften and comfort.",shadow:"Hiding behind work to avoid feeling."},Leo:{simple:"With the North Node in Leo you grow by shining, creating and following your heart. Your comfort zone is blending into the group.",detailed:"The North Node in Leo pairs with the South Node in Aquarius. What comes easily is detachment, group work, ideas and being one of many. You may be comfortable in the background, serving a cause or a crowd.\n\nThe growth direction is Leo: personal creativity, joy, romance, play and the courage to be seen as an individual. Standing out can feel exposing at first; over time it becomes your gift to the group.\n\nIts house shows where you are called to shine. The Sun, ruler of Leo, shows the heart you are growing into.",magic:"Solar and creative magic supports your path: art as devotion, confidence spells, and joyful celebration rituals. Sundays and the new Moon in Leo suit you. Sunstone, Citrine and Sunflower bring warmth and courage.",shadow:"Hiding in the crowd to avoid the risk of being seen."},Virgo:{simple:"With the North Node in Virgo you grow by bringing your gifts down to earth through practical work and service. Your comfort zone is dreaming and drifting.",detailed:"The North Node in Virgo pairs with the South Node in Pisces. What comes easily is intuition, compassion, imagination and escape. You may be used to going with the flow, rescuing others or retreating into dreams.\n\nThe growth direction is Virgo: discernment, routines, health, skill, boundaries and real, useful service. Order can feel limiting at first; it turns out to be the vessel your gifts needed.\n\nIts house shows where this practicality is most needed. Mercury, ruler of Virgo, shows how you are best organised.",magic:"Practical, ordered magic supports your path: herbcraft, cleansing rituals, a daily devotional routine and a carefully kept grimoire. Wednesdays and the new Moon in Virgo suit you. Amazonite, Fluorite and fennel focus and steady.",shadow:"Drifting, and helping in ways that drain you."},Libra:{simple:"With the North Node in Libra you grow by learning partnership, cooperation and fairness. Your comfort zone is doing everything alone.",detailed:"The North Node in Libra pairs with the South Node in Aries. What comes easily is independence, quick action, self-reliance and looking after yourself. You may be used to fighting your own battles and finding it hard to ask for help.\n\nThe growth direction is Libra: partnership, listening, compromise, beauty and diplomacy. Considering others can feel like losing yourself at first; it becomes a deeper kind of strength.\n\nIts house shows where cooperation is most needed. Venus, ruler of Libra, shows how you relate best.",magic:"Relationship and balance magic supports your path: sweetening spells, partnership blessings and rituals for harmony. Fridays and the new Moon in Libra suit you. Rose Quartz, Lapis Lazuli and rose support the work.",shadow:"Going it alone out of habit, not choice."},Scorpio:{simple:"With the North Node in Scorpio you grow by letting go, sharing deeply and embracing change. Your comfort zone is security and things staying the same.",detailed:"The North Node in Scorpio pairs with the South Node in Taurus. What comes easily is stability, comfort, self-reliance and holding on. You may be used to building security and resisting change.\n\nThe growth direction is Scorpio: intimacy, shared resources, transformation, depth and letting go of what is finished. Change can feel like loss at first; it turns out to be rebirth.\n\nIts house shows where transformation is most needed. Mars and Pluto, the rulers of Scorpio, show how you meet change.",magic:"Transformation magic supports your path: shadow work, release rituals at the waning Moon, and divination. Tuesdays and the dark Moon suit you. Obsidian, Labradorite and Wormwood help.",shadow:"Holding on to comfort when it is time to change."},Sagittarius:{simple:"With the North Node in Sagittarius you grow by seeking meaning, trusting your intuition and exploring wide horizons. Your comfort zone is endless information and chatter.",detailed:"The North Node in Sagittarius pairs with the South Node in Gemini. What comes easily is collecting facts, talking, adapting and staying busy. You may be used to knowing a little about everything.\n\nThe growth direction is Sagittarius: faith, philosophy, travel, higher learning and trusting the big picture. Committing to a belief can feel risky at first; it gives your life direction.\n\nIts house shows where meaning is most needed. Jupiter, ruler of Sagittarius, shows how you grow.",magic:"Seeking and devotional magic supports your path: pilgrimage, travel blessings, and study as devotion. Thursdays and the new Moon in Sagittarius suit you. Turquoise, Lapis Lazuli and Sage support the search.",shadow:"Busyness that keeps meaning out of reach."},Capricorn:{simple:"With the North Node in Capricorn you grow by taking responsibility, building structure and pursuing goals. Your comfort zone is the safety of home and feeling.",detailed:"The North Node in Capricorn pairs with the South Node in Cancer. What comes easily is nurturing, emotional sensitivity and retreating to the safety of home and family. You may be used to being looked after or looking after others.\n\nThe growth direction is Capricorn: ambition, discipline, public responsibility and standing on your own authority. Stepping into the world can feel cold at first; it becomes your own solid ground.\n\nIts house shows where responsibility is most needed. Saturn, ruler of Capricorn, shows how you build.",magic:"Structured, long-term magic supports your path: career spells, ancestor rites for guidance, and boundary charms. Saturdays and the new Moon in Capricorn suit you. Onyx, Garnet and cypress steady the climb.",shadow:"Retreating into the familiar when the world calls."},Aquarius:{simple:"With the North Node in Aquarius you grow by joining with others for a shared vision. Your comfort zone is being the star of your own story.",detailed:"The North Node in Aquarius pairs with the South Node in Leo. What comes easily is self-expression, creativity, drama and needing to be seen. You may be used to being the centre.\n\nThe growth direction is Aquarius: friendship, community, ideals and working for something bigger than yourself. Sharing the stage can feel like losing yourself at first; it turns out to be belonging.\n\nIts house shows where community is most needed. Saturn and Uranus, the rulers of Aquarius, show how you connect.",magic:"Communal magic supports your path: group rituals, coven work, and spells for a cause. Saturdays and the new Moon in Aquarius suit you. Amethyst, Aquamarine and lavender help.",shadow:"Needing the spotlight when the group needs you."},Pisces:{simple:"With the North Node in Pisces you grow by trusting, surrendering and opening to spirit. Your comfort zone is control, analysis and keeping busy.",detailed:"The North Node in Pisces pairs with the South Node in Virgo. What comes easily is order, analysis, service and criticism. You may be used to fixing, worrying and staying in control.\n\nThe growth direction is Pisces: faith, compassion, imagination, rest and surrender to something greater. Letting go can feel frightening at first; it becomes peace.\n\nIts house shows where surrender is most needed. Jupiter and Neptune, the rulers of Pisces, show how you open to spirit.",magic:"Dream and devotional magic supports your path: meditation, dreamwork, prayer and water rituals. Thursdays and the new Moon in Pisces suit you. Amethyst, Aquamarine and mugwort help.",shadow:"Worry and over-control in place of trust."}},t={Aries:{simple:"With the South Node in Aries, independence and quick action come easily to you, perhaps too easily. The North Node in Libra asks you to grow into partnership.",detailed:"The South Node shows a familiar groove: talents you arrive with, and habits that can hold you back if you lean on them alone. In Aries that groove is self-reliance, courage and acting first. You can look after yourself, fight your own battles and start things on your own.\n\nThe risk is staying there: impatience, going it alone, and not letting others in. Many astrologers read the South Node as what you are here to share and slowly release, not to discard. Your courage is a gift; the North Node in Libra asks you to offer it within partnership.",magic:"Release and gratitude magic suits the South Node: thank the old strength at the waning Moon, then turn toward the new. Bloodstone and rose together honour courage and partnership.",shadow:"Fighting alone out of habit."},Taurus:{simple:"With the South Node in Taurus, security and steadiness come easily to you. The North Node in Scorpio asks you to grow into change and intimacy.",detailed:"With the South Node in Taurus the familiar groove is comfort, stability, self-sufficiency and holding on. You know how to build security and enjoy simple pleasures, and those are real gifts.\n\nThe risk is resisting change, accumulating for safety, and staying in what is comfortable after it has stopped feeding you. The North Node in Scorpio asks you to share, merge and let go, so that what you have built can be transformed.",magic:"Release magic suits this node: give away what you no longer need at the waning Moon, with thanks. Smoky Quartz and Obsidian together honour holding and letting go.",shadow:"Holding on past the time."},Gemini:{simple:"With the South Node in Gemini, quick thinking and talking come easily to you. The North Node in Sagittarius asks you to grow into faith and meaning.",detailed:"With the South Node in Gemini the familiar groove is information, communication, adaptability and staying busy. You can learn fast and connect easily.\n\nThe risk is scattering, collecting facts without wisdom, and talking around the big questions. The North Node in Sagittarius asks you to choose a direction, trust intuition and seek meaning.",magic:"Clearing magic suits this node: a waning Moon ritual to let go of mental clutter, followed by quiet contemplation. Fluorite and Sage help.",shadow:"Busyness that avoids depth."},Cancer:{simple:"With the South Node in Cancer, nurturing and emotional sensitivity come easily to you. The North Node in Capricorn asks you to grow into responsibility in the world.",detailed:"With the South Node in Cancer the familiar groove is family, home, feeling and care. You know how to nurture and how to retreat into safety.\n\nThe risk is staying in the shell, depending on family, or avoiding the wider world. The North Node in Capricorn asks you to step into your own authority and build something lasting outside the home.",magic:"Ancestral thanksgiving suits this node: honour your family's gifts at the ancestor altar, then ask for their blessing on your own road. Moonstone and Onyx together hold both.",shadow:"Retreating into the familiar nest."},Leo:{simple:"With the South Node in Leo, self-expression and confidence come easily to you. The North Node in Aquarius asks you to grow into community.",detailed:"With the South Node in Leo the familiar groove is creativity, warmth, leadership and being seen. You know how to shine.\n\nThe risk is needing the spotlight, pride and making everything personal. The North Node in Aquarius asks you to use your light for the group and to find belonging as one among many.",magic:"Gratitude and sharing magic suits this node: a creative offering made for your community. Sunstone and Amethyst together balance heart and vision.",shadow:"Needing to be the centre."},Virgo:{simple:"With the South Node in Virgo, order, analysis and service come easily to you. The North Node in Pisces asks you to grow into trust and surrender.",detailed:"With the South Node in Virgo the familiar groove is skill, detail, health routines and being useful. You know how to fix things and help.\n\nThe risk is worry, perfectionism and criticism. The North Node in Pisces asks you to let go, trust life and open to spirit.",magic:"Release magic suits this node: let go of a list of worries at the waning Moon, then meditate. Amazonite and Amethyst together help.",shadow:"Worry in place of faith."},Libra:{simple:"With the South Node in Libra, partnership and diplomacy come easily to you. The North Node in Aries asks you to grow into independence.",detailed:"With the South Node in Libra the familiar groove is harmony, partnership, charm and considering others. You know how to keep the peace.\n\nThe risk is losing yourself in others, indecision and people-pleasing. The North Node in Aries asks you to know your own mind and act on it.",magic:"Balancing magic suits this node: thank your gift for harmony, then light a red candle for your own will. Rose Quartz and Carnelian together help.",shadow:"People-pleasing at your own cost."},Scorpio:{simple:"With the South Node in Scorpio, depth, intensity and crisis come easily to you. The North Node in Taurus asks you to grow into peace and simplicity.",detailed:"With the South Node in Scorpio the familiar groove is intensity, crisis, intimacy and transformation. You know how to survive and go deep.\n\nThe risk is drama, control and being drawn to crisis. The North Node in Taurus asks you to build calm, simple security and to enjoy life.",magic:"Grounding magic suits this node: after shadow work, always ground with earth: soil, bread, a long walk. Obsidian and Green Aventurine together help.",shadow:"Seeking intensity when peace would heal."},Sagittarius:{simple:"With the South Node in Sagittarius, faith, adventure and big ideas come easily to you. The North Node in Gemini asks you to grow into curiosity and listening.",detailed:"With the South Node in Sagittarius the familiar groove is belief, philosophy, travel and freedom. You know how to inspire.\n\nThe risk is preaching, restlessness and certainty. The North Node in Gemini asks you to listen, ask questions and stay curious about the people near you.",magic:"Humility magic suits this node: honour your teachers, then learn something new from someone near you. Turquoise and Citrine together help.",shadow:"Certainty that does not listen."},Capricorn:{simple:"With the South Node in Capricorn, ambition and responsibility come easily to you. The North Node in Cancer asks you to grow into tenderness.",detailed:"With the South Node in Capricorn the familiar groove is achievement, discipline, control and duty. You know how to work and lead.\n\nThe risk is coldness, overwork and hiding feeling behind responsibility. The North Node in Cancer asks you to come home to your heart and let yourself be cared for.",magic:"Hearth magic suits this node: a home blessing and a nourishing meal made as ritual. Onyx and Moonstone together help.",shadow:"Work as a shield against feeling."},Aquarius:{simple:"With the South Node in Aquarius, detachment, ideas and group work come easily to you. The North Node in Leo asks you to grow into personal expression.",detailed:"With the South Node in Aquarius the familiar groove is objectivity, friendship and the collective. You know how to be part of a group.\n\nThe risk is hiding in the crowd and detaching from personal feeling. The North Node in Leo asks you to create, love and shine as yourself.",magic:"Creative magic suits this node: make something just for joy, and offer it. Amethyst and Sunstone together help.",shadow:"Detachment from your own heart."},Pisces:{simple:"With the South Node in Pisces, intuition and compassion come easily to you. The North Node in Virgo asks you to grow into practical service.",detailed:"With the South Node in Pisces the familiar groove is spirituality, imagination, empathy and escape. You know how to dream and feel.\n\nThe risk is drifting, confusion and losing yourself in others. The North Node in Virgo asks you to ground your gifts in daily practice and useful work.",magic:"Grounding magic suits this node: after dreamwork, write it down and act on one small thing. Amethyst and Amazonite together help.",shadow:"Drifting instead of doing."}}},3077,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PLUTO_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o={Aries:{simple:"Pluto in Aries marks a generation that transforms the world through raw will and new beginnings. Nobody alive has it; it last occurred from about 1822 to 1853.",detailed:"Pluto was last in Aries from about 1822 to 1853, a time of revolutions, nationalism and the rise of the individual will. It will return around 2068. The gift of the placement is the courage to begin again from nothing; its risk is violence and conquest.\n\nIf you see it, you are looking at a historical chart or one cast far into the future. For a person born then, its house showed where they were called to fight for renewal.",magic:"Fire and rebirth magic suits this energy: burning what is finished, courage rites, and the phoenix as an image. Bloodstone, Obsidian and nettle honour fierce renewal.",shadow:"Destruction for its own sake, and power taken by force."},Taurus:{simple:"Pluto in Taurus marks a generation that transforms wealth, land and resources. Nobody alive has it; it last occurred from about 1851 to 1884.",detailed:"Pluto was last in Taurus from about 1851 to 1884, the height of the industrial age, when land, money and the means of production were transformed and fought over. The gift is deep resourcefulness and endurance; the risk is greed and exploitation of the earth.\n\nIf you see it, you are looking at a historical chart. For a person born then, its house showed where they met the power of money and land.",magic:"Earth and prosperity magic with respect for the land suits this energy: offerings to land spirits and rituals for honest wealth. Smoky Quartz, Moss Agate and patchouli honour deep earth.",shadow:"Greed, and holding on to power through ownership."},Gemini:{simple:"Pluto in Gemini marks a generation that transforms communication and ideas. Very few, if any, alive now have it; it occurred from about 1882 to 1914.",detailed:"Pluto was in Gemini from about 1882 to 1914, as telephones, cars, radio and mass newspapers transformed how ideas spread. The gift is powerful, penetrating thought and the drive to transform through information; the risk is propaganda and the misuse of words.\n\nIf you see it, you are most likely looking at a historical chart. For a person born then, its house showed where their mind had transforming power.",magic:"Word magic of power suits this energy: binding with words, deep research as devotion, and spells for truth to come out. Fluorite, Obsidian and rosemary honour a deep mind.",shadow:"Manipulation through words, and obsessive thinking."},Cancer:{simple:"Pluto in Cancer marks a generation transformed through family, home and homeland. In you it can show as deep, protective emotional intensity.",detailed:"Pluto was in Cancer from about 1912 to 1939, through world war, revolution and the Depression, when homes and homelands were destroyed and rebuilt. That generation knew the power of family and nation, for good and ill. The gift is fierce protectiveness and emotional resilience; the risk is clannishness and the misuse of belonging.\n\nFor elders who carry it, when Pluto touches personal planets or angles, it can show as intense family bonds, deep emotional memory, and a drive to protect the home at any cost. Its house shows where they rebuilt their roots.",magic:"Ancestral and protective magic suits this placement: ancestor healing, home warding, and rituals for family wounds. Moonstone, Obsidian and rosemary support deep emotional protection.",shadow:"Clannishness, and controlling through family ties."},Leo:{simple:"Pluto in Leo marks a generation that transforms through self-expression, creativity and power. In you it can show as a strong will to create and lead.",detailed:"Pluto was in Leo from about 1937 to 1958, through the Second World War and the post-war boom. This generation saw the power of charismatic leaders, for terrible ill and great good, and later transformed creativity and youth culture. The gift is creative power and personal authority; the risk is ego and the abuse of power.\n\nFor those who carry it, when Pluto touches personal planets or angles, it can show as a powerful need for self-expression and a strong presence. Its house shows where they insist on their power.",magic:"Solar transformation magic suits this energy: creative work as ritual, confidence rituals, and spells to reclaim personal power. Sunstone, Obsidian and Sunflower honour a strong heart.",shadow:"Ego, and the urge to dominate."},Virgo:{simple:"Pluto in Virgo marks a generation that transforms work, health and the environment. In you it can show as a deep drive to fix, heal and perfect.",detailed:"Pluto was in Virgo from about 1956 to 1972, much of it alongside Uranus. This generation saw computing, ecology and alternative health become forces for change, and later reshaped work and medicine. The gift is the power to heal, reform and purify; the risk is obsessive perfectionism and anxious control.\n\nPersonally, when Pluto touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as intensity about health, work and service, and a talent for deep analysis. Its house shows where you transform the everyday.",magic:"Healing and purification magic suits this placement: herbal medicine made with care, cleansing rituals, and spells for health beside proper care. Amazonite, Obsidian and Hyssop support deep purification.",shadow:"Obsessive control, and perfectionism that never rests."},Libra:{simple:"Pluto in Libra marks a generation that transforms relationship, partnership and justice. In you it can show as intense relationships that change you.",detailed:"Pluto was in Libra from about 1971 to 1984. This generation grew up as divorce, equal rights and new forms of partnership reshaped relationship. The gift is the power to transform how we relate and to fight for justice; the risk is power struggles in love and control through charm.\n\nPersonally, when Pluto touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as intense, transforming relationships and a deep sense of fairness. Its house shows where you meet power in partnership.",magic:"Relationship and justice magic suits this energy: rituals for healing partnership wounds, justice spells, and cord cutting when needed. Rose Quartz, Obsidian and Vervain support balance and depth.",shadow:"Power struggles in love, and manipulation through charm."},Scorpio:{simple:"Pluto in Scorpio, its modern home, marks a generation of great depth and intensity. In you it can show as fearless emotional power and a drive for truth.",detailed:"Pluto was in Scorpio from about 1983 to 1995, the sign modern astrologers give it to rule. This generation grew up amid the AIDS crisis, the end of the Cold War and new conversations about sex, death and trauma. The gift is resilience and fearless honesty about the depths; the risk is intensity, control and survival mode.\n\nPersonally, when Pluto touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as strong intuition, emotional intensity and the power to transform yourself and others. Its house shows where you go deepest.",magic:"Deep transformation magic suits this placement: shadow work, banishing, protection, and death-and-rebirth rituals. Obsidian, Garnet and Wormwood honour the depths; Hades and Persephone are their old keepers.",shadow:"Control, obsession, and living in survival mode."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Pluto in Sagittarius marks a generation that transforms beliefs, education and global culture. In you it can show as a powerful search for truth.",detailed:"Pluto was in Sagittarius from about 1995 to 2008. This generation grew up with globalisation, religious conflict and the internet opening the world. The gift is the power to transform beliefs and to seek a truth that holds for everyone; the risk is extremism and dogmatic certainty.\n\nPersonally, when Pluto touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as intense beliefs, a passion for learning and travel, and a drive to change how people think. Its house shows where you seek deeper truth.",magic:"Seeking, devotional magic suits this energy: pilgrimage, study as devotion, and rituals for truth and wisdom. Turquoise, Obsidian and Sage honour the search.",shadow:"Fanaticism, and certainty that silences others."},Capricorn:{simple:"Pluto in Capricorn marks a generation that transforms institutions, governments and structures of power. In you it can show as deep ambition and resilience.",detailed:"Pluto was in Capricorn from about 2008 to 2024. This generation was born through financial crisis, a pandemic and the shaking of many institutions. The gift is the power to rebuild structures from the ground up and to wield authority responsibly; the risk is cynicism about power or a hunger for control.\n\nPersonally, when Pluto touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as strong ambition, endurance and a drive to transform how things are run. Its house shows where you rebuild.",magic:"Structured, powerful magic suits this placement: long-term spells for success, ancestor rites, and banishing outdated structures. Onyx, Obsidian and cypress support steady, deep change.",shadow:"Hunger for control, and cynicism about authority."},Aquarius:{simple:"Pluto in Aquarius marks a generation transforming technology, community and collective power. In you it can show as a radical vision for the future.",detailed:"Pluto entered Aquarius in 2023 to 2024 and will stay until about 2044. Children born now arrive in a world being remade by artificial intelligence, networks and new ideas of community. The gift is the power to transform society and give power to the many; the risk is the misuse of technology and collective control.\n\nPersonally, Pluto's house and its aspects to personal planets show where a child of this generation carries the collective's change most strongly.",magic:"Communal and visionary magic suits this energy: group ritual, spells for social change, and protection in digital spaces. Amethyst, Obsidian and Labradorite suit this transforming vision.",shadow:"Collective control, and losing the person to the cause."},Pisces:{simple:"Pluto in Pisces marks a generation that transforms spirituality, art and compassion. Nobody alive has it; it last occurred from about 1797 to 1823.",detailed:"Pluto was last in Pisces from about 1797 to 1823, the Romantic age, when art, mysticism and feeling transformed culture. It will return around 2043. The gift is spiritual transformation and deep compassion; the risk is escapism, addiction and confusion of power.\n\nIf you see it, you are looking at a historical chart or one cast for the future. For a person born then, its house showed where they dissolved and were remade.",magic:"Spiritual, dreaming magic suits this energy: meditation, trance, water rituals and dreamwork. Amethyst, Obsidian and mugwort honour the depths of the sea.",shadow:"Escapism, and dissolving into others."}}},3078,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SATURN_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const t={Aries:{simple:"With Saturn in Aries you learn to act with patience and earned courage. Self-assertion may feel hard at first, and becomes a real strength with practice.",detailed:"Saturn is in fall in Aries, opposite its exaltation in Libra. Traditional astrologers read this as Saturn's caution at odds with Aries's urge to act. In life it can show as hesitancy about putting yourself first, or the opposite: a defensive, push-through will that never rests. Early on, starting things may feel blocked, or you may have learned that your anger or independence was not welcome.\n\nThe lesson is disciplined courage: learning to act from a settled centre, take initiative responsibly and lead without either freezing or forcing. Over time, people with this placement often become strong, self-made leaders who know exactly what it costs to begin.\n\nSaturn takes about two and a half years to cross a sign, so your whole age group shares this. Its house shows where you meet the lesson. Your Saturn return, around twenty-nine, is often a time when this placement's work comes due.",magic:"Courage built slowly is your Saturn magic: a candle lit for a few minutes each day before a hard task, protection charms for independence, and banishing spells for fear. Saturdays and Tuesdays suit you. Bloodstone, Hematite, Onyx and nettle steady the will.",shadow:"Frustration, blocked anger, and pushing on alone when you could ask for help."},Taurus:{simple:"With Saturn in Taurus you learn the slow building of security, worth and resources. Money and comfort may be hard-won, and you build them to last.",detailed:"Saturn in Taurus asks you to take the material world seriously. You may have grown up with scarcity or with a strong fear of it, and security can feel like something you must earn with effort. Over time you tend to become patient, practical and wise about money, land, the body and what really has value.\n\nThe lesson is grounded self-worth: knowing your value is not the same as your bank balance, and building stability without hoarding or denying yourself pleasure. People with this placement often become excellent stewards of resources and builders of lasting things.\n\nEveryone born in the same two or three years carries it, so the personal story is in its house: the part of life where you learn what security really means. Venus rules Taurus, so your Venus has much to say about how you learn to enjoy what you build.",magic:"Slow prosperity and grounding magic suit your Saturn: a money jar added to every Saturday, a garden tended as a long-term spell, and rituals to bless and protect what you own. Saturdays and Fridays suit you. Smoky Quartz, Jet, Pyrite and patchouli help build steady worth.",shadow:"Scarcity thinking, hoarding, and denying yourself pleasure."},Gemini:{simple:"With Saturn in Gemini you learn to think, speak and study with depth and care. Communication may feel like hard work early, and becomes your mastery.",detailed:"Saturn in Gemini brings seriousness to the mind. You may have felt slow or unheard as a child, struggled with school, or had a sibling or early learning situation that was difficult. In response you often become careful, precise and thorough in how you think and speak, and you may master a subject or craft of words over many years.\n\nThe lesson is disciplined thought: learning to focus, to finish, and to trust your mind. People with this placement often become excellent writers, teachers, researchers or editors precisely because nothing came easily.\n\nYour schoolmates share it; its house shows where in life your mind is asked to slow down and go deep. Mercury rules Gemini, so your Mercury shows how this work is done.",magic:"Structured word magic suits your Saturn: a daily writing practice as ritual, carefully worded petitions, binding spells for gossip, and study blessings before exams. Saturdays and Wednesdays suit you. Fluorite, Sodalite, rosemary and Clear Quartz support focus and memory.",shadow:"Self-doubt about your mind, rigid thinking, and fear of speaking."},Cancer:{simple:"With Saturn in Cancer you learn to build emotional security and a true home. Feelings and family may have felt heavy early, and you become a steady keeper of both.",detailed:"Saturn is in detriment in Cancer, opposite its home in Capricorn. Traditionally this means Saturn's coolness sits uneasily in the sign of nurture. In life it can show as early experiences of emotional reserve, responsibility for family, or a home that felt more duty than comfort. You may have learned to hide your needs or to look after others before you were ready.\n\nThe lesson is building your own emotional foundation: learning to care for yourself, create a home that truly holds you, and let others in. Over time people with this placement often become deeply reliable protectors and wise keepers of family history.\n\nSaturn returns to this place around twenty-nine and again near fifty-eight, and many people with Saturn in Cancer find those years are when they finally build the home they needed. The Moon rules Cancer, so your Moon is part of how you heal it.",magic:"Ancestor and hearth magic is your Saturn work: ancestor altars, family healing rituals, home protection, and slow, nourishing kitchen spells. Saturdays and Mondays, and the waning Moon for release, suit you. Moonstone, Jet, Smoky Quartz and comfrey support emotional healing and steady roots.",shadow:"Emotional coldness, fear of dependency, and duty in place of tenderness."},Leo:{simple:"With Saturn in Leo you learn to shine with confidence and authentic self-expression. Being seen may feel risky at first, and you grow into real presence.",detailed:"Saturn is in detriment in Leo, opposite its home in Aquarius. Traditionally this means Saturn's restraint is uncomfortable in the sign of joy and display. In life it can show as shyness about being seen, a feeling that play and creativity had to be earned, or a strong need for recognition paired with fear of it.\n\nThe lesson is authentic confidence: learning to express yourself, create, play and lead without needing applause or hiding from it. People with this placement often become serious, dedicated artists, teachers or leaders, whose presence is earned and steady.\n\nIt is shared by a cohort born across two or three years; its house shows the stage on which you learn to be seen. The Sun rules Leo, so your Sun shows where the work of shining is done.",magic:"Confidence built slowly is your Saturn magic: a creative practice kept as devotion, a self-worth spell renewed each Sunday, and rituals for courage to be seen. Saturdays and Sundays suit you. Sunstone, Tiger Eye, Onyx and Calendula help you hold your light.",shadow:"Fear of being seen, rigid pride, and joy kept on a short leash."},Virgo:{simple:"With Saturn in Virgo you learn mastery through work, health and service. You hold high standards and become truly skilled with time.",detailed:"Saturn in Virgo asks for precision and discipline in daily life. You may feel a strong pressure to do things perfectly, be useful, or keep your body and routines under control. Health and work can be areas of anxiety, especially early, and the inner critic can be loud.\n\nThe lesson is skilled, kind service: learning that good enough is often good, that routine can support rather than imprison you, and that your worth is not only in your usefulness. People with this placement often become masters of a craft and excellent healers or organisers.\n\nEveryone born near you shares it, so look to its house for the part of life where your standards are highest. Mercury rules Virgo, so your Mercury shows how the work is done.",magic:"Ordered, practical magic suits your Saturn: herbal remedies made with care, cleansing rituals, routine devotions, and spells for health (beside proper care). Saturdays and Wednesdays suit you. Amazonite, Smoky Quartz, rosemary and Chamomile help soften perfectionism.",shadow:"Perfectionism, anxiety about health, and harsh self-criticism."},Libra:{simple:"With Saturn in Libra, where it is exalted, you learn fairness, commitment and balance in relationships. Partnership is serious work, and it can become your strength.",detailed:"Saturn is exalted in Libra, which traditional astrologers read as Saturn's most honoured place: law and justice in their finest form. You take relationships, contracts and fairness seriously, and you may be drawn to law, mediation, design or diplomacy. Partnerships can be a place of lessons, delays or responsibilities, especially early.\n\nThe lesson is mature partnership: learning to commit, to be fair to yourself as well as others, and to build relationships on respect and clear agreements. Over time people with this placement often become wise, steady partners and just leaders.\n\nA whole cohort shares it; its house shows where your commitments are tested and proved. Venus rules Libra, so your Venus shows how love and law meet in you.",magic:"Justice and commitment magic suits your Saturn: spells for a fair outcome, partnership blessings, binding agreements written and sealed, and rituals for balance. Saturdays and Fridays suit you. Lapis Lazuli, Jade, Vervain and Rose Quartz support just, lasting bonds; Maat's feather of truth is a good image for the altar.",shadow:"Fear of commitment or rigid duty in it, and judging by rules rather than hearts."},Scorpio:{simple:"With Saturn in Scorpio you learn to face depths, power and transformation with courage. Trust and intimacy may come slowly, and become profound.",detailed:"Saturn in Scorpio brings seriousness to the hidden places: intimacy, shared resources, death, sexuality, power and control. You may have met loss, secrets or crisis early, and learned to guard yourself carefully. Trust is hard-won.\n\nThe lesson is mastery of the depths: learning to face fear, share power, let go and transform. People with this placement often become strong, wise guides through crisis, and gifted researchers, therapists or financial stewards.\n\nYour generation shares it, and its house shows where you will be asked to face what frightens you most, and where you grow strongest for having done so. Mars and Pluto, the rulers of Scorpio, colour this Saturn.",magic:"Deep, slow transformation magic suits your Saturn: shadow work, ancestor healing, banishing and protection, and rituals for grief. Saturdays and Tuesdays, and the dark Moon, suit you. Obsidian, Jet, Smoky Quartz and cypress support the work; Hekate and Hades are old guardians of these thresholds.",shadow:"Control, distrust, and fear of vulnerability."},Sagittarius:{simple:"With Saturn in Sagittarius you learn to build a faith and philosophy that is truly your own. Belief is serious work, and you earn your wisdom.",detailed:"Saturn in Sagittarius asks you to take meaning seriously. You may have grown up with strict beliefs, doubts, or a sense that wisdom and freedom must be earned. Higher education, travel or religion can be places of effort, delay or deep commitment.\n\nThe lesson is a lived philosophy: building your own beliefs through study and experience, and holding them with humility. People with this placement often become serious teachers, scholars, lawyers or spiritual guides whose wisdom is tested.\n\nThose born in the same few years share it; its house shows where your beliefs are tested by life. Jupiter rules Sagittarius, so your Jupiter shows how your faith can grow.",magic:"Study and devotion suit your Saturn: a disciplined reading or meditation practice, pilgrimage, and long-term devotions to a god of your path. Saturdays and Thursdays suit you. Lapis Lazuli, Sodalite, Sage and Juniper support steady faith.",shadow:"Dogmatism, cynicism, and fear of believing anything."},Capricorn:{simple:"With Saturn in Capricorn, its own sign, you learn mastery through ambition, discipline and responsibility. You are built for the long climb.",detailed:"Saturn is at home in Capricorn, and here it is strong and steady. You understand structure, time, effort and consequence, and you often carry responsibility early. You can be ambitious, patient and deeply reliable, and you build things that last: careers, institutions, families.\n\nThe lesson is wise authority: learning to lead without coldness, to rest without guilt, and to measure success by more than status. Traditional astrologers read Saturn in its own sign as able to deliver its gifts of endurance and mastery.\n\nYour cohort shares it; its house shows the mountain you are climbing. As Saturn rules this sign, its house and aspects tell the story.",magic:"Structured, long-term magic is natural for you: career and success spells over a season, boundary charms, ancestor rites, and devotions on Saturdays. The waning Moon helps clear obstacles. Onyx, Garnet, Jet and cypress are allies; Saturn himself, god of time and the harvest, is the old patron.",shadow:"Workaholism, rigidity, and coldness in the name of duty."},Aquarius:{simple:"With Saturn in Aquarius, its traditional home, you learn to build communities and systems that serve everyone. You bring structure to new ideas.",detailed:"Saturn is at home in Aquarius, its day house, and here it is the builder of the future: principled, systematic, community-minded. You take friendship, groups and social responsibility seriously, and you can turn ideals into working structures.\n\nThe lesson is belonging without losing yourself: learning to work with others, to be part of a group while staying true to your vision, and to let your principles have warmth. People with this placement often become strong organisers, scientists, reformers or community builders.\n\nYour cohort shares this; its house shows the group or system you are here to help build. Uranus, the modern ruler of Aquarius, adds its own story.",magic:"Communal and systematic magic suits your Saturn: group rituals, coven structure, sigils and planetary squares, and long-term spells for a cause. Saturdays suit you. Amethyst, Hematite, Labradorite and Clear Quartz support steady vision.",shadow:"Emotional distance, rigid ideals, and loneliness in a crowd."},Pisces:{simple:"With Saturn in Pisces you learn to give shape to dreams, compassion and spirit. Boundaries may be hard, and become a gift with practice.",detailed:"Saturn in Pisces asks you to bring structure to what is fluid. You may feel the pull between duty and dreams, between the practical world and spiritual longing. Boundaries, both emotional and physical, may be difficult, and you may have absorbed others' sorrows early.\n\nThe lesson is grounded compassion: learning to serve without losing yourself, to create with discipline, and to build a spiritual practice that holds you. People with this placement often become dedicated artists, healers or mystics whose work is both deep and real.\n\nA cohort born across two or three years shares it; its house shows where your dreams most need a container. Jupiter and Neptune, the rulers of Pisces, colour this Saturn.",magic:"Disciplined spiritual practice is your Saturn magic: daily meditation, dream journals, cleansing baths, and protective rituals for sensitive people. Saturdays and Mondays suit you. Amethyst, Smoky Quartz, Black Tourmaline and mugwort support boundaries and vision.",shadow:"Escapism, martyrdom, and fear of the unknown."}}},3079,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"URANUS_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n={Aries:{simple:"Uranus in Aries marks a generation of pioneers who break rules by acting first. In you it can show as a restless, independent streak and a need to be free to start things your own way.",detailed:"Uranus was in Aries from about 1927 to 1935 and again from 2010 to 2019. Both groups arrived when individual will and new technologies were reshaping the world: radio and flight for the first, smartphones and social platforms for the second. The generation's gift is courage to try the new; its risk is impatience and rebellion without a plan.\n\nPersonally, this placement matters most if Uranus touches your Sun, Moon, Ascendant or chart ruler, or sits in an angular house. Then it can show as sudden decisions, a strong allergy to being told what to do, and an inventive, impulsive streak. Its house shows where you need the most freedom to act.",magic:"Lightning-quick, improvised magic suits this energy: spells cast on the spot, sigils made in a moment of inspiration, and fire-and-air workings to break a stuck pattern. Storm energy, captured carefully in water or a charged object, is a classic Uranian tool. Carnelian, Labradorite and ginger hold the spark.",shadow:"Rebellion for its own sake, and impatience with anything slow."},Taurus:{simple:"Uranus in Taurus marks a generation that changes how we value money, food, land and the body. In you it can bring surprising ideas about security and worth.",detailed:"Uranus was in Taurus from about 1934 to 1942 and again from 2018 to 2026. The first group grew up through depression and war, when money and food were overturned; the second arrives with digital currencies, a changing climate and new ways of farming, eating and owning. The generation's gift is reinventing what security means; its risk is stubborn resistance to change, or upheaval in the things that should be steady.\n\nPersonally, it matters most when it aspects your personal planets or sits on an angle. Then it can show as an unusual relationship to money, possessions or the body, sudden changes in income, and a taste for unconventional beauty. Its house shows where your security keeps being reinvented.",magic:"Earth magic with a twist suits this placement: new methods of growing, money spells that experiment, and grounding rituals to steady sudden change. Green Aventurine, Labradorite and Smoky Quartz help hold the ground when the earth shifts.",shadow:"Clinging to old security while it crumbles, or recklessness with resources."},Gemini:{simple:"Uranus in Gemini marks a generation of quick, inventive minds who change how we talk and learn. In you it can show as original ideas and restless curiosity.",detailed:"Uranus was in Gemini from about 1941 to 1949 and entered it again in 2025, staying until 2033. The first group grew up as radio, early computing and codebreaking changed communication; the new one is born into a world remade by artificial intelligence and instant networks. The generation's gift is brilliant, unconventional thinking; its risk is scattered attention and information without wisdom.\n\nPersonally, when Uranus touches your personal planets or angles, it can bring flashes of insight, an unusual way of speaking or writing, and a mind that jumps across subjects. Its house shows where your thinking breaks new ground.",magic:"Word and air magic with innovation suits this energy: digital sigils, new forms of divination, spells written in code or cipher, and rituals for clear communication. Fluorite, Citrine and peppermint steady a fast-moving mind.",shadow:"Nervous restlessness, and clever ideas that never land."},Cancer:{simple:"Uranus in Cancer marks a generation that changed what family and home can be. In you it can bring unusual roots and a need for freedom within belonging.",detailed:"Uranus was in Cancer from about 1948 to 1956, the post-war years of new suburbs, television in the living room and changing family roles. That generation later reshaped ideas of family, gender and home. The gift is reinventing belonging; the risk is emotional unpredictability or a home life that never quite settles.\n\nPersonally, when this Uranus touches your Moon, Sun or angles, it can show as an unconventional family, frequent moves, a need for independence even in close bonds, and sudden emotional insights. Its house shows where your sense of home is reinvented.",magic:"Hearth magic with a new shape suits this placement: blessing a chosen family, unusual home altars, ancestor work that includes the family you made, and rituals for emotional freedom. Moonstone, Labradorite and Lemon Balm steady changing tides.",shadow:"Restlessness at home, and fear of being tied by belonging."},Leo:{simple:"Uranus in Leo marks a generation that rebelled through creativity and self-expression. In you it can show as a bold, original creative streak.",detailed:"Uranus was in Leo from about 1955 to 1962. This generation grew up with rock and roll and youth culture, and came of age insisting on the right to be themselves. The gift is creative revolution and fearless self-expression; the risk is ego and the need to be the unique one in every room.\n\nPersonally, when it aspects your personal planets or angles, it can show as an unusual creative talent, unconventional romance, and a strong need to express yourself in your own way. Its house shows where you insist on being original.",magic:"Creative and performative magic suits this energy: improvised ritual, dance and song as power, and glamour that breaks the rules. Sunstone, Labradorite and Sunflower hold bright, original fire.",shadow:"Self-centred rebellion, and drama to prove you are different."},Virgo:{simple:"Uranus in Virgo marks a generation that changed work, health and technology. In you it can bring inventive skill and new ideas about wellbeing.",detailed:"Uranus was in Virgo from about 1961 to 1969, alongside Pluto for much of that time. This generation saw computers move into work and grew up as ideas about diet, ecology and alternative health took root. The gift is practical innovation; the risk is nervous tension and anxious perfectionism about systems that keep changing.\n\nPersonally, when it touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as unusual work patterns, a gift for technology or alternative healing, and a restless, inventive approach to daily routines. Its house shows where you reform the everyday.",magic:"Practical, experimental magic suits this placement: new herbal methods, healing rituals beside proper care, and spells to reorganise daily life. Fluorite, Amazonite and fennel steady an inventive, anxious mind.",shadow:"Nervous tension, and critical restlessness with every routine."},Libra:{simple:"Uranus in Libra marks a generation that changed the rules of relationship and partnership. In you it can show as a need for freedom and equality in love.",detailed:"Uranus was in Libra from about 1968 to 1975. This generation grew up as divorce became common and the shapes of marriage and partnership opened up. The gift is reinventing relationship on equal terms; the risk is instability, or valuing freedom so much that commitment feels impossible.\n\nPersonally, when it aspects your Venus, Moon or angles, it can show as unconventional relationships, sudden attractions and endings, and a strong sense of justice. Its house shows where you need fairness on new terms.",magic:"Relationship magic with freedom built in suits this energy: spells for equal partnership, honest agreements, and rituals that honour unusual bonds. Rose Quartz, Lapis Lazuli and Labradorite suit this airy, changeable heart.",shadow:"Restlessness in love, and keeping one foot out of the door."},Scorpio:{simple:"Uranus in Scorpio marks a generation that broke taboos around sex, death and power. In you it can bring sudden transformations and deep, radical insight.",detailed:"Uranus was in Scorpio from about 1974 to 1981. This generation grew up as taboos around sexuality, death and psychology were being challenged, and as new crises and medical discoveries changed how we think of the body and survival. The gift is fearless honesty about the depths; the risk is upheaval in intimacy and power.\n\nPersonally, when it touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as sudden changes in shared resources or intimacy, intense intuition, and a drive to expose and transform what is hidden. Its house shows where you break through.",magic:"Radical transformation magic suits this placement: shadow work, breaking curses or old patterns, and rituals for rebirth after upheaval. Obsidian, Labradorite and Wormwood suit this intense, electric depth.",shadow:"Explosive intensity, and upheaval for its own sake."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Uranus in Sagittarius marks a generation that changed beliefs, travel and education. In you it can bring unconventional ideas about faith and freedom.",detailed:"Uranus was in Sagittarius from about 1981 to 1988. This generation grew up as travel became cheap, the world became connected and religious and philosophical ideas began to mix. The gift is open-minded, global thinking; the risk is restless searching and rejecting every tradition without finding one's own.\n\nPersonally, when it aspects your personal planets or angles, it can show as sudden changes of belief, unusual education or travel, and a strong need for intellectual freedom. Its house shows where you seek new horizons.",magic:"Eclectic, seeking magic suits this energy: rituals that blend traditions with care and respect, travel spells, and divination by new methods. Turquoise, Labradorite and Star Anise suit this wide, restless mind.",shadow:"Restless seeking, and rebellion against every belief."},Capricorn:{simple:"Uranus in Capricorn marks a generation that challenges and rebuilds structures and institutions. In you it can show as innovative ambition.",detailed:"Uranus was in Capricorn from about 1988 to 1996, mostly with Neptune alongside. This generation was born as the Berlin Wall fell, the internet arrived and old institutions began to shake. The gift is rebuilding structures in new ways; the risk is cynicism about all authority, or rigid rebellion.\n\nPersonally, when it touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as an unusual career path, sudden changes in status, and a drive to reform how things are run. Its house shows where you rebuild the rules.",magic:"Structured innovation suits this placement: spells for unconventional success, rituals to break outdated rules in your life, and grounding work for sudden change. Onyx, Labradorite and cypress steady this ambitious, restless energy.",shadow:"Cynicism about authority, and rebellion that becomes its own rigid rule."},Aquarius:{simple:"Uranus in Aquarius, its modern home, marks a generation of digital natives and network thinkers. In you it can bring originality and a strong sense of community.",detailed:"Uranus was in Aquarius from about 1995 to 2003, the sign modern astrologers give it to rule. This generation grew up with the internet and networks as a given. The gift is collective vision and comfort with the new; the risk is detachment, and living more in the network than in the body.\n\nPersonally, when it aspects your personal planets or angles, it can show as strong individuality, unusual friendships and a natural gift for technology and group work. Its house shows where you are most yourself by being unlike anyone else.",magic:"Networked, communal magic suits this energy: online circles, group sigils, rituals for a cause and astrology-timed spells. Amethyst, Labradorite and lavender support this clear, electric vision.",shadow:"Detachment, and feeling like an outsider everywhere."},Pisces:{simple:"Uranus in Pisces marks a generation that changes spirituality, art and compassion. In you it can bring sudden intuitions and unusual spiritual gifts.",detailed:"Uranus was in Pisces from about 2003 to 2011. This generation is growing up with streaming art, virtual worlds and changing ideas of spirituality and mental health. The gift is imaginative, compassionate innovation; the risk is confusion, and escaping into the virtual.\n\nPersonally, when it touches your personal planets or angles, it can show as sudden psychic flashes, unusual creative talent, and a need for spiritual freedom. Its house shows where your intuition breaks new ground.",magic:"Dream and water magic with new forms suits this placement: digital art as offering, new forms of meditation, and dreamwork. Amethyst, Aquamarine and mugwort suit this sensitive, inventive spirit.",shadow:"Confusion, and escape into dreams or screens."}}},3080,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"VENUS_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o={Aries:{simple:"With Venus in Aries you love boldly and fall fast. You are drawn to courage, honesty and a little excitement, and you show affection by acting on it.",detailed:"Venus is in detriment in Aries, the sign opposite her home in Libra. Traditionally that means Venus's soft arts of patience, harmony and courtship are hurried by Mars's fire. In life it often looks like a lover who chases, declares and acts: you know quickly when you like someone, and you would rather say so than wait to be noticed. Attraction is sparked by confidence, challenge and a bit of a chase.\n\nThe gift is ardour and honesty. You do not play games for long, you defend the people you love, and you bring energy and fun to relationships. The challenge is staying power once the chase is over, and a tendency to put your own wants first without meaning to. Impatience can make you leave just before something deepens.\n\nIn relationships you need independence, a partner with their own fire, and room to be impulsive together. Your taste tends toward the bright, the sporty and the new. Mars rules Aries, so Mars's sign and house say a great deal about how you pursue what you desire.",magic:"Love magic for you is quick and fiery: a red candle lit to call courage in love, a self-love spell before a first date, a charm to bring passion back. Tuesdays and Fridays both suit, especially a Venus hour on a Tuesday. Carnelian, Garnet, rose and cinnamon warm the heart; Aphrodite in her armed form, as worshipped at Sparta and Cythera, is a fitting patron.",shadow:"Impatience in love, selfishness when excited, and boredom once the chase ends."},Taurus:{simple:"With Venus in Taurus, her own sign, you love steadily, sensually and loyally. You treasure comfort, beauty, good food and touch, and you build love to last.",detailed:"Venus is at home in Taurus, and here she is at her most earthy. You love through the senses: touch, taste, scent, music, a beautiful room, a meal made with care. You are slow to fall but very loyal once you do, and you show love through presence and reliability more than drama. Money and possessions matter to you as sources of security and pleasure, and you often have good taste and a good eye for quality.\n\nThe gift is constancy and the ability to make life genuinely pleasant for yourself and others. People feel safe with you. The challenge is possessiveness and resistance to change: holding on to a person, habit or thing because letting go feels like loss, or settling into comfort that becomes a rut.\n\nIn relationships you need physical affection, reliability and time. At work you may be drawn to the arts, music, design, food, gardening, beauty or finance. Traditional astrologers read Venus in her own sign as strong and well able to bring her blessings: affection, comfort and grace.",magic:"Earthy Venus magic is yours: prosperity jars, slow candle spells over seven nights, herb gardens grown as devotion, love-drawing baths with flowers you picked yourself. Fridays and Venus hours, Beltane and the Moon in Taurus suit you. Rose Quartz, Emerald, rose and patchouli are natural allies; offerings of bread, honey and flowers please both Venus and Aphrodite.",shadow:"Possessiveness, stubborn comfort-seeking, and measuring love by what it gives you."},Gemini:{simple:"With Venus in Gemini you fall for minds as much as bodies. You love conversation, wit and variety, and you keep love alive by keeping it interesting.",detailed:"Venus in Gemini loves through words. Flirting, banter, messages, shared jokes and long talks are how you connect, and a quick mind is very attractive to you. You like variety in company and in pleasures, and you can enjoy many kinds of people. You are often charming, youthful in spirit and lovely to be around.\n\nThe gift is lightness: you keep relationships playful and curious, and you rarely let things grow stale. You are a good friend first and often stay friends with exes. The challenge is depth and constancy. When conversation runs dry you can drift, and you may intellectualise feelings rather than sit in them. Mixed messages can come from genuinely mixed feelings.\n\nIn relationships you need a partner who talks, who surprises you and who does not mind a little freedom. Your taste runs to books, gadgets, clever design and the latest thing. Mercury rules Gemini, so where your Mercury sits shapes what you find charming.",magic:"Love letters, love poems and spoken charms are your best tools: a sweetening spell written as a letter, a knot of two ribbons tied with words, a sigil for friendship carried in a pocket. Fridays and Wednesdays, and the Moon in Gemini or Libra, suit you. Citrine, Blue Lace Agate, lavender and mint support honest, happy talk in love.",shadow:"Fickleness, flirting to avoid intimacy, and talking around what you feel."},Cancer:{simple:"With Venus in Cancer you love tenderly and protectively. You want closeness, safety and a home to share, and you show love by caring for people.",detailed:"Venus in Cancer loves the way a hearth loves: with warmth, food, shelter and memory. You are drawn to people who feel like home, and you show affection by nurturing, remembering what matters to them and making them comfortable. You are sentimental, often keep keepsakes and letters, and love deeply once you trust.\n\nThe gift is devotion and a true talent for making others feel safe. Family, chosen or born, may be at the centre of what you value. The challenge is vulnerability: fear of rejection can make you guarded at first, and once attached you may cling, sulk or give care in a way that quietly asks for it back. Moods can colour how loved you feel from day to day.\n\nIn relationships you need emotional security, regular reassurance and a shared nest. You often love old things, family recipes, the sea and the comforts of home. The Moon rules Cancer, so the Moon's sign in your chart shows what makes you feel loved.",magic:"Hearth and moon magic is your love language: a home blessing for a new household, a kitchen spell baked into a cake for someone dear, a moon water bath for self-love, keepsakes laid on an altar to the family. Mondays and Fridays, and the full Moon, suit you. Moonstone, Rose Quartz, jasmine and Lemon Balm comfort and draw love home.",shadow:"Clinging, moodiness in love, and care that keeps score."},Leo:{simple:"With Venus in Leo you love generously, playfully and with your whole heart. You want romance, admiration and loyalty, and you give them back in full.",detailed:"Venus in Leo loves like a summer afternoon: warm, bright and a little theatrical. You enjoy courtship, grand gestures, gifts and making people feel special, and you want to be adored in return. You are loyal and proud of the people you love. Creativity, beauty, glamour and fun are deeply important pleasures for you.\n\nThe gift is generosity: you bring joy, warmth and celebration to relationships and are a wonderful friend and lover. The challenge is pride. If you feel unappreciated or upstaged you may sulk or withdraw, and you can need more reassurance than a partner knows how to give. Love can become a stage when it would rather be a home.\n\nIn relationships you need admiration, play and a partner who is proud to be with you. Your taste runs to the dramatic, the golden and the luxurious. The Sun rules Leo, so your Sun's sign and house show what you need to feel cherished.",magic:"Glamour and joy are your Venus magic: a confidence spell before a date, a love-drawing working with gold and red candles, a creative offering made for someone you adore. Sundays and Fridays, Lughnasadh and the Moon in Leo suit you. Sunstone, Amber, Calendula and Sunflower bring warmth; Hathor, goddess of joy, music and love, is a patron many people with this placement feel close to.",shadow:"Pride in love, needing applause, and drama when you feel overlooked."},Virgo:{simple:"With Venus in Virgo you love through care, attention and practical help. You notice what people need, and you show love by doing small things well.",detailed:"Venus is in fall in Virgo, the sign opposite her exaltation in Pisces. Traditionally this was read as Venus's grace held back by Virgo's caution and critique. In life it often looks like a lover who is modest, discerning and devoted in quiet ways: you show love by remembering, fixing, tidying, cooking and helping, more than by declarations. You notice detail, and the right small gesture moves you more than grand romance.\n\nThe gift is real, practical devotion and a refined taste for what is well made and healthy. You are a loyal partner who makes life work. The challenge is criticism, of others and especially of yourself. It can be hard to believe you are lovable as you are, and the urge to improve a partner can feel to them like disapproval. Anxiety can creep into love.\n\nIn relationships you need trust, usefulness and a partner who appreciates your quiet care. Your taste runs to the natural, the simple and the well crafted. Mercury rules Virgo, so its sign and house show how your heart thinks.",magic:"Herbal and household love magic suits you: a sachet stitched by hand, a healing tea for someone dear, a cleansing of the bedroom to make space for love, a self-acceptance spell written and kept in your grimoire. Fridays and Wednesdays, and the harvest months, suit you. Peridot, Moss Agate, rosemary and Chamomile soften the inner critic.",shadow:"Self-criticism, fault-finding in love, and holding back affection until things are perfect."},Libra:{simple:"With Venus in Libra, her own sign, you love with grace, charm and a deep wish for harmony. Partnership, beauty and fairness matter greatly to you.",detailed:"Venus is at home in Libra, here in her airy, social form. You love partnership itself: the meeting of two people as equals, the courtesy, the dialogue, the shared life. You are charming, considerate and good at making others feel welcome. Beauty matters to you, in art, clothes, rooms and manners, and you often have a fine eye for balance and proportion.\n\nThe gift is relationship: you know how to create harmony, mediate between people and make love feel civilised and kind. The challenge is losing yourself in the other. You may avoid conflict at all costs, say what pleases rather than what is true, or find it hard to be alone. Indecision can stall love when choices are needed.\n\nIn relationships you need fairness, beauty, conversation and a real partner. You are often drawn to the arts, design, law, diplomacy or anything where grace is a skill. Traditional astrologers read Venus in her own sign as strong: able to bring affection, friendship and agreement.",magic:"Balancing and sweetening magic is yours: honey jars for a relationship, a rite of reconciliation, a love-drawing working with two candles moved a little closer each night, and beauty rituals as devotion. Fridays and Venus hours, and the Moon in Libra, suit you. Rose Quartz, Lapis Lazuli, rose and Vervain are allies; Aphrodite and Venus both welcome flowers, mirrors and perfume.",shadow:"People-pleasing, avoiding conflict until it festers, and fear of being alone."},Scorpio:{simple:"With Venus in Scorpio you love intensely and all the way. You want depth, loyalty and real intimacy, and you are not interested in anything shallow.",detailed:"Venus is in detriment in Scorpio, opposite her home in Taurus, which traditional astrologers read as Venus's easy pleasures turned toward Mars's intensity. In life it looks like a lover who wants all or nothing. You are drawn to depth, mystery and emotional truth, and you can bond with someone at the level of the soul. Desire is strong, loyalty fierce, and you notice everything about the people you love.\n\nThe gift is real intimacy: you are not afraid of the dark parts of love, and you can stay with a partner through crisis, grief and change. The challenge is trust and control. Jealousy, testing, secrecy or holding on to hurt can creep in when you feel unsafe, and endings can feel like small deaths.\n\nIn relationships you need honesty, privacy and a partner who can match your depth. Your taste runs to the dark, the rich and the hidden. Mars rules Scorpio traditionally and Pluto in modern astrology; both show how your love transforms you.",magic:"Deep love magic is yours, used with care for others' free will: self-love and shadow work, rituals to heal from betrayal, passion and fidelity charms for a consenting couple, and cord-cutting when it is time to let go. Tuesdays and Fridays, and the dark and full Moon, suit you. Garnet, Obsidian, Rhodochrosite and Damiana fit; Persephone, queen of the depths and of spring's return, is a fitting patron for love that survives the underworld.",shadow:"Jealousy, possessiveness, and testing love instead of trusting it."},Sagittarius:{simple:"With Venus in Sagittarius you love freely and joyfully. You want a companion for adventure, laughter and big ideas, and you need room to roam.",detailed:"Venus in Sagittarius loves like a journey. You are drawn to people who expand your world: different cultures, bright minds, big laughs, honest hearts. You are generous, warm and open, and your affection is often expressed in shared adventures, travel, learning or play. Freedom is part of love for you, not its enemy.\n\nThe gift is optimism and an open heart: you bring joy and possibility to relationships and rarely hold grudges. The challenge is commitment and tact. You can be blunt in love, restless once things become routine, or keep one foot out of the door in case something better comes along.\n\nIn relationships you need trust, space, honesty and a partner who is also your friend and fellow traveller. Your taste runs to the exotic, the outdoorsy and the philosophical. Jupiter rules Sagittarius, so Jupiter's sign and house show where your love finds its luck.",magic:"Your love magic is expansive and lucky: a blessing for a new love's journey, a working for joy and good fortune shared, love charms carried on travels, and gratitude rituals for the people you love. Thursdays and Fridays, and the Moon in Sagittarius, suit you. Turquoise, Sodalite, cinnamon and Star Anise help; Artemis, who keeps her freedom, is a patron for loving without being caged.",shadow:"Restlessness, fear of being tied down, and careless honesty."},Capricorn:{simple:"With Venus in Capricorn you love seriously, loyally and for the long run. You show affection through commitment, reliability and building a life together.",detailed:"Venus in Capricorn takes love seriously. You are cautious at first, often reserved, and you want to know someone is worth it before you open up. Once committed you are steady, dependable and devoted, and your love shows in practical ways: turning up, providing, planning a future, keeping promises. You value quality, tradition and things that age well, and many people with this placement grow more romantic and relaxed with age.\n\nThe gift is durability: your relationships can weather hard times, and your affection is real and earned. The challenge is guardedness and control. Fear of rejection or of looking foolish can keep feelings locked away, and love can become another place to work hard rather than rest.\n\nIn relationships you need respect, loyalty and a partner who is building something too. Your taste is classic, understated and well made. Saturn rules Capricorn, so Saturn's sign and house show what love asks you to grow into.",magic:"Steady, long-term love magic suits you: commitment and fidelity charms, prosperity work for a shared household, a blessing for a home bought together, and ancestral rites that honour the family line. Saturdays and Fridays, and the waxing Moon in an earth sign, suit you. Garnet, Jet, Onyx and comfrey are allies for loyal, lasting love.",shadow:"Emotional reserve, love that waits for status or security, and coldness when hurt."},Aquarius:{simple:"With Venus in Aquarius you love as a friend and an equal. You are drawn to the unusual and the free, and you need a relationship that leaves room to be yourself.",detailed:"Venus in Aquarius loves best in freedom. Friendship is the root of romance for you, and you are often attracted to people who are original, clever, unconventional or committed to a cause. You value independence in yourself and your partner, and you may be drawn to relationship shapes that do not follow the usual script. You are loyal, though in your own way.\n\nThe gift is acceptance: you love people as they are, quirks and all, and you treat partners as equals. You bring openness, honesty and a sense of the future to relationships. The challenge is emotional distance. You can retreat into ideas when feelings get messy, or value freedom so highly that closeness feels like a threat.\n\nIn relationships you need friendship, mental connection and space. Your taste runs to the modern, the unusual and the communal. Saturn rules Aquarius traditionally and Uranus in modern astrology, so both show how your love reshapes the rules.",magic:"Your Venus magic is communal and inventive: friendship spells, a circle working for chosen family, self-love rituals that honour your difference, and sigils for the kind of love you actually want. Fridays and Saturdays, and the Moon in Aquarius, suit you. Amethyst, Aquamarine, Turquoise and lavender suit your clear, cool heart.",shadow:"Detachment, fear of dependency, and contrariness in love."},Pisces:{simple:"With Venus in Pisces, where she is exalted, you love with compassion, romance and imagination. You see the best in people and love without conditions.",detailed:"Venus is exalted in Pisces, which traditional astrologers read as her most honoured place: love made spiritual, compassionate and boundless. You fall in love with souls, and you can see beauty and goodness in people who cannot yet see it in themselves. Romance, music, art and the sea move you deeply. Your kindness is real, and you forgive easily.\n\nThe gift is unconditional love and a deep sense of beauty, often with artistic or musical talent. You can heal people simply by loving them. The challenge is boundaries. It is easy to idealise, rescue or sacrifice yourself, to love the dream of someone rather than who they are, and to be taken advantage of by people who do not deserve your devotion.\n\nIn relationships you need tenderness, spiritual connection and a partner who protects your softness rather than using it. Jupiter rules Pisces traditionally and Neptune in modern astrology, and both show where your love reaches toward the divine.",magic:"Dreamy, devotional love magic is yours: a moonlit bath with rose petals and sea salt, love poetry offered at the altar, dream spells to meet your heart's truth, and healing rituals for a heart that gives too much. Fridays and Thursdays, and the Moon in Pisces, suit you. Aquamarine, Rose Quartz, jasmine and Hibiscus are allies; Aphrodite, born from the sea foam, is close to this placement.",shadow:"Rescuing, idealising, and losing yourself in someone else's needs."}}},3081,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"POINT_READINGS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return l}});var o=r(d[0]),n=r(d[1]),t=r(d[2]),s=r(d[3]);const u={Aries:['Your luck comes when you act first and trust your nerve.','Fortune favours initiative here: chances come to the one who moves, competes and begins. Wellbeing comes through physical activity and independence.'],Taurus:['Your luck comes through patience, the body and building slowly.','Fortune grows like a garden here: steady work, good food, land, craft and savings. Wellbeing comes through comfort and the senses.'],Gemini:['Your luck comes through words, contacts and curiosity.','Fortune arrives in conversations, messages, short trips and learning. Wellbeing comes from a lively mind and good company.'],Cancer:['Your luck comes through home, family and caring for others.','Fortune is found close to home: family ties, property, nurturing work and a safe nest. Wellbeing comes from belonging.'],Leo:['Your luck comes when you shine, create and lead with heart.','Fortune follows generosity and self-expression: performance, children, creative work. Wellbeing comes from joy and being seen.'],Virgo:['Your luck comes through skill, service and careful work.','Fortune is earned by craft and attention to detail, and by helping. Wellbeing comes through good routines and health.'],Libra:['Your luck comes through partnership, fairness and beauty.','Fortune arrives through others: partners, collaborators, clients, a pleasing manner. Wellbeing comes from harmony.'],Scorpio:['Your luck comes through depth, trust and shared resources.','Fortune lies in what is hidden or shared: research, investment, inheritance, deep bonds. Wellbeing comes from emotional honesty.'],Sagittarius:['Your luck comes through faith, travel and learning.','Fortune is found far off: travel, study, teaching and faith. Wellbeing comes from freedom and meaning.'],Capricorn:['Your luck comes through effort, responsibility and time.','Fortune is built: careers, structures, reputation earned slowly. Wellbeing comes from achievement and self-respect.'],Aquarius:['Your luck comes through friends, groups and fresh ideas.','Fortune arrives through community, networks, causes and invention. Wellbeing comes from freedom and belonging to something larger.'],Pisces:['Your luck comes through intuition, compassion and letting go.','Fortune flows through imagination, art, spirit and kindness, often unplanned. Wellbeing comes from rest and faith.']},h={Aries:['Your public path calls for courage and leadership. You are seen as a pioneer.','With Aries on the Midheaven you are drawn to work where you can lead, start things and compete: running your own venture, physical or protective work, campaigning. Your reputation is built on initiative.','Courage and success spells at noon on a Tuesday; carnelian on the desk.'],Taurus:['Your public path is steady and practical. You are seen as reliable and grounded.','Taurus on the Midheaven draws you to work that builds lasting value: finance, land, food, craft, music and beauty. Your reputation grows slowly and holds.','Prosperity work on a Friday; a green candle and a coin on the altar.'],Gemini:['Your public path involves words and ideas. You are seen as clever and versatile.','Gemini on the Midheaven suits teaching, writing, media, trade and anything with variety. You may have more than one career.','Word magic on a Wednesday; write your aim in yellow ink.'],Cancer:['Your public path involves care. You are seen as nurturing and protective.','Cancer on the Midheaven draws you to caring professions, homes, food, history and family business. Your public life often grows from your private one.','Moon magic on a Monday; moon water to anoint your work tools.'],Leo:['Your public path calls you to shine. You are seen as warm and creative.','Leo on the Midheaven suits leadership, the arts, performance and work with children. You want to be recognised for what you create.','Sun magic at noon on a Sunday; gold candles and sunflowers.'],Virgo:['Your public path is skilled service. You are seen as capable and precise.','Virgo on the Midheaven draws you to health, crafts, analysis and work that improves things. Your reputation rests on competence.','Mercury magic on a Wednesday; herbs bundled for good work.'],Libra:['Your public path involves people and beauty. You are seen as fair and gracious.','Libra on the Midheaven suits law, art, design, diplomacy and partnership work. You do best in collaboration.','Venus magic on a Friday; balanced pairs of candles.'],Scorpio:['Your public path goes deep. You are seen as intense and capable.','Scorpio on the Midheaven draws you to research, healing, finance, crisis work and the hidden. Your reputation is built on depth and trust.','Protection and power work on a Tuesday or at the dark moon.'],Sagittarius:['Your public path is about meaning and horizons. You are seen as wise or adventurous.','Sagittarius on the Midheaven suits teaching, publishing, law, travel and faith. You want work with a larger purpose.','Jupiter magic on a Thursday; bay leaves for success.'],Capricorn:['Your public path is ambitious and enduring. You are seen as an authority.','Capricorn on the Midheaven draws you to leadership, institutions and long careers built step by step. Its own sign on its own house: ambition is natural to you.','Saturn magic on a Saturday; a black candle for endurance.'],Aquarius:['Your public path is original. You are seen as an innovator or reformer.','Aquarius on the Midheaven suits technology, science, community and causes. You may change careers suddenly.','Change and community magic; storm water and clear quartz.'],Pisces:['Your public path is compassionate or artistic. You are seen as gentle and inspired.','Pisces on the Midheaven draws you to the arts, healing, spirituality and service. Your calling may be hard to name but strongly felt.','Neptune and Jupiter magic; sea water and amethyst.']};const c=['first','second','third','fourth','fifth','sixth','seventh','eighth','ninth','tenth','eleventh','twelfth'],l=(function(){const l={};for(const t of o.SIGNS){const[c,p]=u[t],f=o.TRADITIONAL_RULER[t];l[s.keys.pointInSign('Part of Fortune',t)]={simple:c,detailed:`${p}\n\nThe Part of Fortune is the oldest of the lots used by ancient astrologers: the Moon's distance from the Sun, measured from the Ascendant (reversed in a night chart). It shows the body, wellbeing and the material luck that comes to you. Its ruler, here ${f}, shows by its sign and house how that fortune arrives.`,magic:`Charge a coin or charm for luck under the ${t} moon and carry it; ${f}'s day and hour suit fortune work for you.`,sources:'Vettius Valens, Anthology II; Paulus Alexandrinus, Introduction.'};const[y,b,w]=h[t];l[s.keys.pointInSign('Midheaven',t)]=(0,n.deepenBig)({simple:y,detailed:`${b}\n\nThe Midheaven is the point of the zodiac culminating (crossing the meridian, due south in the northern hemisphere) at your birth: vocation, reputation and the life you build in public. It is not always the point straight overhead.`,magic:w},'Midheaven',t)}for(const o of t.HOUSE_MEANINGS)l[s.keys.pointInHouse('Part of Fortune',o.house)]={simple:`Your fortune and wellbeing are found in the matters of the ${o.name.toLowerCase().replace(/^the /,'')}: ${o.keywords.slice(0,3).join(', ')}.`,detailed:`With the Part of Fortune in the ${c[o.house-1]} house, luck, comfort and bodily wellbeing gather around ${o.keywords.slice(0,4).join(', ')}. Ancient astrologers also counted houses from the Part of Fortune itself: the eleventh from it was the place of acquisition, and planets there showed how wealth comes.\n\n${'angular'===o.kind?'An angular house gives the Part strength and visibility.':'succedent'===o.kind?'A succedent house gives the Part steadiness: fortune that accumulates.':'A cadent house makes the Part quieter: fortune that comes through work, learning or behind the scenes.'}`,magic:`Prosperity and wellbeing work aimed at ${o.keywords.slice(0,2).join(' and ')}: ${o.magic}`};return l})()},3082,[2705,3048,897,3046]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"RISING_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n={Aries:{simple:'With Aries rising you meet the world head-first: quick, frank and ready to begin. People see you as energetic and brave.',detailed:'Aries on the Ascendant gives a direct, active manner and often a quick walk and a strong presence. You approach life as a series of challenges and start things easily. Mars is your chart ruler: its sign and house show where your life\'s energy is directed.\n\nThe lesson of this rising is patience and listening; the gift is courage that gets things going for everyone.',magic:'Mars is your planetary ally: Tuesdays, Mars hours, red candles, iron, basil, nettle, garnet. Protection and courage spells come naturally.',shadow:'Coming across as rushed, combative or careless.'},Taurus:{simple:'With Taurus rising you come across calm, steady and warm. People find you trustworthy, grounded and easy to be near.',detailed:'Taurus on the Ascendant gives a relaxed, unhurried manner, often a love of comfort and a good eye for beauty. You take life at your own pace and build security around you. Venus is your chart ruler: its sign and house show what draws you and what you build your life around.\n\nThe lesson is flexibility; the gift is steadiness others can rest on.',magic:'Venus is your planetary ally: Fridays, Venus hours, green and pink, copper, rose, vervain, rose quartz. Prosperity and home magic come naturally.',shadow:'Coming across as stubborn or slow to move.'},Gemini:{simple:'With Gemini rising you meet people with curiosity and conversation. You come across lively, witty and quick.',detailed:'Gemini on the Ascendant gives an animated, youthful manner and a mind that is always gathering. You approach life by asking, talking and trying things. Mercury is your chart ruler: its sign and house show where your curiosity leads.\n\nThe lesson is focus; the gift is connecting people and ideas.',magic:'Mercury is your planetary ally: Wednesdays, Mercury hours, yellow and mixed colours, lavender, mint, agate. Word and divination magic come naturally.',shadow:'Seeming scattered or hard to pin down.'},Cancer:{simple:'With Cancer rising you come across gentle and caring, a little guarded at first. People feel looked after around you.',detailed:'Cancer on the Ascendant gives a soft, receptive manner, sensitive to atmosphere, and a protective outer shell. You approach life cautiously, testing whether it is safe, then give wholeheartedly. The Moon is your chart ruler: its sign, phase and house matter greatly for you.\n\nThe lesson is to let your strength show; the gift is making others feel at home.',magic:'The Moon is your planetary ally: Mondays, Moon hours, silver and white, moonstone, jasmine, mugwort. Every phase of the Moon is a timing tool for you.',shadow:'Seeming moody or withdrawn.'},Leo:{simple:'With Leo rising you arrive warmly and get noticed. You come across confident, generous and bright.',detailed:'Leo on the Ascendant gives a warm, dignified presence and often a striking look. You approach life as something to create and to share generously. The Sun is your chart ruler: its sign and house show where you are meant to shine.\n\nThe lesson is humility without dimming; the gift is lighting up a room.',magic:'The Sun is your planetary ally: Sundays, Sun hours, gold and orange, sunstone, calendula, bay. Confidence and success magic come naturally.',shadow:'Coming across as proud or attention-seeking.'},Virgo:{simple:'With Virgo rising you come across thoughtful, capable and modest. People see you as the one who notices what needs doing.',detailed:'Virgo on the Ascendant gives a neat, observant, helpful manner and often a youthful, careful presence. You approach life by analysing and improving. Mercury is your chart ruler: its sign and house show where your skill is put to use.\n\nThe lesson is self-acceptance; the gift is making things work.',magic:'Mercury is your planetary ally: Wednesdays, Mercury hours, fennel, lavender, amazonite. Herbcraft, healing and practical magic come naturally.',shadow:'Seeming critical or anxious.'},Libra:{simple:'With Libra rising you meet the world with charm and tact. You come across graceful, pleasant and fair.',detailed:'Libra on the Ascendant gives an easy, gracious manner and often a love of style and beauty. You approach life through relationship, seeking balance in every room. Venus is your chart ruler: its sign and house show what you love and how you connect.\n\nThe lesson is decisiveness; the gift is bringing people together.',magic:'Venus is your planetary ally: Fridays, Venus hours, pink and pale blue, rose, violet, rose quartz. Love, harmony and glamour magic come naturally.',shadow:'Seeming indecisive or too eager to please.'},Scorpio:{simple:'With Scorpio rising you come across quiet and intense. You read a room before you show yourself, and people sense your depth.',detailed:'Scorpio on the Ascendant gives a magnetic, watchful presence and a strong privacy. You approach life cautiously and deeply, and you are hard to fool. Mars (traditional) and Pluto (modern) are your chart rulers: their signs and houses show where your power goes.\n\nThe lesson is openness; the gift is the courage to face what is real.',magic:'Mars and Pluto are your allies: Tuesdays, Mars hours, black and deep red, obsidian, garnet. Protection, shadow work and transformation come naturally.',shadow:'Seeming secretive or intimidating.'},Sagittarius:{simple:'With Sagittarius rising you meet life openly and with humour. You come across friendly, frank and adventurous.',detailed:'Sagittarius on the Ascendant gives an open, expansive manner and a restless love of horizons. You approach life as a journey and a search for meaning. Jupiter is your chart ruler: its sign and house show where your luck and faith grow.\n\nThe lesson is follow-through; the gift is hope that is catching.',magic:'Jupiter is your planetary ally: Thursdays, Jupiter hours, royal blue and purple, tin, sage, clove, lapis. Luck, travel and devotional magic come naturally.',shadow:'Seeming tactless or restless.'},Capricorn:{simple:'With Capricorn rising you come across composed and serious, someone who means what they say. People trust your competence.',detailed:'Capricorn on the Ascendant gives a reserved, dignified manner, often looking older when young and younger when old. You approach life with a plan and a long view. Saturn is your chart ruler: its sign and house show where you build your life\'s work.\n\nThe lesson is lightness; the gift is endurance.',magic:'Saturn is your planetary ally: Saturdays, Saturn hours, black and indigo, onyx, jet, cypress. Boundary, protection and long-term magic come naturally.',shadow:'Seeming cold or guarded.'},Aquarius:{simple:'With Aquarius rising you meet the world as yourself: friendly, a little apart and hard to predict.',detailed:'Aquarius on the Ascendant gives an independent, unusual presence and an open, friendly manner that keeps some distance. You approach life by questioning and doing it your own way. Saturn (traditional) and Uranus (modern) are your chart rulers: their signs and houses show how you build and how you break the mould.\n\nThe lesson is closeness; the gift is originality.',magic:'Saturn and Uranus are your allies: Saturdays, Saturn hours, electric blue, aquamarine, labradorite. Community, freedom and breaking-free magic come naturally.',shadow:'Seeming aloof or contrary.'},Pisces:{simple:'With Pisces rising you come across soft, kind and dreamy, catching moods before words.',detailed:'Pisces on the Ascendant gives a gentle, receptive presence, often a faraway look and a chameleon quality. You approach life intuitively, feeling your way. Jupiter (traditional) and Neptune (modern) are your chart rulers: their signs and houses show where your faith and dreams lead.\n\nThe lesson is boundaries; the gift is compassion that others feel at once.',magic:'Jupiter and Neptune are your allies: Thursdays, Jupiter hours, sea-green and lavender, amethyst, mugwort. Dream, water and divination magic come naturally.',shadow:'Seeming vague or easily swayed.'}}},3083,[]);
__d(function(g,_r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"RULER_PLANETS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"RULER_READINGS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return l}});var r=_r(d[0]),n=_r(d[1]);const o={Sun:{rising:'Leo',simple:'With Leo rising, the Sun rules your chart: your life is steered by purpose, warmth and the wish to shine.',detailed:'The Sun as chart ruler makes the whole chart turn on identity and vitality: you live best when you are wholehearted, creative and visible. Its sign and house show where you are meant to shine, and your health follows your sense of purpose.',style:'by shining, leading and creating',magic:'The Sun is your personal ruler: Sundays, the hour of the Sun, gold and sunflowers are always yours to call on.'},Moon:{rising:'Cancer',simple:'With Cancer rising, the Moon rules your chart: your life follows feeling, care and the tides of your moods.',detailed:'The Moon as chart ruler makes the whole chart responsive and changeable: your direction shifts with your needs and the people you care for. Its sign, house and phase at birth say a great deal about your life, and the monthly Moon cycle will affect you more than most.',style:'by caring, sensing and belonging',magic:'The Moon is your personal ruler: Mondays, the lunar phases, silver and moon water are always yours.'},Mercury:{rising:'Gemini or Virgo',simple:'With Gemini or Virgo rising, Mercury rules your chart: your life is steered by curiosity, learning and skill.',detailed:'Mercury as chart ruler makes the mind the engine of your life: you find your way by thinking, talking, studying and making. Its sign and house show what you most need to learn and where you use your wits; its retrogrades will often be noticeable for you.',style:'by learning, speaking and making',magic:'Mercury is your personal ruler: Wednesdays, the hour of Mercury, ink, agate and lavender are always yours.'},Venus:{rising:'Taurus or Libra',simple:'With Taurus or Libra rising, Venus rules your chart: your life is steered by love, beauty, pleasure and relationships.',detailed:'Venus as chart ruler makes harmony and value central: you find your way through relationships, art and what you love. Its sign and house show where you seek beauty and connection, and how you attract what you need.',style:'by loving, harmonising and enjoying',magic:'Venus is your personal ruler: Fridays, the hour of Venus, roses, copper and rose quartz are always yours.'},Mars:{rising:'Aries (or Scorpio, traditionally)',simple:'With Aries (or, traditionally, Scorpio) rising, Mars rules your chart: your life is steered by drive, courage and challenge.',detailed:'Mars as chart ruler makes action the theme of your life: you find your way by doing, competing and defending. Its sign and house show where you fight, and where your energy goes; looking after your body and your temper matters.',style:'by acting, striving and protecting',magic:'Mars is your personal ruler: Tuesdays, the hour of Mars, red candles, iron and carnelian are always yours.'},Jupiter:{rising:'Sagittarius (or Pisces, traditionally)',simple:'With Sagittarius (or, traditionally, Pisces) rising, Jupiter rules your chart: your life is steered by faith, growth and the search for meaning.',detailed:'Jupiter as chart ruler gives an expansive life direction: you find your way through learning, travel, generosity and belief. Its sign and house show where you grow and where luck tends to find you.',style:'by seeking, teaching and growing',magic:'Jupiter is your personal ruler: Thursdays, the hour of Jupiter, blue and purple, oak and sage are always yours.'},Saturn:{rising:'Capricorn (or Aquarius, traditionally)',simple:'With Capricorn (or, traditionally, Aquarius) rising, Saturn rules your chart: your life is steered by responsibility, effort and time.',detailed:'Saturn as chart ruler gives a life that matures with age: you find your way through discipline, structure and earned authority, and often feel younger as you grow older. Its sign and house show where you build and what you must master.',style:'by building, enduring and mastering',magic:'Saturn is your personal ruler: Saturdays, the hour of Saturn, black candles, salt and onyx are always yours.'},Uranus:{rising:'Aquarius (in modern astrology)',simple:'With Aquarius rising, modern astrologers name Uranus as co-ruler beside Saturn: your life is steered by freedom, originality and change.',detailed:'Uranus as modern chart ruler adds a need to be different and to break new ground. Traditional astrologers read Saturn alone; many modern readers weigh both, Saturn for structure and Uranus for the sudden turns.',style:'by innovating, rebelling and freeing',magic:'Uranus adds storm water, clear quartz and sudden inspiration to your personal magic.'},Neptune:{rising:'Pisces (in modern astrology)',simple:'With Pisces rising, modern astrologers name Neptune as co-ruler beside Jupiter: your life is steered by imagination, compassion and spirit.',detailed:'Neptune as modern chart ruler adds a dreamy, porous quality to your life\'s direction. Traditional astrologers read Jupiter alone; many modern readers weigh both, Jupiter for faith and growth and Neptune for vision and surrender.',style:'by dreaming, healing and dissolving',magic:'Neptune adds sea water, amethyst and dreamwork to your personal magic.'},Pluto:{rising:'Scorpio (in modern astrology)',simple:'With Scorpio rising, modern astrologers name Pluto as co-ruler beside Mars: your life is steered by depth, power and transformation.',detailed:'Pluto as modern chart ruler adds intensity and repeated rebirths to your life\'s direction. Traditional astrologers read Mars alone; many modern readers weigh both, Mars for courage and Pluto for depth.',style:'by transforming, uncovering and renewing',magic:'Pluto adds obsidian, the dark moon and shadow work to your personal magic.'}},s=Object.keys(o),t=['first','second','third','fourth','fifth','sixth','seventh','eighth','ninth','tenth','eleventh','twelfth'],u=['Life is about you: your body, your presence and becoming yourself. You are your own project, and your personality is hard to miss.','Life is drawn to resources and worth: earning, owning, building security and knowing what you value.','Life is drawn to learning, talking, writing and your local world: siblings, neighbours and the daily round.','Life is drawn home: family, roots, property and the private self. Many with this placement come into their own later in life.','Life is drawn to creativity, pleasure, romance and children: making things and enjoying them.','Life is drawn to work, service, health and craft: being useful and doing things well.','Life is drawn to others: partnership, marriage, collaboration and the people who mirror you.','Life is drawn to depth: intimacy, shared resources, crisis, death and rebirth, and the hidden.','Life is drawn to the far horizon: travel, study, faith, philosophy and teaching.','Life is drawn to career and public life: achievement, reputation and leaving a mark.','Life is drawn to friends, groups and causes: community, networks and hopes for the future.','Life is drawn inward and behind the scenes: solitude, spirit, retreat, healing and the unseen.'];const l=(function(){const l={};for(const h of s){const s=o[h];l[n.keys.chartRuler(h)]={simple:s.simple,detailed:`${s.detailed}\n\nThe chart ruler is the planet that rules your rising sign (${s.rising}). Ancient astrologers called it the ruler of the Hour, and read its condition (its sign, house, speed and aspects) as the condition of the whole life.`,magic:s.magic};for(const o of r.HOUSE_MEANINGS){const r=o.house;l[n.keys.rulerInHouse(h,r)]={simple:`${h} rules your chart from the ${t[r-1]} house. ${u[r-1]}`,detailed:`${u[r-1]} You meet it ${s.style}: ${h}'s way.\n\nThe chart ruler's house is where the whole chart is "sent": the area of life your rising sign's energy is spent on. ${'angular'===o.kind?'An angular house makes the ruler strong and visible.':'succedent'===o.kind?'A succedent house makes the ruler steady and accumulating.':'A cadent house makes the ruler work through learning, service or quiet adjustment.'} Read this with ${h}'s sign and aspects.`,magic:`${s.magic} Aim your personal workings at ${o.keywords.slice(0,3).join(', ')}. ${o.magic}`}}}return l})()},3084,[897,3046]);
__d(function(g,r,_i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SIGN_ON_CUSP_BY_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SIGN_ON_CUSP",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return f}});var _=r(d[0]),P=r(d[1]),E=r(d[2]),S=r(d[3]),C=r(d[4]),U=r(d[5]),t=r(d[6]),n=r(d[7]),D=r(d[8]),R=r(d[9]),u=r(d[10]),c=r(d[11]);const i=[U.CUSP_1_DEEPER,U.CUSP_2_DEEPER,U.CUSP_3_DEEPER,t.CUSP_4_DEEPER,t.CUSP_5_DEEPER,t.CUSP_6_DEEPER,n.CUSP_7_DEEPER,D.CUSP_8_DEEPER,R.CUSP_9_DEEPER,R.CUSP_10_DEEPER,R.CUSP_11_DEEPER,R.CUSP_12_DEEPER],o=[P.CUSP_1,P.CUSP_2,P.CUSP_3,E.CUSP_4,E.CUSP_5,E.CUSP_6,S.CUSP_7,S.CUSP_8,S.CUSP_9,C.CUSP_10,C.CUSP_11,C.CUSP_12].map((P,E)=>Object.fromEntries(_.SIGNS.map(_=>[_,(0,u.deepen)(P[_],i[E][_])]))),f=Object.fromEntries(o.flatMap((P,E)=>_.SIGNS.map(_=>[c.keys.signOnCusp(E+1,_),P[_]])))},3085,[2705,3086,3087,3088,3089,3090,3091,3092,3093,3094,3069,3046]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_1",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_2",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_3",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const o={Aries:{simple:"Aries on the first cusp makes you meet life head-on, quick to act and slow to wait.",detailed:"The door you walk through into every situation is a fiery one: you arrive moving, you say what you think, and you take the first step before most people have stood up. Mars rules your Ascendant, so Mars's sign and house show where your vitality goes and how you defend yourself. Your body may run hot, and you recover quickly.",magic:"Begin self-work on a Tuesday or at the Aries new Moon; a red candle and Carnelian make a simple personal altar for courage."},Taurus:{simple:"Taurus on the first cusp gives a calm, steady, sensual way of meeting the world.",detailed:"You take your time to arrive, and when you do, you bring a sense of ease and solidity that steadies others. People trust you. Venus rules your Ascendant, so Venus's sign and house show what makes you feel most like yourself: beauty, comfort, a particular pleasure or value.",magic:"Self-blessing with oils, flowers and a slow bath on a Friday suits you; Rose Quartz and rose make a gentle personal altar."},Gemini:{simple:"Gemini on the first cusp makes you curious, quick and talkative as you meet the world.",detailed:"You meet life with questions, often with a quick smile and quicker words, and you can seem younger than your years. Mercury rules your Ascendant, so Mercury's sign and house show where your restless mind leads your whole life.",magic:"Personal sigils and spoken charms suit you; Wednesday and Mercury hours are your self-work times, with Citrine and lavender close by."},Cancer:{simple:"Cancer on the first cusp gives a gentle, protective and sensitive way of meeting the world.",detailed:"You approach new situations cautiously, sensing the mood before you open up, and you often look after people instinctively. The Moon rules your Ascendant, so its sign, house and phase say a great deal about your whole temperament and how your moods colour your days.",magic:"Moon-timed self-care is your craft: a Monday bath, moon water on the brow, Moonstone worn close."},Leo:{simple:"Leo on the first cusp gives a warm, bright, generous presence that people notice.",detailed:"You walk into a room as if you belong there, and you usually make others feel welcome too. Pride and dignity matter to you. The Sun rules your Ascendant, so the Sun's house shows where you are most meant to shine, and your Sun sign gains extra weight.",magic:"Sunday glamour and confidence spells suit you; Sunstone, Calendula and a gold candle make a personal sun altar."},Virgo:{simple:"Virgo on the first cusp gives a careful, modest and observant way of meeting the world.",detailed:"You notice details others miss and tend to be useful before you are noticed. You may seem reserved, neat or quietly competent. Mercury rules your Ascendant, so its sign and house show where your discerning mind directs your life.",magic:"Cleansing rituals and herbal self-care suit you, especially on Wednesdays; Amazonite and lavender calm the inner critic."},Libra:{simple:"Libra on the first cusp gives a graceful, charming and diplomatic way of meeting the world.",detailed:"You make people feel at ease, you care how things look and sound, and you often see both sides before you take one. Venus rules your Ascendant, so Venus's sign and house show what brings your life into balance.",magic:"Beauty rituals and balance spells suit you on Fridays; Rose Quartz and a pair of matched candles make a good personal altar."},Scorpio:{simple:"Scorpio on the first cusp gives a private, intense and perceptive way of meeting the world.",detailed:"You read people quickly and reveal yourself slowly. Others may find you magnetic or hard to read. Mars rules your Ascendant traditionally and Pluto in modern astrology; Mars's house shows where your power is directed, Pluto's where it is deepened.",magic:"Protective and transformation work suits you, especially at the dark Moon; Obsidian and a black candle make a strong personal ward."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Sagittarius on the first cusp gives an open, adventurous and optimistic way of meeting the world.",detailed:"You approach life as a journey, often with humour and frankness, and you need room to roam. Jupiter rules your Ascendant, so Jupiter's sign and house show where your life finds its meaning and luck. People often meet you laughing, and you may look as if you are about to set off somewhere.",magic:"Luck and travel blessings suit you on Thursdays; Turquoise and a sprig of Sage make a lucky personal charm."},Capricorn:{simple:"Capricorn on the first cusp gives a serious, capable and reserved way of meeting the world.",detailed:"You may seem older or more composed than those around you, and you approach life with a plan. Respect matters. Saturn rules your Ascendant, so Saturn's sign and house show where your life's effort and mastery are centred.",magic:"Protection and long-term goal magic suit you on Saturdays; Onyx and cypress make a steady personal ward."},Aquarius:{simple:"Aquarius on the first cusp gives an independent, friendly and slightly unusual way of meeting the world.",detailed:"You come across as your own person, open to everyone and owned by no one. Saturn rules your Ascendant traditionally and Uranus in modern astrology; Saturn shows what you build, Uranus where you break the mould.",magic:"Invented rituals and personal sigils suit you; Amethyst and Labradorite on a Saturday make a clear personal altar."},Pisces:{simple:"Pisces on the first cusp gives a gentle, dreamy and compassionate way of meeting the world.",detailed:"You absorb the atmosphere around you and often reflect back what others feel. You may seem soft, mysterious or artistic. Jupiter rules your Ascendant traditionally and Neptune in modern astrology; their houses show where your compassion and dreams lead your life.",magic:"Cleansing baths and protective veiling suit you, especially on Thursdays and Mondays; Amethyst and Aquamarine keep your edges clear."}},s={Aries:{simple:"Aries on the second cusp: you earn by initiative and spend on impulse.",detailed:"Money comes through effort, competition and being first: starting your own thing, selling, physical or pioneering work. Spending can be quick and impulsive. Mars rules this house for you, so Mars's place shows where your income is won.",magic:"Money spells with a red and a green candle on a Tuesday suit you; Carnelian and cinnamon spark income."},Taurus:{simple:"Taurus on the second cusp: you build wealth slowly and value quality and comfort.",detailed:"Taurus is at home here. You tend to save, invest in lasting things and earn steadily, often through beauty, food, land or craft. Venus rules your second house, so Venus's place shows where money and pleasure meet.",magic:"A money jar fed every Friday and a blessed purse suit you; Green Aventurine and patchouli draw slow plenty."},Gemini:{simple:"Gemini on the second cusp: you earn through words, ideas and variety, often from more than one source.",detailed:"Income may come through writing, teaching, sales, trade or several jobs at once. You value information and connection. Mercury rules your second house, so its place shows where your wits earn. You may keep money in several pots and change how you earn more than once; a simple record keeps it from scattering.",magic:"Written prosperity petitions on Wednesdays suit you; Citrine and basil help."},Cancer:{simple:"Cancer on the second cusp: money is tied to feeling safe, family and home.",detailed:"You may earn through caring, food, property or family business, and save carefully for security. Income can ebb and flow. The Moon rules your second house, so its place shows where you find financial safety.",magic:"Prosperity spells begun at the new Moon and grown through the waxing suit you; Moonstone and a bowl of rice on the altar help."},Leo:{simple:"Leo on the second cusp: you earn through creativity and leadership, and you like to spend generously.",detailed:"Money may come through performance, management or creative work, and you value things that let you shine. Generosity can outrun income. The Sun rules your second house, so its place shows where you earn your gold.",magic:"Sunday success spells with a gold candle suit you; Citrine and Sunflower draw golden income."},Virgo:{simple:"Virgo on the second cusp: you earn through skill, service and attention to detail, and manage money carefully.",detailed:"Income often comes from practical work, health, craft or analysis, and you keep good accounts. Worry about money is the thing to watch. Mercury rules your second house, so its place shows where your skill earns.",magic:"A carefully kept money ledger blessed each new Moon suits you; Amazonite and Moss Agate help."},Libra:{simple:"Libra on the second cusp: you earn through partnership, beauty and good relations.",detailed:"Money may come through design, art, law, clients or a partner, and you value fairness and beauty. Venus rules your second house, so its place shows where money and harmony meet. Spending on beauty, clothes and gifts comes easily, and money matters can affect your relationships, so fairness about who pays matters to you.",magic:"Honey-sweetened money spells on Fridays suit you; Rose Quartz and Green Aventurine together help."},Scorpio:{simple:"Scorpio on the second cusp: money is intense, private and tied to shared resources and power.",detailed:"You may earn through research, finance, investment or crisis work, and guard your resources closely. Gains and losses can be dramatic. Mars and Pluto rule your second house; their places show where your resources transform.",magic:"Prosperity and protection magic at the dark Moon suits you; Obsidian and Pyrite together guard and draw."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Sagittarius on the second cusp: money comes generously and goes generously.",detailed:"Income may come through teaching, travel, publishing or law, and you value freedom more than security. Overspending in optimism is the risk. Jupiter rules your second house, so its place shows where your luck with money lies.",magic:"Thursday luck spells suit you; Citrine and nutmeg draw expansive fortune."},Capricorn:{simple:"Capricorn on the second cusp: you build wealth slowly and carefully, often through long-term work.",detailed:"You save, plan and earn through steady effort and expertise. Security matters a great deal. Saturn rules your second house, so its place shows where your resources are built. You may have known lean times early and learned thrift that served you well. Wealth often grows in the second half of life.",magic:"A Saturday money jar fed patiently suits you; Pyrite and cypress support lasting wealth."},Aquarius:{simple:"Aquarius on the second cusp: you earn in unusual ways and value freedom over security.",detailed:"Money may come through technology, innovation or group work, and income can be irregular. Saturn and Uranus rule your second house; Saturn's place shows how you build, Uranus's where money surprises you.",magic:"Sigils for income and experimental money magic suit you; Labradorite and Green Aventurine help."},Pisces:{simple:"Pisces on the second cusp: money and values are fluid, generous and sometimes unclear.",detailed:"Income may come through art, healing or spiritual work, and you may give freely. Clear records protect you. Jupiter and Neptune rule your second house; their places show where your money flows. You may undervalue your gifts or give them away; learning to charge fairly for inspired work is part of the path.",magic:"Prosperity spells with clarity built in suit you; Amethyst and Green Aventurine together help."}},n={Aries:{simple:"Aries on the third cusp: you think fast, speak bluntly and learn by doing.",detailed:"Conversation is lively and sometimes combative, and you rush about your neighbourhood. Siblings may be competitive. Mars rules your third house, so its place shows where your words have force. You may drive fast, walk fast and finish other people's sentences, and arguments with brothers or sisters may have sharpened your wit.",magic:"Courage-to-speak spells on Tuesdays suit you; Carnelian at the throat helps."},Taurus:{simple:"Taurus on the third cusp: you think slowly, speak calmly and learn through the senses.",detailed:"You learn best by handling things and repeating them, and your words are measured. Siblings and neighbours are steady presences. Venus rules your third house, so its place shows where your mind finds pleasure.",magic:"Slow, repeated charms spoken over seven nights suit you; Green Aventurine helps."},Gemini:{simple:"Gemini on the third cusp: your mind is quick, curious and endlessly busy.",detailed:"Gemini is at home here. You love talk, books and short trips, and you may write or teach. Mercury rules your third house, so its place shows how your mind travels. Many people with this cusp are gifted writers, translators, teachers or simply the best-informed person on the street. Siblings may be close in age and in mind.",magic:"Letter spells and divination on Wednesdays suit you; Citrine and peppermint help."},Cancer:{simple:"Cancer on the third cusp: you think with feeling and remember everything.",detailed:"Your mind is shaped by memory and mood, and family talk matters. Siblings may feel like parents, or need you as one. The Moon rules your third house, so its place shows where your mind finds safety. Letters, family stories and conversations at the kitchen table are where your mind feels at home.",magic:"A moon journal and family stories as spells suit you; Moonstone helps."},Leo:{simple:"Leo on the third cusp: you speak with warmth and flair and love to tell a story.",detailed:"Your communication is dramatic, generous and confident. You may teach, perform or write creatively. The Sun rules your third house, so its place shows where your words shine. School may have been a stage, and you may still remember a teacher who believed in you. You learn best when you can show what you know.",magic:"Spoken confidence charms on Sundays suit you; Sunstone helps."},Virgo:{simple:"Virgo on the third cusp: you think precisely and communicate carefully.",detailed:"You notice detail, edit well and learn methodically. Worry can loop in the mind. Mercury rules your third house, so its place shows how your careful mind works. You may be the family's note-taker or editor, and you notice errors on menus and signs whether you want to or not. Lists calm you.",magic:"Carefully worded petitions and study blessings on Wednesdays suit you; Fluorite helps."},Libra:{simple:"Libra on the third cusp: you speak diplomatically and think in terms of balance.",detailed:"Your words are gracious and you see both sides. Relationships with siblings and neighbours matter, and you dislike conflict nearby. Venus rules your third house, so its place shows where your words find harmony.",magic:"Sweetening spells for neighbours or siblings on Fridays suit you; Blue Lace Agate helps."},Scorpio:{simple:"Scorpio on the third cusp: your mind is deep, private and searching.",detailed:"You say less than you know, and your words cut to the truth. Siblings may hold secrets or intensity. Mars and Pluto rule your third house; their places show where your mind digs. Gossip does not interest you; secrets do. You may be drawn to research, puzzles and the psychology of the people around you.",magic:"Written banishings and scrying suit you; Obsidian helps."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Sagittarius on the third cusp: you think big and speak frankly.",detailed:"You love ideas, travel and big conversations, and you may talk in principles rather than details. Jupiter rules your third house, so its place shows where your mind finds meaning. You may live far from siblings, or treat your own neighbourhood as somewhere to explore. Learning languages can come easily.",magic:"Bibliomancy and travel blessings on Thursdays suit you; Turquoise helps."},Capricorn:{simple:"Capricorn on the third cusp: you think carefully and speak with authority.",detailed:"Your communication is structured and serious, and early learning may have been hard work. Saturn rules your third house, so its place shows where your mind builds. You may have been the serious child, or had a sibling to look after. Over time your words gain weight and people listen.",magic:"A daily writing practice as ritual on Saturdays suits you; Onyx helps."},Aquarius:{simple:"Aquarius on the third cusp: your mind is original and independent.",detailed:"You think in systems and ideas, and your communication can be unusual. Saturn and Uranus rule your third house; their places show where your mind breaks new ground. You may have learned differently at school, or found your own way through books and machines. Neighbours may become a community you organise.",magic:"Digital sigils and new divination methods suit you; Labradorite helps."},Pisces:{simple:"Pisces on the third cusp: your mind is intuitive, poetic and imaginative.",detailed:"You think in images and feelings, and details can slip. You may write poetry or music. Jupiter and Neptune rule your third house; their places show where your mind dreams. School may have felt like a dream you drifted through, and yet you remember stories, songs and images others forget.",magic:"Automatic writing and dream journals suit you; Amethyst helps."}}},3086,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_4",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_5",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_6",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const o={Aries:{simple:"Aries on the fourth cusp makes home a lively, busy and sometimes heated place, and your roots a source of fire.",detailed:"Home is where you recharge by doing: renovating, rearranging, moving on when a place no longer fits. Early family life may have prized independence or held a good deal of argument, and you may have learned young to stand up for yourself under your own roof. As an adult you often want a home that is truly yours, run your way. Mars rules this house for you, so Mars's sign and house show where your energy at home goes and what you are defending.",magic:"Threshold protection on a Tuesday suits you: iron by the door, Black Tourmaline on the sill, and a red candle lit to bless the hearth after any family quarrel."},Taurus:{simple:"Taurus on the fourth cusp makes home a place of comfort, beauty and stability, somewhere to put down deep roots.",detailed:"You need a solid, sensual home: good bed, good food, perhaps a garden or a view of growing things. Many people with this cusp stay in one place a long time, or keep family furniture and recipes for decades. The roots you come from may have valued security, land or thrift. Venus rules your fourth house, so Venus's sign and house show what makes home feel good to you.",magic:"Home blessings with flowers, bread and salt on a Friday suit you, and a house plant tended as a living charm; Rose Quartz on the hearth keeps the peace."},Gemini:{simple:"Gemini on the fourth cusp fills home with books, talk and comings and goings.",detailed:"Your home is rarely quiet: phones, neighbours, siblings, a desk in every room. Family may have been talkative, restless or split between two households, and you may still keep more than one base or move more often than most. Home is where you think. Mercury rules your fourth house, so its sign and house show how your home life moves and what it is always talking about.",magic:"A written home blessing kept by the door suits you, refreshed each Wednesday; a bundle of lavender and a Citrine on the desk keep a busy home clear."},Cancer:{simple:"Cancer on the fourth cusp makes home and family deeply important and emotionally rich, the centre of your life.",detailed:"Cancer is at home on this cusp. Roots run deep: family memory, inherited recipes, the house you grew up in, the place your people come from. Home is your shell and sanctuary, and you may be the one who keeps the family together. The Moon rules your fourth house, so its sign, house and phase show how you make a home and what you need there to feel safe.",magic:"Ancestor offerings and moon water for the household on Mondays suit you; Moonstone on the kitchen windowsill and a bowl of water refreshed at each full Moon bless the house."},Leo:{simple:"Leo on the fourth cusp makes home warm, proud and generous, a place to gather people around you.",detailed:"You love to host, decorate and make home a stage for the people you love. Family pride runs strong, and a parent may have been a big, bright personality whose approval mattered. Your home needs warmth and light, both literal and emotional. The Sun rules your fourth house, so the Sun's house and sign show where your home's warmth comes from.",magic:"A hearth fire or golden candle blessed on a Sunday suits you, and a gathering of loved ones treated as ritual; Sunstone and Calendula welcome guests."},Virgo:{simple:"Virgo on the fourth cusp makes home orderly, practical and a place of care.",detailed:"You keep a tidy, useful home, often with herbs on the sill, animals underfoot and a place for everything. Family may have valued work, health and good habits, sometimes with a critical edge you still hear. Home is where you restore yourself through small routines. Mercury rules your fourth house, so its place shows how you run your home and where your worries settle.",magic:"Floor washes, herb bundles and a regular clearing of clutter on Wednesdays suit you; rosemary over the door and Amazonite in the kitchen keep home healthy."},Libra:{simple:"Libra on the fourth cusp makes home beautiful, peaceful and shared.",detailed:"You want harmony at home and may put great care into how it looks: colour, balance, art. Family may have valued manners and keeping the peace, sometimes at the cost of saying what was true. You often prefer to share a home rather than live alone. Venus rules your fourth house, so its place shows what brings peace at home.",magic:"Peace and beauty blessings for the home on Fridays suit you; a pair of matched candles and Rose Quartz on the mantel, and a honey jar for household harmony."},Scorpio:{simple:"Scorpio on the fourth cusp makes home private, intense and fiercely protected.",detailed:"Your home is your lair: few people see all of it. Family may have held secrets, strong emotional undercurrents or a crisis that shaped everyone, and you may spend years making peace with your roots. You guard your private life closely. Mars and Pluto rule your fourth house, so their places show where home's power lies.",magic:"Home protection and ancestor healing at the dark Moon suit you; a witch bottle buried near the door, and Obsidian by the bed."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Sagittarius on the fourth cusp makes home open, roaming and full of ideas.",detailed:"You may move far from where you were born, live abroad, or keep an open house full of travellers and books. Family may have valued faith, learning or freedom, and home feels best with a horizon in view. Settling down can feel like a trap unless it leaves room to roam. Jupiter rules your fourth house, so its place shows where home grows.",magic:"Travel and home blessings together on Thursdays suit you; a map or souvenir on the altar, Turquoise by the door, and a sprig of Sage for the journey home."},Capricorn:{simple:"Capricorn on the fourth cusp makes home serious and structured, something you build carefully over time.",detailed:"Family may have been strict, reserved or burdened with duty, and you may have taken responsibility early. As an adult you build your own foundations deliberately, often owning property or keeping traditions. Home becomes truly comfortable later in life. Saturn rules your fourth house, so its place shows how you build your roots.",magic:"Ancestor altars and protective wards on Saturdays suit you; Jet or Smoky Quartz at the foundations, and cypress for the family line."},Aquarius:{simple:"Aquarius on the fourth cusp makes home unusual, free and open to friends.",detailed:"Family may have been unconventional, or you may have felt like the odd one out in it. You may create a chosen family, share a house, or live in an unusual way that gives everyone room. Home needs to accept who you really are. Saturn and Uranus rule your fourth house; their places show how home holds and how it changes.",magic:"Blessings for chosen family and a home altar of your own design suit you; Labradorite and lavender keep a free home calm."},Pisces:{simple:"Pisces on the fourth cusp makes home a sanctuary, dreamy and spiritual.",detailed:"You long for a home that feels like a retreat, perhaps near water, full of music and soft light. Family may have been elusive, idealised, or touched by illness or sorrow, and you may still be untangling what was real. Home is where your spirit rests. Jupiter and Neptune rule your fourth house; their places show where home becomes sacred.",magic:"A home altar with a bowl of water, moon water blessings and regular cleansing suit you; Amethyst by the bed and jasmine in the hall."}},s={Aries:{simple:"Aries on the fifth cusp: you play hard, love boldly and create with fire.",detailed:"Fun is active and competitive: sport, dares, new hobbies taken up with passion. Romance starts fast and wants excitement; creative work comes in bursts of inspiration rather than steady practice. With children you are a lively, adventurous presence. Mars rules your fifth house, so its sign and house show where your joy burns hottest.",magic:"Fire rituals for creative courage on Tuesdays suit you; Carnelian on the desk and a candle lit to begin each new project."},Taurus:{simple:"Taurus on the fifth cusp: your pleasures are sensual, slow and loyal.",detailed:"You enjoy food, music, gardens, craft and touch, and you take time over your pleasures. Romance is steady and physical, and you tend to stay with a creative medium for years. Children are a source of comfort and continuity. Venus rules your fifth house, so its place shows where pleasure lives for you.",magic:"Sensual pleasure rituals on Fridays suit you: a long bath with rose, music, good food; Rose Quartz and patchouli for love that lasts."},Gemini:{simple:"Gemini on the fifth cusp: you play with words, games and ideas.",detailed:"Romance is flirtatious and conversational: you fall for wit. Creativity is verbal and varied, from writing and puzzles to clever crafts, and you may have several projects on the go. You are a playful companion for children. Mercury rules your fifth house, so its place shows how you play.",magic:"Poems as love spells and word games as divination suit you on Wednesdays; Citrine and peppermint keep play bright."},Cancer:{simple:"Cancer on the fifth cusp: joy is tender, nurturing and family-centred.",detailed:"Children, home-based creativity and cooking for people bring delight. Romance is emotional and protective, and you need to feel safe before you can play. Creative work often draws on memory and family. The Moon rules your fifth house, so its place shows where your heart plays.",magic:"Moonlit celebration and fertility blessings suit you; Moonstone and jasmine, and baking as a creative offering."},Leo:{simple:"Leo on the fifth cusp: you love to create, perform and celebrate.",detailed:"Leo is at home on this cusp. Romance is grand and generous, creativity bold, and play a real need rather than a luxury. You may be drawn to performance, children's work or anything with an audience. The Sun rules your fifth house, so its place shows where your joy shines.",magic:"Performance as ritual on Sundays suits you; Sunstone, Sunflower and a party held as a rite of joy."},Virgo:{simple:"Virgo on the fifth cusp: you enjoy skilled crafts and careful, patient creativity.",detailed:"Pleasure comes through making things well: sewing, carpentry, gardening, editing a story until it sings. Romance may be shy and devoted, shown through acts of care rather than grand gestures. The inner critic can spoil fun, so play needs permission to be imperfect. Mercury rules your fifth house, so its place shows how you play.",magic:"Crafting as devotion on Wednesdays suits you; Moss Agate and a handmade charm given in love."},Libra:{simple:"Libra on the fifth cusp: you love romance, beauty and the arts.",detailed:"Creativity is graceful, often visual or musical, and romance is charming and courtly. You enjoy pleasures shared with a partner more than alone, and you have an eye for beauty in everything you make. Venus rules your fifth house, so its place shows where you find delight.",magic:"Love-drawing and beauty spells on Fridays suit you; Rose Quartz and rose, and art made as an offering to Aphrodite."},Scorpio:{simple:"Scorpio on the fifth cusp: romance and creativity are intense and transforming.",detailed:"You love deeply and create from the depths, often drawn to dark, powerful or cathartic art. Romance is all or nothing, and casual flings rarely satisfy. Relationships with children can be intense and protective. Mars and Pluto rule your fifth house; their places show where your passions live.",magic:"Passion and creative catharsis at the dark Moon suit you; Garnet and Damiana, and art made to release what you cannot say."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Sagittarius on the fifth cusp: fun is adventurous, generous and free.",detailed:"You love travel, sport, games of chance and big ideas, and romance needs freedom and laughter. Creative work is often expansive: stories, teaching, philosophy. Children bring out your sense of adventure. Jupiter rules your fifth house, so its place shows where your joy grows.",magic:"Luck for creative ventures on Thursdays suits you; Turquoise and Star Anise, and a blessing before any trip taken for joy."},Capricorn:{simple:"Capricorn on the fifth cusp: you take pleasure seriously and create with discipline.",detailed:"Creativity is crafted slowly and often becomes a real skill or career. Romance is cautious, and you may grow more playful with age. You may feel responsible for children early or deeply. Saturn rules your fifth house, so its place shows where joy has to be earned and then holds.",magic:"A disciplined creative practice blessed on Saturdays suits you; Onyx and Garnet, and a small daily ritual of play."},Aquarius:{simple:"Aquarius on the fifth cusp: creativity is original and romance unconventional.",detailed:"You play with ideas, technology and experiment; your art may be unusual or collective. Romance needs friendship and freedom, and you may love in ways others do not expect. Saturn and Uranus rule your fifth house; their places show where your joy breaks the rules.",magic:"Experimental art as ritual suits you; Labradorite and Amethyst, and a sigil made for creative freedom."},Pisces:{simple:"Pisces on the fifth cusp: creativity is dreamy and romance idealistic.",detailed:"You love music, film, dance and imagination, and fall for ideals as much as people. Creative work flows from feeling and dream. Romance can be magical or disillusioning, so tenderness needs clear eyes. Jupiter and Neptune rule your fifth house; their places show where your joy dreams.",magic:"Music and dance as devotion suit you; Amethyst and jasmine, and a dream journal kept for creative seeds."}},t={Aries:{simple:"Aries on the sixth cusp: you work fast and need active, challenging routines.",detailed:"You do best with goals, deadlines and physical outlets, and you may resent slow colleagues. The body can signal stress through headaches, fevers or minor injuries from rushing. Exercise is medicine for you. Mars rules your sixth house, so its place shows where your work drive goes.",magic:"Exercise as ritual on Tuesdays suits you; Carnelian in your pocket at work, and nettle tea for strength."},Taurus:{simple:"Taurus on the sixth cusp: you work steadily and need comfortable, reliable routines.",detailed:"You do best at a reliable pace, in pleasant surroundings, with good food and rest. Change in routine unsettles you. The throat and neck may need care, and comfort eating is worth watching. Venus rules your sixth house, so its place shows where daily life finds ease.",magic:"Herbal teas and steady routines blessed on Fridays suit you; Green Aventurine at the desk and thyme in the kitchen."},Gemini:{simple:"Gemini on the sixth cusp: you need variety and conversation at work and in daily routine.",detailed:"You juggle tasks well and get bored with repetition. Many people with this cusp do two jobs or switch tasks through the day. Nerves, breathing and the hands may need care when stress builds. Mercury rules your sixth house, so its place shows how you work.",magic:"Lists as spells on Wednesdays suit you; Fluorite on the desk and peppermint for clear breath."},Cancer:{simple:"Cancer on the sixth cusp: you work best in caring, homely settings.",detailed:"Your moods affect your health, especially digestion, and a kind workplace matters more to you than prestige. You may care for others at work, or work from home. The Moon rules your sixth house, so its place shows where daily life feels safe.",magic:"Kitchen healing and moon-timed routines suit you; Moonstone, Chamomile and a nourishing broth made with intention."},Leo:{simple:"Leo on the sixth cusp: you want to shine in daily work.",detailed:"You do best when appreciated and given some creative ownership; dull, unseen work wears you down. The heart and back may need care, and pride can keep you from asking for help. The Sun rules your sixth house, so its place shows where your work shines.",magic:"Sunday blessings for good work suit you; Sunstone at the desk and Calendula for vitality."},Virgo:{simple:"Virgo on the sixth cusp: you are a natural, careful worker who loves routine.",detailed:"Virgo is at home on this cusp. You thrive on order, method and skill, and you notice what others miss. Digestion may react to worry, and perfectionism can turn work into anxiety. Mercury rules your sixth house, so its place shows how your craft works.",magic:"Herbcraft and cleansing on Wednesdays suit you; fennel, Amazonite and a tidy altar kept as a daily practice."},Libra:{simple:"Libra on the sixth cusp: you work best in pleasant, cooperative settings.",detailed:"Harmony with colleagues matters a great deal, and conflict at work can make you unwell. You do well in pairs or partnerships, and in work that beautifies or balances. Balance in diet and rest keeps you well; the kidneys and lower back may need care. Venus rules your sixth house, so its place shows where work finds harmony.",magic:"Workplace sweetening spells on Fridays suit you; Rose Quartz on the desk and a honey jar for good colleagues."},Scorpio:{simple:"Scorpio on the sixth cusp: you work intensely and with deep focus.",detailed:"You are driven and thorough, drawn to research, healing, crisis work or anything others find too hard. Workplace politics can become power struggles. Health can respond strongly to emotional stress, and recovery is often remarkable. Mars and Pluto rule your sixth house; their places show where your work goes deep.",magic:"Deep cleansing and protection at work suit you; Obsidian at the desk and Hyssop for purification."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Sagittarius on the sixth cusp: you need freedom and meaning in daily work.",detailed:"You do best with variety, travel or teaching, and dread tedious routine. Overdoing food, drink or work can strain the hips and liver. A job that feels meaningful keeps you healthy. Jupiter rules your sixth house, so its place shows where work grows.",magic:"Thursday blessings for meaningful work suit you; Turquoise and Sage, and a walk outside as daily devotion."},Capricorn:{simple:"Capricorn on the sixth cusp: you are a disciplined, hard worker.",detailed:"You thrive on structure, responsibility and long-term goals, and you may take on more than your share. Bones, joints, skin and teeth may need care, especially under stress. Rest is part of the work. Saturn rules your sixth house, so its place shows where your work is built.",magic:"Saturday routines and protection at work suit you; Hematite for endurance and comfrey for the bones."},Aquarius:{simple:"Aquarius on the sixth cusp: you need freedom and innovation in work and routine.",detailed:"Flexible, irregular routines suit you better than rigid ones, and you may work remotely, in technology, or for a cause. Circulation and nerves may need care when stress builds. Saturn and Uranus rule your sixth house; their places show how you reinvent work.",magic:"Newly designed routines blessed as rituals suit you; Labradorite and lavender for steady nerves."},Pisces:{simple:"Pisces on the sixth cusp: you serve with compassion and need gentle routines.",detailed:"You may work in care, healing, the arts or anywhere people need kindness. Clear routines are hard and necessary. Sensitivity to substances, medicines and stress needs watching, and the feet may need care. Jupiter and Neptune rule your sixth house; their places show where service flows.",magic:"Ritual baths and a gentle daily devotion suit you; Amethyst and Chamomile, and cleansing after caring for others."}}},3087,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_7",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_8",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_9",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const o={Aries:{simple:"Aries on the seventh cusp draws you to bold, independent partners who bring out your own fire.",detailed:"With Libra rising, you are the diplomat, and you often seek partners who are direct, brave and decisive in the ways you hold back. Relationships can be lively and sometimes competitive; a good partnership gives each of you room to act. In business you work well with someone who will take the first step. Mars rules your seventh house, so Mars's place shows the kind of partner you meet and how you handle conflict with them.",magic:"Courage-in-partnership spells on Tuesdays suit you, and honest words spoken over a red candle when something needs saying; Carnelian and rose together balance fire and love."},Taurus:{simple:"Taurus on the seventh cusp draws you to steady, loyal and sensual partners.",detailed:"With Scorpio rising, you carry intensity, and you look for calm, constancy and simple affection in others. Partnerships are slow to form and long to last, and you value a partner who is reliable with money and kind to your body. Possessiveness on either side is the thing to watch. Venus rules your seventh house, so its place shows what you value in a partner.",magic:"Partnership blessings with honey and bread on Fridays suit you; Rose Quartz and Green Aventurine on a shared altar."},Gemini:{simple:"Gemini on the seventh cusp means you need a partner you can talk to, endlessly.",detailed:"With Sagittarius rising, you bring the big picture, and you seek wit, conversation and variety in others. You may meet partners through study, writing or travel, and you may marry a friend. Relationships stay alive through talk and fade without it. Mercury rules your seventh house, so its place shows the kind of mind that draws you.",magic:"Honest-communication spells for couples on Wednesdays suit you, and love letters kept as charms; Blue Lace Agate helps hard conversations."},Cancer:{simple:"Cancer on the seventh cusp draws you to nurturing, family-minded partners.",detailed:"With Capricorn rising, you lead with competence, and you may look to partners for the tenderness you find hard to show. Partnership often feels like family, and you may build a home together early. Being cared for can feel strange at first, and then essential. The Moon rules your seventh house, so its place shows what makes a partner feel like home.",magic:"Moonlit partnership blessings suit you, and a meal cooked together as ritual; Moonstone on the shared bedside."},Leo:{simple:"Leo on the seventh cusp draws you to warm, confident, radiant partners.",detailed:"With Aquarius rising, you are cool and independent, and you often seek in others the personal warmth and spotlight you may avoid. Partners may be creative, proud or very visible. A good partnership lets you both shine. The Sun rules your seventh house, so its place shows the kind of partner who lights you up.",magic:"Sunday love-drawing with gold candles suits you; Sunstone and a celebration of your partnership each year."},Virgo:{simple:"Virgo on the seventh cusp draws you to practical, helpful and careful partners.",detailed:"With Pisces rising, you are dreamy and open, and you look for order, reliability and good sense in others. Partners may be health-minded, skilled or a little critical. Love shows in shared routines and practical help more than in grand romance. Mercury rules your seventh house, so its place shows what you need from a partner.",magic:"Partnership spells for good daily life on Wednesdays suit you; Moss Agate and a herb sachet stitched for the home you share."},Libra:{simple:"Libra on the seventh cusp means you seek harmony and equality in partnership.",detailed:"With Aries rising, you are bold and self-starting, and Libra on this cusp, its natural home, asks you to share. You seek partners who bring balance, grace and diplomacy, and partnership can soften and complete you. Fairness is essential. Venus rules your seventh house, so its place shows how you love.",magic:"Honey jars and love-drawing on Fridays suit you; Rose Quartz, rose and a pair of candles lit together."},Scorpio:{simple:"Scorpio on the seventh cusp draws you to deep, intense and powerful partners.",detailed:"With Taurus rising, you are steady and easy-going, and partnership is where you meet transformation. Partners may be magnetic, private or challenging, and relationships change you. Trust and loyalty are everything; jealousy and control are the shadow. Mars and Pluto rule your seventh house; their places show the depth you seek.",magic:"Fidelity and protection for a partnership suit you, and cord cutting when a bond must end; Garnet and Obsidian help."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Sagittarius on the seventh cusp draws you to free-spirited, adventurous partners.",detailed:"With Gemini rising, you are curious and quick, and you look for meaning, adventure and wisdom in others. Partners may be from another culture, older, or teachers of a kind. You need freedom within commitment. Jupiter rules your seventh house, so its place shows where partners bring growth.",magic:"Thursday blessings for a shared journey suit you; Turquoise and a travel charm carried by both of you."},Capricorn:{simple:"Capricorn on the seventh cusp draws you to serious, reliable and mature partners.",detailed:"With Cancer rising, you are tender and protective, and you look for structure and steadiness in others. Commitment is taken seriously and may come later in life, or with someone older. A good partnership is a shared building project. Saturn rules your seventh house, so its place shows what lasting love asks of you.",magic:"Commitment blessings on Saturdays suit you; Jet and Garnet for loyalty, and a written agreement kept on the altar."},Aquarius:{simple:"Aquarius on the seventh cusp draws you to independent, unusual partners who are also friends.",detailed:"With Leo rising, you are warm and visible, and you are drawn to originality, freedom and a cool head in others. Partnerships may follow their own rules, and friendship is the root of love. Space is not distance. Saturn and Uranus rule your seventh house; their places show what kind of bond you build.",magic:"Agreements of freedom and friendship suit you; Aquamarine and Amethyst on a shared altar."},Pisces:{simple:"Pisces on the seventh cusp draws you to compassionate, artistic and spiritual partners.",detailed:"With Virgo rising, you are careful and practical, and you may look to partners for the dreaminess and faith you keep in check. Partnership can be deeply spiritual or confusing; idealising or rescuing partners is the risk. Jupiter and Neptune rule your seventh house; their places show the love you dream of.",magic:"Clarity-in-love spells suit you, alongside devotion; Aquamarine and Rose Quartz, and a shared ritual bath."}},s={Aries:{simple:"Aries on the eighth cusp: you meet crisis and intimacy head-on.",detailed:"Transformation tends to come quickly, through sudden events you have to face directly. Shared money can become a battleground, and desire is direct and fiery. Your courage in crisis is real. Mars rules your eighth house, so its place shows how you face the depths.",magic:"Courage rituals before hard conversations or medical moments suit you; Bloodstone and a red candle for strength."},Taurus:{simple:"Taurus on the eighth cusp: you approach intimacy and shared money slowly and steadily.",detailed:"You need trust before you share your body, money or secrets, and change comes gradually. Inheritance, a partner's resources or long-term investments may be solid. Letting go of possessions or people can be hard. Venus rules your eighth house, so its place shows how intimacy feels safe.",magic:"Shared prosperity spells on Fridays suit you; Pyrite and Rose Quartz together."},Gemini:{simple:"Gemini on the eighth cusp: you understand the depths by talking and thinking.",detailed:"You process crisis through words, research and conversation, and you are curious about death, sex and the occult. Shared finances may involve paperwork, contracts or more than one source. Talk can keep feeling at a distance. Mercury rules your eighth house, so its place shows how your mind meets the depths.",magic:"Divination and research as devotion suit you; Fluorite and a journal kept for dreams and omens."},Cancer:{simple:"Cancer on the eighth cusp: intimacy is emotional and tied to family.",detailed:"Inheritance and family resources can be significant, and grief for the family runs deep. Intimacy needs emotional safety first. You may be a keeper of family memory and of the dead. The Moon rules your eighth house, so its place shows how you heal.",magic:"Ancestor rites and grief rituals suit you; Moonstone and a candle for the family dead each Samhain."},Leo:{simple:"Leo on the eighth cusp: you transform through pride, love and creativity.",detailed:"Intimacy needs warmth, loyalty and admiration. Crisis can bring out great courage, and pride can make it hard to show need. Shared resources may come through a generous partner. The Sun rules your eighth house, so its place shows where you are reborn.",magic:"Solar rebirth rituals at the solstice suit you; Sunstone and Obsidian together."},Virgo:{simple:"Virgo on the eighth cusp: you handle crisis and shared money carefully.",detailed:"You analyse the depths, manage joint resources well and are calm in practical emergencies. Worry about health or debt can creep in. Intimacy grows through trust and small acts of care. Mercury rules your eighth house, so its place shows how you meet change.",magic:"Careful shared-prosperity work suits you; Amazonite and Hyssop for clearing."},Libra:{simple:"Libra on the eighth cusp: intimacy needs fairness and grace.",detailed:"Shared resources may come through partnership or marriage, and you transform through relationship. Fairness in joint money matters a great deal. Avoiding the hard conversations is the risk. Venus rules your eighth house, so its place shows how you merge with another.",magic:"Sweetening for shared finances suits you; Rose Quartz and Vervain."},Scorpio:{simple:"Scorpio on the eighth cusp: you go deep, fearlessly.",detailed:"Scorpio is at home on this cusp. Intimacy, crisis, death and the occult are natural territory, and you can sit with what others avoid. Power and control in shared resources need care. Mars and Pluto rule your eighth house; their places show your power.",magic:"Shadow work and transformation at the dark Moon suit you; Obsidian, Wormwood and Hekate's keys."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Sagittarius on the eighth cusp: you meet the depths with faith.",detailed:"Crisis becomes a search for meaning, and you often come through hard times wiser. Shared resources may be generous; overconfidence with debt is the risk. You may be drawn to religious ideas about death. Jupiter rules your eighth house, so its place shows where you grow through change.",magic:"Faith rituals for hard times suit you; Turquoise and a prayer of your own."},Capricorn:{simple:"Capricorn on the eighth cusp: you approach intimacy and shared money cautiously.",detailed:"Trust takes time, and you manage joint resources responsibly. Inheritance or debt can carry duty. Loss may come early and teach endurance. Saturn rules your eighth house, so its place shows how you build trust.",magic:"Protection for shared resources on Saturdays suits you; Onyx and cypress."},Aquarius:{simple:"Aquarius on the eighth cusp: transformation comes suddenly and unusually.",detailed:"Intimacy needs freedom and friendship, and you may hold unusual views on death, sex and the occult. Shared finances can change suddenly. Detachment can protect you in crisis, and also keep you from feeling it. Saturn and Uranus rule your eighth house; their places show how you change.",magic:"Sudden release rituals suit you; Labradorite and a written vow burned when it is time to let go."},Pisces:{simple:"Pisces on the eighth cusp: intimacy is spiritual and boundaries can blur.",detailed:"You may have psychic gifts and a deep connection to the dead. Shared money can be confusing, so clear agreements protect you. Intimacy can feel like dissolving into another. Jupiter and Neptune rule your eighth house; their places show where you dissolve and are renewed.",magic:"Mediumship with protection suits you; Amethyst, a circle cast first, and a cleansing bath after."}},t={Aries:{simple:"Aries on the ninth cusp: you seek truth boldly and travel on impulse.",detailed:"Belief is something you fight for, and adventure calls without warning. You learn best by going and doing, and you may be drawn to activist causes or physical pilgrimages. Mars rules your ninth house, so its place shows where you crusade.",magic:"Courage for a pilgrimage suits you; Carnelian and a candle lit before setting out."},Taurus:{simple:"Taurus on the ninth cusp: your faith is practical, grounded and slow to change.",detailed:"You believe what you can experience, and you may love nature-based paths, land spirits and the sacredness of the body. Travel is best slow and comfortable. Venus rules your ninth house, so its place shows where you find meaning.",magic:"Earth devotion and pilgrimage to sacred land suit you; Moss Agate and an offering left at a holy tree."},Gemini:{simple:"Gemini on the ninth cusp: your faith is curious and questioning.",detailed:"You explore many beliefs, love languages, books and travel writing, and may study more than one subject at university. Doubt is part of your faith. Mercury rules your ninth house, so its place shows how you seek.",magic:"Bibliomancy and study as devotion suit you; Citrine and a commonplace book of sacred texts."},Cancer:{simple:"Cancer on the ninth cusp: your faith is emotional and rooted in family.",detailed:"Belief may come from family tradition, and you may travel to find your ancestors or to feel at home somewhere far away. Learning is best when it feels safe. The Moon rules your ninth house, so its place shows where faith comforts.",magic:"Ancestral devotion and pilgrimage to family places suit you; Moonstone."},Leo:{simple:"Leo on the ninth cusp: your faith is warm, generous and proud.",detailed:"You may teach or preach with flair, love the drama of ritual, and travel for joy. Belief is something you live loudly. The Sun rules your ninth house, so its place shows where your faith shines. Faith for you is a celebration, and pilgrimage can feel like a festival.",magic:"Solar devotion at the solstices suits you; Sunstone, and Apollo as a fitting patron."},Virgo:{simple:"Virgo on the ninth cusp: your faith is practical and discerning.",detailed:"You test beliefs carefully and may study health, herbs or service as a spiritual path. You prefer practice to doctrine. Mercury rules your ninth house, so its place shows how you seek. You may study one subject to the bottom rather than many on the surface, and teach it carefully.",magic:"Herbal study as devotion suits you; Amazonite and a grimoire of tested practice."},Libra:{simple:"Libra on the ninth cusp: your faith seeks justice and harmony.",detailed:"You may be drawn to law, ethics, or the beauty of religious art and music, and you see truth in more than one tradition. Travel is best with a companion. Venus rules your ninth house, so its place shows where you find meaning.",magic:"Devotion through beauty suits you; Lapis Lazuli and offerings of flowers."},Scorpio:{simple:"Scorpio on the ninth cusp: your faith is deep and transforming.",detailed:"You seek hidden truths, mysteries, initiations and the occult, and you may change belief dramatically after a crisis. Shallow answers will not do. Mars and Pluto rule your ninth house; their places show where you search.",magic:"Mystery study and initiation rites suit you; Obsidian and a vigil kept through the dark."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Sagittarius on the ninth cusp: you are a natural seeker, teacher and traveller.",detailed:"Sagittarius is at home on this cusp. Faith, philosophy and adventure come naturally, and you may teach, publish or live abroad. Your optimism is catching. Jupiter rules your ninth house, so its place shows where you grow.",magic:"Pilgrimage and prayer on Thursdays suit you; Turquoise and Sage."},Capricorn:{simple:"Capricorn on the ninth cusp: your faith is serious, traditional and earned.",detailed:"You build beliefs slowly and may study law, history or old traditions. Higher education may come later or with effort. Saturn rules your ninth house, so its place shows how your faith is built. You may find the religion of your ancestors again after years away.",magic:"Disciplined devotion suits you; Onyx and a daily reading of a sacred text."},Aquarius:{simple:"Aquarius on the ninth cusp: your faith is unconventional and forward-looking.",detailed:"You may be drawn to astrology, science, humanism or new spiritual movements, and you resist dogma. You think about faith for humanity as a whole. Saturn and Uranus rule your ninth house; their places show how you seek.",magic:"Astrology as devotion suits you; Labradorite."},Pisces:{simple:"Pisces on the ninth cusp: your faith is mystical and compassionate.",detailed:"You seek the divine through feeling, art, music and dreams, and you may be drawn to contemplative traditions or pilgrimage to the sea. Boundaries in belief can blur. Jupiter and Neptune rule your ninth house; their places show where you meet spirit.",magic:"Meditation and dreamwork as devotion suit you; Amethyst."}}},3088,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_10",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_11",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_12",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const o={Aries:{simple:"Aries on the tenth cusp: you want a career where you lead, pioneer and answer to yourself.",detailed:"You are driven, competitive and impatient with slow hierarchies, and many people with this cusp end up self-employed or starting something new. You are seen as brave and direct. Clashes with bosses are likely until you are the boss. Mars rules your tenth house, so its sign and house show where your ambition fights.",magic:"Career courage spells on Tuesdays suit you; Carnelian in your pocket for interviews and a candle lit before a bold move."},Taurus:{simple:"Taurus on the tenth cusp: you build a steady, lasting career.",detailed:"You may work with money, beauty, food, land or craft, and you value security over speed. You are seen as dependable, and your reputation grows slowly and solidly. Change of career is a big decision for you. Venus rules your tenth house, so its place shows where your vocation finds value.",magic:"Prosperity for career on Fridays suits you; Green Aventurine and a plant on the desk that grows with your work."},Gemini:{simple:"Gemini on the tenth cusp: your career involves words, ideas and variety.",detailed:"You may have more than one career at once, or work in media, teaching, writing, sales or trade. You are seen as clever and adaptable; settling on one path can be hard. Mercury rules your tenth house, so its place shows how your mind works in public.",magic:"Petitions for a good interview on Wednesdays suit you; Citrine and a blessed pen."},Cancer:{simple:"Cancer on the tenth cusp: your career involves caring, nurturing or home.",detailed:"You may work in care, food, property, history or a family business, and your reputation is tied to how you look after people. A parent, often the mother, may have shaped your ambitions strongly. The Moon rules your tenth house, so its place shows your public role.",magic:"Moon-timed career spells, begun at the new Moon, suit you; Moonstone for intuition at work."},Leo:{simple:"Leo on the tenth cusp: you want a career where you shine and are recognised.",detailed:"Leadership, performance, teaching or creative work suit you, and recognition matters. You are seen as warm and confident. Needing applause can make dull stretches hard. The Sun rules your tenth house, so its place shows where you are meant to be seen.",magic:"Sunday success spells suit you; Sunstone and bay laurel for honour."},Virgo:{simple:"Virgo on the tenth cusp: your career involves skill, service and precision.",detailed:"Health, analysis, craft, editing or research may suit you, and you are known for doing things well. You can be underrated because you do not boast. Mercury rules your tenth house, so its place shows where your skill is seen.",magic:"Blessing your work tools on Wednesdays suits you; Amazonite and a clean, ordered desk as a working altar."},Libra:{simple:"Libra on the tenth cusp: your career involves partnership, beauty or justice.",detailed:"Law, design, diplomacy, the arts or client work may suit you, and you are known for grace and fairness. Partners or collaborators often help your career. Venus rules your tenth house, so its place shows how you succeed.",magic:"Career glamour on Fridays suits you; Rose Quartz and Lapis Lazuli for good relations at work."},Scorpio:{simple:"Scorpio on the tenth cusp: your career involves depth, power or transformation.",detailed:"Research, finance, healing, psychology or investigation may suit you, and you work behind a strong, private image. You may rise and fall and rise again. Mars and Pluto rule your tenth house; their places show where your power works.",magic:"Protection of reputation suits you; Obsidian and a ward against gossip."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Sagittarius on the tenth cusp: your career involves teaching, travel or meaning.",detailed:"Publishing, law, education, religion or travel may suit you, and you need freedom and a sense of purpose at work. You are seen as wise or adventurous. Jupiter rules your tenth house, so its place shows where your career grows.",magic:"Thursday luck for career suits you; Turquoise and nutmeg in a success sachet."},Capricorn:{simple:"Capricorn on the tenth cusp: you are built for long-term achievement.",detailed:"Capricorn is at home on this cusp. You climb steadily to authority and are seen as responsible and capable. Success may come later and last longer. Saturn rules your tenth house, so its place shows where your mastery is built.",magic:"Saturday career spells suit you; Onyx and cypress for endurance."},Aquarius:{simple:"Aquarius on the tenth cusp: your career is unconventional or future-minded.",detailed:"Technology, science, activism, astrology or community work may suit you, and you may change direction suddenly. You are seen as original. Saturn and Uranus rule your tenth house; their places show how you reinvent your path.",magic:"Career sigils suit you; Labradorite and a vision board blessed at the new Moon."},Pisces:{simple:"Pisces on the tenth cusp: your career is a calling, creative or caring.",detailed:"Art, healing, ministry, music or film may suit you, and your public image may be elusive or idealised. Purpose matters more than status. Jupiter and Neptune rule your tenth house; their places show your vocation.",magic:"Spells for a true calling suit you; Amethyst and a dream question asked about your work."}},s={Aries:{simple:"Aries on the eleventh cusp: you are an active, bold friend and team player.",detailed:"You lead groups, champion causes and gather friends who like to do things. Friendships can be lively, competitive and sometimes short-lived. Your hopes are bold. Mars rules your eleventh house, so its place shows how you act with others.",magic:"Team blessings on Tuesdays suit you; Carnelian for courage in a cause."},Taurus:{simple:"Taurus on the eleventh cusp: your friendships are loyal, warm and lasting.",detailed:"You value steady friends you have known for years, and practical groups that make or grow something. Your hopes are for security and comfort shared. Venus rules your eleventh house, so its place shows what you treasure in friends.",magic:"Friendship blessings with shared food on Fridays suit you; Rose Quartz and a garden tended together."},Gemini:{simple:"Gemini on the eleventh cusp: you have many friends and love group talk.",detailed:"You are a natural networker, with friends in many circles and a love of clubs, classes and online groups. Depth can come second to breadth. Mercury rules your eleventh house, so its place shows how you connect.",magic:"Group divination and online circles suit you; Citrine and a shared journal of wishes."},Cancer:{simple:"Cancer on the eleventh cusp: your friends feel like family.",detailed:"You nurture your circle and seek emotional belonging in groups. Friends may become chosen family, and your hopes centre on home and care. The Moon rules your eleventh house, so its place shows where you belong.",magic:"Full Moon circles suit you; Moonstone and a meal shared under the full Moon."},Leo:{simple:"Leo on the eleventh cusp: you are a warm, generous friend and group leader.",detailed:"You bring people together with heart and enjoy friends who are creative and fun. Your hopes are big and bright. Being the star of every group is the thing to watch. The Sun rules your eleventh house, so its place shows where your hopes shine.",magic:"Celebration rituals for friends suit you; Sunstone and a toast offered to the gods of friendship."},Virgo:{simple:"Virgo on the eleventh cusp: you help your friends in practical ways.",detailed:"You are the organiser of groups, and you may make friends through work, health or service. Your hopes are modest and useful. Mercury rules your eleventh house, so its place shows how you serve your community.",magic:"Practical group workings suit you; Amazonite and a shared herb garden or charity."},Libra:{simple:"Libra on the eleventh cusp: friendships are graceful and balanced.",detailed:"You are a peacemaker in groups and enjoy friends who love art, conversation and fairness. Friends may become partners. Venus rules your eleventh house, so its place shows what you value in friendship.",magic:"Friendship sweetening on Fridays suits you; Rose Quartz."},Scorpio:{simple:"Scorpio on the eleventh cusp: friendships are few, deep and loyal.",detailed:"You trust slowly, keep friends for life and may be drawn to powerful or secret groups. Betrayal by a friend cuts deep. Mars and Pluto rule your eleventh house; their places show how you bond. The friends you have, you would go to the underworld for, and they know it.",magic:"Protective group magic suits you; Obsidian and an oath of friendship sealed with care."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Sagittarius on the eleventh cusp: your friends are adventurous and many.",detailed:"You may have friends from many cultures and faiths, and you love groups with a purpose or a journey. Your hopes are generous. Jupiter rules your eleventh house, so its place shows where your hopes grow.",magic:"Thursday wishes for your circle suit you; Turquoise."},Capricorn:{simple:"Capricorn on the eleventh cusp: friendships are serious and long-term.",detailed:"You may have older friends, professional networks and roles in established groups. Friendships deepen over decades. Saturn rules your eleventh house, so its place shows how you build community. Your friendships often begin at work and outlast the job.",magic:"Structured group ritual suits you; Onyx and a yearly rite with old friends."},Aquarius:{simple:"Aquarius on the eleventh cusp: you are a natural member of communities and causes.",detailed:"Aquarius is at home on this cusp. Friends are unusual and groups progressive, and your hopes are for humanity. Saturn and Uranus rule your eleventh house; their places show your vision. You may find your people online or in movements long before you find them nearby.",magic:"Group sigils and coven work suit you; Amethyst."},Pisces:{simple:"Pisces on the eleventh cusp: friendships are compassionate and spiritual.",detailed:"You may be drawn to spiritual groups, artistic circles and caring causes. Friends may lean on you, and boundaries help. Jupiter and Neptune rule your eleventh house; their places show your dreams for the world.",magic:"Group meditation suits you; Aquamarine and a shared prayer for the world."}},t={Aries:{simple:"Aries on the twelfth cusp: hidden anger, private courage and a fire kept out of sight.",detailed:"You may hold back anger or drive that you were not allowed to show, and it can surface as restlessness or fatigue. Solitude restores you best when it is active: a walk, a hard workout alone. Mars rules your twelfth house, so its place shows where hidden drive goes.",magic:"Banishing hidden anger at the dark Moon suits you; Bloodstone, and writing what you could not say."},Taurus:{simple:"Taurus on the twelfth cusp: hidden comfort-seeking and quiet private pleasures.",detailed:"You may keep your need for security, rest and pleasure private, or retreat into comfort when life is hard. Time in nature is deeply healing. Venus rules your twelfth house, so its place shows where you retreat.",magic:"Private sensual self-care suits you; Rose Quartz and a bath taken as a solitary rite."},Gemini:{simple:"Gemini on the twelfth cusp: a busy hidden mind and private thoughts.",detailed:"You may keep thoughts to yourself, write in secret, or have a mind that will not quiet at night. Journaling helps empty it. Mercury rules your twelfth house, so its place shows your hidden mind. Writing in the early hours can be the quiet that settles you.",magic:"Secret journals and dreamwork suit you; Fluorite under the pillow quiets a mind that talks all night."},Cancer:{simple:"Cancer on the twelfth cusp: hidden feelings and private nurture.",detailed:"You may show warmth outwardly and keep tenderness private, or carry family sorrow quietly. Retreat to water and home restores you. The Moon rules your twelfth house, so its place shows where you retreat.",magic:"Private moon rituals suit you: moon water drunk at the full, Moonstone under the pillow, and tears allowed."},Leo:{simple:"Leo on the twelfth cusp: hidden pride and a private creative life.",detailed:"You may hide your light, create in secret, or need recognition you do not admit. Solitary creative work restores you. The Sun rules your twelfth house, so its place shows where hidden light waits. Hidden generosity, given anonymously, can be deeply healing for you.",magic:"Private creative devotion suits you: something made only for the gods or for yourself, on a Sunday, with Sunstone beside it."},Virgo:{simple:"Virgo on the twelfth cusp: hidden worries and quiet service.",detailed:"You may keep anxieties private or serve behind the scenes, in hospitals or quiet places. Small routines in solitude calm you. Mercury rules your twelfth house, so its place shows where worry hides. Small acts of unseen care are a spiritual practice for you.",magic:"Releasing worries at the waning Moon suits you: write them, fold them away from you and bury them, with Amazonite to hold the calm."},Libra:{simple:"Libra on the twelfth cusp: hidden longing for harmony and secret relationships.",detailed:"You may keep your gentleness private, or carry hidden relationships or unspoken grievances. Beauty in solitude, like music or art, restores you. Venus rules your twelfth house, so its place shows hidden love.",magic:"Private self-love rituals suit you on Fridays: a candle, a mirror, kind words, and Rose Quartz kept by the bed."},Scorpio:{simple:"Scorpio on the twelfth cusp: hidden depths and private power.",detailed:"You may hide your intensity behind cheerfulness and carry secrets well. Deep solitude and shadow work restore you. Mars and Pluto rule your twelfth house; their places show hidden strength. Old griefs may surface in dreams, asking to be faced.",magic:"Shadow work in private suits you, best at the dark Moon with a journal and Obsidian, and always closed by grounding."},Sagittarius:{simple:"Sagittarius on the twelfth cusp: hidden faith and private seeking.",detailed:"You may keep your hopes and beliefs private, and many with this cusp feel quietly protected in hard times. Solitary study or pilgrimage restores you. Jupiter rules your twelfth house, so its place shows hidden protection.",magic:"Private prayer suits you, in your own words, on Thursdays; Turquoise carried as a quiet amulet of protection."},Capricorn:{simple:"Capricorn on the twelfth cusp: hidden fears about failure and private discipline.",detailed:"You may carry hidden responsibilities or fears you do not share. Structured solitude, such as a daily meditation, steadies you. Saturn rules your twelfth house, so its place shows where fears are faced.",magic:"Banishing fear on Saturdays suits you: name it, write it, and bind it with black thread, with Smoky Quartz to ground you after."},Aquarius:{simple:"Aquarius on the twelfth cusp: hidden rebellion and private originality.",detailed:"You may keep your strangeness private or feel an outsider inside. Unusual spiritual practice in solitude restores you. Saturn and Uranus rule your twelfth house; their places show hidden freedom. You may find peace in solitary study of the stars or of strange subjects.",magic:"Private sigil work suits you, made and charged alone and kept secret; Labradorite guards the inner spark."},Pisces:{simple:"Pisces on the twelfth cusp: deep spiritual life and hidden sensitivity.",detailed:"Pisces is at home on this cusp. You may hide your softness, and you need solitude, sleep and spiritual practice to stay well. Dreams are vivid. Jupiter and Neptune rule your twelfth house; their places show your inner sanctuary.",magic:"Dreamwork and meditation suit you: a dream pillow of mugwort and lavender, a journal by the bed, and Amethyst on the nightstand."}}},3089,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_1_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_2_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_3_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const o={Aries:["In practice you may be the first to volunteer, the first to object and the first to leave when things go slack. Headaches, small cuts and burns are the classic Aries complaints, mostly from hurrying. Your growth is in finishing: the fire that starts things can learn to stay. Look at what you began this year and choose one thing to see through.","Each birthday, light a red candle at sunrise and name one thing you will finish before the next."],Taurus:["You may change slowly and dislike being rushed, but once you have chosen a way of being it lasts. The throat, neck and voice are sensitive places, and many with Taurus rising sing or speak well. The growth edge is stubbornness: comfort can become a rut. Let one small new pleasure in each season to keep the body curious.","Anoint the throat with a drop of rose oil in a carrier before you speak in public, and ask Venus for an easy voice."],Gemini:["You often meet people through talk, and first impressions of you are of quickness and wit. Hands, lungs and nerves are the Gemini places, so breath work and something to do with the hands calm you. The growth edge is scattering: so many open doors that none is walked through. Choose a few interests to go deep with.","Breathe slowly over a lavender sprig for nine breaths before any spell, to gather a scattered mind."],Cancer:["Your face often shows your feelings before you choose to, and people may tell you their troubles within minutes of meeting. The stomach and breasts are Cancer's places, and you may feel moods in the gut. The growth edge is the shell: protection that keeps out the good with the bad. Practise letting a few safe people all the way in.","At each full moon, wash the face in moon water and let one guarded feeling be spoken aloud."],Leo:["You light up a room without trying, and you may be treated as a leader before you feel like one. The heart and spine are Leo's places, so posture, circulation and joy all matter to your health. The growth edge is needing an audience; your warmth is real even when no one is clapping. Practise generosity in private too.","On a Sunday, stand in the sun with a piece of Citrine and say aloud one thing you are proud of."],Virgo:["You meet life by noticing: what needs doing, what is out of place, who is struggling. The gut and nerves are Virgo's places, so diet, routine and rest affect you strongly. The growth edge is self-criticism; the same eye that improves the world can wound you. Turn your care inward as readily as you turn it out.","Brew a cup of chamomile on a Wednesday, and with each sip name something you did well this week."],Libra:["People find you pleasant and fair, and you may smooth over difficulty without thinking. The kidneys, lower back and skin are Libra's places, and balance in diet and rest serves you well. The growth edge is avoiding conflict to keep the peace. Practise stating a preference, even about small things, so that your own self is in the balance.","Hold a stone in each hand on a Friday and say which way you lean before asking anyone else."],Scorpio:["Others may sense power or reserve in you before you have said a word, and you may reveal yourself only slowly. The reproductive organs and elimination are Scorpio's places, and stress tends to go deep before it shows. The growth edge is trust: armour that served you once can keep you lonely. Let one person see you as you are.","At the dark moon, hold Obsidian and speak one true thing about yourself aloud, then let the candle burn down."],Sagittarius:["You meet life with optimism and a sense of adventure, and you may seem younger and freer than you feel. Hips, thighs and liver are Sagittarius's places, so walking and moderation matter. The growth edge is restlessness and overpromising. Pick the journey that means most, and give it your full attention.","Before a trip or new venture, carry a piece of Lapis and a bay leaf, and speak your aim to the open sky."],Capricorn:["You often seem older and more capable than your years, and people may hand you responsibility early. Bones, knees, teeth and skin are Capricorn's places, and you benefit from steady care. The growth edge is seriousness that forgets to laugh. Time is your ally; let yourself be lighter as the years go on.","On a Saturday, set a small stone on the altar for each goal you have reached, building a cairn of your own achievements."],Aquarius:["You may seem friendly yet a little apart, someone who sees the bigger picture. The ankles, circulation and nervous system are Aquarius's places, and fresh air helps you. The growth edge is detachment: standing back so far that you cannot be touched. Let your difference be a gift you share rather than a wall.","Charge Clear Quartz under open sky on a windy day, then carry it as a charm for your own way of being."],Pisces:["You meet life gently and absorb atmospheres, sometimes without realising which feelings are yours. The feet and lymph are Pisces's places, and rest, water and sleep matter. The growth edge is boundaries; you can be kind without dissolving. A clear daily practice of returning to yourself keeps the sensitivity a gift.","Soak your feet in warm water with sea salt at the end of a full day, and let other people's moods run away."]},n={Aries:["You earn best when you can start things, compete or work for yourself, and you may make money quickly and spend it quickly. Impulse buying is the risk. Your worth grows each time you act bravely on your own behalf. A habit of waiting a day before spending big turns the fire into lasting resources.","Light a red candle on a Tuesday over a written savings goal, and put the first coin aside that day."],Taurus:["Money comes steadily through patience, quality and things that can be touched: land, craft, food, art, beauty. You value security and good things that last. The risk is holding on too tightly. Spend on what gives real, lasting pleasure, and let your values guide your purse.","Keep a green jar with coins and a sprig of basil, adding to it each Friday for slow, steady growth."],Gemini:["Income may come from words, trade, teaching, writing or more than one job at a time. You may have several streams and value variety. The risk is scattering money as well as attention. Keep simple records, and let your cleverness work for your security.","On a Wednesday, write your income sources on paper and tie it with a green thread around a cinnamon stick."],Cancer:["You value security for family and home, and you may earn through care, food, property or anything that nurtures. Money can rise and fall with feelings. The risk is emotional spending or hoarding. Build a nest egg that lets you feel safe, and give from it generously.","Keep a silver coin in a bowl of rice in the kitchen, renewed each new moon, for the household's plenty."],Leo:["You earn through creativity, leadership or being seen, and you are generous with what you have. Money may be tied to pride. The risk is spending for show. Invest in your own talents, and let generosity be from the heart rather than for the audience.","On a Sunday, anoint a gold coin with a drop of orange oil and keep it in your purse for sunny prosperity."],Virgo:["You earn through skill, service and attention to detail, and you are usually careful with money. You value what is useful. The risk is anxiety about not having enough, or undervaluing your work. Charge fairly for your skill; it is worth more than you think.","On a Wednesday, write your rate on paper, read it aloud with confidence and keep it under a piece of Green Aventurine."],Libra:["Money may come through partnership, art, design, law or diplomacy, and you value beauty and fairness. You may spend on lovely things. The risk is depending on others for security or overspending to please. Make shared money clear and fair.","Set two coins on a rose quartz on a Friday, one for you and one for a partner or friend, for balanced prosperity."],Scorpio:["Money can be a matter of power and depth: you may earn through research, finance, healing or other people's resources. You may go through cycles of loss and renewal. The risk is control or secrecy around money. Clear accounts and honest exchange keep it clean.","At the dark moon, burn a list of debts or money fears, and plant a coin in earth for renewal."],Sagittarius:["You earn through teaching, travel, publishing, law or faith, and you may be lucky with money. You value freedom over possessions. The risk is overspending on optimism. A simple budget keeps the generous spirit generous. Money may come through teaching, travel, publishing, law or faith, and you may be generous to a fault. You value experience and growth more than possessions. A simple plan for savings lets you keep being generous without worry.","On a Thursday, place a coin under a blue candle with a sprig of sage, asking for luck that lasts."],Capricorn:["You build resources slowly and steadily, and you may earn more as you age. You value security and hard work. The risk is meanness or never enjoying what you build. Plan for the future, and allow some pleasure now.","Keep a coin under a black stone on a Saturday, adding one each week for long-term security."],Aquarius:["Money may come through unusual work, technology, groups or causes. You value freedom and fairness, and your income may be irregular. The risk is detachment from practical money matters. Keep a cushion so that freedom does not become fear. You may earn through technology, science, groups, astrology or work that is ahead of its time, and income may come in bursts. Your values may be unconventional; you may care more for freedom than things. Keep a steady base so that your independence is secure.","Keep a jar for the unexpected, with a coin and Clear Quartz, adding to it at each new moon."],Pisces:["Money may come through art, healing, spirituality or charity, and it may be hard to track. You value what cannot be bought. The risk is confusion or being taken advantage of. Get help with money, keep it simple, and value your gifts.","On a Monday, write your money truths clearly on paper and keep them under Amethyst to clear the fog."]},t={Aries:["You speak first and think later, and your words carry energy and challenge. Sibling rivalry may have been strong. Short trips may be taken in a rush. Learning to pause before speaking turns directness into courage that others can hear.","Before an important talk, hold a piece of Carnelian and breathe once for each word you want to choose."],Taurus:["You think slowly and surely, and you remember what you learn. Your speech may be calm and pleasant. Siblings may be steady companions. The risk is fixed opinions. Let new ideas take root slowly, and your mind grows rich. You prefer to learn by doing and handling, and you may have a pleasant speaking or singing voice. Your local area matters to you, and you may stay in one neighbourhood a long time. Give yourself time to form an opinion; once formed, it is well grounded.","On a Friday, write a learning goal in green ink and keep it under a rose quartz."],Gemini:["This is Gemini's own house, so the mind is quick and curious, and talk, writing and short journeys fill the days. You may have many siblings or close neighbours. The risk is scattering. Keep a notebook and let your ideas find a home.","Write a charm in rhyme on a Wednesday and say it aloud three times at a crossroads."],Cancer:["You learn through feeling and memory, and your words carry emotion. Siblings may be close or protective. Your local neighbourhood may feel like home. The risk is taking words personally. Let feeling inform your thinking without ruling it.","Write a letter of love to a sibling or neighbour on a Monday, whether or not you send it."],Leo:["You speak with warmth and drama, and you may be a natural storyteller or teacher. Siblings may compete for attention. The risk is talking over others. Let your words shine and leave room for others to speak.","On a Sunday, tell a story aloud to someone you love, and dedicate the telling to the Sun."],Virgo:["You think precisely and notice details. Writing, editing and analysis come easily. Siblings may be practical helpers. The risk is worrying or criticising. Use your clear mind to help, and be as kind to your own thoughts as to others'.","On a Wednesday, write three precise intentions and keep them in a small notebook kept only for spells."],Libra:["You speak diplomatically and like to hear all sides. Siblings may be companions or partners in ventures. The risk is indecision. Practise saying what you think first, and listen after. You often learn best in pairs, with a study partner or in conversation, and you may write well in letters and dialogue. Neighbours and siblings may be where you practise fairness. When you say what you mean first and soften it after, your words gain weight.","On a Friday, write a balanced statement of a decision on rose-scented paper and keep it until it is made."],Scorpio:["You think deeply and notice what others hide. Your words can cut or heal. Siblings may have been intense. The risk is suspicion. Use your perception to understand, not to judge.","At the dark moon, write what you suspect on paper and burn it, asking to see the truth plainly."],Sagittarius:["You think in big pictures and love ideas, travel and debate. Siblings may be far away or adventurous. The risk is carelessness with details. Check facts, and let your vision inspire.","Before a journey, write a blessing on paper and keep it in your shoe for safe travel."],Capricorn:["You think carefully and practically, and your words carry weight. Learning may have been hard early and improve with age. Siblings may have responsibilities. The risk is pessimism. Let your serious mind lighten with humour.","On a Saturday, write one fact you have mastered this year and keep it on the altar beside a black stone."],Aquarius:["You think in original ways and may be ahead of your time. Siblings or neighbours may be unusual. The risk is detachment from feeling. Let your ideas serve people.","Charge a pen under open sky and use it only for writing spells and new ideas."],Pisces:["You think in images and feelings, and you may be poetic or intuitive. Siblings may be sensitive or need care. The risk is confusion. Keep notes and check facts, and let your intuition guide your words.","Write your spells as poems on a Monday, reading them aloud over a bowl of water."]}},3090,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_4_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_5_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_6_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const o={Aries:["Home may have been busy, loud or quick to quarrel, with a parent whose temper set the weather. As an adult you may move often, or rebuild houses with your own hands, and you are rarely content to leave a place as you found it. The growth is making home somewhere the energy is used well: projects rather than rows, and a door you can shut when you need to rest. Late in life this cusp often brings a burst of fresh starts at home.","Lay an iron key or nail under the doormat and bless it on a Tuesday, asking that strength stay at the threshold and quarrels stay outside."],Taurus:["You need a home that feels solid in the body: good bread, a soft chair, a garden or at least a window box, and things around you that last. You may stay in one house a long time and grow very attached to it. Family may have valued comfort, land or thrift. The growth is letting the haven stay open to change, so that the comfort of home does not become a reason never to leave it.","Plant a herb pot by the door on a Friday, basil or thyme, and tend it as the heart of the home; when it thrives, so does the house."],Gemini:["Home may have been lively, full of books, radio, visitors and talk, or a place you moved between, with two households or many addresses. You may still keep several bases, or work from home. The growth is finding a still centre in the bustle: one quiet corner where no one talks to you, and a routine that lets the mind settle before sleep.","Hang a small bell by the door and ring it on a Wednesday as you walk through the rooms, to clear the air of old words."],Cancer:["This is Cancer's own house, so home and family are central, and your sense of safety depends on the hearth. You may be the one who keeps the family together, who remembers birthdays and keeps old photographs. Memory and ancestry run deep. The growth is letting family give back to you, and keeping a little privacy of your own inside the warmth you make for others.","Keep a jar of moon water by the hearth, renewed each full moon, and touch a drop to each doorframe to bless the house."],Leo:["You want a home you can be proud of, warm, generous and full of colour, where you can host and be at the centre. A parent may have been a strong, bright or dramatic figure. Family pride runs deep. The growth is letting home be a place to rest as well as to shine: somewhere you are loved when you are tired, not only when you are dazzling.","Light a gold candle at the heart of the home on a Sunday, with a sprig of calendula or a sunflower, for warmth and joy in the house."],Virgo:["You want a clean, orderly, useful home, and you may feel unsettled until things are in their places. Family life may have run on duties, routines or worry about health. You may care for a family member. The growth is letting home be imperfect and loved: a lived-in kitchen is still a sacred one, and rest is part of keeping house.","Sweep the home on a Wednesday with a broom tied with lavender, sweeping out worry with the dust and leaving the door open for fresh air."],Libra:["You want a beautiful, peaceful home and may share it with a partner from early on. Family may have valued harmony, manners or the look of things, sometimes at the cost of honesty. The growth is allowing honest conflict at home, kindly said, so that the peace is real rather than kept at a cost to someone.","Place rose petals in a bowl at the heart of the home each Friday, and name one honest thing that could be said in the house this week."],Scorpio:["Home may have held secrets, intensity or a family story that was never fully told. You may need great privacy, and your home is a fortress or a sanctuary. Family life may have changed through crisis. The growth is making home a place of healing and trust, where the old silences are broken gently and the walls protect rather than imprison.","At the dark moon, burn a black candle at the hearth and name a family pattern to release; let the candle burn down safely."],Sagittarius:["Home may be large, open, foreign or always on the move, and you may live abroad or far from where you were born. Family may have valued faith, learning or freedom. You need room, a view and books. The growth is putting down roots without losing freedom: home as a base camp, not a cage.","Keep a stone or a map from a far place on the hearth, and bless it each Thursday with a sprig of sage for a home that welcomes the wanderer."],Capricorn:["Home may have been strict, responsible or short of warmth, and you may have grown up quickly. A parent may have been absent through work or duty. You may build your own home slowly, often owning property later in life. The growth is letting home be warm as well as solid: comfort is not a failing, and the house you build can hold softness.","Bless the foundations of the home on a Saturday with a pinch of salt in each of the four corners, asking for a home that stands and a heart that softens."],Aquarius:["Home may have been unusual, shared or always changing: a commune, a household of friends, sudden moves or a family that broke the usual mould. You may need freedom at home and dislike feeling tied down. The growth is giving yourself enough stability to rest, and a few rituals that make anywhere feel like home.","Keep a piece of Clear Quartz at the heart of the home, and once a month carry it outside under open sky to cleanse and recharge it."],Pisces:["Home may have been dreamy, spiritual, chaotic or sad, with a missing, ill or idealised family member. You may long for a home that feels like a sanctuary, and find it near water or in quiet places. The growth is clear boundaries at home: who comes in, what you take on, and how you rest.","Keep a bowl of water on the home altar, changed each Monday, and pour the old water onto a plant with a word of thanks for the house."]},t={Aries:["Romance begins with a spark and a chase, and you may love the first thrill more than the long middle. Sport, competition and bold creative projects give you joy, and you are often happiest when you are a little out of your depth. With children you are lively and encouraging. The growth is learning to stay for the second act, where love and art both deepen.","Begin a creative project on a Tuesday with a red candle, and promise to work on it for one full moon cycle, whatever happens."],Taurus:["Pleasure is sensual and lasting: good food, music, gardens, art and slow love. Creative work may be in craft, music, cookery or beauty, and you are proud of things well made. Children are cherished and comforted. The care is indulgence or possessiveness in love. At its best, this cusp gives a gift for making joy last.","On a Friday, make something beautiful by hand and offer the first of it to Venus with a rose."],Gemini:["Fun is talk, wit, games and play with words, and romance often begins in conversation or in messages. You may write, teach, play or juggle several hobbies at once. Children may be clever and chatty. The care is flirting without commitment, or starting more projects than you finish. Joy deepens when one of them is carried to the end.","Write a playful charm in rhyme on a Wednesday and give it to someone you love, folded into a paper bird."],Cancer:["Joy comes from family, home and nurturing, and romance is tender and protective. Creative work may draw on memory, childhood and the past. Children are central to your happiness, your own or others'. The care is smothering, in love or in parenting. Let joy be gentle and let others go free.","At the full moon, make a creative offering from a family memory, a recipe, a story or a drawing, and leave it on the home altar."],Leo:["This is Leo's own house: joy, creativity, romance and children are strongly marked. You may be a natural performer, artist or teacher, and you light up when you create or play. Love is generous and dramatic. The care is pride or needing applause. Let joy be generous, shared and sometimes private.","On a Sunday, perform something, even for one person, and give thanks to the Sun with a gold candle."],Virgo:["Pleasure comes from skill, craft and doing things well, and you may enjoy hobbies that need patience and precision. Romance may be careful or practical, and you show love through help. Children may be taught carefully. The care is criticism that spoils joy. Let some things be done for fun and done badly.","On a Wednesday, make something by hand slowly and well, and keep it as a talisman of skill and pleasure."],Libra:["Romance is graceful, and beauty, art and good company bring joy. You may love creative partnerships and social pleasures. Children may be charming and sociable. The care is people-pleasing in love, or losing yourself in the beloved's tastes. Let your own pleasures matter.","Light two pink candles on a Friday for a love or a creative partnership that is balanced and joyful."],Scorpio:["Love and creativity are intense and transforming, and you may throw yourself into passions completely. Romance may be deep, secret or life-changing. Children may change you profoundly. The care is jealousy or possessiveness. Your art can go to places others avoid.","At the dark moon, make art from what you feel most deeply, and keep it as a private offering."],Sagittarius:["Joy comes from adventure, travel, ideas, sport and play. Romance may begin abroad or with someone very different from you. Children may be free spirits. The care is restlessness in love. Joy deepens when the adventure is shared.","Before a trip, make a small creative offering and leave it at a beautiful place you visit, with thanks."],Capricorn:["Pleasure may come late or seriously, and creative work matures with time. Romance may be with someone older or responsible, and you may take love seriously. The care is not allowing play. Joy can be a discipline: protect time for it.","On a Saturday, set aside one hour for pure play, and keep the hour as you would keep a vow."],Aquarius:["Fun comes from friends, groups, ideas and freedom. Romance may be unconventional or begin as friendship. Children may be independent and original. The care is detachment in love. Let yourself feel the joy as well as think it.","Make art with friends at the new moon, and keep a shared piece on the altar for the group's joy."],Pisces:["Joy comes from music, art, dreams, film and spirit. Romance is idealised and tender. Children may be sensitive and imaginative. The care is disappointment when dreams meet life. Let art hold the longing.","Make music or art at the full moon, and offer it to the sea or a river with a flower."]},n={Aries:["You work fast and like a challenge, and you may be drawn to physical, competitive or emergency work. You want to get on with it and can be impatient with slow colleagues. Health issues tend to come on suddenly and pass quickly, often from overdoing it: headaches, strains and fevers. A morning routine that burns energy cleanly keeps you well and calmer at work.","Begin each working week with a red candle on Tuesday morning and a short burst of movement to set the pace."],Taurus:["You work steadily and well with your hands, and you need comfort, fair pay and stability at work. You may be drawn to craft, food, gardening, money or the body. The throat and neck may hold stress. Regular meals, walks and rest keep you strong. The care is resisting needed change at work.","Keep a rose quartz on the desk and touch it at the start of each working day for steadiness and ease."],Gemini:["You need variety at work and may do many tasks or jobs at once. Communication, writing, trade and teaching suit you. The nerves, lungs and hands need care: breaks, fresh air and something to do with the hands help. The care is scattering. Lists are your friend.","Keep a sprig of lavender at your workplace and breathe its scent between tasks to gather a scattered mind."],Cancer:["You work best in a caring, familiar setting, and may nurture colleagues or work in care, food or home. The stomach reacts to stress. Regular meals, a calm workplace and feeling valued keep you well. The care is taking work home emotionally.","Wash your hands with moon water at the end of work to leave the day behind before you walk through your own door."],Leo:["You want work that lets you shine, create or lead, and you work best when appreciated. The heart and back need care, and joy at work is part of health. The care is pride or overwork for recognition. Rest is not failure.","Keep a piece of Citrine at your workplace for warm confidence, and cleanse it in sunlight on Sundays."],Virgo:["This is Virgo's own house, so work and health are central. You are skilled, careful and helpful, and may work in health, craft, analysis or service. The gut and nerves need care, and routine helps. The care is worry and perfectionism. Good enough is often good.","Brew a cup of chamomile and peppermint tea as a daily ritual at work, and let it mark a pause."],Libra:["You work best in pleasant surroundings with good colleagues, and may be drawn to art, design, law or diplomacy. The kidneys, skin and lower back need care. Balance between work and rest keeps you well. The care is avoiding hard tasks to keep the peace.","Keep a vase of flowers at your workplace, refreshed each Friday, for grace in the working day."],Scorpio:["You work intensely and may be drawn to research, healing, crisis or investigation. You can give work your whole self. Health may need deep attention, as stress tends to go inward. The care is obsession or burnout. Rest as fully as you work.","At the dark moon, write a work habit to release and burn it in a black candle's flame."],Sagittarius:["You need freedom and meaning at work, and may work in teaching, travel, law, publishing or outdoors. The hips, thighs and liver need care. Movement and moderation help. The care is overcommitting. Choose the work that means most.","On a Thursday, bless your work with a blue candle and a sprig of sage, asking for work that feeds the spirit."],Capricorn:["You work hard and reliably, and may take on great responsibility early. Structure suits you. Bones, teeth, joints and skin need care. The care is overwork as proof of worth. Rest is part of the job.","On a Saturday, rest from work entirely and keep the day as a sacred rest, with a black candle lit at dusk."],Aquarius:["You need freedom and innovation at work, and may work with technology, groups or reform. Routine chafes. The circulation and nerves need care, and fresh air helps. The care is restlessness. Flexible routines work best.","Keep a piece of Clear Quartz at your workplace and cleanse it under open sky each month."],Pisces:["You need meaningful, compassionate work, and may be drawn to care, healing, art or spiritual service. The feet and immune system need care, and rest and water help. The care is martyrdom at work. Give without giving yourself away.","Wash in water with a little sea salt after work to cleanse the energy of the day."]}},3091,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_7_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o={Aries:["With Aries on the Descendant, Libra rises, so you may seem gentle and accommodating while being drawn to bold, direct, sometimes combative partners. They carry the fire you have not yet claimed. Quarrels can be quick and clear the air. The growth is learning to say what you want yourself, so that partnership becomes two people of equal spirit rather than one who acts and one who smooths.","Light one red and one pink candle on a Friday, and say aloud one want of your own before you name the partner's."],Taurus:["Scorpio rises with Taurus on the Descendant, so your intensity looks for a partner who is calm, loyal and grounded. You want a relationship that lasts and feels safe in the body. The risk is possessiveness on either side, or staying in comfort past its time. At its best, partnership is your place of rest and slow, faithful pleasure.","Plant something perennial with a partner on a Friday, and tend it together as the bond grows."],Gemini:["Sagittarius rises with Gemini on the Descendant, so you want a partner who can talk, joke, question and keep you curious. A relationship needs conversation to stay alive. The risk is keeping things light to avoid depth, or a partner who never quite commits. Share ideas, travel together, and let the talk go deep sometimes.","Write each other short notes on a Wednesday and keep them in a box together on the altar."],Cancer:["Capricorn rises with Cancer on the Descendant, so you may seem self-sufficient while looking for warmth, care and a sense of family in partnership. Partners may mother you, or you them. The risk is dependency or moods that go unspoken. The growth is letting yourself be cared for, and saying what you feel.","At the full moon, cook a meal for a partner and bless the pot as you stir, for a nourishing bond."],Leo:["Aquarius rises with Leo on the Descendant, so your cool independence looks for a warm, generous, expressive partner. They may carry your need for attention and joy. The risk is a partner who needs the spotlight or pride that won't bend. The growth is letting yourself shine in partnership too.","On a Sunday, light a gold candle for the partnership and speak one thing you admire in the other."],Virgo:["Pisces rises with Virgo on the Descendant, so your dreaminess looks for a partner who is practical, helpful and clear. The risk is criticism, or a relationship that becomes all duty. The growth is mutual care, each helping the other with grace rather than correction.","Make a small daily act of practical care for a partner your spell, beginning on a Wednesday."],Libra:["This is Libra's own house, and Aries rises: you meet life boldly and look for balance, beauty and fairness in partnership. Relationships are central and may come easily. The risk is losing yourself in the other. The growth is a partnership of true equals.","Two candles lit from one flame on a Friday, set side by side, for a fair and loving bond."],Scorpio:["Taurus rises with Scorpio on the Descendant, so your steadiness looks for depth, intensity and transformation in partnership. Relationships may change you profoundly. The risk is jealousy or power struggles. The growth is trust and honest depth.","At the dark moon, share a secret with a partner and burn a black candle for trust."],Sagittarius:["Gemini rises with Sagittarius on the Descendant, so your curiosity looks for a partner who brings meaning, adventure and wider horizons. You may partner with someone from far away. The risk is restlessness. The growth is a partnership that grows together.","Before a shared journey, bless a pair of tokens with sage on a Thursday and carry one each."],Capricorn:["Cancer rises with Capricorn on the Descendant, so your tenderness looks for a stable, responsible partner. You may marry later or someone older. The risk is coldness or duty. The growth is a lasting partnership with warmth.","On a Saturday, tie a black and a silver cord together with three knots for a lasting bond."],Aquarius:["Leo rises with Aquarius on the Descendant, so your warmth looks for a partner who is unusual, free and a friend. The risk is detachment. The growth is a partnership of friends who stay free together.","Light two blue candles a little apart and let them burn together for freedom in love."],Pisces:["Virgo rises with Pisces on the Descendant, so your practicality looks for a partner who is gentle, spiritual and compassionate. The risk is rescuing or confusion. The growth is love with clear eyes.","Pour two cups of water into one bowl at the full moon and share a drink for a tender bond."]}},3092,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_8_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const t={Aries:["You meet crisis head-on and may recover quickly from shocks, sometimes before you have felt them. Intimacy is passionate and direct, and you want honesty in bed and in money. Shared finances may bring quarrels, so clear agreements help. The growth is letting vulnerability in rather than fighting every change, and grieving as well as acting.","At the dark moon, light a red candle and name a change you will stop resisting; let it burn down."],Taurus:["You want security in intimacy and in shared resources, and you may resist change long after it has come. Inheritances, joint property and debts are matters of real weight. Touch and loyalty matter in love. The growth is letting go of what you cannot keep, and finding that what is real stays.","Bury a coin wrapped in a bay leaf in earth at the dark moon, for the renewal of shared resources."],Gemini:["You think and talk your way through crises, and you may be curious about death, sex, money and the hidden, reading widely about them. Intimacy may begin with words. The care is staying in your head when feelings need to be felt. The growth is letting knowledge become understanding.","Write a question about a mystery on paper at the dark moon and keep it under a black stone until the next."],Cancer:["Intimacy needs emotional safety, and you may take a long time to trust. Crises often touch family, and inheritances may come through family, with feelings attached. Grief may be deep and long. The growth is trusting others with your feelings and letting old griefs be held.","At the dark moon, bathe in water with a handful of salt and name an old family grief to release."],Leo:["You meet crisis with courage and pride, and you may want to be strong for everyone. Intimacy is warm and generous. The care is pride that refuses help or hides pain. The growth is letting others see you in hard times, which deepens love rather than weakening it.","At the dark moon, light a gold candle and speak a fear aloud to someone you trust."],Virgo:["You manage crises practically and may be good with shared finances, wills and paperwork. Intimacy may be cautious and careful. The care is control and worry. The growth is letting go of what you cannot fix, and letting intimacy be imperfect.","At the dark moon, write a worry on paper, burn it, and sweep the ashes out of the door."],Libra:["Shared resources may come through partners, and fairness in intimacy and money matters greatly. You may avoid conflict over money until it is pressing. The growth is honest negotiation of power, desire and resources, with neither person giving way too much.","Balance two coins on a rose quartz at the dark moon, for fair shared resources and honest intimacy."],Scorpio:["This is Scorpio's own house: depth, intensity and transformation are natural to you. You may be gifted in crisis, research, therapy or the occult, and unafraid of the dark. The care is control, secrecy or jealousy. The growth is using power well, and letting change change you.","Keep a death and rebirth rite with a black candle at each dark moon and a white one lit from it at the new."],Sagittarius:["You meet crisis with faith and optimism, and shared resources may come with luck. You may be drawn to philosophies of death and rebirth. The care is skipping past pain with hope. The growth is facing the dark as well as the light.","At the dark moon, light a blue candle for faith through change and read a passage that steadies you."],Capricorn:["You meet crisis with endurance and may manage shared resources very responsibly. Intimacy may be slow to build, and trust earned over years. The care is coldness or fear of losing control. The growth is trust. You may handle wills, debts and shared property for others because you are the reliable one. Grief may be held in and expressed late. Let yourself lean on someone in hard times, and let the long view you naturally take include the healing that slow trust brings.","At the dark moon on a Saturday, bury salt with a written fear and walk away without looking back."],Aquarius:["Crises may come suddenly, and intimacy needs freedom and friendship. You may be detached in a crisis, which helps others. The care is detachment from your own feelings. The growth is staying present in change.","At an eclipse, write what you are ready to change on paper and release it to the wind."],Pisces:["Boundaries in intimacy may blur, and you may be psychically sensitive to others' pain. Shared money needs extra care. You may be drawn to mediumship or grief work. The growth is clear agreements and a grounded practice.","Before spirit work, draw a circle of salt and hold a black stone to bring you back."]}},3093,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_9_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_10_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_11_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CUSP_12_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}});const o={Aries:["Beliefs arrive like conversions: you may take up a cause, a faith or a philosophy in a rush of conviction and defend it hotly. Travel tends to be spontaneous, and you learn best by doing rather than by sitting in lectures. The growth is letting a belief be tested without feeling attacked, and finding that a faith which can be questioned is stronger for it. Teach by example more than by argument.","Before a journey or a course of study, light a red candle and vow to learn with courage and an open mind; carry Carnelian on the first day."],Taurus:["Your beliefs are grounded in experience and the senses: you may find the sacred in a garden, a meal, the turning seasons or the body itself, and distrust ideas you cannot feel. Travel tends to be slow, comfortable and to beautiful places. Study suits you when it is practical. The growth is letting your faith move when life moves, rather than holding to a view because it is familiar.","Make a pilgrimage to a beautiful natural place on a Friday and leave a flower or a little bread in thanks for what the earth has taught you."],Gemini:["You are a sampler of ideas, drawn to many teachings, books and courses, and you may hold several beliefs at once without much trouble. Travel is frequent and often short, and you learn by talking to people where you go. The care is collecting ideas without letting any change you. The growth is choosing one path to go deeper with, while keeping your lively curiosity.","On a Wednesday, read a page from a different sacred or philosophical text and write one line in your book on what it asks of you."],Cancer:["Faith may be rooted in family, childhood or a deep sense of belonging, and you may feel most spiritual at home or among your own people. Travel may take you to ancestral places, or you may make a home abroad. The growth is making faith your own: keeping what nourishes from what you were given, and letting go gently of what does not.","Visit a place your ancestors lived, or hold a picture of it, and leave a small offering of water while you name what you inherit and what you choose."],Leo:["You hold beliefs with warmth and pride, and you may be a natural teacher, preacher or storyteller of what you believe. Travel may be grand or celebratory. Study goes well when you can make it creative. The care is needing to be the authority. The growth is humility in faith: remaining a student, glad to learn from anyone.","On a Sunday, light a gold candle and give thanks aloud for three things you have learned this year, and for who taught you."],Virgo:["Your faith is practical and often expressed through service, and you may study carefully, testing teachings against evidence and experience. Travel may be for work or study. The care is a critical mind that dismisses what it cannot measure. The growth is letting the sacred include what cannot be proved, alongside what can.","Keep a plain study notebook for your spiritual path and write in it each Wednesday, noting both what you learned and what you still doubt."],Libra:["Faith may be shaped by partners, friends or a love of beauty, fairness and harmony, and you may be drawn to ethics, law, art or philosophies of balance. Travel is often with a companion. The care is borrowing a partner's beliefs. The growth is finding a faith of your own that can sit beside theirs.","On a Friday, share a spiritual question with a partner or friend, listen fully to their answer, and then write your own."],Scorpio:["Faith is deep and transforming, and you may be drawn to mysteries, initiation, the occult and teachings that face death squarely. Travel may change you profoundly. The care is fanaticism or secrecy. The growth is a faith that stays open to question, even as it goes deep.","Study one mystery tradition through a year, and mark each step with a black candle at the dark moon and a note in your book."],Sagittarius:["This is Sagittarius's own house, so faith, study, travel and teaching come naturally, and you may live abroad, publish or teach for a living. Your optimism is infectious. The care is preaching, or never settling to one path. The growth is staying a student as well as a teacher, and letting experience test your beliefs.","Bibliomancy on a Thursday: ask a clear question, open a sacred book at random and read where your finger falls, then sit with the answer."],Capricorn:["Faith is earned through discipline, and you may study formally, join a structured tradition or come to faith late in life after long thought. Travel may be for work or delayed until later. The care is a cold or rule-bound faith. The growth is a belief with warmth as well as structure, and a practice kept with joy.","On a Saturday, set a regular hour for study and keep it as a vow for a full season, lighting a single black candle each time."],Aquarius:["Faith is original and may be unconventional, scientific, humanist or radical, and you may build your own philosophy from many sources. Travel may be sudden or to unusual places. Astrology itself often appeals. The care is a new dogma replacing an old one. The growth is keeping an open mind as well as an original one.","Read the sky each month, noting the planets you can see and what they mean to you, and keep the notes as your own sacred text."],Pisces:["Faith is mystical and may embrace many paths, with a sense of the sacred everywhere. Travel may be to the sea, to holy places or into the imagination. The care is idealising teachers or drifting between faiths. The growth is discernment: testing teachers by their conduct, and trusting your own experience.","Make a pilgrimage to water, a holy well, river or the sea, and leave an offering of a flower or clean water."]},t={Aries:["You want to lead, pioneer and build your own path in the world, and you may change careers boldly or start your own ventures. A parent may have been forceful or competitive. Authority figures may be challenged until you become one. The growth is patience with the long climb, and leading by courage rather than force.","At noon on a Tuesday, write your career goal and burn it in a red candle's flame, asking for courage rather than conquest."],Taurus:["You build your career steadily, often in finance, art, craft, food, land or beauty, and you want success that lasts and pays. You may stay in one field for years and become known for reliability. A parent may have valued security. The growth is embracing change when it serves you, rather than holding on from habit.","Keep a piece of Green Aventurine at your workplace and touch it each Friday, asking for steady, lasting success."],Gemini:["Your career may be in communication, writing, teaching, media or trade, and you may have more than one at once, or change often. Your reputation may rest on your words and wit. A parent may have been clever or restless. The growth is focus and follow-through, so that your many talents build one name.","Write your calling in one sentence on a Wednesday, fold it small and keep it in your wallet as a reminder."],Cancer:["Your career may involve care, food, home, history, property or the public, and you may be known as a nurturer. A parent, often the mother, may have shaped your ambitions strongly. Public life may rise and fall with moods. The growth is balancing home and work, so that neither starves.","At the full moon, bless your work tools with moon water and a word of thanks for the work that feeds you."],Leo:["You want a career where you can shine, lead and create, and you may be known for warmth and presence. A parent may have been proud or dramatic. Recognition matters to you. The growth is leading with generosity, so that your light helps others shine too.","At noon on a Sunday, light a gold candle with a sprig of calendula for your public life and its generosity."],Virgo:["Your career may involve service, health, detail, analysis or craft, and you are known for skill and reliability. A parent may have been exacting. You may undervalue yourself at work. The growth is seeing your worth as clearly as you see what needs fixing, and asking for it.","On a Wednesday, write the skills you bring to your work and keep the list on the altar beside a sprig of lavender."],Libra:["Your career may involve art, design, law, diplomacy or partnership, and you are known for grace and fairness. A parent may have valued appearances. You may do best working with a partner. The growth is making decisions and standing by them, even when not everyone is pleased.","Place a rose quartz at your workplace for grace in public life, and cleanse it each Friday."],Scorpio:["Your career may involve power, research, healing, finance or transformation, and you may be known as formidable or private. A parent may have been powerful. You may rebuild your career more than once. The growth is integrity: using power in public as you would want it used on you.","At noon at the dark moon, burn a written statement of how you will use power in your work, and keep the ashes with Obsidian."],Sagittarius:["Your career may involve teaching, travel, law, publishing or faith, and you may be known for vision and enthusiasm. A parent may have been a seeker or a believer. The care is promising more than you deliver. The growth is follow-through, so that the vision becomes a body of work.","On a Thursday, bless your work with a blue candle and a bay leaf, asking for luck matched with steady effort."],Capricorn:["This is Capricorn's own house, so career and ambition are central, and you may rise steadily to real authority. A parent may have been strict or absent through work. Success often comes later and lasts. The care is sacrificing everything to status. The growth is warmth on the climb.","At noon on a Saturday, light a black candle over a written plan for the next year, asking for patience and endurance."],Aquarius:["Your career may be unusual, technological, scientific or humanitarian, and you may be known as an innovator or a rebel. A parent may have been unconventional or distant. You may change direction suddenly. The growth is staying the course long enough for your ideas to take root.","Write three possible futures for your work and keep them under Clear Quartz for a lunar month; act on the one that keeps calling."],Pisces:["Your career may be in the arts, healing, charity or spiritual work, and your public image may be hard to pin down or misunderstood. A parent may have been absent or idealised. The care is drifting. The growth is clarity: a plain plan alongside the dream.","At noon, write the dream of your work and the first practical step beneath it; burn the dream and keep the step."]},n={Aries:["You may lead groups, start movements or gather friends around a cause, and you are loyal in a fight. Friendships may begin quickly and burn bright, and quarrels may be quick too. The growth is staying through disagreements and letting others lead sometimes, so that the group belongs to everyone.","Before a group working, pass a red cord round the circle so each person holds it, and tie one knot for the shared aim."],Taurus:["Friendships are steady and lasting, and you value practical, loyal friends who show up with soup when you are ill. Groups may centre on food, craft, music, gardening or the land. You may keep the same friends for decades. The growth is welcoming new friends as well as keeping the old.","Share a meal with friends on a Friday and pour the first drop of drink as an offering for the friendship."],Gemini:["You have many friends and acquaintances, and your groups may be lively, talkative and full of ideas. You may network easily and connect people to each other. The care is many light friendships and few deep ones. The growth is giving time to the few who matter most.","Write a letter by hand to an old friend on a Wednesday and post it, with a sprig of lavender folded inside."],Cancer:["Friends become family, and you may nurture groups or host gatherings at home. You may stay loyal to childhood friends. Hopes for the future often centre on home and family. The growth is letting friends care for you in turn, rather than always being the one who looks after.","Host a gathering at home at the full moon, with a shared dish and a candle lit for the friendships."],Leo:["You may lead or shine in groups, and your friends are warm, loyal and fun. Creative groups, theatre and celebration suit you. Hopes are big and generous. The care is needing to be the centre. The growth is sharing the stage and celebrating others.","Light a gold candle for friends on a Sunday and name each one aloud, with a word of thanks."],Virgo:["Friends are helpful and practical, and your groups may serve a cause, a craft or a community. You may be the one who organises. The care is criticism of friends or of the group. The growth is celebrating people as they are. You may join groups that do practical good: volunteers, crafts, health or local causes. Friends know they can rely on you. Let friendship also be for fun, not only for usefulness, and let others help you as often as you help them.","Do a practical kindness for a friend on a Wednesday, quietly, and let that be the spell."],Libra:["Friends are graceful, sociable and often artistic, and you value harmony and beauty in groups. You may make friends through partners. The care is avoiding conflict in friendship. The growth is honest disagreement held with kindness. Your friendships tend to be graceful and fair, and you may bring people together and keep the peace in groups. You may make friends through partners or art. Let friends see your own opinions; honest disagreement is a sign of a real friendship.","Give flowers to a friend on a Friday, with a word of thanks for the friendship."],Scorpio:["Friends are few and deep, and your groups may be intense, private or concerned with hidden matters. Betrayal by a friend may cut deep. The growth is trust after hurt, and choosing friends who can meet you in depth.","At the dark moon, write a wish for a friendship and burn it in a black candle's flame."],Sagittarius:["Friends are adventurous and may come from far places, and your groups may share a faith, a philosophy or a love of travel. Hopes are broad and optimistic. The care is moving on before friendships deepen. The growth is commitment. You may make friends across borders, faiths and backgrounds, and your hopes are generous and wide. Groups that travel, study or worship together suit you. The gift is a sense of a larger family; keep in touch with the friends you meet along the way.","Share a journey with friends and bless it before you set out with a sprig of sage."],Capricorn:["Friends are loyal and often older, and your groups may be professional or traditional. You may come to friendship slowly and keep friends for life. The care is seriousness. The growth is warmth and play among friends.","Give a small, lasting gift to an old friend on a Saturday, with thanks for the years."],Aquarius:["This is Aquarius's own house, so friends, groups and causes are central to your life, and your hopes may be for humanity as well as yourself. You may belong to many circles. The care is breadth without closeness. The growth is closeness as well as breadth.","Host a working for a shared future at the new moon: each friend writes a hope, and all are woven into one cord."],Pisces:["Friends are sensitive, artistic or spiritual, and your groups may be compassionate or devotional. You may be drawn to help friends in trouble. The care is losing yourself in others' needs. The growth is boundaries in friendship. You may belong to spiritual, artistic or caring circles, and friends may lean on you for comfort. Your hopes for the world are compassionate. Keep friendships honest and balanced, and let some friends care for you in return.","Lead a shared visualisation with friends at the full moon, with a bowl of water at the centre."]},s={Aries:["Anger and drive may be hidden, even from you, and may surface suddenly or turn inward as tension. Solitary physical practice, walking, running or a martial art done alone, helps you meet that fire. The growth is noticing anger early and giving it a clean outlet, so that it becomes quiet courage.","In a quiet Mars hour, write what makes you angry and keep it under a black stone until you can act calmly."],Taurus:["Hidden comforts and quiet pleasures restore you, and you may need nature, music and time alone to recover from the world. You may hold a private stubbornness. The growth is not hiding in comfort, and letting your quiet strength be known. You may need time in nature, a garden or a quiet room with good food and music to recover from the world. Private comforts are healing, as long as they do not become a hiding place. Hidden steadiness helps others when they are lost.","Walk alone in a garden on a Friday and leave an offering of a flower beneath a tree."],Gemini:["Your mind is busy behind the scenes, and you may write privately, talk to yourself or lie awake thinking. Secret thoughts can be a gift for fiction and reflection. The growth is quieting the inner chatter through journalling or meditation.","Keep a private journal and write in it each night before sleep, to empty the mind onto the page."],Cancer:["Hidden feelings and family memories live here, and you may cry alone or keep your needs secret. You may care for others in hidden ways. The growth is gentle healing, and letting a few trusted people see your tender side. You may care for others quietly, out of sight, and need the same care in return. Memories of home and family may surface in dreams. A small private ritual each night, a cup, a candle, a word of comfort, lets the tide of feeling settle.","Keep a bowl of water by the bed and pour it out each morning with the night's feelings."],Leo:["Hidden pride or creativity may need expression, and you may shine in private long before public. You may help others secretly. The growth is letting the light out, a little at a time.","Make art alone and keep it as an offering to your hidden self, then show one piece to someone you trust."],Virgo:["Hidden worries and self-criticism may need care, and you may serve quietly in hospitals, retreats or behind the scenes. The growth is self-compassion: the same care you give others. You may serve quietly and notice others' needs without being asked, and also criticise yourself in private. Hidden service, in hospitals, retreats or care, can be deeply satisfying. Rest without earning it, and let small mistakes go.","Brew chamomile tea at night and name your worries one by one, setting each down with the cup."],Libra:["Hidden longing for peace or partnership may shape you, and you may keep the peace at a cost to yourself. Secret loves are possible. The growth is inner balance that does not depend on others. You may give way in private to keep the peace and then feel the cost alone. Quiet time with beauty, music or art restores your balance. Some with Libra here find a hidden partner in prayer, a muse or an inner companion who steadies them.","Place rose petals by the bed on a Friday and ask for peace within, not only around you."],Scorpio:["Hidden depths and secrets live here, and you may have strong intuition and a gift for working with others' pain. The care is buried resentment. The growth is shadow work, done with support. You may sense hidden things in people and places, and carry strong feelings that rarely show. Solitary practices of depth, journalling, therapy, divination, help you know yourself. Your quiet strength helps others in their darkest hours.","Keep a shadow journal by a black candle at the dark moon, writing one thing you have hidden."],Sagittarius:["A hidden faith and a sense of a protective guardian may carry you through hard times. You may find meaning in retreat or solitude. The growth is trusting that protection, and acting on it. Faith may be private and hard to explain, but it has carried you through more than once. Retreats, long walks and reading in solitude restore you. Trust the quiet sense that you are looked after, and let it make you generous to others in hidden ways.","Ask for a dream of guidance on a Thursday, with a bay leaf under your pillow."],Capricorn:["Hidden fears and responsibilities may weigh on you, often from an old sense of duty or guilt. You may work hard behind the scenes. The growth is rest, and letting go of burdens that were never yours. Many with Capricorn here carry a private sense of duty from childhood, as if they must earn their rest. Solitude spent building something slowly, a practice, a skill, a garden, is healing. Ask who first gave you the burden, and whether it is still yours to carry.","Write a fear on paper and keep it under a bowl of salt until the next new moon, then bury the salt."],Aquarius:["Hidden rebellion and sudden intuitions live here, and you may have flashes of insight in solitude or dreams. The growth is calm: a practice that lets the inner lightning settle. Your intuition may come in sudden flashes, often in solitude, and you may feel quietly apart from the crowd. Time alone with ideas restores you. Meditation and walking help the inner lightning settle into insight you can use.","Keep a dream book with Amethyst by the bed, and note every sudden insight on waking."],Pisces:["This is Pisces's own house, so the inner world is rich and the boundary with the unseen thin. You may need much solitude. The growth is grounded practice that gives the sensitivity a channel. Dreams, music, prayer and the sea are your medicine, and you may sense what others feel before they speak. Give the sensitivity a regular form, a daily practice or a quiet hour, so that it nourishes you rather than overwhelms you.","Keep a small hidden shrine, a box or drawer, with a shell, a candle and a written prayer."]}},3094,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SUN_IN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n={Aries:{simple:'With the Sun in Aries you come alive by beginning things. You are brave, direct and honest, happiest when there is a challenge to meet head-on.',detailed:'The Sun is exalted in Aries, the sign of the spring equinox, and here it burns clean and quick. Your sense of self is built by acting: you learn who you are by trying, starting, competing and standing up for what you believe. You tend to say what you think and move before others have finished deciding.\n\nThe growth for an Aries Sun is in staying: learning patience with the middle of things, and letting other people arrive at their own pace. Mars, your Sun\'s ruler, shows by its sign and house where that fire most wants to go.',magic:'Your natural magic is fire and beginnings: candle work, courage and protection spells, cord cutting, and anything that clears a path. Tuesdays and Mars hours suit you, as does Aries season and the waxing crescent. Carnelian, bloodstone, basil and nettle are allies.',shadow:'Impatience, picking fights you don\'t need, and leaving a trail of brilliant starts.'},Taurus:{simple:'With the Sun in Taurus you are steady, sensual and loyal. You build slowly and well, and you know the worth of comfort, beauty and things that last.',detailed:'Venus rules Taurus, and with your Sun here you find yourself through the body and the senses: good food, music, touch, land, making something real with your hands. You are patient, reliable and hard to rush; once you have chosen, you stay.\n\nThe growth for a Taurus Sun is in change: trusting that letting go can make room for something better, and that your worth is not the same as what you own. Where Venus sits in your chart shows what you most love and value.',magic:'Earth magic suits you: herbs, gardens, money and prosperity work, home blessings, slow candle spells over several nights, and charm bags you carry. Fridays and Venus hours, Beltane and a Taurus moon are your times. Rose quartz, emerald, rose and thyme are allies.',shadow:'Stubbornness, holding on past time, and comfort that turns into a rut.'},Gemini:{simple:'With the Sun in Gemini you are curious, quick and talkative. You light up with ideas, conversation and learning, and you see more than one side of everything.',detailed:'Mercury rules Gemini, and your self is a moving thing: you find out who you are by asking questions, meeting people and trying on ideas. You are adaptable, witty and good at linking people and information.\n\nThe growth for a Gemini Sun is depth: following one thread long enough to see where it goes, and trusting feelings as well as thoughts. Mercury\'s sign and house in your chart show how your mind likes to work.',magic:'Air and word magic: petitions, letter spells, sigils, divination, study and travel blessings. Wednesdays and Mercury hours suit you. Agate, citrine, lavender and mint are allies.',shadow:'Scattering, restlessness, and talking around a feeling instead of through it.'},Cancer:{simple:'With the Sun in Cancer you are caring, protective and deeply feeling. Home, family and the people you belong to are at the centre of who you are.',detailed:'The Moon rules Cancer, so your Sun takes on lunar qualities: you are intuitive, responsive and tied to memory and roots. You build safety for others and fight fiercely for those you love; your shell protects a very soft heart.\n\nThe growth for a Cancer Sun is in letting yourself be cared for too, and in feeling your feelings without being ruled by every tide. The Moon\'s sign and phase at your birth say a great deal about you.',magic:'Water, moon and hearth magic: kitchen witchery, home protection, ancestor offerings, moon water, healing baths and dreamwork. Mondays and Moon hours, and every full moon, are your times. Moonstone, pearl, lemon balm and jasmine are allies.',shadow:'Moodiness, worry dressed as care, and retreating into the shell when hurt.'},Leo:{simple:'With the Sun in Leo you are warm, generous and creative. You shine, you lead with your heart, and you love to make others feel special.',detailed:'The Sun is at home in Leo, and here it shows itself fully: you are expressive, loyal, playful and proud, with a strong need to create and to be seen for who you are. People gather round your warmth.\n\nThe growth for a Leo Sun is in shining for the joy of it rather than for applause, and in letting others have the stage too. Your Sun\'s house shows where you are meant to shine.',magic:'Sun and fire magic: confidence and glamour spells, creative work offered as devotion, success and recognition, and celebration rites. Sundays and Sun hours, Lughnasadh and Leo season are yours. Sunstone, citrine, calendula and sunflower are allies.',shadow:'Pride, needing praise, and drama when you feel unseen.'},Virgo:{simple:'With the Sun in Virgo you are thoughtful, skilful and helpful. You notice details, love to improve things, and show care through practical acts.',detailed:'Mercury rules Virgo and is exalted here, and your mind is precise and discerning. You find yourself through craft, service, health and doing a thing well; you are often the one who quietly makes everything work.\n\nThe growth for a Virgo Sun is in self-acceptance: letting yourself be good enough, and turning your keen eye with kindness on yourself. Mercury\'s place in your chart shows how you analyse and serve.',magic:'Herbcraft, healing work (beside proper care), cleansing and purification, kitchen and household magic, and well-ordered ritual. Wednesdays and Mercury hours, and the harvest season of Mabon, suit you. Amazonite, moss agate, fennel and lavender are allies.',shadow:'Perfectionism, worry and criticism turned inward.'},Libra:{simple:'With the Sun in Libra you are gracious, fair and drawn to beauty and harmony. You understand people and you thrive in partnership.',detailed:'Venus rules Libra, and the Sun is in fall here: your self is found through others, through relationship, fairness and balance rather than through standing alone. You are diplomatic, aesthetic and keen on justice, and good at seeing every side.\n\nThe growth for a Libra Sun is in knowing your own mind and saying it, even when it unsettles the peace. Venus\'s sign and house show what you love and how you relate.',magic:'Love and friendship work, harmony and reconciliation, justice spells, beauty and glamour, and partnership blessings. Fridays and Venus hours, and the balance of Mabon, are yours. Rose quartz, lapis, rose and violet are allies.',shadow:'Indecision, people-pleasing, and keeping the peace instead of making it.'},Scorpio:{simple:'With the Sun in Scorpio you are intense, loyal and private. You go deep, you see what others miss, and you are not afraid of life\'s hidden places.',detailed:'Mars rules Scorpio traditionally and Pluto in modern astrology, and both speak to your strength: you are determined, perceptive and transformative. You find yourself through depth, intimacy, crisis and renewal, and you can rebuild after almost anything.\n\nThe growth for a Scorpio Sun is in trust: letting yourself be known, and letting go of control and old hurts. Mars and Pluto in your chart show how your power moves.',magic:'Shadow work, transformation, banishing and protection, psychic work, death and ancestor work, and the mysteries. Tuesdays and Mars hours, Samhain and the dark moon are your times. Obsidian, garnet, wormwood and pomegranate are allies.',shadow:'Secrecy, jealousy, control, and holding a grudge as protection.'},Sagittarius:{simple:'With the Sun in Sagittarius you are free, honest and hopeful. You love to explore, learn and find meaning, and you lift others with your humour.',detailed:'Jupiter rules Sagittarius, and your self is found on the road: travel, study, faith, philosophy and adventure. You are generous, frank and optimistic, a natural teacher and seeker.\n\nThe growth for a Sagittarius Sun is in commitment and in tact: staying with what matters and aiming your honesty with care. Jupiter\'s place in your chart shows where your faith and luck grow.',magic:'Luck and expansion work, travel blessings, learning, devotion and deity work, and divination for the bigger picture. Thursdays and Jupiter hours suit you. Turquoise, lapis, sage and clove are allies.',shadow:'Restlessness, over-promising, and bluntness that wounds.'},Capricorn:{simple:'With the Sun in Capricorn you are ambitious, patient and responsible. You climb steadily, build things that last, and have a dry, quiet humour.',detailed:'Saturn rules Capricorn, and your self is built through effort, mastery and time: you often grow younger in spirit as you age. You are practical, disciplined and reliable, someone others lean on.\n\nThe growth for a Capricorn Sun is in rest and tenderness: letting achievement be a choice, not your worth. Saturn\'s place in your chart shows where you are building your mastery.',magic:'Career and goal work, long-term spells, boundaries and protection, binding, ancestor and land work. Saturdays and Saturn hours, Yule and the winter dark suit you. Onyx, jet, garnet, comfrey and cypress are allies.',shadow:'Coldness under pressure, overwork, and fear of failure.'},Aquarius:{simple:'With the Sun in Aquarius you are independent, inventive and idealistic. You think for yourself, care about the wider world, and value friendship deeply.',detailed:'Saturn rules Aquarius traditionally and Uranus in modern astrology, and your self holds both: you are principled and steady in your ideals, and original, even rebellious, in how you live them. You find yourself in community, causes and the future.\n\nThe growth for an Aquarius Sun is in closeness: letting individual people in as warmly as you hold humanity. Saturn and Uranus in your chart show how you build and how you break the mould.',magic:'Community and coven work, breaking habits and bindings, innovation, freedom spells, and work for causes. Saturdays and Saturn hours, Imbolc and Aquarius season suit you. Amethyst, aquamarine, labradorite and lavender are allies.',shadow:'Detachment, contrariness, and keeping feelings at arm\'s length.'},Pisces:{simple:'With the Sun in Pisces you are compassionate, imaginative and intuitive. You feel the world deeply and you are drawn to art, spirit and dreams.',detailed:'Jupiter rules Pisces traditionally and Neptune in modern astrology, and Venus is exalted here: your self is porous, kind and creative. You find yourself through empathy, imagination, devotion and the life of the spirit, and you can sense what is unsaid.\n\nThe growth for a Pisces Sun is in boundaries and grounding: keeping your gifts your own, and knowing which feelings are yours. Jupiter and Neptune in your chart show how your faith and dreams move.',magic:'Dreamwork, divination, meditation and trance, water and moon magic, spiritual healing, and devotion. Thursdays and Jupiter hours, and the dark and new moon, suit you. Amethyst, aquamarine, mugwort and jasmine are allies.',shadow:'Escapism, losing yourself in others, and avoiding hard edges.'}}},3095,[]);
__d(function(g,r,_i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TRANSITING_BODIES",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return h}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TRANSIT_TARGETS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return u}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TRANSIT_ASPECTS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return l}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TRANSIT_VOICE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return p}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TRANSIT_TARGET_NOTE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return f}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CYCLE_READINGS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return A}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TRANSIT_DEEPER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return S}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TRANSIT_READINGS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return N}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"RETURN_GUIDES",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return j}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"RETURN_HOUSE_READINGS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return R}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PROGRESSED_MOON_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return O}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PROGRESSED_MOON_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return P}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PROGRESSED_PHASE_READINGS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return I}});var t=r(d[0]),n=r(d[1]),o=r(d[2]),s=r(d[3]),i=r(d[4]);const h=['Jupiter','Saturn','Uranus','Neptune','Pluto','Chiron','North Node'],u=['Sun','Moon','Mercury','Venus','Mars','Ascendant','Midheaven'],l=['conjunction','sextile','square','trine','opposition'],c=['first','second','third','fourth','fifth','sixth','seventh','eighth','ninth','tenth','eleventh','twelfth'],y={conjunction:'conjunction',square:'hard',opposition:'hard',trine:'soft',sextile:'soft'},p={Jupiter:'Jupiter takes about twelve years to go round the zodiac, so its transits last a few weeks, or a few months when it turns retrograde across the point. They bring growth, help and a wider view.',Saturn:'Saturn takes about twenty-nine years round the zodiac; its transits last months and often come in three passes (direct, retrograde, direct again). They bring tests, structure and things that last.',Uranus:'Uranus takes eighty-four years round the zodiac; its transits build over a year or two, with sudden moments inside them. They bring awakenings, freedom and change.',Neptune:'Neptune takes about 165 years round the zodiac; its transits are slow and misty, lasting a year or two. They bring dissolving, longing, compassion and spiritual opening.',Pluto:'Pluto takes about 248 years round the zodiac; its transits last two years or more and work deep. They bring endings, power and rebirth.',Chiron:'Chiron takes about fifty years round the zodiac, moving fast in some signs and slowly in others; its transits last months. They bring old hurts to the surface to be tended.','North Node':'The nodes move backwards through the zodiac in about 18.6 years, staying around a year and a half in each sign; eclipses happen near them. The North Node points forward to growth; the South Node, opposite, to release.'},f={Sun:'Your natal Sun is your core self, vitality and purpose.',Moon:'Your natal Moon is your feelings, needs, body rhythms and home.',Mercury:'Your natal Mercury is how you think, learn, speak and move about.',Venus:'Your natal Venus is love, pleasure, money and what you value.',Mars:'Your natal Mars is drive, courage, anger and the body\'s energy.',Ascendant:'Your Ascendant is your body, manner and the direction of your life; a transit to it is felt personally, and a transit opposite it falls on your Descendant, the place of partners.',Midheaven:'Your Midheaven is your vocation and public life; a transit opposite it falls on the IC, home and roots.'},w={conjunction:'The conjunction is the start of a new cycle between the two: the most strongly felt of the transits.',square:'The square is a turning point felt from within: pressure to act or change, often felt as frustration until you do.',opposition:'The opposition is the cycle\'s full moon: what began at the conjunction comes to light, often through other people or events.',trine:'The trine is easy and supportive, so it can pass unnoticed; use it on purpose.',sextile:'The sextile is an opening that needs a small step from you.'},b={conjunction:'',square:' As a square, it pushes from within.',opposition:' As an opposition, it often comes through other people.',trine:' As a trine, it flows; use it.',sextile:' As a sextile, it opens a door you choose to walk through.'},k={Jupiter:'Jupiter\'s help comes on Thursdays and in Jupiter hours, with blue or purple candles, sage, oak and lapis.',Saturn:'Saturn\'s help comes on Saturdays and in Saturn hours, with black candles, salt, cypress and onyx.',Uranus:'Uranus answers sudden, inventive work: storm water, clear quartz and a working done the moment it occurs to you.',Neptune:'Neptune answers water and dream: moon water, sea salt, amethyst and a dream journal kept by the bed.',Pluto:'Pluto answers the dark moon: obsidian, a black candle and something written and burned.',Chiron:'Chiron answers healing arts: yarrow, comfrey, chamomile and a green candle.','North Node':'The nodes answer the eclipse seasons: a black and a white candle lit together, and dragon\'s blood.'},v={conjunction:'Begin the working as the transit begins and renew it at each pass.',square:'Work at the exact square to turn pressure into action.',opposition:'Work at the exact opposition to bring what is hidden into balance.',trine:'Work while the trine lasts to make the most of the ease.',sextile:'Work while the sextile lasts, and act on it within days.'},A={[i.keys.transit('Jupiter','conjunction','Jupiter')]:{simple:'Your Jupiter return, about every twelve years (around 12, 24, 36, 48, 60, 72, 84): a new cycle of growth, faith and opportunity begins.',detailed:'Jupiter comes back to its birth place roughly every twelve years. Each return opens a new chapter of growth: a time to widen your world through study, travel, faith or generosity, and to notice what you now believe. Many people remember their Jupiter returns as times of new beginnings, moving, or meeting a teacher.\n\nRead the return through Jupiter\'s natal sign and house, which show where the growth wants to happen. The year before is often a time of clearing space.',magic:'A Jupiter return is a season for blessing and increase: a gratitude rite, a new altar to your guides, a vow to learn something for twelve years. Thursdays, blue and purple candles, oak, bay and sage.'},[i.keys.transit('Jupiter','opposition','Jupiter')]:{simple:'About six years after each Jupiter return: the growth begun then is tested by the wider world, and you see what it has become.',detailed:'Halfway round its twelve-year cycle, transiting Jupiter opposes its natal place. What you reached for at the last return is now in full view, sometimes as success, sometimes as overreach. Other people, teachers and institutions often show you where you have grown and where you have promised too much.\n\nIt is a time to share what you have, and to rebalance faith with good sense.',magic:'Work a gratitude and sharing rite: give away something from your abundance, and bless what has grown.'},[i.keys.transit('Saturn','conjunction','Saturn')]:{simple:'Your Saturn return, around 29, 58 and 87: a coming of age, when life asks you to build on what is truly yours and let go of the rest.',detailed:'Saturn takes about twenty-nine and a half years to go round the zodiac, so it returns to its birth place in your late twenties, late fifties and late eighties. The first return is astrology\'s best-known transit: a coming of age when the life you inherited or drifted into is tested. Careers, relationships, homes and beliefs that don\'t fit often end, and what is real is built on.\n\nIt can feel heavy, and it lasts about two years from first to last pass. Many people look back on it as the time they became themselves. The second return asks what your elder years are for; the third is a harvest of wisdom.',magic:'A Saturn return is a time for vows and foundations: a dedication, a rite of passage, a commitment to a path or practice. Saturdays, black and indigo candles, salt, cypress and onyx; honour your elders and ancestors, and bind away what you are leaving behind.',shadow:'Fear, heaviness and clinging to structures that are ending.'},[i.keys.transit('Saturn','square','Saturn')]:{simple:'Around 7, 21, 36, 51 and 66, Saturn squares its natal place: a checkpoint where structures are tested and must be adjusted.',detailed:'Between returns, transiting Saturn squares its natal place twice: the waxing square (about seven years after a return) and the waning square (about seven years before the next). Each is a checkpoint. At the waxing square, what you began must be built upon or abandoned; at the waning square, what you built is examined and what no longer serves starts to be cleared.\n\nThese squares often coincide with changes in school, work or family. Steady effort and honest review carry you through.',magic:'Work a checking and mending rite: tidy the altar, renew wards and protections, and recommit to the practices that hold you.'},[i.keys.transit('Saturn','opposition','Saturn')]:{simple:'Around 14\u201315, 44 and 73, Saturn opposes its natal place: a time of reckoning with others, authority and the shape of your life.',detailed:'Halfway through its cycle, Saturn opposes its natal position. In adolescence it marks the push against rules and parents; in midlife it often brings career peaks or crises and a hard look at commitments; later it is a review before the third return.\n\nThe opposition shows the structure of your life from the outside, often through other people\'s demands. It asks for balance between duty and self.',magic:'Balance work: two candles, black and white, one for your duties and one for yourself, lit together on a Saturday.'},[i.keys.transit('Uranus','square','Uranus')]:{simple:'Around 21 and 63, Uranus squares its natal place: a restless urge for independence and change.',detailed:'Uranus\'s waxing square, around 21, coincides with leaving home, rebellion and finding your own path; the waning square, around 63, often brings retirement, reinvention and a second freedom.\n\nBoth ask you to break with what confines you, and to choose change rather than be ambushed by it.',magic:'Freedom work: untie a knotted cord, gather storm water, write what you are breaking free of and burn it.'},[i.keys.transit('Uranus','opposition','Uranus')]:{simple:'Around 40\u201342, Uranus opposes its natal place: the heart of the midlife awakening, when what you have suppressed asks to live.',detailed:'The Uranus opposition is the classic signature of the midlife turning. Half of Uranus\'s eighty-four-year cycle is done, and parts of you set aside in your twenties ask to be lived. Some people change career, relationships or appearance; others make quieter inner revolutions.\n\nIt often overlaps with Neptune\'s and Pluto\'s squares to themselves, so the early forties can feel like a whole-life reckoning. The gift is authenticity: becoming more yourself while there is time.',magic:'An awakening rite: name what you have kept asleep and invite it in. Clear quartz, electric blue, storm water, and something you have never done before.',shadow:'Breaking things for the sake of it, or refusing all change and calling it peace.'},[i.keys.transit('Neptune','square','Neptune')]:{simple:'Around 39\u201342, Neptune squares its natal place: old dreams dissolve and a deeper longing for meaning appears.',detailed:'Neptune\'s square to itself, part of the midlife transits, often brings disillusionment with goals that once seemed everything, and a pull toward spirit, art or service.\n\nThe fog is a doorway: what dissolves makes room for a truer dream. Avoid escape; make space for devotion.',magic:'Dreamwork and devotion: keep a dream journal through the transit, and make a water offering at each new moon.'},[i.keys.transit('Pluto','square','Pluto')]:{simple:'Pluto squares its natal place in midlife (its timing depends on your generation): a deep reckoning with power, fear and what must end.',detailed:'Because Pluto moves at very different speeds through the signs, people born in the mid-twentieth century met this square around 36\u201340; those born later meet it later. It brings buried matters to the surface: power, control, grief and desire.\n\nIt is a time to face what you have avoided and let something die so that something truer can live.',magic:'Shadow work at the dark moon: obsidian, a black candle, and a written letter to what you are ready to bury.'},[i.keys.transit('Chiron','conjunction','Chiron')]:{simple:'Your Chiron return, around 49\u201351: the old wound comes round again, ready to become your wisdom.',detailed:'Chiron takes about fifty years to complete its orbit, so the return comes around fifty. Many people find their oldest hurts resurfacing, not to wound again but to be finally understood. It is often the time someone becomes a mentor, a healer or a teacher of what they learned the hard way.\n\nRead it through Chiron\'s natal sign and house.',magic:'A healing and elder rite: tend the wound with herbs (yarrow, comfrey, chamomile), then teach or give something from what it taught you.'},[i.keys.transit('North Node','conjunction','North Node')]:{simple:'Your nodal return, about every 18.6 years (around 18\u201319, 37, 56, 74): a reset of direction, often around eclipses.',detailed:'The nodes come back to their birth places about every eighteen and a half years, with eclipses near your natal nodes. These returns often bring meetings, endings and choices that feel destined: leaving home at 18, a change of path at 37, new purpose at 56.\n\nThe North Node\'s sign and house show what you are growing toward; the return asks whether you are walking that way.',magic:'An eclipse-season rite of direction: draw a card or cast lots for your path, and set an intention at the eclipse new moon.'},[i.keys.transit('North Node','opposition','North Node')]:{simple:'About nine years after each nodal return (around 9, 28, 47, 65): the nodal reversal, when old habits and new growth swap places for a while.',detailed:'When the transiting North Node crosses your natal South Node, the familiar and the new are reversed. Old patterns, people or places may come back, sometimes to be released for good.\n\nIt is a time to honour your past and let it go, with eclipses lighting up the axis.',magic:'A release rite at the eclipse full moon: write what you are finishing and give it to running water.'}},S={...o.TRANSIT_DEEPER_A,...s.TRANSIT_DEEPER_B},T={conjunction:0,hard:1,soft:2};const N=(function(){const o={};for(const s of h)for(const h of u){const u=n.TRANSIT_SEEDS[`${s}|${h}`];if(u)for(const n of l){const[l,c]=u[y[n]],A=S[`${s}|${h}`],N=A?.[T[y[n]]],j=N?`${c}\n\n${N}`:c;o[i.keys.transit(s,n,h)]={simple:`${l}${l.length<60?` Transiting ${s} is working on ${t.BODY_WORDS[h]}.`:''}${b[n]}`,detailed:`${(0,i.tidyParagraphs)(j)}\n\n${u.core} ${f[h]} ${w[n]}\n\n${p[s]}`,magic:`${u.magic}${A?` ${A[3]}`:''} ${k[s]} ${v[n]}`}}}return{...o,...A}})(),j={solar:{simple:'A solar return is the chart for the moment the Sun comes back to its exact birth degree, once a year near your birthday. It is read for the year ahead.',detailed:'Cast for the moment of return (and, many say, for where you are that day rather than where you were born), the solar return is a snapshot of the year from one birthday to the next. Read it in steps:\n\n1. The house the Sun falls in: the year\'s main stage.\n2. The rising sign and its ruler: the year\'s tone and how you meet it.\n3. Planets on the angles (close to the Ascendant, Midheaven, Descendant or IC): the year\'s loudest themes.\n4. The Moon\'s sign and house: where feelings and needs gather.\n5. How the return chart lies on your natal chart: return angles on natal planets are strong.\n\nRead it alongside the year\'s transits; the return sets the scene, the transits time the events. Treat it as a weather map, not a script.',magic:'Your solar return is your personal new year: light a candle at the exact moment, write intentions for the year, bless yourself with sun-charged water, and keep the chart in your Grimoire to look back on.',sources:'Solar returns go back to the ancient Greek-speaking and Persian astrologers (Masha\'allah and Abu Ma\'shar wrote on the "revolutions of the years of nativities").'},lunar:{simple:'A lunar return is the chart for each time the Moon comes back to its birth degree, about every 27 days. It is read for the month ahead.',detailed:'The lunar return repeats the solar return\'s method on a monthly scale. Look first at the house the Moon falls in (where your feelings and needs will gather this month), then at the rising sign, and at any planets on the angles.\n\nBecause it comes thirteen times a year, it is best for noticing rhythms: keep a short journal for each return and patterns of mood and energy show themselves over a year.',magic:'Each lunar return is a small personal full moon: refresh your moon water, tend the altar, and set one intention for the month.'}},$=[{solar:'A year about you: your body, appearance and a fresh start. You are the project.',lunar:'A month to focus on yourself, your body and how you feel in it.',magic:'self-blessing and glamour'},{solar:'A year about money, possessions, skills and self-worth. Build security.',lunar:'A month for money, comforts and what you value.',magic:'prosperity jars and money spells'},{solar:'A year of learning, writing, short trips, siblings and neighbours.',lunar:'A busy month of messages, errands and conversations.',magic:'word magic and travel protection'},{solar:'A year about home, family and roots: moving, renovating or tending family.',lunar:'A month to nest, rest at home and tend family.',magic:'home blessing and ancestor offerings'},{solar:'A year of creativity, romance, play and children. Let yourself enjoy it.',lunar:'A month for fun, creativity and love.',magic:'love, joy and creative magic'},{solar:'A year about work, health and daily routine. Build good habits.',lunar:'A month to sort routines, work and health.',magic:'health and cleansing work'},{solar:'A year about partnership: marriage, business partners, or important one-to-one relationships.',lunar:'A month where relationships take the stage.',magic:'partnership and harmony spells'},{solar:'A year of depth: shared money, intimacy, endings and transformation.',lunar:'A month of intensity, shared resources and inner change.',magic:'shadow work and protection'},{solar:'A year of travel, study, belief and big horizons.',lunar:'A month to learn, travel or think about meaning.',magic:'study blessings and journeys'},{solar:'A year about career, reputation and achievement. You are seen.',lunar:'A month focused on work and public life.',magic:'career and success spells'},{solar:'A year of friends, groups, community and hopes for the future.',lunar:'A month for friends and community.',magic:'community and wish magic'},{solar:'A quiet, inward year: rest, retreat, spirituality and endings before a new start.',lunar:'A quiet month: rest, retreat and dreams.',magic:'dreamwork, rest and release'}],R=Object.fromEntries(['solar','lunar'].flatMap(t=>$.map((n,o)=>{const s='solar'===t?'Sun':'Moon',i='solar'===t?'year':'month';return[`${t}|house|${o+1}`,{simple:'solar'===t?n.solar:n.lunar,detailed:`The ${s} in the ${c[o]} house of your ${t} return puts the ${i}'s light there. ${'solar'===t?n.solar:n.lunar} Read this with the return's rising sign and anything on its angles, and with what your natal ${c[o]} house holds.`,magic:`For this ${i}, ${n.magic} suit the work, timed to the ${'solar'===t?'birthday and the new moons that follow':'lunar return itself'}.`}]}))),E={Aries:['A bold, restless chapter: you want to start things and act for yourself.','Feelings become quicker and more direct; patience runs short. It is a time of new beginnings, independence and courage, often after a long period of waiting.','courage and new-start spells'],Taurus:['A slow, settling chapter: comfort, security and the body matter.','Feelings steady. You want to build, save, garden and enjoy. Change slows down, and that is the point.','prosperity, garden and home magic'],Gemini:['A curious, busy chapter: learning, talking and moving about.','Feelings become lighter and more changeable. You need variety, conversation and new ideas.','word magic and study blessings'],Cancer:['A tender, home-centred chapter: family, roots and belonging.','Feelings deepen and turn toward home. Moving, nesting, children and family matters come to the fore.','hearth and family magic'],Leo:['A warm, expressive chapter: creativity, joy and being seen.','Feelings want expression. Romance, play, art and confidence grow.','creative and confidence magic'],Virgo:['A practical, healing chapter: work, health and getting things right.','Feelings turn toward usefulness. You sort, refine and improve, and tend body and routine.','health and cleansing work'],Libra:['A relational chapter: partnership, beauty and balance.','Feelings seek company and harmony. Relationships, art and fairness take centre stage.','love and harmony spells'],Scorpio:['A deep, intense chapter: intimacy, endings and transformation.','Feelings go deep. Old matters surface to be faced, and bonds become profound.','shadow work and protection'],Sagittarius:['An expansive chapter: travel, study and searching for meaning.','Feelings want freedom and adventure. Beliefs widen, and you may travel or study.','journey and wisdom magic'],Capricorn:['A serious, building chapter: responsibility, ambition and structure.','Feelings become more reserved and purposeful. You build for the long term.','career and endurance magic'],Aquarius:['An independent chapter: friends, causes and change.','Feelings detach a little; you want freedom and community, and may break with old patterns.','community and freedom magic'],Pisces:['A dreamy, closing chapter: spirit, compassion and endings before a new cycle.','Feelings become porous and intuitive. Rest, retreat, spirituality and letting go prepare you for the next progressed Aries chapter.','dreamwork and devotion']},O=Object.fromEntries(Object.keys(E).map(t=>{const[n,o,s]=E[t];return[`sign|${t}`,{simple:n,detailed:`${o}\n\nThe progressed Moon spends about two and a half years in each sign, and its sign shows the emotional climate of that chapter: what you need, what comforts you, and what you are growing through. Read it with the house it passes through.`,magic:`While the progressed Moon is in ${t}, ${s} suit your practice, and so does the transiting Moon's monthly visit to ${t}.`}]})),P=Object.fromEntries([['Your focus turns to yourself: a new start, a new look, a new direction.','self-blessing'],['Your focus turns to money, possessions and self-worth.','prosperity'],['Your focus turns to learning, writing, siblings and your local world.','word magic'],['Your focus turns to home, family and roots; a time to nest or move.','hearth magic'],['Your focus turns to creativity, romance, children and joy.','creative magic'],['Your focus turns to work, health and daily routines.','health work'],['Your focus turns to partnership and one-to-one relationships.','partnership magic'],['Your focus turns to intimacy, shared resources and inner change.','shadow work'],['Your focus turns to travel, study and meaning.','journey magic'],['Your focus turns to career, reputation and public life.','career magic'],['Your focus turns to friends, groups and hopes.','community magic'],['Your focus turns inward: rest, retreat, spirituality and endings.','dreamwork']].map(([t,n],o)=>[`house|${o+1}`,{simple:t,detailed:`${t} The progressed Moon spends roughly two to three years in each house of your natal chart, so it marks a chapter, not a day.\n\nThat house's matters are where your emotional life gathers now: what you need, what you notice, what you tend. Planets in the house will be touched as the Moon passes them.`,magic:`Lean on ${n} in this chapter, and on the ${c[o]} house's own correspondences.`}])),q={New:['A new thirty-year cycle begins: seeds, instinct and starting again, often without knowing where it leads.','new-moon intentions'],Crescent:['Struggling forward: the new direction meets resistance from the old, and you push on.','courage spells'],'First Quarter':['Crisis in action: you build, decide and commit to the direction.','action and commitment work'],Gibbous:['Refining: you improve, study and perfect what you are building.','refining and study'],Full:['Fulfilment and awareness: what you built is seen, and relationships mirror it back.','full-moon charging and gratitude'],Disseminating:['Sharing: you teach and spread what you learned.','teaching and blessing'],'Last Quarter':['Turning away: old structures are questioned and you begin to let go.','release work'],Balsamic:['Closing: rest, wisdom and endings before a new cycle; a time for spirit and solitude.','dark-moon rest and banishing']},I=Object.fromEntries(Object.keys(q).map(t=>[`phase|${t}`,{simple:q[t][0],detailed:`${q[t][0]}\n\nThe progressed Sun and Moon make a full cycle of phases in about thirty years, each phase lasting three to four years. Dane Rudhyar, who popularised the idea, read it as the great rhythm of a life; the ${t.toLowerCase()} phase is one season of it.`,magic:`In this phase, ${q[t][1]} match the season of your life, as they match the Moon's own phase each month.`,sources:'Dane Rudhyar, The Lunation Cycle (1967).'}]))},3096,[3036,3097,3098,3099,3046]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TRANSIT_SEEDS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});const n={"Jupiter|Sun":{core:"Transiting Jupiter to your Sun brings growth, confidence and opportunity to your sense of self.",magic:"Cast for success, recognition and blessing; a gold and a blue candle together on a Thursday or Sunday.",conjunction:["A year-high point for confidence and opportunity. Say yes to growth that feels like you.","Jupiter crossing your Sun is one of the most welcome transits: doors open, people are generous, and you feel more yourself. It is a good time to start something that matters to you, to travel, study or step into a bigger role.\n\nThe only risk is overdoing it: promising too much, or spending as though the good feeling will last for ever. Plant seeds you can tend."],hard:["You want more, and may overreach. Aim the hunger at one real goal.","Jupiter in hard aspect to your Sun swells ambition and appetite. You may feel restless with your life as it is, or tempted to take on more than you can carry.\n\nUsed well, it gives the push to grow; used carelessly, it gives overcommitment and excess. Choose the opportunity that you will still want when the glow fades."],soft:["Things go your way with less effort. A good time to ask, apply and expand.","Jupiter in easy aspect to your Sun brings luck and goodwill: help from others, small wins, and a sense that life is on your side.\n\nBecause it is easy, it passes quietly unless you use it. Make the request, send the application, book the trip."]},"Jupiter|Moon":{core:"Transiting Jupiter to your Moon brings comfort, generosity and growth to home, family and feelings.",magic:"Bless the home, host a meal, cast for family abundance; silver and blue candles on a Monday or Thursday.",conjunction:["Your heart opens and home feels abundant. A good time for family, moving or making a home bigger.","Jupiter on your Moon brings emotional generosity and a sense of being looked after. Families grow, homes expand, and old hurts can soften.\n\nWatch comfort-eating and over-giving; let abundance flow both ways."],hard:["Feelings run big, and home may feel too small. Give yourself room without overdoing it.","Jupiter in hard aspect to your Moon can inflate emotional needs or restlessness at home. You may want more space, more comfort, more people.\n\nThe gift is growth in your emotional life; the care is proportion."],soft:["Emotional ease and help from family or friends. A gentle, nourishing time.","Jupiter in easy aspect to your Moon brings contentment and support. Home life eases and kindness comes back to you.\n\nUse it to heal family ties and to rest."]},"Jupiter|Mercury":{core:"Transiting Jupiter to your Mercury expands your thinking, learning and communication.",magic:"Cast for study, exams, writing and good news; bibliomancy and travel blessings suit.",conjunction:["Big ideas and good news. A fine time to learn, write, teach or travel.","Jupiter on your Mercury fills the mind with plans and possibilities. Learning comes easily and your words carry further.\n\nCheck the details: the vision is wide, the small print still matters."],hard:["Too many ideas and promises. Focus on what you can finish.","Jupiter in hard aspect to Mercury can bring overcommitment, scattered study or overconfident decisions.\n\nThe mind is lively; give it one big project rather than ten."],soft:["Clear, hopeful thinking and good news. Study, sign, write and share.","Jupiter in easy aspect to Mercury brings good judgement and lucky conversations.\n\nA good time for contracts, courses and publishing."]},"Jupiter|Venus":{core:"Transiting Jupiter to your Venus brings pleasure, affection and abundance to love and money.",magic:"Love and prosperity spells, beauty rites, gratitude offerings; Fridays and Thursdays with green and pink candles.",conjunction:["Love, pleasure and money tend to flow. Enjoy it, and share.","Jupiter on your Venus is one of the classic happy transits: romance, friendship, art and income can all grow.\n\nThe care is indulgence; enjoy without overspending."],hard:["Temptation to overspend or overindulge. Pleasure with proportion.","Jupiter in hard aspect to Venus inflates desire: love affairs, shopping and sweets beckon.\n\nGenerosity is lovely; budgets help it last."],soft:["Easy affection and small windfalls. A sweet time for love and art.","Jupiter in easy aspect to Venus brings grace, kindness and pleasant luck.\n\nMake art, celebrate, reach out to people you love."]},"Jupiter|Mars":{core:"Transiting Jupiter to your Mars boosts energy, courage and ambition.",magic:"Courage and victory spells, protection for a venture; Tuesdays and Thursdays, red and blue candles.",conjunction:["A surge of confidence and energy. Start the bold thing.","Jupiter on your Mars gives drive and nerve: competitions, campaigns and physical challenges go well.\n\nWatch recklessness; enthusiasm is not the same as preparation."],hard:["Energy runs high and patience low. Channel it before it spills.","Jupiter in hard aspect to Mars can bring overconfidence, risk-taking or quarrels about beliefs.\n\nGive the fire a worthy target."],soft:["Effort pays off. A good time for sport, work and courage.","Jupiter in easy aspect to Mars brings successful action.\n\nPush forward on what matters."]},"Jupiter|Ascendant":{core:"Transiting Jupiter to your Ascendant brings growth to your body, manner and personal life.",magic:"Self-blessing, glamour for confidence, and luck charms carried on the body.",conjunction:["A fresh start: you feel bigger, brighter and more optimistic. Jupiter enters your first house.","Jupiter crossing your Ascendant begins its twelve-year journey through your houses again. You feel more confident and others see you favourably.\n\nWatch weight and overcommitment; otherwise, begin things."],hard:["You may take on too much or feel pulled by others' big plans.","Jupiter in hard aspect to your Ascendant can bring overextension or relationships that promise much.\n\nKeep your own measure."],soft:["People are warm to you and opportunities find you.","Jupiter in easy aspect to your Ascendant brings goodwill and easy social life.\n\nSay yes to invitations."]},"Jupiter|Midheaven":{core:"Transiting Jupiter to your Midheaven brings growth and recognition in career and public life.",magic:"Career and success spells at noon on a Thursday; bay leaves written with your aim.",conjunction:["A career high: recognition, promotion or a new calling. Step up.","Jupiter on your Midheaven is often the peak of its twelve-year career cycle: promotions, public success, new responsibility.\n\nAccept the bigger role, and do not let the success go to your head."],hard:["Career ambitions may outrun home life, or the other way round.","Jupiter in hard aspect to the Midheaven can bring overcommitment at work or a pull between public and private growth.\n\nBalance them."],soft:["Career goes smoothly and doors open.","Jupiter in easy aspect to the Midheaven brings professional luck.\n\nApply, pitch, ask."]},"Saturn|Sun":{core:"Transiting Saturn to your Sun tests and strengthens your sense of self, asking you to take responsibility for who you are becoming.",magic:"Binding, boundary and endurance work; long workings over many nights; Saturdays with a black candle and a pinch of salt.",conjunction:["A serious, demanding chapter. Hard work now lays foundations for years.","Saturn on your Sun is a time of reckoning: energy may dip, responsibilities grow and you see your life without illusions. It can feel heavy.\n\nIt is also a time of real achievement: what you commit to now lasts. Rest more than usual, simplify, and build."],hard:["Obstacles and pressure test you. Keep going; you are being strengthened.","Saturn in hard aspect to your Sun brings friction with authority, tiredness, and a sense of being blocked. The square asks you to restructure your life; the opposition often comes through others' demands.\n\nPatience, health care and honest choices see you through, and you come out more solid."],soft:["Steady progress. A good time to build, commit and take on responsibility.","Saturn in easy aspect to your Sun supports discipline and long-term plans.\n\nUse it to consolidate: savings, training, commitments you mean to keep."]},"Saturn|Moon":{core:"Transiting Saturn to your Moon tests your emotional foundations, home and family.",magic:"Protection of the home, ancestor work, slow emotional healing; Mondays and Saturdays.",conjunction:["A sober, sometimes lonely time for feelings. Care for yourself steadily.","Saturn on your Moon can bring sadness, family responsibility or a sense that comfort is scarce.\n\nIt also matures your emotional life. Build routines that nourish you, and ask for help."],hard:["Emotional pressure or family duty. Steady self-care sees you through.","Saturn in hard aspect to your Moon brings feelings of restriction at home or in relationships.\n\nBoundaries and rest are your medicine."],soft:["Emotional steadiness. A good time to build home and family security.","Saturn in easy aspect to your Moon supports practical care.\n\nFix the house, settle the family plan."]},"Saturn|Mercury":{core:"Transiting Saturn to your Mercury disciplines the mind and asks for careful thought and words.",magic:"Study rituals, written contracts and focus spells; black ink and rosemary.",conjunction:["Serious thinking and hard study. Slow down and get it right.","Saturn on Mercury brings mental focus and sometimes worry. It suits study, writing and planning.\n\nAvoid pessimistic thinking; get the facts."],hard:["Communication may feel blocked or heavy. Patience with words.","Saturn in hard aspect to Mercury brings delays, doubts or difficult conversations.\n\nWrite things down; take time."],soft:["Clear, disciplined thinking. A good time for serious study.","Saturn in easy aspect to Mercury supports concentration.\n\nFinish the hard project."]},"Saturn|Venus":{core:"Transiting Saturn to your Venus tests love, money and what you value.",magic:"Binding of committed love, money discipline spells, self-worth rites; Fridays and Saturdays.",conjunction:["Love and money get serious. Commit, or let go of what is not real.","Saturn on Venus can bring commitment, endings, or a sober look at relationships and finances.\n\nWhat is true lasts; what is not, leaves."],hard:["Relationships or money may feel strained. Honesty strengthens them.","Saturn in hard aspect to Venus brings tests in love and finance.\n\nThe work is self-worth and realism."],soft:["Stable love and sound money choices.","Saturn in easy aspect to Venus supports commitment and saving.\n\nA good time for lasting decisions."]},"Saturn|Mars":{core:"Transiting Saturn to your Mars disciplines your drive, asking for patient, well-aimed effort.",magic:"Endurance and protection spells, binding of harmful anger; Tuesdays and Saturdays.",conjunction:["Energy feels restrained. Steady effort beats force.","Saturn on Mars can bring frustration and blocked energy.\n\nIt rewards disciplined, persistent effort; avoid pushing through injury."],hard:["Frustration and obstacles. Choose your battles and pace yourself.","Saturn in hard aspect to Mars brings stop-start energy and conflict with authority.\n\nThe work is patience and safety."],soft:["Disciplined effort pays off.","Saturn in easy aspect to Mars supports hard work.\n\nTrain, build, persist."]},"Saturn|Ascendant":{core:"Transiting Saturn to your Ascendant asks you to take responsibility for yourself, your body and your direction.",magic:"Personal protection, body care rituals and boundary work.",conjunction:["A new, serious chapter of self. Saturn enters your first house.","Saturn crossing your Ascendant begins a new 29-year cycle of self-definition. You may feel tired or heavy, and more mature.\n\nTake care of your body; set your course."],hard:["Others' demands or your own doubts weigh on you.","Saturn in hard aspect to the Ascendant can bring relationship tests or self-doubt.\n\nStand firm, kindly."],soft:["You carry yourself with steadiness and earn respect.","Saturn in easy aspect to the Ascendant supports maturity.\n\nA good time to commit to a path."]},"Saturn|Midheaven":{core:"Transiting Saturn to your Midheaven tests and rewards your career and public standing.",magic:"Career magic for lasting success at noon on Saturdays.",conjunction:["A career peak or reckoning: you reap what you sowed.","Saturn on your Midheaven brings responsibility and recognition earned over years, or a reckoning if the foundations are weak.\n\nStep into authority with integrity."],hard:["Career pressures or a pull between home and work.","Saturn in hard aspect to the Midheaven brings professional tests.\n\nPersist and restructure."],soft:["Steady career progress.","Saturn in easy aspect to the Midheaven supports professional building.\n\nInvest in your craft."]},"Uranus|Sun":{core:"Transiting Uranus to your Sun awakens a need for freedom and change in who you are.",magic:"Spells for breaking free and sudden opportunity; storm water and clear quartz.",conjunction:["A life-changing awakening. You need to be more yourself, and fast.","Uranus on your Sun shakes up identity: sudden changes, new freedoms, and a strong urge to break out of what no longer fits.\n\nLet change happen, but don't burn everything down at once."],hard:["Restlessness and sudden changes. Make room for freedom.","Uranus in hard aspect to your Sun brings upheaval and rebellion.\n\nThe work is choosing change rather than being dragged by it."],soft:["Exciting, easy change. Try something new.","Uranus in easy aspect to your Sun brings inspiration and fresh starts.\n\nExperiment boldly."]},"Uranus|Moon":{core:"Transiting Uranus to your Moon unsettles home, feelings and routines, and frees them.",magic:"Home clearing, freedom spells, new-routine rites.",conjunction:["Sudden changes at home or in feelings. Let in the new.","Uranus on your Moon can bring moves, family changes or emotional awakenings.\n\nStay flexible; ground yourself daily."],hard:["Emotional upheaval. Space and honesty help.","Uranus in hard aspect to your Moon brings unrest at home.\n\nBuild new routines that leave room."],soft:["Refreshing changes to home and feelings.","Uranus in easy aspect to your Moon brings liberating change.\n\nRearrange your life."]},"Uranus|Mercury":{core:"Transiting Uranus to your Mercury electrifies your thinking.",magic:"Sigil magic, technology spells, sudden divination.",conjunction:["Brilliant, sudden ideas. Write them down.","Uranus on Mercury brings flashes of insight and new interests.\n\nThe care is scattered nerves."],hard:["Mental restlessness and surprises.","Uranus in hard aspect to Mercury brings disruptions to plans.\n\nStay adaptable."],soft:["Inventive thinking flows.","Uranus in easy aspect to Mercury brings fresh ideas.\n\nLearn something new."]},"Uranus|Venus":{core:"Transiting Uranus to your Venus shakes up love, money and taste.",magic:"Freedom in love, glamour reinvention.",conjunction:["Sudden attractions or changes in love.","Uranus on Venus brings exciting new loves or a need for freedom within love.\n\nBe honest about what you want."],hard:["Unstable relationships or finances.","Uranus in hard aspect to Venus brings romantic upheaval.\n\nAvoid rash decisions."],soft:["Exciting, easy changes in love and style.","Uranus in easy aspect to Venus brings refreshing romance.\n\nTry new things."]},"Uranus|Mars":{core:"Transiting Uranus to your Mars brings sudden energy and the urge to break free.",magic:"Courage to change, freedom spells.",conjunction:["Sudden bursts of energy. Act, safely.","Uranus on Mars brings impulsive, liberating action.\n\nTake care with accidents."],hard:["Restless, erratic energy. Slow down.","Uranus in hard aspect to Mars brings sudden conflicts.\n\nSafety first."],soft:["Inventive action flows.","Uranus in easy aspect to Mars brings exciting initiatives.\n\nGo for it."]},"Uranus|Ascendant":{core:"Transiting Uranus to your Ascendant changes how you present and live.",magic:"Reinvention rites, new image magic.",conjunction:["A personal reinvention.","Uranus on the Ascendant brings sudden change to image and direction.\n\nExperiment."],hard:["Sudden changes in relationships or self.","Uranus in hard aspect to the Ascendant brings disruption.\n\nStay flexible."],soft:["Easy personal change.","Uranus in easy aspect to the Ascendant brings freedom.\n\nEnjoy it."]},"Uranus|Midheaven":{core:"Transiting Uranus to your Midheaven shakes up career and calling.",magic:"Career change magic.",conjunction:["A sudden career change.","Uranus on the Midheaven brings new directions at work.\n\nFollow your true calling."],hard:["Career disruption.","Uranus in hard aspect to the Midheaven brings instability at work.\n\nAdapt."],soft:["Exciting career opportunities.","Uranus in easy aspect to the Midheaven brings innovation.\n\nTake the leap."]},"Neptune|Sun":{core:"Transiting Neptune to your Sun dissolves old identity and opens you to spirit, art and compassion.",magic:"Dreamwork, devotion, sea rites; strong grounding and cleansing.",conjunction:["A dreamy, uncertain time. Your old self dissolves to make room for a gentler one.","Neptune on your Sun can bring confusion, low energy and loss of direction, alongside spiritual opening and creativity.\n\nAvoid big decisions in a fog; rest, make art and pray."],hard:["Confusion or disillusionment. Check facts and protect your energy.","Neptune in hard aspect to your Sun brings uncertainty and escapism.\n\nGround yourself and avoid deception."],soft:["Inspiration and gentle spiritual growth.","Neptune in easy aspect to your Sun brings imagination and compassion.\n\nCreate and meditate."]},"Neptune|Moon":{core:"Transiting Neptune to your Moon softens and sensitises feelings, home and intuition.",magic:"Psychic work, moon water and dream journalling; cleanse often.",conjunction:["Heightened sensitivity and dreams. Protect your energy.","Neptune on your Moon opens intuition and empathy, and can blur boundaries.\n\nRest, cleanse and keep a dream journal."],hard:["Emotional confusion. Clarity and boundaries help.","Neptune in hard aspect to your Moon brings uncertainty at home.\n\nAvoid escapism."],soft:["Gentle intuition and compassion.","Neptune in easy aspect to your Moon brings spiritual comfort.\n\nMeditate."]},"Neptune|Mercury":{core:"Transiting Neptune to your Mercury makes thinking intuitive and imaginative.",magic:"Automatic writing, poetry, divination by symbols.",conjunction:["Imaginative but foggy thinking.","Neptune on Mercury inspires poetry and intuition and blurs details.\n\nDouble-check contracts."],hard:["Misunderstandings and confusion.","Neptune in hard aspect to Mercury brings muddled communication.\n\nGet it in writing."],soft:["Inspired, intuitive thinking.","Neptune in easy aspect to Mercury brings creative insight.\n\nWrite."]},"Neptune|Venus":{core:"Transiting Neptune to your Venus brings romance, art and idealism to love.",magic:"Devotional love magic, art as offering.",conjunction:["Romantic, idealistic love. Keep your eyes open.","Neptune on Venus brings enchanting love and artistic inspiration.\n\nSee people as they are."],hard:["Disappointment or confusion in love.","Neptune in hard aspect to Venus brings romantic illusions.\n\nTake time."],soft:["Gentle romance and artistic flow.","Neptune in easy aspect to Venus brings grace.\n\nMake art."]},"Neptune|Mars":{core:"Transiting Neptune to your Mars softens drive and asks for inspired action.",magic:"Spiritual protection, trance dance.",conjunction:["Low energy or inspired action.","Neptune on Mars can sap drive and inspire service.\n\nRest and act from compassion."],hard:["Unclear motives and fatigue.","Neptune in hard aspect to Mars brings confusion about aims.\n\nGround yourself."],soft:["Inspired, graceful action.","Neptune in easy aspect to Mars brings spiritual drive.\n\nServe."]},"Neptune|Ascendant":{core:"Transiting Neptune to your Ascendant softens your image and boundaries.",magic:"Glamour and protection magic.",conjunction:["A dreamy, sensitive time. Protect yourself.","Neptune on the Ascendant blurs identity and heightens sensitivity.\n\nShield and rest."],hard:["Confusion in relationships.","Neptune in hard aspect to the Ascendant brings misreadings.\n\nBe clear."],soft:["Gentle charm and intuition.","Neptune in easy aspect to the Ascendant brings grace.\n\nTrust it."]},"Neptune|Midheaven":{core:"Transiting Neptune to your Midheaven brings inspiration or uncertainty to your calling.",magic:"Career magic for artists and healers.",conjunction:["Your calling may become spiritual or unclear.","Neptune on the Midheaven dissolves old career ideas.\n\nFollow inspiration carefully."],hard:["Career confusion.","Neptune in hard aspect to the Midheaven brings professional uncertainty.\n\nClarify."],soft:["Inspired work.","Neptune in easy aspect to the Midheaven brings creative success.\n\nTrust it."]},"Pluto|Sun":{core:"Transiting Pluto to your Sun transforms your identity from the roots.",magic:"Shadow work, rebirth rites, protection; obsidian and black candles at the dark moon.",conjunction:["A deep transformation of self. Something ends so something truer can begin.","Pluto on your Sun is one of the most profound transits: power struggles, endings and rebirth. You may feel stripped back to essentials.\n\nLet go of what is dead; your core grows stronger."],hard:["Intense pressure to change. Face it rather than fight it.","Pluto in hard aspect to your Sun brings power struggles and crises.\n\nThe work is transformation through honesty."],soft:["Empowering change. Quiet strength grows.","Pluto in easy aspect to your Sun brings regeneration.\n\nTake your power."]},"Pluto|Moon":{core:"Transiting Pluto to your Moon transforms emotional life, home and family patterns.",magic:"Ancestral healing, shadow work, home clearing.",conjunction:["Deep emotional transformation.","Pluto on your Moon brings intense feelings and family change.\n\nSeek support; heal old patterns."],hard:["Emotional intensity and power struggles.","Pluto in hard aspect to your Moon brings crises at home.\n\nFace your feelings."],soft:["Emotional regeneration.","Pluto in easy aspect to your Moon brings deep healing.\n\nUse it."]},"Pluto|Mercury":{core:"Transiting Pluto to your Mercury deepens and intensifies thought.",magic:"Research, binding words, secrets.",conjunction:["Penetrating, obsessive thinking.","Pluto on Mercury brings depth and persuasion.\n\nAvoid mental fixation."],hard:["Intense debates or secrets.","Pluto in hard aspect to Mercury brings power struggles over ideas.\n\nSpeak carefully."],soft:["Deep insight.","Pluto in easy aspect to Mercury brings research power.\n\nInvestigate."]},"Pluto|Venus":{core:"Transiting Pluto to your Venus transforms love, money and values.",magic:"Deep love magic with consent, worth rites.",conjunction:["Intense love and changing values.","Pluto on Venus brings consuming relationships and transformation.\n\nWatch control."],hard:["Jealousy or power in love.","Pluto in hard aspect to Venus brings intense tests.\n\nTrust and honesty."],soft:["Deep, transforming love.","Pluto in easy aspect to Venus brings magnetic bonds.\n\nEnjoy them."]},"Pluto|Mars":{core:"Transiting Pluto to your Mars intensifies drive and will.",magic:"Powerful protection and transformation magic.",conjunction:["Enormous drive and power.","Pluto on Mars brings intense ambition.\n\nUse it ethically."],hard:["Power struggles and conflict.","Pluto in hard aspect to Mars brings confrontation.\n\nChannel rage into change."],soft:["Empowered action.","Pluto in easy aspect to Mars brings strength.\n\nAct."]},"Pluto|Ascendant":{core:"Transiting Pluto to your Ascendant transforms how you meet the world.",magic:"Rebirth and protection magic.",conjunction:["A profound personal rebirth.","Pluto on the Ascendant transforms image and life direction.\n\nLet it."],hard:["Intense relationships.","Pluto in hard aspect to the Ascendant brings power struggles.\n\nStay equal."],soft:["Quiet empowerment.","Pluto in easy aspect to the Ascendant brings strength.\n\nUse it."]},"Pluto|Midheaven":{core:"Transiting Pluto to your Midheaven transforms career and reputation.",magic:"Career transformation magic.",conjunction:["A career transformation.","Pluto on the Midheaven brings profound career change.\n\nEmbrace it."],hard:["Career power struggles.","Pluto in hard aspect to the Midheaven brings crisis at work.\n\nTransform."],soft:["Empowered career.","Pluto in easy aspect to the Midheaven brings influence.\n\nLead."]},"Chiron|Sun":{core:"Transiting Chiron to your Sun touches wounds around identity and opens healing.",magic:"Healing rites, self-acceptance work.",conjunction:["Old wounds about who you are surface to heal.","Chiron on your Sun brings vulnerability and healing.\n\nSeek help; teach what you learn."],hard:["Sore places press. Tend them.","Chiron in hard aspect to your Sun brings hurt.\n\nGentleness heals."],soft:["Healing comes easily.","Chiron in easy aspect to your Sun brings wisdom.\n\nShare it."]},"Chiron|Moon":{core:"Transiting Chiron to your Moon touches emotional wounds and opens healing.",magic:"Comfort rites, herbal baths.",conjunction:["Emotional wounds surface to heal.","Chiron on your Moon brings tender feelings.\n\nCare for yourself."],hard:["Old hurts press.","Chiron in hard aspect to your Moon brings sensitivity.\n\nBe gentle."],soft:["Emotional healing flows.","Chiron in easy aspect to your Moon brings comfort.\n\nAccept it."]},"Chiron|Mercury":{core:"Transiting Chiron to your Mercury touches wounds around voice and learning.",magic:"Healing words, affirmations.",conjunction:["Old hurts about being heard surface.","Chiron on Mercury brings healing through words.\n\nSpeak."],hard:["Communication touches old wounds.","Chiron in hard aspect to Mercury brings sensitivity.\n\nBe patient."],soft:["Healing conversations.","Chiron in easy aspect to Mercury brings wise words.\n\nTeach."]},"Chiron|Venus":{core:"Transiting Chiron to your Venus touches wounds around love and worth.",magic:"Self-love rites, rose baths.",conjunction:["Love wounds surface to heal.","Chiron on Venus brings tenderness in love.\n\nLove yourself."],hard:["Love touches old hurts.","Chiron in hard aspect to Venus brings sensitivity.\n\nBe kind."],soft:["Healing through love.","Chiron in easy aspect to Venus brings gentle healing.\n\nShare it."]},"Chiron|Mars":{core:"Transiting Chiron to your Mars touches wounds around strength and anger.",magic:"Courage spells for healing.",conjunction:["Old wounds about strength surface.","Chiron on Mars brings healing through courage.\n\nAct gently."],hard:["Anger touches old hurts.","Chiron in hard aspect to Mars brings sensitivity.\n\nPause."],soft:["Healing action.","Chiron in easy aspect to Mars brings brave care.\n\nAdvocate."]},"Chiron|Ascendant":{core:"Transiting Chiron to your Ascendant touches wounds around body and self-image.",magic:"Body blessing rites.",conjunction:["Self-image wounds surface to heal.","Chiron on the Ascendant brings vulnerability.\n\nBe gentle with your body."],hard:["Relationships touch old hurts.","Chiron in hard aspect to the Ascendant brings sensitivity.\n\nHeal."],soft:["You heal by being yourself.","Chiron in easy aspect to the Ascendant brings a healing presence.\n\nShare it."]},"Chiron|Midheaven":{core:"Transiting Chiron to your Midheaven touches wounds around career and calling.",magic:"Career healing magic.",conjunction:["Career wounds surface; a healing vocation may emerge.","Chiron on the Midheaven brings healing to your calling.\n\nFollow it."],hard:["Career touches old hurts.","Chiron in hard aspect to the Midheaven brings sensitivity at work.\n\nHeal."],soft:["Healing in your work.","Chiron in easy aspect to the Midheaven brings a healer's success.\n\nShare it."]},"North Node|Sun":{core:"The transiting nodes to your Sun bring fated-feeling turns of identity, often around eclipses.",magic:"Eclipse-season intention and release rites.",conjunction:["A turning point: growth calls you forward.","The North Node on your Sun brings opportunities to grow into yourself, often through new people.\n\nSay yes to the future."],hard:["A crossroads, or a release. The square asks you to choose; the opposition (the South Node on your Sun) asks you to let go.","The nodes in hard aspect to your Sun bring turning points. When the South Node crosses your Sun, the work is release; at the square, it is choice.\n\nLet go of what you have outgrown."],soft:["Helpful connections support your growth.","The North Node in easy aspect to your Sun brings well-timed help.\n\nAccept it."]},"North Node|Moon":{core:"The transiting nodes to your Moon bring emotional turning points.",magic:"Lunar eclipse rites.",conjunction:["Emotional growth calls you forward.","The North Node on your Moon brings new emotional connections.\n\nOpen your heart."],hard:["Emotional release or choice.","The nodes in hard aspect to your Moon bring endings and crossroads at home.\n\nRelease the old."],soft:["Supportive emotional connections.","The North Node in easy aspect to your Moon brings comfort.\n\nAccept it."]},"North Node|Mercury":{core:"The transiting nodes to your Mercury bring turning points in thinking and communication.",magic:"Eclipse journalling.",conjunction:["New ideas lead you forward.","The North Node on Mercury brings important conversations.\n\nListen."],hard:["Release old thinking.","The nodes in hard aspect to Mercury bring mental crossroads.\n\nChoose."],soft:["Helpful ideas and contacts.","The North Node in easy aspect to Mercury brings useful news.\n\nFollow it."]},"North Node|Venus":{core:"The transiting nodes to your Venus bring turning points in love and values.",magic:"Love magic at eclipse seasons.",conjunction:["New love or values lead you forward.","The North Node on Venus brings fated-feeling connections.\n\nOpen up."],hard:["Release old loves or values.","The nodes in hard aspect to Venus bring endings in love.\n\nLet go kindly."],soft:["Supportive relationships.","The North Node in easy aspect to Venus brings harmony.\n\nEnjoy it."]},"North Node|Mars":{core:"The transiting nodes to your Mars bring turning points in action and drive.",magic:"Courage magic at eclipse seasons.",conjunction:["Bold action leads you forward.","The North Node on Mars brings new ventures.\n\nAct."],hard:["Release old battles.","The nodes in hard aspect to Mars bring conflict crossroads.\n\nChoose wisely."],soft:["Well-timed action.","The North Node in easy aspect to Mars brings support for effort.\n\nPush on."]},"North Node|Ascendant":{core:"The transiting nodes to your Ascendant bring turning points in self and relationships.",magic:"Eclipse-season self and partnership rites.",conjunction:["Personal growth calls you forward.","The North Node on the Ascendant (the South Node on the Descendant) brings new self-direction.\n\nGrow."],hard:["Relationship turning points.","The nodes in hard aspect to the Ascendant bring partnership crossroads; the North Node on the Descendant asks you to grow through others.\n\nChoose."],soft:["Helpful people appear.","The North Node in easy aspect to the Ascendant brings support.\n\nAccept it."]},"North Node|Midheaven":{core:"The transiting nodes to your Midheaven bring turning points in career and home.",magic:"Career magic at eclipse seasons.",conjunction:["Career growth calls you forward.","The North Node on the Midheaven brings career opportunities.\n\nStep up."],hard:["Home and career turning points.","The nodes in hard aspect to the Midheaven bring crossroads between public and private life.\n\nChoose."],soft:["Supportive career connections.","The North Node in easy aspect to the Midheaven brings help at work.\n\nUse it."]}}},3097,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TRANSIT_DEEPER_A",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o={"Jupiter|Sun":["This crossing comes round about every twelve years. Look back twelve years to the last one: what began then often shows what is ripe to grow now, and what you planted then may be ready to bear fruit.","Notice whether the restlessness is pointing at something real. The square often marks a growth spurt that is uncomfortable because the old life is too small; the opposition brings the opportunity through someone else. Either way, choose deliberately and keep something in reserve.","Easy luck tends to arrive through people who like you and through the confidence you feel. Write down what you would ask for if you knew it would be granted, and then ask for one of those things within the fortnight.","Write a wish for the year on a bay leaf at noon on a Sunday or Thursday and keep it in your purse until the transit passes."],"Jupiter|Moon":["Many people move house, extend the family or simply feel more at home in themselves under this transit. It is a kind time to reconnect with a parent or with your own childhood, and to give the body more rest and good food than usual.","The heart wants more than the day can hold: more company, more food, more space. Notice whether the hunger is for comfort or for something you have been missing. Generosity at home is welcome; just keep the larder and the calendar in proportion.","This is a gentle season for healing family ties, hosting, cooking and saying thank you to the people who looked after you. Small kindnesses at home tend to be repaid quickly.","Bake bread or cook a shared meal on a Monday and set aside the first portion as an offering for the household's plenty."],"Jupiter|Mercury":["A good season to begin a course, start writing, take a journey for learning or send off the manuscript. Your words carry further than usual and people listen. Keep a notebook close: ideas come quickly and some of them are worth years.","Watch for promising more than you can deliver, signing in a rush or starting several courses at once. Under the square or opposition, read contracts twice and finish one piece of writing before the next.","Conversations bring opportunities, and study, travel and writing go well. It is a good time for exams, interviews, publishing and agreements, especially when you prepare. A teacher or a book met now may matter for years; follow the threads that excite you.","Before an exam, interview or signing, carry a sprig of rosemary and a blue stone, and read a line of a favourite book for luck."],"Jupiter|Venus":["Relationships may begin, deepen or be celebrated, and creative work tends to find an audience. Money can come in more easily. Share the good fortune: generosity under this transit seems to return in kind.","Desire swells: for a person, a purchase or a pleasure. Some of it is right and some of it is excess. Under the hard aspects, a cooling-off day before big purchases or declarations is wise.","Grace and goodwill come easily, and pleasant surprises in love, friendship or money are likely. Use the season deliberately: make art, mend a friendship, ask for a raise, plan a celebration, or simply enjoy life a little more on purpose.","On a Friday, give a gift of flowers or food to someone you love and keep one flower on your altar for Venus and Jupiter together."],"Jupiter|Mars":["Energy and courage run high, and this is a fine time to start a physical challenge, a campaign or a bold venture. Train for it; the transit gives confidence, not preparation, and injuries come from overreach.","Impatience, overconfidence or quarrels about principle may flare. Give the fire a target: a project with a deadline, hard exercise or a cause that needs a champion.","Effort pays off, and you can achieve more than usual with the same work. Use the season for the tasks that need courage and stamina: a training goal, a difficult conversation, a venture you have been putting off. Momentum builds quickly.","On a Tuesday, light a red candle and a blue one side by side and name the bold act you will undertake."],"Jupiter|Ascendant":["As Jupiter crosses the Ascendant you may feel more confident, be noticed more, and find new beginnings opening. It is a good time for a fresh look, travel, study and starting the next twelve-year chapter. Watch weight and overcommitment.","The square brings growth that asks you to change direction; the opposition, crossing the Descendant, brings opportunities through partners, sometimes a marriage or a business partnership. Choose well; Jupiter enlarges whatever you take on.","Your manner is welcomed and people tend to help you. Use the season to introduce yourself, apply for things, travel and say yes to invitations. Small investments in your health and appearance pay off well.","Each morning of the transit, before you dress, ask for luck in your first meeting of the day."],"Jupiter|Midheaven":["Jupiter at the top of your chart is often a peak of recognition: a promotion, a public role, an award or simply a sense that your work is seen. It marks the high point of a twelve-year career cycle. Use it to step up.","The square may bring growth that strains home against work; the opposition, on the IC, brings good fortune at home, a move or family growth, which may need you to take time from career.","Your work goes well and goodwill follows. Ask, apply and offer your skills; the doors are more open than usual. It is a good time to seek a mentor, a promotion or a public role that suits you.","At noon on a Thursday, burn a bay leaf with your career wish written on it and let the smoke rise."],"Saturn|Sun":["Saturn crossing the Sun is a time of reckoning and building: what is solid stays, what is false falls away. Energy may be lower and responsibilities greater. It is the start of a new twenty-nine-year cycle of effort; plant what you mean to grow for decades.","The square brings a test from within: are you living as yourself? The opposition brings the test through others or events. Both ask for patience, honest work and letting go of what no longer fits.","Steady effort is rewarded, and structures, elders and institutions support you. This is a good time to commit, plan, sign long agreements and build. What you begin now tends to last, so choose what you truly want to keep.","On a Saturday, write your next long goal on paper, wrap it in black cloth and keep it under Onyx for the length of the transit."],"Saturn|Moon":["Feelings may be heavy, and home and family may ask for responsibility: caring for a parent, a move, or facing old emotional patterns. Rest and steady routines help. What you build at home now tends to last.","Emotional pressure, loneliness or a sense of duty at home may weigh on you. Give feelings a safe place and ask for help; this transit eases when you stop carrying everything alone.","Emotional maturity grows more easily, and home life can be put on a firm footing. It is a good time for long-term decisions about where and how you live, for quiet self-care routines, and for caring for older relatives without resentment.","Keep a bowl of salt by the bed and change it each Monday, asking for steady feelings and a safe home."],"Saturn|Mercury":["Thinking becomes serious and focused, good for study, writing a long piece, contracts and planning. You may feel slower or more pessimistic. Work steadily and check facts.","Communication may be blocked or delayed, plans may stall, and worry or pessimism may increase. Write things down, slow down and be precise; the obstacles teach clarity. Check contracts carefully and give important conversations time.","Concentration and practical thinking come easily. Use the season for serious study, long writing projects, planning and agreements. Your words carry authority; people take you seriously when you speak carefully.","On a Wednesday or Saturday, write a plan in black ink and keep it in a notebook kept only for this purpose."],"Saturn|Venus":["Love and money are tested: relationships may be committed or ended, and finances tightened or put on firmer footing. What is real stays. It is a time for loyalty and realistic love.","Loneliness, coldness or money worries may come, and a relationship may face a hard test. Ask what is truly valuable, and let go of what is not. Love that survives this transit is strong; budgets made now tend to protect you for years.","Relationships and finances can be put on a steady footing. It is a good time for commitments, budgets, long-term savings and art that takes patience. Loyalty is rewarded, and older friends may be especially helpful.","On a Friday, tie a black and a green thread together with three knots for love and money that last."],"Saturn|Mars":["Energy may feel blocked, or channelled into hard, slow work. Frustration is common when effort does not bring quick results. The gift is discipline: training, building, finishing. Many people achieve their hardest physical or practical goals under this transit by pacing themselves and keeping at it.","Anger may build against obstacles, authorities or your own limits, and pushing harder often makes things worse. Find a steady, physical outlet, avoid forcing confrontations, and take extra care with tools, driving and the body. Patience is the strength being trained.","Disciplined effort pays off, and you can sustain work that would usually wear you out. Use the season for long, demanding projects, physical training or anything that needs both courage and stamina.","On a Tuesday or Saturday, carry an iron nail wrapped in black thread as a charm for disciplined strength."],"Saturn|Ascendant":["Saturn crossing the Ascendant begins a new chapter of personal life: you may feel older, more serious and more responsible, and you may restructure your life, your habits and your care of the body. It is a time to take yourself seriously and to commit to the person you are becoming.","The square brings pressure to restructure your life from within. The opposition, crossing the Descendant, tests partnerships: a relationship may be committed to, renegotiated or ended. Both ask for honesty about what you can sustain.","Your presence carries quiet authority, and steady self-improvement works well. A good time for disciplined health routines, a new professional image or taking on responsibility.","At sunrise on a Saturday, stand straight and name aloud the commitment you make to your own life."],"Saturn|Midheaven":["Saturn at the top of the chart is a career peak or reckoning: you reap what you have built over the last decades, and may take on authority or face a public test. Work done well is recognised; shortcuts are exposed. It marks the high point of Saturn's long cycle through your houses.","The square tests career against home and inner life. The opposition, on the IC, turns attention to home and family, often bringing a move, a family responsibility or a time of quiet rebuilding before the next public chapter.","Career goes steadily, and efforts are rewarded in proportion. It is a good time for planning, promotion, qualifications and laying foundations for the long term. People in authority tend to take you seriously.","At noon on a Saturday, light a black candle over a written career plan and leave it for the length of the transit."],"Uranus|Sun":["Uranus crossing the Sun is an awakening: you may change direction, break free from something that confined you, or discover a side of yourself you did not know. It can be exciting and unsettling at once. Make room for the new self, and avoid burning bridges you may want later.","The square and opposition bring restlessness and sudden change, from within or through events and other people. Old roles may feel unbearable. Change what must change, but give each decision a little time; the urgency passes and the truth remains.","Change comes easily and brings freedom. It is a good time to try new things, learn new skills, travel or experiment with how you live. You may feel younger and freer; use the energy to make a change you have wanted for a long time.","Charge a piece of Clear Quartz under a storm or open sky and carry it as a charm for the new self."],"Uranus|Moon":["Feelings and home may be shaken up: a sudden move, a change in the family, or an emotional awakening that changes what you need. You may need more freedom in your private life than before. Let the household change shape; it may become a better fit.","Restlessness at home and emotional upheaval may come, sometimes through a parent, a child or a household change. Sleep and routine can be disrupted. Keep a few steady rituals, and let the rest move.","Emotional freedom comes more easily, and you may find new ways to feel at home. It is a good time to redecorate, move, change household routines or bring new people into your home life. Feelings feel lighter.","Keep a bowl of rainwater by the bed during the transit, poured out and refilled at each new moon."],"Uranus|Mercury":["Sudden insights, new ideas and a change in how you think. You may take up a new subject, technology or way of writing. The mind is quick and inventive; capture the flashes in a notebook.","Nervous tension, scattered thoughts and sudden changes of plan may come. Information arrives fast and contradicts itself. Slow down before deciding, and rest the nervous system.","Inventive thinking flows, and you may learn quickly or solve old problems in a new way. It is a good time for new courses, technology, astrology and original writing. Follow the ideas that surprise you.","Write sudden insights on paper and keep them in a box with Clear Quartz, read once a month."],"Uranus|Venus":["Sudden love, a sudden change in love, or a new taste in beauty and pleasure. Relationships may need more freedom. Money may come or go unexpectedly. Enjoy the surprise without staking everything on it.","Restlessness in love or a sudden attraction may unsettle an existing bond, and money may be erratic. Ask what freedom you need, and say so honestly before acting. Avoid impulsive purchases or declarations you cannot unmake.","Exciting new pleasures, friendships and creative ideas come easily, and love may feel refreshed. It is a good time for fresh art, new styles and experiments in how you enjoy life, alone or together.","Charge a rose quartz under a thunderstorm and wear it for love that leaves room to breathe."],"Uranus|Mars":["Sudden bursts of energy and action, and a need to act independently. You may start something bold or break away from a constraint. Take care with speed and tools.","Accidents and impulsive anger are more likely, especially when you feel trapped or rushed. Move the body, take breaks, slow down on the road and around tools, and avoid rash confrontations. Find a safe outlet for sudden energy.","Bold, original action works well, and you may find energy for things you thought you could not do. It is a good time for new sports, independent projects, technology and decisive change.","Carry an iron nail charged under a storm as a charm for safe, bold action."],"Uranus|Ascendant":["Sudden change in your life, look or direction. You may feel freer, stranger or more yourself than before, and new beginnings arrive unexpectedly. Let the change happen; it often clears the way for a truer life.","Restlessness and sudden change may unsettle your daily life. The opposition, crossing the Descendant, may bring sudden changes in partnership: new people, sudden endings, or a need for more freedom in a relationship.","Easy, welcome change in how you live and present yourself. It is a good time to experiment with your look, routine or direction, and to meet unusual people who widen your world.","Change one thing you wear or carry, and charge it under open sky."],"Uranus|Midheaven":["Sudden career change, a new direction or a break from an old role. You may move into a new field, go independent or be recognised for something unusual. Expect the unexpected at work and keep options open.","Career disruption may come, or home changes that affect work, since the opposition falls on the IC. Adapt, keep your skills portable, and treat the shake-up as a chance to rethink what you want.","Career innovation goes well. It is a good time to try new methods, technology and roles, and to suggest changes at work; people are more open to your ideas than usual.","Write three possible futures for your work and keep them under Clear Quartz until one calls."]}},3098,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TRANSIT_DEEPER_B",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o={"Neptune|Sun":["Neptune on the Sun can feel like a slow fog over who you thought you were: ambitions soften, energy dips, and something more spiritual or creative calls. It is a poor time for hard-edged decisions and a fine one for art, retreat, prayer and compassion. Let the old self dissolve gently; the new one takes shape over a year or two.","Under the hard aspects, confusion, tiredness or disillusion may come, and you may be tempted to escape through substances, fantasy or other people's plans. Check facts, rest more, and be wary of offers that sound too good. What remains when the fog lifts is truly yours.","Imagination and intuition are heightened, and it is a lovely time for art, music, spiritual practice and kindness. Use it on purpose: a creative project or a devotional practice begun now can carry you for years.","Float a gold candle on a bowl of water on a Sunday or Monday and ask to be shown who you are becoming."],"Neptune|Moon":["Feelings become tender and porous, and you may absorb other people's moods more easily than usual. Dreams are vivid. Home may become more spiritual, or a family member may need care. Protect your rest and give your sensitivity a gentle outlet.","Emotional confusion, longing or sadness without a clear cause may come, and boundaries at home may blur. Look after sleep, avoid numbing, and ask for clear help. This tide goes out again.","Compassion and intuition flow, and it is a lovely time for dream work, music, prayer and caring for others. Home can become a sanctuary. Let yourself rest and be soothed by water, music and quiet.","Keep a bowl of water by the bed, with a moonstone in it, and write down each dream on waking."],"Neptune|Mercury":["Thinking turns imaginative and poetic, and facts may slip. A good time for poetry, music, fiction and spiritual study; a poor one for contracts and fine print. Double-check what you sign and what you are told.","Misunderstandings, forgetfulness and confused communication are common, and deception is possible. Write things down, confirm arrangements and wait for clarity before deciding.","Intuition and imagination help the mind, and creative writing, music and spiritual reading flow. Use the season for inspired work, poetry and study of symbols, dreams and myth.","Write your spells as poems during this transit and read them aloud over a bowl of water."],"Neptune|Venus":["Love becomes romantic and idealised, art inspired, and you may fall for a dream. Creative work can be beautiful. Keep one foot on the ground in money and relationships; the glow is real, but so is the person.","Disillusion in love, confusion about money or a longing that cannot be met may come. Check facts before committing heart or savings, and let art hold the longing.","Romance, art and compassion flow sweetly. It is a lovely time for music, painting, film and tender love, and for acts of kindness and charity. Beauty feels close to the sacred.","On a Friday, float rose petals on a bowl of water and ask for love that is true as well as beautiful."],"Neptune|Mars":["Drive may soften or turn towards spiritual, creative or compassionate goals. Energy can be lower, and you may not know what you want. Rest, swim, dance, and let action follow inspiration.","Fatigue, confusion about direction, or anger that turns inward may come. Avoid fighting fog; wait for clarity, and take extra care with health and with substances.","Action guided by intuition and compassion works well. It is a good time for dance, swimming, art, yoga and service, and for working towards a spiritual or creative goal rather than a competitive one.","Wash in sea-salt water before acting on a hunch, asking that the action be clean."],"Neptune|Ascendant":["Neptune crossing the Ascendant can make you softer, more sensitive and harder to pin down, even to yourself. People may project onto you. The body may be more sensitive. Look after boundaries, and let your presence become more compassionate.","The square may blur your sense of direction; the opposition, on the Descendant, may bring idealised or confusing partners. See people clearly before committing.","Grace and intuition come easily, and you may seem gentler and more attractive to others. It is a good time for art, spiritual work and gentle change in how you present yourself.","Each morning, wash your face in water with a pinch of salt and say your own name aloud."],"Neptune|Midheaven":["Career may lose its clear outline: ambitions dissolve, a calling to art, healing or service grows, or your public image becomes uncertain. Do not force a decision; let the new direction emerge, and keep practical income steady meanwhile.","Career confusion or disillusion may come, or your reputation may become unclear. The opposition, on the IC, may bring a dreamy or unsettled home life. Keep clear agreements at work and avoid big decisions in a fog.","Inspiration supports your work, and creative, healing or compassionate projects go well. It is a good time to bring more meaning into your career, or to begin work in the arts or care.","At noon, write your work dream and one practical step, and keep the step under Amethyst."],"Pluto|Sun":["Pluto on the Sun is a long, deep transformation of who you are. Old identities, roles or ambitions may end, sometimes through crisis, and a stronger, truer self is forged. It can be hard. Seek support, face what comes, and trust that you are being remade rather than unmade.","Under the square or opposition, power struggles with authorities or others may come, or a crisis that forces change. Ask what is being asked to end, and let it go before it is torn away.","Deep, empowering change comes more easily, and you may feel a quiet strength growing. It is a good time for therapy, research, reclaiming your power and letting go of old roles without crisis.","At the dark moon, burn a written list of the roles you are leaving and keep the ashes with Obsidian."],"Pluto|Moon":["Deep emotional change: old family patterns, grief or buried feelings come to the surface to be transformed. Home may change through crisis or a move. Therapy and ancestral work are powerful now.","Emotional crises, power struggles at home or with family may come, and old feelings may surface forcefully. Let feelings be felt rather than controlled, seek support, and resist using control at home as a shield.","Emotional depth and healing come more easily. It is a good time for inner work, ancestral healing and honest conversations with family, and for making home a place of real safety.","Light a black candle for the ancestors at each dark moon of the transit, naming a pattern you are ending."],"Pluto|Mercury":["Thinking becomes deep, probing and sometimes obsessive. Research, investigation, therapy and writing about hidden things go well, and your words gain weight. You may change your mind about something fundamental, or uncover a truth that changes how you see your life.","Obsessive thinking, power struggles in conversation, or secrets coming to light may mark this time. Words can wound. Speak carefully, check your sources, and resist the urge to win every argument; some truths need time.","Penetrating insight and persuasive speech come more easily. A strong time for research, study of the occult or psychology, and conversations that heal old misunderstandings.","Write a hard truth on paper and keep it under Obsidian until you are ready to speak it plainly."],"Pluto|Venus":["Love and money go through deep change: intense attractions, endings, or a transformation of what you value and find beautiful. Passion can be overwhelming. Relationships that survive come out deeper; those that end clear the way. Watch possessiveness, in yourself and others.","Jealousy, power struggles in love, or a financial crisis may come. You may be drawn to people or things that are not good for you. Let go of control, and ask what you truly value beneath the craving.","Passionate love, deep friendship and powerful creative work come more easily. It is a good time to invest in what lasts and to let love grow deeper and more honest.","At the dark moon, offer a pomegranate and a red candle for love that transforms rather than controls."],"Pluto|Mars":["Drive becomes intense and determined, and you may take on a huge challenge, physical or otherwise, and see it through by sheer will. Power struggles are possible. Use the force constructively, and pace the body; Pluto's energy can push past healthy limits.","Conflict, power struggles or deep anger may surface, sometimes with people who use force. Avoid danger, do not meet force with force, and find a channel for the anger in hard work or exercise.","Powerful, effective action comes more easily, and you can achieve things that need endurance and nerve. Use it for a goal that matters, and let the strength serve others as well as yourself.","Carry an iron nail wrapped in black cloth as a charm for strength used well, and give it to the earth when the transit ends."],"Pluto|Ascendant":["Pluto crossing the Ascendant transforms your presence, body and the direction of your life. You may go through a profound reinvention, often after a crisis or a long inner change. People may see you as more powerful or intense. Let the old skin go.","The square brings pressure to transform how you live; the opposition, crossing the Descendant, brings power struggles or deep change in partnership. Meet others as equals, and let what must end, end.","Deep, empowering change in how you meet life comes more easily. It is a good time to reclaim your body, presence and personal power, through training, therapy or a change of direction.","At the dark moon, hold Obsidian before a mirror and name the self you are becoming."],"Pluto|Midheaven":["A career transformation: a rise to real power, a fall and rebuilding, or a complete change of calling. Your public life may be remade. Integrity is your protection; work that is true survives this transit, and work that is not falls away.","Power struggles at work or with authorities may come; the opposition, on the IC, brings deep change at home, in the family or in your roots. Stand on your values and let the structure be rebuilt.","Empowering career change comes more easily. It is a good time to take on influence and responsibility, and to work for real change in your field, with integrity as your guide.","At noon at the dark moon, burn a written statement of how you will use power in your work."],"Chiron|Sun":["Chiron on the Sun brings old hurts about identity to the surface: questions of worth, purpose, or how you were seen and not seen. It can be painful and healing at once. Many people find a calling to help others through this transit, or come to accept a part of themselves they had rejected.","Old wounds may be triggered by people or events, often at the points where you feel least sure of yourself. Give them care rather than shame, and look for a healer, teacher or friend who can witness them.","Healing comes more easily, and you may find yourself helping others or drawn to learn a healing art. It is a good time for therapy, teaching and self-acceptance, and for making peace with a part of your story.","Light a green candle on a Sunday and speak kindly, aloud, to the part of you that hurts."],"Chiron|Moon":["Old emotional and family wounds come to the surface to be healed: early needs that were not met, a parent's pain, or grief carried for years. Home may become a place of healing. Be gentle with yourself, and let feelings be felt.","Emotional pain may be triggered by family, home or people who remind you of the past, and old needs may feel raw. Care for yourself gently, let others care for you, and give the feelings time and a safe place.","Emotional healing comes more easily. It is a good time for family reconciliation, inner-child work and tending the body with rest and good food, and for letting someone look after you.","Drink chamomile tea on a Monday evening with a hand on your heart, and name one old need you will now meet yourself."],"Chiron|Mercury":["Old wounds around learning, speaking and being heard come up. You may revisit school memories, a sibling relationship, or a time you were silenced. Writing and speaking about them can heal, and you may find words for others too.","Communication may hurt: misunderstandings, criticism or a sense of being unheard. Old doubts about your intelligence may surface. Give yourself time to answer, write before you speak, and find one listener you trust.","Healing words come easily. It is a good time to write, teach or counsel, to speak about old hurts, or to learn something you once believed you could not. Your words may help someone else heal.","Write a letter to your younger self, the one who was afraid to speak, and read it aloud by a green candle."],"Chiron|Venus":["Old love wounds come up: rejection, betrayal, or a sense of not being lovable or beautiful. Relationships may bring them to the surface. This is a chance to heal how you love and how you let yourself be loved.","Love may hurt, or old patterns in love and self-worth may repeat. You may feel unlovable or unattractive for a time. Notice the pattern, be gentle with yourself, and choose differently when you can.","Love heals, and art and beauty become medicine. It is a good time to make peace with your body and your heart, to mend a relationship, or to make art from what has hurt.","Light a green and a pink candle together on a Friday and say one kind thing about your own body."],"Chiron|Mars":["Old wounds around anger, courage and action come up: times you could not defend yourself, or times your anger hurt others. The body may carry the memory. Healing comes through safe, strong action and honest anger.","Anger may be triggered, or you may feel unable to act or defend yourself, as old memories stir. Move the body gently, seek support for old hurts, and avoid fights that are really about the past.","Healing action comes more easily. It is a good time for martial arts, physical therapy or standing up for others, and for learning to use anger cleanly and well.","Carry a sprig of yarrow on a Tuesday as a charm for brave healing."],"Chiron|Ascendant":["Old wounds about the body, appearance and how you meet the world come up. You may face a health issue or a visible change, and with it a chance to accept yourself more deeply.","Wounds may be triggered in how others see you, and you may feel exposed or judged. The opposition, on the Descendant, brings them through partnership. Choose kind people and kind mirrors.","A healing presence comes more easily, and others may find you gentle and safe. It is a good time for bodywork, self-acceptance and helping others feel at home in themselves.","Each morning of the transit, speak one kind sentence to your reflection."],"Chiron|Midheaven":["Old wounds about success, failure and vocation come up. You may feel exposed in public, or face a setback, and find in it a calling that grows from your own healing. Many people change career towards care or teaching under this transit.","Career wounds may be triggered by criticism or setbacks; the opposition, on the IC, brings family wounds to the surface. Heal the roots, and let your work grow from that healing rather than from fear.","Healing work goes well. It is a good time to begin or deepen a vocation in care, teaching or advocacy, and to let your own story inform how you help others.","At noon, write the healing work you are called to and keep it under a green candle."],"North Node|Sun":["The North Node on your Sun points your whole self towards growth: you may meet people, choices or events that feel destined, often around eclipses. Say yes to what moves you forward, even when it is unfamiliar.","Your direction may be tested, and you may feel pulled between old habits and new growth, especially around eclipses. People or events may ask you to choose. Let go of what holds you back, and lean towards the unfamiliar.","Growth flows easily, and opportunities support who you are becoming. Act on them; they often come through people met by chance, and around eclipse seasons.","At an eclipse new moon, set an intention for the self you are growing into."],"North Node|Moon":["Growth comes through feelings, home and family. You may meet people who feel like family, move to a place that feels meant, or find your emotional needs changing in a way that points forward. Follow what nourishes you.","Feelings may be tested, and old emotional habits or family patterns may pull you back towards what is familiar. Let them go gently; the comfort of the old way is not the same as what you need.","Emotional growth comes easily, with support from family and friends. It is a good time to deepen bonds at home and let your feelings guide your direction.","Make moon water at an eclipse full moon and use it to bless the home."],"North Node|Mercury":["Growth comes through learning, writing and conversation. A meeting, a course or a book may change your direction. Say yes to the conversations that open new ways of thinking.","Your thinking may be tested, and old ideas or habits of speech may hold you back. Stay open, ask questions, and let yourself be wrong about something important.","Learning comes easily and moves you forward. It is a good time for study, writing and conversations that help you find your direction.","Write a question at an eclipse and keep it until the next one."],"North Node|Venus":["Growth comes through love, beauty and values. A relationship, friendship or creative work may feel destined, and what you value may shift towards what serves your path.","Love or money may be tested, and old patterns of attachment or spending may hold you back. Ask whether what you love is helping you grow.","Love and art come easily and move you forward. It is a good time for creative work, new friendships and relationships that help you grow.","Offer a rose at an eclipse for love that helps you grow."],"North Node|Mars":["Growth comes through action, courage and drive. You may take a bold step that changes your direction, often around an eclipse. Act on what moves you forward.","Your drive may be tested, and old anger or old ways of fighting may hold you back. Choose your battles by whether they serve your path.","Brave action comes easily and moves you forward. It is a good time to start something bold that fits your direction.","Light a red candle at an eclipse for courage on your path."],"North Node|Ascendant":["Growth comes through the self: independence, a new look or a new beginning. The South Node on the Descendant asks you to stop living through others. You may meet people who help you become yourself.","Your path may be tested in how you meet the world. The opposition puts the North Node on the Descendant, asking for growth through partnership and cooperation rather than going it alone.","Growth flows easily into how you meet life, and new beginnings tend to point the right way. Trust your instincts about who you are becoming.","At an eclipse, look in a mirror and name your direction."],"North Node|Midheaven":["Growth comes through career and public life. A role, opportunity or calling may feel destined, often around an eclipse. Step forward and let yourself be seen.","Career and home may be tested against each other; the opposition puts the North Node on the IC, asking for growth through home and family.","Career growth comes easily, and work that fits your path finds you. It is a good time to take on roles that stretch you in the right direction.","At noon at an eclipse, write a vocational aim."]}},3099,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"GLOSSES",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SIGN_PLAIN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"ELEMENT_PLAIN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"ELEMENT_SAME",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"ELEMENT_PAIR",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return h}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MODE_PLAIN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return l}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MODE_SAME",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return u}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MODE_PAIR",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return y}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PLANET_PLAIN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return c}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"RULER_PLAIN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return f}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MODERN_CORULER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return p}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"HOUSE_PLAIN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return w}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SIDE_PLAIN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return b}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"QUADRANT_PLAIN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return k}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"ELEMENT_LEAN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return v}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MODE_LEAN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return x}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TEMPERAMENT",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return M}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"ASPECT_PLAIN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return Y}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PATTERN_PLAIN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return j}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"BIRTH_PHASE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return P}});const t={'rising sign':'the sign that was coming up over the eastern horizon as you were born','chart ruler':'the planet that rules your rising sign, and so steers the whole chart',house:'a slice of the chart standing for one area of life','on an angle':'in one of the four most powerful places in a chart: the rising point, the setting point, the top and the bottom',exalted:'in the sign where it is traditionally honoured and works at its best','in detriment':'in the sign opposite its home, where it has to work in an unfamiliar way','in fall':'in the sign opposite the one where it is honoured, so it has to try harder',retrograde:'seeming to move backwards from Earth, which many read as turning its energy inwards',conjunction:'two planets side by side, acting as one',opposition:'two planets facing each other across the chart',square:'two planets a quarter of the circle apart',trine:'two planets a third of the circle apart, usually in the same element',sextile:'two planets a sixth of the circle apart',quincunx:'two planets five signs apart, with little in common',stellium:'three or more planets bunched in one sign or house','T-square':'two planets facing each other, both pressing on a third','grand trine':'three planets evenly spaced round the chart in one element','grand cross':'four planets in a cross, each facing one and pressing on two',yod:'two planets in an easy link, both at an awkward angle to a third','kite pattern':'three planets in an easy triangle, with a fourth opposite one corner',cardinal:'starting: the signs that begin each season',fixed:'keeping: the signs in the settled middle of each season',mutable:'adapting: the signs that end each season and change it',modality:'how a sign moves: starting, keeping or adapting',Midheaven:'the top of the chart, tied to career and public life'},n={Aries:{adj:'bold, quick and direct',core:'to act, to lead and to meet a challenge head on',need:'freedom to act, honest heat and something to aim at',front:'quick, frank and ready to go'},Taurus:{adj:'steady, patient and sensual',core:'to build something lasting and enjoy the good things of life',need:'comfort, routine, good food and time that is not rushed',front:'calm, solid and unhurried'},Gemini:{adj:'curious, lively and talkative',core:'to learn, connect and keep the mind moving',need:'conversation, variety and something new to think about',front:'bright, chatty and quick to engage'},Cancer:{adj:'tender, protective and loyal',core:'to care for your own and make a home',need:'closeness, a safe nest and people who stay',front:'gentle, watchful and slow to trust strangers'},Leo:{adj:'warm, proud and generous',core:'to create, to shine and to be loved for who you are',need:'warmth, appreciation and a chance to play',front:'warm, confident and hard to miss'},Virgo:{adj:'careful, useful and observant',core:'to improve things, to be skilled and to be of real use',need:'order, a useful task and things done properly',front:'modest, neat and quietly observant'},Libra:{adj:'gracious, fair and sociable',core:'to make things balanced, beautiful and fair',need:'harmony, good company and peace in the room',front:'charming, polite and easy to like'},Scorpio:{adj:'deep, intense and private',core:'to get to the truth and to transform what you touch',need:'trust, depth and loyalty you can count on',front:'reserved, magnetic and hard to read'},Sagittarius:{adj:'free, hopeful and outspoken',core:'to explore, to find meaning and to tell the truth as you see it',need:'room to roam, honesty and something to believe in',front:'open, friendly and restless'},Capricorn:{adj:'serious, ambitious and dependable',core:'to achieve, to build a reputation and to master your craft',need:'a plan, respect and a sense of being in control',front:'composed, capable and a little formal'},Aquarius:{adj:'independent, original and fair-minded',core:'to be your own person and make things better for everyone',need:'space, friendship and freedom from fuss',front:'friendly but cool, and a little unusual'},Pisces:{adj:'dreamy, kind and sensitive',core:'to imagine, to heal and to feel part of something larger',need:'quiet, kindness and time to drift',front:'soft, gentle and hard to pin down'}},o={fire:{is:'energy, enthusiasm and action',wants:'charge ahead and act on it'},earth:{is:'practical sense, steadiness and the body',wants:'take it slowly and make it real'},air:{is:'ideas, words and other people',wants:'think it over and talk it through'},water:{is:'feeling, intuition and closeness',wants:'feel its way and trust its gut'}},s={fire:'Fire feeds fire, so these parts of you agree about wanting life to be lively, brave and moving. You tend to act on enthusiasm without much inner argument. The thing to watch is burning out: with nothing in you saying "wait", rest and follow-through can slip.',earth:'Earth on earth makes firm ground. These parts of you agree about wanting things to be real, useful and lasting, and you rarely feel torn between them. You can be very dependable. The thing to watch is getting stuck: when nothing inside asks for change, a rut can feel like safety.',air:'Air with air keeps the mind turning. These parts of you agree that life is about ideas, talk and connection, so you think quickly and get on with people easily. The thing to watch is living in your head: feelings and the body can get left behind while you analyse.',water:'Water joins water easily. These parts of you agree about what matters most: feeling, closeness and the people you love. Your emotional world is rich and your instincts strong. The thing to watch is being swamped: with nothing inside saying "step back", other people\'s moods can become yours.'},h={'fire|earth':{image:'Fire and earth: a forge',text:'Fire wants to leap; earth wants to build. Together they can be very productive, with the spark of an idea and the patience to make it real, but they run at different speeds. One side gets restless at the other\'s caution, the other side gets uneasy at the first one\'s risks.',work:'Let the fire side start things and the earth side finish them, and agree a pace both can live with.'},'fire|air':{image:'Fire and air: a fanned flame',text:'Air feeds fire, so these two lift each other. Ideas turn into enthusiasm and enthusiasm into more ideas; you are likely lively, sociable and quick to get going. What they share is speed, and what they can both lack is staying power and attention to feelings.',work:'Pick one idea at a time to see through, and check in with how you actually feel, not only what you think.'},'fire|water':{image:'Fire and water: steam',text:'Fire and water are the classic odd couple. Fire wants to act now, water wants to feel its way first; fire is outgoing, water protective. That can feel like being pulled between boldness and sensitivity, or like reacting strongly and then feeling it deeply afterwards. Handled well, it makes steam: passion with real heart behind it.',work:'Give feelings a moment before you act, and give action a chance before you sink into feeling.'},'earth|air':{image:'Earth and air: a plan on paper',text:'Earth deals in what is real and air in what is possible. One side of you wants proof and practical results; the other wants ideas, talk and new angles. That can feel like a sensible voice arguing with a curious one. Together they make a good planner: ideas tested against reality.',work:'Let ideas run free for a while, then ask the practical questions; neither voice needs to win outright.'},'earth|water':{image:'Earth and water: a garden',text:'Water softens earth and earth gives water a shape, so these two get on well. You are likely caring in practical ways, steady in your feelings and loyal. What they share is a love of security, so the risk is caution: both sides can hold on to people, habits and things a little too long.',work:'Use the steadiness to take one small risk at a time, knowing you have firm ground to come back to.'},'air|water':{image:'Air and water: mist',text:'Air wants to understand; water wants to feel. One side of you steps back to think, the other dives in to feel, and they do not always trust each other. It can show as talking about feelings instead of having them, or being swept by feelings you cannot explain. Together they can make a rare thing: emotional intelligence.',work:'Name what you feel in words, and let some feelings simply be felt without having to explain them.'}},l={cardinal:{who:'a starter',style:'begins things and takes the lead'},fixed:{who:'a keeper',style:'holds steady and sees things through'},mutable:{who:'an adapter',style:'bends, adjusts and moves with change'}},u={cardinal:'Both are starters, so you like to begin, decide and take charge, and you do not wait to be asked. Finishing and sticking with things may take more conscious effort.',fixed:'Both are keepers, so you are steady, loyal and very hard to push. Once you have decided, you stay decided. Change, when it comes, may need to be your own idea.',mutable:'Both are adapters, so you are flexible, quick to adjust and good at seeing several sides. Choosing one path and holding to it can be the harder part.'},y={'cardinal|fixed':'One side wants to start something new and the other wants to keep what works. It can feel like an accelerator and a brake pressed together, but it also means you can both begin and sustain.','cardinal|mutable':'One side wants to lead and decide, the other wants to keep options open. You can be quick to start and quick to change course; the risk is starting more than you finish.','fixed|mutable':'One side holds firm while the other wants to adapt. You can be steady at the core and flexible at the edges, though sometimes you may dig in where bending would help, or bend where you should hold.'},c={Sun:{self:'your sense of who you are',wants:'to be seen and to live by your own purpose',gift:'warmth, confidence and a clear sense of direction',practice:'doing one thing each day that is wholly your own choice',strong:'A strong Sun tends to make a person noticed. You carry a sense of purpose and often end up at the centre of things, whether you mean to or not. Day to day it shows as a need to make your mark and a low tolerance for living by someone else\'s plan.'},Moon:{self:'your feelings and needs',wants:'to feel safe, fed and at home',gift:'sensitivity, care and a feel for what others need',practice:'regular rest, good food and time at home, kept like an appointment',strong:'A strong Moon makes feelings and instincts central. You likely read moods quickly, care for people without being asked and need a real home base. Day to day your energy rises and falls with how safe and looked after you feel, so routine and rest matter more than they might for others.'},Mercury:{self:'your mind and the way you talk',wants:'to understand things, name them and pass them on',gift:'quick thinking, a way with words and curiosity',practice:'writing things down, learning something new and talking it through',strong:'A strong Mercury makes the mind the main tool. You are likely quick, observant and good with words, and people may come to you to explain, sort out or put things into words. Day to day you need mental stimulation; boredom is harder on you than tiredness.'},Venus:{self:'what you love and value',wants:'pleasure, beauty, closeness and fairness',gift:'charm, taste and an easy way with people',practice:'making something beautiful and spending time with people you like',strong:'A strong Venus brings charm and a feel for beauty and people. Relationships, art, pleasure and fairness are likely to matter a great deal, and people often find you easy to be around. Day to day you need some beauty and affection around you; a harsh or ugly setting drains you quickly.'},Mars:{self:'your drive and fight',wants:'to act, to win and to defend what matters',gift:'courage, energy and the nerve to begin',practice:'hard physical work or exercise and plain, honest disagreement',strong:'A strong Mars brings energy, nerve and a competitive edge. You are likely direct, quick to act and willing to fight for what matters. Day to day you need a physical outlet and a goal; without them the same energy can turn into irritation.'},Jupiter:{self:'your hope and appetite for growth',wants:'more room, more meaning and more of life',gift:'generosity, faith and a knack for good fortune',practice:'study, travel and giving something away',strong:'A strong Jupiter brings optimism, generosity and a big-picture view. Doors tend to open, and you are likely the one who believes things will work out. Day to day you need something to grow towards; the risk is overdoing it, saying yes to too much.'},Saturn:{self:'your sense of duty and limits',wants:'order, mastery and things done properly',gift:'patience, staying power and skill built slowly',practice:'small, steady routines and promises you can keep',strong:'A strong Saturn brings seriousness, responsibility and staying power. You may have grown up early, and you likely earn what you get through patience and work. Day to day you need structure and a sense of progress; you may also need reminding that rest is not failure.'},Uranus:{self:'your urge for freedom and change',wants:'to break the pattern and be yourself, however unusual',gift:'originality and sudden insight',practice:'room to experiment, and a little rebellion with a purpose',strong:'A strong Uranus marks someone who does not fit the mould. You likely value freedom, have flashes of insight and get restless with rules that make no sense. Day to day you need room to do things your own way; too much routine feels like a cage.'},Neptune:{self:'your imagination and longing',wants:'to merge with something larger: art, faith, love or dream',gift:'imagination, compassion and spiritual feeling',practice:'music, prayer, time by water and writing down dreams, with clear boundaries',strong:'A strong Neptune brings imagination, sensitivity and a feel for the unseen. You may be artistic, spiritual or deeply empathetic, and boundaries between you and others can be thin. Day to day you need quiet and beauty to recharge, and clear limits so you do not lose yourself in other people.'},Pluto:{self:'your depth and power',wants:'the truth underneath, and control over your own life',gift:'resilience and the power to remake yourself',practice:'honest inner work and letting go of what is finished',strong:'A strong Pluto brings intensity and depth. You are likely drawn to what is hidden, see through pretence and go through big changes rather than small ones. Day to day you need honesty and a sense of control over your own life; shallowness wears you out.'},Ascendant:{self:'the way you meet the world',wants:'to be met as you are',gift:'a ready presence',practice:'care of the body and attention to how you begin things',strong:''},Midheaven:{self:'your public path and calling',wants:'a place in the world that means something',gift:'a sense of vocation',practice:'small steps towards the work you want to be known for',strong:''}},f={Sun:'With the Sun as your chart ruler, life is steered by the need to be fully yourself in full view: to create, to lead and to be recognised for what you do. You tend to come alive when you have something that is clearly yours.',Moon:'With the Moon as your chart ruler, life is steered by feeling. Your moods, your home and the people you care for set your direction more than any plan, and your sense of safety colours everything.',Mercury:'With Mercury as your chart ruler, life is steered by the mind. Curiosity, learning, talk and making connections lead you on, and you often find your way by thinking or talking it through.',Venus:'With Venus as your chart ruler, life is steered by what you love. Relationships, beauty, pleasure and fairness lead you on, and you tend to move towards what feels harmonious and away from what feels ugly or unjust.',Mars:'With Mars as your chart ruler, life is steered by drive. You move forward by acting, competing and pushing through, and you tend to feel most yourself when you have a challenge in front of you.',Jupiter:'With Jupiter as your chart ruler, life is steered by hope and growth. You are led on by meaning, learning, travel and faith, and you tend to trust that the next horizon holds something good.',Saturn:'With Saturn as your chart ruler, life is steered by responsibility and long effort. You tend to build slowly and surely, take duties seriously and grow into yourself with age; many people with this ruler find life gets easier, not harder, as the years go on.'},p={Uranus:'Modern astrologers add Uranus as a co-ruler, bringing a streak of independence and a need to do things your own way.',Neptune:'Modern astrologers add Neptune as a co-ruler, bringing imagination, sensitivity and a pull towards the spiritual.',Pluto:'Modern astrologers add Pluto as a co-ruler, bringing intensity and a life marked by deep changes.'},w={1:{area:'yourself, your body and how you come across',cluster:'Life keeps bringing you back to yourself: your body, your look and your way of starting things. You are often the visible one, and much of your growth comes through learning who you are and acting on it.'},2:{area:'money, possessions and what you value',cluster:'Much of your energy goes into security: earning, owning, saving and working out what is truly worth something to you. Your sense of self-worth and your bank balance can feel closely tied.'},3:{area:'talk, learning, siblings and your neighbourhood',cluster:'Your energy goes into communication: talking, writing, learning, short journeys and the people close by, including brothers and sisters. A busy mind and a busy phone are likely.'},4:{area:'home, family and roots',cluster:'Home and family are at the centre: where you live, where you come from and the private life behind closed doors. Your roots, and the home you make, shape you more than most.'},5:{area:'pleasure, creativity, romance and children',cluster:'Your energy goes into joy: creating, playing, falling in love, children and whatever lets you express yourself. You need fun, and you do your best work when you enjoy it.'},6:{area:'daily work, health and routines',cluster:'Your energy goes into the everyday: work, habits, health and being useful. How you spend an ordinary Tuesday matters a great deal to how you feel about your life.'},7:{area:'partners and close one-to-one relationships',cluster:'Your energy goes into partnership: marriage, close friendships, business partners and even rivals. You often learn who you are through other people, and relationships are where your life\'s lessons tend to arrive.'},8:{area:'intimacy, shared money, endings and the hidden depths',cluster:'Your energy goes into the deep end: intimacy, trust, shared resources, loss and renewal. Life asks you to go below the surface, and you are rarely satisfied with shallow answers.'},9:{area:'beliefs, study, travel and the search for meaning',cluster:'Your energy goes into the search for meaning: travel, higher learning, faith, philosophy and other cultures. You need a bigger picture to make sense of life.'},10:{area:'career, reputation and your public role',cluster:'Your energy goes into your public life: career, reputation, ambition and what you are known for. People notice what you do, and you likely feel driven to achieve something visible.'},11:{area:'friends, groups, community and hopes for the future',cluster:'Your energy goes into community: friends, groups, causes and hopes for the future. You do well in a network, and the people you gather around you shape where you go.'},12:{area:'solitude, the unconscious and quiet inner work',cluster:'Your energy goes inwards: solitude, dreams, spirituality, rest and the things you keep to yourself. Much happens behind the scenes, and you need time alone to stay well.'}},b={above:'Most of your planets sit in the top half of the chart, the part above the horizon. Many astrologers read this as a life lived outwards, in public and among others; your attention tends to go to the world, your role and what you do.',below:'Most of your planets sit in the bottom half of the chart, the part below the horizon. Many astrologers read this as a more private, inward life; your attention tends to go to home, feelings and personal matters, and you may build quietly before you are seen.',east:'Most of your planets sit on the left-hand side of the chart, the rising side. This is often read as self-directed: you tend to make your own choices and shape your own life, and you may find it harder to wait on others.',west:'Most of your planets sit on the right-hand side of the chart, the setting side. This is often read as a life shaped through others: partners, clients and friends bring your opportunities, and you do well by working with people rather than alone.'},k={1:'The busiest quarter is the first (the first to third houses): much of your energy is about yourself, your resources and your mind, finding out who you are and what you have.',2:'The busiest quarter is the second (the fourth to sixth houses): much of your energy goes into home, creative self-expression and the daily work of living well.',3:'The busiest quarter is the third (the seventh to ninth houses): much of your energy goes into other people, what you share with them and how they widen your world.',4:'The busiest quarter is the fourth (the tenth to twelfth houses): much of your energy goes into your place in the wider world: career, community and the larger spiritual picture.'},v={fire:{dominant:'With fire leading, you likely run on enthusiasm and do best when life feels like an adventure. You start fast and inspire others; the work is in keeping going once the excitement fades.',missing:'With no fire, getting started and pushing yourself forward may not come naturally. You might find energy and confidence in livelier friends, or build it on purpose through movement and small, brave acts.',practice:'a candle lit with an intention, movement first thing, and one small brave act a week'},earth:{dominant:'With earth leading, you are likely practical, steady and good with your hands, money and time. You trust what you can see and touch; the work is in staying open to what cannot be measured.',missing:'With no earth, practical matters such as money, routines and the body may feel like hard work or an afterthought. You might lean on practical people, or build earth on purpose through simple routines, cooking and time outdoors.',practice:'gardening, cooking from scratch, a regular bedtime and bare feet on the ground'},air:{dominant:'With air leading, you likely live a good deal in ideas, words and people. You see patterns, talk well and need conversation; the work is in coming back into your body and feelings.',missing:'With no air, stepping back to see things from outside, or putting feelings into words, may take more effort. You might lean on talkative friends, or build air on purpose by writing, reading and asking questions.',practice:'journalling, reading, a walk in the wind and talking things through with a friend'},water:{dominant:'With water leading, you likely feel things deeply and read people well. Closeness, memory and intuition guide you; the work is in protecting your energy and not taking on everyone\'s moods.',missing:'With no water, feelings may be something you think about more than sit with, and you may be puzzled by more emotional people. You might find depth through others, or grow it on purpose with music, baths, tears and time with people you trust.',practice:'baths, moon-water, music that moves you and time by the sea or a river'}},x={cardinal:{dominant:'Most of your chart is in the starting signs, so you are likely an initiator: quick to begin, decide and take the lead. Life tends to feel like a series of fresh starts.',missing:'None of your planets is in the starting signs, so beginning things may be the hardest part. A firm date or a friend who gets things moving can help.'},fixed:{dominant:'Most of your chart is in the keeping signs, so you are likely steady, loyal and persistent. You finish what you start; the challenge is letting go when something has run its course.',missing:'None of your planets is in the keeping signs, so sticking with one thing for a long time may not come easily. Small, regular habits can build the staying power you need.'},mutable:{dominant:'Most of your chart is in the adapting signs, so you are likely flexible, versatile and good in a crisis. You can see every side; the challenge is choosing one and holding to it.',missing:'None of your planets is in the adapting signs, so changing plans or going with the flow may be hard. Building in a little slack can help when life does not follow the plan.'}},M={'fire|cardinal':{like:'Aries',text:'a spark: quick to see what needs doing and to do it first, brave, impatient and best at the beginning of things'},'fire|fixed':{like:'Leo',text:'a steady fire: warm, proud, loyal and creative, with a heart that keeps burning once it is lit'},'fire|mutable':{like:'Sagittarius',text:'a wildfire: restless, hopeful and adventurous, always heading for the next horizon'},'earth|cardinal':{like:'Capricorn',text:'a builder with a plan: ambitious, responsible and able to turn long goals into steady steps'},'earth|fixed':{like:'Taurus',text:'bedrock: calm, patient, sensual and very hard to move once settled'},'earth|mutable':{like:'Virgo',text:'a craftsperson: practical, skilled, helpful and always refining'},'air|cardinal':{like:'Libra',text:'a diplomat: sociable, fair-minded and quick to bring people together'},'air|fixed':{like:'Aquarius',text:'a free thinker: independent, principled and loyal to ideas and friends'},'air|mutable':{like:'Gemini',text:'a messenger: curious, quick-witted and endlessly interested in everything'},'water|cardinal':{like:'Cancer',text:'a protector: caring, intuitive and quick to look after your own'},'water|fixed':{like:'Scorpio',text:'deep water: intense, loyal, private and capable of great change'},'water|mutable':{like:'Pisces',text:'the sea: sensitive, imaginative and compassionate, shaped by everything around you'}},Y={conjunction:{framing:'a fusion: you rarely feel one without the other, and they act as one, for good and ill',work:'notice when one is running the other, and give each its own turn'},opposition:{framing:'a see-saw: you swing between the two, or meet one side in other people and argue with it there',work:'look for the middle way, and notice when you hand one side to someone else to carry'},square:{framing:'friction: the two get in each other\'s way, which is uncomfortable but keeps you moving',work:'use the friction as fuel, in small deliberate steps rather than blow-ups'},quincunx:{framing:'an awkward fit: the two speak different languages and need constant small adjustments',work:'make room for both in your week rather than hoping they will merge'},trine:{framing:'an easy flow: they help each other without effort',work:'use it on purpose, since easy gifts are easy to take for granted'},sextile:{framing:'an open door: a helpful link that works best when you take it up',work:'act on it: this gift grows with use'}},j={'t-square':'is a built-in engine of pressure: two parts of you pull against each other and both push on a third, which becomes where you try hardest and achieve most. It can be stressful, but people with one tend to get things done.','grand-cross':'is four parts of you pulling in four directions. Life can feel demanding, as though everything needs attention at once, but it builds great resilience: you learn to hold a lot together.','grand-trine':'is a closed circle of ease: a talent that comes so naturally you may not notice it. The risk is comfort; it shines when something else in the chart gives it a reason to work.',kite:'is an easy triangle with a purpose: the talent of the triangle, with a fourth planet opposite that pulls it out into the world and gives it a job.',yod:'is sometimes called the finger of fate: two parts of you that get along both point awkwardly at a third. Many people with one feel a sense of special task, reached through repeated adjustment rather than a straight line.',stellium:'puts a lot of you in one place. That sign or house becomes a strong theme in your life: a focus, a speciality, sometimes an obsession, and the place where your energy most naturally goes.'},P=[{name:'new Moon',text:'You were born near a new Moon, when the Sun and Moon stand together. Many astrologers read this as a person whose head and heart point the same way: instinctive, single-minded and starting fresh, sometimes without much distance on yourself.'},{name:'waxing crescent',text:'You were born under a waxing crescent Moon, as the light grows. This is often read as a person pushing out of the old towards something new: hopeful, determined and still finding their feet.'},{name:'first quarter Moon',text:'You were born near a first quarter Moon, when the Sun and Moon stand at right angles. This is often read as a builder\'s Moon: a life that moves forward by meeting obstacles and acting on them.'},{name:'waxing gibbous',text:'You were born under a waxing gibbous Moon, nearly full. This is often read as a refiner: someone who keeps improving, questioning and polishing until things are right.'},{name:'full Moon',text:'You were born near a full Moon, when the Sun and Moon face each other. Many astrologers read this as a person very aware of other people and of their own inner split: what you want and what you need often show up as two sides to balance, and relationships bring them into the open.'},{name:'waning gibbous',text:'You were born under a waning gibbous Moon, just past full. This is often read as a sharer: someone who wants to pass on what they know and make meaning of experience.'},{name:'last quarter Moon',text:'You were born near a last quarter Moon, as the light shrinks. This is often read as a person who questions and reforms: comfortable letting go of old forms to make room for better ones.'},{name:'balsamic Moon',text:'You were born under a balsamic Moon, the last thin crescent before the new. This is often read as a wise or old soul: reflective, a little apart and attuned to endings, rest and what comes next.'}]},3100,[]);
